GB-BKM,21,2020-12-23,52.0336802,-0.9402602,"<div id=""html_097ef48a81781a56e687e4419a444d5d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Leckhampstead</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Leckhampstead was impacted by flooding during the 23rd&ndash;24th December 2020 event. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Leckhampstead,England,Leckhampstead was impacted by flooding during the 23rd–24th December 2020 event. (p15),,GB-BKM_21_2020-12-23.html,GB-BKM_21_2020-12-23,Buckingham flooding 23 Dec 2020 - 24 Dec 2020,Buckingham Section 19 Flood Investigation: Final Technical Report,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2020/Buckinghamshire County/buckingham/technical/report-final-sept-2021-v1/V3sC5LE.pdf
GB-BKM,21,2020-12-23,52.0154955,-0.9053801,"<div id=""html_6893464d39a96890f0faed1d7dc0c93c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Thornton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Thornton and Thornborough were impacted by flooding during the 23rd&ndash;24th December 2020 event. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Thornton,England,Thornton and Thornborough were impacted by flooding during the 23rd–24th December 2020 event. (p15),,GB-BKM_21_2020-12-23.html,GB-BKM_21_2020-12-23,Buckingham flooding 23 Dec 2020 - 24 Dec 2020,Buckingham Section 19 Flood Investigation: Final Technical Report,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2020/Buckinghamshire County/buckingham/technical/report-final-sept-2021-v1/V3sC5LE.pdf
GB-BKM,21,2020-12-23,51.9955872,-0.9136531,"<div id=""html_344d4fd1f3dc65414bfd8d6ccd61a889"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Thornborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Thornton and Thornborough were impacted by flooding during the 23rd&ndash;24th December 2020 event. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Thornborough,England,Thornton and Thornborough were impacted by flooding during the 23rd–24th December 2020 event. (p15),,GB-BKM_21_2020-12-23.html,GB-BKM_21_2020-12-23,Buckingham flooding 23 Dec 2020 - 24 Dec 2020,Buckingham Section 19 Flood Investigation: Final Technical Report,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2020/Buckinghamshire County/buckingham/technical/report-final-sept-2021-v1/V3sC5LE.pdf
GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.3752877,-0.2666856,"<div id=""html_5e3a154985a0c6ffa42486b7c139704d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Alconbury Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a source of flooding in the catchment and contributed to flooding of downstream settlements (feeding into the Great Ouse system) during the reported event. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rising river levels in Alconbury Brook were identified as the primary driver of flooding in the Hamerton Road/Spires End area and caused sewer flooding in the Hamerton Road area. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rising river levels in Alconbury Brook caused river flooding that contributed to sewer and internal property flooding in nearby areas (notably North Road and High Street). (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Alconbury Brook was implicated in the December 2020 flooding of the catchment; flood flows caused erosion of the brook bank beneath the A1 flyover along High Street (work to stabilise the eroded bank has been discussed). The brook has since been the focus of desilting, bank vegetation works and installation of Natural Flood Management structures to reduce future flood risk. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Alconbury Brook had insufficient conveyance during the December 2020 flood, prompting flood&ndash;alleviation actions and planned hydraulic modelling to increase its ability to convey water during flood events. [PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Alconbury Brook was associated with flood&ndash;related RMA operational issues noted in the report, indicating it contributed to flooding impacts that required authority action. [TAB] (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 residential properties (North Road); 8 residential properties (High Street) (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Alconbury Brook,England,"Identified as a source of flooding in the catchment and contributed to flooding of downstream settlements (feeding into the Great Ouse system) during the reported event. (p5)
Rising river levels in Alconbury Brook were identified as the primary driver of flooding in the Hamerton Road/Spires End area and caused sewer flooding in the Hamerton Road area. (p12)
Rising river levels in Alconbury Brook caused river flooding that contributed to sewer and internal property flooding in nearby areas (notably North Road and High Street). (p13)
Alconbury Brook was implicated in the December 2020 flooding of the catchment; flood flows caused erosion of the brook bank beneath the A1 flyover along High Street (work to stabilise the eroded bank has been discussed). The brook has since been the focus of desilting, bank vegetation works and installation of Natural Flood Management structures to reduce future flood risk. (p16)
Alconbury Brook had insufficient conveyance during the December 2020 flood, prompting flood–alleviation actions and planned hydraulic modelling to increase its ability to convey water during flood events. [PAG] (p21)
Alconbury Brook was associated with flood–related RMA operational issues noted in the report, indicating it contributed to flooding impacts that required authority action. [TAB] (p22)",7 residential properties (North Road); 8 residential properties (High Street) (p13),GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01,Alconbury flooding December 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Alconbury and Alconbury Weston,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Alconbury-December-2020-Flood-Investigation-Version-1.1.pdf
GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.3348817,-0.2448297,"<div id=""html_607da7dc61291a5794bd0d096e084f0b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ellington Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ellington Brook, which drains the southern part of the catchment and flows along the A14, contributed to catchment flooding by conveying enhanced flows and surface&ndash;water runoff into downstream areas during the December 2020 event. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Ellington Brook,England,"Ellington Brook, which drains the southern part of the catchment and flows along the A14, contributed to catchment flooding by conveying enhanced flows and surface–water runoff into downstream areas during the December 2020 event. (p5)",,GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01,Alconbury flooding December 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Alconbury and Alconbury Weston,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Alconbury-December-2020-Flood-Investigation-Version-1.1.pdf
GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.3778108,-0.2685802,"<div id=""html_c2c108aa6548aec427dbe4d393057b47"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Vinegar Hill, Alconbury Weston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water run&ndash;off flowed downslope through the Vinegar Hill area between properties (Butcher's Close), entered properties through external walls and floors and was conveyed away via a foul sewer in a wet room. A formerly present ditch in the area had been filled, altering flow paths. [IMG,PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water run&ndash;off flowed down Vinegar Hill into the centre of Alconbury Weston; water entered properties through external walls and floors and was conveyed away through a foul sewer in a wet room. Cellar, outbuilding and garden flooding also occurred. [TAB] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reports of flooding and surface water runoff from fields to the north of Alconbury Weston; RMA attended the site to investigate and perform a walkover, and the LLFA met residents to gather local information. The landowner is investigating measures to manage runoff to prevent future flooding. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred at Vinegar Hill (Alconbury Weston), as identified in the report. [TAB] (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential property [TAB] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Vinegar Hill, Alconbury Weston",England,"Surface water run–off flowed downslope through the Vinegar Hill area between properties (Butcher's Close), entered properties through external walls and floors and was conveyed away via a foul sewer in a wet room. A formerly present ditch in the area had been filled, altering flow paths. [IMG,PAG] (p11)
Surface water run–off flowed down Vinegar Hill into the centre of Alconbury Weston; water entered properties through external walls and floors and was conveyed away through a foul sewer in a wet room. Cellar, outbuilding and garden flooding also occurred. [TAB] (p12)
Reports of flooding and surface water runoff from fields to the north of Alconbury Weston; RMA attended the site to investigate and perform a walkover, and the LLFA met residents to gather local information. The landowner is investigating measures to manage runoff to prevent future flooding. [TAB] (p17)
Surface water flooding occurred at Vinegar Hill (Alconbury Weston), as identified in the report. [TAB] (p22)",1 residential property [TAB] (p12),GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01,Alconbury flooding December 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Alconbury and Alconbury Weston,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Alconbury-December-2020-Flood-Investigation-Version-1.1.pdf
GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.384483,-0.2786632,"<div id=""html_30aa01c0ba7e5b56ee4d049de5e159b0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hamerton Road, Alconbury Weston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as one of the key areas where internal property flooding was reported during the December 2020 event. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced combined flooding driven primarily by rising river levels in Alconbury Brook, with associated sewer flooding and exacerbation from surface water run&ndash;off; 17 residential properties were flooded internally (to c.1200mm) and outbuildings and gardens were also flooded; residents reported having to leave their homes for periods over six months. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties to a depth of around 1200 mm; additional outbuilding and garden flooding; residents displaced from their homes for periods greater than six months. [TAB] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 residential properties [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 residential properties; depth c.1200mm; displacement periods &gt;6 months [TAB] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Hamerton Road, Alconbury Weston",England,"Identified as one of the key areas where internal property flooding was reported during the December 2020 event. (p11)
Experienced combined flooding driven primarily by rising river levels in Alconbury Brook, with associated sewer flooding and exacerbation from surface water run–off; 17 residential properties were flooded internally (to c.1200mm) and outbuildings and gardens were also flooded; residents reported having to leave their homes for periods over six months. [PAG] (p12)
