GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.36887428630241,-0.26004605156404725,"<div id=""html_23b307c5c9bd2d7aaef83f9a3a2825bb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Alconbury</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal property flooding was reported in this area during the December 2020 event. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties to a depth of about 750mm; additional outbuilding and garden flooding. Pumps at Rusts Lane (a Cambridgeshire Highways asset) failed to convey surface water, contributing to the local flooding. Residents reported being displaced from their homes for periods over 6 months. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding associated with the December 2020 event eroded the bank beneath the A1 flyover along High Street. The LLFA, the Alconbury Brook Flood Group, Cambridgeshire Highways, Cllr Ian Gardener, Highways England and a contractor met in August 2021 to discuss potential future stabilisation works for the eroded bank. [MUL] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>LLFA/RMA attended to investigate reports of flooding; Cambridgeshire Highways ordered cleaning of pumps at Rusts Lane to address flooding issues. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 residential properties; depth c.750mm; displacement over 6 months (High Street and Rusts Lane) [TAB] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"High Street, Alconbury",England,"Internal property flooding was reported in this area during the December 2020 event. (p11)
