GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.3673267,-0.2607482,"<div id=""html_4f76c01d7b0c4854a361946b573499ce"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mill Road, Alconbury</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in the area affected by river flooding from rising Alconbury Brook; residential properties in the area were flooded (area total 24 properties internally flooded to about 550mm), with outbuilding and garden flooding and residents displaced for periods of over 6 months. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>24 residential properties (area total); periods of over 6 months (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Mill Road, Alconbury",England,"Included in the area affected by river flooding from rising Alconbury Brook; residential properties in the area were flooded (area total 24 properties internally flooded to about 550mm), with outbuilding and garden flooding and residents displaced for periods of over 6 months. (p14)",24 residential properties (area total); periods of over 6 months (p14),GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01,Alconbury flooding December 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Alconbury and Alconbury Weston,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Alconbury-December-2020-Flood-Investigation-Version-1.1.pdf
GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.360534,-0.2690709,"<div id=""html_4cc3b8283efeb1545c45e7e515e422ea"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Globe Lane, Alconbury</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the locality affected by river flooding from Alconbury Brook; the area experienced internal flooding (area total 24 residential properties affected to about 550mm), plus outbuilding and garden flooding and prolonged displacement of residents. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>24 residential properties (area total); periods of over 6 months (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Globe Lane, Alconbury",England,"Part of the locality affected by river flooding from Alconbury Brook; the area experienced internal flooding (area total 24 residential properties affected to about 550mm), plus outbuilding and garden flooding and prolonged displacement of residents. (p14)",24 residential properties (area total); periods of over 6 months (p14),GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01,Alconbury flooding December 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Alconbury and Alconbury Weston,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Alconbury-December-2020-Flood-Investigation-Version-1.1.pdf
GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.3658114,-0.255938,"<div id=""html_ecd1514df0efdfb69effec50ec29d364"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Frumetty Lane, Alconbury</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the area that experienced multi&ndash;source flooding (primarily driven by rising river levels with sewer flooding in conjunction and surface water exacerbated by pump failure); resulted in 22 residential properties flooded internally to c.750mm, plus outbuilding and garden flooding; residents reported being displaced for periods over 6 months. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 residential properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Frumetty Lane, Alconbury",England,"Part of the area that experienced multi–source flooding (primarily driven by rising river levels with sewer flooding in conjunction and surface water exacerbated by pump failure); resulted in 22 residential properties flooded internally to c.750mm, plus outbuilding and garden flooding; residents reported being displaced for periods over 6 months. (p14)",22 residential properties (p14),GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01,Alconbury flooding December 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Alconbury and Alconbury Weston,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Alconbury-December-2020-Flood-Investigation-Version-1.1.pdf
GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.3729017,-0.04493599422000649,"<div id=""html_7fc2d4318cd8b9874a71317c1bfba5b0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cambridgeshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall on 23 December 2020, following a prolonged wet period and saturated ground, produced very high runoff and high river levels and caused significant flooding in Alconbury and nearby Alconbury Weston. Properties were inundated internally and gardens/outbuildings damaged. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Pumps identified as a Cambridgeshire Highways asset at Rusts Lane failed during the December 2020 event; the asset failure contributed to the inability to convey surface water and to the overall flooding in Alconbury. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>95 properties; 59 properties in Alconbury; 36 properties in Alconbury Weston; 46 residential properties flooded internally in Alconbury; 32 residential properties flooded internally in Alconbury Weston; 13 properties with outbuilding/garage/garden damage in Alconbury; 4 properties with outbuilding/garage/garden damage in Alconbury Weston [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Cambridgeshire,England,"Intense rainfall on 23 December 2020, following a prolonged wet period and saturated ground, produced very high runoff and high river levels and caused significant flooding in Alconbury and nearby Alconbury Weston. Properties were inundated internally and gardens/outbuildings damaged. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Pumps identified as a Cambridgeshire Highways asset at Rusts Lane failed during the December 2020 event; the asset failure contributed to the inability to convey surface water and to the overall flooding in Alconbury. (p14)","95 properties; 59 properties in Alconbury; 36 properties in Alconbury Weston; 46 residential properties flooded internally in Alconbury; 32 residential properties flooded internally in Alconbury Weston; 13 properties with outbuilding/garage/garden damage in Alconbury; 4 properties with outbuilding/garage/garden damage in Alconbury Weston [PAG,IMG] (p10)",GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01,Alconbury flooding December 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Alconbury and Alconbury Weston,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Alconbury-December-2020-Flood-Investigation-Version-1.1.pdf
GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.368714542527975,-0.25833707792256316,"<div id=""html_125ff43f67062c9253f9f085d196671f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Alconbury</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwaters from Alconbury Brook and overland/surface&ndash;water runoff entered the settlement from surrounding agricultural fields, causing inundation of the settlement; flooding was exacerbated by saturated ground and the impermeable Oxford Clay. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding occurred in the settlement. [PAG,IMG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding occurred on 23rd December 2020 in Alconbury; flooding arose from both high river levels and surface water due to very high runoff following intense rainfall and saturated ground conditions. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding from both river and surface water following very high runoff and rising river levels; internal flooding of residential properties and damage to outbuildings/garages/gardens. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential and other properties experienced internal flooding; additional damage to outbuildings, garages and gardens. [IMG,PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rising Alconbury Brook levels caused river flooding and sewer flooding in conjunction with surface water run&ndash;off from fields; 17 residential properties flooded internally to about 1200mm, with additional outbuilding and garden flooding. Residents reported having to leave their homes for periods of over six months. [TAB,PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple areas of Alconbury experienced flooding: High Street (Alconbury Weston) &mdash; 8 residential properties flooded internally to c.1200mm with outbuilding and garden flooding, residents displaced for periods over 6 months; Brookside / Splash Lane / Mill Road / Globe Lane / Ford End &mdash; 24 residential properties flooded internally to c.550mm with outbuilding and garden flooding, residents displaced for periods over 6 months; High Street / Frumetty Lane / Coulson Close / Rusts Lane area &mdash; 22 residential properties flooded internally to c.750mm with outbuilding and garden flooding, residents displaced for periods over 6 months. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area&ndash;wide surface water flooding during the December 2020 event, including internal flooding of residential properties (notably 22 properties on High Street & Rusts Lane and 2 properties on Hill Field / School Lane). Local highway drainage and pumps (Rusts Lane) were unable to convey runoff, contributing to the overall flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Alconbury experienced flooding during December 2020 as part of the wider catchment event; residents were impacted and required community&ndash;level inspections and resilience activities afterwards. Residents reported being forced to leave their homes for prolonged periods following the flooding. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas of Alconbury (including High Street and Rusts Lane) experienced flooding during the December 2020 event, leading to local flood&ndash;alleviation actions, community support and planned hydraulic modelling. [PAG] (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>59 properties; 46 residential properties flooded internally; 13 properties with damage to outbuildings/garages/gardens [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>59 properties affected; 46 residential properties flooded internally; 13 properties damaged (outbuildings/garages/gardens). [IMG,PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 residential properties [TAB,PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 residential properties; 24 residential properties; 22 residential properties [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 residential properties; 2 residential properties; depth c.750mm; depth c.600mm [TAB,PAG] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Alconbury,England,"Floodwaters from Alconbury Brook and overland/surface–water runoff entered the settlement from surrounding agricultural fields, causing inundation of the settlement; flooding was exacerbated by saturated ground and the impermeable Oxford Clay. (p5)
Significant flooding occurred in the settlement. [PAG,IMG] (p7)
Significant flooding occurred on 23rd December 2020 in Alconbury; flooding arose from both high river levels and surface water due to very high runoff following intense rainfall and saturated ground conditions. (p8)
Significant flooding from both river and surface water following very high runoff and rising river levels; internal flooding of residential properties and damage to outbuildings/garages/gardens. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Residential and other properties experienced internal flooding; additional damage to outbuildings, garages and gardens. [IMG,PAG] (p11)
Rising Alconbury Brook levels caused river flooding and sewer flooding in conjunction with surface water run–off from fields; 17 residential properties flooded internally to about 1200mm, with additional outbuilding and garden flooding. Residents reported having to leave their homes for periods of over six months. [TAB,PAG] (p12)
Multiple areas of Alconbury experienced flooding: High Street (Alconbury Weston) — 8 residential properties flooded internally to c.1200mm with outbuilding and garden flooding, residents displaced for periods over 6 months; Brookside / Splash Lane / Mill Road / Globe Lane / Ford End — 24 residential properties flooded internally to c.550mm with outbuilding and garden flooding, residents displaced for periods over 6 months; High Street / Frumetty Lane / Coulson Close / Rusts Lane area — 22 residential properties flooded internally to c.750mm with outbuilding and garden flooding, residents displaced for periods over 6 months. [TAB] (p14)
Area–wide surface water flooding during the December 2020 event, including internal flooding of residential properties (notably 22 properties on High Street & Rusts Lane and 2 properties on Hill Field / School Lane). Local highway drainage and pumps (Rusts Lane) were unable to convey runoff, contributing to the overall flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p15)
Alconbury experienced flooding during December 2020 as part of the wider catchment event; residents were impacted and required community–level inspections and resilience activities afterwards. Residents reported being forced to leave their homes for prolonged periods following the flooding. [PAG] (p16)
Areas of Alconbury (including High Street and Rusts Lane) experienced flooding during the December 2020 event, leading to local flood–alleviation actions, community support and planned hydraulic modelling. [PAG] (p21)","59 properties; 46 residential properties flooded internally; 13 properties with damage to outbuildings/garages/gardens [PAG,IMG] (p10)
59 properties affected; 46 residential properties flooded internally; 13 properties damaged (outbuildings/garages/gardens). [IMG,PAG] (p11)
17 residential properties [TAB,PAG] (p12)
8 residential properties; 24 residential properties; 22 residential properties [TAB] (p14)
22 residential properties; 2 residential properties; depth c.750mm; depth c.600mm [TAB,PAG] (p15)",GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_12_2020-12-01,Alconbury flooding December 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Alconbury and Alconbury Weston,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Alconbury-December-2020-Flood-Investigation-Version-1.1.pdf
GB-CAM,12,2020-12-01,52.3804327,-0.2743296,"<div id=""html_1bf55063faab9261511366cc244a54c1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Alconbury Weston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater entered the settlements from surrounding agricultural fields and overland/surface runoff as a result of saturated ground and increased runoff velocity; settlements experienced flooding during the reported event. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding affected the settlement of Alconbury on 23 December 2020. [PAG,IMG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from river and surface water led to internal flooding of residential properties and damage to outbuildings/garages/gardens. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Combined reports from the LLFA and the Alconbury Brook Flood Group indicate widespread localised flooding across the two villages. A total of 95 properties were affected (59 in Alconbury; 36 in Alconbury Weston). Internal residential flooding occurred in multiple locations (46 residential properties internally flooded in Alconbury; 32 residential properties internally flooded in Alconbury Weston). Additional damage was noted to outbuildings, garages and gardens (13 properties in Alconbury; 4 properties in Alconbury Weston). The report groups impacted streets into seven key risk areas (Vinegar Hill, Hamerton Road, North Road, High Street (Alconbury Weston), Brookside, High Street and Rusts Lane, Hill Field and School Lane). [IMG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Alconbury Weston (including Hamerton Road, North Road and High Street) experienced internal residential flooding, outbuilding and garden flooding, and prolonged displacement of residents (periods &gt;6 months) due to river&ndash;driven and associated sewer flooding. [TAB] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential areas experienced flooding during December 2020; residents were identified as 'impacted by flooding' and visited by the LLFA. Flooding also caused erosion of the brook bank beneath the A1 flyover on High Street requiring discussion of stabilisation works. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Alconbury Brook's limited conveyance caused flooding in Alconbury and Alconbury Weston during the December 2020 event. Partners have undertaken and plan further actions (including hydraulic modelling) and the Environment Agency and the local Flood Group are working to improve conveyance; the LLFA is supporting residents and community flood action measures are being delivered in 2021&ndash;22. (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>36 properties; 32 residential properties flooded internally; 4 properties with damage to outbuildings/garages/gardens [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>95 properties; 59 properties; 36 properties; 46 residential properties; 32 residential properties; 13 properties; 4 properties [IMG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 residential properties (Hamerton Road); 7 residential properties (North Road); 8 residential properties (High Street); displacement periods &gt;6 months [TAB] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Alconbury Weston,England,"Floodwater entered the settlements from surrounding agricultural fields and overland/surface runoff as a result of saturated ground and increased runoff velocity; settlements experienced flooding during the reported event. (p5)
Significant flooding affected the settlement of Alconbury on 23 December 2020. [PAG,IMG] (p7)
