GB-CAM,21,2020-12-23,52.4380447,-0.3063495,"<div id=""html_5e1d4b3833c42069927e1ff0cdfa5d14"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Gidding Road, Sawtry</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding affected outbuildings and gardens (external flooding reported by LLFA and Parish Council). [TAB] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 flood report; 0 properties reporting internal flooding [TAB] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Gidding Road, Sawtry",England,External flooding affected outbuildings and gardens (external flooding reported by LLFA and Parish Council). [TAB] (p10),1 flood report; 0 properties reporting internal flooding [TAB] (p10),GB-CAM_21_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_21_2020-12-23,Sawtry flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Sawtry,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Sawtry-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,21,2020-12-23,52.4617238,0.6975642,"<div id=""html_6dec157d4b083bd93da0a7710e14984f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>East Anglia</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Prolonged higher&ndash;than&ndash;average rainfall through autumn and December 2020 produced a high water table and saturated ground across East Anglia, which contributed to surface water drainage systems being unable to cope and increased risk and occurrence of surface water flooding during the 23 December 2020 event. [PAG] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,East Anglia,England,"Prolonged higher–than–average rainfall through autumn and December 2020 produced a high water table and saturated ground across East Anglia, which contributed to surface water drainage systems being unable to cope and increased risk and occurrence of surface water flooding during the 23 December 2020 event. [PAG] (p8)",,GB-CAM_21_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_21_2020-12-23,Sawtry flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Sawtry,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Sawtry-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,21,2020-12-23,52.3729017,-0.04493599422000649,"<div id=""html_283545d68fa0393c048faf5d04ced803"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cambridgeshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External areas flooded. [TAB] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Cambridgeshire,England,External areas flooded. [TAB] (p13),,GB-CAM_21_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_21_2020-12-23,Sawtry flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Sawtry,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Sawtry-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,21,2020-12-23,52.4380671,-0.2820551,"<div id=""html_afe6052aa4fcd3654027c5aa5b969505"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sawtry</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water drainage systems were unable to convey runoff from intense rainfall on an already saturated catchment, resulting in excess surface water flowing over ground following local topography and affecting properties located in areas at risk of surface water flooding. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Nine flood reports were received for Sawtry on 23 December 2020, including at least one internal property flood reported to the LLFA; Parish Council communication indicated more widespread external and internal flooding across the village and reports of foul manholes surcharging. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from intense rainfall on 23 December 2020 caused significant overland surface water flooding and flooding from drainage systems that exceeded capacity in Sawtry; this prompted actions on riparian maintenance, highway drainage improvements and ongoing liaison with landowners and Risk Management Authorities. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 flood reports; 1 internal property flooded; c.2 properties; c.4 properties (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Sawtry,England,"Surface water drainage systems were unable to convey runoff from intense rainfall on an already saturated catchment, resulting in excess surface water flowing over ground following local topography and affecting properties located in areas at risk of surface water flooding. (p8)
Nine flood reports were received for Sawtry on 23 December 2020, including at least one internal property flood reported to the LLFA; Parish Council communication indicated more widespread external and internal flooding across the village and reports of foul manholes surcharging. (p10)
Runoff from intense rainfall on 23 December 2020 caused significant overland surface water flooding and flooding from drainage systems that exceeded capacity in Sawtry; this prompted actions on riparian maintenance, highway drainage improvements and ongoing liaison with landowners and Risk Management Authorities. (p19)",9 flood reports; 1 internal property flooded; c.2 properties; c.4 properties (p10),GB-CAM_21_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_21_2020-12-23,Sawtry flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Sawtry,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Sawtry-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-BKM,2,2014-09-20,51.70344210498221,-0.613103833671937,"<div id=""html_408b512d812da46ea38a91c2aca05612"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Market Square, Chesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Mainly business properties flooded originating at Market Square and extending along the High Street north to The Broadway (identified as Area B). (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>CCTV footage showed surface water flooding in Market Square exceeding the capacity of the slot drain along the eastern edge and the gullies along the western edge, producing ponding that peaked around 05:00 and had fully dissipated by 06:00. The recent replacement of the Vale Brook culvert section in Market Square was followed by compaction of sand around the new culvert and collapse of brick pavers at the surface during the rainfall event; the collapse did not affect culvert performance. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water exceeded the capacity of the slot drain along the eastern edge and gullies on the western edge, producing ponding across the width of Market Square (peak ponding ~05:00, dissipated by ~06:03). The event caused compaction of sand around a recently replaced Vale Brook culvert and collapse of brick pavers at the surface (surface damage), though culvert performance was not reduced. Properties in the square were flooded internally. [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water entered shops from the street&ndash;facing front causing internal shallow flooding; businesses reported some floor&ndash;level stock loss, damaged carpets and reduced trading hours while cleaning and drying took place. (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water drainage in Market Square performed poorly during the flooding (works were completed in 2014 but further improvements were recommended); the EA was asked to identify possible improvements linked to the Flood Alleviation Scheme. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,"Market Square, Chesham",England,"Mainly business properties flooded originating at Market Square and extending along the High Street north to The Broadway (identified as Area B). (p8)
CCTV footage showed surface water flooding in Market Square exceeding the capacity of the slot drain along the eastern edge and the gullies along the western edge, producing ponding that peaked around 05:00 and had fully dissipated by 06:00. The recent replacement of the Vale Brook culvert section in Market Square was followed by compaction of sand around the new culvert and collapse of brick pavers at the surface during the rainfall event; the collapse did not affect culvert performance. (p18)
Surface water exceeded the capacity of the slot drain along the eastern edge and gullies on the western edge, producing ponding across the width of Market Square (peak ponding ~05:00, dissipated by ~06:03). The event caused compaction of sand around a recently replaced Vale Brook culvert and collapse of brick pavers at the surface (surface damage), though culvert performance was not reduced. Properties in the square were flooded internally. [PAG] (p19)
Surface water entered shops from the street–facing front causing internal shallow flooding; businesses reported some floor–level stock loss, damaged carpets and reduced trading hours while cleaning and drying took place. (p20)
Surface water drainage in Market Square performed poorly during the flooding (works were completed in 2014 but further improvements were recommended); the EA was asked to identify possible improvements linked to the Flood Alleviation Scheme. [TAB] (p27)","5 properties [PAG] (p19)
5 properties (p20)",GB-BKM_2_2014-09-20.html,GB-BKM_2_2014-09-20,Chesham flooding 20 Sep 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Chesham 20 September 2014,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2014/Buckinghamshire County/150629-chesham-s19-report/final.pdf
GB-BKM,2,2014-09-20,51.7059356,-0.6123262,"<div id=""html_b8d4eaed83e58e256af6c39c44ff9f82"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Broadway, Chesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected The Broadway as the northern extent of business/property flooding that ran along the High Street from Market Square. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Building occupiers reported manhole surcharging within at least three shops along the High Street and Broadway. A shop owner on The Broadway observed a tidemark of water and dirt after the event; the visible water had dissipated via the surface water drainage system. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water entered properties from the street&ndash;facing front causing internal shallow flooding similar to other town&ndash;centre shops; impacts included wet flooring, some stock damage and cleanup/repairs where applicable. (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 3 shops (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,"The Broadway, Chesham",England,"Flooding affected The Broadway as the northern extent of business/property flooding that ran along the High Street from Market Square. (p8)
Building occupiers reported manhole surcharging within at least three shops along the High Street and Broadway. A shop owner on The Broadway observed a tidemark of water and dirt after the event; the visible water had dissipated via the surface water drainage system. (p18)
Surface water entered properties from the street–facing front causing internal shallow flooding similar to other town–centre shops; impacts included wet flooring, some stock damage and cleanup/repairs where applicable. (p20)","at least 3 shops (p18)
2 properties (p20)",GB-BKM_2_2014-09-20.html,GB-BKM_2_2014-09-20,Chesham flooding 20 Sep 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Chesham 20 September 2014,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2014/Buckinghamshire County/150629-chesham-s19-report/final.pdf
GB-BKM,2,2014-09-20,51.7080936,-0.6108903,"<div id=""html_cfd3e2dd493626d5b6f05068cf6a8d2e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Broad Street, Chesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property flooding occurred along Broad Street during the incident. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties were flooded internally, mainly by water entering from the street&ndash;facing front; two properties on the east side (at the St Mary's Way roundabout) were flooded by water entering from the rear. Impacts included stock water damage, carpet replacement and cleanup operations. (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties; 2 properties from the rear at St Mary's Way roundabout (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,"Broad Street, Chesham",England,"Property flooding occurred along Broad Street during the incident. (p8)
Properties were flooded internally, mainly by water entering from the street–facing front; two properties on the east side (at the St Mary's Way roundabout) were flooded by water entering from the rear. Impacts included stock water damage, carpet replacement and cleanup operations. (p20)",4 properties; 2 properties from the rear at St Mary's Way roundabout (p20),GB-BKM_2_2014-09-20.html,GB-BKM_2_2014-09-20,Chesham flooding 20 Sep 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Chesham 20 September 2014,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2014/Buckinghamshire County/150629-chesham-s19-report/final.pdf
GB-BKM,2,2014-09-20,51.7028683,-0.6178902,"<div id=""html_f7b950a4c22dbca3a567867a765df998"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pednormead End, Chesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties in the Pednormead End area flooded during the incident; Pednormead End is identified as Area A where several residential properties flooded. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the Pednormead End area were flooded, possibly caused by water backing up upstream of the undersized River Chess culvert beneath Missenden Road. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding affected properties around Pednormead End. [PAG] (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties [PAG] (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,"Pednormead End, Chesham",England,"Residential properties in the Pednormead End area flooded during the incident; Pednormead End is identified as Area A where several residential properties flooded. [PAG] (p8)
