42 properties (p12)",GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13.html,GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13,Lancashire flooding 13 Sep 2016,13 September 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-13-september-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,13,2016-09-13,53.8790402,-2.1717795,"<div id=""html_791563bc3b5b32c127aaf92cc4117dc9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pendle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Earby area of Pendle experienced the most significant impacts of the event and several other locations in the district reported flooding to property during the same period. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall caused Earby Beck to burst its banks, producing significant flash flooding in Earby; police closed roads and firefighters rescued people; properties were internally flooded. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Particularly damaging flooding occurred in Pendle during the extreme rainfall event of 13 September 2016. Impacts associated with the intense rainfall/urban flooding included water ingress at low&ndash;lying properties, vehicles abandoned in flooded roads impeding access, and traffic creating bow waves that washed onto private property. (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties internally flooded; ten people rescued (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Pendle,England,"The Earby area of Pendle experienced the most significant impacts of the event and several other locations in the district reported flooding to property during the same period. (p3)
Intense rainfall caused Earby Beck to burst its banks, producing significant flash flooding in Earby; police closed roads and firefighters rescued people; properties were internally flooded. (p12)
Particularly damaging flooding occurred in Pendle during the extreme rainfall event of 13 September 2016. Impacts associated with the intense rainfall/urban flooding included water ingress at low–lying properties, vehicles abandoned in flooded roads impeding access, and traffic creating bow waves that washed onto private property. (p15)",9 properties internally flooded; ten people rescued (p12),GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13.html,GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13,Lancashire flooding 13 Sep 2016,13 September 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-13-september-2016-flooding.pdf
