GB-LAN,13,2016-09-13,53.7271527,-2.7330066,"<div id=""html_9b272b5faf0895cd8005cd2bc383d7b1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Ribble</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the district were reported flooded during the intense thundery downpours on 13 September 2016 (part of the 42 properties reported across Lancashire). (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>part of 42 properties reported across Lancashire (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,South Ribble,England,Properties in the district were reported flooded during the intense thundery downpours on 13 September 2016 (part of the 42 properties reported across Lancashire). (p12),part of 42 properties reported across Lancashire (p12),GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13.html,GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13,Lancashire flooding 13 Sep 2016,13 September 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-13-september-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,13,2016-09-13,53.89728410091331,-2.903724352506046,"<div id=""html_fc2f1df40f921f7d533c372c9b60275e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wyre</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the district were reported flooded during the intense thundery downpours on 13 September 2016 (part of the 42 properties reported across Lancashire). (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>part of 42 properties reported across Lancashire (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Wyre,England,Properties in the district were reported flooded during the intense thundery downpours on 13 September 2016 (part of the 42 properties reported across Lancashire). (p12),part of 42 properties reported across Lancashire (p12),GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13.html,GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13,Lancashire flooding 13 Sep 2016,13 September 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-13-september-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,13,2016-09-13,54.04133154198799,-2.7654051465975726,"<div id=""html_ba59dac74a906eeb27a5818d61c88653"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancaster District</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Particularly damaging flooding occurred in Lancaster during the extreme rainfall event of 13 September 2016. Impacts associated with the intense rainfall/urban flooding included water ingress at low&ndash;lying properties, vehicles abandoned in flooded roads impeding access, and traffic creating bow waves that washed onto private property. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancaster District,England,"Particularly damaging flooding occurred in Lancaster during the extreme rainfall event of 13 September 2016. Impacts associated with the intense rainfall/urban flooding included water ingress at low–lying properties, vehicles abandoned in flooded roads impeding access, and traffic creating bow waves that washed onto private property. (p15)",,GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13.html,GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13,Lancashire flooding 13 Sep 2016,13 September 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-13-september-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,13,2016-09-13,53.914757,-2.1356368,"<div id=""html_6defb286c76b1019e5ac47b1f4e18103"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Earby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Earby experienced the most significant impacts. Earby Beck burst its banks, flooding the road and leaving silt and debris; blocked gullies and drains led to residents' properties being inundated; roads and footways were inundated and police closed roads. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall caused Earby Beck to burst its banks, producing significant flash flooding in the town. Roads were closed by police. Firefighters rescued people stranded in a restaurant. Local highways crews attended to surcharging gullies, conducted jetting and cleaned roads to enable reopening. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Urban flash&ndash;flooding occurred in Earby village with gullies surcharging; response crews cleared gullies and jetting/clean&ndash;up was required to make the road passable. Firefighters were mobilised to evacuate members of the public and to clear floodwater from affected areas. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported flooding affected homes and public highways in the locality during the event; the LLFA intends to contact Earby to establish a more complete picture of extent and impact. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 150mm (6 inches) of water (inundation reported in properties) (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties; 10 people [PAG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Earby,England,"Earby experienced the most significant impacts. Earby Beck burst its banks, flooding the road and leaving silt and debris; blocked gullies and drains led to residents' properties being inundated; roads and footways were inundated and police closed roads. (p3)
Intense rainfall caused Earby Beck to burst its banks, producing significant flash flooding in the town. Roads were closed by police. Firefighters rescued people stranded in a restaurant. Local highways crews attended to surcharging gullies, conducted jetting and cleaned roads to enable reopening. [PAG] (p12)
Urban flash–flooding occurred in Earby village with gullies surcharging; response crews cleared gullies and jetting/clean–up was required to make the road passable. Firefighters were mobilised to evacuate members of the public and to clear floodwater from affected areas. (p13)
Reported flooding affected homes and public highways in the locality during the event; the LLFA intends to contact Earby to establish a more complete picture of extent and impact. (p14)","up to 150mm (6 inches) of water (inundation reported in properties) (p3)
9 properties; 10 people [PAG] (p12)",GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13.html,GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13,Lancashire flooding 13 Sep 2016,13 September 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-13-september-2016-flooding.pdf
