GB-LAN,13,2016-09-13,53.83634,-2.2116468,"<div id=""html_f4be7e754776ba2e03b04ce76ad90a27"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Nelson</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Firefighters from Nelson were mobilised to evacuate the public and to clear floodwater from affected areas. [PAG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Nelson,England,Firefighters from Nelson were mobilised to evacuate the public and to clear floodwater from affected areas. [PAG] (p13),,GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13.html,GB-LAN_13_2016-09-13,Lancashire flooding 13 Sep 2016,13 September 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-13-september-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-KEN,11,2019-06-10,51.3574884,0.2600065,"<div id=""html_97510ef3aa6e8142764dd856468bda6f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brands Hatch Circuit</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A noise bund at the edge of the Brands Hatch Circuit contributed to creating a topographical low where water became trapped, which exacerbated very deep surface water flooding on Neal Road. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Deep water collected behind the noise bund at Brands Hatch contributed to build&ndash;up and overland flow paths that increased water at local low points, contributing to surface water flooding of properties in West Kingsdown. (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Brands Hatch Circuit,England,"A noise bund at the edge of the Brands Hatch Circuit contributed to creating a topographical low where water became trapped, which exacerbated very deep surface water flooding on Neal Road. (p6)
Deep water collected behind the noise bund at Brands Hatch contributed to build–up and overland flow paths that increased water at local low points, contributing to surface water flooding of properties in West Kingsdown. (p7)",,GB-KEN_11_2019-06-10.html,GB-KEN_11_2019-06-10,West Kingsdown flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: West Kingsdown,063/Kent/Section-19-Flood-Investigation-West-Kingsdown.pdf
GB-KEN,11,2019-06-10,51.3438496,0.2610838,"<div id=""html_6d73ffd5b5e2d4574fa4f51eb143e9e3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ash Tree Close, West Kingsdown</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood water from fields south of the A20 crossed into Ash Tree Close causing internal flooding to multiple properties and structural damage (part of a conservatory wall collapsed). [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland run&ndash;off flowed through Ash Tree Close (originating from fields and the A20 corridor) toward Southfields Road, with run&ndash;off travelling through properties and causing extensive damage where it passed through them. [IMG] (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties internally flooded; 1 conservatory wall collapsed [TAB] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Ash Tree Close, West Kingsdown",England,"Flood water from fields south of the A20 crossed into Ash Tree Close causing internal flooding to multiple properties and structural damage (part of a conservatory wall collapsed). [TAB] (p2)
Overland run–off flowed through Ash Tree Close (originating from fields and the A20 corridor) toward Southfields Road, with run–off travelling through properties and causing extensive damage where it passed through them. [IMG] (p6)",5 properties internally flooded; 1 conservatory wall collapsed [TAB] (p2),GB-KEN_11_2019-06-10.html,GB-KEN_11_2019-06-10,West Kingsdown flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: West Kingsdown,063/Kent/Section-19-Flood-Investigation-West-Kingsdown.pdf
GB-KEN,11,2019-06-10,51.3394857,0.2689976,"<div id=""html_9643a8e2be7293c0d3a0c0e85440ca7c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>London Road, West Kingsdown</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flow of muddy water from adjacent farmland affected the A20 (London Road), flowed along the carriageway and towards nearby residential streets; a commercial property and a residential property on the road were internally flooded. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Muddy greenfield run&ndash;off and overland flows flooded the A20 London Road; the run&ndash;off flowed through Ash Tree Close and towards Southfields Road and caused extensive damage where it travelled through properties along this corridor. [IMG] (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property flooded; 1 commercial property internally flooded [TAB] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"London Road, West Kingsdown",England,"Overland flow of muddy water from adjacent farmland affected the A20 (London Road), flowed along the carriageway and towards nearby residential streets; a commercial property and a residential property on the road were internally flooded. [TAB] (p2)
Muddy greenfield run–off and overland flows flooded the A20 London Road; the run–off flowed through Ash Tree Close and towards Southfields Road and caused extensive damage where it travelled through properties along this corridor. [IMG] (p6)",1 property flooded; 1 commercial property internally flooded [TAB] (p2),GB-KEN_11_2019-06-10.html,GB-KEN_11_2019-06-10,West Kingsdown flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: West Kingsdown,063/Kent/Section-19-Flood-Investigation-West-Kingsdown.pdf
