GB-KEN,11,2019-06-10,51.353817,0.2561847,"<div id=""html_7900477bfc46ccfc19c1bddd5af3cb2c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Neal Road, West Kingsdown</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding affected properties on Neal Road (waist&ndash;high reported in at least one case); one resident required evacuation by KFRS; one other property on the road suffered external flooding. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road flooded early in the event (first report at 20:41) to a depth of 10 inches and later suffered very deep surface water flooding when water was trapped in the topographical low by the noise bund at the edge of the Brands Hatch Circuit. An out&ndash;of&ndash;hours officer attended and closed the road within one hour. Tankers were deployed to assist with controlling trapped flood water. (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties internally flooded; 1 property externally flooded; 1 resident evacuated [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 inches; closed within one hour (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Neal Road, West Kingsdown",England,"Internal flooding affected properties on Neal Road (waist–high reported in at least one case); one resident required evacuation by KFRS; one other property on the road suffered external flooding. [TAB] (p2)
