GB-MIK,1,2018-05-27,52.0212869,-0.731115,"<div id=""html_83e3942fd233f371b6dff536a2f13bb6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Netherfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A surface&ndash;water flood map (with LiDAR) for Netherfield is presented, indicating occurrence/risk of surface water flooding and associated surface&ndash;water impacts in the area. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On the evening of 27 May 2018 significant rainfall caused surface water/urban flooding in Netherfield, resulting in reported inundation of residential properties and local buildings (incidents recorded by Milton Keynes Council). (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple flood incidents were reported in Netherfield, including numerous households experiencing internal flooding. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following the flood event, indicators of flooding were observed in these areas during the site inspection. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the site inspection there were indicators of surface water flooding at a number of properties (notably where garages and door thresholds were below the carriageway and where kerbs were low). [PAG] (p31)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Site inspection and the surface&ndash;water flood map (Figure 13) show surface water accumulation in low&ndash;lying parts of Netherfield. Properties with garages and door thresholds below the carriageway and with low kerbs exhibited indicators of flooding (water reaching thresholds/garages). [IMG] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced an extreme short&ndash;duration rainfall event on 27 May 2018 likely causing surface water flooding in the locality (data point reported for the event). [TAB] (p36)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>49 incidents; 31 properties; 2 unclear [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Return Period 1 in 460 years [TAB] (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Milton Keynes,Netherfield,England,"A surface–water flood map (with LiDAR) for Netherfield is presented, indicating occurrence/risk of surface water flooding and associated surface–water impacts in the area. (p7)
On the evening of 27 May 2018 significant rainfall caused surface water/urban flooding in Netherfield, resulting in reported inundation of residential properties and local buildings (incidents recorded by Milton Keynes Council). (p13)
Multiple flood incidents were reported in Netherfield, including numerous households experiencing internal flooding. [TAB] (p15)
Following the flood event, indicators of flooding were observed in these areas during the site inspection. (p21)
During the site inspection there were indicators of surface water flooding at a number of properties (notably where garages and door thresholds were below the carriageway and where kerbs were low). [PAG] (p31)
Site inspection and the surface–water flood map (Figure 13) show surface water accumulation in low–lying parts of Netherfield. Properties with garages and door thresholds below the carriageway and with low kerbs exhibited indicators of flooding (water reaching thresholds/garages). [IMG] (p32)
Experienced an extreme short–duration rainfall event on 27 May 2018 likely causing surface water flooding in the locality (data point reported for the event). [TAB] (p36)","49 incidents; 31 properties; 2 unclear [TAB] (p15)
Return Period 1 in 460 years [TAB] (p36)",GB-MIK_1_2018-05-27.html,GB-MIK_1_2018-05-27,Milton Keynes Unitary Authority flooding 27 May 2018,FWMA Section 19 Report: Flood Event: May 2018,081/Milton Keynes/081/2018/Milton Keynes/Milton Keynes/10/18.pdf
GB-MIK,1,2018-05-27,52.0174613,-0.7396021,"<div id=""html_e83c0760cfad121698e400cba8d3c376"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Beanhill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On the evening of 27 May 2018 significant rainfall caused surface water/urban flooding in Beanhill, resulting in reported inundation of residential properties and local buildings (incidents recorded by Milton Keynes Council). (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding reported across the estate with multiple incidents; internal flooding affected properties on the estate. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area recorded intense rainfall during 27 May 2018 and the report notes indicators of flooding in locations with similar rainfall, indicating surface water / urban flooding affected the area. [TAB] (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the storm on 27 May 2018 Beanhill experienced surface water flooding. Anglian Water confirmed the local surface water system had root ingress and was subject to planned maintenance; they judged that completion of that maintenance prior to the storm would have had negligible effect on the extent of flooding. (p38)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>106 total incidents; 55 internal flooding; 2 unclear [TAB] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Milton Keynes,Beanhill,England,"On the evening of 27 May 2018 significant rainfall caused surface water/urban flooding in Beanhill, resulting in reported inundation of residential properties and local buildings (incidents recorded by Milton Keynes Council). (p13)
Flooding reported across the estate with multiple incidents; internal flooding affected properties on the estate. [TAB] (p15)
Area recorded intense rainfall during 27 May 2018 and the report notes indicators of flooding in locations with similar rainfall, indicating surface water / urban flooding affected the area. [TAB] (p36)
During the storm on 27 May 2018 Beanhill experienced surface water flooding. Anglian Water confirmed the local surface water system had root ingress and was subject to planned maintenance; they judged that completion of that maintenance prior to the storm would have had negligible effect on the extent of flooding. (p38)",106 total incidents; 55 internal flooding; 2 unclear [TAB] (p15),GB-MIK_1_2018-05-27.html,GB-MIK_1_2018-05-27,Milton Keynes Unitary Authority flooding 27 May 2018,FWMA Section 19 Report: Flood Event: May 2018,081/Milton Keynes/081/2018/Milton Keynes/Milton Keynes/10/18.pdf
GB-MIK,1,2018-05-27,52.0242985,-0.7455273,"<div id=""html_906d41a8c60459a8d17345e7910f4e34"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Coffee Hall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On the evening of 27 May 2018 significant rainfall caused surface water/urban flooding in Coffee Hall, resulting in reported inundation of residential properties and local buildings (incidents recorded by Milton Keynes Council). (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Large number of reported flood incidents on the estate with many households experiencing internal flooding and likely damage to internal contents. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding was noted within roads in Coffee Hall, mainly in the southern half; flood depths increased as surface water flowed west to east. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced an extreme short&ndash;duration rainfall event on 27 May 2018 that is considered very likely to have produced surface water flooding in the area (indicators of flooding were noted in the wider report). [TAB] (p36)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>241 total; 3 unclear if internal or external; 104 internal flooding [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Return Period 1 in 602 years [TAB] (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Milton Keynes,Coffee Hall,England,"On the evening of 27 May 2018 significant rainfall caused surface water/urban flooding in Coffee Hall, resulting in reported inundation of residential properties and local buildings (incidents recorded by Milton Keynes Council). (p13)
Large number of reported flood incidents on the estate with many households experiencing internal flooding and likely damage to internal contents. [TAB] (p15)
Surface water flooding was noted within roads in Coffee Hall, mainly in the southern half; flood depths increased as surface water flowed west to east. (p21)
Experienced an extreme short–duration rainfall event on 27 May 2018 that is considered very likely to have produced surface water flooding in the area (indicators of flooding were noted in the wider report). [TAB] (p36)","241 total; 3 unclear if internal or external; 104 internal flooding [TAB] (p15)
Return Period 1 in 602 years [TAB] (p36)",GB-MIK_1_2018-05-27.html,GB-MIK_1_2018-05-27,Milton Keynes Unitary Authority flooding 27 May 2018,FWMA Section 19 Report: Flood Event: May 2018,081/Milton Keynes/081/2018/Milton Keynes/Milton Keynes/10/18.pdf
GB-MIK,1,2018-05-27,52.0308647,-0.7557316,"<div id=""html_cc90a6814c112a8676a6ac6f4bdba5a6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oldbrook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On the evening of 27 May 2018 significant rainfall caused surface water/urban flooding in Oldbrook, resulting in reported inundation of residential properties and local buildings (incidents recorded by Milton Keynes Council). (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported flood incidents included internal flooding of residential properties in Oldbrook. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following the flood event, indicators of flooding were observed in these areas during the site inspection. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Observed flooding along a historic flow path (now part of the public sewer) with evidence on Larwood Place, Hutton Avenue, Verity Place and Shackleton Place; accumulation at the Hatton Avenue/Shackleton Place roundabout and a burst sewer at Kirkstall Place/Grace Avenue were recorded. (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood mapping (Environment Agency 1% AEP) and LiDAR&ndash;derived flow routing show a significant surface&ndash;water flood extent through low&ndash;lying central and southwestern Oldbrook associated with the burst pipe area; photographic indicators of flooding were recorded in the area. [IMG,PAG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Post&ndash;flood evidence at a residential property: a large pile of water&ndash;damaged household items and bags placed on a driveway in front of the garage, indicating significant interior or garage flooding and removal of damaged possessions during clean&ndash;up. [IMG] (p27)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>71 reported incidents; 1 unclear if internal or external; 25 internal flooding [TAB] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Milton Keynes,Oldbrook,England,"On the evening of 27 May 2018 significant rainfall caused surface water/urban flooding in Oldbrook, resulting in reported inundation of residential properties and local buildings (incidents recorded by Milton Keynes Council). (p13)
Reported flood incidents included internal flooding of residential properties in Oldbrook. [TAB] (p15)
Following the flood event, indicators of flooding were observed in these areas during the site inspection. (p21)
Observed flooding along a historic flow path (now part of the public sewer) with evidence on Larwood Place, Hutton Avenue, Verity Place and Shackleton Place; accumulation at the Hatton Avenue/Shackleton Place roundabout and a burst sewer at Kirkstall Place/Grace Avenue were recorded. (p25)
Flood mapping (Environment Agency 1% AEP) and LiDAR–derived flow routing show a significant surface–water flood extent through low–lying central and southwestern Oldbrook associated with the burst pipe area; photographic indicators of flooding were recorded in the area. [IMG,PAG] (p26)
Post–flood evidence at a residential property: a large pile of water–damaged household items and bags placed on a driveway in front of the garage, indicating significant interior or garage flooding and removal of damaged possessions during clean–up. [IMG] (p27)",71 reported incidents; 1 unclear if internal or external; 25 internal flooding [TAB] (p15),GB-MIK_1_2018-05-27.html,GB-MIK_1_2018-05-27,Milton Keynes Unitary Authority flooding 27 May 2018,FWMA Section 19 Report: Flood Event: May 2018,081/Milton Keynes/081/2018/Milton Keynes/Milton Keynes/10/18.pdf
