GB-DBY,1,2023-10-18,54.7023545,-3.2765753,"<div id=""html_ecd2afb31d8187a0123e3d09c44679fd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>UK</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storm Babet (18&ndash;21 Oct 2023) produced extreme rainfall across the UK, causing widespread river, surface water and drainage&ndash;network (sewer) flooding in multiple regions. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,UK,England,"Storm Babet (18–21 Oct 2023) produced extreme rainfall across the UK, causing widespread river, surface water and drainage–network (sewer) flooding in multiple regions. (p5)",,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-1-introduction-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,1,2023-10-18,53.2718354,-1.377915,"<div id=""html_b347fc775d72a8e8883141dffe9f335a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Rother</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Rother catchment was reported to have experienced higher concentrations of internally flooded properties than catchments to the west of the county, associated with the Storm Babet rainfall and resulting watercourse overtopping. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,River Rother,England,"The Rother catchment was reported to have experienced higher concentrations of internally flooded properties than catchments to the west of the county, associated with the Storm Babet rainfall and resulting watercourse overtopping. (p3)",,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-1-introduction-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,1,2023-10-18,52.995808,-1.3017821,"<div id=""html_46f42cd16de704b388c4b679836e38f5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Erewash</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Erewash catchment experienced higher concentrations of internally flooded properties during the Storm Babet event, driven by higher magnitude rainfall in the east of the county and local population density; watercourse overtopping and surface water were significant causes, with some sewer&ndash;related flooding where pumping stations were overwhelmed. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,River Erewash,England,"The Erewash catchment experienced higher concentrations of internally flooded properties during the Storm Babet event, driven by higher magnitude rainfall in the east of the county and local population density; watercourse overtopping and surface water were significant causes, with some sewer–related flooding where pumping stations were overwhelmed. (p3)",,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-1-introduction-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,1,2023-10-18,53.118504,-1.556618,"<div id=""html_d81d032f30968ebf26b3e22bdaf0bc7c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Derbyshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Between 18 and 21 October 2023 Derbyshire experienced extensive property flooding. Watercourse overtopping was the main cause of property flooding at most communities; surface water flooding was the main cause at some communities and a contributing cause at many; some sewer network flooding occurred where pumping stations were overwhelmed by other sources of flooding. The worst affected communities included Chesterfield, Sandiacre and Long Eaton, with higher concentrations of flooded properties in the Don and Rother, Derwent Lower, and Erewash catchments (east of the county). [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding across the county during Storm Babet. A total of 1,647 properties were internally flooded across all eight districts and boroughs. Infrastructure damage recorded included bridge scouring, damage to an electricity substation, and a footbridge washed away. Several roads became impassable causing local traffic disruption. The borough of Chesterfield (within Derbyshire) was especially badly affected, with one resident killed and a large number of properties flooded. [PAG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread internal flooding of residential properties across the county; communities investigated where five or more residential properties were internally flooded. [PAG] (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1,647 properties internally flooded; 1,251 residential; 396 non&ndash;residential; 35 communities investigated encompassing 1,284 of the internally flooded properties [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1,647 properties; 1 fatality; more than 400 properties (Chesterfield) [PAG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1,647 internally flooded residential properties; 35 communities identified containing five or more flooded properties; 1,284 of the flooded properties are within the investigated communities [PAG] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Derbyshire,England,"Between 18 and 21 October 2023 Derbyshire experienced extensive property flooding. Watercourse overtopping was the main cause of property flooding at most communities; surface water flooding was the main cause at some communities and a contributing cause at many; some sewer network flooding occurred where pumping stations were overwhelmed by other sources of flooding. The worst affected communities included Chesterfield, Sandiacre and Long Eaton, with higher concentrations of flooded properties in the Don and Rother, Derwent Lower, and Erewash catchments (east of the county). [PAG] (p3)
Widespread flooding across the county during Storm Babet. A total of 1,647 properties were internally flooded across all eight districts and boroughs. Infrastructure damage recorded included bridge scouring, damage to an electricity substation, and a footbridge washed away. Several roads became impassable causing local traffic disruption. The borough of Chesterfield (within Derbyshire) was especially badly affected, with one resident killed and a large number of properties flooded. [PAG] (p5)
Widespread internal flooding of residential properties across the county; communities investigated where five or more residential properties were internally flooded. [PAG] (p6)","1,647 properties internally flooded; 1,251 residential; 396 non–residential; 35 communities investigated encompassing 1,284 of the internally flooded properties [PAG] (p3)
1,647 properties; 1 fatality; more than 400 properties (Chesterfield) [PAG] (p5)
1,647 internally flooded residential properties; 35 communities identified containing five or more flooded properties; 1,284 of the flooded properties are within the investigated communities [PAG] (p6)",GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-1-introduction-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,1,2023-10-18,53.9825271,-1.3852499932684972,"<div id=""html_c86cd7d9354c98e6724f92c46246459c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Yorkshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding was observed in parts of Yorkshire during Storm Babet, driven by exceptional rainfall and elevated watercourses. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Yorkshire,England,"Significant flooding was observed in parts of Yorkshire during Storm Babet, driven by exceptional rainfall and elevated watercourses. (p5)",,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-1-introduction-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,1,2023-10-18,53.145927,-1.0214971,"<div id=""html_21e3a1aa46e260102487495eb4194ca6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Nottinghamshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Nottinghamshire experienced significant flooding associated with Storm Babet as intense rainfall fell on already saturated ground, causing river, surface&ndash;water and drainage&ndash;related flooding in parts of the county. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Nottinghamshire,England,"Nottinghamshire experienced significant flooding associated with Storm Babet as intense rainfall fell on already saturated ground, causing river, surface–water and drainage–related flooding in parts of the county. (p5)",,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-1-introduction-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,1,2023-10-18,52.8246942,-2.0074547,"<div id=""html_610b77d7ee780aa5353cb64fe9b0c438"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Staffordshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Staffordshire experienced significant flooding during Storm Babet due to exceptional rainfall on saturated ground, producing river and surface&ndash;water flooding impacts. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Staffordshire,England,"Parts of Staffordshire experienced significant flooding during Storm Babet due to exceptional rainfall on saturated ground, producing river and surface–water flooding impacts. (p5)",,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-1-introduction-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,1,2023-10-18,52.241001350000005,1.0466830312565236,"<div id=""html_354c590fde9eec499f7d9ddd5cd4acae"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Suffolk</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Suffolk was among the areas reported to have significant flooding associated with Storm Babet between 18&ndash;21 October 2023. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Suffolk,England,Suffolk was among the areas reported to have significant flooding associated with Storm Babet between 18–21 October 2023. (p5),,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-1-introduction-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,1,2023-10-18,52.53102,-1.2649062,"<div id=""html_2dc0f66a6e2bb232fb53db269d95f982"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>England</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding occurred across multiple counties in England during 18&ndash;21 Oct 2023, driven by exceptional rainfall on already saturated ground and manifesting as river, surface water and drainage&ndash;network flooding. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,England,England,"Significant flooding occurred across multiple counties in England during 18–21 Oct 2023, driven by exceptional rainfall on already saturated ground and manifesting as river, surface water and drainage–network flooding. (p5)",,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_1_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-1-introduction-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,1,2023-10-18,53.25,-1.41667,"<div id=""html_ac9ea41079e0612428eff7b3ee8e4dbb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Community was among the worst&ndash;impacted in Derbyshire during Storm Babet with internal property flooding reported. Flooding was associated with watercourse overtopping (the main cause at most communities) with surface&ndash;water flooding a contributing or primary cause in some areas. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During 18&ndash;21 Oct 2023 Chesterfield experienced severe flooding impacts: one resident died and more than 400 properties were internally flooded. (p5)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 fatality; more than 400 properties (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Chesterfield,England,"Community was among the worst–impacted in Derbyshire during Storm Babet with internal property flooding reported. Flooding was associated with watercourse overtopping (the main cause at most communities) with surface–water flooding a contributing or primary cause in some areas. (p3)
