GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.1260806,0.2578267,"<div id=""html_57c6b8d8d75f65b9b041da1897123feb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pantiles</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Commercial premises experienced internal flooding. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified on Figure 1 and the map as one of the locations affected by the 2017 flood events. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall exceeded the drainage system and culverted River Grom, causing surface water flooding across the Pantiles area and inundating properties and businesses. (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 commercial properties [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 residential properties; 17 businesses (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Pantiles,England,"Commercial premises experienced internal flooding. [TAB] (p7)
Identified on Figure 1 and the map as one of the locations affected by the 2017 flood events. [IMG] (p8)
Intense rainfall exceeded the drainage system and culverted River Grom, causing surface water flooding across the Pantiles area and inundating properties and businesses. (p17)","17 commercial properties [TAB] (p7)
18 residential properties; 17 businesses (p17)",GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.13489597839591,0.2664838857043647,"<div id=""html_0c32e00f93d5ff77aaf1e6d22dd5b213"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Royal Victoria Place</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Royal Victoria Place shopping area was affected by flooding during the 19 July 2017 event. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred during the intense rainfall when highway gullies and the combined sewer system were overwhelmed and likely overflowed. Flooding was reported between 02:21 and 04:12 and affected properties within the shopping&ndash;centre area. [PAG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall exceeded the capacity of drainage and the combined sewer serving Royal Victoria Place, causing the sewer system to be exceeded and overflow in the area around the centre. [PAG] (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 basement flat property; 1 commercial property (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties; 11 residential properties; 4 commercial properties [PAG] (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Royal Victoria Place,England,"The Royal Victoria Place shopping area was affected by flooding during the 19 July 2017 event. [TAB] (p7)
Flooding occurred during the intense rainfall when highway gullies and the combined sewer system were overwhelmed and likely overflowed. Flooding was reported between 02:21 and 04:12 and affected properties within the shopping–centre area. [PAG] (p20)
Intense rainfall exceeded the capacity of drainage and the combined sewer serving Royal Victoria Place, causing the sewer system to be exceeded and overflow in the area around the centre. [PAG] (p21)","1 basement flat property; 1 commercial property (p7)
15 properties; 11 residential properties; 4 commercial properties [PAG] (p20)",GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.116978,0.1621546,"<div id=""html_9d0205efc5ff076d29a80141a1a8c21b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Grom</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Grom overflowed at the culvert entrance near Rodmell Road during the heavy rainfall, inundating gardens on the north&ndash;eastern side of Warwick Park and causing internal flooding to a property; culvert entrance arrangements may have impeded flow and contributed to the flooding. (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culverted River Grom was likely overwhelmed by excessive rainfall, contributing to local flooding; the culvert entrance arrangement (largely closed with a small opening and lower entrance chamber) is likely to impede inflow and may lead to flooding of gardens at Warwick Park. A CCTV inspection found only minor deposits and a root mass but no major defects. [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>KCC replaced the previous vertical trash screens at the River Grom entrance with a single raked trash screen to allow safer and more effective clearing of debris during higher flows; the River Grom culvert was subject to CCTV inspection to assess for damage, defects and blockages after the 2017 flood. [PAG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Grom reached peak flows and overflowed at the entrance to the culvert system, contributing to flooding adjacent to properties as surface water drainage discharged into the watercourse. [PAG] (p28)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,River Grom,England,"The River Grom overflowed at the culvert entrance near Rodmell Road during the heavy rainfall, inundating gardens on the north–eastern side of Warwick Park and causing internal flooding to a property; culvert entrance arrangements may have impeded flow and contributed to the flooding. (p17)
The culverted River Grom was likely overwhelmed by excessive rainfall, contributing to local flooding; the culvert entrance arrangement (largely closed with a small opening and lower entrance chamber) is likely to impede inflow and may lead to flooding of gardens at Warwick Park. A CCTV inspection found only minor deposits and a root mass but no major defects. [PAG] (p19)
KCC replaced the previous vertical trash screens at the River Grom entrance with a single raked trash screen to allow safer and more effective clearing of debris during higher flows; the River Grom culvert was subject to CCTV inspection to assess for damage, defects and blockages after the 2017 flood. [PAG] (p26)
The River Grom reached peak flows and overflowed at the entrance to the culvert system, contributing to flooding adjacent to properties as surface water drainage discharged into the watercourse. [PAG] (p28)",one property (p17),GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.1320123,0.2708909,"<div id=""html_cfeb8a39a8ce9a1e755b7fe178b7dcb3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Calverley Road, Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding occurred to a basement flat and to a commercial property during the 19 July 2017 event. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Marked in the report map (Figure 1) as a location of flooding in 2017 (appears twice on the map); the road was flooded during the 19 July 2017 event and identified as affected by surface water flooding. [IMG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Calverley Road is listed within the Royal Victoria Place area where intensive rainfall on 19th July 2017 overwhelmed highway gullies and the combined sewer system, contributing to surface water entering properties in the area. (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 basement flat property; 1 commercial property [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties affected in the area (approximately 11 residential, 4 commercial) (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Calverley Road, Tunbridge Wells",England,"Internal flooding occurred to a basement flat and to a commercial property during the 19 July 2017 event. [TAB] (p7)
Marked in the report map (Figure 1) as a location of flooding in 2017 (appears twice on the map); the road was flooded during the 19 July 2017 event and identified as affected by surface water flooding. [IMG] (p9)
Calverley Road is listed within the Royal Victoria Place area where intensive rainfall on 19th July 2017 overwhelmed highway gullies and the combined sewer system, contributing to surface water entering properties in the area. (p20)","1 basement flat property; 1 commercial property [TAB] (p7)
15 properties affected in the area (approximately 11 residential, 4 commercial) (p20)",GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
