GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.1262777,0.2573881,"<div id=""html_f3b851b6893122f43fcf45e4df7ca11d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>London Road, Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Named on map/listing of main areas affected by the 2017 floods (19 July 2017). The location experienced localised flooding with properties inundated during the event; KFRS attended to pump properties and assist residents. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported on the highway; Kent Police reported the incident to KCC and an officer found that the water had cleared by the time of attendance. Three blocked drains on Castle Street and the High Street were identified, cleansed and audited following the event. [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water accumulated on the highway because drainage capacity was exceeded; water was present on the highway but had cleared by 03:54 am on the day of the event. (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"London Road, Tunbridge Wells",England,"Named on map/listing of main areas affected by the 2017 floods (19 July 2017). The location experienced localised flooding with properties inundated during the event; KFRS attended to pump properties and assist residents. [IMG] (p8)
Flooding was reported on the highway; Kent Police reported the incident to KCC and an officer found that the water had cleared by the time of attendance. Three blocked drains on Castle Street and the High Street were identified, cleansed and audited following the event. [PAG] (p19)
Surface water accumulated on the highway because drainage capacity was exceeded; water was present on the highway but had cleared by 03:54 am on the day of the event. (p20)",,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.1280587,0.2609699,"<div id=""html_83671770c74773703b827c16daef6afc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Castle Street, Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed alongside London Road as a main area affected by the 2017 flooding (19 July 2017); experienced localised inundation of properties during the event and attended by fire crews. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported on the highway; three blocked drains on Castle Street and the High Street were identified and subsequently cleansed and audited. [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Blocked highway drains were reported on Castle Street associated with the surface water event; drains were cleansed and audited following the event. (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Castle Street, Tunbridge Wells",England,"Listed alongside London Road as a main area affected by the 2017 flooding (19 July 2017); experienced localised inundation of properties during the event and attended by fire crews. [IMG] (p8)
Flooding was reported on the highway; three blocked drains on Castle Street and the High Street were identified and subsequently cleansed and audited. [PAG] (p19)
Blocked highway drains were reported on Castle Street associated with the surface water event; drains were cleansed and audited following the event. (p20)",,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.1233932,0.2666719,"<div id=""html_f3456054262e5a27aef532af07bf6730"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Upper Cumberland Walk, Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included (as Upper Cumberland/Upper Cumberland Walk) among the locations highlighted as affected in the 2017 floods (19 July 2017); experienced localised inundation and was part of the areas where emergency pumping and assistance occurred. [IMG] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Upper Cumberland Walk, Tunbridge Wells",England,Included (as Upper Cumberland/Upper Cumberland Walk) among the locations highlighted as affected in the 2017 floods (19 July 2017); experienced localised inundation and was part of the areas where emergency pumping and assistance occurred. [IMG] (p8),,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.1276435,0.2608956,"<div id=""html_831e04c3bc5567e29de4641430f94467"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Blocked highway drains were reported on the High Street in association with the surface water event; these were cleansed and audited after the event. (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"High Street, Tunbridge Wells",England,Blocked highway drains were reported on the High Street in association with the surface water event; these were cleansed and audited after the event. (p20),,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.1367415,0.268207,"<div id=""html_8541a70ca2e769568820cc7268ef6062"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kirkdale Road, Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Manholes in Kirkdale Road surcharged and released sewer water that flowed towards Jackwood Way. (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Kirkdale Road, Tunbridge Wells",England,Manholes in Kirkdale Road surcharged and released sewer water that flowed towards Jackwood Way. (p21),,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.13772,0.2693431,"<div id=""html_e26a59f16e59158b56e748ba0bb93b4d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Commercial Road, Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Manholes in Commercial Road surcharged and discharged sewer water that flowed towards Jackwood Way. (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Commercial Road, Tunbridge Wells",England,Manholes in Commercial Road surcharged and discharged sewer water that flowed towards Jackwood Way. (p21),,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.1371483,0.2673446,"<div id=""html_24be4ce2fc96f8d34032bb98c5fcefa4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected the Tunbridge Wells area (report subject). [PAG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extensive highway flooding and inundation of properties across parts of the town. [PAG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding reported across the town on 19 July 2017; many of the areas flooded in July 2017 had also been affected by flooding on 24 August 2015. [PAG,MUL] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding across the town on 19 July 2017 affected multiple residential and commercial properties; emergency services (KFRS) attended and pumped properties and provided humanitarian assistance; water had receded by 04:30. [PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple locations across Tunbridge Wells experienced flooding in 2017; properties were inundated (reports of over 1 metre of water in some properties) and emergency services received over 60 calls and carried out pumping and assistance. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense, short&ndash;duration rainfall on 19 July 2017 caused flash/surface&ndash;water flooding across Tunbridge Wells, producing urban flooding in shopping and residential areas (figures show locations of flooding in Royal Victoria Place and High Brooms). [IMG,PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from surrounding hills and roads converged in the central area (The Pantiles / Nevill Street / Warwick Park low point ~80.3mAOD). Converging flow routes and limited ability for water to flow away, combined with a small local pump serving basements, increased loads on drainage and the pump and led to surface water and sewer&ndash;related flooding in the central area, including flooding of basements and water on highways during the 19 July 2017 event. [IMG] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Excessive rainfall exceeded drainage capacity across the area, overwhelming systems and causing surface water to accumulate in low points and combined sewers to surcharge into properties (including areas such as Mount Pleasant Road, Castle Street and Warwick Park). (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 19th July 2017 excessive/intensive rainfall exceeded the capacity of the town's drainage and combined sewer systems. Surface water accumulated in topographic low points and entered properties; parts of the town (including London Road, Castle Street and the Royal Victoria Place area) experienced overwhelmed gullies/combined sewers and blocked drains. Kent County Council attended (water had cleared from some highways by 03:54) and drains were cleansed and audited following the event. (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following the 19 July 2017 flood event, KCC undertook drainage cleansing on roads in Tunbridge Wells that were affected by flooding; a resident flood action group was formed (facilitated by the National Flood Forum) to address local flood issues; natural flood management measures were delivered in local green spaces (Hilbert Woods and Grosvenor Park) to reduce peak flows. (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall exceeded drainage design standards so surface water could not enter drainage networks quickly enough; drainage capacity was exceeded and floodwaters flowed to local low points causing flooding across the town and to properties. [PAG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding formed on Nevill Street due to rapid overland flow from the Common; overland flow discharged onto surrounding roads and posed risk to downstream properties. [PAG] (p29)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 60 calls; over 1 metre of water within some properties [PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 60 calls; over 1 metre of water within some properties; 3 fire engines [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 commercial properties; 3 blocked drains (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 blocked drains; 15 properties affected (approximately 11 residential, 4 commercial) (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Tunbridge Wells,England,"Flooding affected the Tunbridge Wells area (report subject). [PAG] (p1)
Extensive highway flooding and inundation of properties across parts of the town. [PAG] (p5)
Widespread flooding reported across the town on 19 July 2017; many of the areas flooded in July 2017 had also been affected by flooding on 24 August 2015. [PAG,MUL] (p6)
Widespread flooding across the town on 19 July 2017 affected multiple residential and commercial properties; emergency services (KFRS) attended and pumped properties and provided humanitarian assistance; water had receded by 04:30. [PAG] (p7)
Multiple locations across Tunbridge Wells experienced flooding in 2017; properties were inundated (reports of over 1 metre of water in some properties) and emergency services received over 60 calls and carried out pumping and assistance. [IMG] (p8)
Intense, short–duration rainfall on 19 July 2017 caused flash/surface–water flooding across Tunbridge Wells, producing urban flooding in shopping and residential areas (figures show locations of flooding in Royal Victoria Place and High Brooms). [IMG,PAG] (p10)
Surface water from surrounding hills and roads converged in the central area (The Pantiles / Nevill Street / Warwick Park low point ~80.3mAOD). Converging flow routes and limited ability for water to flow away, combined with a small local pump serving basements, increased loads on drainage and the pump and led to surface water and sewer–related flooding in the central area, including flooding of basements and water on highways during the 19 July 2017 event. [IMG] (p18)
Excessive rainfall exceeded drainage capacity across the area, overwhelming systems and causing surface water to accumulate in low points and combined sewers to surcharge into properties (including areas such as Mount Pleasant Road, Castle Street and Warwick Park). (p19)
On 19th July 2017 excessive/intensive rainfall exceeded the capacity of the town's drainage and combined sewer systems. Surface water accumulated in topographic low points and entered properties; parts of the town (including London Road, Castle Street and the Royal Victoria Place area) experienced overwhelmed gullies/combined sewers and blocked drains. Kent County Council attended (water had cleared from some highways by 03:54) and drains were cleansed and audited following the event. (p20)
Following the 19 July 2017 flood event, KCC undertook drainage cleansing on roads in Tunbridge Wells that were affected by flooding; a resident flood action group was formed (facilitated by the National Flood Forum) to address local flood issues; natural flood management measures were delivered in local green spaces (Hilbert Woods and Grosvenor Park) to reduce peak flows. (p26)
Intense rainfall exceeded drainage design standards so surface water could not enter drainage networks quickly enough; drainage capacity was exceeded and floodwaters flowed to local low points causing flooding across the town and to properties. [PAG] (p28)
Surface water flooding formed on Nevill Street due to rapid overland flow from the Common; overland flow discharged onto surrounding roads and posed risk to downstream properties. [PAG] (p29)","over 60 calls; over 1 metre of water within some properties [PAG] (p7)
over 60 calls; over 1 metre of water within some properties; 3 fire engines [IMG] (p8)
2 commercial properties; 3 blocked drains (p19)
3 blocked drains; 15 properties affected (approximately 11 residential, 4 commercial) (p20)",GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19.html,GB-KEN_19_2017-07-19,Tunbridge Wells flooding 19 Jul 2017,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area on 19 July 2017,063/Kent/Tunbridge-Wells-Section-19-report.pdf
GB-KEN,19,2017-07-19,51.14958039738272,0.2733030786084968,"<div id=""html_0c37a04e681cc05ccf5ee1797ef4ff17"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Brooms</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple streets within the High Brooms area experienced flooding, affecting numerous residential properties across the area. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area within the catchment experienced flooding when the Southborough Stream overtopped, resulting in residential properties in the High Brooms area being flooded. (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>14 properties; 6 residential properties; 2 residential properties [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>20 residential properties (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,High Brooms,England,"Multiple streets within the High Brooms area experienced flooding, affecting numerous residential properties across the area. [TAB] (p7)
