one location (included among the nine locations examined that reached Merton's Section 19 threshold) (p82)",GB-MRT_2_2016-06-23_etc.html,GB-MRT_2_2016-06-23_etc,"London Borough of Merton flooding 23 Jun 2016, London Borough of Merton flooding 29 Jul 2017 - 30 Jul 2017 and London Borough of Merton flooding 09 Aug 2017",Section 19: Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3/final.pdf
GB-MRT,2,2016-06-23,51.3901736,-0.2263873,"<div id=""html_144f987b3e417259abebaf1edeaed6f2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lower Morden Lane, Lower Morden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sewer flooding recorded on Lower Malden Lane (sic) as measured by the nearest TWUL sewer gauge. Estimated maximum storm return periods recorded: 1 in 30 year (June 2016), 1 in 2 year (July 2017), 1 in 4 year (August 2017). [TAB,MUL] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was constrained to the highway only; no properties were affected. TWUL reported the adjacent surface water sewer network was completely blocked with silt and tree root ingress, preventing runoff discharging to the East Pyl Brook and increasing local runoff. [MUL] (p78)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>0 properties affected [MUL] (p78)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Lower Morden Lane, Lower Morden",England,"Sewer flooding recorded on Lower Malden Lane (sic) as measured by the nearest TWUL sewer gauge. Estimated maximum storm return periods recorded: 1 in 30 year (June 2016), 1 in 2 year (July 2017), 1 in 4 year (August 2017). [TAB,MUL] (p21)
