GB-DBY,8,2023-10-18,53.3273166,-1.7411554,"<div id=""html_51e8517ec6f76288346024af09f7c007"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bradwell</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in Bradwell prompted investigation of the condition of highway culverts through the village to assess flood risk. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Bradwell,England,Flooding in Bradwell prompted investigation of the condition of highway culverts through the village to assess flood risk. (p5),,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-8-post-event-response-and-recovery-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,8,2023-10-18,53.25,-1.41667,"<div id=""html_bf065e364ad3a0c2bf0a45f8db9cc8e5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Central Chesterfield was identified as being at risk from high flows entering the River Rother / Spital Brook and from Holme Brook and River Hipper; RMAs are seeking upstream flood storage sites (Spital Brook catchment, Holme Brook including Linacre Reservoir, and River Hipper) to slow flows and reduce flood risk to downstream communities in Chesterfield. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Chesterfield,England,"Central Chesterfield was identified as being at risk from high flows entering the River Rother / Spital Brook and from Holme Brook and River Hipper; RMAs are seeking upstream flood storage sites (Spital Brook catchment, Holme Brook including Linacre Reservoir, and River Hipper) to slow flows and reduce flood risk to downstream communities in Chesterfield. (p5)",,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-8-post-event-response-and-recovery-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,8,2023-10-18,53.2746354,-1.2685349,"<div id=""html_35e17759e5970fb0268f309cde6ec57f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clowne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Derbyshire County Council liaised with riparian landowners and Bolsover District Council to remove restrictions and improve capacity in an unnamed watercourse adjacent to properties on Station Road; after this, the Highways Team planned to clear blockages in the twin culvert beneath Creswell Road to alleviate flooding. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Clowne,England,"Derbyshire County Council liaised with riparian landowners and Bolsover District Council to remove restrictions and improve capacity in an unnamed watercourse adjacent to properties on Station Road; after this, the Highways Team planned to clear blockages in the twin culvert beneath Creswell Road to alleviate flooding. (p6)",,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-8-post-event-response-and-recovery-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,8,2023-10-18,52.89521917269419,-1.3439244894064815,"<div id=""html_93438a5a19538ddc283148c3dac5e12e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Draycott</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Derbyshire County Council is investigating surface water drainage systems and the condition of ordinary watercourses in the community to identify maintenance needs to mitigate flooding. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Draycott,England,Derbyshire County Council is investigating surface water drainage systems and the condition of ordinary watercourses in the community to identify maintenance needs to mitigate flooding. (p6),,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-8-post-event-response-and-recovery-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,8,2023-10-18,53.0206084,-1.3356727,"<div id=""html_21e49f74883cb00ee3941bb9ba416b39"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Langley Mill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drainage issues at Deans Street in Langley Mill led to local flooding concerns; Severn Trent have been made aware and are investigating the drainage problems. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Langley Mill,England,Drainage issues at Deans Street in Langley Mill led to local flooding concerns; Severn Trent have been made aware and are investigating the drainage problems. (p6),,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-8-post-event-response-and-recovery-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,8,2023-10-18,52.8613422,-1.3840477,"<div id=""html_319a8d1db1aca445c021e98db5199364"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Aston-On-Trent</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Investigations by Derbyshire County Council into flooding mechanisms from ordinary watercourses to identify maintenance needs following flood incidents. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Aston-On-Trent,England,Investigations by Derbyshire County Council into flooding mechanisms from ordinary watercourses to identify maintenance needs following flood incidents. (p6),,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_8_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-8-post-event-response-and-recovery-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-BNS,1,2019-11-07,53.52779609477775,-1.3791851445967933,"<div id=""html_bedaec4a97e30300a3d481c0f4c49494"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wombwell Ings Caravan Site</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in a flood warning for the River Dove (issued 7 Nov 2019) and lies within Low Valley, which was identified as one of the two main areas impacted by flooding during the event. The inclusion in the warning indicates the caravan site was at risk from river flooding during the heavy rainfall on 7 November 2019 and formed part of the area subject to the local flood response. (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Barnsley,Wombwell Ings Caravan Site,England,"Included in a flood warning for the River Dove (issued 7 Nov 2019) and lies within Low Valley, which was identified as one of the two main areas impacted by flooding during the event. The inclusion in the warning indicates the caravan site was at risk from river flooding during the heavy rainfall on 7 November 2019 and formed part of the area subject to the local flood response. (p4)",,GB-BNS_1_2019-11-07.html,GB-BNS_1_2019-11-07,Barnsley flooding 07 Nov 2019 - 08 Nov 2019,Flood and Water Management Act 2010: Section 19 Statutory Report: Investigation of Flooding Event in Barnsley on 7th and 8th November 2019,003/Barnsley/003/2021/Barnsley/Barnsley/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BNS,1,2019-11-07,53.5527719,-1.4827755,"<div id=""html_e0edc5afd85d549f1166ddab5570a4cc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Barnsley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 7 November 2019 heavy rainfall caused elevated river depths and widespread highway drainage/surface water issues. Flood warnings were issued for the River Dearne and River Dove, resulting in road closures, tactical sandbagging and identification of two main areas (Low Valley and Burton Grange) as being impacted. (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Barnsley,Barnsley,England,"On 7 November 2019 heavy rainfall caused elevated river depths and widespread highway drainage/surface water issues. Flood warnings were issued for the River Dearne and River Dove, resulting in road closures, tactical sandbagging and identification of two main areas (Low Valley and Burton Grange) as being impacted. (p4)",,GB-BNS_1_2019-11-07.html,GB-BNS_1_2019-11-07,Barnsley flooding 07 Nov 2019 - 08 Nov 2019,Flood and Water Management Act 2010: Section 19 Statutory Report: Investigation of Flooding Event in Barnsley on 7th and 8th November 2019,003/Barnsley/003/2021/Barnsley/Barnsley/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BNS,1,2019-11-07,53.52277,-1.1335312,"<div id=""html_6ee797c3077107d42204970bc7b5a632"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Doncaster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as area where the worst flooding impacts were seen; Barnsley Council provided multi&ndash;service mutual aid to Doncaster MBC during the incident. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Barnsley,Doncaster,England,Identified as area where the worst flooding impacts were seen; Barnsley Council provided multi–service mutual aid to Doncaster MBC during the incident. (p5),,GB-BNS_1_2019-11-07.html,GB-BNS_1_2019-11-07,Barnsley flooding 07 Nov 2019 - 08 Nov 2019,Flood and Water Management Act 2010: Section 19 Statutory Report: Investigation of Flooding Event in Barnsley on 7th and 8th November 2019,003/Barnsley/003/2021/Barnsley/Barnsley/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BNS,1,2019-11-07,53.5603,-1.4714344,"<div id=""html_9e5af6e151966e6e969a8434317fbee5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Dearne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall on the Dearne catchment increased runoff and contributed to watercourses and drainage systems becoming overwhelmed, leading to flooding of properties and roads in the borough. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Barnsley,River Dearne,England,"Heavy rainfall on the Dearne catchment increased runoff and contributed to watercourses and drainage systems becoming overwhelmed, leading to flooding of properties and roads in the borough. (p6)",,GB-BNS_1_2019-11-07.html,GB-BNS_1_2019-11-07,Barnsley flooding 07 Nov 2019 - 08 Nov 2019,Flood and Water Management Act 2010: Section 19 Statutory Report: Investigation of Flooding Event in Barnsley on 7th and 8th November 2019,003/Barnsley/003/2021/Barnsley/Barnsley/Oct/2021.pdf
