GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.30153,-0.695107,"<div id=""html_6bd8cc252238356cf262bf9bf1251f69"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Silver Street, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding affected properties on/around Silver Street as part of the single flood incident at Sheep Street / Silver Street. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties on Silver Street as part of the single flood incident; water entered buildings (crossed thresholds) causing internal flooding. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding affecting property on Silver Street caused by blocked drainage. [TAB,MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water rushed down Silver Street like a river, moving wheelie bins, temporary pedestrian barriers and areas of temporary asphalt and making the street dangerous for pedestrians. Floodwater entered ground&ndash;floor shop premises (under front doors and via letterboxes), contaminating floors with litter and debris and washing rats out of sewers. Businesses cleared stock/water and used a VAX&ndash;type floor cleaner; at least one premises lost electricity for approximately 24 hours due to wiring at floor level. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The strong flow continued southwest to Silver Street, affecting properties on both sides. Properties experienced internal flooding from flows and from water pooling to the rear where there was no drainage path; large debris (wheelie bins, barriers) was carried by the water, posing danger to pedestrians and affecting vehicles. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowed to the rear of properties on the east side of Silver Street with no means to drain away. Water increased in depth behind buildings and flowed under doors and through other voids, causing internal flooding of rear areas and properties. [PAG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed along Silver Street, leaving the road wet and displacing street infrastructure (temporary pedestrian barriers and sections of asphalt), disrupting pedestrian access and affecting shopfront frontage. [IMG,PAG] (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Temporary pedestrian barriers and sections of asphalt were moved/displaced by flood water on Silver Street. [IMG,PAG] (p37)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than five buildings (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than five buildings (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10&ndash;20 mm depth; 25 mm depth; 200 mm depth throughout ground floor; lost electricity for approx. 24 hours [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Silver Street, Wellingborough",England,"Internal flooding affected properties on/around Silver Street as part of the single flood incident at Sheep Street / Silver Street. (p5)
Internal flooding of properties on Silver Street as part of the single flood incident; water entered buildings (crossed thresholds) causing internal flooding. (p8)
External flooding affecting property on Silver Street caused by blocked drainage. [TAB,MUL] (p11)
Surface water rushed down Silver Street like a river, moving wheelie bins, temporary pedestrian barriers and areas of temporary asphalt and making the street dangerous for pedestrians. Floodwater entered ground–floor shop premises (under front doors and via letterboxes), contaminating floors with litter and debris and washing rats out of sewers. Businesses cleared stock/water and used a VAX–type floor cleaner; at least one premises lost electricity for approximately 24 hours due to wiring at floor level. [TAB] (p17)
The strong flow continued southwest to Silver Street, affecting properties on both sides. Properties experienced internal flooding from flows and from water pooling to the rear where there was no drainage path; large debris (wheelie bins, barriers) was carried by the water, posing danger to pedestrians and affecting vehicles. (p19)
Surface water flowed to the rear of properties on the east side of Silver Street with no means to drain away. Water increased in depth behind buildings and flowed under doors and through other voids, causing internal flooding of rear areas and properties. [PAG] (p20)
Floodwater flowed along Silver Street, leaving the road wet and displacing street infrastructure (temporary pedestrian barriers and sections of asphalt), disrupting pedestrian access and affecting shopfront frontage. [IMG,PAG] (p36)
Temporary pedestrian barriers and sections of asphalt were moved/displaced by flood water on Silver Street. [IMG,PAG] (p37)","more than five buildings (p5)
more than five buildings (p8)
10–20 mm depth; 25 mm depth; 200 mm depth throughout ground floor; lost electricity for approx. 24 hours [TAB] (p17)
1 property (p19)",GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.30069,-0.6859694,"<div id=""html_38caac502218aa5c4e0c9a5515bba2ce"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Castle Street, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Castle Street experienced flooding during the incident; occupiers were visited by the investigating officer and flood report forms were hand&ndash;delivered to properties to record internal flooding and discuss impacts. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Castle Street were flooded by overland surface water flow during the event; Swanspool Brook remained in&ndash;channel and was not a contributing factor. (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Castle Street, Wellingborough",England,"Properties on Castle Street experienced flooding during the incident; occupiers were visited by the investigating officer and flood report forms were hand–delivered to properties to record internal flooding and discuss impacts. (p8)
Properties on Castle Street were flooded by overland surface water flow during the event; Swanspool Brook remained in–channel and was not a contributing factor. (p14)",,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.3009948,-0.684621,"<div id=""html_75b6cbb4253079795d125fa4eed56ec3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fields View, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Fields View were in the vicinity of known flooding; DSA hand&ndash;delivered flood report forms to record flooding impacts and occupiers were visited to discuss the flooding. (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Fields View, Wellingborough",England,Properties on Fields View were in the vicinity of known flooding; DSA hand–delivered flood report forms to record flooding impacts and occupiers were visited to discuss the flooding. (p8),,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.3029656,-0.6935226,"<div id=""html_86c229dc0988a2c53a579b61c88610bc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church Street, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a property on Church Street due to blocked drainage. [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported as a source of significant surface&ndash;water flow that ran down into Silver Street and contributed to flooding of shop frontages and ground&ndash;floor areas in the town centre. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Church Street experienced internal flooding from both the rear (linked to Queens Lane) and the front. Deep water and a fast, powerful destructive flow from High Street/Church Street moved directly towards front doors, causing damage to building exteriors (for example mortar loss). (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Church Street, Wellingborough",England,"Internal flooding of a property on Church Street due to blocked drainage. [TAB] (p11)
Reported as a source of significant surface–water flow that ran down into Silver Street and contributed to flooding of shop frontages and ground–floor areas in the town centre. [TAB] (p17)
Properties on Church Street experienced internal flooding from both the rear (linked to Queens Lane) and the front. Deep water and a fast, powerful destructive flow from High Street/Church Street moved directly towards front doors, causing damage to building exteriors (for example mortar loss). (p19)",2 properties (p19),GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.30345,-0.6979148,"<div id=""html_acc06c15a03438a1f2229f4c4e6731e6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported as conveying surface&ndash;water runoff down into adjoining streets (including Silver Street and Sheep Street), contributing to flooding of properties in the town centre. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water ran down High Street into Sheep Street, contributing to flows and localised flooding along the route. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flows from High Street combined with Church Street to form a powerful, damaging flow at the junction; at least one property had a flooded basement, low wall to a sunken frontage was overtopped, and multiple properties sustained external damage and possible internal flooding from the destructive flow. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Powerful flow of surface water caused damage to brick mortar on the street's buildings (reported for High Street). [IMG,PAG] (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Powerful surface water flow eroded the mortar between bricks at the base/corner of a building, washing out mortar joints. [IMG] (p37)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"High Street, Wellingborough",England,"Reported as conveying surface–water runoff down into adjoining streets (including Silver Street and Sheep Street), contributing to flooding of properties in the town centre. [TAB] (p17)
