Flows from High Street combined with Church Street to form a powerful, damaging flow at the junction; at least one property had a flooded basement, low wall to a sunken frontage was overtopped, and multiple properties sustained external damage and possible internal flooding from the destructive flow. (p19)
Powerful flow of surface water caused damage to brick mortar on the street's buildings (reported for High Street). [IMG,PAG] (p36)
Powerful surface water flow eroded the mortar between bricks at the base/corner of a building, washing out mortar joints. [IMG] (p37)",3 properties (p19),GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.301914,-0.6943913,"<div id=""html_a8a3c4c5cb8ce41cf8f44302919d6d6f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Orient Way, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from Orient Way flowed through a rear car park and contributed to flood ingress at rear doors and walls of town&ndash;centre premises. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowed south from Orient Way to the rear of properties on the east side of Silver Street; the water had no outlet, increased in depth behind buildings and flowed under doors and through voids, causing internal flooding of those properties. (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Orient Way, Wellingborough",England,"Surface water runoff from Orient Way flowed through a rear car park and contributed to flood ingress at rear doors and walls of town–centre premises. [TAB] (p17)
