GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.2997133,-0.6915408,"<div id=""html_c046451811eba45941bfbeaa3b647636"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Doddington Road, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water collected at the low point around the junction with Sheep Street and Doddington Road, forming a deep pool that made the area hazardous and impeded access. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The junction with Sheep Street became a low&ndash;point where runoff collected, forming a lake that increased in size and depth and made the area hazardous to vehicles and pedestrians. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The low point at the junction with Sheep Street caused water from the catchment to settle and form a lake that deepened over time, extending around Doddington Road; standing water in this area affected nearby properties. (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Doddington Road, Wellingborough",England,"Surface water collected at the low point around the junction with Sheep Street and Doddington Road, forming a deep pool that made the area hazardous and impeded access. [TAB] (p17)
The junction with Sheep Street became a low–point where runoff collected, forming a lake that increased in size and depth and made the area hazardous to vehicles and pedestrians. (p18)
The low point at the junction with Sheep Street caused water from the catchment to settle and form a lake that deepened over time, extending around Doddington Road; standing water in this area affected nearby properties. (p20)",,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.293346,-0.6842572,"<div id=""html_5c9b51f392ced96de680d2c5dc224532"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>London Road, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from High Street ran into London Road during the event on 16/08/2020, contributing to deep external flooding nearby and to internal flooding of adjacent properties (basements and ground&ndash;floor entrance halls/annexes). The flooding made the road impassable in places and required recovery actions at affected premises. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed from High Street into Sheep Street and along London Road, indicating surface water impacts on the road. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Standing water that formed at the low point extended around London Road; properties in the area were affected by the deepening water. (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>external depth between 1200mm to 1800mm [TAB] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"London Road, Wellingborough",England,"Surface water from High Street ran into London Road during the event on 16/08/2020, contributing to deep external flooding nearby and to internal flooding of adjacent properties (basements and ground–floor entrance halls/annexes). The flooding made the road impassable in places and required recovery actions at affected premises. [TAB] (p17)
Floodwater flowed from High Street into Sheep Street and along London Road, indicating surface water impacts on the road. (p18)
Standing water that formed at the low point extended around London Road; properties in the area were affected by the deepening water. (p20)",external depth between 1200mm to 1800mm [TAB] (p17),GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.3031347,-0.695786,"<div id=""html_fe36067a04de473bd6dca3cf30d96b7c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Queen Street, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from Queens Lane (sic) entered the rear of a Church Street property, causing internal flooding. (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Queen Street, Wellingborough",England,"Surface water from Queens Lane (sic) entered the rear of a Church Street property, causing internal flooding. (p19)",,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.3045519,-0.6995654,"<div id=""html_e96c4863ae816d1b76c3460455d695e0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Broad Green, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Strong surface water flows originated from Broad Green and met flows from Church Street at High Street, forming a powerful, damaging flow that impacted buildings near the Church Street/High Street junction and continued downstream toward Silver Street, carrying large debris and endangering pedestrians and vehicles. (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Broad Green, Wellingborough",England,"Strong surface water flows originated from Broad Green and met flows from Church Street at High Street, forming a powerful, damaging flow that impacted buildings near the Church Street/High Street junction and continued downstream toward Silver Street, carrying large debris and endangering pedestrians and vehicles. (p19)",,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.3106138,-0.8659129831915817,"<div id=""html_822f267276cc6e7a3956b2a0825da1c5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Northamptonshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense, short&ndash;duration rainfall on 16 August 2020 produced surface&ndash;water and flash flooding in the Wellingborough area of Northamptonshire, resulting in localised flooding in the area documented by the investigation. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Northamptonshire,England,"Intense, short–duration rainfall on 16 August 2020 produced surface–water and flash flooding in the Wellingborough area of Northamptonshire, resulting in localised flooding in the area documented by the investigation. (p10)",,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,20,2020-08-16,52.30189,-0.6937309,"<div id=""html_25eb84f889bce3558fea7dc248295315"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A flood incident at Sheep Street / Silver Street in Wellingborough caused internal flooding of more than five buildings in close proximity. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Town experienced a flood incident on 16 August 2020 that caused internal flooding of properties in the Sheep Street / Silver Street area. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland surface water flows from exceeded drainage in the catchment contributed to flooding within the lower parts of the town (town centre area) during the incident. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The town experienced a surface water flooding incident on 16th August 2020. The report records that highway drainage in the area relies on road gullies connecting to the public surface water sewer; gullies at Silver Street and Sheep Street were last cleansed in September 2019 and those at High Street in June 2017. The investigation notes two StreetDoctor reports of blocked drains on Cambridge Street in the streets surrounding the incident. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The town centre area experienced intense surface water flows from northwest to southeast; drainage systems were exceeded, producing powerful flows along roads (notably Broad Green, Church Street and High Street) that caused destructive impacts to buildings and internal flooding of properties. In total, 19 properties in this area are understood to have flooded internally. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense short&ndash;duration rainfall on 16/08/2020 overwhelmed surface water drainage across the area. Deep, fast&ndash;moving surface water occupied the full width of roads and footways in affected parts of the town; properties and external areas were flooded and emergency crews pumped deep floodwater to safe areas. Town centre surfaces required clearing in follow&ndash;up operations and sandbags were delivered to some properties. (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than five buildings (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than five buildings (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>19 properties (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Wellingborough,England,"A flood incident at Sheep Street / Silver Street in Wellingborough caused internal flooding of more than five buildings in close proximity. (p5)
Town experienced a flood incident on 16 August 2020 that caused internal flooding of properties in the Sheep Street / Silver Street area. (p8)
Overland surface water flows from exceeded drainage in the catchment contributed to flooding within the lower parts of the town (town centre area) during the incident. (p14)
The town experienced a surface water flooding incident on 16th August 2020. The report records that highway drainage in the area relies on road gullies connecting to the public surface water sewer; gullies at Silver Street and Sheep Street were last cleansed in September 2019 and those at High Street in June 2017. The investigation notes two StreetDoctor reports of blocked drains on Cambridge Street in the streets surrounding the incident. (p15)
The town centre area experienced intense surface water flows from northwest to southeast; drainage systems were exceeded, producing powerful flows along roads (notably Broad Green, Church Street and High Street) that caused destructive impacts to buildings and internal flooding of properties. In total, 19 properties in this area are understood to have flooded internally. (p19)
Intense short–duration rainfall on 16/08/2020 overwhelmed surface water drainage across the area. Deep, fast–moving surface water occupied the full width of roads and footways in affected parts of the town; properties and external areas were flooded and emergency crews pumped deep floodwater to safe areas. Town centre surfaces required clearing in follow–up operations and sandbags were delivered to some properties. (p21)","more than five buildings (p5)
more than five buildings (p8)
19 properties (p19)",GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_20_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Sheep Street / Silver Street, Wellingborough: 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Sheep Street and Silver Street, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-CAM,9,2014-08-01,52.3474248,0.2208462,"<div id=""html_f6e77a1486db5570e116ae61eb29f4b0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chapel Lane, Stretham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Chapel Lane experienced localized flooding as the focus of the reported incident; extent and specific impacts are not quantified in the report. [IMG] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Gullies on Chapel Lane were identified as capacity&ndash;limited and implicated in the surface water flooding incident; the Highways Team cleared the gullies on Chapel Lane as a remedial action. [TAB] (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Chapel Lane, Stretham",England,"Chapel Lane experienced localized flooding as the focus of the reported incident; extent and specific impacts are not quantified in the report. [IMG] (p2)
Gullies on Chapel Lane were identified as capacity–limited and implicated in the surface water flooding incident; the Highways Team cleared the gullies on Chapel Lane as a remedial action. [TAB] (p3)",,GB-CAM_9_2014-08-01.html,GB-CAM_9_2014-08-01,Stretham flooding August 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Stretham,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2014/Cambridgeshire County/Flood/Investigation/Report/Stretham.pdf
GB-CAM,9,2014-08-01,52.3486189,0.218727,"<div id=""html_8d0002c2b1993eec4541a0aa2357e1fc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Stretham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Gullies on High Street were identified as capacity&ndash;limited and implicated in the surface water flooding incident; the Highways Team cleared the gullies on High Street as a remedial action. [TAB] (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"High Street, Stretham",England,Gullies on High Street were identified as capacity–limited and implicated in the surface water flooding incident; the Highways Team cleared the gullies on High Street as a remedial action. [TAB] (p3),,GB-CAM_9_2014-08-01.html,GB-CAM_9_2014-08-01,Stretham flooding August 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Stretham,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2014/Cambridgeshire County/Flood/Investigation/Report/Stretham.pdf
GB-CAM,9,2014-08-01,52.3467902,0.2211425,"<div id=""html_9c262f29cfd6a60789a9bd41864809f8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Newmarket Road, Stretham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sections of Newmarket Road had gullies cleared by the Highways Team; ECDC arranged for the Awarded watercourse along Newmarket Road to be cleared (reported completed October 2014). These works were undertaken in response to a surface water flooding incident believed to be caused by gully capacity issues. [TAB] (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Newmarket Road, Stretham",England,Sections of Newmarket Road had gullies cleared by the Highways Team; ECDC arranged for the Awarded watercourse along Newmarket Road to be cleared (reported completed October 2014). These works were undertaken in response to a surface water flooding incident believed to be caused by gully capacity issues. [TAB] (p3),,GB-CAM_9_2014-08-01.html,GB-CAM_9_2014-08-01,Stretham flooding August 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Stretham,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2014/Cambridgeshire County/Flood/Investigation/Report/Stretham.pdf
GB-CAM,9,2014-08-01,52.3395647,0.2231972,"<div id=""html_9a8fb48a0e83f4c582dded0cdbdaa6f7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stretham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Central Stretham &mdash; specifically the area around Chapel Lane &mdash; was affected by a localized flood; the report does not provide quantified extent or damage. [IMG] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Stretham,England,Central Stretham — specifically the area around Chapel Lane — was affected by a localized flood; the report does not provide quantified extent or damage. [IMG] (p2),,GB-CAM_9_2014-08-01.html,GB-CAM_9_2014-08-01,Stretham flooding August 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Stretham,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2014/Cambridgeshire County/Flood/Investigation/Report/Stretham.pdf
GB-HEF,8,2020-02-16,52.2355219,-2.7449348,"<div id=""html_befd1c18775e73effb47a75a104ba5a7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Lugg</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Lugg may have influenced the event by raising downstream water levels and reducing the capacity of small tributaries to drain, contributing to flooding in the village. (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,River Lugg,England,"River Lugg may have influenced the event by raising downstream water levels and reducing the capacity of small tributaries to drain, contributing to flooding in the village. (p2)",,GB-HEF_8_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_8_2020-02-16,Wellington Marsh flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Wellington Marsh,055/Herefordshire County/07/Wellington/Marsh.pdf
GB-HEF,8,2020-02-16,52.1213094,-2.7328091,"<div id=""html_a5fa11585f915d579aff2a876c07265c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wellington Marsh</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Wellington Marsh was the location of the key flood event on 16 February 2020. Environment Agency flood mapping shows flood zones 2 and 3 to the east and southeast of the settlement, with some areas benefiting from flood defences; the main settlement is adjacent to, but not entirely within, the highest&ndash;risk flood zone. [IMG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties caused by runoff and overflowing minor watercourses; depths reported from under 6 inches up to 2 ft. One resident reported garden flooding that lasted 1&ndash;2 days. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties in the settlement. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties; depths <6 inches to 2 ft; 1 garden flooded for 1-2 days (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Wellington Marsh,England,"Wellington Marsh was the location of the key flood event on 16 February 2020. Environment Agency flood mapping shows flood zones 2 and 3 to the east and southeast of the settlement, with some areas benefiting from flood defences; the main settlement is adjacent to, but not entirely within, the highest–risk flood zone. [IMG] (p1)
Internal flooding of residential properties caused by runoff and overflowing minor watercourses; depths reported from under 6 inches up to 2 ft. One resident reported garden flooding that lasted 1–2 days. (p2)
Internal flooding of properties in the settlement. (p3)","9 properties; depths <6 inches to 2 ft; 1 garden flooded for 1-2 days (p2)
9 properties (p3)",GB-HEF_8_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_8_2020-02-16,Wellington Marsh flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Wellington Marsh,055/Herefordshire County/07/Wellington/Marsh.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.70567537357795,-2.1064182473606494,"<div id=""html_35824233621c1f55be1614a51dcf95d0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Shade Chapel</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culvert carrying Walsden Water beneath the building collapsed, damaging the base and sides of the culvert and badly restricting the channel (risking blockage). The partial collapse put the building at risk of falling into the river and could have increased flood risk to other properties. [IMG] (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>250 properties [IMG] (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Shade Chapel,England,"The culvert carrying Walsden Water beneath the building collapsed, damaging the base and sides of the culvert and badly restricting the channel (risking blockage). The partial collapse put the building at risk of falling into the river and could have increased flood risk to other properties. [IMG] (p33)",250 properties [IMG] (p33),GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7003904,-1.7823601,"<div id=""html_b10f367976e02bcaaa10f712a19bd20e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Masonic Hall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Partial flooding in the cellars of Masonic halls located on Bridge End. (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Masonic Hall,England,Partial flooding in the cellars of Masonic halls located on Bridge End. (p44),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7408284,-2.0275944,"<div id=""html_2592d18905e2cba5f28d697e9896d991"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stubbing Wharf</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Three boats were spotted adrift at Stubbing's Wharf during the 9 February 2020 flood. (p49)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Stubbing Wharf,England,Three boats were spotted adrift at Stubbing's Wharf during the 9 February 2020 flood. (p49),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7017957,-1.7753797,"<div id=""html_e4160e1131fa4c6ff90e955e44b125de"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lidl</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood&ndash;related masonry wall collapse occurred near the Lidl shop, indicating structural damage adjacent to the store from the flood event. (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Lidl,England,"Flood–related masonry wall collapse occurred near the Lidl shop, indicating structural damage adjacent to the store from the flood event. (p44)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,54.7023545,-3.2765753,"<div id=""html_42eeefe16fc4f7d913e54be0b9875eeb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>UK</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storm Ciara (8&ndash;9 February 2020) brought heavy, prolonged rainfall across much of the UK, producing widespread flooding; Calderdale accounts for a significant proportion of impacted properties nationally. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>37% of all impacted properties across the UK were Calderdale residential properties (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,UK,England,"Storm Ciara (8–9 February 2020) brought heavy, prolonged rainfall across much of the UK, producing widespread flooding; Calderdale accounts for a significant proportion of impacted properties nationally. (p3)",37% of all impacted properties across the UK were Calderdale residential properties (p3),GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.67699991820208,-1.9503159152582255,"<div id=""html_dd410a8571700055b265546c99e6d2af"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ryburn Ward</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding associated with the River Ryburn at Ripponden produced a significant gauge&ndash;record event and is linked to mapped clusters of flooded properties in the Ryburn and Ripponden ward group (flooding recorded as internal and/or external). [IMG] (p29)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>return period 60&ndash;65 years; ranking 1 in 40&ndash;year gauge record [IMG] (p29)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Ryburn Ward,England,Fluvial flooding associated with the River Ryburn at Ripponden produced a significant gauge–record event and is linked to mapped clusters of flooded properties in the Ryburn and Ripponden ward group (flooding recorded as internal and/or external). [IMG] (p29),return period 60–65 years; ranking 1 in 40–year gauge record [IMG] (p29),GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.74518421753094,-2.0194262678117063,"<div id=""html_da8ca470f8988b9281cae91b4f5114dd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Calder Ward</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded flood incidents are concentrated along the valley within Calder Ward (particularly Hebden Bridge), with a dominance of fluvial and surface water incidents affecting residential and business properties, highways and structures. [PAG,IMG] (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Calder Ward,England,"Recorded flood incidents are concentrated along the valley within Calder Ward (particularly Hebden Bridge), with a dominance of fluvial and surface water incidents affecting residential and business properties, highways and structures. [PAG,IMG] (p34)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.69891098695816,-1.7855268679529341,"<div id=""html_63f7b38df0a42327ac5565a9e624a9d2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brighouse Ward</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Canal overtopping at Brighouse Lock caused a barge to drift out of channel onto the adjacent footpath. At Brighouse Bottom Lock a significant volume of water from the River Calder flowed into the lock basin, flooding the basin and adjacent properties. Flood damage to a river/canal embankment was observed at Cooper Bridge. Anchor Pit towpath at Dyke Bridge suffered scour and wall collapse, leaving the walkway unsafe and requiring rebuilding. The Environment Agency recorded flood outline shows the flooded area concentrated along the main river corridor through Brighouse. [IMG] (p45)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Brighouse Ward,England,"Canal overtopping at Brighouse Lock caused a barge to drift out of channel onto the adjacent footpath. At Brighouse Bottom Lock a significant volume of water from the River Calder flowed into the lock basin, flooding the basin and adjacent properties. Flood damage to a river/canal embankment was observed at Cooper Bridge. Anchor Pit towpath at Dyke Bridge suffered scour and wall collapse, leaving the walkway unsafe and requiring rebuilding. The Environment Agency recorded flood outline shows the flooded area concentrated along the main river corridor through Brighouse. [IMG] (p45)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.73393536249604,-1.9768405513193483,"<div id=""html_abecd35e41729d9b992c79f030475f9f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>White Lea Clough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>White Lea Clough is identified as a watercourse contributing to flooding in Mytholmroyd; Mytholmroyd experienced mass property and infrastructure damage during the Storm Ciara event (8&ndash;9 February 2020). (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,White Lea Clough,England,White Lea Clough is identified as a watercourse contributing to flooding in Mytholmroyd; Mytholmroyd experienced mass property and infrastructure damage during the Storm Ciara event (8–9 February 2020). (p8),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7471001,-1.9439306,"<div id=""html_1b7f30bebbf36f024cc21dc3bd3520ff"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Luddenden Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding of Luddenden Brook contributed to flooding in Luddenden and Luddenden Foot during the Storm Ciara event on 9th February 2020, causing property flooding and contributing to damage to local roads and bridges. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Luddenden Brook contributed to fluvial flooding in Luddenden and Luddenden Foot, which formed part of the areas that suffered property and infrastructure damage during the February 2020 event. [PAG] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Luddenden Brook,England,"Flooding of Luddenden Brook contributed to flooding in Luddenden and Luddenden Foot during the Storm Ciara event on 9th February 2020, causing property flooding and contributing to damage to local roads and bridges. (p8)
Luddenden Brook contributed to fluvial flooding in Luddenden and Luddenden Foot, which formed part of the areas that suffered property and infrastructure damage during the February 2020 event. [PAG] (p9)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.71880636738931,-1.9909485270356786,"<div id=""html_52f5f56f7471781500b32a44e2f22b4e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cragg Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cragg Brook caused fluvial flooding and associated highway flooding in Cragg Vale / Mytholmroyd, contributing to property and infrastructure damage and road closures during the February 2020 event. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Crag Brook (Dauber Bridge) gauge exhibited a sharp rise in stage on 09/02/2020, peaking around midday and then declining while remaining above pre&ndash;event levels. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Cragg Brook,England,"Cragg Brook caused fluvial flooding and associated highway flooding in Cragg Vale / Mytholmroyd, contributing to property and infrastructure damage and road closures during the February 2020 event. [PAG] (p9)
The Crag Brook (Dauber Bridge) gauge exhibited a sharp rise in stage on 09/02/2020, peaking around midday and then declining while remaining above pre–event levels. [PAG,IMG] (p26)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7122329,-1.7776663,"<div id=""html_b9654a2018920d3ab930551529cc4c1b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clifton Beck</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clifton Beck (included in this grouped name) is identified as a cause of historic flooding in Brighouse and contributed to fluvial flooding and associated damage to properties and infrastructure in the local area during the February 2020 event. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Clifton Beck,England,Clifton Beck (included in this grouped name) is identified as a cause of historic flooding in Brighouse and contributed to fluvial flooding and associated damage to properties and infrastructure in the local area during the February 2020 event. (p9),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.72487915208145,-2.066599992128834,"<div id=""html_0791cd2cdb4e0021d563b9cab396a329"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Jumble Hole Clough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High flows and overtopping from the River Calder (and flows from Jumble Hole Clough) increased flood extents in Hebden Bridge and contributed to flooding impacts in the town centre. [PAG] (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Jumble Hole Clough,England,High flows and overtopping from the River Calder (and flows from Jumble Hole Clough) increased flood extents in Hebden Bridge and contributed to flooding impacts in the town centre. [PAG] (p34),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7140101,-1.8538312,"<div id=""html_435e649b10109dcad99201433ac27a90"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hebble Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hebble Brook (Halifax gauge) experienced an exceptional rise in stage during the 9 February 2020 event, with levels much higher than the historical average and a pronounced peak around midday followed by an elevated falling limb. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued a Flood Warning for 'Hebble Brook at Halifax' at 06:57 on 9 February 2020 as part of the Calder catchment warnings. [TAB] (p47)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Hebble Brook,England,"Hebble Brook (Halifax gauge) experienced an exceptional rise in stage during the 9 February 2020 event, with levels much higher than the historical average and a pronounced peak around midday followed by an elevated falling limb. [PAG,IMG] (p26)
Environment Agency issued a Flood Warning for 'Hebble Brook at Halifax' at 06:57 on 9 February 2020 as part of the Calder catchment warnings. [TAB] (p47)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.6724332,-1.8656249,"<div id=""html_0ef5d5a9130d79a5fcb2f295195ced51"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Holywell Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping of the brooks (Black and Holywell Brooks) caused downhill flows along the road network that damaged nearby residential properties and led to a local school closure due to infrastructure damage. (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Holywell Brook,England,Overtopping of the brooks (Black and Holywell Brooks) caused downhill flows along the road network that damaged nearby residential properties and led to a local school closure due to infrastructure damage. (p44),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.6813267,-1.8811163,"<div id=""html_7ea94cb45166b2f466bf3d2419fb6ef3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Black Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping of the brooks (Black and Holywell Brooks) caused downhill flows along the road network that damaged nearby residential properties and led to a local school closure due to infrastructure damage. (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Black Brook,England,Overtopping of the brooks (Black and Holywell Brooks) caused downhill flows along the road network that damaged nearby residential properties and led to a local school closure due to infrastructure damage. (p44),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7402625,-2.0151439,"<div id=""html_bc881ec620f7d743e04b4df5077444bc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hebden Bridge Aqueduct</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Large&ndash;scale deposition of gravel and sand from the River Calder altered the channel and raised concerns over the aqueduct's structural stability; Canal & River Trust reported the aqueduct was potentially destabilised by the changed flow and deposited material. [PAG,IMG] (p35)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Hebden Bridge Aqueduct,England,"Large–scale deposition of gravel and sand from the River Calder altered the channel and raised concerns over the aqueduct's structural stability; Canal & River Trust reported the aqueduct was potentially destabilised by the changed flow and deposited material. [PAG,IMG] (p35)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.711209629850224,-1.9358042209780073,"<div id=""html_61812df86fd3a33060935e36b8656423"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Calder Vale Line Between the Sowerby Bridge Tunnel and Luddenden Foot</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A blocked culvert caused a large volume of surface water to flood across the rail lines between Sowerby Bridge Tunnel and Luddendenfoot, disrupting rail operations. (p49)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A large volume of surface water flowed across the railway lines due to a blocked culvert. Railway track and ballast were partially submerged and the culvert was overwhelmed/blocked with debris, causing disruption to rail services. [IMG] (p50)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Calder Vale Line Between the Sowerby Bridge Tunnel and Luddenden Foot,England,"A blocked culvert caused a large volume of surface water to flood across the rail lines between Sowerby Bridge Tunnel and Luddendenfoot, disrupting rail operations. (p49)
A large volume of surface water flowed across the railway lines due to a blocked culvert. Railway track and ballast were partially submerged and the culvert was overwhelmed/blocked with debris, causing disruption to rail services. [IMG] (p50)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.74339891426743,-2.015223231705138,"<div id=""html_66cacb7a86fe7d673c76f3fc6e5cf968"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mytholm Steeps</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water overland flows (referred to as Mytholm 'Steeps') channelled intense runoff down this location, overwhelming resident diversion measures and causing flood impacts including debris transport and damage to access and properties adjacent to the flow path. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Mytholm Steeps,England,"Surface–water overland flows (referred to as Mytholm 'Steeps') channelled intense runoff down this location, overwhelming resident diversion measures and causing flood impacts including debris transport and damage to access and properties adjacent to the flow path. (p33)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.69683345523028,-1.8124515126741212,"<div id=""html_362622de4c59e60b66176a05d2e221dc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cromwell Bottom Local Nature Reserve</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A boat was stranded on the bank after river levels dropped near Cromwell Bottom following the flood event. (p49)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Cromwell Bottom Local Nature Reserve,England,A boat was stranded on the bank after river levels dropped near Cromwell Bottom following the flood event. (p49),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7023109,-2.1068854,"<div id=""html_a9845a3952a84f21bb3e8a52af6b098b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Walsden Water</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding from Walsden Water is identified as a cause of flooding in Todmorden; Todmorden was one of the areas that experienced mass property and infrastructure damage during the Storm Ciara event (8&ndash;9 February 2020). (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Walsden Water gauge recorded a flood peak of 0.71 m on 9 February 2020 (time of peak 11:45). Feb 2020 was the highest (rank 1) event at this gauge in the listed historical events. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued flood warnings for Walsden Water during the 9 February 2020 event (Walsden at 06:29; Gauxholme at 08:13; Walsden Water and Ramsden Clough at Walsden at 08:14; Walsden Water at Todmorden from Shade to Salford at 08:27). [TAB] (p47)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Walsden Water,England,"Fluvial flooding from Walsden Water is identified as a cause of flooding in Todmorden; Todmorden was one of the areas that experienced mass property and infrastructure damage during the Storm Ciara event (8–9 February 2020). (p8)
The Walsden Water gauge recorded a flood peak of 0.71 m on 9 February 2020 (time of peak 11:45). Feb 2020 was the highest (rank 1) event at this gauge in the listed historical events. [TAB] (p27)
Environment Agency issued flood warnings for Walsden Water during the 9 February 2020 event (Walsden at 06:29; Gauxholme at 08:13; Walsden Water and Ramsden Clough at Walsden at 08:14; Walsden Water at Todmorden from Shade to Salford at 08:27). [TAB] (p47)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7589463,-2.0321427,"<div id=""html_0ac11501d544a24748faf376e5407848"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hebden Water</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding at the Hebden Water / River Calder confluence contributed to significant flooding in Hebden Bridge during Storm Ciara (8&ndash;9 February 2020); this event caused mass property and infrastructure damage in Hebden Bridge and damage to council buildings including Hebden Bridge library. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hebden Water is named as the tributary at the Hebden Bridge confluence with the River Calder. Hebden Bridge was one of the towns that suffered mass property and infrastructure damage during the February 2020 storm, with flooding at the Calder/Hebden Water confluence contributing to the impacts (including damage to council buildings such as Hebden Bridge library). [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hebden Water (Nutclough) gauge rose sharply during the 09/02/2020 event, peaking around midday and then falling while remaining above baseline levels. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Associated gauge peak (Hebden Bridge Nutclough) reached 2.19 m at 11:45 on 9 February 2020; this was ranked 2nd among listed events for that location. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Environment Agency issued flood warnings for Hebden Water at Hebden Bridge (including Old Gate, Valley Road to Midgehole Road) on 9 February 2020; Hebden Water contributed to the river flooding that heavily impacted Hebden Bridge during the event. [TAB] (p47)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Six reservoirs on Hebden Water (Gorple Lower, WD Lower, WD Middle, WD Upper, Widdop and Gorpley) were held at 90% capacity prior to the storm and then filled during the heavy rainfall on 9th February 2020, resulting in those reservoirs spilling at various times between 11:30 and 18:00 on 9th February 2020. (p48)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Hebden Water,England,"Fluvial flooding at the Hebden Water / River Calder confluence contributed to significant flooding in Hebden Bridge during Storm Ciara (8–9 February 2020); this event caused mass property and infrastructure damage in Hebden Bridge and damage to council buildings including Hebden Bridge library. (p8)
Hebden Water is named as the tributary at the Hebden Bridge confluence with the River Calder. Hebden Bridge was one of the towns that suffered mass property and infrastructure damage during the February 2020 storm, with flooding at the Calder/Hebden Water confluence contributing to the impacts (including damage to council buildings such as Hebden Bridge library). [PAG] (p9)
Hebden Water (Nutclough) gauge rose sharply during the 09/02/2020 event, peaking around midday and then falling while remaining above baseline levels. [PAG,IMG] (p26)
Associated gauge peak (Hebden Bridge Nutclough) reached 2.19 m at 11:45 on 9 February 2020; this was ranked 2nd among listed events for that location. [TAB] (p27)
The Environment Agency issued flood warnings for Hebden Water at Hebden Bridge (including Old Gate, Valley Road to Midgehole Road) on 9 February 2020; Hebden Water contributed to the river flooding that heavily impacted Hebden Bridge during the event. [TAB] (p47)
Six reservoirs on Hebden Water (Gorple Lower, WD Lower, WD Middle, WD Upper, Widdop and Gorpley) were held at 90% capacity prior to the storm and then filled during the heavy rainfall on 9th February 2020, resulting in those reservoirs spilling at various times between 11:30 and 18:00 on 9th February 2020. (p48)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.6884889,-1.8393557,"<div id=""html_a1d9e0963dedcb67ed1c309d2e1e6560"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Calder</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rapid rises in the River Calder during Storm Ciara (8&ndash;9 February 2020) contributed to widespread fluvial flooding across the Calder Valley, leading to flooding of residential and business properties and serious damage to roads, bridges and major infrastructure within the borough. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Calder (and its main tributaries) produced fluvial flooding along its course through Todmorden, Hebden Bridge, Mytholmroyd, Sowerby Bridge, Luddenden and Brighouse during the February 2020 event, contributing to property and infrastructure flooding and damage in those towns. [IMG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Calder gauges across the catchment rose sharply beginning late on 08/02/2020, peaking around midday on 09/02/2020 with levels above the historical averages and showing a secondary peak on the falling limb about 12 hours after the main peak. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Calder at the Todmorden Centre Vale gauge reached a peak level of 1.97 m on 9 February 2020 (time of peak 08:45). This event ranked 2nd compared to the listed historical events at this gauge. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High flows and overtopping from the River Calder (and flows from Jumble Hole Clough) increased flood extents in Hebden Bridge and contributed to flooding impacts in the town centre. [PAG] (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Calder contributed fluvial flooding in the Sowerby Bridge town centre around its confluence with the River Ryburn, leading to inundation of nearby businesses and properties. (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Environment Agency issued flood warnings for multiple reaches of the River Calder on 9 February 2020 (warnings covered locations including Brearley & Luddenden Foot, Hebden Bridge, Mytholm and Hebble End, Central Mytholmroyd, Brighouse, Sowerby Bridge, Copley, Elland, Cooper Bridge, Central Mirfield and Bradley). Flooding on and around the River Calder was part of the event that produced widespread impacts across the Calder Valley. [TAB,PAG] (p47)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 schools temporarily closed; 2 schools significantly damaged; ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 39 flood warnings; 3,965 buildings affected across the Calder Valley; 3,433 residential properties; 532 business properties; 50 dwellings deemed unsuitable for living; £6.7m estimated economic damage to local business; £10 million infrastructure damage (including £750,000 Council assets) [TAB,PAG] (p47)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,River Calder,England,"Rapid rises in the River Calder during Storm Ciara (8–9 February 2020) contributed to widespread fluvial flooding across the Calder Valley, leading to flooding of residential and business properties and serious damage to roads, bridges and major infrastructure within the borough. (p8)
The River Calder (and its main tributaries) produced fluvial flooding along its course through Todmorden, Hebden Bridge, Mytholmroyd, Sowerby Bridge, Luddenden and Brighouse during the February 2020 event, contributing to property and infrastructure flooding and damage in those towns. [IMG] (p9)
River Calder gauges across the catchment rose sharply beginning late on 08/02/2020, peaking around midday on 09/02/2020 with levels above the historical averages and showing a secondary peak on the falling limb about 12 hours after the main peak. [PAG,IMG] (p26)
River Calder at the Todmorden Centre Vale gauge reached a peak level of 1.97 m on 9 February 2020 (time of peak 08:45). This event ranked 2nd compared to the listed historical events at this gauge. [TAB] (p27)
High flows and overtopping from the River Calder (and flows from Jumble Hole Clough) increased flood extents in Hebden Bridge and contributed to flooding impacts in the town centre. [PAG] (p34)
The River Calder contributed fluvial flooding in the Sowerby Bridge town centre around its confluence with the River Ryburn, leading to inundation of nearby businesses and properties. (p41)
The Environment Agency issued flood warnings for multiple reaches of the River Calder on 9 February 2020 (warnings covered locations including Brearley & Luddenden Foot, Hebden Bridge, Mytholm and Hebble End, Central Mytholmroyd, Brighouse, Sowerby Bridge, Copley, Elland, Cooper Bridge, Central Mirfield and Bradley). Flooding on and around the River Calder was part of the event that produced widespread impacts across the Calder Valley. [TAB,PAG] (p47)","8 schools temporarily closed; 2 schools significantly damaged; ␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ [PAG] (p9)
at least 39 flood warnings; 3,965 buildings affected across the Calder Valley; 3,433 residential properties; 532 business properties; 50 dwellings deemed unsuitable for living; £6.7m estimated economic damage to local business; £10 million infrastructure damage (including £750,000 Council assets) [TAB,PAG] (p47)",GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.70674,-1.9125793,"<div id=""html_00c7472285d4f9c6b1ff531c6143fcc4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Ryburn</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding of the River Ryburn contributed to the confluence flooding at Sowerby Bridge during the Storm Ciara event on 9th February 2020, causing property flooding and contributing to damage to local roads and bridges. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The gauge on the River Ryburn at Ripponden recorded an exceptional high&ndash;flow event, indicating major river flows affecting the River Ryburn during the event. [TAB] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Ryburn, at its confluence with the River Calder, was associated with fluvial flooding concentrated in the Sowerby Bridge centre and contributed to inundation of nearby commercial and residential properties. (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency flood warnings were issued on 9 February 2020 for the River Calder and River Ryburn around Central Sowerby Bridge and Sowerby Bridge; these rivers were involved in the river flooding during the 8&ndash;10 February 2020 event that affected communities in the Calder catchment. [TAB,PAG] (p47)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>40 water years (length of record); ranking: 1; estimated return period 60&ndash;65 years [TAB] (p29)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,River Ryburn,England,"Flooding of the River Ryburn contributed to the confluence flooding at Sowerby Bridge during the Storm Ciara event on 9th February 2020, causing property flooding and contributing to damage to local roads and bridges. (p8)
The gauge on the River Ryburn at Ripponden recorded an exceptional high–flow event, indicating major river flows affecting the River Ryburn during the event. [TAB] (p29)
The River Ryburn, at its confluence with the River Calder, was associated with fluvial flooding concentrated in the Sowerby Bridge centre and contributed to inundation of nearby commercial and residential properties. (p41)
Environment Agency flood warnings were issued on 9 February 2020 for the River Calder and River Ryburn around Central Sowerby Bridge and Sowerby Bridge; these rivers were involved in the river flooding during the 8–10 February 2020 event that affected communities in the Calder catchment. [TAB,PAG] (p47)",40 water years (length of record); ranking: 1; estimated return period 60–65 years [TAB] (p29),GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7431176,-2.011356,"<div id=""html_baf856dd7a564ff59c0f54d0e5550860"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Keighley Road, Hebden Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Torrential surface&ndash;water overland flows were directed down Keighley Road, quickly defeating residents&#8217; attempts to divert flows; extensive flooding contributed to damage of residential properties, including internal flooding and impacts from debris and large rocks carried by the flows. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Keighley Road, Hebden Bridge",England,"Torrential surface–water overland flows were directed down Keighley Road, quickly defeating residents’ attempts to divert flows; extensive flooding contributed to damage of residential properties, including internal flooding and impacts from debris and large rocks carried by the flows. (p33)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7416685,-2.0142172,"<div id=""html_0c0392232d89d6c65e9cec4662286716"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Old Gate, Hebden Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Environment Agency issued a flood warning for Hebden Water at Hebden Bridge &ndash; Old Gate on 9 February 2020; Old Gate was within the Hebden Bridge locations subject to river flood warnings and formed part of the area impacted by the event. [TAB] (p47)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Old Gate, Hebden Bridge",England,The Environment Agency issued a flood warning for Hebden Water at Hebden Bridge – Old Gate on 9 February 2020; Old Gate was within the Hebden Bridge locations subject to river flood warnings and formed part of the area impacted by the event. [TAB] (p47),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7412675,-2.0180145,"<div id=""html_6734e707df0de9c24294348a91d0a76a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Market Street, Hebden Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extensive flooding in the centre of Hebden Bridge caused internal flooding to properties on Market Street, with external impacts from debris and large rocks transported by the flows. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Market Street, Hebden Bridge",England,"Extensive flooding in the centre of Hebden Bridge caused internal flooding to properties on Market Street, with external impacts from debris and large rocks transported by the flows. (p33)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7146839,-2.0916368,"<div id=""html_745acd4bdaff76e7af1e0a31539a3e02"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cambridge Street, Todmorden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road and adjacent areas were inundated; Cambridge Street acted as a main flow path during fluvial and surface&ndash;water flooding. (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Cambridge Street, Todmorden",England,Road and adjacent areas were inundated; Cambridge Street acted as a main flow path during fluvial and surface–water flooding. (p30),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7220236,-2.1009233,"<div id=""html_dbecb5dca473ed2f2a9d454c78e54eba"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stile Road, Todmorden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road and adjacent areas were inundated; Stile Road formed a principal flow path during the fluvial and surface&ndash;water flooding. (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Stile Road, Todmorden",England,Road and adjacent areas were inundated; Stile Road formed a principal flow path during the fluvial and surface–water flooding. (p30),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7178448,-2.0987635,"<div id=""html_645e2ed49a2386a9b684ccdd21592273"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Gledhill Street, Todmorden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties experienced flooded cellars and flooded ground floors. (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Gledhill Street, Todmorden",England,Properties experienced flooded cellars and flooded ground floors. (p30),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7219502,-2.1073636,"<div id=""html_c13acb0cf2fb70f8562f529643e0b983"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wilson Close, Todmorden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A culvert on Wilson Close burst during the event and damaged the footway above, creating a danger to pedestrians. (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Wilson Close, Todmorden",England,"A culvert on Wilson Close burst during the event and damaged the footway above, creating a danger to pedestrians. (p30)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7243755,-2.1119208,"<div id=""html_2c43fa52a13732b29a22d3e033ad455d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stoney Royd Lane, Todmorden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A culvert in Stoney Road (sic) Playing Fields lifted the access lid during the flooding, leaving an exposed manhole. (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Stoney Royd Lane, Todmorden",England,"A culvert in Stoney Road (sic) Playing Fields lifted the access lid during the flooding, leaving an exposed manhole. (p30)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7383924,-2.0138275,"<div id=""html_b2224058b585199fe54991b2f53fbe02"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Palace House Road, Hebden Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hillside runoff and surface&ndash;water flows were channelled down Palace House Road, quickly overwhelming local diversion efforts and contributing to localised flooding and damage from fast&ndash;moving water and transported debris. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Palace House Road, Hebden Bridge",England,"Hillside runoff and surface–water flows were channelled down Palace House Road, quickly overwhelming local diversion efforts and contributing to localised flooding and damage from fast–moving water and transported debris. (p33)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
