GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7179739,-1.8652527,"<div id=""html_d64ad99fb1aa18f4d240594c8aaa03c3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Savile Road, Halifax</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred along Saville Road due to a series of blocked drains, causing flooding on the roadway and likely affecting adjacent properties. (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Savile Road, Halifax",England,"Surface water flooding occurred along Saville Road due to a series of blocked drains, causing flooding on the roadway and likely affecting adjacent properties. (p41)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7076496,-1.8908903,"<div id=""html_13fbd8870503c54bede665b29cc3611a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Copley Valley Road, Calderdale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties along Copley Valley Road experienced flooding caused by blocked drains and local topographic lows where water ponded, leading to inundation of property curtilages and access. (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Copley Valley Road, Calderdale",England,"Properties along Copley Valley Road experienced flooding caused by blocked drains and local topographic lows where water ponded, leading to inundation of property curtilages and access. (p41)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.6896121,-1.83952,"<div id=""html_62b1e7feec52b4f1e5f1482001a534e6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Park Road, Elland</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Park Road suffered internal flooding. Prolonged heavy rain saturated slopes causing a landslip that extended into the carriageway (~50m) and led to subsequent cracks (50&ndash;70mm). The road, footpath and downhill towpath were fully closed for 6&ndash;12 months, significantly disrupting travel. [PAG] (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant localised flooding began around 10:30am and was slow to recede (reported around 19:30), with reports of front doors buckling and main roads closed due to floodwater. (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The park on Park Road had a drainage system that was blocked and overgrown as a result of the flood and was reported to need testing, clearing and repairs during recovery actions after the 9 February 2020 flood. [TAB] (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Park Road (Elland) was impacted by significant flooding on 9th February 2020 from the interaction of fluvial (river) flows, canal influence and surface water; additional runoff from the hillside contributed and the existing drainage network lacked available capacity (issues noted with surface water culverts and the Park Road pumping station requiring confirmation). [TAB] (p53)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,"Park Road, Elland",England,"Residential properties on Park Road suffered internal flooding. Prolonged heavy rain saturated slopes causing a landslip that extended into the carriageway (~50m) and led to subsequent cracks (50–70mm). The road, footpath and downhill towpath were fully closed for 6–12 months, significantly disrupting travel. [PAG] (p42)
Significant localised flooding began around 10:30am and was slow to recede (reported around 19:30), with reports of front doors buckling and main roads closed due to floodwater. (p50)
The park on Park Road had a drainage system that was blocked and overgrown as a result of the flood and was reported to need testing, clearing and repairs during recovery actions after the 9 February 2020 flood. [TAB] (p51)
Park Road (Elland) was impacted by significant flooding on 9th February 2020 from the interaction of fluvial (river) flows, canal influence and surface water; additional runoff from the hillside contributed and the existing drainage network lacked available capacity (issues noted with surface water culverts and the Park Road pumping station requiring confirmation). [TAB] (p53)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
