GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7213147,-1.9436553,"<div id=""html_7ea240e7b64adb2a023925d6a099003d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Luddenden Foot</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced river flooding on 9 February 2020 when river levels rose rapidly following intense, localised rainfall (Storm Ciara); identified in the report as a local flood hotspot. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding of the River Calder at Luddenden Foot during the Storm Ciara event on 9th February 2020 resulted in property flooding and contributed to wider damage to infrastructure (roads, bridges) in Luddenden, which is listed among the areas that experienced mass property and infrastructural damage. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The figure caption and mapped flood outline indicate Luddenden Foot experienced recorded flooding associated with the same event. [IMG,PAG] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water overwhelmed road gullies causing roads (Butts Green Road / Luddenden Lane near Burnley Road) to become impassable and leading to internal flooding of buildings around the junction. (p39)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Luddenden Foot,England,"Experienced river flooding on 9 February 2020 when river levels rose rapidly following intense, localised rainfall (Storm Ciara); identified in the report as a local flood hotspot. (p3)
Flooding of the River Calder at Luddenden Foot during the Storm Ciara event on 9th February 2020 resulted in property flooding and contributed to wider damage to infrastructure (roads, bridges) in Luddenden, which is listed among the areas that experienced mass property and infrastructural damage. (p8)
