GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.70650352385996,-1.913490708316717,"<div id=""html_3ab585549a713752916caf9cd5ee64cd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sowerby Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced river flooding on 9 February 2020 when river levels rose rapidly following intense, localised rainfall (Storm Ciara); identified in the report as a local flood hotspot. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding at the River Calder / River Ryburn confluence during Storm Ciara led to property flooding and damage to local infrastructure and transport links in Sowerby Bridge. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced fluvial flooding associated with the River Calder / River Ryburn (confluence) during the February 2020 storm and was listed among areas with mass property and infrastructure damage. [IMG,PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River stage recorded at the Calder gauge near Sowerby Bridge rose during the 9 February 2020 event and reached peak levels around midday, as part of the River Calder hydrograph response. [IMG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Sowerby Bridge gauge recorded a high river level, indicating river flooding at Sowerby Bridge during the event. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency recorded flood outline and property points indicate properties in Sowerby Bridge were affected by river (fluvial) flooding during the February 2020 Storm Ciara event; flood extents follow the river corridor and coincide with clusters of affected properties. [IMG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding incidents concentrated in the town centre around the confluence of the River Calder and River Ryburn; recorded incidents affected properties and transport routes (fluvial and surface&ndash;water mechanisms). [IMG,PAG] (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding concentrated in the town centre around the confluence of the River Calder and River Ryburn. Businesses (notably on West Street, Walton Street, Water Street, Station Road and Victoria Road) and residential properties were flooded; blocked drainage and culverts contributed to localised surface water and sewer&ndash;related flooding. Cellar flooding and localised landslip impacts were also recorded. [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding concentrated around the river confluence (River Calder and River Ryburn) inundated the town centre and adjacent low&ndash;lying areas. Many businesses on West Street, Walton Street, Water Street, Station Road and Victoria Road were flooded. Blocked drainage caused flooding along Borland Road and external flooding of properties in Triangle; surface water and debris in fields blocked a culvert. Cellars of several houses along Hill Top Road were flooded. Minor landslips occurred at the rear of properties in Mill Bank. [PAG,IMG,MUL] (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued flood warnings for the River Calder and River Ryburn at Sowerby Bridge on 9 February 2020, identifying risk of river flooding to the town, adjacent low&ndash;lying land and transport routes. [TAB,PAG] (p47)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Yorkshire Water Services recorded reports of flooding in Sowerby Bridge during the storm event; incidents included reports attributed to overloaded sewer systems. (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from a blocked culvert led to flooding across the railway lines between Sowerby Bridge Tunnel and Luddenden Foot, causing rail service disruption. Sowerby Bridge was also listed as a location where a Flood Hub was opened to support affected residents. [IMG,PAG] (p50)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>132 business properties; 76 residential properties [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>132 business properties; 76 residential properties [PAG,IMG,MUL] (p42)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Sowerby Bridge,England,"Experienced river flooding on 9 February 2020 when river levels rose rapidly following intense, localised rainfall (Storm Ciara); identified in the report as a local flood hotspot. (p3)
Flooding at the River Calder / River Ryburn confluence during Storm Ciara led to property flooding and damage to local infrastructure and transport links in Sowerby Bridge. [PAG] (p8)
Experienced fluvial flooding associated with the River Calder / River Ryburn (confluence) during the February 2020 storm and was listed among areas with mass property and infrastructure damage. [IMG,PAG] (p9)
River stage recorded at the Calder gauge near Sowerby Bridge rose during the 9 February 2020 event and reached peak levels around midday, as part of the River Calder hydrograph response. [IMG] (p25)
The Sowerby Bridge gauge recorded a high river level, indicating river flooding at Sowerby Bridge during the event. [TAB] (p27)
Environment Agency recorded flood outline and property points indicate properties in Sowerby Bridge were affected by river (fluvial) flooding during the February 2020 Storm Ciara event; flood extents follow the river corridor and coincide with clusters of affected properties. [IMG] (p30)
Flooding incidents concentrated in the town centre around the confluence of the River Calder and River Ryburn; recorded incidents affected properties and transport routes (fluvial and surface–water mechanisms). [IMG,PAG] (p40)
Flooding concentrated in the town centre around the confluence of the River Calder and River Ryburn. Businesses (notably on West Street, Walton Street, Water Street, Station Road and Victoria Road) and residential properties were flooded; blocked drainage and culverts contributed to localised surface water and sewer–related flooding. Cellar flooding and localised landslip impacts were also recorded. [IMG,PAG] (p41)
Flooding concentrated around the river confluence (River Calder and River Ryburn) inundated the town centre and adjacent low–lying areas. Many businesses on West Street, Walton Street, Water Street, Station Road and Victoria Road were flooded. Blocked drainage caused flooding along Borland Road and external flooding of properties in Triangle; surface water and debris in fields blocked a culvert. Cellars of several houses along Hill Top Road were flooded. Minor landslips occurred at the rear of properties in Mill Bank. [PAG,IMG,MUL] (p42)
Environment Agency issued flood warnings for the River Calder and River Ryburn at Sowerby Bridge on 9 February 2020, identifying risk of river flooding to the town, adjacent low–lying land and transport routes. [TAB,PAG] (p47)
