GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.698794294419834,-1.8731993134228975,"<div id=""html_6bd09f672dd93fb125b6f47fdfbfaed7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Copley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced river flooding on 9 February 2020 when river levels rose rapidly following intense, localised rainfall (Storm Ciara); identified in the report as a local flood hotspot. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Copley Bridge gauge on the River Calder recorded a high flood peak during the 9 February 2020 event, showing one of the larger recorded river levels on that day. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued a flood warning for the River Calder at Copley (and for the reach between Sowerby Bridge and Copley) on 9 February 2020, indicating river flooding risk to Copley and adjacent areas. [TAB,PAG] (p47)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Copley,England,"Experienced river flooding on 9 February 2020 when river levels rose rapidly following intense, localised rainfall (Storm Ciara); identified in the report as a local flood hotspot. (p3)
The Copley Bridge gauge on the River Calder recorded a high flood peak during the 9 February 2020 event, showing one of the larger recorded river levels on that day. [TAB] (p27)
Environment Agency issued a flood warning for the River Calder at Copley (and for the reach between Sowerby Bridge and Copley) on 9 February 2020, indicating river flooding risk to Copley and adjacent areas. [TAB,PAG] (p47)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.6858377,-1.8377141,"<div id=""html_0a331a92e31dbcc4c591194889bc8376"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Elland</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Elland experienced flooding during Storm Ciara that contributed to mass property and infrastructure damage across the Calder Valley, with residential and business properties flooded and damage to roads and other infrastructure. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed among the towns that experienced mass property and infrastructural damage during the February 2020 storm; significant numbers of residential and business properties were flooded and major infrastructure (roads and bridges) were seriously damaged in the Calder Valley. [IMG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Elland gauge recorded a significant flood peak and associated high flow during the 9 February 2020 event. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial (river) flooding associated with the River Calder produced mapped clusters of flooded properties in the Elland and Greetland ward group (flooding recorded as internal and/or external). The Elland gauge record shows the event was significant in the gauge record. [IMG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in the Elland area contributed to increased surface water volumes and local road closures; the broader area saw internal flooding of residential properties and overwhelmed drainage infrastructure. [PAG] (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Elland experienced combined&ndash;source flooding (fluvial, canal breaches, surface water, blocked gullies, sewer overflows and hillslope runoff). Residential properties around Park Road suffered internal flooding. Large volumes of surface water were reported at Stainland Road, Long Heys, Hammerstones Leach Lane, Crestfield Crescent and South Lane. A culvert on Stainland Road was blocked causing water to back up, and drains on Gosport Lane and Gosport Close were overwhelmed. Elland Bridge channel was partially blocked by a 13m shipping container which reduced the bridge opening by 7%, increasing surface water volumes and causing road closures from further bank overtopping. [PAG,IMG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued flood warnings for the River Calder at Elland on 9 February 2020 (covers sections from Saddleworth Road to Lowfields Business Park and North Dean Business Park to Park Road), indicating river flooding risk to Elland and nearby business parks and roads. [TAB,PAG] (p47)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Elland Lock (canal) experienced bank overtopping due to inundation from a flooded towpath; canal water inundation was reported around the lock and dam gates were opened to release water but refilled after reclosure. [PAG] (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Park Road, Elland experienced significant localised flooding from about 10:30 on 9 February 2020. Water was slow to recede (reported around 19:30), some front doors were buckling and main roads were closed. (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Canal towpath in Elland remained covered by silt and sludge following the flood; the park on Park Road (Elland) had a drainage system that was reportedly blocked and overgrown and required testing, clearing and repair after the 9 February 2020 flood. (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas of Elland (notably Park Lane/Park Road) suffered significant flooding on 9th February 2020 due to interacting fluvial, canal and surface water sources, with additional surface runoff from the hillside contributing to impacts. [TAB] (p53)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>return period 35&ndash;40 years; ranking 3 in 50&ndash;year gauge record [IMG] (p29)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Elland,England,"Elland experienced flooding during Storm Ciara that contributed to mass property and infrastructure damage across the Calder Valley, with residential and business properties flooded and damage to roads and other infrastructure. [PAG] (p8)
Listed among the towns that experienced mass property and infrastructural damage during the February 2020 storm; significant numbers of residential and business properties were flooded and major infrastructure (roads and bridges) were seriously damaged in the Calder Valley. [IMG] (p9)
The Elland gauge recorded a significant flood peak and associated high flow during the 9 February 2020 event. [TAB] (p27)
Fluvial (river) flooding associated with the River Calder produced mapped clusters of flooded properties in the Elland and Greetland ward group (flooding recorded as internal and/or external). The Elland gauge record shows the event was significant in the gauge record. [IMG] (p29)
Flooding in the Elland area contributed to increased surface water volumes and local road closures; the broader area saw internal flooding of residential properties and overwhelmed drainage infrastructure. [PAG] (p42)
Elland experienced combined–source flooding (fluvial, canal breaches, surface water, blocked gullies, sewer overflows and hillslope runoff). Residential properties around Park Road suffered internal flooding. Large volumes of surface water were reported at Stainland Road, Long Heys, Hammerstones Leach Lane, Crestfield Crescent and South Lane. A culvert on Stainland Road was blocked causing water to back up, and drains on Gosport Lane and Gosport Close were overwhelmed. Elland Bridge channel was partially blocked by a 13m shipping container which reduced the bridge opening by 7%, increasing surface water volumes and causing road closures from further bank overtopping. [PAG,IMG] (p43)
Environment Agency issued flood warnings for the River Calder at Elland on 9 February 2020 (covers sections from Saddleworth Road to Lowfields Business Park and North Dean Business Park to Park Road), indicating river flooding risk to Elland and nearby business parks and roads. [TAB,PAG] (p47)
Elland Lock (canal) experienced bank overtopping due to inundation from a flooded towpath; canal water inundation was reported around the lock and dam gates were opened to release water but refilled after reclosure. [PAG] (p48)
Park Road, Elland experienced significant localised flooding from about 10:30 on 9 February 2020. Water was slow to recede (reported around 19:30), some front doors were buckling and main roads were closed. (p50)
Canal towpath in Elland remained covered by silt and sludge following the flood; the park on Park Road (Elland) had a drainage system that was reportedly blocked and overgrown and required testing, clearing and repair after the 9 February 2020 flood. (p51)
Areas of Elland (notably Park Lane/Park Road) suffered significant flooding on 9th February 2020 due to interacting fluvial, canal and surface water sources, with additional surface runoff from the hillside contributing to impacts. [TAB] (p53)",return period 35–40 years; ranking 3 in 50–year gauge record [IMG] (p29),GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.722936279096196,-1.8609622226534646,"<div id=""html_22aba580c6192de10ed150a3ae6e20a4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Halifax</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Halifax (Hebble Brook) gauge recorded a sharp rise in river stage during the 9 February 2020 event, peaking around midday and remaining elevated on the falling limb; this gauge showed the greatest deviation from the studied&ndash;event average. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Halifax (Hebble Brook) gauge recorded a flood peak of 1.55 m on 9 February 2020 (time of peak 11:30); this Feb 2020 level was the highest listed event at this gauge. [TAB,PAG] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The centre of Halifax experienced fluvial (river) and surface&ndash;water flooding, affecting both residential properties and businesses; cellar flooding was recorded in multiple properties (e.g. Parkinson Lane) and surface water affected roads such as Saville Road. [IMG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued a flood warning for Hebble Brook at Halifax (06:57) on 9 February 2020. [TAB] (p47)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Yorkshire Water recorded reports of flooding in Halifax associated with the 9th February 2020 storm event. [PAG] (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood&ndash;related incidents were reported from Halifax and attended by the local fire brigade during the event on 9 February 2020. (p50)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Halifax,England,"The Halifax (Hebble Brook) gauge recorded a sharp rise in river stage during the 9 February 2020 event, peaking around midday and remaining elevated on the falling limb; this gauge showed the greatest deviation from the studied–event average. [PAG,IMG] (p26)
The Halifax (Hebble Brook) gauge recorded a flood peak of 1.55 m on 9 February 2020 (time of peak 11:30); this Feb 2020 level was the highest listed event at this gauge. [TAB,PAG] (p27)
The centre of Halifax experienced fluvial (river) and surface–water flooding, affecting both residential properties and businesses; cellar flooding was recorded in multiple properties (e.g. Parkinson Lane) and surface water affected roads such as Saville Road. [IMG] (p41)
Environment Agency issued a flood warning for Hebble Brook at Halifax (06:57) on 9 February 2020. [TAB] (p47)
Yorkshire Water recorded reports of flooding in Halifax associated with the 9th February 2020 storm event. [PAG] (p48)
Flood–related incidents were reported from Halifax and attended by the local fire brigade during the event on 9 February 2020. (p50)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.72866600903454,-2.0526283024920056,"<div id=""html_837d3bf022a99382727f0d68429c0823"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Eastwood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>CMBC recorded clusters of flood incidents in Eastwood during the February 2020 event; flooding in this area was associated with fluvial overbanking and surface&ndash;water runoff driven by blocked/drained infrastructure, producing localised internal and external property flooding as shown on the incident maps. [PAG,IMG] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued flood warnings covering River Calder from Todmorden to Eastwood at 07:26 and River Calder at Eastwood at 08:21 on 9 February 2020. [TAB] (p47)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Eastwood,England,"CMBC recorded clusters of flood incidents in Eastwood during the February 2020 event; flooding in this area was associated with fluvial overbanking and surface–water runoff driven by blocked/drained infrastructure, producing localised internal and external property flooding as shown on the incident maps. [PAG,IMG] (p32)
Environment Agency issued flood warnings covering River Calder from Todmorden to Eastwood at 07:26 and River Calder at Eastwood at 08:21 on 9 February 2020. [TAB] (p47)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7447713,-2.066589,"<div id=""html_377cbba3de7f4ca03d6f9db81b99aa16"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Blackshaw Head</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Damage to bridleway paths caused by flood flows blocked residents' access to properties on Greenland Road and Blackshaw Head. [PAG] (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Blackshaw Head,England,Damage to bridleway paths caused by flood flows blocked residents' access to properties on Greenland Road and Blackshaw Head. [PAG] (p34),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.6730133,-1.9425882,"<div id=""html_c994387bac6d63b5433615492a839aeb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ripponden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The flow gauge at Ripponden (River Ryburn) recorded the 9 February 2020 event: river stage rose in the early hours and tributary peak levels were recorded between about 11:30 and 13:15, indicating a relatively fast catchment response (around 0.5 to 2.25 hours). [IMG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Ryburn at Ripponden reached a flood peak on 9 February 2020, reaching 1.26 m with a recorded flow of 34.8 m3/s at 13:00; the Feb 2020 peak is ranked 1 (highest) compared to the listed historical events. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding associated with the River Ryburn at Ripponden produced a significant gauge&ndash;record event and is linked to mapped clusters of flooded properties in the Ryburn and Ripponden ward group (flooding recorded as internal and/or external). [IMG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Majority of recorded flood incidents affected the highways in Ripponden. Flooding was caused by surface water and fluvial sources. [IMG] (p40)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>return period 60&ndash;65 years; ranking 1 in 40&ndash;year gauge record [IMG] (p29)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Ripponden,England,"The flow gauge at Ripponden (River Ryburn) recorded the 9 February 2020 event: river stage rose in the early hours and tributary peak levels were recorded between about 11:30 and 13:15, indicating a relatively fast catchment response (around 0.5 to 2.25 hours). [IMG] (p25)
The River Ryburn at Ripponden reached a flood peak on 9 February 2020, reaching 1.26 m with a recorded flow of 34.8 m3/s at 13:00; the Feb 2020 peak is ranked 1 (highest) compared to the listed historical events. [TAB] (p27)
Fluvial flooding associated with the River Ryburn at Ripponden produced a significant gauge–record event and is linked to mapped clusters of flooded properties in the Ryburn and Ripponden ward group (flooding recorded as internal and/or external). [IMG] (p29)
Majority of recorded flood incidents affected the highways in Ripponden. Flooding was caused by surface water and fluvial sources. [IMG] (p40)",return period 60–65 years; ranking 1 in 40–year gauge record [IMG] (p29),GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.712011,-2.1004282,"<div id=""html_a4d07d3cedb9177bec84b7125cde1264"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Salford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued a Flood Warning for 'Walsden Water at Todmorden from Shade to Salford' at 08:27 on 9 February 2020 as part of the Calder catchment warnings. [TAB] (p47)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Salford,England,Environment Agency issued a Flood Warning for 'Walsden Water at Todmorden from Shade to Salford' at 08:27 on 9 February 2020 as part of the Calder catchment warnings. [TAB] (p47),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.730164,-1.9607444,"<div id=""html_5e92ee5caaf2e5fe47aebd1847908ddc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brearley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Brearley gauge recorded elevated river levels showing river flooding at this location during the event. [TAB] (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Brearley,England,The Brearley gauge recorded elevated river levels showing river flooding at this location during the event. [TAB] (p27),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.72033716078477,-2.0953612423342483,"<div id=""html_b4088f1713f664a08a99834ec76ad73e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Meadow Bottom</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The area experienced flooding with minor structural damage to the exterior of a small number of properties and internal flooding to houses close to a bridle path (reported depth approximately 0.2 m). (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 0.2 m internal flooding (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Meadow Bottom,England,The area experienced flooding with minor structural damage to the exterior of a small number of properties and internal flooding to houses close to a bridle path (reported depth approximately 0.2 m). (p30),approximately 0.2 m internal flooding (p30),GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.72500776847426,-2.0919541955235914,"<div id=""html_cc761ea5171e01845e9b69dc1f0f904c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wickenberry</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The area experienced flooding with minor structural damage to the exterior of a small number of properties and internal flooding to houses close to a bridle path (reported depth approximately 0.2 m). (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 0.2 m internal flooding (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Wickenberry,England,The area experienced flooding with minor structural damage to the exterior of a small number of properties and internal flooding to houses close to a bridle path (reported depth approximately 0.2 m). (p30),approximately 0.2 m internal flooding (p30),GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7432258,-2.009967,"<div id=""html_8a2b5ff2817ca0b9064202dec6f36e93"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Birchcliffe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Torrential surface&ndash;water flows ran down Birchcliffe, overcoming resident flow&ndash;diversion efforts and causing flooding that resulted in damage to nearby residential properties and transport routes; debris and large rocks were carried in the flow. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Birchcliffe,England,"Torrential surface–water flows ran down Birchcliffe, overcoming resident flow–diversion efforts and causing flooding that resulted in damage to nearby residential properties and transport routes; debris and large rocks were carried in the flow. (p33)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.6967119,-1.9355672,"<div id=""html_52ce2f36bd188ceca6c8370005e71038"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Triangle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding affected properties in the Triangle area (surface water inundation of external areas around properties). (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Triangle,England,External flooding affected properties in the Triangle area (surface water inundation of external areas around properties). (p41),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.6887356,-1.9466079,"<div id=""html_2749275d09520d2c920acc104cc793ef"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mill Bank</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding caused minor landslips at the rear of properties in Mill Bank. (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Mill Bank,England,Flooding caused minor landslips at the rear of properties in Mill Bank. (p41),,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.6570084,-1.8733989,"<div id=""html_e62976e891a73d589cd7ae32e671bdbd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Outlane</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drains on Gosport Lane and Gosport Close were overwhelmed, causing surface water to flood the surrounding roads. [PAG] (p42)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Outlane,England,"Drains on Gosport Lane and Gosport Close were overwhelmed, causing surface water to flood the surrounding roads. [PAG] (p42)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.6877973,-1.8714477,"<div id=""html_d9ebdfac72f2b50aeff7d2f735e31d5f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Greetland</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping from Black and Holywell Brooks produced downhill surface&ndash;water flows along roads, causing minor damage to residential properties and forcing closure of a local school due to infrastructure damage. [PAG] (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Greetland,England,"Overtopping from Black and Holywell Brooks produced downhill surface–water flows along roads, causing minor damage to residential properties and forcing closure of a local school due to infrastructure damage. [PAG] (p44)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
GB-CLD,1,2020-02-09,53.7043341,-1.7958793,"<div id=""html_e2d2634cfdfeb66c800d2620dffd6eb2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brookfoot</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Environment Agency issued a flood warning for the River Calder at Brighouse &ndash; Brookfoot Business Park on 9 February 2020 as part of the Calder catchment flood event; the area was implicated in the river flooding affecting Brighouse. [TAB,PAG] (p47)</p></div></div></body></div>",Calderdale,Brookfoot,England,"The Environment Agency issued a flood warning for the River Calder at Brighouse – Brookfoot Business Park on 9 February 2020 as part of the Calder catchment flood event; the area was implicated in the river flooding affecting Brighouse. [TAB,PAG] (p47)",,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09.html,GB-CLD_1_2020-02-09,Calderdale flooding 09 Feb 2020,Section 19 Report: Flood Event 9th February 2020,020/Calderdale/020/2020/Calderdale/Item 5 App A - Flood Events of 9th February 2020 and 20th February 2022.pdf
