GB-LAN,9,2015-12-01,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_14947baf9d3440a65afac11d1e50767a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding hit the county in December 2015, affecting communities and revealing shortcomings in how flood messages were communicated; this prompted development of district&ndash;level reports to inform affected homeowners and businesses and identify opportunities for further investigation and investment. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding across the county in December 2015 with major impacts on communities, homes and businesses; emergency response and preparatory actions were carried out by risk management authorities to manage the event and support recovery. [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme storms and rainfall in November&ndash;December 2015 caused widespread flooding across the county: over 2,500 properties were flooded and flooding damaged private gardens, garages and out&ndash;buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges, retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings (schools, village and town halls). (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding affected communities across the county during two major storm events in December 2015; stage one of the countywide investigation identified all known communities that experienced flooding and stage two will report progress on recommended remedial actions. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property in Barnoldswick (Kelbrook Road area) suffered internal flooding on 26 December 2015. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties flooded [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [TAB] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Significant flooding hit the county in December 2015, affecting communities and revealing shortcomings in how flood messages were communicated; this prompted development of district–level reports to inform affected homeowners and businesses and identify opportunities for further investigation and investment. (p3)
Widespread flooding across the county in December 2015 with major impacts on communities, homes and businesses; emergency response and preparatory actions were carried out by risk management authorities to manage the event and support recovery. [TAB] (p8)
Extreme storms and rainfall in November–December 2015 caused widespread flooding across the county: over 2,500 properties were flooded and flooding damaged private gardens, garages and out–buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges, retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings (schools, village and town halls). (p9)
Widespread flooding affected communities across the county during two major storm events in December 2015; stage one of the countywide investigation identified all known communities that experienced flooding and stage two will report progress on recommended remedial actions. [PAG] (p10)
One property in Barnoldswick (Kelbrook Road area) suffered internal flooding on 26 December 2015. [TAB] (p14)","over 2,500 properties flooded [TAB] (p8)
over 2,500 properties (p9)
