GB-BNH,1,2023-06-20,50.8432088,-0.1510967,"<div id=""html_d66f626a2f92f6f74367be838760d0b3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Preston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding incidents in the Preston area that required attendance by East Sussex Fire & Rescue Service, affecting roads and nearby properties. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Brighton and Hove,Preston,England,"Flooding incidents in the Preston area that required attendance by East Sussex Fire & Rescue Service, affecting roads and nearby properties. (p15)",,GB-BNH_1_2023-06-20.html,GB-BNH_1_2023-06-20,Brighton and Hove flooding 20 Jun 2023,"FWMA Act S19 Flood Investigation Report, Brighton & Hove City Council",015/Brighton and Hove/015/2023/Brighton and Hove/FWMA Act S19 Flood Investigation with appendices.pdf
GB-BNH,1,2023-06-20,50.8634792,-0.1458904,"<div id=""html_aeff6a6563b2b71bdd486d5c219fe85a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Patcham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas recorded flood incidents during the June 2023 heavy&ndash;shower event; the report states most recorded incidents were located within Preston Park and Patcham. (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Brighton and Hove,Patcham,England,Areas recorded flood incidents during the June 2023 heavy–shower event; the report states most recorded incidents were located within Preston Park and Patcham. (p16),,GB-BNH_1_2023-06-20.html,GB-BNH_1_2023-06-20,Brighton and Hove flooding 20 Jun 2023,"FWMA Act S19 Flood Investigation Report, Brighton & Hove City Council",015/Brighton and Hove/015/2023/Brighton and Hove/FWMA Act S19 Flood Investigation with appendices.pdf
GB-BNH,1,2023-06-20,50.8597766,-0.13225,"<div id=""html_2091d6f42bc2de33c3b123bcc0275741"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hollingbury</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map annotations and analysis identify clusters of recorded flood incident pins in the northern parts of the authority (including Hollingbury) associated with the 20th June 2023 intense 1&ndash;hour rainfall, indicating localised surface&ndash;water flooding in these neighbourhoods. The report does not provide further site&ndash;specific impact details. [IMG] (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Brighton and Hove,Hollingbury,England,"Map annotations and analysis identify clusters of recorded flood incident pins in the northern parts of the authority (including Hollingbury) associated with the 20th June 2023 intense 1–hour rainfall, indicating localised surface–water flooding in these neighbourhoods. The report does not provide further site–specific impact details. [IMG] (p19)",,GB-BNH_1_2023-06-20.html,GB-BNH_1_2023-06-20,Brighton and Hove flooding 20 Jun 2023,"FWMA Act S19 Flood Investigation Report, Brighton & Hove City Council",015/Brighton and Hove/015/2023/Brighton and Hove/FWMA Act S19 Flood Investigation with appendices.pdf
GB-BNH,1,2023-06-20,50.823073531753735,-0.13968549330531355,"<div id=""html_ef45cfd7b5cdf9d5768238464c43da96"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brighton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reports of surface water flooding affecting commercial and residential locations in Brighton during the flood event on 20 June 2023. [PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected the city on 20 June 2023 due to heavy rain and thunderstorms, with runoff following flow routes from the South Downs toward the sea along dry valleys and major roads. [PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>City&ndash;wide impacts from heavy rain and thunderstorms on 20 June 2023: homes and businesses flooded; supermarkets (Waitrose and Poundland on Western Road) experienced internal flooding/evacuation; flooding caused delays on roads including the A23 and A27; East Sussex Fire and Rescue Service attended multiple flood&ndash;related incidents. [TAB,PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple locations within Brighton experienced flooding during the June 2023 events; East Sussex Fire and Rescue Service attended several Brighton addresses on 23rd June 2023. Brighton and Hove Council correspondence indicates 11 reported incidents of flooding during the June 2023 event across the council area. [PAG,MUL] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense 1&ndash;hour rainfall on 20 June 2023 caused surface&ndash;water flooding across the Brighton and Hove authority area, with multiple recorded flood incidents concentrated in the city. The event (≈26.6&ndash;26.8 mm in 1 hour) was modelled as approximately a 150&ndash;year design rainfall, and the report locates the centroid of recorded incidents in the centre of the city. [IMG,PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas within Brighton experienced surface water flooding during the June 2023 event; residents reported blocked gullies and drainage issues and submitted incidents that led to the commissioned investigation. [PAG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced flooding in June 2023 that prompted a Section 19 investigation and led to flood&ndash;related call&ndash;outs (investigation and FOI request reference flooding in Brighton). (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced flooding on 20 June 2023; emergency services (ESFRS) attended multiple addresses in response to flood incidents. (p43)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 flood related incidents; 11 reported incidents of flooding [TAB,PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 reported incidents [PAG,MUL] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Brighton and Hove,Brighton,England,"Reports of surface water flooding affecting commercial and residential locations in Brighton during the flood event on 20 June 2023. [PAG] (p6)
Surface water flooding affected the city on 20 June 2023 due to heavy rain and thunderstorms, with runoff following flow routes from the South Downs toward the sea along dry valleys and major roads. [PAG] (p13)
City–wide impacts from heavy rain and thunderstorms on 20 June 2023: homes and businesses flooded; supermarkets (Waitrose and Poundland on Western Road) experienced internal flooding/evacuation; flooding caused delays on roads including the A23 and A27; East Sussex Fire and Rescue Service attended multiple flood–related incidents. [TAB,PAG] (p14)
Multiple locations within Brighton experienced flooding during the June 2023 events; East Sussex Fire and Rescue Service attended several Brighton addresses on 23rd June 2023. Brighton and Hove Council correspondence indicates 11 reported incidents of flooding during the June 2023 event across the council area. [PAG,MUL] (p15)
Intense 1–hour rainfall on 20 June 2023 caused surface–water flooding across the Brighton and Hove authority area, with multiple recorded flood incidents concentrated in the city. The event (≈26.6–26.8 mm in 1 hour) was modelled as approximately a 150–year design rainfall, and the report locates the centroid of recorded incidents in the centre of the city. [IMG,PAG] (p19)
Areas within Brighton experienced surface water flooding during the June 2023 event; residents reported blocked gullies and drainage issues and submitted incidents that led to the commissioned investigation. [PAG] (p20)
Experienced flooding in June 2023 that prompted a Section 19 investigation and led to flood–related call–outs (investigation and FOI request reference flooding in Brighton). (p41)
Experienced flooding on 20 June 2023; emergency services (ESFRS) attended multiple addresses in response to flood incidents. (p43)","18 flood related incidents; 11 reported incidents of flooding [TAB,PAG] (p14)
11 reported incidents [PAG,MUL] (p15)",GB-BNH_1_2023-06-20.html,GB-BNH_1_2023-06-20,Brighton and Hove flooding 20 Jun 2023,"FWMA Act S19 Flood Investigation Report, Brighton & Hove City Council",015/Brighton and Hove/015/2023/Brighton and Hove/FWMA Act S19 Flood Investigation with appendices.pdf
