GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.880685933289385,-2.7865186448461667,"<div id=""html_c4da44113565b579413c9930d89cd81d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>St Helens Church of England Primary School</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of the school as part of the Churchtown event when flood water entered buildings following runoff from Ainspool and a breach of an embankment along the River Wyre; surface water and sewer surcharging were significant contributors. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>58 properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,St Helens Church of England Primary School,England,Internal flooding of the school as part of the Churchtown event when flood water entered buildings following runoff from Ainspool and a breach of an embankment along the River Wyre; surface water and sewer surcharging were significant contributors. (p14),58 properties (p14),GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
