GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.881414754867706,-2.79305130407062,"<div id=""html_40eee6aff546b5d289b9a4165272f636"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ains Pool</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as the primary source of the flooding that led to internal flooding of properties in Churchtown on 5 December 2015. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>58 properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Ains Pool,England,Identified as the primary source of the flooding that led to internal flooding of properties in Churchtown on 5 December 2015. (p14),58 properties (p14),GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.9309171,-2.7685312,"<div id=""html_3c704d4f811acea4bde7627241f8408b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Wyre</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A breach of an embankment along the River Wyre contributed to the Churchtown flooding event, leading to internal flooding of properties and allowing river water to enter the public sewer network. [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as the main source of flooding that caused property flooding in Garstang and contributed to flooding elsewhere in the catchment; prompted inspections and maintenance by authorities following the December 2015 event. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Wyre fluvial flooding affected adjacent properties and contributed to downstream flooding (including caravans at Six Arches Caravan Park). [MUL] (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>58 properties [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 properties; 4 properties (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property; 6 caravans [MUL] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Wyre,England,"A breach of an embankment along the River Wyre contributed to the Churchtown flooding event, leading to internal flooding of properties and allowing river water to enter the public sewer network. [PAG] (p14)
