GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.8686953,-2.7085841,"<div id=""html_10f11d190f5e5f3e7820b0e5e035b0e5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Brock</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Breach of the River Brock embankment caused fluvial flooding; overflow crossed farmland and led to inundation of properties in St Michaels (Blackpool Road area and Rawcliffe Road area). [TAB] (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>27 properties; 5 residential properties [TAB] (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Brock,England,Breach of the River Brock embankment caused fluvial flooding; overflow crossed farmland and led to inundation of properties in St Michaels (Blackpool Road area and Rawcliffe Road area). [TAB] (p18),27 properties; 5 residential properties [TAB] (p18),GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.9116078,-2.7451765,"<div id=""html_8dd8058bc42106d137d4e6f80ac11723"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Eidsforth Lane, Barnacre</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two properties on Eidsforth Lane (Barnacre) suffered internal flooding on 5 December 2015; properties are adjacent to an unnamed ordinary watercourse, but the exact source of flooding is unclear. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Eidsforth Lane, Barnacre",England,"Two properties on Eidsforth Lane (Barnacre) suffered internal flooding on 5 December 2015; properties are adjacent to an unnamed ordinary watercourse, but the exact source of flooding is unclear. (p12)",2 properties (p12),GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.8851097,-2.7640777,"<div id=""html_f78bb5fe6c666d1085044d53e44684c0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Garstang Road, Catterall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property on the Garstang Road bypass suffered internal flooding (recorded at this location). (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Garstang Road, Catterall",England,One property on the Garstang Road bypass suffered internal flooding (recorded at this location). (p13),1 property (p13),GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.8991294,-2.7741019,"<div id=""html_b374183c8ad07d48a991956db5f6a951"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bridge Street, Garstang</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The majority of properties flooded in Garstang were located on Bridge Street, affecting residential and commercial premises. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Bridge Street, Garstang",England,"The majority of properties flooded in Garstang were located on Bridge Street, affecting residential and commercial premises. (p15)",,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.8617864,-2.8230653,"<div id=""html_957c4ae05754c6b96304d03131fcbed9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Blackpool Road, St Michael's-On-Wyre</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding following a breach of the River Brock embankment flooded properties in the Blackpool Road (A586) area, including a school and a memorial hall. A pumping operation lasting up to a week was required to clear water and the main road (A586 Blackpool Road) was closed for a number of days; floodwater reportedly crossed farmland before flooding properties. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>27 properties (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Blackpool Road, St Michael's-On-Wyre",England,"Fluvial flooding following a breach of the River Brock embankment flooded properties in the Blackpool Road (A586) area, including a school and a memorial hall. A pumping operation lasting up to a week was required to clear water and the main road (A586 Blackpool Road) was closed for a number of days; floodwater reportedly crossed farmland before flooding properties. (p18)",27 properties (p18),GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.8654538,-2.8271935,"<div id=""html_9adb723fd74982f7daef8088e516794b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rawcliffe Road, St Michael's-On-Wyre</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties in the Rawcliffe Road area caused by overland/surface water and associated sewer surcharging when outfalls were locked by high river levels. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 residential properties (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Rawcliffe Road, St Michael's-On-Wyre",England,Internal flooding of residential properties in the Rawcliffe Road area caused by overland/surface water and associated sewer surcharging when outfalls were locked by high river levels. (p19),5 residential properties (p19),GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_10b061792fd864668ba574a91df49e02"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding affected the county in December 2015, impacting communities and prompting review of communication and coordination between risk management authorities. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The December 2015 extreme rainfall and high river flows caused widespread flooding across the county, resulting in significant impacts on people, homes and businesses. [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme storms and rainfall in November and December 2015 caused widespread flooding across December 2015, damaging private gardens, garages and out&ndash;buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges, retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools, village and town halls. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple communities across the county experienced flooding during two major storm events in December 2015; these events prompted a countywide Section 19 investigation to identify and prioritise actions for affected communities and to report findings. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties flooded [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Significant flooding affected the county in December 2015, impacting communities and prompting review of communication and coordination between risk management authorities. [PAG] (p3)
The December 2015 extreme rainfall and high river flows caused widespread flooding across the county, resulting in significant impacts on people, homes and businesses. [TAB] (p8)
Extreme storms and rainfall in November and December 2015 caused widespread flooding across December 2015, damaging private gardens, garages and out–buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges, retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools, village and town halls. (p9)
Multiple communities across the county experienced flooding during two major storm events in December 2015; these events prompted a countywide Section 19 investigation to identify and prioritise actions for affected communities and to report findings. [PAG] (p10)","over 2,500 properties flooded [TAB] (p8)
over 2,500 properties (p9)",GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,54.6143136,-2.9420899,"<div id=""html_e42866334a4d591a54715129c09d3ea1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cumbria</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding in December 2015 affected communities across Lancashire; the event revealed weaknesses in how flood messages were communicated to affected communities and prompted the development of district&ndash;level reports to improve communication and coordination. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Cumbria,England,Significant flooding in December 2015 affected communities across Lancashire; the event revealed weaknesses in how flood messages were communicated to affected communities and prompted the development of district–level reports to improve communication and coordination. (p3),,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.47769049472794,-2.2435460795004105,"<div id=""html_eb730488a8c1e0b5188bded76cdcd250"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Greater Manchester</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The December 2015 flood event struck Lancashire, exposing gaps in communication and coordination; this event prompted Lancashire County Council to develop district&ndash;level reports for affected communities. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Greater Manchester,England,"The December 2015 flood event struck Lancashire, exposing gaps in communication and coordination; this event prompted Lancashire County Council to develop district–level reports for affected communities. (p3)",,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,29,2015-12-01,53.7271527,-2.7330066,"<div id=""html_fca14f4e3e74442da3c6d35634b1e0ad"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Ribble</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred in the district during the December 2015 events; multi&ndash;agency response supported affected residents and businesses and a recovery drop&ndash;in was held on 02 Feb 2016 to provide advice and gather eyewitness reports. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,South Ribble,England,Flooding occurred in the district during the December 2015 events; multi–agency response supported affected residents and businesses and a recovery drop–in was held on 02 Feb 2016 to provide advice and gather eyewitness reports. (p9),,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_29_2015-12-01,Wyre flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Wyre District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/wyre-final-report.pdf
