GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.25866753494731,-1.3359710404418947,"<div id=""html_9cdcaf8485aa5aaa7ca9685bb3f05423"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Erin Court</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Storm Babet recorded flood outline overlaps parts of the Erin Court development; those parts experienced flooding during the Oct 2023 event. The same area was also flooded by the River Doe Lea in June 2007 prior to development. [IMG,MUL] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of newer&ndash;build homes within the Erin Court housing development. [IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the woodland to the south flowed into the Erin Court development and internally flooded two newer&ndash;build homes near the end of Staveley Road. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed from woodland and Ditch 2 into the housing development, causing two newer&ndash;build homes to flood internally. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater storage and flow issues affected Erin Court: Ditch 1 passes through Erin Court and maintenance was requested to improve floodwater storage; blockages were reported within the drainage network at the Erin Court housing development (under construction), which has been investigated as a factor in local flooding and outflow into Erin Court. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential properties [IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential properties (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 homes [IMG] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Erin Court,England,"The Storm Babet recorded flood outline overlaps parts of the Erin Court development; those parts experienced flooding during the Oct 2023 event. The same area was 