GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.24188479830357,-1.420259981000257,"<div id=""html_2f4132c6a58c3eb7c2bf562dd05f4213"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tapton Business Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Non&ndash;residential properties on the industrial estate were flooded following the river overtopping and local flow routes. (p49)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 non&ndash;residential properties (in nearby industrial areas including Brimington Road and Holbeck Close) (p49)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Tapton Business Park,England,Non–residential properties on the industrial estate were flooded following the river overtopping and local flow routes. (p49),17 non–residential properties (in nearby industrial areas including Brimington Road and Holbeck Close) (p49),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.22805938067299,-1.422811267148807,"<div id=""html_c1e6f03bd39ef02dd16822e9aa21c48d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Alma Retail Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the central Chesterfield area that experienced internal flooding during Storm Babet; River Rother flows past the retail park. [PAG] (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area adjacent to the River Rother was within the Storm Babet flood outline and experienced flooding from the river during the event. [IMG,PAG] (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area adjacent to the River Hipper/River Rother corridors and within/near Flood Zone 3. The vicinity of Alma Retail Park was within the Flood Warning Area and was impacted by river flooding risk during the 19 Oct 2023 &ndash; 21 Oct 2023 event, exposing commercial premises and access routes to floodwaters. [IMG] (p52)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas around Alma Retail Park adjacent to the River Rother experienced internal flooding; included in the River Rother at Central Chesterfield flood warning issued on 20 Oct 2023. [IMG] (p53)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the A617 flowed onto Horns Bridge roundabout and south along the A61 (Derby Road), inundating Alma Retail Park and flooding businesses there. (p56)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Part of 49 homes and 30 businesses flooded in central Chesterfield [PAG] (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>four businesses (p56)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Alma Retail Park,England,"Part of the central Chesterfield area that experienced internal flooding during Storm Babet; River Rother flows past the retail park. [PAG] (p50)
