GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.232773,-1.4280857,"<div id=""html_6da8bcaa13e04ab2953055118c920645"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ravenside Retail Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the central Chesterfield area that experienced internal flooding during Storm Babet. (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Hipper passed south of Ravenside Retail Park and nine business units were internally flooded during the river flooding associated with Storm Babet. [IMG,PAG] (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Hipper overflowed its banks at Ravenside Retail Park, causing internal flooding to businesses. Watermarks show flood depths reaching approximately 0.8 m in one internally flooded business. Some buildings within the retail park avoided internal flooding because they were at higher elevation than other buildings in the park. [PAG] (p54)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Retail units at the retail park were internally flooded when the River Hipper overtopped its banks. Watermarks on an internally flooded business show flood depths of about 0.8 m. Some units remained dry because they are at higher ground within the park. [IMG,PAG] (p55)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Post&ndash;event inspections recorded collapsed banks, a missing flap valve from an outfall and sections of walls in poor condition linked to the flood event; riparian owners were notified to make repairs. [MUL] (p59)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Part of 49 homes and 30 businesses flooded in central Chesterfield (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 business units [IMG,PAG] (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 businesses; approx. 0.8m flood depth [PAG] (p54)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approx. 0.8 m internal depth [IMG,PAG] (p55)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Ravenside Retail Park,England,"Part of the central Chesterfield area that experienced internal flooding during Storm Babet. (p50)
River Hipper passed south of Ravenside Retail Park and nine business units were internally flooded during the river flooding associated with Storm Babet. [IMG,PAG] (p51)
The River Hipper overflowed its banks at Ravenside Retail Park, causing internal flooding to businesses. Watermarks show flood depths reaching approximately 0.8 m in one internally flooded business. Some buildings within the retail park avoided internal flooding because they were at higher elevation than other buildings in the park. [PAG] (p54)
Retail units at the retail park were internally flooded when the River Hipper overtopped its banks. Watermarks on an internally flooded business show flood depths of about 0.8 m. Some units remained dry because they are at higher ground within the park. [IMG,PAG] (p55)
Post–event inspections recorded collapsed banks, a missing flap valve from an outfall and sections of walls in poor condition linked to the flood event; riparian owners were notified to make repairs. [MUL] (p59)","Part of 49 homes and 30 businesses flooded in central Chesterfield (p50)
