The bridge was surcharged during the event; debris was caught in the bridge rails on both sides, indicating high flows and overtopping at the structure. [PAG,IMG] (p30)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2357638,-1.4383198,"<div id=""html_d0bf979e4c54a69a1b025d88f2d2cfa2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Bars Roundabout</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping of nearby watercourses caused river channel exceedance that led to the collapse of a riparian&ndash;owned brick wall adjacent to West Bars Roundabout. (p31)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one riparian brick wall (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,West Bars Roundabout,England,Overtopping of nearby watercourses caused river channel exceedance that led to the collapse of a riparian–owned brick wall adjacent to West Bars Roundabout. (p31),one riparian brick wall (p31),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.23980625240668,-1.420956294256167,"<div id=""html_fc646f80b9dec91a652973d479a5ffe9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tapton Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding progressed downstream to the Tapton Bridge area; investigations are ongoing into whether the bridge restricted flow and contributed to the extent of flooding. (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwaters reached down to Tapton Bridge during the event; investigations are ongoing into whether the bridge restricted river flow and contributed to the extent of flooding. [PAG,IMG] (p49)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Chesterfield Borough Council conducted post&ndash;event visits to examine Tapton Bridge's impact on flooding in the locality. (p50)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Tapton Bridge,England,"Flooding progressed downstream to the Tapton Bridge area; investigations are ongoing into whether the bridge restricted flow and contributed to the extent of flooding. (p48)
Floodwaters reached down to Tapton Bridge during the event; investigations are ongoing into whether the bridge restricted river flow and contributed to the extent of flooding. [PAG,IMG] (p49)
Chesterfield Borough Council conducted post–event visits to examine Tapton Bridge's impact on flooding in the locality. (p50)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.230455,-1.4225091,"<div id=""html_7c59772444231adf93769f4101c98788"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Horns Bridge Roundabout</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Located close to the River Hipper/River Rother flood corridors within Flood Zone 3 and inside the Flood Warning Area. The roundabout and immediate transport infrastructure were affected by river flooding during the 19 Oct 2023 &ndash; 21 Oct 2023 event, creating risk and likely disruption to traffic and access. [IMG] (p52)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Was located within the 'River Rother at Central Chesterfield' Flood Warning area issued on 20 October 2023 and is mapped as being within high surface&ndash;water flood risk adjacent to the River Rother; the roundabout and its immediate infrastructure were therefore exposed to flood risk during the 19&ndash;21 October 2023 event. [PAG,IMG] (p53)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>All arms of the roundabout were impassable due to flooding; watermarks on railings and signposts indicate flood depths reached about 0.5m. Flooding at the adjacent A617 low spot (beneath the railway) exceeded 0.5m and was caused by a combination of the River Rother overflowing, sewer surcharging and surface water. (p56)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced surcharging of the sewer/network and was identified as a location that may have contributed to local flooding during the storm; subject of consideration for capacity improvements. (p59)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>water depths about 0.5m (p56)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Horns Bridge Roundabout,England,"Located close to the River Hipper/River Rother flood corridors within Flood Zone 3 and inside the Flood Warning Area. The roundabout and immediate transport infrastructure were affected by river flooding during the 19 Oct 2023 – 21 Oct 2023 event, creating risk and likely disruption to traffic and access. [IMG] (p52)
Was located within the 'River Rother at Central Chesterfield' Flood Warning area issued on 20 October 2023 and is mapped as being within high surface–water flood risk adjacent to the River Rother; the roundabout and its immediate infrastructure were therefore exposed to flood risk during the 19–21 October 2023 event. [PAG,IMG] (p53)
All arms of the roundabout were impassable due to flooding; watermarks on railings and signposts indicate flood depths reached about 0.5m. Flooding at the adjacent A617 low spot (beneath the railway) exceeded 0.5m and was caused by a combination of the River Rother overflowing, sewer surcharging and surface water. (p56)
Experienced surcharging of the sewer/network and was identified as a location that may have contributed to local flooding during the storm; subject of consideration for capacity improvements. (p59)",water depths about 0.5m (p56),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2584979,-1.3404452,"<div id=""html_e7fcbafd25b192768eea0120822acc9f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Staveley Road, Poolsbrook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Staveley Road were included within the Storm Babet recorded flood outline and are adjacent to the area where residential properties suffered internal flooding; Ditch 1 passes beneath Staveley Road and connects local watercourses, contributing to flooding risk in this area. [IMG,PAG,MUL] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties located adjacent to the Staveley Road / Poolsbrook Crescent junction. [IMG,PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed downslope along Staveley Road to the low spot at the Staveley Road / Poolsbrook Crescent junction, causing internal flooding of adjacent properties; the sewer network discharged at the rear of No. 58 Staveley Road and contributed to property flooding. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed downslope along Staveley Road to the low spot at the Staveley Road / Poolsbrook Crescent junction, internally flooding properties. The sewer network also discharged at the rear of No. 58 Staveley Road and at the junction with Poolsbrook Crescent, contributing to flooding at and around Staveley Road. [PAG,IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A request for sandbags was received from one property on Staveley Road, indicating localised threat/occurrence of flooding at that property. (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (across Poolsbrook suffered internal flooding) [IMG,PAG,MUL] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties (part of the total of 6 residential and 1 non&ndash;residential properties) [IMG,PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 residential properties (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 residential properties (at Staveley Road next to the Staveley Road and Poolsbrook Crescent junction); part of the total of 6 residential and 1 non&ndash;residential property flooded across two streets [PAG,IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Staveley Road, Poolsbrook",England,"Parts of Staveley Road were included within the Storm Babet recorded flood outline and are adjacent to the area where residential properties suffered internal flooding; Ditch 1 passes beneath Staveley Road and connects local watercourses, contributing to flooding risk in this area. [IMG,PAG,MUL] (p4)
