GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2587855,-1.3367233,"<div id=""html_28826641c0df5687e4b6aa886aa65b1d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Grove, Poolsbrook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded flood outline from Storm Babet overlaps this street and adjacent parts of the Erin Court development, indicating inundation of the street and nearby properties from River Doe Lea and local surface&ndash;water/ditch flooding. [IMG] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"The Grove, Poolsbrook",England,"Recorded flood outline from Storm Babet overlaps this street and adjacent parts of the Erin Court development, indicating inundation of the street and nearby properties from River Doe Lea and local surface–water/ditch flooding. [IMG] (p5)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2559494,-1.3377516,"<div id=""html_593da0eaaf83027f410aa9f2b78c93c2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cottage Close, Poolsbrook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded Storm Babet flood outline overlaps Cottage Close and the Erin Court development, indicating inundation of the street and nearby properties from River Doe Lea and local drainage/ditch overflow. [IMG] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Cottage Close, Poolsbrook",England,"Recorded Storm Babet flood outline overlaps Cottage Close and the Erin Court development, indicating inundation of the street and nearby properties from River Doe Lea and local drainage/ditch overflow. [IMG] (p5)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2575123,-1.339795,"<div id=""html_ce3e168cc8dc9ccf101ddc2d58de20ed"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Poolsbrook Crescent, Poolsbrook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The low spot at the Staveley Road and Poolsbrook Crescent junction and surrounding area flooded; the sewer network discharged at the junction, contributing to the area&ndash;wide internal flooding. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding concentrated at the low spot at the Staveley Road and Poolsbrook Crescent junction. Floodwater flowed downslope into this low point, contributing to internal flooding of properties at the junction; the sewer network also discharged at the junction. [PAG,IMG] (p8)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties internally flooded at the low spot (part of the wider total of 6 residential and 1 non&ndash;residential properties across the area) [PAG,IMG] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Poolsbrook Crescent, Poolsbrook",England,"The low spot at the Staveley Road and Poolsbrook Crescent junction and surrounding area flooded; the sewer network discharged at the junction, contributing to the area–wide internal flooding. (p7)
Flooding concentrated at the low spot at the Staveley Road and Poolsbrook Crescent junction. Floodwater flowed downslope into this low point, contributing to internal flooding of properties at the junction; the sewer network also discharged at the junction. [PAG,IMG] (p8)","6 properties internally flooded at the low spot (part of the wider total of 6 residential and 1 non–residential properties across the area) [PAG,IMG] (p8)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2610473,-1.4288145,"<div id=""html_1d22d0d2cf16e976677a431ed302167e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Station Road, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ten residential properties suffered internal flooding in the Station Road area (Whittington Moor) as a result of Storm Babet. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ten residential properties suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet; properties are on the River Whitting floodplain and sat at a similar elevation to the top of the river bank, allowing river and surface water to inundate homes. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Station Road and the surrounding retail district were situated on the River Whitting floodplain; the report and mapped figures specifically identify the vicinity of Station Road as being within Flood Zone 3 and having a high chance of surface&ndash;water flooding. Properties here were flooded by river and surface&ndash;water flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties located on Station Road between the River Whitting bridge and the railway bridge during Storm Babet; properties fell within the River Whitting / Upper Rother flood alert/warning areas. [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the overtopped River Whitting inundated Station Road bridge and flowed westwards downslope along Station Road for approximately 300 m, accumulating at a low spot east of the railway bridge. This led to surface depths of around 30 cm at the low spot and internal flooding up to approximately 50 cm in at least one property; nine properties on Station Road suffered internal flooding (eight homes and one business). [IMG,PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater pooled at the low spot on Station Road reaching approximately 30 cm depth; internal flooding occurred in at least one nearby property (watermark indicating ~50 cm internal depth). A resident of one property made a sandbag request on 20 October. [PAG] (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 residential properties (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties (8 homes and 1 business) internally flooded [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties internally flooded on Station Road (8 homes and 1 business); ~300 m of Station Road inundated; ~30 cm surface depth at low spot; ~50 cm internal flooding depth recorded in one property [IMG,PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>~30 cm floodwater depth at road low spot; ~50 cm internal flood watermark on 1 property; 1 property made a sandbag request [PAG] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Station Road, Chesterfield",England,"Ten residential properties suffered internal flooding in the Station Road area (Whittington Moor) as a result of Storm Babet. (p9)
Ten residential properties suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet; properties are on the River Whitting floodplain and sat at a similar elevation to the top of the river bank, allowing river and surface water to inundate homes. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Station Road and the surrounding retail district were situated on the River Whitting floodplain; the report and mapped figures specifically identify the vicinity of Station Road as being within Flood Zone 3 and having a high chance of surface–water flooding. Properties here were flooded by river and surface–water flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p11)
Internal flooding of properties located on Station Road between the River Whitting bridge and the railway bridge during Storm Babet; properties fell within the River Whitting / Upper Rother flood alert/warning areas. [PAG,IMG] (p12)
Floodwater from the overtopped River Whitting inundated Station Road bridge and flowed westwards downslope along Station Road for approximately 300 m, accumulating at a low spot east of the railway bridge. This led to surface depths of around 30 cm at the low spot and internal flooding up to approximately 50 cm in at least one property; nine properties on Station Road suffered internal flooding (eight homes and one business). [IMG,PAG] (p13)
Floodwater pooled at the low spot on Station Road reaching approximately 30 cm depth; internal flooding occurred in at least one nearby property (watermark indicating ~50 cm internal depth). A resident of one property made a sandbag request on 20 October. [PAG] (p14)","10 residential properties (p9)
