GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2644401,-1.4292864,"<div id=""html_f742caaa5d15a5349d95d9e07f1f6a2a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whittington Way, Whittington Moor</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area around the intersection of Station Road and Whittington Way was the focus of Storm Babet flooding; nearby residential properties suffered internal flooding. The community sits on the River Whitting floodplain and properties are at similar elevation to the top of the river bank, contributing to inundation. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road and adjacent retail/residential properties lie within Flood Zone 3 along the River Whitting floodplain and are shown on mapping to have a high risk of surface water flooding. Properties adjacent to Whittington Way were within the flood warning area and exposed to both river inundation and surface water flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Whittington Way, Whittington Moor",England,"Area around the intersection of Station Road and Whittington Way was the focus of Storm Babet flooding; nearby residential properties suffered internal flooding. The community sits on the River Whitting floodplain and properties are at similar elevation to the top of the river bank, contributing to inundation. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Road and adjacent retail/residential properties lie within Flood Zone 3 along the River Whitting floodplain and are shown on mapping to have a high risk of surface water flooding. Properties adjacent to Whittington Way were within the flood warning area and exposed to both river inundation and surface water flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p11)","10 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p10)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2657785,-1.4273025,"<div id=""html_8b8238088e2bbd480a60db31cf626768"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whittington Hill, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Street and nearby properties sit within the Flood Zone 3 area along the River Whitting corridor and are indicated as having high surface water flood risk. They were exposed to river flooding and surface&ndash;water inundation during the event. [IMG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Whittington Hill, Chesterfield",England,Street and nearby properties sit within the Flood Zone 3 area along the River Whitting corridor and are indicated as having high surface water flood risk. They were exposed to river flooding and surface–water inundation during the event. [IMG] (p11),,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2629491,-1.4231733,"<div id=""html_e03682e457915cd1f242c17916fe7774"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whitting Valley Road, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Located adjacent to the River Whitting/Ridding Brook flood corridor within Flood Zone 3 and mapped as high surface water risk; properties and infrastructure on Whitting Valley Road were impacted by river and surface&ndash;water flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A business property located on the banks of the River Whitting (near the Station Road junction) was internally flooded during the Storm Babet event. [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 business property [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Whitting Valley Road, Chesterfield",England,"Located adjacent to the River Whitting/Ridding Brook flood corridor within Flood Zone 3 and mapped as high surface water risk; properties and infrastructure on Whitting Valley Road were impacted by river and surface–water flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p11)
A business property located on the banks of the River Whitting (near the Station Road junction) was internally flooded during the Storm Babet event. [PAG,IMG] (p12)","1 business property [PAG,IMG] (p12)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2465584,-1.4171123,"<div id=""html_8b4c57bd0fbc77e9515bb282f7adafd0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brimington Road, Tapton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Brimington Road lies adjacent to mapped Flood Zone 3 and within the broader flood warning area; adjacent commercial and residential properties were exposed to river flooding and high surface&ndash;water risk during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of non&ndash;residential properties on Brimington Road occurred as part of the Storm Babet event; the area flooded as floodwater tracked the River Rother through the community. [PAG,IMG] (p45)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Brimington Road lies adjacent to the River Rother and intersects mapped Flood Zone 2/3 and the Flood Warning Area on the provided map, indicating it was within or bordering the area affected by river flooding and at risk of inundation or disruption during Storm Babet. [IMG] (p46)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Storm Babet recorded flood outline overlaps Brimington Road on the map and high/medium surface&ndash;water risk zones are adjacent to the road, indicating the road was exposed to floodwater during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p47)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Non&ndash;residential properties in the industrial area around Brimington Road flooded as part of the localised impact from the River Rother. (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Non&ndash;residential properties on and around Brimington Road were flooded by flows from the River Rother during the event (industrial area inundation). [PAG,IMG] (p49)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 non&ndash;residential properties (on Crow Lane and Brimington Road) [PAG,IMG] (p45)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 non&ndash;residential properties (total shared with Holbeck Close) (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>part of 17 non&ndash;residential properties (combined total for Brimington Road and Holbeck Close) [PAG,IMG] (p49)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Brimington Road, Tapton",England,"Brimington Road lies adjacent to mapped Flood Zone 3 and within the broader flood warning area; adjacent commercial and residential properties were exposed to river flooding and high surface–water risk during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p11)
Internal flooding of non–residential properties on Brimington Road occurred as part of the Storm Babet event; the area flooded as floodwater tracked the River Rother through the community. [PAG,IMG] (p45)
Brimington Road lies adjacent to the River Rother and intersects mapped Flood Zone 2/3 and the Flood Warning Area on the provided map, indicating it was within or bordering the area affected by river flooding and at risk of inundation or disruption during Storm Babet. [IMG] (p46)
The Storm Babet recorded flood outline overlaps Brimington Road on the map and high/medium surface–water risk zones are adjacent to the road, indicating the road was exposed to floodwater during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p47)
Non–residential properties in the industrial area around Brimington Road flooded as part of the localised impact from the River Rother. (p48)
Non–residential properties on and around Brimington Road were flooded by flows from the River Rother during the event (industrial area inundation). [PAG,IMG] (p49)","17 non–residential properties (on Crow Lane and Brimington Road) [PAG,IMG] (p45)
17 non–residential properties (total shared with Holbeck Close) (p48)
part of 17 non–residential properties (combined total for Brimington Road and Holbeck Close) [PAG,IMG] (p49)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2675968,-1.4317121,"<div id=""html_382c1e0fdd5d2308b1846579ed83a93b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Holland Road, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Holland Road is shown adjacent to Flood Zone 3 along the River Whitting/Ridding Brook with properties in the vicinity mapped as high surface&ndash;water flood risk; adjacent commercial and residential properties were exposed to river and surface&ndash;water flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Holland Road, Chesterfield",England,"Holland Road is shown adjacent to Flood Zone 3 along the River Whitting/Ridding Brook with properties in the vicinity mapped as high surface–water flood risk; adjacent commercial and residential properties were exposed to river and surface–water flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p11)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.268316,-1.4319374,"<div id=""html_2dc2794d992637a4bc93dd7591984dc9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Prospect Road, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties and commercial buildings on Prospect Road (part of the retail district on the River Whitting floodplain) were inundated by river flooding from the River Whitting and by surface water flooding during the 19 Oct 2023 &ndash; 21 Oct 2023 event. The properties lie in Flood Zone 3 and are shown as high risk for surface water flooding on the Long Term Flood Risk Map. [IMG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Prospect Road, Chesterfield",England,Properties and commercial buildings on Prospect Road (part of the retail district on the River Whitting floodplain) were inundated by river flooding from the River Whitting and by surface water flooding during the 19 Oct 2023 – 21 Oct 2023 event. The properties lie in Flood Zone 3 and are shown as high risk for surface water flooding on the Long Term Flood Risk Map. [IMG] (p11),,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2605615,-1.4094117,"<div id=""html_62f1b711b116a80f436b720404bd9510"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Newbridge Lane, Tapton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties and buildings along Newbridge Lane (within the same retail/residential floodplain area adjacent to the River Whitting and Ridding Brook) were affected by river flooding and surface water flooding during the 19 Oct 2023 &ndash; 21 Oct 2023 event. The street and adjacent properties are located in Flood Zone 3 and are mapped as high risk for surface water flooding. [IMG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Newbridge Lane, Tapton",England,Properties and buildings along Newbridge Lane (within the same retail/residential floodplain area adjacent to the River Whitting and Ridding Brook) were affected by river flooding and surface water flooding during the 19 Oct 2023 – 21 Oct 2023 event. The street and adjacent properties are located in Flood Zone 3 and are mapped as high risk for surface water flooding. [IMG] (p11),,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2638107,-1.4250612,"<div id=""html_3290f9dc8599e4732c2934eb37523624"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whitting Valley Road, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A business located on the banks of the River Whitting near the Station Road junction was flooded when the River Whitting overtopped its east bank directly south of the Station Road bridge. [IMG] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 business internally flooded [IMG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Whitting Valley Road, Chesterfield",England,A business located on the banks of the River Whitting near the Station Road junction was flooded when the River Whitting overtopped its east bank directly south of the Station Road bridge. [IMG] (p13),1 business internally flooded [IMG] (p13),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2264468,-1.4877364,"<div id=""html_2015946906459d98df9abb4a3e17add6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Holymoor Road, Holymoorside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood outlines from Storm Babet recorded at or close to the road at watercourse crossings/low spots; flooding was associated with the local watercourses (River Hipper / unnamed ordinary watercourse) and occurred in proximity to the residential area where internal property flooding was recorded. [IMG] (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (Holymoorside internal flooding, community&ndash;wide) [IMG] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Holymoor Road, Holymoorside",England,Flood outlines from Storm Babet recorded at or close to the road at watercourse crossings/low spots; flooding was associated with the local watercourses (River Hipper / unnamed ordinary watercourse) and occurred in proximity to the residential area where internal property flooding was recorded. [IMG] (p15),"7 properties (Holymoorside internal flooding, community–wide) [IMG] (p15)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2181088,-1.4959208,"<div id=""html_65e3d2c951e86ea138cf7c9d6646f7f5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>New Road, Holymoorside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from Storm Babet was recorded near where an unnamed ordinary watercourse joins the River Hipper about 15 m south of New Road; flood outlines occur at nearby road crossings and low spots, affecting the immediate vicinity of New Road and nearby residences. [IMG,PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties along New Road lie within mapped flood zones adjacent to the River Hipper and were within the area where homes suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet; national mapping also indicates medium&ndash;high surface water flood risk for the internally flooded homes. [PAG,IMG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on New Road suffered internal flooding during the 19&ndash;21 Oct 2023 event. Mapping shows New Road intersects medium and high surface&ndash;water flood risk zones adjacent to the River Hipper. [PAG,IMG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway flooding was observed (video evidence on 20 Oct); floodwater entered properties on New Road at approximately 12:00 and receded by approximately 13:00. Two homes at the New Road / Loads Road junction were internally flooded from combined sources (river overtopping entering from the rear and Loads Road runoff entering from the front). [PAG] (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (Holymoorside internal flooding, community&ndash;wide) [IMG,PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties across the community (5 in Flood Zone 3; 2 in Flood Zone 1) [PAG,IMG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties at the New Road/Loads Road junction [PAG] (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"New Road, Holymoorside",England,"Flooding from Storm Babet was recorded near where an unnamed ordinary watercourse joins the River Hipper about 15 m south of New Road; flood outlines occur at nearby road crossings and low spots, affecting the immediate vicinity of New Road and nearby residences. [IMG,PAG] (p15)
Residential properties along New Road lie within mapped flood zones adjacent to the River Hipper and were within the area where homes suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet; national mapping also indicates medium–high surface water flood risk for the internally flooded homes. [PAG,IMG] (p16)
Residential properties on New Road suffered internal flooding during the 19–21 Oct 2023 event. Mapping shows New Road intersects medium and high surface–water flood risk zones adjacent to the River Hipper. [PAG,IMG] (p17)
Highway flooding was observed (video evidence on 20 Oct); floodwater entered properties on New Road at approximately 12:00 and receded by approximately 13:00. Two homes at the New Road / Loads Road junction were internally flooded from combined sources (river overtopping entering from the rear and Loads Road runoff entering from the front). [PAG] (p18)","7 properties (Holymoorside internal flooding, community–wide) [IMG,PAG] (p15)
7 properties across the community (5 in Flood Zone 3; 2 in Flood Zone 1) [PAG,IMG] (p16)
2 properties at the New Road/Loads Road junction [PAG] (p18)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.219091,-1.4997431,"<div id=""html_abdb4c0a2e06bbfa85893450019791f5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Gallery Lane, Holymoorside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storm Babet flood outlines are shown at several locations along watercourses near Gallery Lane, indicating inundation at or adjacent to the road where it intersects local watercourses and close to the flooded residential area. [IMG] (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (Holymoorside internal flooding, community&ndash;wide) [IMG] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Gallery Lane, Holymoorside",England,"Storm Babet flood outlines are shown at several locations along watercourses near Gallery Lane, indicating inundation at or adjacent to the road where it intersects local watercourses and close to the flooded residential area. [IMG] (p15)","7 properties (Holymoorside internal flooding, community–wide) [IMG] (p15)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2166411,-1.4989296,"<div id=""html_0e97bdea8d8e140e76a53c1a75516bd3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hill Lane, Holymoorside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood outlines from Storm Babet were recorded near watercourse crossings in the Holymoorside map area, with inundation at low spots close to Hill Lane and in the surrounding residential area. [IMG] (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (Holymoorside internal flooding, community&ndash;wide) [IMG] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Hill Lane, Holymoorside",England,"Flood outlines from Storm Babet were recorded near watercourse crossings in the Holymoorside map area, with inundation at low spots close to Hill Lane and in the surrounding residential area. [IMG] (p15)","7 properties (Holymoorside internal flooding, community–wide) [IMG] (p15)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2077679,-1.5206398,"<div id=""html_3485e5155c0d7e59c5745d86fdd2329a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Harewood Road, Holymoorside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storm Babet flood outlines are shown around watercourse intersections and near Old Mill Pond in the map area; Harewood Road is adjacent to these features and experienced inundation at/near road crossings and low spots, in proximity to the affected residential cluster. [IMG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Harewood Road lies adjacent to the River Hipper within Flood Zone 3 and the Environment Agency flood alert area. Flood zones and surface&ndash;water risk overlap residential properties nearby; the community suffered internal flooding of homes during Storm Babet, so the road corridor and adjacent properties were exposed to river flooding and surface&ndash;water flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (Holymoorside internal flooding, community&ndash;wide) [IMG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties flooded (community&ndash;wide); 5 of the 7 flooded homes are in Flood Zone 3 and 2 are in Flood Zone 1 [PAG,IMG] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Harewood Road, Holymoorside",England,"Storm Babet flood outlines are shown around watercourse intersections and near Old Mill Pond in the map area; Harewood Road is adjacent to these features and experienced inundation at/near road crossings and low spots, in proximity to the affected residential cluster. [IMG] (p15)
Harewood Road lies adjacent to the River Hipper within Flood Zone 3 and the Environment Agency flood alert area. Flood zones and surface–water risk overlap residential properties nearby; the community suffered internal flooding of homes during Storm Babet, so the road corridor and adjacent properties were exposed to river flooding and surface–water flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p16)","7 properties (Holymoorside internal flooding, community–wide) [IMG] (p15)
7 properties flooded (community–wide); 5 of the 7 flooded homes are in Flood Zone 3 and 2 are in Flood Zone 1 [PAG,IMG] (p16)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2184619,-1.492126,"<div id=""html_2d81fd115f64bc82213ccca59a24d670"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cotton Mill Hill, Holymoorside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties adjacent to the watercourse experienced internal flooding during Storm Babet. Flood Zone 3 coverage is mapped adjacent to Cotton Mill Hill indicating river flooding from the River Hipper, and national surface water mapping shows medium&ndash;high surface water flood risk for the internally flooded homes. [PAG,IMG] (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties across the community (5 in Flood Zone 3; 2 in Flood Zone 1) [PAG,IMG] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Cotton Mill Hill, Holymoorside",England,"Residential properties adjacent to the watercourse experienced internal flooding during Storm Babet. Flood Zone 3 coverage is mapped adjacent to Cotton Mill Hill indicating river flooding from the River Hipper, and national surface water mapping shows medium–high surface water flood risk for the internally flooded homes. [PAG,IMG] (p16)","7 properties across the community (5 in Flood Zone 3; 2 in Flood Zone 1) [PAG,IMG] (p16)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2192081,-1.4938868,"<div id=""html_4a7b303d3f894001a9055ac8aab75ce5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Alders, Holymoorside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on The Alders suffered internal flooding during the 19&ndash;21 Oct 2023 event (Storm Babet). (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on The Alders were flooded internally; properties were inundated from multiple sides due to River Hipper overtopping and floodwater pooling from Loads Road runoff adjacent to The Alders. [PAG] (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"The Alders, Holymoorside",England,"Residential properties on The Alders suffered internal flooding during the 19–21 Oct 2023 event (Storm Babet). (p17)
Residential properties on The Alders were flooded internally; properties were inundated from multiple sides due to River Hipper overtopping and floodwater pooling from Loads Road runoff adjacent to The Alders. [PAG] (p18)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2196648,-1.4948782,"<div id=""html_e90d7827dc4b635475ce5a4e3dcbdb2b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Loads Road, Holymoorside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Loads Road suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet; flooding was driven by exceptionally high River Hipper levels and overland/surface&ndash;water flow paths. No local flood defences protect Holymoorside. [PAG,IMG] (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 residential properties (across The Alders, New Road and Loads Road); 1 business also internally flooded [PAG,IMG] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Loads Road, Holymoorside",England,"Residential properties on Loads Road suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet; flooding was driven by exceptionally high River Hipper levels and overland/surface–water flow paths. No local flood defences protect Holymoorside. [PAG,IMG] (p17)","7 residential properties (across The Alders, New Road and Loads Road); 1 business also internally flooded [PAG,IMG] (p17)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2203686,-1.4983684,"<div id=""html_63f7069b1703177f10a400a9348107f7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Loads Road, Holymoorside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed eastwards along Loads Road and pooled at the low spot adjacent to The Alders at the Loads Road / New Road junction; this flow (from river overtopping upstream of Loads Road bridge and from runoff from agricultural land) led to internal flooding of properties on Loads Road and left significant soil and silt deposits on the carriageway. [PAG] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood water flowed eastwards along Loads Road and pooled at the low spot at the Loads Road / New Road junction. Water came from an ordinary watercourse that overtopped upstream of Loads Road bridge (bridge arches exceeded capacity) and from runoff from agricultural land upslope; anecdotal reports of debris impeding flow at the bridge were noted. This floodwater was the cause of internal flooding to properties at the junction and left significant soil and silt deposits on Loads Road. [PAG] (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties at the New Road/Loads Road junction [PAG] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties [PAG] (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Loads Road, Holymoorside",England,"Floodwater flowed eastwards along Loads Road and pooled at the low spot adjacent to The Alders at the Loads Road / New Road junction; this flow (from river overtopping upstream of Loads Road bridge and from runoff from agricultural land) led to internal flooding of properties on Loads Road and left significant soil and silt deposits on the carriageway. [PAG] (p18)
Flood water flowed eastwards along Loads Road and pooled at the low spot at the Loads Road / New Road junction. Water came from an ordinary watercourse that overtopped upstream of Loads Road bridge (bridge arches exceeded capacity) and from runoff from agricultural land upslope; anecdotal reports of debris impeding flow at the bridge were noted. This floodwater was the cause of internal flooding to properties at the junction and left significant soil and silt deposits on Loads Road. [PAG] (p19)","2 properties at the New Road/Loads Road junction [PAG] (p18)
2 properties [PAG] (p19)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2311418,-1.4621975,"<div id=""html_c4f5d301437afd5ee2ffa121e492feee"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chatsworth Road, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties near Chatsworth Road suffered internal flooding associated with the storm event; all flooded properties are within 75 m of the River Hipper. [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties near Chatsworth Road suffered internal flooding during the event; part of the main group of flooded properties that experienced internal flooding (18 properties in the local area). [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties in the Chatsworth Road West community. Flooding occurred to residential and commercial properties located on the floodplain of the River Hipper; flooded properties sit at similar elevation to the river top bank. [PAG,IMG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Eighteen properties in the Chatsworth Road West community (on Chatsworth Road, Walton Road, Chapel Lane West and Grove Cottages) suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet; all flooded properties were within 75 m of the River Hipper (eight on the north bank and ten on the south bank). [PAG,IMG] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from Chatsworth Road is understood to have contributed to flooding at Chapel Lane West. Properties on Chatsworth Road are listed among those that flooded internally during the event. [IMG,PAG] (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Chatsworth Road is identified on the map as within the highest flood&ndash;risk area adjacent to the River Hipper; it is therefore likely to have been affected by river and surface&ndash;water flooding, impacting adjacent business and residential areas. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of both residential and non&ndash;residential properties on Chatsworth Road as part of the Brampton inundation caused by high flows in the local watercourses. [TAB] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River floodwater joined Chatsworth Road via the surcharged Lidl culvert and flowed eastwards, pooling at a low spot near School Board Lane/Chatsworth Business Park and flooding properties opposite Bradbury Hall; flooding extended east as far as the Pizza Hut on the north side, with flood depths at the low spot reaching at least 0.5 m. [PAG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater on Chatsworth Road acted as the source of runoff that travelled downslope into Hipper Street West and Alma Street West. Properties at the west end of Chatsworth Road (near West Bars Roundabout) suffered internal flooding. [PAG] (p31)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties flooded (collective for Chatsworth Road and Walton Road): 17 residential semi&ndash;detached; 1 commercial; 8 on the Hipper north bank; 10 on the Hipper south bank [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties; 17 residential; 1 commercial [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 internally flooded properties; 17 residential (all semi&ndash;detached); 1 commercial; 11 properties in Flood Zone 2 [PAG,IMG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties; eight on north bank; ten on south bank [PAG,IMG] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties (total area&ndash;wide internal flooding across Chatsworth Road, Walton Road, Chapel Lane West and Grove Cottages) [IMG,PAG] (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>34 homes; 34 non&ndash;residential (78 properties total) [TAB] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depths at the School Board Lane/Chatsworth Business Park low spot reached at least 0.5m [PAG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>seven homes [PAG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Chatsworth Road, Chesterfield",England,"Properties near Chatsworth Road suffered internal flooding associated with the storm event; all flooded properties are within 75 m of the River Hipper. [PAG] (p19)
