GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2337975,-1.4451443,"<div id=""html_5e4aeab07d7c43d1847aa1c9baeaa64f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Elm Place, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping occurred downstream of the Lidl culvert by Elm Place, contributing to further flooding along Chatsworth Road and adjacent streets. [PAG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Elm Place, Chesterfield",England,"Overtopping occurred downstream of the Lidl culvert by Elm Place, contributing to further flooding along Chatsworth Road and adjacent streets. [PAG] (p30)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2337021,-1.4383542,"<div id=""html_a2d94f2615bc853261796b1656842158"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Dock Walk, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater collected at the low spot on Boythorpe Road by the Dock Walk junction causing internal flooding to a business; an electricity substation on the banks along Dock Walk is reported not to have flooded. (p31)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one business (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Dock Walk, Chesterfield",England,Floodwater collected at the low spot on Boythorpe Road by the Dock Walk junction causing internal flooding to a business; an electricity substation on the banks along Dock Walk is reported not to have flooded. (p31),one business (p31),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2327855,-1.4475078,"<div id=""html_65e9ded2891028c58d27e7a25600953e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Factory Street, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area adjacent to the River Hipper/Home Brook is mapped as Flood Zone 3; Factory Street is identified on the map as within the highest risk area where adjacent business and residential areas were exposed to flooding during the event. Nearby properties contributed to the community&#8217;s internally flooded totals during the 19&ndash;21 Oct 2023 event. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Factory Street is located within high/medium surface&ndash;water flood risk zones adjacent to the River Hipper and Holme Brook. During the 19 Oct 2023 &ndash; 21 Oct 2023 event the area around Factory Street (including nearby commercial premises such as Lidl and Chatsworth Business Park) was within the mapped high/medium surface water flood zones and experienced surface water inundation that contributed to local internal flooding in the community. [PAG,IMG] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a non&ndash;residential property recorded during the event. [TAB] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Inundated after the River Hipper overtopped; low spot at the entrance to Lidl on Factory Street was submerged (likely &gt;0.5m). A public house on Factory Street was internally flooded. Factory Street received flood flows from the overtopped river and low&ndash;lying geometry concentrated depths. [IMG,PAG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping of the River Hipper inundated a low spot on Factory Street, flooding the road and the Lidl car park; a public house on Factory Street was internally flooded. The low spot at the entrance to Lidl (on Factory Street) experienced flood depths likely exceeding 0.5 m. [PAG,IMG] (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 non&ndash;residential property [TAB] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 public house internally flooded; flood depth at Lidl entrance exceeded 0.5m [IMG,PAG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depth likely exceeded 0.5m at the entrance to Lidl (low spot on Factory Street) [PAG,IMG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Factory Street, Chesterfield",England,"Area adjacent to the River Hipper/Home Brook is mapped as Flood Zone 3; Factory Street is identified on the map as within the highest risk area where adjacent business and residential areas were exposed to flooding during the event. Nearby properties contributed to the community’s internally flooded totals during the 19–21 Oct 2023 event. [PAG,IMG] (p26)
