GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2340538,-1.4253454,"<div id=""html_9908f44e8904fb46f1f62ddba452f196"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hipper Street, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hipper Street (labelled on the map as Hipper Street West) lies adjacent to the River Hipper and is within mapped flood zones (Zones 2/3). The street/adjacent properties are in the area identified as higher flood risk and are likely to have been affected during the 19&ndash;21 Oct 2023 flooding event. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties recorded during the event. [TAB] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater travelled downslope along Hipper Street West from Chatsworth Road and rejoined the River Hipper, causing internal flooding to most homes; social media footage shows high&ndash;velocity flow and a car nearly submerged (about 0.4 m from full submersion), indicating depths likely exceeded 1 m and that conditions posed a danger to life. [PAG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater on Chatsworth Road travelled downslope along Hipper Street West before rejoining the River Hipper, causing internal flooding of most homes on Hipper Street West. Media footage and evidence show depths exceeding 0.5 m at the Hipper Street junction with Chatsworth Road and likely exceeded 1 m at the south end next to the River Hipper. High&ndash;velocity flows carried debris along the street, posing a danger to life. [PAG] (p31)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>26 homes [TAB] (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Hipper Street, Chesterfield",England,"Hipper Street (labelled on the map as Hipper Street West) lies adjacent to the River Hipper and is within mapped flood zones (Zones 2/3). The street/adjacent properties are in the area identified as higher flood risk and are likely to have been affected during the 19–21 Oct 2023 flooding event. [PAG,IMG] (p26)
Internal flooding of residential properties recorded during the event. [TAB] (p28)
Floodwater travelled downslope along Hipper Street West from Chatsworth Road and rejoined the River Hipper, causing internal flooding to most homes; social media footage shows high–velocity flow and a car nearly submerged (about 0.4 m from full submersion), indicating depths likely exceeded 1 m and that conditions posed a danger to life. [PAG] (p30)
Floodwater on Chatsworth Road travelled downslope along Hipper Street West before rejoining the River Hipper, causing internal flooding of most homes on Hipper Street West. Media footage and evidence show depths exceeding 0.5 m at the Hipper Street junction with Chatsworth Road and likely exceeded 1 m at the south end next to the River Hipper. High–velocity flows carried debris along the street, posing a danger to life. [PAG] (p31)",26 homes [TAB] (p28),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2367887,-1.4425167,"<div id=""html_370ecb002992c67347a0addc5055b190"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Charles Street, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Charles Street is included on the Brampton map within the spatial extent of Flood Zone 2 and near Flood Zone 3 and within flood alert/warning outlines. As such it is part of the area affected by river and surface&ndash;water flooding associated with the 19&ndash;21 Oct 2023 event; properties here lie in the Hipper / Holme Brook floodplain and were exposed to the flood hazard. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>192 properties internally flooded in the community; 137 homes; 55 businesses; 142 properties (73% of those flooded) had flooded previously. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Charles Street, Chesterfield",England,"Charles Street is included on the Brampton map within the spatial extent of Flood Zone 2 and near Flood Zone 3 and within flood alert/warning outlines. As such it is part of the area affected by river and surface–water flooding associated with the 19–21 Oct 2023 event; properties here lie in the Hipper / Holme Brook floodplain and were exposed to the flood hazard. [PAG,IMG] (p26)","192 properties internally flooded in the community; 137 homes; 55 businesses; 142 properties (73% of those flooded) had flooded previously. [PAG,IMG] (p26)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.237437,-1.4447935,"<div id=""html_cf7701e4b1fcc9a15b2f9bb0aad2e962"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clifton Street, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clifton Street is shown within the mapped Flood Zone 2/3 extent and overlapping flood alert/warning areas in Brampton, and therefore was within the area exposed to river and surface&ndash;water flooding during the 19&ndash;21 Oct 2023 event. Properties here are in the floodplain of the River Hipper / Holme Brook and were part of the mapped flood&ndash;affected area. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>192 properties internally flooded in the community; 137 homes; 55 businesses; 142 properties (73% of those flooded) had flooded previously. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Clifton Street, Chesterfield",England,"Clifton Street is shown within the mapped Flood Zone 2/3 extent and overlapping flood alert/warning areas in Brampton, and therefore was within the area exposed to river and surface–water flooding during the 19–21 Oct 2023 event. Properties here are in the floodplain of the River Hipper / Holme Brook and were part of the mapped flood–affected area. [PAG,IMG] (p26)","192 properties internally flooded in the community; 137 homes; 55 businesses; 142 properties (73% of those flooded) had flooded previously. [PAG,IMG] (p26)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2376095,-1.4484548,"<div id=""html_d4a4a66d4ef5030bc9358a63688283af"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Springfield Avenue, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map and flood&ndash;zone mapping in the report place Springfield Avenue inside the mapped floodplain/flood zone area for the community (overlapping Flood Zone 2 / Flood Zone 3 and Flood Alert/Warning outlines). As such the street and adjacent properties were exposed to river flooding from the River Hipper / Home Brook and to surface&ndash;water inundation during the event, contributing to local urban inundation and risk to nearby properties. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Springfield Avenue, Chesterfield",England,"Map and flood–zone mapping in the report place Springfield Avenue inside the mapped floodplain/flood zone area for the community (overlapping Flood Zone 2 / Flood Zone 3 and Flood Alert/Warning outlines). As such the street and adjacent properties were exposed to river flooding from the River Hipper / Home Brook and to surface–water inundation during the event, contributing to local urban inundation and risk to nearby properties. [PAG,IMG] (p26)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2389219,-1.4502718,"<div id=""html_83ea8016597b7a5f2fe15e331036623b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Old Hall Road, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Old Hall Road is shown within the mapped Brampton floodplain where Flood Zone 2 (and areas of Flood Zone 3 nearby) overlap streets and properties. The street and immediate surrounds were therefore exposed to river flooding from the River Hipper / Home Brook and to surface&ndash;water flooding during the 19&ndash;21 Oct 2023 event, placing adjacent properties at risk of inundation. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Old Hall Road, Chesterfield",England,"Old Hall Road is shown within the mapped Brampton floodplain where Flood Zone 2 (and areas of Flood Zone 3 nearby) overlap streets and properties. The street and immediate surrounds were therefore exposed to river flooding from the River Hipper / Home Brook and to surface–water flooding during the 19–21 Oct 2023 event, placing adjacent properties at risk of inundation. [PAG,IMG] (p26)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2577648,-1.3948115,"<div id=""html_970e589258ed9e7c82c0691a4c7c891c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Foljambe Road, Tapton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Foljambe Road is mapped within the Brampton floodplain area where Flood Zone 2 and Flood Zone 3 extents and Flood Alert/Warning outlines intersect streets and properties. The road and nearby properties were therefore exposed to river flooding from the River Hipper / Home Brook and to surface&ndash;water inundation during the 19&ndash;21 Oct 2023 event, contributing to local property flood risk. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Foljambe Road, Tapton",England,"Foljambe Road is mapped within the Brampton floodplain area where Flood Zone 2 and Flood Zone 3 extents and Flood Alert/Warning outlines intersect streets and properties. The road and nearby properties were therefore exposed to river flooding from the River Hipper / Home Brook and to surface–water inundation during the 19–21 Oct 2023 event, contributing to local property flood risk. [PAG,IMG] (p26)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
