GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.29507273600813,-1.3234390336744752,"<div id=""html_bbeb3aac7400ff87e7c382627bfc151a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sheffield Road, Renishaw</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood outlines from Storm Babet are recorded at the intersection of Sheffield Road with Smithy Brook Road, inundating areas adjacent to the watercourse and affecting nearby residential clusters. [IMG] (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded Storm Babet flood extents and Flood Zone 3 extend into the built&ndash;up area near Sheffield Road, indicating residential properties in this area were affected by the event and adjacent watercourse flooding. [PAG,IMG] (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Smithy Brook floodwater was shown to join Sheffield Road; internal flooding on Sheffield Road was reported with internal depths noted between 0.2m and 0.8m. (p41)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>39 properties [PAG,IMG] (p39)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Sheffield Road, Renishaw",England,"Flood outlines from Storm Babet are recorded at the intersection of Sheffield Road with Smithy Brook Road, inundating areas adjacent to the watercourse and affecting nearby residential clusters. [IMG] (p38)
Recorded Storm Babet flood extents and Flood Zone 3 extend into the built–up area near Sheffield Road, indicating residential properties in this area were affected by the event and adjacent watercourse flooding. [PAG,IMG] (p39)
Smithy Brook floodwater was shown to join Sheffield Road; internal flooding on Sheffield Road was reported with internal depths noted between 0.2m and 0.8m. (p41)","39 properties [PAG,IMG] (p39)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2904705,-1.3227157,"<div id=""html_42b61c21192fd8c1c8f88d8d383815fc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Emmett Carr Lane, Renishaw</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood outlines are concentrated along Emmett Carr Lane; flooding there was spatially associated with inundation of adjacent residential properties during Storm Babet. [IMG] (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Emmett Carr Brook flows parallel to Emmet Carr Lane and the highest flood risk (Flood Zone 3) and Storm Babet recorded flood extents are concentrated near Emmet Carr Lane; flooding along Emmett Carr Brook contributed to internal flooding of nearby properties. [PAG,IMG] (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding was recorded in the area during Storm Babet; the recorded flood outline is concentrated near Emmett Carr Lane and high surface water flood risk is mapped adjacent to Emmett Carr Brook. [IMG] (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant internal flooding of residential properties on Emmett Carr Lane associated with overtopping/overflow at the Emmett Carr Brook culvert inlet and Smithy Brook interactions; at least one property on Emmett Carr Lane experienced up to 1.2 m internal flood depth. [TAB] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping and flow routed along roads caused internal flooding of properties on Emmett Carr Lane; floodwater collected at a low spot ~50 m south of the Main Road/Emmett Carr Lane junction. (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed southwards along the lane to a low spot ~50 m south of the Main Road junction, resulting in internal flooding of properties. Eighteen homes on this street were flooded. Multiple properties also reported sewer flooding on this street during the event. Runoff from agricultural land and overwhelmed culverts contributed to flows along the lane. [PAG] (p43)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>39 properties (village&ndash;wide) [IMG] (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>39 properties [PAG,IMG] (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 homes [TAB] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 homes (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 homes [PAG] (p43)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Emmett Carr Lane, Renishaw",England,"Flood outlines are concentrated along Emmett Carr Lane; flooding there was spatially associated with inundation of adjacent residential properties during Storm Babet. [IMG] (p38)
