six homes (p42)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2948553,-1.3247869,"<div id=""html_6799aca2f879e123d6a4fcbf2807f954"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Abbey Place, Renishaw</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties in Abbey Place as part of the Renishaw event. Flooding was driven by overtopping of Smithy Brook at its culvert inlet and exacerbated by culvert blockages; Renishaw&ndash;wide reports noted external depths up to 1.5 m and internal depths up to 1.0 m. [TAB] (p41)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 homes [TAB] (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Abbey Place, Renishaw",England,Internal flooding of residential properties in Abbey Place as part of the Renishaw event. Flooding was driven by overtopping of Smithy Brook at its culvert inlet and exacerbated by culvert blockages; Renishaw–wide reports noted external depths up to 1.5 m and internal depths up to 1.0 m. [TAB] (p41),6 homes [TAB] (p41),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2937928,-1.3269886,"<div id=""html_5685242296343be94917049081c98e5d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>East Street, Renishaw</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a residential property during the Renishaw event caused by overtopping and culvert blockages associated with Smithy Brook/Emmett Carr Brook flows. [TAB] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple properties reported sewer flooding on East Street during the event. (p43)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 home [TAB] (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"East Street, Renishaw",England,"Internal flooding of a residential property during the Renishaw event caused by overtopping and culvert blockages associated with Smithy Brook/Emmett Carr Brook flows. [TAB] (p41)
Multiple properties reported sewer flooding on East Street during the event. (p43)",1 home [TAB] (p41),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2944471,-1.3245664,"<div id=""html_2bb9947aa64f0cad779a4c3c1ad49111"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Emmett Carr Drive, Renishaw</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties as part of the Renishaw event caused by overtopping and culvert blockages. [TAB] (p41)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 homes [TAB] (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Emmett Carr Drive, Renishaw",England,Internal flooding of residential properties as part of the Renishaw event caused by overtopping and culvert blockages. [TAB] (p41),2 homes [TAB] (p41),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2933127,-1.329602,"<div id=""html_ab5bc97c489decbc6a0462a6191c994c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Carrwood Road, Renishaw</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from agricultural land to the south of Renishaw flowed onto Carwood Road; this water then flowed eastwards and downslope onto Emmett/Emmettt Carr Lane, contributing to the downstream flooding. (p43)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Carrwood Road, Renishaw",England,"Runoff from agricultural land to the south of Renishaw flowed onto Carwood Road; this water then flowed eastwards and downslope onto Emmett/Emmettt Carr Lane, contributing to the downstream flooding. (p43)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2392751,-1.4207142,"<div id=""html_9ec91a41757f5f6c9bd23c8faa1c2747"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tapton Terrace, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Front&ndash;facing terraced homes on Tapton Terrace were internally flooded when the River Rother overtopped/entered the street during Storm Babet; the flooding caused loss of life (one resident) and significant property inundation. [IMG,PAG] (p45)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes in the Tapton Terrace area were internally flooded during Storm Babet (Oct 19&ndash;21, 2023). Seventeen non&ndash;residential properties also flooded. Flood Zone mapping shows many properties adjacent to the River Rother are in Flood Zone 3 (higher risk); one non&ndash;residential property is in Flood Zone 2 and four are in Flood Zone 1. Some homes in the community are mapped with a medium risk of surface water flooding (1%&ndash;3.3% AEP). Historic mapping shows all homes that flooded in Storm Babet had flooded previously; 12 of the 17 flooded non&ndash;residential properties had flooded in 2007, with some also flooding in 2019. [IMG,PAG] (p46)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes on Tapton Terrace were inundated when floodwater exceeded property flood resilience (PFR) measures; floodwater reached depths that exceeded typical PFR capability. [PAG,IMG] (p47)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rear flooding from the River Rother inundated properties then progressed to flood from the front down to Tapton Bridge. Internal flooding occurred in homes; flood depths reached up to 1.5m in some properties and one resident died. [PAG] (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The rear of all 26 homes was flooded when river levels exceeded the east bank low spot; water later entered properties from the front down to Tapton Bridge. Flooding reached depths of up to 1.5 m in some homes and caused one resident fatality. [PAG,IMG] (p49)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Emergency services attended during the event; three properties requested sandbags during Storm Babet; Environment Agency operatives deployed pumps to empty a manhole chamber following the event; one resident lost their life during the event. (p50)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>26 residential properties; 1 death [IMG,PAG] (p45)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 non&ndash;residential properties; 12 flooded previously in 2007; 1 non&ndash;residential property in Flood Zone 2; 4 non&ndash;residential properties in Flood Zone 1 [IMG,PAG] (p46)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>floodwater depths up to 1.5 m in some homes [PAG,IMG] (p47)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>26 homes; 1 fatality; flood depths of 1.5m in some homes [PAG] (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>26 homes; depths up to 1.5m; 1 fatality [PAG,IMG] (p49)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>three properties; two 75mm pumps (one used); one fatality (p50)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Tapton Terrace, Chesterfield",England,"Front–facing terraced homes on Tapton Terrace were internally flooded when the River Rother overtopped/entered the street during Storm Babet; the flooding caused loss of life (one resident) and significant property inundation. [IMG,PAG] (p45)
Homes in the Tapton Terrace area were internally flooded during Storm Babet (Oct 19–21, 2023). Seventeen non–residential properties also flooded. Flood Zone mapping shows many properties adjacent to the River Rother are in Flood Zone 3 (higher risk); one non–residential property is in Flood Zone 2 and four are in Flood Zone 1. Some homes in the community are mapped with a medium risk of surface water flooding (1%–3.3% AEP). Historic mapping shows all homes that flooded in Storm Babet had flooded previously; 12 of the 17 flooded non–residential properties had flooded in 2007, with some also flooding in 2019. [IMG,PAG] (p46)
Homes on Tapton Terrace were inundated when floodwater exceeded property flood resilience (PFR) measures; floodwater reached depths that exceeded typical PFR capability. [PAG,IMG] (p47)
Rear flooding from the River Rother inundated properties then progressed to flood from the front down to Tapton Bridge. Internal flooding occurred in homes; flood depths reached up to 1.5m in some properties and one resident died. [PAG] (p48)
The rear of all 26 homes was flooded when river levels exceeded the east bank low spot; water later entered properties from the front down to Tapton Bridge. Flooding reached depths of up to 1.5 m in some homes and caused one resident fatality. [PAG,IMG] (p49)
Emergency services attended during the event; three properties requested sandbags during Storm Babet; Environment Agency operatives deployed pumps to empty a manhole chamber following the event; one resident lost their life during the event. (p50)","26 residential properties; 1 death [IMG,PAG] (p45)
17 non–residential properties; 12 flooded previously in 2007; 1 non–residential property in Flood Zone 2; 4 non–residential properties in Flood Zone 1 [IMG,PAG] (p46)
floodwater depths up to 1.5 m in some homes [PAG,IMG] (p47)
