GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2391233,-1.4154884,"<div id=""html_58933439579f9f19ef3dd56bf3d3ebb5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Crow Lane, Tapton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The recorded flood outline from Storm Babet and high surface&ndash;water risk zones are shown adjacent to Crow Lane on the map, indicating inundation or direct exposure to floodwater in the event. [PAG,IMG] (p47)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The recorded Storm Babet flood outline crosses Crow Lane, indicating inundation of this low&ndash;lying route adjacent to the River Rother during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p49)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Crow Lane, Tapton",England,"The recorded flood outline from Storm Babet and high surface–water risk zones are shown adjacent to Crow Lane on the map, indicating inundation or direct exposure to floodwater in the event. [PAG,IMG] (p47)
The recorded Storm Babet flood outline crosses Crow Lane, indicating inundation of this low–lying route adjacent to the River Rother during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p49)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2345024,-1.4192181,"<div id=""html_e29d6de22ea336dd26d6b078775dc5ad"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Camlough Walk, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties during Storm Babet as part of the wider central Chesterfield flooding. (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Located on the west bank of the River Rother immediately downstream of Hollis Lane Bridge; 39 homes suffered internal flooding due to the river flood during Storm Babet. [PAG] (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in the Environment Agency 'River Rother at Hady Hill' Flood Warning issued on 20 Oct 2023. This places Camlough Walk at risk from river flooding associated with the River Rother; the text indicates it was covered by a warning that related to affected areas in the community, but it does not explicitly state that properties on Camlough Walk suffered internal flooding. [PAG] (p53)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A majority of the internally flooded homes in the Central Chesterfield community were located on Camlough Walk; these properties experienced internal flooding during the event. (p54)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Rother overflow impacted Camlough Walk, causing internal flooding at ground floor level to two apartment blocks (The Foundry and Markham Quay); sewage presence indicates sewer surcharge or overwhelm. (p57)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ground floors of two apartment blocks on Camlough Walk (The Foundry and Markham Quay) suffered internal flooding; watermarks reached over 0.5 m on The Foundry. Sewage was reported at these buildings indicating the foul sewer system was likely overwhelmed. (p58)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Part of 49 homes and 30 businesses flooded in central Chesterfield (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>39 homes [PAG] (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 apartment blocks (p57)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 apartment blocks (p58)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Camlough Walk, Chesterfield",England,"Internal flooding of properties during Storm Babet as part of the wider central Chesterfield flooding. (p50)
