GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2321208,-1.4226907,"<div id=""html_c404c80e28459714beed241f63478090"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lordsmill Street, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Hipper passed south of Lordsmill Street and two businesses were internally flooded due to the river flooding during Storm Babet. [PAG,IMG] (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a key transport route within or adjacent to Flood Zone 2/3 and inside the Flood Warning Area along the river corridors. Lordsmill Street was affected by river&ndash;flooding impacts during the 19 Oct 2023 &ndash; 21 Oct 2023 event, posing disruption to transport and access in Central Chesterfield. [IMG] (p52)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 businesses [PAG,IMG] (p51)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Lordsmill Street, Chesterfield",England,"River Hipper passed south of Lordsmill Street and two businesses were internally flooded due to the river flooding during Storm Babet. [PAG,IMG] (p51)
Identified as a key transport route within or adjacent to Flood Zone 2/3 and inside the Flood Warning Area along the river corridors. Lordsmill Street was affected by river–flooding impacts during the 19 Oct 2023 – 21 Oct 2023 event, posing disruption to transport and access in Central Chesterfield. [IMG] (p52)","2 businesses [PAG,IMG] (p51)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.22904355259713,-1.4239109582719547,"<div id=""html_76d189a1337f085207fd295cee53c0af"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Byron Street, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The A61 was flooded from Horns Bridge Roundabout to about 200m south at the Byron Street junction; the A61/Around Byron Street was impassable and the electricity substation on the A61 opposite Byron Street was flooded, leaving homes without power. [PAG] (p56)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>around 200 homes without power [PAG] (p56)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Byron Street, Chesterfield",England,"The A61 was flooded from Horns Bridge Roundabout to about 200m south at the Byron Street junction; the A61/Around Byron Street was impassable and the electricity substation on the A61 opposite Byron Street was flooded, leaving homes without power. [PAG] (p56)",around 200 homes without power [PAG] (p56),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2703457,-1.4063222,"<div id=""html_f1f30f7f3f181bdb4710024efa7f7f8b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Meadow Close, Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties in Meadow Close during Storm Babet. (p59)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties during Storm Babet. Flood outlines from the event cover Meadow Close; local culverted ordinary watercourse and proximity to the River Rother provided flood pathways onto the floodplain. [IMG,PAG] (p60)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Meadow Close were internally flooded during the recorded Storm Babet event. The recorded flood outline from the event covers much of Meadow Close and confirms recent inundation. Topographic data show the flooded properties sit at a similar elevation to the top of the River Rother bank, consistent with river&ndash;driven flooding. [PAG,IMG] (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of Meadow Close was within the recorded flood outline from Storm Babet (October 2023). National surface water mapping and the map of the recorded event show low&ndash;to&ndash;medium surface water flood risk extending into Meadow Close, with the recorded flood outline overlapping properties and nearby Station Lane. [PAG,IMG] (p62)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Converging flood routes &mdash; initial surcharging from a double gully/manhole and subsequent overflow from the River Rother (and Brearley Wetlands) &mdash; led to floodwater collecting at a low spot and entering properties, causing internal flooding of homes. [IMG] (p63)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (p59)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties [IMG,PAG] (p60)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 internally flooded properties; 6 of the 15 have historic records of flooding from the River Rother [PAG,IMG] (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 internally flooded homes [IMG] (p63)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Meadow Close, Chesterfield",England,"Internal flooding of residential properties in Meadow Close during Storm Babet. (p59)
