GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2703486,-1.4057553,"<div id=""html_075540303eb5c02e07ea3f38fc23de51"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Station Lane, New Whittington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Station Lane lies within the recorded Storm Babet flood outline adjacent to Meadow Close; ordinary watercourse flows beneath Station Lane and the flood outline overlapped this road, forming part of the local flood pathway that contributed to internal flooding of nearby properties. [PAG,IMG] (p60)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Storm Babet recorded flood outline covers Station Lane, confirming that parts of the street were inundated during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Storm Babet recorded flood outline encircled part of Station Lane. Surface water flood risk and the recorded flood outline overlap here, with the River Rother reaching a very high peak on 20 Oct 2023, causing flooding at the location. [PAG,IMG] (p62)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the River Rother crossed Station Lane, indicating inundation of the highway and flow paths crossing the road. [IMG] (p63)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Station Lane, New Whittington",England,"Station Lane lies within the recorded Storm Babet flood outline adjacent to Meadow Close; ordinary watercourse flows beneath Station Lane and the flood outline overlapped this road, forming part of the local flood pathway that contributed to internal flooding of nearby properties. [PAG,IMG] (p60)
The Storm Babet recorded flood outline covers Station Lane, confirming that parts of the street were inundated during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p61)
The Storm Babet recorded flood outline encircled part of Station Lane. Surface water flood risk and the recorded flood outline overlap here, with the River Rother reaching a very high peak on 20 Oct 2023, causing flooding at the location. [PAG,IMG] (p62)
Floodwater from the River Rother crossed Station Lane, indicating inundation of the highway and flow paths crossing the road. [IMG] (p63)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.3170716,-1.3481825,"<div id=""html_69643ca3496c554b886def8ea111801d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rotherham Road, Eckington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood outline recorded adjacent to The Moss concentrated near the intersection of Rotherham Road and Rotherside Road; road and nearby land were inundated and flooding extended into adjacent residential and business areas. [IMG] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes on Rotherham Road flooded internally during Storm Babet; these homes were flooded due to overbank/tributary flooding associated with The Moss (possible additional influence from high River Rother levels). An additional commercial property in the same immediate area also flooded internally. [PAG] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Five homes on Rotherham Road (north of The Moss tributary and east of the River Rother) flooded internally during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p67)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 homes; 1 commercial property [PAG] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 homes [PAG,IMG] (p67)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Rotherham Road, Eckington",England,"Flood outline recorded adjacent to The Moss concentrated near the intersection of Rotherham Road and Rotherside Road; road and nearby land were inundated and flooding extended into adjacent residential and business areas. [IMG] (p64)
