GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.3127484,-1.3456409,"<div id=""html_7b7916d2e43728592c1835d95921db08"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rotherside Road, Eckington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded flood outline from Storm Babet extended into Rotherside Road and adjacent land; flood waters affected nearby residential and business areas and were associated with internal flooding of properties in Eckington. [IMG] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The recorded Storm Babet flood outline on the map overlaps areas adjacent to Rotherside Road; built&ndash;up areas near the road lie within high/medium modelled surface&ndash;water risk and the observed outline aligns with those risk areas. It is therefore likely the area near Rotherside Road was affected by surface&ndash;water/flooding during Storm Babet, though the map does not explicitly state the road surface itself was inundated. [PAG,IMG] (p66)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Rotherside Road, Eckington",England,"Recorded flood outline from Storm Babet extended into Rotherside Road and adjacent land; flood waters affected nearby residential and business areas and were associated with internal flooding of properties in Eckington. [IMG] (p64)
The recorded Storm Babet flood outline on the map overlaps areas adjacent to Rotherside Road; built–up areas near the road lie within high/medium modelled surface–water risk and the observed outline aligns with those risk areas. It is therefore likely the area near Rotherside Road was affected by surface–water/flooding during Storm Babet, though the map does not explicitly state the road surface itself was inundated. [PAG,IMG] (p66)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.3143254,-1.345448,"<div id=""html_cf0e731a6a167502c80d5ada6e861fe5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pipworth Lane, Eckington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Pipworth Lane flooded internally during Storm Babet; these properties form part of the five homes affected in the area north of The Moss and east of the River Rother. [PAG,IMG] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Pipworth Lane were internally flooded as part of the event driven by The Moss tributary; residents reported flood depths and blockages (fallen trees) on The Moss which exacerbated flooding risk. [PAG,IMG] (p67)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>part of five homes that flooded internally (across Rotherham Road and Pipworth Lane) [PAG,IMG] (p67)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Pipworth Lane, Eckington",England,"Properties on Pipworth Lane flooded internally during Storm Babet; these properties form part of the five homes affected in the area north of The Moss and east of the River Rother. [PAG,IMG] (p66)
Properties on Pipworth Lane were internally flooded as part of the event driven by The Moss tributary; residents reported flood depths and blockages (fallen trees) on The Moss which exacerbated flooding risk. [PAG,IMG] (p67)","part of five homes that flooded internally (across Rotherham Road and Pipworth Lane) [PAG,IMG] (p67)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.3167405,-1.3533884,"<div id=""html_ebff62f3d4e9439c38b6cddbb4bd6b00"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sheffield Road, Eckington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Maped high/medium surface&ndash;water risk zones and the recorded Storm Babet flood outline extend into built&ndash;up areas near Sheffield Road; the recorded flood outline aligns with these risk areas, indicating Sheffield Road environs were likely affected by surface&ndash;water/urban flooding during Storm Babet. The text and map do not give an explicit statement that the road itself was inundated. [PAG,IMG] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The southern end of Sheffield Road was flooded during the incident. [PAG,IMG] (p67)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Sheffield Road, Eckington",England,"Maped high/medium surface–water risk zones and the recorded Storm Babet flood outline extend into built–up areas near Sheffield Road; the recorded flood outline aligns with these risk areas, indicating Sheffield Road environs were likely affected by surface–water/urban flooding during Storm Babet. The text and map do not give an explicit statement that the road itself was inundated. [PAG,IMG] (p66)
The southern end of Sheffield Road was flooded during the incident. [PAG,IMG] (p67)",,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.118504,-1.556618,"<div id=""html_6d2bfa443d54c5103cdb35c6c1223c8e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Derbyshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Communities within the county were affected by flooding during Storm Babet, including internal flooding to seven properties in Holymoorside and flooding at Station Road in Chesterfield. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Soil and silt deposits were left on Loads Road (Holymoorside area) after the flood; Derbyshire County Council highways cleared the soil and silt approximately four days after the event. Eighteen properties near Chatsworth Road and Walton Road (approx. 1 km west of Chesterfield) suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet; 17 of the flooded properties were residential (all semi&ndash;detached) and 1 was commercial. Flooding affected properties adjacent to the River Hipper and Walton Dam. [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storm Babet produced a recorded flood outline in this part of Derbyshire. A built&ndash;up area south of Chatsworth Road (including Anna Street West, Wheatbridge Road and Dock Walk) was covered by the recorded flood extent; properties in the community were internally flooded. The Environment Agency historic maps show many of the properties flooded during the event had flooded previously. [IMG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in Chesterfield during the event included: River Rother flooding in South Chesterfield that caused internal flooding of homes (west of the Rother); River Hipper issues in Brampton and Chesterfield where patrols found debris and land drainage blockages requiring channel clearance and a reported collapsed wall; and a NIRS report of damage to flood defences at Boythorpe. [IMG,PAG] (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storm Babet caused recorded flood outlines and internal flooding of residential properties in Renishaw. Flooding was concentrated along Smithy Brook and Emmett Carr Brook and their culverted sections, inundating parts of the village. [IMG] (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Derbyshire (Chesterfield area) experienced river flooding from the River Rother that caused internal flooding of properties in Tapton Terrace and neighbouring streets. [IMG] (p45)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Portion of the county (Meadow Close, New Whittington) experienced river and surface&ndash;water flooding during Storm Babet; residential properties suffered internal flooding and flood outlines overlapped housing and roads, prompting multi&ndash;agency site visits and engagement. [IMG] (p60)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties; 1 property with internal flooding at Station Road (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties; 17 residential properties; 1 commercial property; 8 properties on north bank; 10 properties on south bank; 11 properties in Flood Zone 2 [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>192 properties internally flooded (137 homes; 55 businesses); 142 properties had flooded previously (73% of properties internally flooded during Storm Babet) [IMG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>103 properties [IMG,PAG] (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>39 properties [IMG] (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>26 residential properties; 17 non&ndash;residential properties; 1 fatality [IMG] (p45)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties [IMG] (p60)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Derbyshire,England,"Communities within the county were affected by flooding during Storm Babet, including internal flooding to seven properties in Holymoorside and flooding at Station Road in Chesterfield. (p14)
Soil and silt deposits were left on Loads Road (Holymoorside area) after the flood; Derbyshire County Council highways cleared the soil and silt approximately four days after the event. Eighteen properties near Chatsworth Road and Walton Road (approx. 1 km west of Chesterfield) suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet; 17 of the flooded properties were residential (all semi–detached) and 1 was commercial. Flooding affected properties adjacent to the River Hipper and Walton Dam. [PAG,IMG] (p20)
Storm Babet produced a recorded flood outline in this part of Derbyshire. A built–up area south of Chatsworth Road (including Anna Street West, Wheatbridge Road and Dock Walk) was covered by the recorded flood extent; properties in the community were internally flooded. The Environment Agency historic maps show many of the properties flooded during the event had flooded previously. [IMG] (p25)
Flooding in Chesterfield during the event included: River Rother flooding in South Chesterfield that caused internal flooding of homes (west of the Rother); River Hipper issues in Brampton and Chesterfield where patrols found debris and land drainage blockages requiring channel clearance and a reported collapsed wall; and a NIRS report of damage to flood defences at Boythorpe. [IMG,PAG] (p33)
Storm Babet caused recorded flood outlines and internal flooding of residential properties in Renishaw. Flooding was concentrated along Smithy Brook and Emmett Carr Brook and their culverted sections, inundating parts of the village. [IMG] (p38)
Parts of Derbyshire (Chesterfield area) experienced river flooding from the River Rother that caused internal flooding of properties in Tapton Terrace and neighbouring streets. [IMG] (p45)
Portion of the county (Meadow Close, New Whittington) experienced river and surface–water flooding during Storm Babet; residential properties suffered internal flooding and flood outlines overlapped housing and roads, prompting multi–agency site visits and engagement. [IMG] (p60)","7 properties; 1 property with internal flooding at Station Road (p14)
