GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2271036,-1.4412398,"<div id=""html_062c36dcaefc24e8bedd763a9851c18a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Boythorpe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Damage to flood defences was reported in Boythorpe during the event (noted via NIRS); the Environment Agency Asset Information and Maintenance Programme records do not indicate the presence of defences at this location. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Boythorpe,England,Damage to flood defences was reported in Boythorpe during the event (noted via NIRS); the Environment Agency Asset Information and Maintenance Programme records do not indicate the presence of defences at this location. (p33),,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.22631916972569,-1.4240453355431884,"<div id=""html_5d100a90054e0c565f446612f31ede13"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Chesterfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal property flooding in the South Chesterfield community during Storm Babet; residential streets either side of the River Rother were inundated and properties on the floodplain were flooded internally. [IMG] (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>103 properties [IMG] (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,South Chesterfield,England,Internal property flooding in the South Chesterfield community during Storm Babet; residential streets either side of the River Rother were inundated and properties on the floodplain were flooded internally. [IMG] (p33),103 properties [IMG] (p33),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2946503,-1.3269578,"<div id=""html_107e40c187f80b0b3e140c309f03c88d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Renishaw</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential area in Renishaw experienced internal flooding of homes during Storm Babet; the main cluster of flooded properties is shown adjacent to Smithy Brook and aligned with the mapped flood outlines. (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties concentrated in the area north of the village where Smithy Brook and Emmett Carr Brook run; flood extents coincide with Flood Zone 3 and high surface&ndash;water&ndash;risk areas, inundating houses near Main Road and Emmet Carr Lane. [PAG,IMG] (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties during Storm Babet; recorded flood outline concentrated near Emmett Carr Lane and Main Road; high surface&ndash;water flood risk adjacent to Emmett Carr Brook and Smithy Brook affecting residential streets and properties. [PAG] (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping of Smithy Brook at its culvert inlet (and overtopping of Emmett Carr Brook upstream of its culvert inlet), exacerbated by culvert/trash&ndash;screen blockages, caused pooling and flow routes through Renishaw. Floodwater flowed west along Smithy Brook Road flooding four businesses, flowed onto the Main Road and east along the A6135 flooding six homes, then flowed south along Emmett Carr Lane flooding eighteen homes. Internal flood depths were reported at 0.2m&ndash;0.8m on Sheffield Road and up to 1.2m inside a property on Emmett Carr Lane. Reports indicate peak severity on 20 Oct between 12:00 and 14:00. [IMG] (p42)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>39 properties (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>39 properties [PAG,IMG] (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 businesses [PAG] (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 businesses; 6 homes; 18 homes; internal depths 0.2m&ndash;0.8m; internal depth up to 1.2m at one property [IMG] (p42)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Renishaw,England,"Residential area in Renishaw experienced internal flooding of homes during Storm Babet; the main cluster of flooded properties is shown adjacent to Smithy Brook and aligned with the mapped flood outlines. (p38)
Internal flooding of residential properties concentrated in the area north of the village where Smithy Brook and Emmett Carr Brook run; flood extents coincide with Flood Zone 3 and high surface–water–risk areas, inundating houses near Main Road and Emmet Carr Lane. [PAG,IMG] (p39)
