GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2476365,-1.4121277,"<div id=""html_5b4c107f6beb087a003049621d912ec5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tapton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Rother flooded properties in the Tapton community. Twenty&ndash;six homes on Tapton Terrace suffered internal flooding (rear of properties first, then the front) with flood depths reaching up to 1.5 m in some properties; external PFR measures were exceeded. One resident died. Nearby industrial areas around Brimington Road and Holbeck Close also experienced internal flooding of non&ndash;residential premises, contributing to a combined total of forty&ndash;three residential and non&ndash;residential properties flooded in the local community. [PAG] (p48)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>26 residential properties; 17 non&ndash;residential properties; 43 properties (total); 1 fatality; flood depths up to 1.5 m [PAG] (p48)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Tapton,England,"Flooding from the River Rother flooded properties in the Tapton community. Twenty–six homes on Tapton Terrace suffered internal flooding (rear of properties first, then the front) with flood depths reaching up to 1.5 m in some properties; external PFR measures were exceeded. One resident died. Nearby industrial areas around Brimington Road and Holbeck Close also experienced internal flooding of non–residential premises, contributing to a combined total of forty–three residential and non–residential properties flooded in the local community. [PAG] (p48)",26 residential properties; 17 non–residential properties; 43 properties (total); 1 fatality; flood depths up to 1.5 m [PAG] (p48),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.2763003,-1.4049104,"<div id=""html_cdd8cb98af811dc05ce0500b1ed15c9c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>New Whittington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding occurred in Meadow Close within New Whittington during Storm Babet, affecting local residences. (p59)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (p59)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,New Whittington,England,"Internal flooding occurred in Meadow Close within New Whittington during Storm Babet, affecting local residences. (p59)",15 properties (p59),GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,4,2023-10-19,53.3089836,-1.3557936,"<div id=""html_78e94ce36ff1f0224a651b684c0ef52a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Eckington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties north of The Moss as a result of Storm Babet; the recorded flood outline extended into residential and business areas near Rotherside Road and adjacent to The Moss, affecting parts of the Eckington Business Park vicinity. [IMG,PAG] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties during Storm Babet: five homes on Rotherham Road and Pipworth Lane flooded internally (north of The Moss tributary and east of the River Rother). An additional commercial property in the same location flooded internally; further commercial units on Eckington Business Park (south of The Moss and east of the River Rother) also flooded internally. Affected properties lie on the River Rother floodplain and are in Flood Zone 2 with some in Flood Zone 3. Flood Alert and Flood Warning were issued prior to the event. [PAG] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties within the Eckington community flooded internally due to The Moss tributary overtopping/peak flows; commercial properties on Eckington Business Park and properties north of The Moss were also internally flooded. Residents reported fallen trees blocking The Moss, raising further flood risk locally. [IMG,PAG] (p67)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties; 5 residential properties; 3 commercial properties [IMG,PAG] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>five homes; one commercial property [PAG] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 homes; 1 additional commercial property; floodwater reported ~0.6m deep (resident report) [IMG,PAG] (p67)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Eckington,England,"Internal flooding of properties north of The Moss as a result of Storm Babet; the recorded flood outline extended into residential and business areas near Rotherside Road and adjacent to The Moss, affecting parts of the Eckington Business Park vicinity. [IMG,PAG] (p64)
Internal flooding of properties during Storm Babet: five homes on Rotherham Road and Pipworth Lane flooded internally (north of The Moss tributary and east of the River Rother). An additional commercial property in the same location flooded internally; further commercial units on Eckington Business Park (south of The Moss and east of the River Rother) also flooded internally. Affected properties lie on the River Rother floodplain and are in Flood Zone 2 with some in Flood Zone 3. Flood Alert and Flood Warning were issued prior to the event. [PAG] (p66)
Properties within the Eckington community flooded internally due to The Moss tributary overtopping/peak flows; commercial properties on Eckington Business Park and properties north of The Moss were also internally flooded. Residents reported fallen trees blocking The Moss, raising further flood risk locally. [IMG,PAG] (p67)","8 properties; 5 residential properties; 3 commercial properties [IMG,PAG] (p64)
five homes; one commercial property [PAG] (p66)
5 homes; 1 additional commercial property; floodwater reported ~0.6m deep (resident report) [IMG,PAG] (p67)",GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19.html,GB-DBY_4_2023-10-19,Derbyshire flooding 19 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-4-don-and-rother-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-NNH,4,2016-03-09,52.396831,-0.6856892,"<div id=""html_a5583cc149dc5912c09decb15e8964df"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>St Catherine's Road, Ise Lodge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment flowed over ground following natural contours into low points around private property, causing internal flooding of a property on St Catherine's Road. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding entered a property on St Catherine's Road (water crossed the building threshold). [PAG,MUL] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A property on St Catherine's Road was flooded. Surface water runoff accumulated to the rear/adjacent to the property (localised area shown at high risk), with roofs and paved areas draining to the surface water sewer that connects to public sewers on Deeble Road. A surface water public sewer manhole and highway gully are located in front of the flooded property; runoff from nearby agricultural fields flowed toward the rear of the property. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from adjacent arable land flowed into rear gardens, ponded to approximately 300mm depth at the rear of a garden, entered air bricks and flooded a garage; properties were affected by the inundation of rear gardens. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from arable fields ponded to the rear of a garden and entered private property. Water collected (~300 mm) at the rear boundary, flowed into a neighbouring garden then down the west side of the garden to the patio and around the north and west elevations of the house, entering air bricks and the garage. Reported water depth at the house was 100&ndash;150 mm. Floodwater then flowed along both sides of the driveway onto St Catherine's Road, overwhelming the adjacent highway gully and flooding across and down the road. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall over a saturated catchment caused drainage systems to be ineffective, resulting in excess surface water flowing over ground following natural contours into low points around private properties on St Catherine's Road. Some properties experienced surface water intrusion to gardens and private areas; one property further west has a raised rear garden wall that provided a defence. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External areas of residential properties (front, side and rear patio) were inundated; residents' photographs from the incident show floodwater affecting property curtilage and entrances. (p43)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [PAG,MUL] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two properties; one property; 300mm depth [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>300 mm ponding at rear of garden; 100&ndash;150 mm depth entering house and garage; 500 mm raised ground height (rear bund) [PAG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"St Catherine's Road, Ise Lodge",England,"Surface water from heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment flowed over ground following natural contours into low points around private property, causing internal flooding of a property on St Catherine's Road. (p7)
Internal flooding entered a property on St Catherine's Road (water crossed the building threshold). [PAG,MUL] (p9)
A property on St Catherine's Road was flooded. Surface water runoff accumulated to the rear/adjacent to the property (localised area shown at high risk), with roofs and paved areas draining to the surface water sewer that connects to public sewers on Deeble Road. A surface water public sewer manhole and highway gully are located in front of the flooded property; runoff from nearby agricultural fields flowed toward the rear of the property. (p10)
Surface water runoff from adjacent arable land flowed into rear gardens, ponded to approximately 300mm depth at the rear of a garden, entered air bricks and flooded a garage; properties were affected by the inundation of rear gardens. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p11)
Surface water runoff from arable fields ponded to the rear of a garden and entered private property. Water collected (~300 mm) at the rear boundary, flowed into a neighbouring garden then down the west side of the garden to the patio and around the north and west elevations of the house, entering air bricks and the garage. Reported water depth at the house was 100–150 mm. Floodwater then flowed along both sides of the driveway onto St Catherine's Road, overwhelming the adjacent highway gully and flooding across and down the road. [PAG] (p12)
Heavy rainfall over a saturated catchment caused drainage systems to be ineffective, resulting in excess surface water flowing over ground following natural contours into low points around private properties on St Catherine's Road. Some properties experienced surface water intrusion to gardens and private areas; one property further west has a raised rear garden wall that provided a defence. (p13)
External areas of residential properties (front, side and rear patio) were inundated; residents' photographs from the incident show floodwater affecting property curtilage and entrances. (p43)","one property (p7)
