GB-CAM,28,2020-12-23,52.4167643,-0.1910317,"<div id=""html_3baf32eec714a4bc7cfdf967bcef07a4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Raveley Road, Woodwalton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A ditch runs along Raveley Road that was reported to regularly back up and overflow during the event; the culvert conveying water away from the Raveley Road ditch required maintenance and Cambridgeshire Highways ordered maintenance on that culvert to restore conveyance. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Raveley Road, Woodwalton",England,A ditch runs along Raveley Road that was reported to regularly back up and overflow during the event; the culvert conveying water away from the Raveley Road ditch required maintenance and Cambridgeshire Highways ordered maintenance on that culvert to restore conveyance. (p10),,GB-CAM_28_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_28_2020-12-23,Woodwalton flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Woodwalton,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Woodwalton-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,28,2020-12-23,52.4241559,-0.2198151,"<div id=""html_c3e28426bf9ab081449d0607ed801478"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>New Road, Woodwalton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water and overland flow routed into a low spot; overflowing highway gullies and an overgrown partially culverted ditch/culverts. Three residential properties, outbuildings and gardens were internally flooded to a maximum depth of c.460mm. Some residents were unable to return to their properties for over one month. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water routed to this low spot, with a partially culverted ditch to the west overgrown and highway gullies overflowing; ditch/culverts overtopped. Floodwater inundated residential properties, outbuildings and gardens to a maximum depth of about 460 mm; some residents were unable to return to their properties for over one month. [TAB] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localized flooding affected New Road; residents reported flooding and maintenance issues with ditches and drainage which prompted LLFA walkovers and follow&ndash;up works (ditch maintenance and gully/culvert cleansing were arranged). [TAB] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected New Road. Riparian maintenance issues were identified and RMA operational issues were recorded, requiring ongoing liaison between the LLFA and relevant Risk Management Authorities. [TAB] (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 residential properties; maximum depth of c.460mm [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 residential properties; over 1 month [TAB] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"New Road, Woodwalton",England,"Surface water and overland flow routed into a low spot; overflowing highway gullies and an overgrown partially culverted ditch/culverts. Three residential properties, outbuildings and gardens were internally flooded to a maximum depth of c.460mm. Some residents were unable to return to their properties for over one month. [PAG] (p9)
Surface water routed to this low spot, with a partially culverted ditch to the west overgrown and highway gullies overflowing; ditch/culverts overtopped. Floodwater inundated residential properties, outbuildings and gardens to a maximum depth of about 460 mm; some residents were unable to return to their properties for over one month. [TAB] (p10)
Localized flooding affected New Road; residents reported flooding and maintenance issues with ditches and drainage which prompted LLFA walkovers and follow–up works (ditch maintenance and gully/culvert cleansing were arranged). [TAB] (p13)
