3 residential properties; over 1 month [TAB] (p10)",GB-CAM_28_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_28_2020-12-23,Woodwalton flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Woodwalton,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Woodwalton-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,28,2020-12-23,52.412563,-0.2142901,"<div id=""html_f944eceb75a381723b91226ce40aec6e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Cross, Woodwalton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties was reported at this location (listed as one of three key risk areas where internal property flooding occurred). Additional local roads and gardens in the village were also identified as flooded. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred; highway gullies and the ditch at The Cross overflowed. Outbuildings and gardens attached to one residential property were inundated. When floodwater leaves the ditch channel it flows toward the centre of the village, worsening flooding. A tree was observed blocking the village&ndash;green ditch, contributing to conveyance problems. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At the Cross and village green, outbuildings and gardens attached to one residential property were inundated with flood water; residents did not have to leave the property. A ditch at the village green was obstructed by a tree trunk and roots, causing water to pool and, when the ditch overtopped, floodwater flowed towards the centre of the village and exacerbated local flooding. In the Braefield area (within Woodwalton), surface water routed from fields to the north flooded one residential property to a depth of about 60 mm internally and flooded the outbuildings of that property to about 180 mm; anecdotal evidence indicates that this floodwater dissipated relatively quickly after the event. [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported at The Cross; investigations identified issues with ditches and highway drainage leading to planned and carried&ndash;out maintenance actions to alleviate future flooding. [TAB] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential property [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential property; internal flooding c.60 mm; outbuildings flooded c.180 mm [TAB] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"The Cross, Woodwalton",England,"Internal flooding of residential properties was reported at this location (listed as one of three key risk areas where internal property flooding occurred). Additional local roads and gardens in the village were also identified as flooded. (p9)
Surface water flooding occurred; highway gullies and the ditch at The Cross overflowed. Outbuildings and gardens attached to one residential property were inundated. When floodwater leaves the ditch channel it flows toward the centre of the village, worsening flooding. A tree was observed blocking the village–green ditch, contributing to conveyance problems. [PAG] (p10)
At the Cross and village green, outbuildings and gardens attached to one residential property were inundated with flood water; residents did not have to leave the property. A ditch at the village green was obstructed by a tree trunk and roots, causing water to pool and, when the ditch overtopped, floodwater flowed towards the centre of the village and exacerbated local flooding. In the Braefield area (within Woodwalton), surface water routed from fields to the north flooded one residential property to a depth of about 60 mm internally and flooded the outbuildings of that property to about 180 mm; anecdotal evidence indicates that this floodwater dissipated relatively quickly after the event. [TAB] (p11)
Flooding was reported at The Cross; investigations identified issues with ditches and highway drainage leading to planned and carried–out maintenance actions to alleviate future flooding. [TAB] (p13)","1 residential property [PAG] (p10)
