GB-BKM,10,2014-01-01,51.5692357,-0.772585,"<div id=""html_972d985944f2418b51b4932d5b6b0a3f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>St Peter Street, Marlow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the area flooded directly from the River Thames; properties in St Peters Street required protection by the fire and rescue service. There are reports of sewage problems throughout most of the area. [PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in St Peter Street on 9 January 2014; BFRS deployed a mobile light pump to remove floodwater. [TAB] (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in the St Peter Street area: two pumps were deployed by BFRS and sandbags were issued to the street as part of the response. [TAB,MUL] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sandbags distributed to protect properties on St Peter's Street in response to flooding. [TAB,MUL] (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,"St Peter Street, Marlow",England,"Part of the area flooded directly from the River Thames; properties in St Peters Street required protection by the fire and rescue service. There are reports of sewage problems throughout most of the area. [PAG] (p21)
