GB-BST,1,2020-03-11,51.4463125,-2.5957329,"<div id=""html_db8590da9d71ef4a399ec883d634d259"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Commercial Road, Bristol</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Inundation of Commercial Road by floodwaters from the tidal River Avon during the high tides on 11&ndash;12 March 2020. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Both Commercial Road and Clarence Road remained open but may have experienced very shallow flooding for a short period during the high tides on the evening of 11 March and morning of 12 March. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed in the report as being affected by the high&ndash;tide / storm&ndash;surge flood of 11&ndash;12 March 2020; highway infrastructure and nearby properties were inundated by tidal/coastal flooding. (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>0.5 hours (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bristol, City of","Commercial Road, Bristol",England,"Inundation of Commercial Road by floodwaters from the tidal River Avon during the high tides on 11–12 March 2020. (p6)
Both Commercial Road and Clarence Road remained open but may have experienced very shallow flooding for a short period during the high tides on the evening of 11 March and morning of 12 March. (p15)
Listed in the report as being affected by the high–tide / storm–surge flood of 11–12 March 2020; highway infrastructure and nearby properties were inundated by tidal/coastal flooding. (p22)",0.5 hours (p15),GB-BST_1_2020-03-11.html,GB-BST_1_2020-03-11,Bristol flooding 11 Mar 2020 - 12 Mar 2020,Flood Investigation: March 2020 Tidal Flooding,016/Bristol/016/2020/Bristol/Flood Investigation Report - River Avon - March 2020.pdf
GB-BST,1,2020-03-11,51.4554817,-2.5394925,"<div id=""html_4b227f96e3a58f4419d574ef810952f9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Crews Hole Road, St George</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Crew's Hole Road footpath was flooded by tidal River Avon waters; it is recorded as the easternmost known flooded location in the sequence on 11&ndash;12 March 2020. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Avon footpath at Crew's Hole Road and St Phillips was impacted by high tides and was actively managed/closed as part of the flood response. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported as affected in the 11&ndash;12 March 2020 high&ndash;tide / storm&ndash;surge event; the report notes the footpath at Crew's Hole Road was inundated during the tidal/coastal flooding. (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Avon footpath at Crew's Hole Road and St Phillips (between Totterdown bridge and Cattle Market Road) was identified for closure due to high tides on 11&ndash;12 March 2020, reflecting anticipated tidal inundation of the footpath area. (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bristol, City of","Crews Hole Road, St George",England,"The Crew's Hole Road footpath was flooded by tidal River Avon waters; it is recorded as the easternmost known flooded location in the sequence on 11–12 March 2020. (p6)
The River Avon footpath at Crew's Hole Road and St Phillips was impacted by high tides and was actively managed/closed as part of the flood response. (p18)
Reported as affected in the 11–12 March 2020 high–tide / storm–surge event; the report notes the footpath at Crew's Hole Road was inundated during the tidal/coastal flooding. (p22)
The River Avon footpath at Crew's Hole Road and St Phillips (between Totterdown bridge and Cattle Market Road) was identified for closure due to high tides on 11–12 March 2020, reflecting anticipated tidal inundation of the footpath area. (p24)",,GB-BST_1_2020-03-11.html,GB-BST_1_2020-03-11,Bristol flooding 11 Mar 2020 - 12 Mar 2020,Flood Investigation: March 2020 Tidal Flooding,016/Bristol/016/2020/Bristol/Flood Investigation Report - River Avon - March 2020.pdf
GB-BST,1,2020-03-11,51.448414,-2.618751,"<div id=""html_6c0d7995e5d5d67b6301eea260f7fee4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cumberland Basin Road, Hotwells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cumberland Basin Road was affected by the high tide on 11 March 2020, with flood levels estimated using the measured/assumed tide heights and road elevations to produce maximum flood depth estimates. [TAB] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cumberland Basin Road experienced tidal inundation resulting in roadway flooding and closure as part of the wider Cumberland Basin area closures. [TAB,PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Closed during the high tides on the evening of 11 March and the morning of 12 March due to tidal flooding, resulting in several hours of road inundation. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road was actively managed and closed during the tidal event as part of highway response and traffic coordination. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cumberland Basin Road was identified for closure around the high tides on 11&ndash;12 March 2020. The Cumberland Basin area was photographed during the high tide, indicating tidal inundation at or near the road. (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>estimated high tide 8.77 mAOD [TAB] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>0.40 m max flood depth; approximately 4.5 hours road closure [TAB,PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3.5 hours; 4 hours (approximate flooding durations during the two closure periods) [TAB] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bristol, City of","Cumberland Basin Road, Hotwells",England,"Cumberland Basin Road was affected by the high tide on 11 March 2020, with flood levels estimated using the measured/assumed tide heights and road elevations to produce maximum flood depth estimates. [TAB] (p13)
