depth of water in Main Street exceeded 1 metre in places; external property areas ~300 mm; internal depths between 20 mm and 150 mm (p18)",GB-NNH_25_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_25_2020-12-23,Southwick flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Main Street, Southwick, 23rd December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Main Street, Southwick.pdf"
GB-NNH,25,2020-12-23,52.56628789856925,-0.2027211766370756,"<div id=""html_19c91bb5fde0472cb84312377d2697b1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Nene</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Minor tributaries of the Nene triggered a Flood Alert (055WAF133MTN) issued on 23 December 2020; rivers in the Northamptonshire/Lincolnshire area (including Nene tributaries) were the subject of numerous Environment Agency warnings as heavy rainfall produced high surface runoff and elevated river flows. [MUL] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,River Nene,England,Minor tributaries of the Nene triggered a Flood Alert (055WAF133MTN) issued on 23 December 2020; rivers in the Northamptonshire/Lincolnshire area (including Nene tributaries) were the subject of numerous Environment Agency warnings as heavy rainfall produced high surface runoff and elevated river flows. [MUL] (p10),,GB-NNH_25_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_25_2020-12-23,Southwick flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Main Street, Southwick, 23rd December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Main Street, Southwick.pdf"
GB-NNH,25,2020-12-23,52.516540389409656,-0.5026549657144336,"<div id=""html_cba7fbd99b55e53968bf7c2b9590a807"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Main Street Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The bridge did not have capacity for the volume of brook flow; this caused water to deepen on the upstream side and contributed to overtopping and subsequent internal flooding of properties on Main Street. [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The bridge lacked capacity for the volume of water in the brook during the event, causing water to deepen upstream and contributing to overtopping upstream of the bridge. This led to flows onto Main Street and contributed to internal flooding of adjacent properties. The existing bypass pipe and bifurcation arrangement influenced how high flows passed the structure. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The bridge lacked capacity for the volume of water in the brook, causing water to deepen upstream. This contributed to the brook overtopping upstream and flow from the brook onto Townsend Farm access track and Main Street, which was part of the chain of flooding that led to internal flooding of at least one property upstream. (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Downstream abutment and adjacent waterway were partially submerged; sediment accumulation and debris collected at the base of the abutment, indicating floodwater reached the structure and deposited material against it. This condition indicates potential local scour/erosion and need for maintenance at the water&ndash;structure interface. [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 properties [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>water depth in Main Street exceeded one metre in places [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>brook overtopped approximately 100m upstream; one property flooded internally at that upstream location (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Main Street Bridge,England,"The bridge did not have capacity for the volume of brook flow; this caused water to deepen on the upstream side and contributed to overtopping and subsequent internal flooding of properties on Main Street. [PAG] (p15)
The bridge lacked capacity for the volume of water in the brook during the event, causing water to deepen upstream and contributing to overtopping upstream of the bridge. This led to flows onto Main Street and contributed to internal flooding of adjacent properties. The existing bypass pipe and bifurcation arrangement influenced how high flows passed the structure. [PAG] (p16)
The bridge lacked capacity for the volume of water in the brook, causing water to deepen upstream. This contributed to the brook overtopping upstream and flow from the brook onto Townsend Farm access track and Main Street, which was part of the chain of flooding that led to internal flooding of at least one property upstream. (p17)
Downstream abutment and adjacent waterway were partially submerged; sediment accumulation and debris collected at the base of the abutment, indicating floodwater reached the structure and deposited material against it. This condition indicates potential local scour/erosion and need for maintenance at the water–structure interface. [IMG,PAG] (p41)","11 properties [PAG] (p15)
water depth in Main Street exceeded one metre in places [PAG] (p16)
brook overtopped approximately 100m upstream; one property flooded internally at that upstream location (p17)",GB-NNH_25_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_25_2020-12-23,Southwick flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Main Street, Southwick, 23rd December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Main Street, Southwick.pdf"
GB-NNH,25,2020-12-23,52.5165938,-0.5001212,"<div id=""html_7ee1339b982faa33d2c6263972c189fe"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Main Street, Southwick</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of buildings on Main Street when excess surface water flowed over ground into low points around properties; drainage systems and watercourses could not convey the rainfall leading to water entering properties. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of buildings on Main Street: floodwater crossed building thresholds and entered premises in the immediate street area. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from Southwick Brook caused internal flooding to properties on Main Street. [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from a blocked/exceeded ditch flowed onto Main Street and east over the bridge; combined with brook overbanking this produced deep water on the street that entered doorways and airbricks, causing internal flooding of residential properties. [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from the ditch/headwall northwest of Main Street bridge and from an exceeded piped minor watercourse, combined with brook flows and brook overtopping upstream of the bridge, led to deep flows along Main Street. Water flowed east over the bridge and into doorways and airbricks of properties on the north side of the street. Highway drainage was overwhelmed and outfall pipes were submerged, restricting discharge. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from an exceeded ditch/pipe and overtopping from the brook flowed onto and along Main Street (east and north). Drainage was overwhelmed; water entered doorways and airbricks and caused internal flooding of properties along the street. [PAG] (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than five buildings (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than five buildings (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 properties [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 properties [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Depth in Main Street exceeded one metre in places; external areas around 300 mm; internal depths between 20 mm and 150 mm; 11 properties flooded [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 properties flooded; depth in Main Street exceeded one metre in places; external areas ~300mm; internal depths 20mm to 150mm. [PAG] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Main Street, Southwick",England,"Internal flooding of buildings on Main Street when excess surface water flowed over ground into low points around properties; drainage systems and watercourses could not convey the rainfall leading to water entering properties. (p7)
