GB-NNH,25,2020-12-23,52.3106138,-0.8659129831915817,"<div id=""html_e0dfa251c8319778c28fe9a71d6ede90"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Northamptonshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall on 23 December 2020 caused catchment saturation and high levels of surface water runoff, resulting in internal flooding of properties on Main Street, Southwick. The Environment Agency issued multiple flood warnings/alerts covering rivers in Northamptonshire during 23&ndash;25 December 2020. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>internal flooding of more than five buildings [PAG] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Northamptonshire,England,"Heavy rainfall on 23 December 2020 caused catchment saturation and high levels of surface water runoff, resulting in internal flooding of properties on Main Street, Southwick. The Environment Agency issued multiple flood warnings/alerts covering rivers in Northamptonshire during 23–25 December 2020. [PAG] (p9)",internal flooding of more than five buildings [PAG] (p9),GB-NNH_25_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_25_2020-12-23,Southwick flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Main Street, Southwick, 23rd December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Main Street, Southwick.pdf"
GB-NNH,25,2020-12-23,52.4175503,-0.6431175,"<div id=""html_fa36f978f834e0bb820b70767d7776d5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Northamptonshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties within North Northamptonshire were affected by surface water flooding during the event; incidents were identified for investigation and recording by the Lead Local Flood Authority. [PAG] (p25)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,North Northamptonshire,England,Properties within North Northamptonshire were affected by surface water flooding during the event; incidents were identified for investigation and recording by the Lead Local Flood Authority. [PAG] (p25),,GB-NNH_25_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_25_2020-12-23,Southwick flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Main Street, Southwick, 23rd December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Main Street, Southwick.pdf"
GB-NNH,25,2020-12-23,52.51658384214896,-0.4990753288424832,"<div id=""html_e4c64aff84330a479e472bc6262bec2c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Southwick</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Main Street in Southwick was the subject of a flood investigation (report title indicates a flooding incident occurred there and was investigated by the Lead Local Flood Authority). (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of more than five buildings in close proximity during the single flood event; excess surface water followed local ground levels to low points in and around properties. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Concentrated internal flooding in the Main Street area of Southwick, with floodwater entering multiple nearby properties. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A small area of Southwick (including one property) was included within a Flood Alert for the minor tributaries of the Nene. The Flood Alert was issued on 23 December 2020 and there was no local Flood Warning coverage or telemetry in the area. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Southwick Brook overtopped approximately 100 m upstream of Main Street bridge and, together with surface water from a blocked/exceeded ditch northwest of the bridge and an exceeded piped minor watercourse from Millennium Cottage, flowed onto Main Street and into properties. Water followed ground levels through rear gardens back to the brook. Streets, gardens and properties were inundated; one property reported water entering from both Main Street (front) and the brook (rear). [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Southwick Brook overtopped and conduits (Main Street bridge and buried pipes) were exceeded, producing overland flows into Main Street and around properties; floodwater followed local ground levels to low points near properties. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than five buildings (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than five buildings [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 properties; depth in Main Street exceeded one metre in places; external areas ~300 mm; internal depths between 20 mm and 150 mm [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depth of water in Main Street exceeded one metre; external areas of affected properties ~300mm; internal depths between 20mm and 150mm (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Southwick,England,"Main Street in Southwick was the subject of a flood investigation (report title indicates a flooding incident occurred there and was investigated by the Lead Local Flood Authority). (p3)
Internal flooding of more than five buildings in close proximity during the single flood event; excess surface water followed local ground levels to low points in and around properties. (p7)
