The flood defence bund within Perry Park was overtopped by flows from the Perry Brook, allowing water to flow out of the park into Church Road and contribute to property flooding. [IMG] (p52)","2 properties [IMG,PAG] (p51)
2 properties [IMG] (p52)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.52715,-1.8984019,"<div id=""html_9109cb3925c059f8b8a306bf1fed103c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church Tavern</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Location adjacent to the culvert entrance where Perry Brook came out of channel (Breach Location 1); the breach occurred at the rear of the Church Tavern and initiated overland flow toward Church Road. [PAG] (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culvert under the Church Tavern car park was identified as much smaller than the culvert under the road, restricting capacity and contributing to water backing up; this restriction, together with local flood defence/backing issues, contributed to property flooding around Church Road/Church Tavern. [PAG,MUL] (p52)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Church Tavern,England,"Location adjacent to the culvert entrance where Perry Brook came out of channel (Breach Location 1); the breach occurred at the rear of the Church Tavern and initiated overland flow toward Church Road. [PAG] (p51)
The culvert under the Church Tavern car park was identified as much smaller than the culvert under the road, restricting capacity and contributing to water backing up; this restriction, together with local flood defence/backing issues, contributed to property flooding around Church Road/Church Tavern. [PAG,MUL] (p52)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.43105235022694,-1.9032265742150427,"<div id=""html_be644db84e065d51774345f016e99d4a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>King Edwards School</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Playing fields produced uncontrolled runoff (overland flows) during an intense storm; these flows exceeded infiltration capacity and routed down slope into neighbouring properties, causing internal flooding at Eastern Road. [IMG] (p67)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties flooded (in Eastern Road) [IMG] (p67)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,King Edwards School,England,"Playing fields produced uncontrolled runoff (overland flows) during an intense storm; these flows exceeded infiltration capacity and routed down slope into neighbouring properties, causing internal flooding at Eastern Road. [IMG] (p67)",2 properties flooded (in Eastern Road) [IMG] (p67),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4503665,-1.913992,"<div id=""html_7f48713e97807f92ecf2a088604953d5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Birmingham Dental Hospital</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A breach in Bourn Brook occurred adjacent to the hospital; floodwater escaped the channel at that location and flowed southwards past the hospital into the Recreation Ground, forming part of the overland flow route into the surrounding streets. (p69)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Birmingham Dental Hospital,England,"A breach in Bourn Brook occurred adjacent to the hospital; floodwater escaped the channel at that location and flowed southwards past the hospital into the Recreation Ground, forming part of the overland flow route into the surrounding streets. (p69)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4478579,-1.9945808,"<div id=""html_9bad46267ea857b1a39bf316e6457cd4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Woodgate Valley Country Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from the Country Park flowed through the western residential area en route to Bourn Brook and, in the central area, received overland flows that then joined the Bourne/Bourn Brook; park&ndash;adjacent runoff contributed to flooding of properties. (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Woodgate Valley Country Park,England,"Runoff from the Country Park flowed through the western residential area en route to Bourn Brook and, in the central area, received overland flows that then joined the Bourne/Bourn Brook; park–adjacent runoff contributed to flooding of properties. (p72)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4434243,-1.9649962,"<div id=""html_d4e431d32f89c89d5065a77bcbab5c54"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stonehouse Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Stonehouse Brook breached where it enters the culvert beneath Mill Lane (Breach Location 2), releasing river waters into Mill Lane and along the footpath into Middle Acre Road; this breach contributed to the flooding of properties in the area. [IMG,PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Breach of the Stonehouse Brook where it enters the culvert beneath Mill Lane (Breach Location 2) caused river water to spill onto Mill Lane, follow the footpath and enter Middle Acre Road and Rush Green, contributing to highway/footpath flooding and property flooding in the immediate area. (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Debris accumulation (reported on the Bourn Brook Walkway footbridge upstream of the confluence with Stonehouse Brook) contributed to blockage and increased flood risk at the confluence area. [IMG,PAG] (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as one of the main rivers in the area contributing to flood risk at the confluence with Bourn Brook; debris and flows around the confluence contributed to reduced capacity and local flooding. [MUL] (p39)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (area&ndash;wide; contributed to by breaches of Stonehouse Brook and Bartley Brook) [IMG,PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Stonehouse Brook,England,"The Stonehouse Brook breached where it enters the culvert beneath Mill Lane (Breach Location 2), releasing river waters into Mill Lane and along the footpath into Middle Acre Road; this breach contributed to the flooding of properties in the area. [IMG,PAG] (p19)
