4 properties (p20)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4400276,-1.9952316,"<div id=""html_5c8df58c78f60ee4339fd8b6fc8a65ba"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bartley Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Breach of the Bartley Brook where it enters the culvert at Mill Lane produced overland flows running south&ndash;east along Mill Lane into Middle Acre Road; these overland flows contributed to flooding of highways, footpaths and residential properties in Bartley Green. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Bartley Brook breached at the point where it enters the culvert at Mill Lane (Breach Location 1). The breach produced overland flows running south&ndash;east along Mill Lane into Middle Acre Road, contributing to flooding of highways, footpaths and nearby properties (area including Middle Acre Road and Rush Green). [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Bartley Brook culvert between Mill Lane and Stonehouse Brook was inspected after the 16 June flood to assess structural condition and blockage; its capacity was recommended for further investigation to address flood issues. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A breach location is identified on Bartley Brook with predicted overland flow routes moving southeast through Dainton Grove and adjacent streets; the overland flow from this breach contributed to the internal flooding of one property in Dainton Grove. [IMG] (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (combined with Stonehouse Brook breaches) [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [IMG] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Bartley Brook,England,"Breach of the Bartley Brook where it enters the culvert at Mill Lane produced overland flows running south–east along Mill Lane into Middle Acre Road; these overland flows contributed to flooding of highways, footpaths and residential properties in Bartley Green. (p19)
The Bartley Brook breached at the point where it enters the culvert at Mill Lane (Breach Location 1). The breach produced overland flows running south–east along Mill Lane into Middle Acre Road, contributing to flooding of highways, footpaths and nearby properties (area including Middle Acre Road and Rush Green). [PAG,IMG] (p20)
The Bartley Brook culvert between Mill Lane and Stonehouse Brook was inspected after the 16 June flood to assess structural condition and blockage; its capacity was recommended for further investigation to address flood issues. [TAB,PAG] (p21)
