Blockage at the culvert entrance (approximately 250 m upstream of its confluence with Bourn Brook) led to the channel overtopping and flooding properties on Quinton Road; culvert was inspected and cleansed after the event. [MUL] (p39)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4333006,-1.9534188,"<div id=""html_09010cda32f74e2c96f4a2e744293424"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wood Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Wood Brook (an Environment Agency Main River) came out of channel where it enters the culvert at Bristol Road because channel and culvert capacity were exceeded, producing overland flow that flooded adjacent parkland, highway and properties. [PAG] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Wood Brook overtopped (came out of channel) where it enters the culvert at Bristol Road (Breach Location 1). Culvert and channel capacity were exceeded (culvert was not blocked), producing overland flow that flooded two adjacent properties, inundated parkland to the rear of properties on Witherford Way and Middle Park Road, and flooded the Bristol Road highway. [PAG] (p65)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties [PAG] (p65)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Wood Brook,England,"Wood Brook (an Environment Agency Main River) came out of channel where it enters the culvert at Bristol Road because channel and culvert capacity were exceeded, producing overland flow that flooded adjacent parkland, highway and properties. [PAG] (p64)
