435 incidents [MUL] (p78)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4315269,-1.9170747,"<div id=""html_a35324dc68b23a8a5e471c696e460438"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Rea</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flows from breached watercourses and overland surface water moved toward the River Rea. A boundary wall at the end of St John's Road prevented surface water discharging into the River Rea, which exacerbated flooding and increased flood depths in St John's Road; conversely, where runoff drained into the River Rea (e.g. at Third Avenue) ponding was reduced and flood depths were lower. [PAG] (p70)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>33 properties (across Pershore Road, Riverside Drive, St John's Road, Third Avenue and Fourth Avenue) [PAG] (p70)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,River Rea,England,"Flows from breached watercourses and overland surface water moved toward the River Rea. A boundary wall at the end of St John's Road prevented surface water discharging into the River Rea, which exacerbated flooding and increased flood depths in St John's Road; conversely, where runoff drained into the River Rea (e.g. at Third Avenue) ponding was reduced and flood depths were lower. [PAG] (p70)","33 properties (across Pershore Road, Riverside Drive, St John's Road, Third Avenue and Fourth Avenue) [PAG] (p70)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.490221,-1.8551892,"<div id=""html_eb1a78d01730e23c991dfc2d42d1342f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Alum Rock Road, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding within properties on Alum Rock Road and inundation of the surrounding highway and gardens caused by surface water overwhelming highway drainage (gullies restricted by debris) leading to overtopping into adjacent properties. [PAG,IMG] (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties [PAG,IMG] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Alum Rock Road, Birmingham",England,"Internal flooding within properties on Alum Rock Road and inundation of the surrounding highway and gardens caused by surface water overwhelming highway drainage (gullies restricted by debris) leading to overtopping into adjacent properties. [PAG,IMG] (p17)","3 properties [PAG,IMG] (p17)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4902092,-1.8316993,"<div id=""html_f95147b7d0f9198ab411c816f5841dd2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Woodwells Road, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map and figure identify a breach location at the intersection of Woodwells Road that generated an overland flow route directing water southward toward Alum Rock Road, contributing to highway inundation and the subsequent internal flooding of properties. [PAG,IMG] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Woodwells Road, Birmingham",England,"Map and figure identify a breach location at the intersection of Woodwells Road that generated an overland flow route directing water southward toward Alum Rock Road, contributing to highway inundation and the subsequent internal flooding of properties. [PAG,IMG] (p17)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
