Received overland flows routed from Mill Lane following the culvert breaches, resulting in roadway and adjacent property flooding in the locality. [PAG] (p20)","4 properties (in the vicinity of Middle Acre Road and Rush Green) [IMG,PAG] (p19)
4 properties [PAG] (p20)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4421453,-1.9831354,"<div id=""html_c498dce9c7a9bbb967e5676859167006"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rush Green, Bartley Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the vicinity of Rush Green were affected by the storms, with flooding of nearby highways and footpaths and property flooding reported. [IMG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwaters flowed into Rush Green from Mill Lane and Middle Acre Road following the breaches, contributing to highway and footpath flooding in the area and affecting nearby properties. [IMG] (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (area&ndash;wide; located in vicinity of Middle Acre Road and Rush Green) [IMG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties [IMG] (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Rush Green, Bartley Green",England,"Properties in the vicinity of Rush Green were affected by the storms, with flooding of nearby highways and footpaths and property flooding reported. [IMG] (p19)
Floodwaters flowed into Rush Green from Mill Lane and Middle Acre Road following the breaches, contributing to highway and footpath flooding in the area and affecting nearby properties. [IMG] (p20)","4 properties (area–wide; located in vicinity of Middle Acre Road and Rush Green) [IMG] (p19)
4 properties [IMG] (p20)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4393713,-1.9942102,"<div id=""html_205c38aedeeb7a5feb81eda688c3f883"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Green Drive, Bartley Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highways and footpaths on Green Drive were flooded during the storm event. (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Green Drive, Bartley Green",England,Highways and footpaths on Green Drive were flooded during the storm event. (p19),,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4398517,-1.9943105,"<div id=""html_4eeaa8b019cdfb624eb026a6edf0478d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ambleside, Bartley Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highways and footpaths in Ambleside were inundated during the storms; Bartley Brook runs to the rear of properties on Ambleside and nearby breaches contributed to local flooding. (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Ambleside, Bartley Green",England,Highways and footpaths in Ambleside were inundated during the storms; Bartley Brook runs to the rear of properties on Ambleside and nearby breaches contributed to local flooding. (p19),,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4418479,-1.9872847,"<div id=""html_61ef778e8837435eb8c5ed054972206f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mill Lane, Bartley Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two watercourse breaches occurred where culverts enter Mill Lane: the Bartley Brook breached at Mill Lane causing overland flows running south&ndash;east along Mill Lane into Middle Acre Road; the Stonehouse Brook also breached where it enters a culvert beneath Mill Lane, sending river waters into Mill Lane, along the footpath and into Middle Acre Road. These flows caused flooding of the highway and footpaths and contributed to nearby property flooding in Bartley Green. [IMG,PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flows from breaches at the Bartley Brook culvert (Breach Location 1) and the Stonehouse Brook culvert (Breach Location 2) ran south&ndash;eastwards along Mill Lane into Middle Acre Road, inundating the street, adjacent footpaths and directing floodwater towards nearby properties. [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties [IMG,PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Mill Lane, Bartley Green",England,"Two watercourse breaches occurred where culverts enter Mill Lane: the Bartley Brook breached at Mill Lane causing overland flows running south–east along Mill Lane into Middle Acre Road; the Stonehouse Brook also breached where it enters a culvert beneath Mill Lane, sending river waters into Mill Lane, along the footpath and into Middle Acre Road. These flows caused flooding of the highway and footpaths and contributed to nearby property flooding in Bartley Green. [IMG,PAG] (p19)
Overland flows from breaches at the Bartley Brook culvert (Breach Location 1) and the Stonehouse Brook culvert (Breach Location 2) ran south–eastwards along Mill Lane into Middle Acre Road, inundating the street, adjacent footpaths and directing floodwater towards nearby properties. [PAG,IMG] (p20)","4 properties [IMG,PAG] (p19)
4 properties [PAG,IMG] (p20)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4665343,-1.9729227,"<div id=""html_3353b0b2ffe0a5f9c56398556771b7ec"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Green Walk, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A breach location is mapped near the intersection of Green Walk; the identified flow route from that breach passes through the residential street network (including Green Walk), indicating overland flood flows through the street and potential inundation of the highway and adjacent properties/footpaths in the area. [IMG] (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Green Walk, Birmingham",England,"A breach location is mapped near the intersection of Green Walk; the identified flow route from that breach passes through the residential street network (including Green Walk), indicating overland flood flows through the street and potential inundation of the highway and adjacent properties/footpaths in the area. [IMG] (p19)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4383456,-1.9961268,"<div id=""html_cb942cda0e608f4108c85eb9c367cfd0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Dainton Grove, Bartley Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a property caused by storm rainfall flowing across the rear garden into the house (garden slopes toward property). Low kitchen/living room thresholds and a small patio drain (unable to cope with storm runoff) worsened ingress. [IMG] (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [IMG] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Dainton Grove, Bartley Green",England,Internal flooding of a property caused by storm rainfall flowing across the rear garden into the house (garden slopes toward property). Low kitchen/living room thresholds and a small patio drain (unable to cope with storm runoff) worsened ingress. [IMG] (p22),1 property [IMG] (p22),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4376822,-1.9963513,"<div id=""html_7738767d4a685cbf99137f8fd416c02a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pomeroy Road, Bartley Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A breach location is mapped near the intersection of Pomeroy Road and Dainton Grove; the breach produced overland flow paths moving southeast through adjacent residential streets and contributed to the surface&ndash;water flooding that led to internal flooding of a property in Dainton Grove. [IMG] (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [IMG] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Pomeroy Road, Bartley Green",England,A breach location is mapped near the intersection of Pomeroy Road and Dainton Grove; the breach produced overland flow paths moving southeast through adjacent residential streets and contributed to the surface–water flooding that led to internal flooding of a property in Dainton Grove. [IMG] (p22),1 property [IMG] (p22),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4334433,-1.9436417,"<div id=""html_8eae5011f23e6a726e804fa2bc913f8b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kingfisher Way, Selly Oak</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water and highway drainage flooding overtopped kerbs (including drop kerbs) and ponding on the highway flowed into lower&ndash;set properties; water ran over the highway, footpaths and gardens and entered a property causing internal flooding. (p26)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Kingfisher Way, Selly Oak",England,"Surface water and highway drainage flooding overtopped kerbs (including drop kerbs) and ponding on the highway flowed into lower–set properties; water ran over the highway, footpaths and gardens and entered a property causing internal flooding. (p26)",1 property (p26),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.563951,-1.7931564,"<div id=""html_c7955dbca356d9884d2422bf179a0e95"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Glover Road, Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flows from a reported breach in Churchill Brook and surface water runoff followed mapped flow routes into Glover Road, inundating the street and directing water toward the low point where ponding occurred. [IMG] (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Glover Road, Sutton Coldfield",England,"Overland flows from a reported breach in Churchill Brook and surface water runoff followed mapped flow routes into Glover Road, inundating the street and directing water toward the low point where ponding occurred. [IMG] (p28)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5530675,-1.8606568,"<div id=""html_1617d8f85d17115c546fce094bb6942b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Churchill Road, Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The low point located between Glover Road and Churchill Road ponded as overbank flows from Churchill Brook and routed surface water collected there, with highways conveying runoff into this area. [IMG] (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Churchill Road, Sutton Coldfield",England,"The low point located between Glover Road and Churchill Road ponded as overbank flows from Churchill Brook and routed surface water collected there, with highways conveying runoff into this area. [IMG] (p28)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5667347,-1.787939,"<div id=""html_c1651580c59ba61449ba41af356506e5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Falcon Lodge Crescent, Falcon Lodge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Located within the Falcon Lodge area and on the mapped flow&ndash;route network; during the storm highway drainage and sewer infrastructure were overwhelmed and highways acted as conveyance channels, allowing overland flows (exacerbated by dropped kerbs) to travel along streets and towards the low point where properties flooded. [IMG] (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Falcon Lodge Crescent, Falcon Lodge",England,"Located within the Falcon Lodge area and on the mapped flow–route network; during the storm highway drainage and sewer infrastructure were overwhelmed and highways acted as conveyance channels, allowing overland flows (exacerbated by dropped kerbs) to travel along streets and towards the low point where properties flooded. [IMG] (p28)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5671012,-1.792323,"<div id=""html_8172fc27746b691ec4fe609939ff2653"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Carhampton Road, Falcon Lodge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater ponded in a low point near properties after flows (reported to have come from Churchill Brook breaching its banks) and surface water runoff from surrounding properties and highways flowed through gardens and open space into the Carhampton Road area. [TAB] (p29)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Carhampton Road, Falcon Lodge",England,Floodwater ponded in a low point near properties after flows (reported to have come from Churchill Brook breaching its banks) and surface water runoff from surrounding properties and highways flowed through gardens and open space into the Carhampton Road area. [TAB] (p29),,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5891944,-1.8520891,"<div id=""html_7216f6fc4246a9057e073a698dbe3741"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Highcroft Drive, Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property experienced internal flooding when intense surface water runoff and overwhelmed drainage overtopped kerbs and entered the property; surrounding highway and garden inundation was also recorded in the immediate area. (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Highcroft Drive, Sutton Coldfield",England,One property experienced internal flooding when intense surface water runoff and overwhelmed drainage overtopped kerbs and entered the property; surrounding highway and garden inundation was also recorded in the immediate area. (p30),1 property (p30),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.588797,-1.8436484,"<div id=""html_5d58cb5ce63525e1b339fb3a32d91776"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Knighton Drive, Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highways and gardens in Knighton Drive were flooded as surface water runoff overwhelmed highway and sewer drainage during the storm. Historic internal property flooding exists for the street but no internal flooding was reported from the June 2016 storms. (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Knighton Drive, Sutton Coldfield",England,Highways and gardens in Knighton Drive were flooded as surface water runoff overwhelmed highway and sewer drainage during the storm. Historic internal property flooding exists for the street but no internal flooding was reported from the June 2016 storms. (p30),,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5916786,-1.8584323,"<div id=""html_8fba457f7ae51fc02133ec0bb211d99f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Park View Road, Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highways and gardens were flooded when intense rainfall overwhelmed property, highway and sewer drainage, allowing surface water to pond and overtop kerbs into low&ndash;lying areas. (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Park View Road, Sutton Coldfield",England,"Highways and gardens were flooded when intense rainfall overwhelmed property, highway and sewer drainage, allowing surface water to pond and overtop kerbs into low–lying areas. (p30)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5884726,-1.8543202,"<div id=""html_54cc32fbbad17cc367c7f9161cc75605"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Streetly Lane, Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map and report indicate potential overland flow routes and a breach north of Streetly Lane; highway inundation and overland flows occurred in the area as blocked gullies and overwhelmed drainage conveyed runoff along roads and into low&ndash;lying areas. [IMG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Streetly Lane, Sutton Coldfield",England,Map and report indicate potential overland flow routes and a breach north of Streetly Lane; highway inundation and overland flows occurred in the area as blocked gullies and overwhelmed drainage conveyed runoff along roads and into low–lying areas. [IMG] (p30),,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5375988,-1.8405074,"<div id=""html_18dfaec845d1203363dbcb722041f7ee"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Highfield Drive, Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Breach location identified on Highfield Drive as the origin of overland flow. Surface water from the intense storm generated an overland flow route here which inundated the highway and directed runoff southeast toward Crown Lane. Blocked highway gullies and overwhelmed drainage/sewer infrastructure contributed to local inundation; floodwaters later receded via onsite drainage. [IMG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Highfield Drive, Sutton Coldfield",England,Breach location identified on Highfield Drive as the origin of overland flow. Surface water from the intense storm generated an overland flow route here which inundated the highway and directed runoff southeast toward Crown Lane. Blocked highway gullies and overwhelmed drainage/sewer infrastructure contributed to local inundation; floodwaters later receded via onsite drainage. [IMG] (p30),,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5359966,-1.9301371,"<div id=""html_f72a00180828e65873c93f15211eca21"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Old Walsall Road, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported internal flooding to one property on the street; additional highway flooding and flooding of rear gardens occurred as surface water flowed from the adjacent open space into properties. (p32)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p32)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Old Walsall Road, Birmingham",England,Reported internal flooding to one property on the street; additional highway flooding and flooding of rear gardens occurred as surface water flowed from the adjacent open space into properties. (p32),1 property (p32),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5336016,-1.9289103,"<div id=""html_ad720d6f98f5a2f0a45a65cd50add0e1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Richmond Croft, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Large area of public open space adjacent to Richmond Croft is identified as the likely source of surface&ndash;water runoff; intense rainfall unable to soak away led to flow from the open space east&ndash;to&ndash;west into rear gardens of properties on Old Walsall Road. (p32)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Richmond Croft, Birmingham",England,Large area of public open space adjacent to Richmond Croft is identified as the likely source of surface–water runoff; intense rainfall unable to soak away led to flow from the open space east–to–west into rear gardens of properties on Old Walsall Road. (p32),,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5204293,-1.938862,"<div id=""html_cfa6a362e18c1ce4885ef93ee9aa1e6f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Grestone Avenue, Handsworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Greystone Avenue were flooded during the storm on 8th June 2016; surface water ponded at the low point of the road as highway and sewer drainage capacity was exceeded, allowing water to overtop kerbs and enter lower&ndash;lying properties. Sewer outfalls to Hilltop Brook were silted, compromising network capacity. (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Grestones Avenue reported internal flooding during the 8th June 2016 storm; the breach location at the watercourse near Greestones Avenue led to a surface flow route along Grestones Avenue, contributing to flooding of properties, highways and gardens. [IMG] (p36)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (across Greystone Avenue and Sunningdale Close) (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties [IMG] (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Grestone Avenue, Handsworth",England,"Properties on Greystone Avenue were flooded during the storm on 8th June 2016; surface water ponded at the low point of the road as highway and sewer drainage capacity was exceeded, allowing water to overtop kerbs and enter lower–lying properties. Sewer outfalls to Hilltop Brook were silted, compromising network capacity. (p34)
Properties on Grestones Avenue reported internal flooding during the 8th June 2016 storm; the breach location at the watercourse near Greestones Avenue led to a surface flow route along Grestones Avenue, contributing to flooding of properties, highways and gardens. [IMG] (p36)","3 properties (across Greystone Avenue and Sunningdale Close) (p34)
