GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5241021,-1.9411021,"<div id=""html_34733b222483a6fae038b73da17e7867"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sunningdale Close, Handsworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Sunningdale Close were reported flooded during the storm on 8th June 2016 as highway and sewer drainage were overwhelmed; surface water runoff followed the topography and ponded at low points, contributing to property flooding. (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse culvert passing under Sunningdale Close had its capacity compromised due to sediment accumulation and vegetation growth, preventing conveyance and contributing to local flooding. Highway gullies in the area were inspected and cleared by Highways. (p35)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (across Greystone Avenue and Sunningdale Close) (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Sunningdale Close, Handsworth",England,"Properties on Sunningdale Close were reported flooded during the storm on 8th June 2016 as highway and sewer drainage were overwhelmed; surface water runoff followed the topography and ponded at low points, contributing to property flooding. (p34)
The watercourse culvert passing under Sunningdale Close had its capacity compromised due to sediment accumulation and vegetation growth, preventing conveyance and contributing to local flooding. Highway gullies in the area were inspected and cleared by Highways. (p35)",3 properties (across Greystone Avenue and Sunningdale Close) (p34),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5266092,-1.9412767,"<div id=""html_997f23c55cb13a05559bc458873c3bc8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Craythorne Avenue, Handsworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the 8th June 2016 storm highways, footpaths and gardens in Craythorne Avenue were flooded as surface water runoff and overwhelmed drainage used highways as conveyance routes; ponding occurred at low points and full highway/sewer drains exacerbated local surface water flooding. (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Craythorne Avenue, Handsworth",England,"During the 8th June 2016 storm highways, footpaths and gardens in Craythorne Avenue were flooded as surface water runoff and overwhelmed drainage used highways as conveyance routes; ponding occurred at low points and full highway/sewer drains exacerbated local surface water flooding. (p34)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5297118,-1.9394446,"<div id=""html_4d409bf67e7534bf95feaec3c0b95011"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Acfold Road, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ponding occurred at the low point in Acfold Road during the storm; the highway became inundated and water overtopped kerbs, contributing to flows into properties lower than the road level. (p34)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (total in the Grestone area) (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Acfold Road, Birmingham",England,"Ponding occurred at the low point in Acfold Road during the storm; the highway became inundated and water overtopped kerbs, contributing to flows into properties lower than the road level. (p34)",3 properties (total in the Grestone area) (p34),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5237334,-1.937516,"<div id=""html_648e4f72b9485d274406fe0b6231ce9f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Medcroft Avenue, Handsworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map annotation shows the flow route crossing Medcroft Avenue; breach&ndash;related overland flow crossed the carriageway causing surface water flooding of the road during the event. [IMG] (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Medcroft Avenue, Handsworth",England,Map annotation shows the flow route crossing Medcroft Avenue; breach–related overland flow crossed the carriageway causing surface water flooding of the road during the event. [IMG] (p34),,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.517528,-1.9389799,"<div id=""html_53d28876e2b4295e42d1bd4f87a2033a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Silvercroft Avenue, Handsworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Six properties located within Silvercroft Avenue reported internal property flooding during the 8th June 2016 storm; adjacent footpath and highway were overtopped when flows in the Hilltop Brook exceeded the culvert capacity and flowed overland into properties and gardens. (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the intense storm on 8th June 2016, formal drainage was overwhelmed and surface water runoff ponded at the low point of Silvercroft Avenue. Water levels rose and overtopped kerbs, flowed down driveways and into properties situated at a lower level than the highway. (p37)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Silvercroft Avenue, Handsworth",England,"Six properties located within Silvercroft Avenue reported internal property flooding during the 8th June 2016 storm; adjacent footpath and highway were overtopped when flows in the Hilltop Brook exceeded the culvert capacity and flowed overland into properties and gardens. (p36)
During the intense storm on 8th June 2016, formal drainage was overwhelmed and surface water runoff ponded at the low point of Silvercroft Avenue. Water levels rose and overtopped kerbs, flowed down driveways and into properties situated at a lower level than the highway. (p37)",6 properties (p36),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4469195,-1.9636595,"<div id=""html_efdcf6250be4333b28f62ace4fcedfd3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Osmaston Road, Metchley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rear garden flooding and internal property flooding caused by Bourn Brook exceeding channel capacity during the 16 June 2016 storm; impacts were exacerbated by debris/vegetation and silt reducing channel/bridge capacity upstream. [IMG] (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal property flooding reported (rear garden and internal flooding attributed to the Bourn Brook exceeding capacity). Properties also experienced front&ndash;of&ndash;house sewer/highway flooding; highways were inundated and gullies could not discharge to the overloaded sewer system. Foul flooding was reported at this location. [PAG] (p39)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>33 incidents of internal property flooding (total across Osmaston Road, Swinford Road, Elford Road, Reservoir Road, Quinton Road and Lismore Drive) [IMG] (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>33 properties (total across Osmaston Road, Swinford Road, Elford Road, Reservoir Road, Quinton Road and Lismore Drive) [PAG] (p39)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Osmaston Road, Metchley",England,"Rear garden flooding and internal property flooding caused by Bourn Brook exceeding channel capacity during the 16 June 2016 storm; impacts were exacerbated by debris/vegetation and silt reducing channel/bridge capacity upstream. [IMG] (p38)
