GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4541268,-1.9668574,"<div id=""html_5b925dd1b3498ea532065c97a8c4df6b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fredas Grove, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a residential property; surface water entered and flowed through rear gardens into properties and onto the highway, with highways and gardens flooded. Highway drainage and sewer infrastructure were unable to accommodate the runoff, allowing surface water to accumulate at the low point immediately west of properties. [IMG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the storm on 16th June 2016 surface water runoff from Harborne Golf Course collected at a low point immediately west of properties, flowed through rear gardens and properties into the highway. This caused internal flooding to a property, inundation of gardens and highways, and overwhelmed highway drainage and sewer infrastructure. The historic culverted watercourse may have exacerbated runoff by removing a natural discharge route. [PAG,IMG] (p42)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [IMG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [PAG,IMG] (p42)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Fredas Grove, Birmingham",England,"Internal flooding of a residential property; surface water entered and flowed through rear gardens into properties and onto the highway, with highways and gardens flooded. Highway drainage and sewer infrastructure were unable to accommodate the runoff, allowing surface water to accumulate at the low point immediately west of properties. [IMG] (p41)
