GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.534349,-1.9035014,"<div id=""html_3252f210091cfb21c6a973c4cdceb43d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Haddon Road, Perry Beeches</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal property flooding occurred on Haddon Road as part of the 44 reported incidents; highway and garden flooding were also reported. Overwhelmed highway drainage and public sewers and overland flows increased flood levels at low points along the road. (p54)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding at the valley low point: overland surface water flows and overwhelmed highway drainage/public sewers caused rising water levels that flooded highways, gardens and properties on Haddon Road. Water from the Motorway Control Centre also entered rear gardens of Haddon Road (via Thornbridge Avenue) contributing to property/garden flooding. [PAG] (p55)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rear gardens of Haddon Road were flooded by water flowing from the Motorway Control Centre/Thornbridge Avenue during the storm; floodwaters subsequently receded through gullies and overland flow routes into watercourses. (p56)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>44 properties (across 10 roads in the Beeches Estate) (p54)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Haddon Road, Perry Beeches",England,"Internal property flooding occurred on Haddon Road as part of the 44 reported incidents; highway and garden flooding were also reported. Overwhelmed highway drainage and public sewers and overland flows increased flood levels at low points along the road. (p54)
