Rear gardens of Haddon Road were flooded by water flowing from the Motorway Control Centre/Thornbridge Avenue during the storm; floodwaters subsequently receded through gullies and overland flow routes into watercourses. (p56)",44 properties (across 10 roads in the Beeches Estate) (p54),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5379471,-1.904286,"<div id=""html_31dbb97cc26d3f0caf2d8e009ac7c154"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hassop Road, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal property flooding was reported on this road as part of the Beeches Estate event; local highway and garden flooding also affected the area. Manhole covers were reported blown off in the wider area due to sewer surcharge. (p54)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the Perry Brook (open channel) flooded out upstream of where the brook enters a culvert at Hassop Road; this water flowed into Hassop Road and caused property flooding. [PAG] (p55)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Water from Perry Brook flooded out of the open channel upstream of the Hassop Road culvert (breach location), flooded adjacent allotments and Chervil Close, then flowed into Hassop Road and flooded properties; flows continued down Becton Grove and contributed to flooding at the rear of properties in Thornbridge Avenue and other nearby streets. [PAG] (p56)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>44 properties (across 10 roads) (p54)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Hassop Road, Birmingham",England,"Internal property flooding was reported on this road as part of the Beeches Estate event; local highway and garden flooding also affected the area. Manhole covers were reported blown off in the wider area due to sewer surcharge. (p54)
