GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5903114,-1.8120286,"<div id=""html_4b092e24e483200cba7485805f422a23"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Willmott Road, Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff flowed south along Willmott Road and accumulated in a low point in the highway, causing ponding; water overtopped kerbs and then flowed into property curtilages and down through rear gardens toward Marlpit Lane and Slade Road, contributing to internal property flooding. [IMG,MUL] (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff followed local topography, ponding occurred in the highway as highway drainage and the underlying sewer infrastructure could not cope; water overtopped kerbs and flowed into property curtilages and down the hill toward Marlpit Lane and Slade Road. [PAG,MUL] (p62)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Willmott Road, Sutton Coldfield",England,"Surface water runoff flowed south along Willmott Road and accumulated in a low point in the highway, causing ponding; water overtopped kerbs and then flowed into property curtilages and down through rear gardens toward Marlpit Lane and Slade Road, contributing to internal property flooding. [IMG,MUL] (p61)
Surface water runoff followed local topography, ponding occurred in the highway as highway drainage and the underlying sewer infrastructure could not cope; water overtopped kerbs and flowed into property curtilages and down the hill toward Marlpit Lane and Slade Road. [PAG,MUL] (p62)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5894447,-1.8110464,"<div id=""html_c3d301972a74b2255e0716a6b114603a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Marlpit Lane, Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Marlpit Lane had water enter from flows travelling down the hill and through rear gardens following ponding and overtopping of highway drainage, resulting in internal flooding during the June 2016 storms. [IMG,MUL] (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from Willmott Road flowed down through rear gardens and entered properties on Marlpit Lane. [PAG,MUL] (p62)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Marlpit Lane, Sutton Coldfield",England,"Properties on Marlpit Lane had water enter from flows travelling down the hill and through rear gardens following ponding and overtopping of highway drainage, resulting in internal flooding during the June 2016 storms. [IMG,MUL] (p61)
Floodwater from Willmott Road flowed down through rear gardens and entered properties on Marlpit Lane. [PAG,MUL] (p62)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5896048,-1.8082389,"<div id=""html_ae9dad79080a941ab8cb8a1df0b15578"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Slade Road, Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Slade Road experienced internal flooding as runoff accumulated and sewer infrastructure became overwhelmed and began to surcharge onto the highway, allowing water to enter properties during the June 2016 storms. [IMG,PAG,MUL] (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Slade Road experienced flooding as overland flows accumulated there; flooding was exacerbated when the sewer infrastructure was overwhelmed and began to surcharge from the underground system onto the highway. Property&ndash;level resilience measures had been installed prior to June 2016 and were subsequently investigated and remediated by Severn Trent Water. [PAG,MUL] (p62)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Slade Road, Sutton Coldfield",England,"Properties on Slade Road experienced internal flooding as runoff accumulated and sewer infrastructure became overwhelmed and began to surcharge onto the highway, allowing water to enter properties during the June 2016 storms. [IMG,PAG,MUL] (p61)
Slade Road experienced flooding as overland flows accumulated there; flooding was exacerbated when the sewer infrastructure was overwhelmed and began to surcharge from the underground system onto the highway. Property–level resilience measures had been installed prior to June 2016 and were subsequently investigated and remediated by Severn Trent Water. [PAG,MUL] (p62)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
