GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4451052,-1.9933296,"<div id=""html_c510a8ffb5028a3cb3938bebf174f338"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Warston Avenue, Bartley Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flow routes originating in Ox Leasow and Warston Avenue followed topography, accumulating in Sommerfield Road and passing through the area; highway and sewer drainage were overwhelmed and properties on Warston Avenue experienced internal flooding. (p72)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>38 properties (across Woodgate Valley) (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Warston Avenue, Bartley Green",England,"Overland flow routes originating in Ox Leasow and Warston Avenue followed topography, accumulating in Sommerfield Road and passing through the area; highway and sewer drainage were overwhelmed and properties on Warston Avenue experienced internal flooding. (p72)",38 properties (across Woodgate Valley) (p72),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4456717,-1.9941025,"<div id=""html_d79ce95437cedee90764fcce6abbc8a2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>County Close, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water and overloaded sewer/highway drainage ponded in low areas and flowed into properties on County Close, causing internal flooding as part of the central Woodgate Valley impacts. (p72)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>38 properties (across Woodgate Valley) (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"County Close, Birmingham",England,"Surface water and overloaded sewer/highway drainage ponded in low areas and flowed into properties on County Close, causing internal flooding as part of the central Woodgate Valley impacts. (p72)",38 properties (across Woodgate Valley) (p72),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4455391,-1.9907624,"<div id=""html_f73f8a901f6272e9c762eeaccfc494b2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sommerfield Road, Bartley Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flow accumulated in the street during the extreme rainfall; runoff ponded in the highway and entered properties, causing internal flooding before receding as gullies and sewer capacity returned. (p72)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>38 properties (across Woodgate Valley) (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Sommerfield Road, Bartley Green",England,"Overland flow accumulated in the street during the extreme rainfall; runoff ponded in the highway and entered properties, causing internal flooding before receding as gullies and sewer capacity returned. (p72)",38 properties (across Woodgate Valley) (p72),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4457071,-1.987822,"<div id=""html_0c8f6c4894b6ca8b22a22cb9a5541f5e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rushy Piece, Bartley Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff followed the local topography into low&ndash;lying Rushy Piece where it ponded and passed through properties, causing internal flooding during the storm. (p72)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>38 properties (across Woodgate Valley) (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Rushy Piece, Bartley Green",England,"Runoff followed the local topography into low–lying Rushy Piece where it ponded and passed through properties, causing internal flooding during the storm. (p72)",38 properties (across Woodgate Valley) (p72),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4451071,-1.9864565,"<div id=""html_ccf9f409fbf4a45a65bb6aef0a46cb2b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Gravel Bank, Bartley Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Low&ndash;lying Gravel Bank experienced ponding and overland flow through properties as highway and property drainage were overwhelmed, resulting in internal flooding. (p72)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>38 properties (across Woodgate Valley) (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Gravel Bank, Bartley Green",England,"Low–lying Gravel Bank experienced ponding and overland flow through properties as highway and property drainage were overwhelmed, resulting in internal flooding. (p72)",38 properties (across Woodgate Valley) (p72),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4468749,-1.9420621,"<div id=""html_4d1e80d58945a6dec6601fbe63570368"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bourn Brook Walkway</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Debris caught on the new footbridge upstream of the confluence with Stonehouse Brook (marked as Breach Location 2), contributing to blockage and localised flooding/overland flow. [MUL] (p39)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Bourn Brook Walkway,England,"Debris caught on the new footbridge upstream of the confluence with Stonehouse Brook (marked as Breach Location 2), contributing to blockage and localised flooding/overland flow. [MUL] (p39)",,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.487072,-1.8315299,"<div id=""html_6c04702cd27cc4c6677b0f549c51f6bc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Alum Rock</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties in the Alum Rock area, inundation of surrounding highway and gardens due to surface water and restricted highway drainage; floodwaters receded slowly because gullies were restricted by debris. [PAG,IMG] (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties [PAG,IMG] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Alum Rock,England,"Internal flooding of properties in the Alum Rock area, inundation of surrounding highway and gardens due to surface water and restricted highway drainage; floodwaters receded slowly because gullies were restricted by debris. [PAG,IMG] (p17)","3 properties [PAG,IMG] (p17)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
