GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5623089,-1.8239794,"<div id=""html_8858117c87a300fc4162bdbff759f8a1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sutton Coldfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Falcon Lodge area of Sutton Coldfield had internal property flooding following the extreme rainfall on 16 June when drainage and sewer systems were overwhelmed and Churchill Brook overtopped, contributing additional flows. (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of Sutton Coldfield (the Roughley neighbourhood) experienced internal flooding during the June 2016 storms when surface water runoff and surcharging sewers caused water to enter properties on local streets (Willmott Road, Marlpit Lane and Slade Road). [IMG,MUL] (p61)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties [IMG,MUL] (p61)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Sutton Coldfield,England,"The Falcon Lodge area of Sutton Coldfield had internal property flooding following the extreme rainfall on 16 June when drainage and sewer systems were overwhelmed and Churchill Brook overtopped, contributing additional flows. (p28)
