GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5391117,-1.9378209,"<div id=""html_8190916a51467864e7b04e56f1c5c77c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hamstead</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from nearby open space flowed west into rear gardens and onto the highway, causing garden and highway flooding and leading to one property experiencing internal flooding. (p32)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p32)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Hamstead,England,"Surface water runoff from nearby open space flowed west into rear gardens and onto the highway, causing garden and highway flooding and leading to one property experiencing internal flooding. (p32)",1 property (p32),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5182394,-1.9192787,"<div id=""html_22dc6c3575e078194452f50da0b0d566"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Handsworth Wood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storm on 8th June 2016 overwhelmed property, highway and sewer drainage across the area. Surface water runoff followed local topography and highways, causing inundation of roads and ponding at low points; sewer outfalls into Hilltop Brook were compromised by sediment and silt, leaving highway drainage and sewers full and exacerbating surface water flooding. (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the storm on 8th June 2016 parts of Handsworth Wood (the Silvercroft area) experienced internal property flooding (residential), plus flooding of highways, footpaths and gardens caused by the Hilltop Brook overtopping when a culvert exceeded capacity. (p36)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Handsworth Wood,England,"Storm on 8th June 2016 overwhelmed property, highway and sewer drainage across the area. Surface water runoff followed local topography and highways, causing inundation of roads and ponding at low points; sewer outfalls into Hilltop Brook were compromised by sediment and silt, leaving highway drainage and sewers full and exacerbating surface water flooding. (p34)
During the storm on 8th June 2016 parts of Handsworth Wood (the Silvercroft area) experienced internal property flooding (residential), plus flooding of highways, footpaths and gardens caused by the Hilltop Brook overtopping when a culvert exceeded capacity. (p36)","3 properties (p34)
6 properties (p36)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.522199105434716,-1.9378325934940912,"<div id=""html_41ba8a4e6d91d8d53889056d78e8a9df"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Grestone</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the 8th June 2016 storm, surface water and sewer flooding occurred in the Grestone area; runoff ponded at low points, highway drainage was overwhelmed and sewer outfalls to Hilltop Brook were found to be silted, reducing capacity and worsening local flooding. (p34)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Grestone,England,"During the 8th June 2016 storm, surface water and sewer flooding occurred in the Grestone area; runoff ponded at low points, highway drainage was overwhelmed and sewer outfalls to Hilltop Brook were found to be silted, reducing capacity and worsening local flooding. (p34)",3 properties (p34),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.50883,-1.9387301,"<div id=""html_bbddecabfc262813f98e9d21a02bac13"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Handsworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Six properties on Silvercroft Avenue and Grestones Avenue experienced internal property flooding; highways, footpaths and gardens were also flooded in the Handsworth Wood &ndash; Silvercroft area. [IMG] (p36)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties [IMG] (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Handsworth,England,"Six properties on Silvercroft Avenue and Grestones Avenue experienced internal property flooding; highways, footpaths and gardens were also flooded in the Handsworth Wood – Silvercroft area. [IMG] (p36)",6 properties [IMG] (p36),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.4595363,-1.9503355,"<div id=""html_e9356a9557e8160468f0dd76c79e0196"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Harborne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall exceeded infiltration across Harborne Golf Course producing substantial surface water runoff that flowed uncontrolled from the course toward lower ground; this runoff contributed to subsequent inundation of nearby properties and highways. A historic culverted watercourse on the golf course (now part of sewer infrastructure) may have exacerbated the surface water flooding by removing an overland discharge route. [IMG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall produced surface water runoff from Queen's Park that was directed southwards through the park into residential parts of Harborne, resulting in internal flooding of properties (Queen's Court and Harts Green Road) and flooding of highways, footpaths and gardens on nearby streets. [IMG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the storm on 16th June 2016 intense rainfall produced surface water runoff that, combined with overwhelmed highway drainage and sewer infrastructure, caused flooding to highways, footpaths and gardens in streets around Queen's Park (including Lelant Grove, Conington Grove and Battenhall Road) and led to ponding in low points. [PAG,IMG] (p44)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties (in Queen's Court and Harts Green Road) [IMG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 internal property flooding incidents [PAG,IMG] (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Harborne,England,"Intense rainfall exceeded infiltration across Harborne Golf Course producing substantial surface water runoff that flowed uncontrolled from the course toward lower ground; this runoff contributed to subsequent inundation of nearby properties and highways. A historic culverted watercourse on the golf course (now part of sewer infrastructure) may have exacerbated the surface water flooding by removing an overland discharge route. [IMG] (p41)
Intense rainfall produced surface water runoff from Queen's Park that was directed southwards through the park into residential parts of Harborne, resulting in internal flooding of properties (Queen's Court and Harts Green Road) and flooding of highways, footpaths and gardens on nearby streets. [IMG] (p43)
During the storm on 16th June 2016 intense rainfall produced surface water runoff that, combined with overwhelmed highway drainage and sewer infrastructure, caused flooding to highways, footpaths and gardens in streets around Queen's Park (including Lelant Grove, Conington Grove and Battenhall Road) and led to ponding in low points. [PAG,IMG] (p44)","6 properties (in Queen's Court and Harts Green Road) [IMG] (p43)
6 internal property flooding incidents [PAG,IMG] (p44)",GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.516903,-1.9012399,"<div id=""html_1f3e33b5f4baa0fa1a5cda27198f2b7f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Perry Barr</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Perry Barr (notably Church Road and Perry Park area) were affected by river and sewer flooding during the storm, with overland flows from a breached Perry Brook and sewer surcharging contributing to property flooding. (p51)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p51)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Perry Barr,England,"Parts of Perry Barr (notably Church Road and Perry Park area) were affected by river and sewer flooding during the storm, with overland flows from a breached Perry Brook and sewer surcharging contributing to property flooding. (p51)",2 properties (p51),GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc.html,GB-BIR_1_2016-06-08_etc,"Birmingham flooding 08 Jun 2016, Birmingham flooding 10 Jun 2016 and Birmingham flooding 16 Jun 2016","June 2016 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2016/Birmingham/S19/Flooding/Report///June/2016/R1.pdf
GB-BIR,1,2016-06-08,52.5381615,-1.9163042,"<div id=""html_8d8d455de708eaaffb91029d0571beb7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Perry Beeches</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding following the storm on 8th June 2016: 44 incidents of internal property flooding across the Beeches Estate (affecting Beeches Road, Bradfield Road, Curbar Road, Grindleford Road, Haddon Road, Hassop Road, Sterndale Road, Thornbridge Avenue, Trehurst Avenue and Turnberry Road). Garden and highway flooding occurred across much of the area; highway drainage and public sewer infrastructure were overwhelmed (manhole covers were blown off by escaping water) and overland flows down steep roads added to flood levels. (p54)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding on 8th June 2016: 44 incidents of internal property flooding reported across 10 roads on the Beeches Estate (including Beeches Road, Grindleford Road, Haddon Road, Hassop Road, Thornbridge Avenue and others). Garden and highway flooding occurred across much of the area; manhole covers were blown off by pressurised sewer discharge as systems were overwhelmed, increasing flood levels and causing flooding to highways, gardens and low&ndash;lying properties. [PAG,IMG] (p55)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flow routes and Perry Brook river flooding affected residential areas in Perry Beeches; the Risk of Flooding from Surface Water map for Perry Beeches correlates with areas flooded on 8th June, with flows funnelled by local topography toward valley low points. [PAG,IMG] (p56)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>44 incidents of internal property flooding; 10 roads reported with internal property flooding (p54)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>44 properties; 10 roads with internal property flooding; more than 20 roads with garden/highway flooding [PAG,IMG] (p55)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Perry Beeches,England,"Significant flooding following the storm on 8th June 2016: 44 incidents of internal property flooding across the Beeches Estate (affecting Beeches Road, Bradfield Road, Curbar Road, Grindleford Road, Haddon Road, Hassop Road, Sterndale Road, Thornbridge Avenue, Trehurst Avenue and Turnberry Road). Garden and highway flooding occurred across much of the area; highway drainage and public sewer infrastructure were overwhelmed (manhole covers were blown off by escaping water) and overland flows down steep roads added to flood levels. (p54)
