at least 10 properties [PAG] (p17)",GB-DER_2_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_2_2014-07-19,Derby flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Bishops Drive, Oakwood 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Bishops-Drive-Oakwood-S19.pdf
GB-DER,2,2014-07-19,52.9402028,-1.4328741,"<div id=""html_4cd619e9ba09964d03a6e853c9b2a27f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Saffron Drive, Derby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported severe highway flooding and external (garden) flooding during the event. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Saffron Drive experienced internal flooding (internal water ingress to homes) as part of the Oakwood flood. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes on the street experienced internal flooding; highways and gardens in the area suffered severe external property flooding, in some cases close to entering ground&ndash;floor living areas. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from an intense short&ndash;duration storm overwhelmed the urban drainage network; surface water flowed along localised routes, accumulated in low spots and affected Saffron Drive, causing internal flooding and damage to ground&ndash;floor living areas. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff and surcharging surface water manholes (with reports of foul sewer surcharging) led to internal flooding of properties up to a reported depth of 230 mm, causing extensive internal property damage. [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff flowed down local topography into Saffron Drive causing internal flooding of ground&ndash;floor living areas and extensive internal property damage; the foul sewer system also surcharged on Saffron Drive (unclear whether internal foul&ndash;water flooding occurred). [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents reported property flooding during the storm on 19th July 2014; reports of foul (sewer) water flooding from Saffron Drive were made to City Council officers and recorded in STW sewer records. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 9 residential properties (across Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close) (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>At least 10 homes affected internally across the six listed streets (collectively). (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 10 properties (internally flooded across the affected area) (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties; 230 mm depth [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties; internal flood depth up to 230 mm [PAG] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Saffron Drive, Derby",England,"Reported severe highway flooding and external (garden) flooding during the event. (p3)
