GB-DER,2,2014-07-19,52.9417225,-1.4354896,"<div id=""html_0f12884d1b2a83aec09be0400e9f7d9d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Columbine Close, Derby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe highway and external garden flooding on the street during the event. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Columbine Close experienced internal flooding (internal water ingress to homes) as part of the Oakwood flood. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes on the street experienced internal flooding; highways and gardens in the area suffered severe external property flooding, in some cases close to entering ground&ndash;floor living areas. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the urban area where the surface water sewer and local topography led to exceedance of drainage capacity; overland flows and ponding resulted in surface&ndash;water flooding affecting properties on Columbine Close during the storm. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two properties flooded internally and up to four other properties experienced external garden flooding. Residents reported accumulation of surface water on the highway, runoff downslope from upslope streets, surcharging of surface water sewer manholes (potentially on Bishops Drive) increasing overland flow towards Columbine Close, and surcharging of foul and surface water manholes on Columbine Close; lifting of the road surface was also reported. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents reported property flooding associated with the storm on 19th July 2014; foul water (sewer) flooding incidents were reported to council officers and recorded in sewer records. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>internal flood damage of at least 10 properties (across the affected area including this street) (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 9 residential properties (across Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close) (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>At least 10 homes affected internally across the six listed streets (collectively). (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 10 properties (across the affected Bishops Drive area) (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties; up to 4 properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Columbine Close, Derby",England,"Severe highway and external garden flooding on the street during the event. (p3)
Residential properties on Columbine Close experienced internal flooding (internal water ingress to homes) as part of the Oakwood flood. (p4)
