GB-DER,2,2014-07-19,52.9432822,-1.4379081,"<div id=""html_3a99a7432621eee3db30ada8f86398f7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Morefern Drive, Derby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe highway and external garden flooding on the street during the event. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Morefern Drive experienced internal flooding (internal water ingress to homes) as part of the Oakwood flood. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes on the street experienced internal flooding; highways and gardens in the area suffered severe external property flooding, in some cases close to entering ground&ndash;floor living areas. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from a surcharged manhole and runoff across Chandlers Ford recreation ground flowed down slope into the Wood Brook valley and onto Morefern Drive, washing towards property boundaries; this overland flow and sewer exceedance caused flooding at property boundaries and internal flooding to at least one property and significant flooding to others. [PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water originating from the adjacent recreation ground (unable to enter the watercourse) spilled under garden boundary fences and entered properties, causing internal flooding. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents reported flooding of properties during the storm on 19th July 2014; incidents of foul (sewer) water flooding in the area were reported to City Council officers and councillors and recorded in Severn Trent Water sewer records. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>internal flood damage of at least 10 properties (across the affected area including this street) (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 9 