GB-DER,2,2014-07-19,52.9428896,-1.4257494,"<div id=""html_2bf134c16c6636f6d43a3f90beac5cd2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Earls Crescent, Oakwood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The junction area at Earls Crescent (with Bishops Drive) was a local topographical low where surface water accumulated during the storm; evidence of foul&ndash;water flooding was photographed near Earls Crescent shortly after the event. [PAG,IMG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Evidence of foul water (sewer) flooding occurring near Earls Crescent during the event; photographed two days after the storm. [PAG] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Earls Crescent, Oakwood",England,"The junction area at Earls Crescent (with Bishops Drive) was a local topographical low where surface water accumulated during the storm; evidence of foul–water flooding was photographed near Earls Crescent shortly after the event. [PAG,IMG] (p15)
