GB-DER,2,2014-07-19,52.9467889,-1.4231323,"<div id=""html_3315cd417533a63d188ccb7188b49995"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Springwood Drive, Oakwood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal foul water flooding: pressure in the foul sewer forced water/ sewage back up into the ground&ndash;floor toilet of a property on Springwood Close (sic) during the event. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Springwood Drive, Oakwood",England,Internal foul water flooding: pressure in the foul sewer forced water/ sewage back up into the ground–floor toilet of a property on Springwood Close (sic) during the event. (p16),1 property (p16),GB-DER_2_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_2_2014-07-19,Derby flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Bishops Drive, Oakwood 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Bishops-Drive-Oakwood-S19.pdf
GB-DER,2,2014-07-19,52.9222738,-1.3940171,"<div id=""html_6450f4fc0fce9d04d6858efa0d39f32d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Caernarvon Close, Derby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Foul (sewer) water flooded a property; this foul water flooding was reported internally and may have been caused by misconnections allowing surface water to enter the foul sewer system. (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Caernarvon Close, Derby",England,Foul (sewer) water flooded a property; this foul water flooding was reported internally and may have been caused by misconnections allowing surface water to enter the foul sewer system. (p17),1 property (p17),GB-DER_2_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_2_2014-07-19,Derby flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Bishops Drive, Oakwood 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Bishops-Drive-Oakwood-S19.pdf
GB-DER,2,2014-07-19,53.118504,-1.556618,"<div id=""html_2954091b76d915179fd8afd436f39364"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Derbyshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>19th July 2014: Intense local thunderstorms produced surface water/urban flooding in the Oakwood area of Derby. At the peak (around 15:30) internal flooding was reported in residential properties on Bishops Drive, Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close; highways and gardens in these areas also suffered severe external flooding, in some cases approaching ground&ndash;floor living areas. 6th July 2012: A separate storm caused external property flooding to a single property on Foxglove Drive; this was attributed to surface water runoff from adjacent fields and there was no internal flooding reported. [IMG,MUL] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 10 homes; 1 property [IMG,MUL] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,Derbyshire,England,"19th July 2014: Intense local thunderstorms produced surface water/urban flooding in the Oakwood area of Derby. At the peak (around 15:30) internal flooding was reported in residential properties on Bishops Drive, Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close; highways and gardens in these areas also suffered severe external flooding, in some cases approaching ground–floor living areas. 6th July 2012: A separate storm caused external property flooding to a single property on Foxglove Drive; this was attributed to surface water runoff from adjacent fields and there was no internal flooding reported. [IMG,MUL] (p10)","at least 10 homes; 1 property [IMG,MUL] (p10)",GB-DER_2_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_2_2014-07-19,Derby flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Bishops Drive, Oakwood 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Bishops-Drive-Oakwood-S19.pdf
GB-DER,2,2014-07-19,52.9425771,-1.4326983,"<div id=""html_eb13d97477c53913c31eea2f66f7ff3a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oakwood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced intense rainfall&ndash;driven surface water flooding: a cluster of properties in the Bishops Drive area suffered internal flooding and there were further isolated cases of internal and external (highway and garden) flooding elsewhere in Oakwood. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties: at least nine homes in the streets Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close were internally flooded, prompting a formal Section 19 investigation. [PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Oakwood area of Derby City was affected by the 19 July 2014 flood event. At least nine residential properties were internally flooded (Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close). The City Council identified a significant cluster of reported internal and external property flooding from a number of sources and highway flooding in the Bishops Drive area. [PAG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Many areas of Oakwood were affected by the 19 July 2014 flood, including internal and external property flooding and highway flooding. The City Council identified a significant cluster of reported internal and external property flooding from multiple sources and highway flooding concentrated in the Bishops Drive area. Flooding was associated with rapid concentration of surface water to the public surface water sewer outfall to local watercourses. [PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal property flooding was reported for the first time in Oakwood during the event; accounts from residents and City Council site visits recorded internal flooding of properties following heavy thundery rainfall. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localized surface&ndash;water and urban flooding on 19th July 2014 caused internal property flooding in Oakwood (Derby). Peak impacts occurred around 15:30 when at least 10 homes were internally flooded on Bishops Drive, Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close. Highways and gardens in these areas also suffered severe external flooding, in some cases close to entering ground&ndash;floor living areas. Separately, a storm on 6th July 2012 caused external flooding to a single property on Foxglove Drive from surface water run&ndash;off from adjacent fields. [PAG,IMG,MUL] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>In the late afternoon of 19 July 2014 (peak around 3:30pm) at least 10 homes in the Oakwood area were affected by internal flooding. Properties on Bishops Drive, Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close experienced internal flooding; an undetermined number of properties in these streets also suffered severe external flooding to highways and gardens, with floodwater in some cases close to entering ground&ndash;floor living areas. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>An intense, highly localised storm on 19 July 2014 caused rapid surface water generation and exceedance of the public surface water sewer system. Floodwaters propagated along local overland flow routes toward the Wood Brook and Oakwood Brook valleys. At least 10 homes were flooded internally on Bishops Drive, Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close. An undetermined number of properties suffered severe external flooding to highways and gardens, with some external inundation close to entering ground&ndash;floor living areas. [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding focused on a cluster of streets between Bishops Drive and Wood Brook; intense runoff and exceeded drainage caused significant flooding to properties and highways in Oakwood. The council carried out formal Section 19 investigations into the impacts. (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>An intense thunderstorm hit Oakwood on the afternoon of 19 July 2014 and caused surface water flooding when highway and private surface water exceeded drainage capacity. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 10 properties (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 residential properties [PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 9 residential properties internally flooded [PAG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 10 homes internally flooded; 1 property externally flooded (Foxglove Drive, 6th July 2012) [PAG,IMG,MUL] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 10 homes [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 10 homes [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 10 properties (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,Oakwood,England,"Experienced intense rainfall–driven surface water flooding: a cluster of properties in the Bishops Drive area suffered internal flooding and there were further isolated cases of internal and external (highway and garden) flooding elsewhere in Oakwood. (p3)
Internal flooding of residential properties: at least nine homes in the streets Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close were internally flooded, prompting a formal Section 19 investigation. [PAG] (p4)
The Oakwood area of Derby City was affected by the 19 July 2014 flood event. At least nine residential properties were internally flooded (Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close). The City Council identified a significant cluster of reported internal and external property flooding from a number of sources and highway flooding in the Bishops Drive area. [PAG] (p5)
Many areas of Oakwood were affected by the 19 July 2014 flood, including internal and external property flooding and highway flooding. The City Council identified a significant cluster of reported internal and external property flooding from multiple sources and highway flooding concentrated in the Bishops Drive area. Flooding was associated with rapid concentration of surface water to the public surface water sewer outfall to local watercourses. [PAG] (p6)
Internal property flooding was reported for the first time in Oakwood during the event; accounts from residents and City Council site visits recorded internal flooding of properties following heavy thundery rainfall. [PAG] (p9)
Localized surface–water and urban flooding on 19th July 2014 caused internal property flooding in Oakwood (Derby). Peak impacts occurred around 15:30 when at least 10 homes were internally flooded on Bishops Drive, Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close. Highways and gardens in these areas also suffered severe external flooding, in some cases close to entering ground–floor living areas. Separately, a storm on 6th July 2012 caused external flooding to a single property on Foxglove Drive from surface water run–off from adjacent fields. [PAG,IMG,MUL] (p10)
In the late afternoon of 19 July 2014 (peak around 3:30pm) at least 10 homes in the Oakwood area were affected by internal flooding. Properties on Bishops Drive, Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close experienced internal flooding; an undetermined number of properties in these streets also suffered severe external flooding to highways and gardens, with floodwater in some cases close to entering ground–floor living areas. [PAG] (p11)
An intense, highly localised storm on 19 July 2014 caused rapid surface water generation and exceedance of the public surface water sewer system. Floodwaters propagated along local overland flow routes toward the Wood Brook and Oakwood Brook valleys. At least 10 homes were flooded internally on Bishops Drive, Saffron Drive, Columbine Close, Santolina Drive, Morefern Drive and Bryony Close. An undetermined number of properties suffered severe external flooding to highways and gardens, with some external inundation close to entering ground–floor living areas. [PAG,IMG] (p12)
Surface water flooding focused on a cluster of streets between Bishops Drive and Wood Brook; intense runoff and exceeded drainage caused significant flooding to properties and highways in Oakwood. The council carried out formal Section 19 investigations into the impacts. (p17)
An intense thunderstorm hit Oakwood on the afternoon of 19 July 2014 and caused surface water flooding when highway and private surface water exceeded drainage capacity. (p18)","at least 10 properties (p3)
9 residential properties [PAG] (p4)
