at least 10 homes internally flooded; 1 property externally flooded (Foxglove Drive, 6th July 2012) [PAG,IMG,MUL] (p10)
at least 10 homes [PAG] (p11)
at least 10 homes [PAG,IMG] (p12)
at least 10 properties (p17)",GB-DER_2_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_2_2014-07-19,Derby flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Bishops Drive, Oakwood 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Bishops-Drive-Oakwood-S19.pdf
GB-DER,2,2014-07-19,52.9294476,-1.440326,"<div id=""html_34cf2e100cc97c5bea32efe611139a39"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chaddesden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Tributaries in the Chaddesden area (Wood Brook and Oakwood Brook feeding the Chaddesden Brook) received concentrated sewer and overland flows when the surface water sewer capacity was exceeded during the intense rainfall on 19th July 2014. Properties and streets at the base of the brooks' valleys (notably Morefern Drive, Santolina Drive, Saffron Drive and Columbine Close) are indicated as being susceptible to flow&ndash;path inundation or surface water accumulation. [PAG,IMG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,Chaddesden,England,"Tributaries in the Chaddesden area (Wood Brook and Oakwood Brook feeding the Chaddesden Brook) received concentrated sewer and overland flows when the surface water sewer capacity was exceeded during the intense rainfall on 19th July 2014. Properties and streets at the base of the brooks' valleys (notably Morefern Drive, Santolina Drive, Saffron Drive and Columbine Close) are indicated as being susceptible to flow–path inundation or surface water accumulation. [PAG,IMG] (p7)",,GB-DER_2_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_2_2014-07-19,Derby flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Bishops Drive, Oakwood 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Bishops-Drive-Oakwood-S19.pdf
GB-BKM,19,2019-09-24,51.6064047,-0.5564089,"<div id=""html_6bcb73bdab4694286fa9537d3f9d18d2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Chalfont St Peter</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of business premises and carriageway closure: five business properties on High Street experienced internal flooding; the road was closed by the local highway authority for the duration of the event. [PAG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road experienced surface water/urban flooding that caused the carriageway to flood and be closed by the local Highway Authority for the duration of the event. The location was the only road affected due to a natural low point in the carriageway profile. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A foul manhole in the middle of the carriageway surcharged and discharged a large amount of water onto the highway, overwhelming highway drainage, causing ponding in the road and rising water levels that encroached into and flooded shops along the High Street. [PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall and surface water runoff entered the highway drainage and foul sewer system, overwhelming the foul sewer. Sewage discharged from a manhole in the middle of the carriageway and flowed into the highway drainage, causing backup, ponding of water in the road and rising water levels that encroached into shops along the High Street. [PAG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Foul sewer became overwhelmed during heavy rainfall and discharged sewage from a manhole in the middle of the carriageway into the highway drainage system. This caused drainage backup, ponding in the road and rising water levels which encroached into shops along High Street; Thames Water attended and pumped flood water away. [PAG,IMG] (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 business properties; 18 inches (maximum flood depth) [PAG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 business properties; 18 inches (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,"High Street, Chalfont St Peter",England,"Internal flooding of business premises and carriageway closure: five business properties on High Street experienced internal flooding; the road was closed by the local highway authority for the duration of the event. [PAG] (p1)
Road experienced surface water/urban flooding that caused the carriageway to flood and be closed by the local Highway Authority for the duration of the event. The location was the only road affected due to a natural low point in the carriageway profile. (p2)
A foul manhole in the middle of the carriageway surcharged and discharged a large amount of water onto the highway, overwhelming highway drainage, causing ponding in the road and rising water levels that encroached into and flooded shops along the High Street. [PAG] (p4)
Heavy rainfall and surface water runoff entered the highway drainage and foul sewer system, overwhelming the foul sewer. Sewage discharged from a manhole in the middle of the carriageway and flowed into the highway drainage, causing backup, ponding of water in the road and rising water levels that encroached into shops along the High Street. [PAG] (p5)
Foul sewer became overwhelmed during heavy rainfall and discharged sewage from a manhole in the middle of the carriageway into the highway drainage system. This caused drainage backup, ponding in the road and rising water levels which encroached into shops along High Street; Thames Water attended and pumped flood water away. [PAG,IMG] (p6)","5 business properties; 18 inches (maximum flood depth) [PAG] (p1)
5 business properties; 18 inches (p2)",GB-BKM_19_2019-09-24.html,GB-BKM_19_2019-09-24,Chalfont St Peter flooding 24 Sep 2019,"Flood Investigation Report: High Street, Chalfont St Peter 2019",018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2019/Buckinghamshire County/s19-invesitgation-report/chalfont/2019/PE6AWeg.pdf
GB-BKM,19,2019-09-24,51.86619751869193,-0.8610230642396219,"<div id=""html_bc1a0f6007f31ac5c86338bfd4d075d0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Buckinghamshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of business properties on High Street, Chalfont St Peter caused by a Thames Water foul sewer network issue; High Street was closed by the highway authority for the duration of the event. [IMG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water flooding occurred in the area shown on Figure 11 on the day of the event; the surface water drainage system was overwhelmed by water and debris discharging from the sewer system and could not drain away the excess. The drainage system was cleaned after the flooding. [PAG] (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 business properties; 18 inches (maximum depth); 1 road closed [IMG] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Buckinghamshire,England,"Internal flooding of business properties on High Street, Chalfont St Peter caused by a Thames Water foul sewer network issue; High Street was closed by the highway authority for the duration of the event. [IMG] (p1)
Surface–water flooding occurred in the area shown on Figure 11 on the day of the event; the surface water drainage system was overwhelmed by water and debris discharging from the sewer system and could not drain away the excess. The drainage system was cleaned after the flooding. [PAG] (p7)",5 business properties; 18 inches (maximum depth); 1 road closed [IMG] (p1),GB-BKM_19_2019-09-24.html,GB-BKM_19_2019-09-24,Chalfont St Peter flooding 24 Sep 2019,"Flood Investigation Report: High Street, Chalfont St Peter 2019",018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2019/Buckinghamshire County/s19-invesitgation-report/chalfont/2019/PE6AWeg.pdf
GB-BKM,19,2019-09-24,51.6082069,-0.5543134,"<div id=""html_ff8bd1cc2e475932c4db04e6ee1a5c9c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chalfont St Peter</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall led to surface runoff entering the highway drainage and foul sewer, which became overwhelmed; sewage discharged from a manhole and floodwater ponded on the road and encroached into shops/properties on the High Street in Chalfont St Peter. [IMG,PAG] (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Chalfont St Peter,England,"Heavy rainfall led to surface runoff entering the highway drainage and foul sewer, which became overwhelmed; sewage discharged from a manhole and floodwater ponded on the road and encroached into shops/properties on the High Street in Chalfont St Peter. [IMG,PAG] (p4)",,GB-BKM_19_2019-09-24.html,GB-BKM_19_2019-09-24,Chalfont St Peter flooding 24 Sep 2019,"Flood Investigation Report: High Street, Chalfont St Peter 2019",018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2019/Buckinghamshire County/s19-invesitgation-report/chalfont/2019/PE6AWeg.pdf
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5717712,-0.1199902,"<div id=""html_5407074c481b58f144a2ee548948dd6c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cromwell House</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Externally flooded when the main trunk sewer backed up and discharged via gullies and manholes in the low spot on Cromwell Road. (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property externally flooded (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Cromwell House,England,Externally flooded when the main trunk sewer backed up and discharged via gullies and manholes in the low spot on Cromwell Road. (p11),1 property externally flooded (p11),GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5540424,-0.1326497,"<div id=""html_52536ce026af2e92e1753c2158ced396"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Laceby Acres Primary Academy</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme surcharge pressures were induced in parts of the trunk sewer running from Laceby Acres during intense rainfall; during the 10 August event this surcharging caused extensive damage to the footpath running above the trunk sewer. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Laceby Acres Primary Academy,England,Extreme surcharge pressures were induced in parts of the trunk sewer running from Laceby Acres during intense rainfall; during the 10 August event this surcharging caused extensive damage to the footpath running above the trunk sewer. (p12),,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5697623,-0.113882,"<div id=""html_059870f9ec6693e28e468d03b8676109"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Grimsby Leisure Centre</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood water containing raw sewage surcharged through toilets, manholes and drains inside the building, causing internal flooding of toilets, changing rooms and corridors. [MUL] (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal and site drainage were obstructed by root ingress and grass cuttings entering the private drainage network. A subsided low spot in the outgoing pipe from the Leisure Centre to the main/public sewer contributed to surcharging of the sewer and backflow risk into the facility. The affected section of sewer was re&ndash;laid by Anglian Water and construction works on site are replacing pipework and diverting some drainage to resolve the low spot. [MUL] (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 community facility internally flooded [MUL] (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Grimsby Leisure Centre,England,"Flood water containing raw sewage surcharged through toilets, manholes and drains inside the building, causing internal flooding of toilets, changing rooms and corridors. [MUL] (p23)
Internal and site drainage were obstructed by root ingress and grass cuttings entering the private drainage network. A subsided low spot in the outgoing pipe from the Leisure Centre to the main/public sewer contributed to surcharging of the sewer and backflow risk into the facility. The affected section of sewer was re–laid by Anglian Water and construction works on site are replacing pipework and diverting some drainage to resolve the low spot. [MUL] (p24)",1 community facility internally flooded [MUL] (p23),GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5683934,-0.1133306,"<div id=""html_6d95a6ec1a78a9fca30872d98b7ed538"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Grimsby Auditorium</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood water containing raw sewage surcharged through toilets and from a number of external manholes into the building, causing internal flooding of toilets and the foyer. [MUL] (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 community facility internally flooded [MUL] (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Grimsby Auditorium,England,"Flood water containing raw sewage surcharged through toilets and from a number of external manholes into the building, causing internal flooding of toilets and the foyer. [MUL] (p23)",1 community facility internally flooded [MUL] (p23),GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5659395,-0.086861,"<div id=""html_cb22e3143469f371a00a53002326a182"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Freshney Place</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of commercial premises and precinct areas; businesses and parts of the shopping precinct were flooded internally. [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding within the shopping centre: floodwater containing raw sewage surcharged through toilets and manholes, affecting business premises; flooding was localised around toilets/walkways but certain businesses were flooded throughout. (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Freshney Place is located within the mapped red 'Area of Flooding' and/or blue/cyan shaded surface&ndash;water risk zones, indicating the shopping centre area was within the extent of surface&ndash;water flooding during the reported events. [IMG,MUL] (p59)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 businesses [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 businesses internally flooded (p42)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Freshney Place,England,"Internal flooding of commercial premises and precinct areas; businesses and parts of the shopping precinct were flooded internally. [IMG,PAG] (p41)
Internal flooding within the shopping centre: floodwater containing raw sewage surcharged through toilets and manholes, affecting business premises; flooding was localised around toilets/walkways but certain businesses were flooded throughout. (p42)
Freshney Place is located within the mapped red 'Area of Flooding' and/or blue/cyan shaded surface–water risk zones, indicating the shopping centre area was within the extent of surface–water flooding during the reported events. [IMG,MUL] (p59)","6 businesses [IMG,PAG] (p41)
6 businesses internally flooded (p42)",GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.557065,-0.0846882,"<div id=""html_09185410b42c1cc8ebe58c2ddc58c00e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Peoples Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The park was extensively flooded as a result of a surcharging trunk sewer running in Welholme Road. (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Peoples Park,England,The park was extensively flooded as a result of a surcharging trunk sewer running in Welholme Road. (p44),,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5618883,-0.0817676,"<div id=""html_d52ac8f942276549c959d522463537c9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ainslie Street Recreation Ground</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The recreation ground is adjacent to the mapped red&ndash;outlined area of flooding (1 in 30 annual chance zones) and contains large storage pipes that Anglian Water have suggested could be used as part of mitigation for storm flows associated with the summer 2014 events. [IMG,MUL] (p50)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Ainslie Street Recreation Ground,England,"The recreation ground is adjacent to the mapped red–outlined area of flooding (1 in 30 annual chance zones) and contains large storage pipes that Anglian Water have suggested could be used as part of mitigation for storm flows associated with the summer 2014 events. [IMG,MUL] (p50)",,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.564797049999996,-0.0822509563732041,"<div id=""html_9a1a83469243cd34992766c75684d90e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Grimsby Town Hall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement flooding occurred from sewer surcharge/backflow via gullies, affecting rooms including the boiler room; water receded after rainfall ceased. [MUL] (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater in the Town Hall boiler room rose close to causing failure of a newly installed boiler. [MUL] (p52)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding of the Town Hall boiler room; extensive damage to a newly installed boiler was narrowly avoided. [PAG,MUL] (p53)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one room (boiler room) [MUL] (p51)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Grimsby Town Hall,England,"Basement flooding occurred from sewer surcharge/backflow via gullies, affecting rooms including the boiler room; water receded after rainfall ceased. [MUL] (p51)
Floodwater in the Town Hall boiler room rose close to causing failure of a newly installed boiler. [MUL] (p52)
Flooding of the Town Hall boiler room; extensive damage to a newly installed boiler was narrowly avoided. [PAG,MUL] (p53)",one room (boiler room) [MUL] (p51),GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5411084,-0.0144217,"<div id=""html_72ee531db0314d6effebf7d7c9ee1624"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cleethorpes Golf Club</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water sewers outfell into boundary ditches at the golf club. Open ditches were generally free running but a piped section had built&ndash;up silt and an undersized piped section; this constrained the outfall capacity and exacerbated surcharging of surface water sewers that caused flooding to nearby properties. Investigations into the piped ditch are ongoing and remedial measures are planned to restore free&ndash;running outfalls. [MUL] (p77)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Cleethorpes Golf Club,England,Surface water sewers outfell into boundary ditches at the golf club. Open ditches were generally free running but a piped section had built–up silt and an undersized piped section; this constrained the outfall capacity and exacerbated surcharging of surface water sewers that caused flooding to nearby properties. Investigations into the piped ditch are ongoing and remedial measures are planned to restore free–running outfalls. [MUL] (p77),,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5654722,-0.1023513,"<div id=""html_d242a3f7893ad12e04a700acc6d88b03"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lidl</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area adjacent to the store was identified as being close to the site of the deepest inundation during the flood events; flooding was driven by catchment flows down Cromwell Road and surcharge of the public sewer in front of Lynton Parade. [MUL] (p32)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Lidl,England,Area adjacent to the store was identified as being close to the site of the deepest inundation during the flood events; flooding was driven by catchment flows down Cromwell Road and surcharge of the public sewer in front of Lynton Parade. [MUL] (p32),,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5799552,-0.0951088,"<div id=""html_e4ee2b9288f6ca78ee6fe5fca2d5f473"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>New Cut Drain</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the events the New Cut Drain was unable to receive runoff because of a flood embankment and new sheet piling flood defence. This prevented drainage into the drain, causing water to back up towards properties and contributing to sewer surcharging and property flooding in adjacent streets. [MUL] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,New Cut Drain,England,"During the events the New Cut Drain was unable to receive runoff because of a flood embankment and new sheet piling flood defence. This prevented drainage into the drain, causing water to back up towards properties and contributing to sewer surcharging and property flooding in adjacent streets. [MUL] (p10)",,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5553088,-0.1386367,"<div id=""html_6044616b39319ddaef9751dc5e8e1961"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Freshney</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The map shows River Freshney as a local watercourse whose presence and associated drainage infrastructure correlates with the mapped surface water flood risk centred on the residential area north of Cromwell Road. This association indicates the river/drain network is a factor in the flood&ndash;prone conditions for that area. [IMG,MUL] (p91)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,River Freshney,England,"The map shows River Freshney as a local watercourse whose presence and associated drainage infrastructure correlates with the mapped surface water flood risk centred on the residential area north of Cromwell Road. This association indicates the river/drain network is a factor in the flood–prone conditions for that area. [IMG,MUL] (p91)",,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5604319,-0.1397849,"<div id=""html_83e2ca3717f71f0942b2ab256410ac37"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>St Nicholas Drive, Wybers Wood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Some properties on St. Nicholas Drive were internally flooded during the intense rainfall on 8 August 2014. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Main sewer surcharged out of highway gullies; water flowed down the falling land across the footpath, down driveways into garages and houses, causing internal and external flooding of properties. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Frequent surcharging of the public sewer causing sewer flooding of properties/driveways; residents dug relief channels/swales to divert floodwater from properties (later formalised/improved as mitigation). [PAG,MUL] (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 properties internally flooded; 9 properties externally flooded (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>20% siltation levels in a section of the St Nicholas Drive sewer; sewer flooding of a house driveway reported as occurring twice a year [PAG,MUL] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,"St Nicholas Drive, Wybers Wood",England,"Some properties on St. Nicholas Drive were internally flooded during the intense rainfall on 8 August 2014. (p7)
Main sewer surcharged out of highway gullies; water flowed down the falling land across the footpath, down driveways into garages and houses, causing internal and external flooding of properties. (p10)
Frequent surcharging of the public sewer causing sewer flooding of properties/driveways; residents dug relief channels/swales to divert floodwater from properties (later formalised/improved as mitigation). [PAG,MUL] (p12)","16 properties internally flooded; 9 properties externally flooded (p10)
20% siltation levels in a section of the St Nicholas Drive sewer; sewer flooding of a house driveway reported as occurring twice a year [PAG,MUL] (p12)",GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.56351784700427,-0.1331543332156759,"<div id=""html_14bef8d7942b1e72390ccc29c24ab34a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Greyfriars, Wybers Wood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater originated from a surcharging main trunk sewer at the rear of the properties; the sewer surcharge forced a manhole lid off and, because a flood embankment prevented drainage to the New Cut Drain, water backed up towards the properties causing external and internal flooding. [MUL] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties externally flooded on 20 July 2014; 1 property internally flooded and 4 properties externally flooded on 10 August 2014. [MUL] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,"Greyfriars, Wybers Wood",England,"Floodwater originated from a surcharging main trunk sewer at the rear of the properties; the sewer surcharge forced a manhole lid off and, because a flood embankment prevented drainage to the New Cut Drain, water backed up towards the properties causing external and internal flooding. [MUL] (p10)",5 properties externally flooded on 20 July 2014; 1 property internally flooded and 4 properties externally flooded on 10 August 2014. [MUL] (p10),GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.56598941545565,-0.13169566510237607,"<div id=""html_603954a301f0ab2140b47cf9fce02512"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Grasby Crescent, Grimsby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater was from a surcharging main trunk sewer (manhole located at the junction with Anderby Drive). The land drained towards the New Cut Drain but a new sheet piling flood defence prevented drainage into the drain, causing external flooding to properties. [MUL] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties externally flooded on 20 July 2014; 4 properties externally flooded on 10 August 2014. [MUL] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,"Grasby Crescent, Grimsby",England,"Floodwater was from a surcharging main trunk sewer (manhole located at the junction with Anderby Drive). The land drained towards the New Cut Drain but a new sheet piling flood defence prevented drainage into the drain, causing external flooding to properties. [MUL] (p10)",4 properties externally flooded on 20 July 2014; 4 properties externally flooded on 10 August 2014. [MUL] (p10),GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5665002,-0.1293761,"<div id=""html_27327a00a5bcd1e8e54ac04e10aaa10a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Anderby Drive, The Willows</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of Anderby Drive was flooded by surcharge from the main trunk sewer (similar mechanism to Grasby Crescent). Other parts, towards Wingate Road, experienced external flooding caused by highway gullies and manholes surcharging around a new mini roundabout, sending water into the highway and properties. [MUL] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surcharging of the sewer system with water discharging from highway gullies and manholes; external flooding occurred in the same manner as at Barmouth Drive. Residents reported more frequent surcharging at this location, with at least one resident describing sewer flooding of a house driveway occurring twice a year. (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties externally flooded on 20 July 2014; 9 properties externally flooded on 10 August 2014. [MUL] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>reports of driveway sewer flooding occurring twice a year (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,"Anderby Drive, The Willows",England,"Part of Anderby Drive was flooded by surcharge from the main trunk sewer (similar mechanism to Grasby Crescent). Other parts, towards Wingate Road, experienced external flooding caused by highway gullies and manholes surcharging around a new mini roundabout, sending water into the highway and properties. [MUL] (p10)
Surcharging of the sewer system with water discharging from highway gullies and manholes; external flooding occurred in the same manner as at Barmouth Drive. Residents reported more frequent surcharging at this location, with at least one resident describing sewer flooding of a house driveway occurring twice a year. (p11)","3 properties externally flooded on 20 July 2014; 9 properties externally flooded on 10 August 2014. [MUL] (p10)
reports of driveway sewer flooding occurring twice a year (p11)",GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
