GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5646762,-0.1389268,"<div id=""html_dfd33e9f2dfa7a9f6973e20c10cb7164"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wybers Wood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Wybers Wood estate was affected by the intense rainfall on 8 August 2014 (part of the westerly area of Grimsby) and had properties internally flooded during the event that peaked 11:15&ndash;12:15 on 10 August 2014. [PAG,MUL] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on the Wybers Wood estate experienced internal flooding (noted for the 10 August event) and the estate was within the area affected by intense rainfall on 8 August. [PAG,MUL] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense summer storms overwhelmed the public sewer network capacity, causing urban/surface water and sewer&ndash;related flooding in the Wybers Wood estate; the estate's sewerage system is described as 40&ndash;50 years old, contributing to capacity and performance issues during the events. [MUL] (p92)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Wybers Wood,England,"The Wybers Wood estate was affected by the intense rainfall on 8 August 2014 (part of the westerly area of Grimsby) and had properties internally flooded during the event that peaked 11:15–12:15 on 10 August 2014. [PAG,MUL] (p7)
