Intense summer storms overwhelmed the public sewer network capacity, causing urban/surface water and sewer–related flooding in the Willows estate; the estate's sewerage system is described as 40–50 years old, contributing to capacity and performance issues during the events. [MUL] (p92)",,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.537901,-0.167312,"<div id=""html_20fd185d67bd70d53b2703813937e83c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Laceby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Laceby by&ndash;pass area was affected by the intense rainfall on 8 August 2014, with external/surface&ndash;water flooding causing some minor disruption. (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Laceby,England,"The Laceby by–pass area was affected by the intense rainfall on 8 August 2014, with external/surface–water flooding causing some minor disruption. (p7)",,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc.html,GB-LIN_2_2014-08-08_etc,,,
GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5339693,-0.0234751,"<div id=""html_6f9544b230294d8a3b6cd4e23f41a0cc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Humberston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Some properties in Humberston were internally flooded as a result of heavy rainfall that peaked between 03:30 and 04:30 on 20 July 2014; residents woke to varying levels of flooding ranging from wet carpets to a few inches of flood water. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties within Humberston (on Parker Road and Hewson Road) experienced internal flooding due to surcharging surface water sewers and associated sewer issues. (p76)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on North Sea Lane experienced surface water inundation and sewer&ndash;related flooding: floodwater ran from a private road through gardens and into a property via airbricks; poor condition of surface water sewers (displaced joint, root ingress, structural defects) and lack of drainage on the private road increased impacts. (p79)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed among the main wards where Anglian Water performed high&ndash;power jetting of public sewers after the 2014 floods to mitigate siltation and reduce sewer surcharging. (p93)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties internally flooded (p76)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property internally flooded; 1 property externally flooded (p79)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Humberston,England,"Some properties in Humberston were internally flooded as a result of heavy rainfall that peaked between 03:30 and 04:30 on 20 July 2014; residents woke to varying levels of flooding ranging from wet carpets to a few inches of flood water. (p7)
