GB-LIN,2,2014-08-08,53.5124111,-0.0922872,"<div id=""html_1bef7b2e182bc19aa6c211c925136927"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Waltham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Some properties in Waltham were affected by the rainfall/ surface water flooding during the event. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The foul sewer network in Waltham was under pressure during high&ndash;intensity rainfall; at least one property in Salisbury Avenue flooded due to a surcharging foul sewer exacerbated by misconnected surface water and an upstream water leak. [PAG] (p73)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Cheesemans Close (in Waltham) experienced flooding when a driveway gully surcharged and floodwater entered gardens and a conservatory. (p82)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [PAG] (p73)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property internally flooded; 1 property externally flooded (p82)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lincolnshire,Waltham,England,"Some properties in Waltham were affected by the rainfall/ surface water flooding during the event. (p8)
