Floodwater and sewage emerged from a manhole outside the school (photo taken October 2020), indicating combined sewer overflow and surface–water inundation on Sheldon Road that would affect the highway and immediate surroundings. [PAG] (p22)
Sheldon Road experienced surface water flooding with flood water and sewage emerging from a manhole outside the school (photograph dated October 2020). Church Road is shown/reported with drainage/ditch capacity exceeded (photograph dated January 2021) and is identified in the report as a location at risk and affected by drainage exceedance. [PAG] (p23)
Surface water flooding made the junction of Worminghall Road and Ickford Road impassable to regular vehicles. Sheldon Road experienced surface water together with foul/sewer flooding (sewage emerging from manholes) during the October 2020 heavy rainfall event. [PAG,TAB] (p24)
Flooding along Worminghall Road and Sheldon Road; surface water (and foul) flooding on Sheldon Road with water in places exceeding the kerb height. (p25)
