1 property flooded internally; at least 4 flooding events in the last three years (p55)",GB-BKM_23_2020-10-02.html,GB-BKM_23_2020-10-02,Ickford flooding 02 Oct 2020 - 04 Oct 2020,Ickford Section 19 Flood Investigation: Final Technical Report,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2020/Buckinghamshire County/Ickford/Flood/Investigation/Oct/2020.pdf
GB-BKM,23,2020-10-02,51.77046124271444,-1.0713099463953613,"<div id=""html_bccfd2417982a2318c41ad9f889b66d9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Worminghall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Photographs referenced in the report (Figures 8&ndash;4 and 8&ndash;5) show flooding affecting Worminghall Road and adjacent areas in October 2020, inundating the highway and impacting local access. [PAG,IMG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water flooding affected Worminghall Road (photos dated October 2020), inundating the road corridor and threatening access between Ickford and surrounding areas. [PAG] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water and fluvial incidents have impacted the Worminghall area on multiple occasions. Relevant reported impacts include: 3 June 2008 when Worminghall Brook exceeded channel capacity and flowed across fields towards Worminghall Road and down to Church Road causing property flooding; July 2019 surface&ndash;water flooding along Worminghall Road and Golders Close; and the 02&ndash;04 Oct 2020 event which flooded the junction of Worminghall Road and Ickford Road, making the junction impassable to regular vehicles. [PAG,TAB,MUL] (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas around Worminghall experienced road and surface&ndash;water flooding during the October 2020 event (photographic evidence of flooding on Worminghall Road and at its junctions). Local watercourses in the Worminghall/Lappingford area are noted in the report as being outside the EA annual maintenance programme, contributing to local vulnerability. [PAG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The area experienced surface water runoff and ponding along roads and verges; high groundwater levels and groundwater ponding were reported in fields adjacent to Worminghall Road; foul sewer surcharging occurred in nearby streets, combining sewage with surface water. [PAG,IMG] (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Roads in and out of the village towards Worminghall were cut off by floodwater, heavily impacting access and egress to the village for several days. (p43)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Worminghall,England,"Photographs referenced in the report (Figures 8–4 and 8–5) show flooding affecting Worminghall Road and adjacent areas in October 2020, inundating the highway and impacting local access. [PAG,IMG] (p21)
Surface–water flooding affected Worminghall Road (photos dated October 2020), inundating the road corridor and threatening access between Ickford and surrounding areas. [PAG] (p22)
Surface–water and fluvial incidents have impacted the Worminghall area on multiple occasions. Relevant reported impacts include: 3 June 2008 when Worminghall Brook exceeded channel capacity and flowed across fields towards Worminghall Road and down to Church Road causing property flooding; July 2019 surface–water flooding along Worminghall Road and Golders Close; and the 02–04 Oct 2020 event which flooded the junction of Worminghall Road and Ickford Road, making the junction impassable to regular vehicles. [PAG,TAB,MUL] (p24)
Areas around Worminghall experienced road and surface–water flooding during the October 2020 event (photographic evidence of flooding on Worminghall Road and at its junctions). Local watercourses in the Worminghall/Lappingford area are noted in the report as being outside the EA annual maintenance programme, contributing to local vulnerability. [PAG] (p30)
The area experienced surface water runoff and ponding along roads and verges; high groundwater levels and groundwater ponding were reported in fields adjacent to Worminghall Road; foul sewer surcharging occurred in nearby streets, combining sewage with surface water. [PAG,IMG] (p40)
Roads in and out of the village towards Worminghall were cut off by floodwater, heavily impacting access and egress to the village for several days. (p43)",,GB-BKM_23_2020-10-02.html,GB-BKM_23_2020-10-02,Ickford flooding 02 Oct 2020 - 04 Oct 2020,Ickford Section 19 Flood Investigation: Final Technical Report,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2020/Buckinghamshire County/Ickford/Flood/Investigation/Oct/2020.pdf
GB-BKM,23,2020-10-02,51.757924790624955,-1.0367201800728332,"<div id=""html_93e2c1e03fdcae7e27445891836d390b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Shabbington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Roads in and out of the village towards Shabbington and Draycot were cut off by floodwater, heavily impacting access and egress for several days. (p43)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Shabbington,England,"Roads in and out of the village towards Shabbington and Draycot were cut off by floodwater, heavily impacting access and egress for several days. (p43)",,GB-BKM_23_2020-10-02.html,GB-BKM_23_2020-10-02,Ickford flooding 02 Oct 2020 - 04 Oct 2020,Ickford Section 19 Flood Investigation: Final Technical Report,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2020/Buckinghamshire County/Ickford/Flood/Investigation/Oct/2020.pdf
GB-BKM,23,2020-10-02,51.7483571,-1.0627505,"<div id=""html_d9733cb140cac41d504494663e3cdbe4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Draycot</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Roads in and out of the village towards Shabbington and Draycot were cut off by floodwater, heavily impacting access and egress for several days. (p43)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Draycot,England,"Roads in and out of the village towards Shabbington and Draycot were cut off by floodwater, heavily impacting access and egress for several days. (p43)",,GB-BKM_23_2020-10-02.html,GB-BKM_23_2020-10-02,Ickford flooding 02 Oct 2020 - 04 Oct 2020,Ickford Section 19 Flood Investigation: Final Technical Report,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2020/Buckinghamshire County/Ickford/Flood/Investigation/Oct/2020.pdf
