over 70 properties; over 200 reports of flooding [PAG] (p9)
over 70 properties flooded internally; over 200 reports of flooding [PAG] (p10)",GB-NNH_3_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_3_2016-03-09,Oundle flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Warren Bridge, Oundle, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22328/FIR-Oundle/Rev03/161116.pdf
GB-NNH,3,2016-03-09,52.480678744170966,-0.46597423959156464,"<div id=""html_548edd0826b762b8e2d02d5ce3313bea"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oundle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood incident at Warren Bridge in Oundle on 9 March 2016 caused internal flooding of at least one property; heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment led to ordinary watercourses and surface water runoff flowing to low points around private property. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Town location of the Warren Bridge flood incident on 9 March 2016; at least one property in Oundle experienced internal flooding associated with that incident. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The town and its western developed area lie within the Lyveden Brook catchment. During the 9 March 2016 event ordinary watercourse (river) flooding and surface water runoff contributed to reported flooding affecting properties in the catchment and residential developments near where Lyveden Brook meets the River Nene. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred in Oundle (at Warren Bridge) when heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment caused ordinary watercourses to be unable to convey rainwater, resulting in excess surface water flowing to low points around private property. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [PAG] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Oundle,England,"Flood incident at Warren Bridge in Oundle on 9 March 2016 caused internal flooding of at least one property; heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment led to ordinary watercourses and surface water runoff flowing to low points around private property. (p7)
