GB-HEF,18,2020-02-16,52.1204596,-3.0069283,"<div id=""html_9bf3ec16676c9919c1a256eff3cc8059"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Willersley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Environment Agency Flood Map for Planning (Rivers and Sea) shows much of the area around Willersley, particularly to the north and south, is in Flood Zone 3 (high flood risk); some areas are shown as benefiting from flood defences. [IMG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Five residential properties flooded internally; flood depths recorded internally between 6 inches and 3 ft, and one property experienced 4 ft externally. Respondents described water from a watercourse (River Wye/tributaries) and contributory issues including an overflowing ditch, a blocked gully and a blocked bridge/culvert. A road closure was implemented on the A438 during the flooding. (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; internal depths 6 inches to 3 ft; one external depth 4 ft (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Willersley,England,"The Environment Agency Flood Map for Planning (Rivers and Sea) shows much of the area around Willersley, particularly to the north and south, is in Flood Zone 3 (high flood risk); some areas are shown as benefiting from flood defences. [IMG] (p1)
Five residential properties flooded internally; flood depths recorded internally between 6 inches and 3 ft, and one property experienced 4 ft externally. Respondents described water from a watercourse (River Wye/tributaries) and contributory issues including an overflowing ditch, a blocked gully and a blocked bridge/culvert. A road closure was implemented on the A438 during the flooding. (p2)",5 properties; internal depths 6 inches to 3 ft; one external depth 4 ft (p2),GB-HEF_18_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_18_2020-02-16,Willersley flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Willersley,055/Herefordshire County/17/Willersley.pdf
GB-HEF,22,2020-02-16,52.0345352,-2.8141252,"<div id=""html_9e7a9e99e5fc779571b6d66da0b43169"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cage Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Cage Brook catchment is the named watercourse/catchment for the area where the surface water flood event occurred; the surface water flooding in this catchment was associated with internal flooding of properties in Madley (recorded during the Feb 2020 event). Herefordshire Council historic records attribute flooding in the location to surface water runoff from the highway. (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties; one basement (flood depth < 6 inches) (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Cage Brook,England,The Cage Brook catchment is the named watercourse/catchment for the area where the surface water flood event occurred; the surface water flooding in this catchment was associated with internal flooding of properties in Madley (recorded during the Feb 2020 event). Herefordshire Council historic records attribute flooding in the location to surface water runoff from the highway. (p2),4 properties; one basement (flood depth < 6 inches) (p2),GB-HEF_22_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_22_2020-02-16,Madley flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Madley,055/Herefordshire County/21/Madley.pdf
GB-HEF,22,2020-02-16,52.0445728,-2.8493961,"<div id=""html_39804c7d8aa681c0becd9b754e85aab6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Madley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding associated with Cage Brook (an ordinary watercourse) affected parts of the village during the key event; flood risk mapping shows some areas of the village lie within higher risk zones (Flood Zone 2 and 3). [IMG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties during the 16 February 2020 surface water flood event. Four properties flooded internally (including one basement) and two of the flooded properties are close to an area identified as high risk on the Surface Water Flood Map; Herefordshire Council records indicate surface water runoff from the highway as the likely cause for at least some properties. (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties; one basement (flood depth < 6 inches) (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Madley,England,"Flooding associated with Cage Brook (an ordinary watercourse) affected parts of the village during the key event; flood risk mapping shows some areas of the village lie within higher risk zones (Flood Zone 2 and 3). [IMG] (p1)
Internal flooding of residential properties during the 16 February 2020 surface water flood event. Four properties flooded internally (including one basement) and two of the flooded properties are close to an area identified as high risk on the Surface Water Flood Map; Herefordshire Council records indicate surface water runoff from the highway as the likely cause for at least some properties. (p2)",4 properties; one basement (flood depth < 6 inches) (p2),GB-HEF_22_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_22_2020-02-16,Madley flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Madley,055/Herefordshire County/21/Madley.pdf
GB-DOR,5,2016-09-16,50.8003134,-1.987983,"<div id=""html_fad8b48fe2564d15a932c79c033cae36"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Square, Wimborne Minster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Square was within the area described as most affected by surface water flooding during the heavy storm on 16 September 2016; it forms the northern boundary of the affected area in the town centre. [IMG,PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flood risk extends across The Square in the 1 in 100 year event, and a commercial property in The Square was reported as experiencing internal and external flooding following the heavy storm. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding reported to 1 commercial property; the reporter indicated a further 2 commercial properties were also affected. [TAB] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water run&ndash;off from the public highway collected at a slot highway drainage location immediately in front of a commercial property during the storm and could not drain quickly enough, resulting in surface water entering and causing internal flooding of the commercial property. [IMG,PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water run&ndash;off from the road and pavement collected at the location of slot highway drainage on the eastern side of The Square during the storm in the early hours of 16 September 2016 and entered a commercial property, causing internal flooding. The slot drainage was later found to be blocked and required jetting. Records and proprietor account also identify previous similar occurrences (including an event thought to be in August 2011) where standing water and bow waves from vehicular movement contributed to water entering the same commercial property. [PAG,MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Slot drain jetting was carried out throughout The Square following the storm; the Wimborne Square Enhancement Scheme had installed slot drains and paved footpaths intended to pass excess flows if slot drains surcharged or blocked. [IMG] (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>three commercial properties (total across The Square, High Street and East Street) [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial property internally flooded; 2 additional commercial properties affected [TAB] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial property [IMG,PAG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"The Square, Wimborne Minster",England,"The Square was within the area described as most affected by surface water flooding during the heavy storm on 16 September 2016; it forms the northern boundary of the affected area in the town centre. [IMG,PAG] (p6)
