GB-DOR,5,2016-09-16,50.798271,-1.9854442,"<div id=""html_9645d8d305e3ef66b0449ef1b5a160d4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>East Street, Wimborne Minster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>East Street formed the southern extent of the town&ndash;centre area most affected by surface water flooding during the heavy rainfall event in the early hours of 16 September 2016. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected East Street during heavy rainfall; maps show flow/ponding down High Street into East Street (1 in 30 year) and along East Street as part of the 1 in 100 year flood risk corridor. A commercial property in East Street was reported to have both internal and external flooding during the storm. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding reported to 1 commercial property; the reporter indicated a further 3 commercial properties were also affected. [TAB] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reports were received of commercial properties on East Street suffering internal flooding during/after the heavy storm in the early hours of 16th September 2016. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>three commercial properties (total across The Square, High Street and East Street) [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial property internally flooded; 3 additional commercial properties affected [TAB] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"East Street, Wimborne Minster",England,"East Street formed the southern extent of the town–centre area most affected by surface water flooding during the heavy rainfall event in the early hours of 16 September 2016. (p6)
