GB-NNH,5,2016-03-09,52.3106138,-0.8659129831915817,"<div id=""html_9f171e05351d610c4088de64ad5cf272"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Northamptonshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding of surrounding sports facilities led to water entering a community building; river flood water flowed around the front and rear of the property and ponded to an approximate depth of up to 300mm. The community building operators reported this was the second occasion the river level reached the property boundary. [MUL] (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>ponding up to 300mm; flooding incidents recorded on 21/12/2012 and 09/03/2016 [MUL] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Northamptonshire,England,Flooding of surrounding sports facilities led to water entering a community building; river flood water flowed around the front and rear of the property and ponded to an approximate depth of up to 300mm. The community building operators reported this was the second occasion the river level reached the property boundary. [MUL] (p11),ponding up to 300mm; flooding incidents recorded on 21/12/2012 and 09/03/2016 [MUL] (p11),GB-NNH_5_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_5_2016-03-09,Kettering flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Community Building, Ise Lodge, Kettering, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22333/FIR/Ise-Lodge/Kettering/Rev-03/161116.pdf
GB-NNH,5,2016-03-09,52.3927151,-0.6951522,"<div id=""html_180b309b3881a97fbc67eed2cc593701"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ise Lodge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The community building at Ise Lodge is the subject of the Flood Investigation Report, indicating it was impacted by flooding and investigated for flood damage/impacts. [PAG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Northamptonshire County Council Section 19 flood investigation concerns the community building at Ise Lodge, indicating the building was affected by flooding and is the subject of the report. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a community building: water entered the building fabric. Building lies within the floodplain and flooded due to heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment, overwhelmed drainage and river overtopping. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The community building at Ise Lodge was flooded when the River Ise, receiving high volumes of water from a saturated catchment, overwhelmed the channel and flooded onto the adjacent floodplain around the building. Surface water runoff from nearby residential closes and car park areas also contributed to the volume of water present around the building. The building lies within the floodplain and was identified as being at risk of flooding without resistance measures. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Ise Lodge,England,"The community building at Ise Lodge is the subject of the Flood Investigation Report, indicating it was impacted by flooding and investigated for flood damage/impacts. [PAG] (p1)
