The community building at Ise Lodge was flooded when the River Ise, receiving high volumes of water from a saturated catchment, overwhelmed the channel and flooded onto the adjacent floodplain around the building. Surface water runoff from nearby residential closes and car park areas also contributed to the volume of water present around the building. The building lies within the floodplain and was identified as being at risk of flooding without resistance measures. (p13)",1 property (p7),GB-NNH_5_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_5_2016-03-09,Kettering flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Community Building, Ise Lodge, Kettering, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22333/FIR/Ise-Lodge/Kettering/Rev-03/161116.pdf
GB-NNH,5,2016-03-09,52.3994233,-0.728004,"<div id=""html_c1eb8b010f6fd604f0de1112b29bc2bb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kettering</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The community building at Ise Lodge in Kettering was investigated for flood impacts, indicating flooding affected a location within Kettering. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Location of the reported incident where a community building in Ise Lodge (within Kettering) suffered internal flooding due to heavy rainfall, overwhelmed drainage and river levels overtopping banks. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred at the community building at Ise Lodge in Kettering when the River Ise overflowed onto the adjacent floodplain following heavy rainfall over a saturated catchment. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Kettering,England,"The community building at Ise Lodge in Kettering was investigated for flood impacts, indicating flooding affected a location within Kettering. (p1)
