GB-DER,1,2019-11-08,52.9243097,-1.4727315,"<div id=""html_f2251e6dc4dc9404f328a21217ac0aab"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Exeter Place, Little Chester</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping of the flood bank in front of Exeter House and seepage through the flood wall resulted in flood water flowing onto Exeter Place. Sandbags were used to contain the overtopping and prevent further ingress. No internal flooding of properties at Exeter Place was reported. [IMG,PAG] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The flood bank in front of Exeter House was overtopped as river levels rose, resulting in flood water flowing onto Exeter Place. Seepage through flood defences was also observed. Derby City Council deployed sandbags along the top of the flood bank and at the junction of the bank and flood wall, which contained the flood waters and prevented further overtopping. No internal flooding was reported at Exeter Place. (Sandbag deployment is shown in an image timestamped 20:41 8 Nov 2019.) [PAG,IMG] (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Exeter Place experienced seepage through flood defences and overtopping of flood defences during the 8&ndash;9 November flood. (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River flooding during 8&ndash;9 Nov 2019 affected flood defences along the riverbank at Exeter Place; missing coping on the flood wall was identified and reinstalling it was recommended. [TAB] (p44)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flood depths exceeding 2m; flood depths of up to 50mm [PAG,IMG] (p32)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Exeter Place, Little Chester",England,"Overtopping of the flood bank in front of Exeter House and seepage through the flood wall resulted in flood water flowing onto Exeter Place. Sandbags were used to contain the overtopping and prevent further ingress. No internal flooding of properties at Exeter Place was reported. [IMG,PAG] (p32)
