five commercial properties [PAG] (p15)",GB-CRY_3_2015-08-01.html,GB-CRY_3_2015-08-01,Croydon flooding August 2015,Croydon Flood Investigation Report – 24th August 2015,030/Croydon/030/2015/Croydon/flood-investigation-august15.pdf
GB-CRY,3,2015-08-01,51.3199954,-0.1371432,"<div id=""html_cb5d26b5cf9d93eeab6723489afb220c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Station Approach, Croydon</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple commercial properties were inundated by surface water flooding. Text indicates a pump failure and surcharge of existing surface water sewer systems may have contributed to the inundation of commercial premises at this location. [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Croydon,"Station Approach, Croydon",England,Multiple commercial properties were inundated by surface water flooding. Text indicates a pump failure and surcharge of existing surface water sewer systems may have contributed to the inundation of commercial premises at this location. [TAB] (p7),,GB-CRY_3_2015-08-01.html,GB-CRY_3_2015-08-01,Croydon flooding August 2015,Croydon Flood Investigation Report – 24th August 2015,030/Croydon/030/2015/Croydon/flood-investigation-august15.pdf
GB-CRY,3,2015-08-01,51.3389331,-0.1163358,"<div id=""html_efcf4c1510072e948ae7e1e5668a1c88"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brighton Road, Purley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Brighton Road experienced highway/surface&ndash;water flooding at locations including junctions with Smitham Downs Road and Brantwood Road during the August 2015 event. [TAB] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from an intense rainfall event overwhelmed the highway drainage on the approaches to Purley Cross, including the A23 Brighton Road, causing floodwater to flow over the road surface and causing travel disruption as the drainage network surcharged and manhole covers lifted. (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Croydon,"Brighton Road, Purley",England,"Brighton Road experienced highway/surface–water flooding at locations including junctions with Smitham Downs Road and Brantwood Road during the August 2015 event. [TAB] (p12)
