Overland surface water flowed when the open section of Slade Dyke exceeded capacity and water followed the culverted watercourse along Slade Close. Properties were internally flooded and gardens/outbuildings inundated; Fire Service attended and were able to protect some properties by pumping. [TAB] (p14)
Open section of Slade Dyke exceeded channel capacity and a blocked culvert/security screen caused water to flow overland along the culverted watercourse into Field Road and Slade Close. Resulting surface water and fluvial/overland flooding caused internal flooding of properties, inundation of gardens and outbuildings, and displacement of residents; Fire Service attended and pumped to protect some properties. [PAG,IMG] (p15)","5 properties [TAB] (p11)
