GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.7396929,-1.4155765,"<div id=""html_fbe11e19a017e283feeb1db5df8455a2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wood Row, Methley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties and adjacent low&ndash;lying land at Wood Row were affected by fluvial flooding / overland flows linked to the River Aire/River Calder overtopping and resultant spread into the flood washland; incidents here were smaller in number compared with central Mickletown. [IMG] (p94)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,"Wood Row, Methley",England,Properties and adjacent low–lying land at Wood Row were affected by fluvial flooding / overland flows linked to the River Aire/River Calder overtopping and resultant spread into the flood washland; incidents here were smaller in number compared with central Mickletown. [IMG] (p94),,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.7428759,-1.3559436,"<div id=""html_6947431e0bf2c2c6124eea48f09ce55b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Station Road, Leeds Metropolitan District</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Station Road in Allerton Bywater was submerged on 28 December 2015, rendered impassable with multiple road signs partially inundated and floodwater extending close to residential buildings. [IMG] (p97)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,"Station Road, Leeds Metropolitan District",England,"Station Road in Allerton Bywater was submerged on 28 December 2015, rendered impassable with multiple road signs partially inundated and floodwater extending close to residential buildings. [IMG] (p97)",,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.746507850058165,-1.3552572736881736,"<div id=""html_997f245bc240ae8d4edf2f1d80bab0d4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Barnsdale Road, Allerton Bywater</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Barnsdale Road lies within the natural floodplain and was inundated by fluvial flooding. It flooded regularly at lower&ndash;level events (modelled as ~50% / 1 in 2 year AEP) and modelled to be approximately 1.5 m under water in a 20% / 1 in 5 year AEP event. River Aire was the primary influence; high River Calder levels can also back up into the Aire and cause Allerton Ings to operate, flooding Barnsdale Road independently. (p101)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Isolated properties along Barnsdale Road were flooded by overland flows resulting from River Aire and River Calder overtopping and inundation of nearby washland storage areas. (p103)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1.5 m under water; flooding at approximately 50% (1 in 2 year) AEP (p101)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,"Barnsdale Road, Allerton Bywater",England,"Barnsdale Road lies within the natural floodplain and was inundated by fluvial flooding. It flooded regularly at lower–level events (modelled as ~50% / 1 in 2 year AEP) and modelled to be approximately 1.5 m under water in a 20% / 1 in 5 year AEP event. River Aire was the primary influence; high River Calder levels can also back up into the Aire and cause Allerton Ings to operate, flooding Barnsdale Road independently. (p101)
Isolated properties along Barnsdale Road were flooded by overland flows resulting from River Aire and River Calder overtopping and inundation of nearby washland storage areas. (p103)",1.5 m under water; flooding at approximately 50% (1 in 2 year) AEP (p101),GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.90932819237455,-1.657272164272282,"<div id=""html_c961659b7a7b0a84817e50d3189af203"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Old Pool Road, Otley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Wharfe fluvial flooding and associated backwater effects caused localised inundation at Old Pool Road; surface&ndash;water systems draining to the river were temporarily inoperable or surcharged, contributing to flooding of the road and nearby properties. (p107)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,"Old Pool Road, Otley",England,"River Wharfe fluvial flooding and associated backwater effects caused localised inundation at Old Pool Road; surface–water systems draining to the river were temporarily inoperable or surcharged, contributing to flooding of the road and nearby properties. (p107)",,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
