GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.9009367,-1.510442,"<div id=""html_dd32669745487aaa2d5f39b91ed16d9f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Harewood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Impacted by the Lower River Wharfe flooding on Boxing Day (25&ndash;29 Dec 2015) when record river levels caused fluvial flooding that exceeded drainage capacity and affected the community. (p111)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced highest&ndash;ever river levels leading to Main River overtopping and fluvial flooding; elevated river levels surcharged surface water drains and contributed to local backing up of drainage and highway flooding. (p120)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding from the Lower River Wharfe overtopped the channel and inundated adjacent low&ndash;lying properties and amenity areas; highest recorded river levels led to internal property flooding and local inundation. (p127)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On Boxing Day during the 25&ndash;29 Dec 2015 event the Lower River Wharfe reached record&ndash;high levels and caused fluvial flooding affecting Harewood. River overtopping and surcharging of surface water drainage led to backup through highway gullies and manholes and inundation consistent with drainage systems being exceeded. (p134)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flood depths in some cases in excess of 2m; internal property flooding depths of 800mm recorded (p127)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 in 100 year event (1% AEP) affecting the Lower River Wharfe; highest recorded flood levels (p134)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,Harewood,England,"Impacted by the Lower River Wharfe flooding on Boxing Day (25–29 Dec 2015) when record river levels caused fluvial flooding that exceeded drainage capacity and affected the community. (p111)
Experienced highest–ever river levels leading to Main River overtopping and fluvial flooding; elevated river levels surcharged surface water drains and contributed to local backing up of drainage and highway flooding. (p120)
Fluvial flooding from the Lower River Wharfe overtopped the channel and inundated adjacent low–lying properties and amenity areas; highest recorded river levels led to internal property flooding and local inundation. (p127)
On Boxing Day during the 25–29 Dec 2015 event the Lower River Wharfe reached record–high levels and caused fluvial flooding affecting Harewood. River overtopping and surcharging of surface water drainage led to backup through highway gullies and manholes and inundation consistent with drainage systems being exceeded. (p134)","flood depths in some cases in excess of 2m; internal property flooding depths of 800mm recorded (p127)
