GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.8953666,-1.4532104,"<div id=""html_3e0d63a0e36a0bec8c1e51c4b05283a1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>East Keswick</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding incidents were mapped in East Keswick during the event, with property&ndash; and garden&ndash;flooding incidents clustered along local watercourses. [IMG] (p116)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,East Keswick,England,"Flooding incidents were mapped in East Keswick during the event, with property– and garden–flooding incidents clustered along local watercourses. [IMG] (p116)",,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.8902126,-1.4372824,"<div id=""html_f840d29fc1805e6b4d9807582e3c5a76"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>East Rigton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding incidents were recorded in East Rigton during the event, shown as smaller clusters of property flooding on the incident map. [IMG] (p116)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,East Rigton,England,"Flooding incidents were recorded in East Rigton during the event, shown as smaller clusters of property flooding on the incident map. [IMG] (p116)",,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.8836959,-1.4474736,"<div id=""html_30559ae10b3aa3553a0f795aa9d6d901"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bardsey</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Smaller clustered property&ndash;flooding incidents were mapped near Bardsey associated with watercourses during the event. [IMG] (p116)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,Bardsey,England,Smaller clustered property–flooding incidents were mapped near Bardsey associated with watercourses during the event. [IMG] (p116),,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.722936279096196,-1.8609622226534646,"<div id=""html_25a78fd5d85cc84de45f1570f12d093a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Halifax</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>EHV/HV substations in the Halifax area were recorded as affected by EHV/HV faults during the event; these faults were associated with flooding and contributed to the regional power interruptions and asset flooding recorded by Northern Powergrid. [IMG] (p232)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Contributed to the Northern Powergrid (Yorkshire) totals of 62 flooded assets and 49 HV incidents (event&ndash;wide figures) [IMG] (p232)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,Halifax,England,EHV/HV substations in the Halifax area were recorded as affected by EHV/HV faults during the event; these faults were associated with flooding and contributed to the regional power interruptions and asset flooding recorded by Northern Powergrid. [IMG] (p232),Contributed to the Northern Powergrid (Yorkshire) totals of 62 flooded assets and 49 HV incidents (event–wide figures) [IMG] (p232),GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.646664,-1.7822483,"<div id=""html_0a64c3f7818a170b0ecd360b9e3db940"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Huddersfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>EHV/HV substations in the Huddersfield area were recorded as affected by EHV/HV faults during the event; these faults were associated with flooding and contributed to the regional power interruptions and asset flooding recorded by Northern Powergrid. [IMG] (p232)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Contributed to the Northern Powergrid (Yorkshire) totals of 62 flooded assets and 49 HV incidents (event&ndash;wide figures) [IMG] (p232)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,Huddersfield,England,EHV/HV substations in the Huddersfield area were recorded as affected by EHV/HV faults during the event; these faults were associated with flooding and contributed to the regional power interruptions and asset flooding recorded by Northern Powergrid. [IMG] (p232),Contributed to the Northern Powergrid (Yorkshire) totals of 62 flooded assets and 49 HV incidents (event–wide figures) [IMG] (p232),GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.740490255068494,-2.0130210180932617,"<div id=""html_03f094cb8912357f018714d437ad889f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hebden Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Town centre streets experienced severe flooding; commercial streets were submerged with water reaching shopfronts and building facades, causing significant local disruption. [IMG] (p234)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,Hebden Bridge,England,"Town centre streets experienced severe flooding; commercial streets were submerged with water reaching shopfronts and building facades, causing significant local disruption. [IMG] (p234)",,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.8852975,-1.2595975,"<div id=""html_0d15f57cb4b1a43dd132794242e3e82a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tadcaster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Historic stone bridge in the town collapsed with large sections missing and debris scattered in the river; emergency responders were present to assess the damage. [IMG] (p237)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,Tadcaster,England,Historic stone bridge in the town collapsed with large sections missing and debris scattered in the river; emergency responders were present to assess the damage. [IMG] (p237),,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.7291686,-1.9818986,"<div id=""html_67085efd49ddf3cfe627e553d292afb8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mytholmroyd</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe river and surface&ndash;water flooding during 25 Dec 2015 &ndash; 29 Dec 2015 inundated streets and properties in the village and caused damage to local infrastructure and buildings. (p238)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,Mytholmroyd,England,Severe river and surface–water flooding during 25 Dec 2015 – 29 Dec 2015 inundated streets and properties in the village and caused damage to local infrastructure and buildings. (p238),,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.8530231,-1.7715325784169593,"<div id=""html_ee5bae58bc3c9f08176ca6d234ab7995"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Baildon</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Roads and the ground floor/lower floors of residential buildings were submerged. Emergency responders conducted rescue and evacuation operations using an inflatable rescue boat to remove residents from flooded homes. [IMG] (p239)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,Baildon,England,Roads and the ground floor/lower floors of residential buildings were submerged. Emergency responders conducted rescue and evacuation operations using an inflatable rescue boat to remove residents from flooded homes. [IMG] (p239),,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-LDS,1,2015-12-25,53.70183689988059,-1.7796395422957454,"<div id=""html_67ab3c97f3b3cd6d41f354e8e838ddbd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brighouse</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe urban flooding inundated streets and ground&ndash;floor areas. A two&ndash;storey bar/food premises was partially inundated at street level; outdoor seating, planters and street furniture were submerged. Vehicles were surrounded by floodwater, and normal business activity and local transport were disrupted. [IMG] (p240)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leeds,Brighouse,England,"Severe urban flooding inundated streets and ground–floor areas. A two–storey bar/food premises was partially inundated at street level; outdoor seating, planters and street furniture were submerged. Vehicles were surrounded by floodwater, and normal business activity and local transport were disrupted. [IMG] (p240)",,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25.html,GB-LDS_1_2015-12-25,Leeds Metropolitan District flooding 25 Dec 2015 - 29 Dec 2015,"Leeds Strategic Flood Investigation Report: Storm Eva Flood Event, 25-29 Dec 2015",070/Leeds/Section 19 Report Appendix 1 060217.pdf
GB-HEF,13,2020-02-16,52.0625321,-2.7362102,"<div id=""html_e334e0a00064009c4c2582375e8ce873"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Yazor Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as the main river (blue line) along which Flood Zones 2 and 3 are concentrated; the brook is the watercourse driving river flooding that exposes adjacent properties and infrastructure to inundation. [IMG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overflowing Yazor Brook (and associated blocked bridge/culvert and overflowing ditch) contributed to fluvial flooding that caused internal flooding of nearby properties close to the confluence with an unnamed tributary draining Crowmoor. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Yazor Brook feeds a fishing lake via a weir and has a series of small weirs upstream of Roman Road; the diverted watercourse can break out of bank (towards the south&ndash;east) and flood lower&ndash;lying farmland, contributing to local flood risk around Roman Road. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; flood depths from less than 6 inches up to 4 ft (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Yazor Brook,England,"Identified as the main river (blue line) along which Flood Zones 2 and 3 are concentrated; the brook is the watercourse driving river flooding that exposes adjacent properties and infrastructure to inundation. [IMG] (p1)
Overflowing Yazor Brook (and associated blocked bridge/culvert and overflowing ditch) contributed to fluvial flooding that caused internal flooding of nearby properties close to the confluence with an unnamed tributary draining Crowmoor. (p2)
The Yazor Brook feeds a fishing lake via a weir and has a series of small weirs upstream of Roman Road; the diverted watercourse can break out of bank (towards the south–east) and flood lower–lying farmland, contributing to local flood risk around Roman Road. (p3)",5 properties; flood depths from less than 6 inches up to 4 ft (p2),GB-HEF_13_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_13_2020-02-16,Hereford flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hereford (Towtree Lane/Roman Road),055/Herefordshire County/12/Hereford/Towtree/L/Roman/R.pdf
GB-HEF,13,2020-02-16,52.081078,-2.7630056,"<div id=""html_5907200df83a0fc936fcc925a84e1894"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Towtree Lane, Burghill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A ditch on Towtree Lane has been culverted; the absence of a surface feature (pond/ditch) prevents easy discharge of floodwater from the flood zone, increasing local flood risk and reducing drainage capacity. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial (river) flooding affected areas around Towtree Lane, prompting proposals to improve the land drain on Towtree Lane and consideration of bunding works as mitigation. (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,"Towtree Lane, Burghill",England,"A ditch on Towtree Lane has been culverted; the absence of a surface feature (pond/ditch) prevents easy discharge of floodwater from the flood zone, increasing local flood risk and reducing drainage capacity. (p3)
Fluvial (river) flooding affected areas around Towtree Lane, prompting proposals to improve the land drain on Towtree Lane and consideration of bunding works as mitigation. (p4)",,GB-HEF_13_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_13_2020-02-16,Hereford flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hereford (Towtree Lane/Roman Road),055/Herefordshire County/12/Hereford/Towtree/L/Roman/R.pdf
GB-HEF,13,2020-02-16,52.0751867,-2.7223744,"<div id=""html_88e5052cbe4ddbc2203ee96244aa6e30"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Roman Road, Hereford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A4110 Roman Road (Roman Road) was affected during the event; it is a known location of surface water flooding and lies close to flood flow paths. The highway was implicated in the event (strategic highway network impact) and road&ndash;raising works previously included structures to convey floodwater beneath the carriageway. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood water is conveyed under the carriageway via a concrete weir and overflow channel constructed when Roman Road was raised in the 2000s; Herefordshire Council has identified a requirement to promote drainage improvements at Roman Road and scheduled a highway drainage project (2021/22) in response to recent flooding. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial (river) flooding affected areas of Roman Road in Hereford, leading to a proposed flood risk study and consideration of local mitigation measures. (p4)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties (in the Towtree Lane / Roman Road area); flood depths from less than 6 inches up to 4 ft [TAB] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,"Roman Road, Hereford",England,"A4110 Roman Road (Roman Road) was affected during the event; it is a known location of surface water flooding and lies close to flood flow paths. The highway was implicated in the event (strategic highway network impact) and road–raising works previously included structures to convey floodwater beneath the carriageway. [TAB] (p2)
Flood water is conveyed under the carriageway via a concrete weir and overflow channel constructed when Roman Road was raised in the 2000s; Herefordshire Council has identified a requirement to promote drainage improvements at Roman Road and scheduled a highway drainage project (2021/22) in response to recent flooding. (p3)
Fluvial (river) flooding affected areas of Roman Road in Hereford, leading to a proposed flood risk study and consideration of local mitigation measures. (p4)",5 properties (in the Towtree Lane / Roman Road area); flood depths from less than 6 inches up to 4 ft [TAB] (p2),GB-HEF_13_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_13_2020-02-16,Hereford flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hereford (Towtree Lane/Roman Road),055/Herefordshire County/12/Hereford/Towtree/L/Roman/R.pdf
GB-HEF,13,2020-02-16,52.0553813,-2.7151735,"<div id=""html_6bdb251223c5caf3d5dff5a900a31400"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hereford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Five properties in the Towtree Lane / Roman Road area of Hereford reported internal flooding during the February 2020 fluvial event; affected properties are within or adjacent to Flood Zone 3 and are close to the confluence of Yazor Brook and its unnamed tributary draining Crowmoor. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas of Hereford (notably Towtree Lane and Roman Road) experienced fluvial flooding, prompting pursuit of DEFRA grant funding for a flood risk study and consideration of conveyance improvements to the local brook (weir level adjustments and overflow channel optimisation) and bunding. (p4)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; flood depths from less than 6 inches up to 4 ft [TAB] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Hereford,England,"Five properties in the Towtree Lane / Roman Road area of Hereford reported internal flooding during the February 2020 fluvial event; affected properties are within or adjacent to Flood Zone 3 and are close to the confluence of Yazor Brook and its unnamed tributary draining Crowmoor. [TAB] (p2)
Areas of Hereford (notably Towtree Lane and Roman Road) experienced fluvial flooding, prompting pursuit of DEFRA grant funding for a flood risk study and consideration of conveyance improvements to the local brook (weir level adjustments and overflow channel optimisation) and bunding. (p4)",5 properties; flood depths from less than 6 inches up to 4 ft [TAB] (p2),GB-HEF_13_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_13_2020-02-16,Hereford flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hereford (Towtree Lane/Roman Road),055/Herefordshire County/12/Hereford/Towtree/L/Roman/R.pdf
GB-NNH,12,2012-07-14,52.2847067,-0.726483,"<div id=""html_91915902911bfbf4d9e095d8367c6c4c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Swanspool Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The map and accompanying description indicate flood incidents are concentrated near labelled watercourses; Swanspool Brook is a labelled watercourse near recorded flood incident dates and is therefore associated with historical flooding in the locality (map places incident dates along watercourses and near hotspots). [IMG,MUL] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Swanspool Brook,England,"The map and accompanying description indicate flood incidents are concentrated near labelled watercourses; Swanspool Brook is a labelled watercourse near recorded flood incident dates and is therefore associated with historical flooding in the locality (map places incident dates along watercourses and near hotspots). [IMG,MUL] (p7)",,GB-NNH_12_2012-07-14.html,GB-NNH_12_2012-07-14,Northamptonshire flooding 14 Jul 2012,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding on the A45 Eastbound between Great Doddington and Wilby Way 14th July 2012,090/North Northamptonshire/A45-Flood-Investigaton-Report.pdf
GB-NNH,12,2012-07-14,52.2837999,-0.7103024,"<div id=""html_eddc9c62d1751abd3b845033caceff0c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wilby Way Roundabout</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The A45 eastbound stretch up to the Wilby Way roundabout was affected by surface water flooding from adjacent land and a blocked drainage network, causing road closures and requiring drainage clearance. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Wilby Way Roundabout,England,"The A45 eastbound stretch up to the Wilby Way roundabout was affected by surface water flooding from adjacent land and a blocked drainage network, causing road closures and requiring drainage clearance. (p6)",,GB-NNH_12_2012-07-14.html,GB-NNH_12_2012-07-14,Northamptonshire flooding 14 Jul 2012,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding on the A45 Eastbound between Great Doddington and Wilby Way 14th July 2012,090/North Northamptonshire/A45-Flood-Investigaton-Report.pdf
GB-NNH,12,2012-07-14,52.27911665874844,-0.7175676565029692,"<div id=""html_0f863d7f745bfe35f3f05463b0c415cf"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>A45 Between Great Doddington and Wilby Way</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Excess surface water flowed over and accumulated on the eastbound carriageway due to intense rainfall on a saturated catchment, inundation of the drainage network and an identified blockage. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road carriageway inundated by water flowing from an adjacent field and an inundated drainage network; the A45 (critical infrastructure) was closed and diversion routes put in place. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Eastbound carriageway was inundated as water from an adjacent field crossed the carriageway due to an inundated and blocked drainage network; traffic flow disrupted, central reserve barrier damaged after a single RTC associated with the event; drainage blockage required specialist jetting to clear. [IMG,PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from adjacent higher ground entered the carriageway; the highway drainage system (gullies, drains and drainage network) was completely inundated by the heavy rainfall and runoff, allowing water onto the carriageway. [PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding on the A45 caused a full road closure and required manpower to alleviate flooding. The closure created knock&ndash;on impacts on the surrounding road network due to diversion routes, causing localised congestion. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Photo (Highways Agency 14.07.12 09:55) and text reference indicate water running off surrounding land associated with flooding on the A45; surface water runoff affected the highway/roadside drainage and was a reported cause of flooding on this road. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall onto a saturated catchment and an inundated/drainage network (with an identified blockage) caused excess surface water to flow over and accumulate on the carriageway of the A45 eastbound between Great Doddington and Wilby Way. (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 Road Traffic Collision causing central reserve barrier damage; suspected drainage blockage depth ~40 metres; 1 jetter (from Telford) attended and cleared the blockage (arrived 13:21, cleared 14:18) [IMG,PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>road closure duration: 7 hours and 8 minutes (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,A45 Between Great Doddington and Wilby Way,England,"Excess surface water flowed over and accumulated on the eastbound carriageway due to intense rainfall on a saturated catchment, inundation of the drainage network and an identified blockage. (p4)
Road carriageway inundated by water flowing from an adjacent field and an inundated drainage network; the A45 (critical infrastructure) was closed and diversion routes put in place. (p5)
Eastbound carriageway was inundated as water from an adjacent field crossed the carriageway due to an inundated and blocked drainage network; traffic flow disrupted, central reserve barrier damaged after a single RTC associated with the event; drainage blockage required specialist jetting to clear. [IMG,PAG] (p6)
Surface water runoff from adjacent higher ground entered the carriageway; the highway drainage system (gullies, drains and drainage network) was completely inundated by the heavy rainfall and runoff, allowing water onto the carriageway. [PAG] (p7)
Flooding on the A45 caused a full road closure and required manpower to alleviate flooding. The closure created knock–on impacts on the surrounding road network due to diversion routes, causing localised congestion. (p8)
Photo (Highways Agency 14.07.12 09:55) and text reference indicate water running off surrounding land associated with flooding on the A45; surface water runoff affected the highway/roadside drainage and was a reported cause of flooding on this road. (p10)
Intense rainfall onto a saturated catchment and an inundated/drainage network (with an identified blockage) caused excess surface water to flow over and accumulate on the carriageway of the A45 eastbound between Great Doddington and Wilby Way. (p11)","1 Road Traffic Collision causing central reserve barrier damage; suspected drainage blockage depth ~40 metres; 1 jetter (from Telford) attended and cleared the blockage (arrived 13:21, cleared 14:18) [IMG,PAG] (p6)
road closure duration: 7 hours and 8 minutes (p8)",GB-NNH_12_2012-07-14.html,GB-NNH_12_2012-07-14,Northamptonshire flooding 14 Jul 2012,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding on the A45 Eastbound between Great Doddington and Wilby Way 14th July 2012,090/North Northamptonshire/A45-Flood-Investigaton-Report.pdf
