GB-BNS,2,2023-10-17,53.532104,-1.6401665,"<div id=""html_3d509c83846f927146b5d183b3692107"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Penistone</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road closures due to flooding were reported across the borough, described as extending from Penistone in the west to Thurnscoe in the east. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Barnsley,Penistone,England,"Road closures due to flooding were reported across the borough, described as extending from Penistone in the west to Thurnscoe in the east. (p6)",,GB-BNS_2_2023-10-17.html,GB-BNS_2_2023-10-17,Barnsley flooding 17 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Flood And Water Management Act 2010: Section 19 Statutory Report: Investigation Of Flooding Event In Barnsley Storm Babet Oct 2023,003/Barnsley/003/2023/Barnsley/Barnsley/Oct/2023.pdf
GB-BNS,2,2023-10-17,53.54582,-1.31536,"<div id=""html_fd99c6201bf996a0d7c25edec2110def"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Thurnscoe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood&ndash;related road closures were reported across the borough, described as extending to Thurnscoe in the east. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Barnsley,Thurnscoe,England,"Flood–related road closures were reported across the borough, described as extending to Thurnscoe in the east. (p6)",,GB-BNS_2_2023-10-17.html,GB-BNS_2_2023-10-17,Barnsley flooding 17 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Flood And Water Management Act 2010: Section 19 Statutory Report: Investigation Of Flooding Event In Barnsley Storm Babet Oct 2023,003/Barnsley/003/2023/Barnsley/Barnsley/Oct/2023.pdf
GB-HEF,16,2020-02-16,52.018846,-2.842977,"<div id=""html_a30bc013b512026c28b9427ca5100cab"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kingstone</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties caused by overland/surface water flow and overflowing sewers; sewage contamination reported. Internal flood depths recorded ranging from less than 6 inches up to 1 ft. Sandbags were delivered to a property during the event. (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; internal flood depths ranging from <6 inches up to 1 ft; sandbags delivered to 1 property on 16 February 2020 (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Kingstone,England,Internal flooding of residential properties caused by overland/surface water flow and overflowing sewers; sewage contamination reported. Internal flood depths recorded ranging from less than 6 inches up to 1 ft. Sandbags were delivered to a property during the event. (p2),5 properties; internal flood depths ranging from <6 inches up to 1 ft; sandbags delivered to 1 property on 16 February 2020 (p2),GB-HEF_16_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_16_2020-02-16,Kingstone flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Kingstone,055/Herefordshire County/15/Kingstone.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.3035775,-0.4159677,"<div id=""html_4fe3b23f41430aa71a72de13edc7757d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Scalby Beck</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A modelling study for Scalby Beck (from Lady Edith's Drive) corroborated the number of properties at risk from flooding along the watercourse; further blockage&ndash;consequence modelling is planned to assess flood risk from ordinary watercourse assets. [TAB,MUL] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Scalby Beck,England,"A modelling study for Scalby Beck (from Lady Edith's Drive) corroborated the number of properties at risk from flooding along the watercourse; further blockage–consequence modelling is planned to assess flood risk from ordinary watercourse assets. [TAB,MUL] (p6)",,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.2594787,-0.4128623,"<div id=""html_0da1bb6adf41272de9b2f08a21efdca4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Mere</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Scarborough Mere acted as a storage feature and its outfall into the Yorkshire Water sewer prevented properties from discharging their surface water to the public sewer during the events, contributing to local sewer surcharge and periodic local flooding issues. [TAB,MUL] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,The Mere,England,"Scarborough Mere acted as a storage feature and its outfall into the Yorkshire Water sewer prevented properties from discharging their surface water to the public sewer during the events, contributing to local sewer surcharge and periodic local flooding issues. [TAB,MUL] (p6)",,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.273049,-0.4062995,"<div id=""html_f32b46643d0e39aba21cbf1409a0c055"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Westbourne Grove, Scarborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed as a location affected by the August and September 2023 flood events. Properties and/or highway areas were impacted by flooding. Emergency response activity across the affected locations included pump&ndash;outs by the Fire Service, road closures and post&ndash;event drainage survey/clearing by NYC Highways, provision of sandbags to residents, and follow&ndash;up visits by NYC Flood Risk Team and the Environment Agency to assess impacts and provide advice. [MUL] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Westbourne Grove, Scarborough",England,"Listed as a location affected by the August and September 2023 flood events. Properties and/or highway areas were impacted by flooding. Emergency response activity across the affected locations included pump–outs by the Fire Service, road closures and post–event drainage survey/clearing by NYC Highways, provision of sandbags to residents, and follow–up visits by NYC Flood Risk Team and the Environment Agency to assess impacts and provide advice. [MUL] (p1)",,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.295238,-0.4441378,"<div id=""html_319debac95bf29bc2e3e5753a608309d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hackness Road, Newby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified in the report as one of the Newby streets affected by the August and September 2023 flood events. Impacts and responses recorded for the affected locations included property flooding and highway impacts, pump&ndash;outs by the Fire Service, road closures and drainage survey/clearing by NYC Highways, sandbags provided to residents, and follow&ndash;up visits by NYC Flood Risk Team and the Environment Agency. [MUL] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Repeated flooding of the highway during 2023 with associated risk of property flooding; highways flooding can occur almost annually and property flooding estimated every 2&ndash;5 years. Up to seven properties may be affected in a 1&ndash;in&ndash;25&ndash;year event. Location experienced flooding on 05/08/2023 and 18/09/2023. [PAG,MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culverted section of the main river surcharged and, together with overwhelmed highways, private drains and sewers, caused excess surface water to fall to the low point on Hackness Road, flowing onto the highway and into/under properties. Road users driving through the floodwater generated bow waves that exacerbated the flooding. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flows towards the culverted main river under Hackness Road contributed to internal flooding risk to nearby properties; a proposed diversion scheme would provide approximate 1:100 year protection to properties currently affected or at risk. [TAB,MUL] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Hackness Road were affected by flooding; the council is offering property flood resilience grants to affected properties as a response measure. [MUL] (p5)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>seven properties [PAG,MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>27 properties [TAB,MUL] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately ␀A37,000 per property; estimated overall cost approximately ␀A356,000 [MUL] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Hackness Road, Newby",England,"Identified in the report as one of the Newby streets affected by the August and September 2023 flood events. Impacts and responses recorded for the affected locations included property flooding and highway impacts, pump–outs by the Fire Service, road closures and drainage survey/clearing by NYC Highways, sandbags provided to residents, and follow–up visits by NYC Flood Risk Team and the Environment Agency. [MUL] (p1)
Repeated flooding of the highway during 2023 with associated risk of property flooding; highways flooding can occur almost annually and property flooding estimated every 2–5 years. Up to seven properties may be affected in a 1–in–25–year event. Location experienced flooding on 05/08/2023 and 18/09/2023. [PAG,MUL] (p2)
The culverted section of the main river surcharged and, together with overwhelmed highways, private drains and sewers, caused excess surface water to fall to the low point on Hackness Road, flowing onto the highway and into/under properties. Road users driving through the floodwater generated bow waves that exacerbated the flooding. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p3)
Flows towards the culverted main river under Hackness Road contributed to internal flooding risk to nearby properties; a proposed diversion scheme would provide approximate 1:100 year protection to properties currently affected or at risk. [TAB,MUL] (p4)
Properties on Hackness Road were affected by flooding; the council is offering property flood resilience grants to affected properties as a response measure. [MUL] (p5)","seven properties [PAG,MUL] (p2)
27 properties [TAB,MUL] (p4)
approximately ␀A37,000 per property; estimated overall cost approximately ␀A356,000 [MUL] (p5)",GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.2899758,-0.4450719,"<div id=""html_bfeb713c1162fe19f0590fd8e676f248"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Moor Lane, Newby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Named in the report as one of the Newby streets affected by the August and September 2023 flood events. Reported responses across affected locations included property pump&ndash;outs by the Fire Service, road closures and drainage clearing by NYC Highways, provision of sandbags to residents, and visits by NYC Flood Risk Team and the Environment Agency to assess and advise. [MUL] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Moor Lane were affected by flooding; the council is offering property flood resilience grants to affected properties as a response measure. [MUL] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a location for property flood resilience measures after being affected by local flooding that caused or risked internal property flooding; measures proposed include flood doors and air brick covers. [TAB,MUL] (p8)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately ␀A37,000 per property; estimated overall cost approximately ␀A356,000 [MUL] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Moor Lane, Newby",England,"Named in the report as one of the Newby streets affected by the August and September 2023 flood events. Reported responses across affected locations included property pump–outs by the Fire Service, road closures and drainage clearing by NYC Highways, provision of sandbags to residents, and visits by NYC Flood Risk Team and the Environment Agency to assess and advise. [MUL] (p1)
Properties on Moor Lane were affected by flooding; the council is offering property flood resilience grants to affected properties as a response measure. [MUL] (p5)
Identified as a location for property flood resilience measures after being affected by local flooding that caused or risked internal property flooding; measures proposed include flood doors and air brick covers. [TAB,MUL] (p8)","approximately ␀A37,000 per property; estimated overall cost approximately ␀A356,000 [MUL] (p5)",GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.2942445,-0.4443341,"<div id=""html_0f370b98ba2f26ab930181ac52d90985"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lawrence Grove, Newby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flows towards the culverted main river under Lawrence Grove contributed to internal flooding risk to nearby properties; a proposed diversion scheme would provide approximate 1:100 year protection to properties currently affected or at risk. [TAB,MUL] (p4)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>27 properties [TAB,MUL] (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Lawrence Grove, Newby",England,"Flows towards the culverted main river under Lawrence Grove contributed to internal flooding risk to nearby properties; a proposed diversion scheme would provide approximate 1:100 year protection to properties currently affected or at risk. [TAB,MUL] (p4)","27 properties [TAB,MUL] (p4)",GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.2926518,-0.4079732,"<div id=""html_02e023b2920124086f224ee525ca68fd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Peasholm Gap, Scarborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A piped watercourse narrows to a 375mm culverted pipe at Peasholm Gap, restricting outfall and contributing to surface water surcharge and exceedance flows; increasing the outfall was considered not cost beneficial. [TAB,MUL] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Peasholm Gap, Scarborough",England,"A piped watercourse narrows to a 375mm culverted pipe at Peasholm Gap, restricting outfall and contributing to surface water surcharge and exceedance flows; increasing the outfall was considered not cost beneficial. [TAB,MUL] (p6)",,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.2877021,-0.4088562,"<div id=""html_72d244de6b0ccebef87d43dce1d082a1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Columbus Ravine, Scarborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff caused surcharge of the drainage system at this location. Manholes were damaged by surface water surcharge and exceedance flows occurred; the location receives significant runoff due to topography and the piped system is constrained in capacity. [TAB,MUL] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Columbus Ravine, Scarborough",England,"Surface water runoff caused surcharge of the drainage system at this location. Manholes were damaged by surface water surcharge and exceedance flows occurred; the location receives significant runoff due to topography and the piped system is constrained in capacity. [TAB,MUL] (p6)",,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.2837744,-0.3942082,"<div id=""html_106ca052b9b2510a6f08e2b50d94e036"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Eastborough, Scarborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water surcharge caused damage to a number of manholes; the area receives significant runoff and functions as an exceedance flowpath due to topography, contributing to flooding and surcharge of the highway/drainage network. [TAB,MUL] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Eastborough, Scarborough",England,"Surface–water surcharge caused damage to a number of manholes; the area receives significant runoff and functions as an exceedance flowpath due to topography, contributing to flooding and surcharge of the highway/drainage network. [TAB,MUL] (p6)",,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.2857,-0.4335331,"<div id=""html_92290b3c48dc0dbd25e2eab0238c59a9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lady Edith's Drive, Scarborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Modelling from Lady Edith's Drive into Scalby Beck corroborated that properties in this area are at risk of flooding; the location is included in further blockage and consequence studies. [TAB,MUL] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Lady Edith's Drive, Scarborough",England,"Modelling from Lady Edith's Drive into Scalby Beck corroborated that properties in this area are at risk of flooding; the location is included in further blockage and consequence studies. [TAB,MUL] (p6)",,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.29589540778722,-0.4435402017543148,"<div id=""html_bb1b3a153e0f7f9c153abc2212c135f0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Harkness Road, Newby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a location for property flood resilience measures after being affected by local flooding that caused or risked internal property flooding; measures proposed include flood doors and air brick covers. [TAB,MUL] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Harkness Road, Newby",England,"Identified as a location for property flood resilience measures after being affected by local flooding that caused or risked internal property flooding; measures proposed include flood doors and air brick covers. [TAB,MUL] (p8)",,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.282,-0.4011868,"<div id=""html_6baaafd6cedfe831feabe81fdd747ef4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Scarborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Scarborough were affected by flooding during the events in August and September 2023; properties and highways were reported as flooded and emergency services (fire service) and NYC teams responded, including pumping out properties and closing roads. [MUL] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Emergency response across the area for the 05/08/2023 and 18/09/2023 events: Fire Service pumped out a number of properties, NYC Highways closed roads and surveyed/cleared drainage debris, NYC provided sandbags; Flood Risk Team and Environment Agency visited locations to assess impacts and provide advice to residents. [MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Hackness Road and Moor Lane were affected by flooding. The council recommended and approved property flood resilience grants for properties impacted in those streets to mitigate future risk. [MUL] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Scarborough Mere acted as a storage with a baffle plate at the outfall into the Yorkshire Water sewer; this prevented some properties discharging surface water to the sewer system and contributed to periodic surface&ndash;water flooding issues in the Scarborough area. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood events in the town caused internal flooding to properties and prompted the proposal to fund property flood resilience measures for affected properties. [TAB,MUL] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred in the town; the report covers flooding impacts and responses in Scarborough and the surrounding areas during the specified flood events. [MUL] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately £7,000.00 per property; estimated overall cost approximately £56,000 [MUL] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Scarborough,England,"Parts of Scarborough were affected by flooding during the events in August and September 2023; properties and highways were reported as flooded and emergency services (fire service) and NYC teams responded, including pumping out properties and closing roads. [MUL] (p1)
Emergency response across the area for the 05/08/2023 and 18/09/2023 events: Fire Service pumped out a number of properties, NYC Highways closed roads and surveyed/cleared drainage debris, NYC provided sandbags; Flood Risk Team and Environment Agency visited locations to assess impacts and provide advice to residents. [MUL] (p2)
Properties on Hackness Road and Moor Lane were affected by flooding. The council recommended and approved property flood resilience grants for properties impacted in those streets to mitigate future risk. [MUL] (p5)
Scarborough Mere acted as a storage with a baffle plate at the outfall into the Yorkshire Water sewer; this prevented some properties discharging surface water to the sewer system and contributed to periodic surface–water flooding issues in the Scarborough area. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p6)
Flood events in the town caused internal flooding to properties and prompted the proposal to fund property flood resilience measures for affected properties. [TAB,MUL] (p8)
Flooding occurred in the town; the report covers flooding impacts and responses in Scarborough and the surrounding areas during the specified flood events. [MUL] (p10)","approximately £7,000.00 per property; estimated overall cost approximately £56,000 [MUL] (p5)",GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.2924798,-0.4424421,"<div id=""html_6005bdd31249305a95e954e5083f53a5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Newby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Named in the report as affected by the August and September 2023 flood events (specifically the Newby area including Hackness Road and Moor Lane). Emergency response actions following the events included pump&ndash;outs by the Fire Service at properties, road closures and drainage clearing by NYC Highways, sandbags provided to residents, and visits by NYC Flood Risk Team and the Environment Agency to assess and advise. [MUL] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Newby,England,"Named in the report as affected by the August and September 2023 flood events (specifically the Newby area including Hackness Road and Moor Lane). Emergency response actions following the events included pump–outs by the Fire Service at properties, road closures and drainage clearing by NYC Highways, sandbags provided to residents, and visits by NYC Flood Risk Team and the Environment Agency to assess and advise. [MUL] (p1)",,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.433222,-0.5344748,"<div id=""html_255b8dd2b4f8a459053f6914f6fa9e99"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Robin Hood's Bay</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties internally flooded. [MUL] (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties internally flooded [MUL] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Robin Hood's Bay,England,Properties internally flooded. [MUL] (p2),6 properties internally flooded [MUL] (p2),GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.22814781733018,-0.589239600326728,"<div id=""html_8c4e6d94f334e794ddda7287c59d5d88"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Snainton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties and local highway closure. [MUL] (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties [MUL] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Snainton,England,Internal flooding of residential properties and local highway closure. [MUL] (p2),8 properties [MUL] (p2),GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,1,2023-08-05,54.29051247681476,-0.4141855255084341,"<div id=""html_fe71087f40dd023dcc31b180f3b41cce"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Peasholm</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A watercourse through Peasholm narrows to a 375mm culverted pipe at Peasholm Gap, restricting the outfall of the piped system and contributing to surcharge and reduced capacity during intense runoff, exacerbating local flooding. [TAB,MUL] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Peasholm,England,"A watercourse through Peasholm narrows to a 375mm culverted pipe at Peasholm Gap, restricting the outfall of the piped system and contributing to surcharge and reduced capacity during intense runoff, exacerbating local flooding. [TAB,MUL] (p6)",,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc.html,GB-NYK_1_2023-08-05_etc,Scarborough flooding 05 Aug 2023 and Scarborough flooding 18 Sep 2023,Flood events affecting Scarborough and the surrounding Areas,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood Events affecting Scarborough and surrounding areas.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.00604591455792,-1.4346784170446831,"<div id=""html_90f98ce59d88b541466edf804a199421"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Riverside Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties at Riverside Park were affected by high water levels in the River Nidd and its tributary (The Rampart), causing internal flooding of properties. [TAB] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Riverside Park,England,"Properties at Riverside Park were affected by high water levels in the River Nidd and its tributary (The Rampart), causing internal flooding of properties. [TAB] (p5)",,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.0062535,-1.4415474,"<div id=""html_8c151487d26cec66d67fb5836afd24b9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Nidderdale Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties at Nidderdale Park were affected by high water levels in the River Nidd and its tributary (The Rampart), resulting in internal property flooding. [TAB] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Nidderdale Park,England,"Properties at Nidderdale Park were affected by high water levels in the River Nidd and its tributary (The Rampart), resulting in internal property flooding. [TAB] (p5)",,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.0322022,-1.5638727,"<div id=""html_155b963367f74686b5ffa2723ded2b96"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Nidd</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heightened river levels in the River Nidd caused the river to overtop its banks and inundate properties in Knaresborough. [TAB] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Nidd catchment received substantial rainfall (November&ndash;December 2015) and experienced saturated ground conditions and high runoff which contributed to surface water flooding of downstream communities (including the Greenfields Avenue area). [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Exceptional rainfall in December 2015 across the Nidd catchment contributed to flooding affecting communities in the catchment and downstream areas. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,River Nidd,England,"Heightened river levels in the River Nidd caused the river to overtop its banks and inundate properties in Knaresborough. [TAB] (p5)
The Nidd catchment received substantial rainfall (November–December 2015) and experienced saturated ground conditions and high runoff which contributed to surface water flooding of downstream communities (including the Greenfields Avenue area). [TAB] (p8)
Exceptional rainfall in December 2015 across the Nidd catchment contributed to flooding affecting communities in the catchment and downstream areas. (p10)",,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.8849895,-1.2599117,"<div id=""html_9bc23530e98431d5d098979345f8588e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tadcaster Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Structural failure of Tadcaster bridge during the December 2015 storm events. (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Tadcaster Bridge,England,Structural failure of Tadcaster bridge during the December 2015 storm events. (p1),,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.006446289530565,-1.470513195763802,"<div id=""html_a59455426d4bd319d54684c263e3f053"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Waterside, Knaresborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties along Waterside experienced internal flooding as the River Nidd overflowed its banks. [TAB] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Waterside, Knaresborough",England,Properties along Waterside experienced internal flooding as the River Nidd overflowed its banks. [TAB] (p5),,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.996715,-1.4586471,"<div id=""html_7e3f92912d4e8ed5895e74760a9b2982"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Abbey Road, Knaresborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties along Abbey Road experienced internal flooding as the River Nidd overflowed its banks. [TAB] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Abbey Road, Knaresborough",England,Properties along Abbey Road experienced internal flooding as the River Nidd overflowed its banks. [TAB] (p5),,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.9641282,-1.2733786,"<div id=""html_f444b14dbcb01bbe0440876ad85e3869"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Marston Road, Tockwith</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sike Beck was the primary source of flood waters; two culverts had insufficient capacity and surcharged, causing flood waters to flow onto Marston Road. Quick action by residents and farmers limited the potential for more extensive internal property flooding. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Marston Road, Tockwith",England,"Sike Beck was the primary source of flood waters; two culverts had insufficient capacity and surcharged, causing flood waters to flow onto Marston Road. Quick action by residents and farmers limited the potential for more extensive internal property flooding. (p6)",,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.9642931,-1.2953902,"<div id=""html_b198d0e01f7dba6b17eeefc90396f395"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Prince Rupert Drive, Tockwith</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A large catchment to the south discharged into a historic culvert system; a 750mm culvert reduced to 300mm under properties created a pinch point that was a significant factor contributing to flooding at Prince Rupert Drive. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Prince Rupert Drive, Tockwith",England,A large catchment to the south discharged into a historic culvert system; a 750mm culvert reduced to 300mm under properties created a pinch point that was a significant factor contributing to flooding at Prince Rupert Drive. (p6),,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.0160487,-1.4642278,"<div id=""html_ddf266a888f0c945fddb0d9e9b113adc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Blind Lane, Knaresborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooded by surface water runoff from agricultural land with apparently no outfall; extensive flooding to gardens and internal property flooding occurred. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Blind Lane, Knaresborough",England,Flooded by surface water runoff from agricultural land with apparently no outfall; extensive flooding to gardens and internal property flooding occurred. (p6),,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.96559227813623,-1.290216863319507,"<div id=""html_abc95115ce964936bb2567d58ccaf9d8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Westfield Road, Tockwith</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties along Westfield Road were affected by flood water contaminated with sewage, indicating the foul sewer received surface water which caused the sewer to overflow. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Westfield Road, Tockwith",England,"Properties along Westfield Road were affected by flood water contaminated with sewage, indicating the foul sewer received surface water which caused the sewer to overflow. (p6)",,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.9680617,-1.2933155,"<div id=""html_43be4cd255bae4cf940f1e815f5648f0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fleet Lane, Tockwith</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties along Fleet Lane were affected by flood water contaminated with sewage, indicating the foul sewer received surface water and overflowed. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Fleet Lane, Tockwith",England,"Properties along Fleet Lane were affected by flood water contaminated with sewage, indicating the foul sewer received surface water and overflowed. (p6)",,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.7246564,-1.2704871,"<div id=""html_2cc52b3b14725b00f1bc088c3fc1f778"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Low Street, Brotherton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway runoff from the rainfall event flowed from Low Street into properties; flooding at Low Street was caused by excess surface water from the second rainfall pulse (25&ndash;26 December 2015). Low Street was not directly affected by the River Aire. [TAB] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Low Street, Brotherton",England,Highway runoff from the rainfall event flowed from Low Street into properties; flooding at Low Street was caused by excess surface water from the second rainfall pulse (25–26 December 2015). Low Street was not directly affected by the River Aire. [TAB] (p8),,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.7219767,-1.2680297,"<div id=""html_f57ea0f65d63171c9bf51238789f72fe"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Marsh Croft, Brotherton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway drainage on Marsh Croft was overwhelmed during the 25&ndash;26 December 2015 rainfall, the surface water system was unable to discharge and this led to surface&ndash;water flooding in the area. [TAB] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Marsh Croft, Brotherton",England,"Highway drainage on Marsh Croft was overwhelmed during the 25–26 December 2015 rainfall, the surface water system was unable to discharge and this led to surface–water flooding in the area. [TAB] (p8)",,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.0205851,-1.3375012,"<div id=""html_60d7689686c234f25743e1456dbb55a5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Lane, Whixley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway surface water from surrounding agricultural land discharged onto West Lane; a grass verge prevented free flow into a critical ditch system which exacerbated surface water flooding on the highway. [TAB] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"West Lane, Whixley",England,Highway surface water from surrounding agricultural land discharged onto West Lane; a grass verge prevented free flow into a critical ditch system which exacerbated surface water flooding on the highway. [TAB] (p8),,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
