GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.170840247776326,-1.3013084540705857,"<div id=""html_51315f8ac4a7ff09ef129ad55007fbd9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sessay Garth, Sessay</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowed towards and entered properties on Sessay Garth. [MUL] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Sessay Garth, Sessay",England,Surface water flowed towards and entered properties on Sessay Garth. [MUL] (p10),,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.1345328,-1.4986285,"<div id=""html_5d0b20b34b798de0fb7fef80be550a00"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Yorkshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding across the county from multiple sources. Impacts reported include approximately 600 properties (business and residential) flooded internally, the closure of the A59 between Skipton and Harrogate, closure of the A1 in the Catterick area and the structural failure of Tadcaster bridge. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>County council (NYCC) led a countywide review after the December 2015&ndash;January 2016 flood incidents, identified locations for formal Section 19 investigations, presented outcomes to Area Committees in May&ndash;June 2016, commissioned Mouchel to produce formal investigation reports, and carried out data collection and liaison with consultants and responsible RMAs. [IMG] (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Approximately 600 properties (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,North Yorkshire,England,"Significant flooding across the county from multiple sources. Impacts reported include approximately 600 properties (business and residential) flooded internally, the closure of the A59 between Skipton and Harrogate, closure of the A1 in the Catterick area and the structural failure of Tadcaster bridge. (p1)
County council (NYCC) led a countywide review after the December 2015–January 2016 flood incidents, identified locations for formal Section 19 investigations, presented outcomes to Area Committees in May–June 2016, commissioned Mouchel to produce formal investigation reports, and carried out data collection and liaison with consultants and responsible RMAs. [IMG] (p2)",Approximately 600 properties (p1),GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.1345328,-1.4986285,"<div id=""html_f1957af338320551bd9fa0c282fba1a2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Yorkshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The area experienced widespread flooding from a range of sources, resulting in internal flooding to properties and transport infrastructure impacts (road closures and bridge failure) as described in the report. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread and substantial rainfall over North Yorkshire in late December 2015 led to significant flooding in the county. Specific impacts described in the report included a Boxing Day (26 December 2015) flood event affecting the village of Sessay and a flood event in Whixley where Cherry Tree Farm Development experienced surface water overtopping (Church Street access ramp), North Yorkshire Fire and Rescue Service undertook pumping operations and constructed a temporary bund to divert excess surface water, Yorkshire Water cleared obstructions in the foul sewer on Back Lane, the County Council as Highway Authority carried out gully jetting and repairs, and the owner of Cherry Tree Farmhouse constructed a masonry wall after the Boxing Day 2015 event. [MUL] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread and substantial rainfall over North Yorkshire in late December 2015 (on already saturated ground from a very wet November) contributed to runoff and flooding in the Nidd catchment and affected communities. [MUL] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Approximately 600 properties (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,North Yorkshire,England,"The area experienced widespread flooding from a range of sources, resulting in internal flooding to properties and transport infrastructure impacts (road closures and bridge failure) as described in the report. (p1)
Widespread and substantial rainfall over North Yorkshire in late December 2015 led to significant flooding in the county. Specific impacts described in the report included a Boxing Day (26 December 2015) flood event affecting the village of Sessay and a flood event in Whixley where Cherry Tree Farm Development experienced surface water overtopping (Church Street access ramp), North Yorkshire Fire and Rescue Service undertook pumping operations and constructed a temporary bund to divert excess surface water, Yorkshire Water cleared obstructions in the foul sewer on Back Lane, the County Council as Highway Authority carried out gully jetting and repairs, and the owner of Cherry Tree Farmhouse constructed a masonry wall after the Boxing Day 2015 event. [MUL] (p9)
Widespread and substantial rainfall over North Yorkshire in late December 2015 (on already saturated ground from a very wet November) contributed to runoff and flooding in the Nidd catchment and affected communities. [MUL] (p10)",Approximately 600 properties (p1),GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.89933113967193,-1.9826201342823537,"<div id=""html_a41398dedd95ccf4aa8e9a6f41a9dd1d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Craven</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding occurred during the December 2015 flood events (South Craven listed among impacted locations). (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Named as one of the locations where a formal Section 19 investigation was progressed because it experienced significant numbers of properties flooded or repeat incidents during the December 2015&ndash;January 2016 events. [IMG] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 26 December 2015 South Craven experienced flooding from rivers, surface water and groundwater. Surface water runoff from steep agricultural land and overloaded historic masonry culverts and highway drainage caused significant local flooding; highways conveyed flows into communities, gullies were blocked by gravel/sediment, and roads were described as looking like 'rivers'. [TAB,PAG] (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one of 8 Section 19 investigation locations (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>74 properties [TAB,PAG] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,South Craven,England,"Significant flooding occurred during the December 2015 flood events (South Craven listed among impacted locations). (p1)
Named as one of the locations where a formal Section 19 investigation was progressed because it experienced significant numbers of properties flooded or repeat incidents during the December 2015–January 2016 events. [IMG] (p2)
On 26 December 2015 South Craven experienced flooding from rivers, surface water and groundwater. Surface water runoff from steep agricultural land and overloaded historic masonry culverts and highway drainage caused significant local flooding; highways conveyed flows into communities, gullies were blocked by gravel/sediment, and roads were described as looking like 'rivers'. [TAB,PAG] (p6)","one of 8 Section 19 investigation locations (p2)
74 properties [TAB,PAG] (p6)",GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.006741961160174,-1.5144704578826116,"<div id=""html_2de59ddd4eb827a30edf6e6dfa36beaa"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Harrogate District</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>These places were identified as having experienced significant property flooding (including repeat incidents where no prior formal investigation existed) and were progressed as formal Section 19 investigations to better understand the events and RMA actions. (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one of 8 Section 19 investigation locations (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Harrogate District,England,These places were identified as having experienced significant property flooding (including repeat incidents where no prior formal investigation existed) and were progressed as formal Section 19 investigations to better understand the events and RMA actions. (p2),one of 8 Section 19 investigation locations (p2),GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
