GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,54.0101765,-1.4651279311880052,"<div id=""html_8e4049e1fdce446a45e6a535f3b38b5b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Knaresborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding occurred during the December 2015 flood events (Knaresborough listed among impacted locations). (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>These places were identified as having experienced significant property flooding (including repeat incidents where no prior formal investigation existed) and were progressed as formal Section 19 investigations to better understand the events and RMA actions. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 26 December 2015 heightened River Nidd levels caused the river to overtop and inundate properties in central and eastern Knaresborough, causing internal damage. In central Knaresborough properties flooded along Waterside and Abbey Road as the River Nidd overtopped between the A59 and the A658. In eastern Knaresborough high water in the River Nidd and its tributary (The Rampart) affected properties at Riverside Park and Nidderdale Park. Some properties may also have been affected by surface water runoff overwhelming drainage systems. [TAB] (p5)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one of 8 Section 19 investigation locations (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Knaresborough,England,"Significant flooding occurred during the December 2015 flood events (Knaresborough listed among impacted locations). (p1)
