GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.8995159,-1.9998245,"<div id=""html_db6feb5f59ed5abc146e468e35b89cb1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Glusburn</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from saturated surrounding land and overwhelmed highway drainage led to significant surface water flows and internal property flooding in Glusburn. [TAB] (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Internal flooding as part of the total 74 properties flooded across the six South Craven communities [TAB] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Glusburn,England,Surface water runoff from saturated surrounding land and overwhelmed highway drainage led to significant surface water flows and internal property flooding in Glusburn. [TAB] (p6),Internal flooding as part of the total 74 properties flooded across the six South Craven communities [TAB] (p6),GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-NYK,4,2015-12-01,53.8917524,-1.9922285,"<div id=""html_b76a590756845fdc0f1216272655e938"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sutton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff conveyed by highways and overloaded culverted systems intensified flooding in Sutton&ndash;in&ndash;Craven, resulting in internal property flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Internal flooding as part of the total 74 properties flooded across the six South Craven communities [TAB,PAG] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Sutton,England,"Surface water runoff conveyed by highways and overloaded culverted systems intensified flooding in Sutton–in–Craven, resulting in internal property flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p6)","Internal flooding as part of the total 74 properties flooded across the six South Craven communities [TAB,PAG] (p6)",GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01.html,GB-NYK_4_2015-12-01,North Yorkshire flooding December 2015 - January 2016,Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yorkshire,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Reports on the December 2015 Flooding Events in North Yo.pdf
GB-HEF,10,2020-02-16,52.1409552,-3.0105158,"<div id=""html_175d8f02abb48532a05a386dc1e61cd4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Woodseaves Road, Eardisley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Woodseaves Road is labelled in the study area where Flood Zone 3 (high risk) and Flood Zone 2 are mapped along the river, so the road is indicated to be within or adjacent to the mapped river&ndash;flood risk zones. [IMG] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,"Woodseaves Road, Eardisley",England,"Woodseaves Road is labelled in the study area where Flood Zone 3 (high risk) and Flood Zone 2 are mapped along the river, so the road is indicated to be within or adjacent to the mapped river–flood risk zones. [IMG] (p1)",,GB-HEF_10_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_10_2020-02-16,Eardisley flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Eardisley,055/Herefordshire County/09/Eardisley.pdf
GB-HEF,10,2020-02-16,52.1388657,-3.0072073,"<div id=""html_c841cd875b6656c5d580cd12d1d8c9ac"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church Road, Eardisley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Folly Brook is culverted below Church Road; the culvert can become overwhelmed during storms, causing surface water flooding throughout the village that affects Church Road. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 internally flooded properties (related to key flood event); 22 internally flooded properties (most acute flood) &mdash; area&ndash;wide (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,"Church Road, Eardisley",England,"The Folly Brook is culverted below Church Road; the culvert can become overwhelmed during storms, causing surface water flooding throughout the village that affects Church Road. (p3)",6 internally flooded properties (related to key flood event); 22 internally flooded properties (most acute flood) — area–wide (p3),GB-HEF_10_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_10_2020-02-16,Eardisley flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Eardisley,055/Herefordshire County/09/Eardisley.pdf
GB-HEF,10,2020-02-16,52.1427778,-3.0016533,"<div id=""html_a359937cab098f5eb1f577c1de53c4c7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Almeley Road, Eardisley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property flooding occurred on Almeley Road as a result of surface water flooding, which may have been exacerbated by the condition of a highway culvert. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,"Almeley Road, Eardisley",England,"Property flooding occurred on Almeley Road as a result of surface water flooding, which may have been exacerbated by the condition of a highway culvert. (p3)",,GB-HEF_10_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_10_2020-02-16,Eardisley flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Eardisley,055/Herefordshire County/09/Eardisley.pdf
GB-HEF,10,2020-02-16,52.1372723,-3.0045408,"<div id=""html_b097e736b9913b3b9f53b1bf512ab54f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Eardisley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Built&ndash;up parts of the village lie within high flood risk zones (Flood Zone 3) adjacent to the main river; areas to the west and south of the river are the most affected. Local flood defences and a flood storage area are present but do not cover all high&ndash;risk areas. [IMG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding occurred to properties within the village during the key event; sandbags were also delivered to a property (separately noted on 26 October 2019). Some respondents recorded previous flood events (2007, ~13 years prior to report, and one reporting 'almost annually'). [IMG,MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties are located in Flood Zone 3 and experienced both fluvial and surface&ndash;water flooding. During the key event properties were internally flooded; watercourses (Willersey Brook and Folly Brook) overflowed, the Folly Brook culvert below Church Road can become overwhelmed causing surface&ndash;water flooding through the village, and flows out of bank on Willersey Brook near the weir caused surface&ndash;water flooding affecting properties alongside the A4111. Cultural heritage is affected: listed properties lie within the flood zone. [MUL] (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties; depth 6 inches to 1 ft; duration less than 1 day [IMG,MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 internally flooded properties related to key flood event; 22 internally flooded properties during most acute flood; 17 listed properties located within the Flood Zone [MUL] (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Eardisley,England,"Built–up parts of the village lie within high flood risk zones (Flood Zone 3) adjacent to the main river; areas to the west and south of the river are the most affected. Local flood defences and a flood storage area are present but do not cover all high–risk areas. [IMG] (p1)
Internal flooding occurred to properties within the village during the key event; sandbags were also delivered to a property (separately noted on 26 October 2019). Some respondents recorded previous flood events (2007, ~13 years prior to report, and one reporting 'almost annually'). [IMG,MUL] (p2)
Properties are located in Flood Zone 3 and experienced both fluvial and surface–water flooding. During the key event properties were internally flooded; watercourses (Willersey Brook and Folly Brook) overflowed, the Folly Brook culvert below Church Road can become overwhelmed causing surface–water flooding through the village, and flows out of bank on Willersey Brook near the weir caused surface–water flooding affecting properties alongside the A4111. Cultural heritage is affected: listed properties lie within the flood zone. [MUL] (p3)","6 properties; depth 6 inches to 1 ft; duration less than 1 day [IMG,MUL] (p2)
6 internally flooded properties related to key flood event; 22 internally flooded properties during most acute flood; 17 listed properties located within the Flood Zone [MUL] (p3)",GB-HEF_10_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_10_2020-02-16,Eardisley flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Eardisley,055/Herefordshire County/09/Eardisley.pdf
GB-DBY,2,2023-10-18,52.995808,-1.3017821,"<div id=""html_64cb42a0d643b41c0217d18e10a46a5f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Erewash</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A Flood Alert was issued for the River Erewash (covering Derbyshire and Nottinghamshire) on 19 Oct 2023 at 01:13, and a Flood Warning was issued for the River Erewash at Langley Mill on 20 Oct 2023 at 06:44 during the storm period. (p8)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Flood Alert issued 19 Oct 2023 01:13; Flood Warning issued 20 Oct 2023 06:44. (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,River Erewash,England,"A Flood Alert was issued for the River Erewash (covering Derbyshire and Nottinghamshire) on 19 Oct 2023 at 01:13, and a Flood Warning was issued for the River Erewash at Langley Mill on 20 Oct 2023 at 06:44 during the storm period. (p8)",Flood Alert issued 19 Oct 2023 01:13; Flood Warning issued 20 Oct 2023 06:44. (p8),GB-DBY_2_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_2_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-2-county-wide-impacts-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,2,2023-10-18,53.1395212,-1.5590102,"<div id=""html_da8bf288d5cf4004f2516c74602fdc15"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Derwent</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A Severe Flood Warning was issued for the River Derwent at Racecourse Park (Chaddesden) on 21 Oct 2023 at 09:45 during the storm period. (p8)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 Severe Flood Warning (River Derwent at Racecourse Park, issued 21 Oct 2023 09:45). (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,River Derwent,England,A Severe Flood Warning was issued for the River Derwent at Racecourse Park (Chaddesden) on 21 Oct 2023 at 09:45 during the storm period. (p8),"1 Severe Flood Warning (River Derwent at Racecourse Park, issued 21 Oct 2023 09:45). (p8)",GB-DBY_2_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_2_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-2-county-wide-impacts-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,2,2023-10-18,53.2718354,-1.377915,"<div id=""html_f2b9ff97ee16b2eab91002ee39f73174"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Rother</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Rother (as part of the Don and Rother WFD catchment) was part of the most severely affected catchment during the event; the Don and Rother catchment accounted for 514 internally flooded properties. [TAB] (p8)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>514 properties (Don and Rother catchment) [TAB] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,River Rother,England,The Rother (as part of the Don and Rother WFD catchment) was part of the most severely affected catchment during the event; the Don and Rother catchment accounted for 514 internally flooded properties. [TAB] (p8),514 properties (Don and Rother catchment) [TAB] (p8),GB-DBY_2_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_2_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-2-county-wide-impacts-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
