GB-LAN,14,2016-06-16,53.5494817,-2.7896368,"<div id=""html_959d01be034a7f4a9f24f7f05e019744"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Willow Hey</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater had entered or was about to enter premises (Willow Hey); fire crews pumped out affected properties. Flooded properties in Skelmersdale received follow&ndash;up visits and drying work the next day. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Willow Hey,England,Floodwater had entered or was about to enter premises (Willow Hey); fire crews pumped out affected properties. Flooded properties in Skelmersdale received follow–up visits and drying work the next day. (p13),flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) (p13),GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16.html,GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16,Lancashire flooding 16 Jun 2016,16 June 2016 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-16-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,14,2016-06-16,53.5538156,-2.7934817,"<div id=""html_8b9c8963f0c16b9ce32fc66e03b955bc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>School Lane, Skelmersdale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater had entered or was about to enter properties on School Lane; fire crews pumped out affected properties. A council surveyor visited flooded properties in Skelmersdale the following day and drying out with dehumidifiers began. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"School Lane, Skelmersdale",England,Floodwater had entered or was about to enter properties on School Lane; fire crews pumped out affected properties. A council surveyor visited flooded properties in Skelmersdale the following day and drying out with dehumidifiers began. (p13),flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) (p13),GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16.html,GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16,Lancashire flooding 16 Jun 2016,16 June 2016 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-16-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,14,2016-06-16,53.55393726881829,-2.7922440281314396,"<div id=""html_88839f59ec963a136fb205f2d7a480e8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Thornton, Skelmersdale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater had entered or was about to enter premises; fire crews pumped out affected properties. Properties in Skelmersdale were visited the next day and drying out commenced with dehumidifiers. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Thornton, Skelmersdale",England,Floodwater had entered or was about to enter premises; fire crews pumped out affected properties. Properties in Skelmersdale were visited the next day and drying out commenced with dehumidifiers. (p13),flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) (p13),GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16.html,GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16,Lancashire flooding 16 Jun 2016,16 June 2016 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-16-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,14,2016-06-16,53.5502831,-2.7831178,"<div id=""html_7375dfcfbc7f9cac2037fd05008c7ce5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Yewdale, Skelmersdale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater had entered or was about to enter premises; fire crews pumped out affected properties. A council surveyor visited flooded properties across Skelmersdale the following day and drying out with dehumidifiers began. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Yewdale, Skelmersdale",England,Floodwater had entered or was about to enter premises; fire crews pumped out affected properties. A council surveyor visited flooded properties across Skelmersdale the following day and drying out with dehumidifiers began. (p13),flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) (p13),GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16.html,GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16,Lancashire flooding 16 Jun 2016,16 June 2016 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-16-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,14,2016-06-16,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_1a4bc92692cceacebb87f3e05d01735c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred across parts of Lancashire during the event. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 16 June 2016 a heavy downpour caused surface water and urban flooding in parts of western Lancashire, inundating homes and roads as local drainage networks were overwhelmed. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The county experienced flooding on 16 June 2016. This report provides a commentary on those flooding events based on reports made to the Lead Local Flood Authority and by Risk Management Authorities and local representatives. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 16 June 2016 intense rainfall overwhelmed natural and man&ndash;made drainage networks across western Lancashire. Particularly damaging flash flooding occurred across a large portion of West Lancashire district, causing flooding of homes and of the public highway network. [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 16 June 2016 extreme rainfall overwhelmed natural and man&ndash;made drainage networks across parts of the county, producing flash and surface&ndash;water/urban flooding. Impacts described include traffic driving through standing water creating bow waves that washed onto private property, vehicles abandoned in flooded roads impeding access for emergency vehicles, and water ingress at low&ndash;lying properties. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 60 residential properties (in Skelmersdale) [PAG] (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Flooding occurred across parts of Lancashire during the event. (p1)
On 16 June 2016 a heavy downpour caused surface water and urban flooding in parts of western Lancashire, inundating homes and roads as local drainage networks were overwhelmed. [PAG] (p3)
The county experienced flooding on 16 June 2016. This report provides a commentary on those flooding events based on reports made to the Lead Local Flood Authority and by Risk Management Authorities and local representatives. (p10)
On 16 June 2016 intense rainfall overwhelmed natural and man–made drainage networks across western Lancashire. Particularly damaging flash flooding occurred across a large portion of West Lancashire district, causing flooding of homes and of the public highway network. [PAG] (p15)
On 16 June 2016 extreme rainfall overwhelmed natural and man–made drainage networks across parts of the county, producing flash and surface–water/urban flooding. Impacts described include traffic driving through standing water creating bow waves that washed onto private property, vehicles abandoned in flooded roads impeding access for emergency vehicles, and water ingress at low–lying properties. [PAG] (p16)",over 60 residential properties (in Skelmersdale) [PAG] (p3),GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16.html,GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16,Lancashire flooding 16 Jun 2016,16 June 2016 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-16-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,14,2016-06-16,53.6109397,-2.8565713,"<div id=""html_bb4b990ecc0dc196140691a37dcce227"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 16 June 2016 intense rainfall in West Lancashire overwhelmed drainage networks, causing widespread surface water flooding of homes and roads; Skelmersdale (within the district) was especially badly affected. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Prolonged heavy rain and flash flooding across western Lancashire impacted the district: a total of 159 properties were flooded internally and/or externally; roads were closed in places. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as the area significantly affected during the event; residents reported properties flooded (water ingress up to 100mm) in Upholland and Skelmersdale; West Lancashire properties were visited and drying works began the following day. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Particularly damaging flash flooding on 16 June 2016 affected a large portion of West Lancashire district: intense rainfall overwhelmed drainage, causing standing water on roads, abandoned vehicles that impeded emergency access, and water ingress at low&ndash;lying properties. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 60 residential properties (Skelmersdale) (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>159 properties [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>properties flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) in Upholland and Skelmersdale (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,West Lancashire,England,"On 16 June 2016 intense rainfall in West Lancashire overwhelmed drainage networks, causing widespread surface water flooding of homes and roads; Skelmersdale (within the district) was especially badly affected. (p3)
Prolonged heavy rain and flash flooding across western Lancashire impacted the district: a total of 159 properties were flooded internally and/or externally; roads were closed in places. [PAG] (p12)
Identified as the area significantly affected during the event; residents reported properties flooded (water ingress up to 100mm) in Upholland and Skelmersdale; West Lancashire properties were visited and drying works began the following day. (p13)
Particularly damaging flash flooding on 16 June 2016 affected a large portion of West Lancashire district: intense rainfall overwhelmed drainage, causing standing water on roads, abandoned vehicles that impeded emergency access, and water ingress at low–lying properties. (p16)","over 60 residential properties (Skelmersdale) (p3)
159 properties [PAG] (p12)
properties flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) in Upholland and Skelmersdale (p13)",GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16.html,GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16,Lancashire flooding 16 Jun 2016,16 June 2016 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-16-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,14,2016-06-16,53.7271527,-2.7330066,"<div id=""html_b16dfba55ed2e8d94204385119e960df"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Ribble</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Manholes became overwhelmed during the event, spilling sewage onto roads and driveways in the South Ribble area on 16 June 2016. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,South Ribble,England,"Manholes became overwhelmed during the event, spilling sewage onto roads and driveways in the South Ribble area on 16 June 2016. (p12)",,GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16.html,GB-LAN_14_2016-06-16,Lancashire flooding 16 Jun 2016,16 June 2016 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-16-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,14,2016-06-16,53.5504323,-2.8097184,"<div id=""html_51501583c6d7a8bba0337bd64dd93086"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Skelmersdale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 16 June 2016 intense, rapid rainfall overwhelmed natural and constructed drainage networks in Skelmersdale, resulting in widespread surface water flooding that entered homes and inundated roads. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Particularly severely affected by the downpour on 16 June 2016: over 60 homes estimated flooded; several roads closed; residents reported flood depths up to 100 mm (4 inches); emergency services received over 70 calls relating to around 30 incidents and Lancashire Fire and Rescue Service responded from 1600hrs. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties flooded with up to 100mm of water reported by residents; fire crews pumped out floodwater that had entered or was about to enter properties; council surveyor visits and drying with dehumidifiers began the day after the flood. [PAG] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 60 residential properties (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 60 homes; over 70 calls; around 30 incidents; 100 mm (4 inches) (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>properties flooded up to 100mm (4 inches) in Upholland and Skelmersdale [PAG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Skelmersdale,England,"On 16 June 2016 intense, rapid rainfall overwhelmed natural and constructed drainage networks in Skelmersdale, resulting in widespread surface water flooding that entered homes and inundated roads. (p3)
Particularly severely affected by the downpour on 16 June 2016: over 60 homes estimated flooded; several roads closed; residents reported flood depths up to 100 mm (4 inches); emergency services received over 70 calls relating to around 30 incidents and Lancashire Fire and Rescue Service responded from 1600hrs. (p12)
Properties flooded with up to 100mm of water reported by residents; fire crews pumped out floodwater that had entered or was about to enter properties; council surveyor visits and drying with dehumidifiers began the day after the flood. [PAG] (p13)","over 60 residential properties (p3)
