GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6787832,-0.4332332,"<div id=""html_b32925531e5a81d53d57206975bbcbdb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Caistor Road, Barrow-Upon-Humber</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flow flooded a property adjacent to Caistor Road. [MUL] (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [MUL] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Caistor Road, Barrow-Upon-Humber",England,Overland flow flooded a property adjacent to Caistor Road. [MUL] (p9),1 property [MUL] (p9),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6836932,-0.441577,"<div id=""html_d9186f7726d87835c2862f6800fe7589"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Holydyke, Barton-Upon-Humber</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in Holydyke was caused by a blocked Anglian Water combined sewer serving the Bowmandale area; Anglian Water attended site to clear blockages. The issue reoccurred in February 2020. [MUL] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Holydyke, Barton-Upon-Humber",England,Flooding in Holydyke was caused by a blocked Anglian Water combined sewer serving the Bowmandale area; Anglian Water attended site to clear blockages. The issue reoccurred in February 2020. [MUL] (p10),,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6773661,-0.4439123,"<div id=""html_6cf086cf78f7cd6b968b34c2a453a926"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bowmandale, Barton-Upon-Humber</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Combined sewer issues serving the Bowmandale area led to flooding; Anglian Water attended to clear blockages. The problem has been reported multiple times over several years and reoccurred in February 2020. [MUL] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Bowmandale, Barton-Upon-Humber",England,Combined sewer issues serving the Bowmandale area led to flooding; Anglian Water attended to clear blockages. The problem has been reported multiple times over several years and reoccurred in February 2020. [MUL] (p10),,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5629219,-0.81603,"<div id=""html_4d3b4ca73fbbee0f0d3832a7a8de81f3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Woodhouse Lane, Belton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Woodhouse Lane was flooded on 15 Nov 2019 due to excess overland flow from the highway; highway drainage and downstream IDB dyke capacity were implicated and investigations/works were initiated. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Woodhouse Lane, Belton",England,Woodhouse Lane was flooded on 15 Nov 2019 due to excess overland flow from the highway; highway drainage and downstream IDB dyke capacity were implicated and investigations/works were initiated. (p10),,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5729944,-0.7370646,"<div id=""html_8fd7f6b029d0f28248a5925d6198434f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Meadows, Burringham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Excess overland runoff from the Burringham area overwhelmed the Burringham pumping station (inflow greatly exceeding capacity) and a blocked/full riparian outfall ditch prevented drainage away from properties on The Meadows; the foul&ndash;water system was also implicated due to known hydraulic problems and surface&ndash;water connections into the foul sewer. LLFA level, jet and CCTV surveys found only minor faults; STW carried out a connectivity survey. Ongoing liaison and investigations with STW and the IDB to consider improvements. [MUL] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Meadows, Burringham",England,"Excess overland runoff from the Burringham area overwhelmed the Burringham pumping station (inflow greatly exceeding capacity) and a blocked/full riparian outfall ditch prevented drainage away from properties on The Meadows; the foul–water system was also implicated due to known hydraulic problems and surface–water connections into the foul sewer. LLFA level, jet and CCTV surveys found only minor faults; STW carried out a connectivity survey. Ongoing liaison and investigations with STW and the IDB to consider improvements. [MUL] (p11)",,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5987279,-0.8434872,"<div id=""html_e5c3a6ae4491e752bc176c73a757a5d2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Godnow Road, Crowle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding of properties caused by excess foul/sewer water from known hydraulic issues in the foul system; highway runoff may have exacerbated the event. Investigations and potential upgrades being scoped by Severn Trent Water; IDB and WLMB investigations on nearby drains are planned. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>three properties [PAG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Godnow Road, Crowle",England,Flooding of properties caused by excess foul/sewer water from known hydraulic issues in the foul system; highway runoff may have exacerbated the event. Investigations and potential upgrades being scoped by Severn Trent Water; IDB and WLMB investigations on nearby drains are planned. [PAG] (p11),three properties [PAG] (p11),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6168692,-0.8515801,"<div id=""html_7e64adbeb0a214b463e25af09c5ba9ce"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Dole Road, Crowle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property flooding attributed to poor riparian management that prevented water entering the downstream riparian ditch, resulting in water entering properties. (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Dole Road, Crowle",England,"Property flooding attributed to poor riparian management that prevented water entering the downstream riparian ditch, resulting in water entering properties. (p11)",one property (p11),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6100902,-0.8503039,"<div id=""html_5a5033eeea0905f23de1d00593c0e20a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Middle Common Road, Crowle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property flooding attributed to poor riparian management preventing drainage into downstream ditches. (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Middle Common Road, Crowle",England,Property flooding attributed to poor riparian management preventing drainage into downstream ditches. (p11),one property (p11),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.617738,-0.8179568,"<div id=""html_3b2d00bf57924b65ee3367b8b6d99e89"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Crowle Road, Crowle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding at one property on Crowle Road (Eastoft) on 12 November 2019 caused by excess surface water; Severn Trent Water found the surface water outfall partially blocked by silt and debris, cleansed the surface water system and completed CCTV; outfall remains partially restricted due to ditch level (being addressed by Isle of Axholme and North Nottinghamshire WLMB); LLFA issued riparian ownership letters to adjacent landowners. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Crowle Road, Crowle",England,"Flooding at one property on Crowle Road (Eastoft) on 12 November 2019 caused by excess surface water; Severn Trent Water found the surface water outfall partially blocked by silt and debris, cleansed the surface water system and completed CCTV; outfall remains partially restricted due to ditch level (being addressed by Isle of Axholme and North Nottinghamshire WLMB); LLFA issued riparian ownership letters to adjacent landowners. (p12)",one property (p12),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5397974,-0.848021,"<div id=""html_fdd1b42c4730fdcbd2471590c5fd7b6a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West End Road, Epworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The surface water sewer and the foul pump station overflow/outfall serving approximately a 500m length of West End Road (and Station Road) was partially blocked and the foul system was inundated by surface water, resulting in sewer flooding that affected properties on West End Road. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"West End Road, Epworth",England,"The surface water sewer and the foul pump station overflow/outfall serving approximately a 500m length of West End Road (and Station Road) was partially blocked and the foul system was inundated by surface water, resulting in sewer flooding that affected properties on West End Road. (p12)",2 properties (p12),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6227451,-0.6958513,"<div id=""html_e3d097a1229a79a7d5b72632d48fd3ce"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ninth Avenue, Flixborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A commercial property on Ninth Avenue was flooded on 8 Nov 2019 due to excess overland flow from the east which overwhelmed local drainage and the pumping station system. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial property (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Ninth Avenue, Flixborough",England,A commercial property on Ninth Avenue was flooded on 8 Nov 2019 due to excess overland flow from the east which overwhelmed local drainage and the pumping station system. (p13),1 commercial property (p13),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
