GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.488845,-0.8819334,"<div id=""html_1c62bb066eefd2380db19e647ae29d64"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Westmoreland Close, Westwoodside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Three properties experienced flooding caused by foul sewer surcharge from STW's foul water system, which was overwhelmed due to surface water inundation. (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected Westmoreland Close; LLFA attempted to jet the surface water system but blocked ditches to the west prevented clearing, contributing to the flooding issues. (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Westmoreland Close, Westwoodside",England,"Three properties experienced flooding caused by foul sewer surcharge from STW's foul water system, which was overwhelmed due to surface water inundation. (p20)
Flooding affected Westmoreland Close; LLFA attempted to jet the surface water system but blocked ditches to the west prevented clearing, contributing to the flooding issues. (p21)",3 properties (p20),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.487572,-0.8750021,"<div id=""html_d78c4c254c3bcd57aaa7b7d4f4b8f272"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Doncaster Road, Westwoodside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Pumping station on Doncaster Road was full for longer than designed during the November 2019 events; pump efficiency dropped but the station did not fail. (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Doncaster Road, Westwoodside",England,Pumping station on Doncaster Road was full for longer than designed during the November 2019 events; pump efficiency dropped but the station did not fail. (p20),,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.4896244,-0.8712021,"<div id=""html_78bbb40c054664a33d897c7f0370de59"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Birches, Westwoodside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Excess overland flow travelled from the east of the property and caused flooding at The Birches. (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"The Birches, Westwoodside",England,Excess overland flow travelled from the east of the property and caused flooding at The Birches. (p21),,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6781124,-0.5902329,"<div id=""html_aff2dc1b2e49abec8e3b7e31a3b516a5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Winterton Road, Winteringham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding from excess overland flow on 13 November 2019 affected the vicinity of Winterton Road. Flooding was driven by overland flow from the west and exacerbated by poorly maintained riparian ditches and a culvert adjacent to the road. LLFA actions included sending riparian ownership letters, jetting the culverts adjacent to Winterton Road and refreshing verge drainage grips; the landowner also dug a rough ditch and bund on the west side of Winterton Road. (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,"Winterton Road, Winteringham",England,"Surface water flooding from excess overland flow on 13 November 2019 affected the vicinity of Winterton Road. Flooding was driven by overland flow from the west and exacerbated by poorly maintained riparian ditches and a culvert adjacent to the road. LLFA actions included sending riparian ownership letters, jetting the culverts adjacent to Winterton Road and refreshing verge drainage grips; the landowner also dug a rough ditch and bund on the west side of Winterton Road. (p21)",4 properties (p21),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5897441,-0.602323,"<div id=""html_db87840bcc9d098491a61dfd59678215"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Lincolnshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial, surface water, groundwater and sewer flooding caused internal and external flooding of residential and commercial properties; local highway and transport networks experienced disturbances due to elevated water levels. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall (notably the torrential downpour on 7 November 2019, with further rain on 9&ndash;10 November 2019) caused intense surface water runoff; overwhelmed adopted and private sewerage and highway drainage systems; raised the groundwater table and triggered springs; filled open watercourses so urban drainage could not discharge; and raised main river levels leading to overtopping in some areas. Reports of groundwater emergence and related issues were mainly received from Barton, Barrow, Kirton, Elsham and surrounding low&ndash;lying villages. [PAG,MUL] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall on 7 November 2019 and continued rain caused widespread surface water runoff, overwhelmed sewerage and highway drainage (adopted and private), raised the groundwater table and filled open watercourses so urban drainage could not discharge; main river levels rose leading to overtopping in some areas. The council received reports and followed up with affected residents and RMAs. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurrences were recorded in the town during the report event. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following flood events in November 2019 affecting the area, the council indicated the LFRMS priority settlement list should be reviewed. The LFRMS identifies specific settlements within North Lincolnshire with estimated numbers of people and critical assets at local flood risk (local sources such as surface water, groundwater and ordinary watercourses). [PAG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The unitary authority coordinated emergency response to the November 2019 floods: a flood incident emergency room was established to organise and coordinate operations; North Lincolnshire Council staff, drainage improvement teams and neighbourhood services provided emergency flooding support; information was issued to the public and recovery activity followed the event. [PAG] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant rainfall in November 2019 caused district&ndash;wide flooding: 54 properties reported internal flooding (including damage to homes) and 3 commercial/industrial businesses reported internal flooding; local highways experienced extensive flooding leading to multiple road closures and traffic disruption across the district. [PAG] (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than 300 reports of flooding; 54 properties internally flooded; 3 commercial/industrial businesses internally flooded (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Approximately 100 members of Highways and Neighbourhood Services directly responded to the flooding incidents. [PAG] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>54 properties; 3 commercial/industrial businesses [PAG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,North Lincolnshire,England,"Fluvial, surface water, groundwater and sewer flooding caused internal and external flooding of residential and commercial properties; local highway and transport networks experienced disturbances due to elevated water levels. (p5)
Heavy rainfall (notably the torrential downpour on 7 November 2019, with further rain on 9–10 November 2019) caused intense surface water runoff; overwhelmed adopted and private sewerage and highway drainage systems; raised the groundwater table and triggered springs; filled open watercourses so urban drainage could not discharge; and raised main river levels leading to overtopping in some areas. Reports of groundwater emergence and related issues were mainly received from Barton, Barrow, Kirton, Elsham and surrounding low–lying villages. [PAG,MUL] (p6)
Heavy rainfall on 7 November 2019 and continued rain caused widespread surface water runoff, overwhelmed sewerage and highway drainage (adopted and private), raised the groundwater table and filled open watercourses so urban drainage could not discharge; main river levels rose leading to overtopping in some areas. The council received reports and followed up with affected residents and RMAs. (p7)
Flooding occurrences were recorded in the town during the report event. [IMG] (p8)
Following flood events in November 2019 affecting the area, the council indicated the LFRMS priority settlement list should be reviewed. The LFRMS identifies specific settlements within North Lincolnshire with estimated numbers of people and critical assets at local flood risk (local sources such as surface water, groundwater and ordinary watercourses). [PAG] (p25)
The unitary authority coordinated emergency response to the November 2019 floods: a flood incident emergency room was established to organise and coordinate operations; North Lincolnshire Council staff, drainage improvement teams and neighbourhood services provided emergency flooding support; information was issued to the public and recovery activity followed the event. [PAG] (p27)
Significant rainfall in November 2019 caused district–wide flooding: 54 properties reported internal flooding (including damage to homes) and 3 commercial/industrial businesses reported internal flooding; local highways experienced extensive flooding leading to multiple road closures and traffic disruption across the district. [PAG] (p30)","more than 300 reports of flooding; 54 properties internally flooded; 3 commercial/industrial businesses internally flooded (p7)
Approximately 100 members of Highways and Neighbourhood Services directly responded to the flooding incidents. [PAG] (p27)
54 properties; 3 commercial/industrial businesses [PAG] (p30)",GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.685651729489095,-0.4445463678739146,"<div id=""html_f5d408a43fbaa0f2deed462525140dfe"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Barton-Upon-Humber</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Torrential rainfall and very high groundwater resulted in springs being triggered in the Barton area; surface water runoff and overwhelmed drainage/sewer systems led to reported flooding incidents that contributed to internal property flooding across the district. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland surface water flow flooded two properties to the south of Barton Upon Humber adjacent to Brigg Road and Caistor Road. [MUL] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties and streets in Barton were affected by flooding during the November 2019 event: a property adjacent to Brigg Road flooded and recurring combined sewer issues affected the Holydyke/Bowmandale area; the LLFA carried out investigations and follow&ndash;up actions. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a priority settlement presenting the greatest local flood risk and targeted for a Flood Alleviation Scheme; received FDGiA&ndash;funded Outline Business Case development in response to the November 2019 floods to plan measures to reduce future flood impacts. (p27)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties [MUL] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Barton-Upon-Humber,England,"Torrential rainfall and very high groundwater resulted in springs being triggered in the Barton area; surface water runoff and overwhelmed drainage/sewer systems led to reported flooding incidents that contributed to internal property flooding across the district. (p7)
Overland surface water flow flooded two properties to the south of Barton Upon Humber adjacent to Brigg Road and Caistor Road. [MUL] (p9)
Properties and streets in Barton were affected by flooding during the November 2019 event: a property adjacent to Brigg Road flooded and recurring combined sewer issues affected the Holydyke/Bowmandale area; the LLFA carried out investigations and follow–up actions. (p10)
Identified as a priority settlement presenting the greatest local flood risk and targeted for a Flood Alleviation Scheme; received FDGiA–funded Outline Business Case development in response to the November 2019 floods to plan measures to reduce future flood impacts. (p27)",2 properties [MUL] (p9),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6732961,-0.380954,"<div id=""html_fefb776d9c6484ea63d07f0d06639409"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Barrow-Upon-Humber</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High groundwater (springs) and intense surface water runoff overwhelmed local drainage and sewers in the Barrow area, generating reported flooding incidents during the November 2019 rainfall. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two properties on Town Street experienced external flooding when foul manholes became full and overflowed during excess rainfall; Anglian Water inspected manholes and completed sewage debris clean&ndash;up at both properties. (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two properties (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Barrow-Upon-Humber,England,"High groundwater (springs) and intense surface water runoff overwhelmed local drainage and sewers in the Barrow area, generating reported flooding incidents during the November 2019 rainfall. (p7)
Two properties on Town Street experienced external flooding when foul manholes became full and overflowed during excess rainfall; Anglian Water inspected manholes and completed sewage debris clean–up at both properties. (p9)",two properties (p9),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.4763818,-0.58913,"<div id=""html_2390caee5872a7bb3ff5a3ba280227fb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kirton In Lindsey</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reports from the Kirton area describe very high groundwater with springs activating and surface water runoff overwhelming drainage, contributing to local flooding reports during November 2019. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Kirton in Lindsey experienced surface water flooding at Station Road where a commercial property was inundated; LLFA investigation found and removed a culvert blockage. (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>54 properties (district&ndash;wide internal flooding; includes 3 commercial/industrial) (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial property (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Kirton In Lindsey,England,"Reports from the Kirton area describe very high groundwater with springs activating and surface water runoff overwhelming drainage, contributing to local flooding reports during November 2019. (p7)
Kirton in Lindsey experienced surface water flooding at Station Road where a commercial property was inundated; LLFA investigation found and removed a culvert blockage. (p15)","54 properties (district–wide internal flooding; includes 3 commercial/industrial) (p7)
1 commercial property (p15)",GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.59760634258772,-0.43867104167814186,"<div id=""html_3129a3654549ab20baef0a4235ef50c9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Elsham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Elsham was reported among areas where very high groundwater led to springs and where intense surface water runoff and overwhelmed drainage contributed to flooding incidents during the November 2019 storms. (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Elsham,England,Elsham was reported among areas where very high groundwater led to springs and where intense surface water runoff and overwhelmed drainage contributed to flooding incidents during the November 2019 storms. (p7),,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6393166,-0.7450246,"<div id=""html_050e6a7820714304e1ae463e840ce164"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Luddington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified by North Lincolnshire Council as one of the areas predominantly affected by the November 2019 heavy rainfall. Flooding mechanisms reported across the district that affected the area included intense surface water runoff, overwhelmed sewer and highway drainage, raised groundwater and activation of springs, and elevated river levels causing overtopping; properties in the area suffered internal flooding. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The village of Luddington experienced property flooding on Meredyke Road (two properties). LLFA and STW investigations identified pump failure/overwhelmed pumping station and contributing overland flow; ongoing monitoring and liaison are reported. (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>54 properties (district&ndash;wide internal flooding; includes 3 commercial/industrial) (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Luddington,England,"Identified by North Lincolnshire Council as one of the areas predominantly affected by the November 2019 heavy rainfall. Flooding mechanisms reported across the district that affected the area included intense surface water runoff, overwhelmed sewer and highway drainage, raised groundwater and activation of springs, and elevated river levels causing overtopping; properties in the area suffered internal flooding. (p7)
The village of Luddington experienced property flooding on Meredyke Road (two properties). LLFA and STW investigations identified pump failure/overwhelmed pumping station and contributing overland flow; ongoing monitoring and liaison are reported. (p15)","54 properties (district–wide internal flooding; includes 3 commercial/industrial) (p7)
2 properties (p15)",GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.64044961313053,-0.2793657339820251,"<div id=""html_d254f09549d42361369185731ce9e51f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Killingholme</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified by North Lincolnshire Council as one of the areas predominantly affected by the November 2019 heavy rainfall. Flooding in the area resulted from surface water runoff, overwhelmed drainage and sewers, raised groundwater/springs and raised river levels leading to overtopping; properties in the area experienced internal flooding. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding at one property on Church Lane. Anglian Water attended; manhole to rear of property was found clear but pump station was suspected to be operating inefficiently due to excessive inflow. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A property experienced flooding in November 2019; AW repair team investigated and found the rear manhole clear and suspected the local pump station was operating inefficiently due to excessive inflow, contributing to the flooding. (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>54 properties (district&ndash;wide internal flooding; includes 3 commercial/industrial) (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,North Killingholme,England,"Identified by North Lincolnshire Council as one of the areas predominantly affected by the November 2019 heavy rainfall. Flooding in the area resulted from surface water runoff, overwhelmed drainage and sewers, raised groundwater/springs and raised river levels leading to overtopping; properties in the area experienced internal flooding. (p7)
Internal flooding at one property on Church Lane. Anglian Water attended; manhole to rear of property was found clear but pump station was suspected to be operating inefficiently due to excessive inflow. (p16)
