GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5922488,-0.6450841,"<div id=""html_a770eca1f30b79622a7004484df373ab"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Scunthorpe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed by the council as among the areas predominantly affected by the November 2019 heavy rainfall. District&ndash;wide impacts that affected Scunthorpe included intense surface water runoff and overwhelmed sewer/highway drainage; groundwater remained high contributing to local flooding and some properties suffered internal flooding. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two properties in Scunthorpe were flooded during the event (one at Rochester Close due to an overwhelmed surface water system; one at Brumby Hall Gardens due to elevated groundwater), reported on 7 and 8 November 2019. (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A specific location in Scunthorpe (Rochester Close area) experienced a flooding incident; the LLFA is liaising with the water company and advised affected residents at Brumby Hall Gardens to contact insurers. The report notes no previous reports of flooding at that specific location. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>54 properties (district&ndash;wide internal flooding; includes 3 commercial/industrial) (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (1 Rochester Close; 1 Brumby Hall Gardens) (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Scunthorpe,England,"Listed by the council as among the areas predominantly affected by the November 2019 heavy rainfall. District–wide impacts that affected Scunthorpe included intense surface water runoff and overwhelmed sewer/highway drainage; groundwater remained high contributing to local flooding and some properties suffered internal flooding. (p7)
