GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6078121,-0.832644,"<div id=""html_4dbfc065e20395a0956823be609ab925"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Crowle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as an area affected during the November 2019 event; suffered internal flooding of properties with local drainage overwhelmed and high groundwater contributing to runoff and discharge issues. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected five properties between 11 and 14 November 2019: three properties on Godnow Road flooded due to excess foul water (properties on the Hydraulic Sewer Flooding Risk Register), and one property on Dole Road plus one property near Middle Common Road flooded due to poor riparian management preventing drainage into downstream ditches. LLFA, IDB (Isle of Axholme and North Nottinghamshire WLMB) and STW investigations were initiated; a partnership highway and drainage improvement scheme for Godnow Road is in design. (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Part of 54 properties that suffered internal flooding across North Lincolnshire (including 3 commercial/industrial businesses). (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>three properties on Godnow Road; one property on Dole Road; one property near Middle Common Road; five properties total (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Crowle,England,"Identified as an area affected during the November 2019 event; suffered internal flooding of properties with local drainage overwhelmed and high groundwater contributing to runoff and discharge issues. (p7)
