GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6355292,-0.7845935,"<div id=""html_97194502974b672ca92561025c50fd9b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Eastoft</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded among the areas affected by the November 2019 heavy rainfall; experienced internal flooding to properties, overwhelmed drainage and raised groundwater/springs. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Excess surface water led to flooding at a property on Crowle Road; blockage/silt in the STW surface water outfall and lack of downstream channel maintenance restricted flow. STW cleansed the surface water system and CCTV&ndash;inspected it; riparian ownership letters were sent to adjacent landowners; ditch level remediation is being progressed by drainage authorities. [MUL] (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Part of 54 properties that suffered internal flooding across North Lincolnshire (including 3 commercial/industrial businesses). (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property [MUL] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Eastoft,England,"Recorded among the areas affected by the November 2019 heavy rainfall; experienced internal flooding to properties, overwhelmed drainage and raised groundwater/springs. (p7)
