GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.524303,-0.8215111,"<div id=""html_ad2db61e7b9a05c767100e972bdf7ac5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Epworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Named as one of the areas predominantly affected in November 2019; properties suffered internal flooding and local drainage systems were overwhelmed due to intense rainfall and high groundwater. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two properties on West End Road were flooded on 14 Nov 2019 after the STW foul system became inundated by excess surface water; the outfall/consented overflow ditch serving the surface water sewer and CSO was partially blocked due to lack of maintenance. LLFA issued riparian ownership letters to adjacent landowners. [MUL] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>LLFA response actions included sending riparian ownership letters to adjacent landowners to ensure land drainage features were properly maintained; ongoing progress to be monitored through the Strategic Flood Board and operational Risk Management Authority Group meetings. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Part of 54 properties that suffered internal flooding across North Lincolnshire (including 3 commercial/industrial businesses). (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two properties [MUL] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Epworth,England,"Named as one of the areas predominantly affected in November 2019; properties suffered internal flooding and local drainage systems were overwhelmed due to intense rainfall and high groundwater. (p7)
