LLFA response actions included sending riparian ownership letters to adjacent landowners to ensure land drainage features were properly maintained; ongoing progress to be monitored through the Strategic Flood Board and operational Risk Management Authority Group meetings. (p13)","Part of 54 properties that suffered internal flooding across North Lincolnshire (including 3 commercial/industrial businesses). (p7)
two properties [MUL] (p12)",GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6248597,-0.6822297,"<div id=""html_f4845591c252d2e7217f8447acfbbc58"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Flixborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Local flooding caused by the November 2019 heavy rainfall: rapid surface water runoff onto saturated ground, overwhelmed sewer and highway drainage, very high groundwater/setting off springs, and raised watercourse/main river levels leading to overtopping and local inundation. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from the Flixborough area flowed into Flixborough Pumping Station and, during November 2019, inflow was almost ten times greater than the station's capacity, contributing to flooding at a commercial property; LLFA investigated local riparian drainage (Wood Bottom), removed a blocked culvert and scheduled regular inspections. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 pumping station; 1 commercial property; 1 culvert (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Flixborough,England,"Local flooding caused by the November 2019 heavy rainfall: rapid surface water runoff onto saturated ground, overwhelmed sewer and highway drainage, very high groundwater/setting off springs, and raised watercourse/main river levels leading to overtopping and local inundation. (p7)
Runoff from the Flixborough area flowed into Flixborough Pumping Station and, during November 2019, inflow was almost ten times greater than the station's capacity, contributing to flooding at a commercial property; LLFA investigated local riparian drainage (Wood Bottom), removed a blocked culvert and scheduled regular inspections. (p13)",1 pumping station; 1 commercial property; 1 culvert (p13),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5741816,-0.7381881,"<div id=""html_06f711d714638eaaf3b7d1239f863b6a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Burringham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from excess overland flow affected properties on The Meadows; runoff flowed into the Burringham Pumping Station which experienced inflow far beyond capacity, and the riparian outfall ditch was full/blocked preventing drainage. Severn Trent Water suggested foul sewer hydraulic problems contributed. LLFA carried out level, jet and CCTV surveys and STW completed a connectivity survey; discussions with STW and the IDB on solutions are ongoing. [MUL] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two properties; inflow almost 10x greater than the capacity of the station [MUL] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Burringham,England,"Flooding from excess overland flow affected properties on The Meadows; runoff flowed into the Burringham Pumping Station which experienced inflow far beyond capacity, and the riparian outfall ditch was full/blocked preventing drainage. Severn Trent Water suggested foul sewer hydraulic problems contributed. LLFA carried out level, jet and CCTV surveys and STW completed a connectivity survey; discussions with STW and the IDB on solutions are ongoing. [MUL] (p10)",two properties; inflow almost 10x greater than the capacity of the station [MUL] (p10),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6766712,-0.3374071,"<div id=""html_2f8901e26388fa804d84800f59a44f58"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Goxhill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property in Goxhill (on Ruards Lane) experienced internal flooding on 15 November 2019 due to a failed surface water culvert under the lane, with blocked dykes and poorly maintained riparian ditches downstream exacerbating the flooding; LLFA repair works and riparian letters were planned. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a priority settlement presenting the greatest local flood risk and targeted for a Flood Alleviation Scheme; received FDGiA&ndash;funded Outline Business Case development in response to the November 2019 floods to plan measures to reduce future flood impacts. (p27)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Goxhill,England,"One property in Goxhill (on Ruards Lane) experienced internal flooding on 15 November 2019 due to a failed surface water culvert under the lane, with blocked dykes and poorly maintained riparian ditches downstream exacerbating the flooding; LLFA repair works and riparian letters were planned. (p13)
Identified as a priority settlement presenting the greatest local flood risk and targeted for a Flood Alleviation Scheme; received FDGiA–funded Outline Business Case development in response to the November 2019 floods to plan measures to reduce future flood impacts. (p27)",one property (p13),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5105797,-0.5253879,"<div id=""html_aee6aa34403d9fc751930751cf7ed387"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hibaldstow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to a property (on Station Road) within Hibaldstow attributable to excess overland flow and low&ndash;lying ground leading to surface runoff. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Hibaldstow,England,Internal flooding to a property (on Station Road) within Hibaldstow attributable to excess overland flow and low–lying ground leading to surface runoff. (p14),1 property (p14),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
