GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6398884,-0.6676919,"<div id=""html_0f2edbf2bf833f5da4fe3cd27e9be226"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Normanby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding at one property occurred when excess overland flow from the adjacent highway entered the property. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Normanby,England,Internal flooding at one property occurred when excess overland flow from the adjacent highway entered the property. (p16),1 property (p16),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.4873185,-0.5357835,"<div id=""html_a1841d1794e799d283562e96d47e6400"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Redbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Village&ndash;wide impact on 7 November 2019 when the River Beck overflowed following excessive rainfall, flooding five properties (three on Beck Lane, one on School Lane, one on Park Lane). Debris at the B1206 culvert trash screen exacerbated flooding; LLFA commissioned hydraulic modelling, investigated mitigation (replace trash screen, upstream storage, downstream overflow channel) and found a crack in the High Street culvert to be remedied. (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>five properties (three on Beck Lane; one on School Lane; one on Park Lane) (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Redbourne,England,"Village–wide impact on 7 November 2019 when the River Beck overflowed following excessive rainfall, flooding five properties (three on Beck Lane, one on School Lane, one on Park Lane). Debris at the B1206 culvert trash screen exacerbated flooding; LLFA commissioned hydraulic modelling, investigated mitigation (replace trash screen, upstream storage, downstream overflow channel) and found a crack in the High Street culvert to be remedied. (p17)",five properties (three on Beck Lane; one on School Lane; one on Park Lane) (p17),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.676031248784106,-0.5066510591172384,"<div id=""html_e15e7f6936e4c5ce7a2e8f1339f67cae"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Ferriby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported at one property in South Ferriby caused by excess surface water run&ndash;off due to a blocked highways gully. The LLFA completed jetting and CCTV investigations, repaired a surface water pipe near 'The Rise', installed an additional gully and ACO drainage system, and gas repairs were undertaken where a gas service had been located in a surface water sewer upstream. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,South Ferriby,England,"Flooding was reported at one property in South Ferriby caused by excess surface water run–off due to a blocked highways gully. The LLFA completed jetting and CCTV investigations, repaired a surface water pipe near 'The Rise', installed an additional gully and ACO drainage system, and gas repairs were undertaken where a gas service had been located in a surface water sewer upstream. (p18)",1 property (p18),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6300423,-0.2642896,"<div id=""html_4e695d1484a40ad7d2f6c8a672fbd11a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Killingholme</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding at two properties on Town Street caused by issues with the foul (AWA) sewer system exacerbated by excess surface water runoff from nearby impermeable car parks; investigations by AW identified private pipework issues which were resolved by residents; meeting held with MPs and councillors to discuss drainage improvements. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,South Killingholme,England,Internal flooding at two properties on Town Street caused by issues with the foul (AWA) sewer system exacerbated by excess surface water runoff from nearby impermeable car parks; investigations by AW identified private pipework issues which were resolved by residents; meeting held with MPs and councillors to discuss drainage improvements. (p18),2 properties (p18),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6783095,-0.670984,"<div id=""html_972a4e235b993150bfb0eb27ba59dd7a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Walcot</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property on Burton Stather Road in Walcott (sic) was flooded due to excess overland flow from adjacent land. Riparian owners were contacted to maintain ditches and culverts as a response. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Walcot,England,One property on Burton Stather Road in Walcott (sic) was flooded due to excess overland flow from adjacent land. Riparian owners were contacted to maintain ditches and culverts as a response. (p19),1 property (p19),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5123608,-0.7438959,"<div id=""html_5bcc163091431d0d49fc795badf55d75"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Ewster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property flooded as a result of excess overland flow, suspected to have been exacerbated by highways runoff from the east. (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,South Ewster,England,"Property flooded as a result of excess overland flow, suspected to have been exacerbated by highways runoff from the east. (p20)",1 property (p20),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5428481,-0.7409949,"<div id=""html_cd23615f56ffe9662cd180ac5cd2c6cd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Butterwick</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property on South Ewsters flooded due to excess overland flow suspected to have been exacerbated by highway runoff travelling from the east. (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,West Butterwick,England,One property on South Ewsters flooded due to excess overland flow suspected to have been exacerbated by highway runoff travelling from the east. (p20),1 property (p20),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.4872209,-0.8694043,"<div id=""html_f19f8d41e2b8ed422f357d19b928b25a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Westwoodside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas within Westwoodside (including Westmoreland Close and The Birches) experienced flooding caused by excess overland flow and drainage issues associated with poorly maintained riparian ditches. (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Westwoodside,England,Areas within Westwoodside (including Westmoreland Close and The Birches) experienced flooding caused by excess overland flow and drainage issues associated with poorly maintained riparian ditches. (p21),,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.6878513,-0.590982,"<div id=""html_3b2b4b64a2da947bb8d6c272be3dd119"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Winteringham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding on 13 November 2019 affected four properties in Winteringham (in the vicinity of Mere Farm) due to excess overland flow from the west, influenced by poorly maintained riparian ditches and an adjacent culvert. LLFA response actions included sending riparian ownership letters and clearing/jetting drainage features and highway verge grips to improve surface water capture. (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Winteringham,England,"Flooding on 13 November 2019 affected four properties in Winteringham (in the vicinity of Mere Farm) due to excess overland flow from the west, influenced by poorly maintained riparian ditches and an adjacent culvert. LLFA response actions included sending riparian ownership letters and clearing/jetting drainage features and highway verge grips to improve surface water capture. (p21)",4 properties (p21),GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-NLN,1,2019-11-01,53.5525329,-0.4896411,"<div id=""html_f4a08d7213b8768df15e0b5f90bc6408"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brigg</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a priority settlement presenting the greatest local flood risk and targeted for a Flood Alleviation Scheme; received FDGiA&ndash;funded Outline Business Case development in response to the November 2019 floods to plan measures to reduce future flood impacts. (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Lincolnshire,Brigg,England,Identified as a priority settlement presenting the greatest local flood risk and targeted for a Flood Alleviation Scheme; received FDGiA–funded Outline Business Case development in response to the November 2019 floods to plan measures to reduce future flood impacts. (p27),,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01.html,GB-NLN_1_2019-11-01,North Lincolnshire flooding 01 Nov 2019 - 30 Nov 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Events of November 2019,086/North Lincolnshire/NLC-Section-19-Nov/2019-Floods-a.pdf
GB-CAM,10,2014-02-01,52.2709138,0.192522,"<div id=""html_8e4ff574956157a67893e25bbd40339d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bannold Road, Waterbeach</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred on Bannold Road and the immediate surrounding area (incident location concentrated here as shown on the map). [IMG] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Bannold Road, Waterbeach",England,Flooding occurred on Bannold Road and the immediate surrounding area (incident location concentrated here as shown on the map). [IMG] (p2),,GB-CAM_10_2014-02-01_etc.html,GB-CAM_10_2014-02-01_etc,Waterbeach flooding February 2014 and Waterbeach flooding August 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Waterbeach,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2014/Cambridgeshire County/Flood/Investigation/Report/Waterbeach.pdf
GB-CAM,10,2014-02-01,52.265766,0.1909734,"<div id=""html_bed14464cb90b5069f81c035a62ccfef"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Waterbeach</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Eastern Waterbeach (around Bannold Road) experienced flooding incidents documented in the formal investigation. [IMG] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Waterbeach,England,Eastern Waterbeach (around Bannold Road) experienced flooding incidents documented in the formal investigation. [IMG] (p2),,GB-CAM_10_2014-02-01_etc.html,GB-CAM_10_2014-02-01_etc,Waterbeach flooding February 2014 and Waterbeach flooding August 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Waterbeach,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2014/Cambridgeshire County/Flood/Investigation/Report/Waterbeach.pdf
GB-DER,5,2014-07-19,52.9212617,-1.4761491,"<div id=""html_e971c2423a93f3e0138ad031a7b4929b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Derby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A flood event within the city boundary led to internal flooding of residential properties; the event triggered a formal Section 19 investigation. [PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of the city experienced surface water flooding during the intense localised storm on 19 July 2014, notably the eastern areas (including Spondon) where drainage was overwhelmed and properties were internally flooded. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 residential properties [PAG] (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,Derby,England,"A flood event within the city boundary led to internal flooding of residential properties; the event triggered a formal Section 19 investigation. [PAG] (p4)
Parts of the city experienced surface water flooding during the intense localised storm on 19 July 2014, notably the eastern areas (including Spondon) where drainage was overwhelmed and properties were internally flooded. [PAG] (p12)",7 residential properties [PAG] (p4),GB-DER_5_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_5_2014-07-19,Spondon flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Willowcroft Road, Spondon, 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Willowcroft-Road-Spondon-S19.pdf
GB-DER,5,2014-07-19,52.9150811,-1.407162,"<div id=""html_970e6cc7e4c8d459da5428015ba16733"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Willowcroft Road, Spondon</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense short&ndash;duration rainfall caused surface water flooding on Willowcroft Road resulting in internal flood damage to properties, severe highway flooding and external property flooding. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties occurred on Willowcroft Road during the flood event. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A significant cluster of internal property flooding occurred with multiple residential properties flooded internally on Willowcroft Road, triggering a formal Section 19 investigation. [PAG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Roofs, driveways and highway gullies in the catchment drain to the surface water sewer along Willowcroft Road. Willowcroft Road lies on a natural flow path and conveys collected surface water down the slope towards Nottingham Road, concentrating urban runoff from a large catchment during intense rainfall. [PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ground&ndash;floor living areas of properties on Willowcroft Road were inundated; external property flooding also occurred in the area and in some cases was close to entering ground&ndash;floor living areas. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 19 July 2014 intense, highly localised convective rainfall produced rapid surface runoff that inundated gullies and the public surface water sewer network. Excess runoff flowed downslope along localised routes into lower&ndash;elevation areas and entered properties on Willowcroft Road, causing internal flooding of ground&ndash;floor living areas and significant damage to those areas. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from an intense, localised summer storm overwhelmed the local drainage; rapid runoff down steep local topography affected properties on Willowcroft Road as surface water travelled from highways, roofs and driveways. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents reported floodwater on Willowcroft Road to Derby City Council following the intense, isolated storm; the street experienced surface water flooding during the event. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 residential properties (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 residential properties [PAG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 homes (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Willowcroft Road, Spondon",England,"Intense short–duration rainfall caused surface water flooding on Willowcroft Road resulting in internal flood damage to properties, severe highway flooding and external property flooding. (p3)
Internal flooding of residential properties occurred on Willowcroft Road during the flood event. (p4)
A significant cluster of internal property flooding occurred with multiple residential properties flooded internally on Willowcroft Road, triggering a formal Section 19 investigation. [PAG] (p5)
Roofs, driveways and highway gullies in the catchment drain to the surface water sewer along Willowcroft Road. Willowcroft Road lies on a natural flow path and conveys collected surface water down the slope towards Nottingham Road, concentrating urban runoff from a large catchment during intense rainfall. [PAG] (p6)
Ground–floor living areas of properties on Willowcroft Road were inundated; external property flooding also occurred in the area and in some cases was close to entering ground–floor living areas. (p10)
On 19 July 2014 intense, highly localised convective rainfall produced rapid surface runoff that inundated gullies and the public surface water sewer network. Excess runoff flowed downslope along localised routes into lower–elevation areas and entered properties on Willowcroft Road, causing internal flooding of ground–floor living areas and significant damage to those areas. (p11)
Surface water from an intense, localised summer storm overwhelmed the local drainage; rapid runoff down steep local topography affected properties on Willowcroft Road as surface water travelled from highways, roofs and driveways. (p12)
Residents reported floodwater on Willowcroft Road to Derby City Council following the intense, isolated storm; the street experienced surface water flooding during the event. (p14)","7 properties (p3)
7 residential properties (p4)
7 residential properties [PAG] (p5)
7 homes (p10)
7 properties (p11)",GB-DER_5_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_5_2014-07-19,Spondon flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Willowcroft Road, Spondon, 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Willowcroft-Road-Spondon-S19.pdf
GB-DER,5,2014-07-19,52.911363,-1.3973782,"<div id=""html_8138b7228387489ee621b8f8b62eeccf"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Nottingham Road, Spondon</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from Willowcroft Road enters the public surface water sewer network at/near Nottingham Road and is conveyed towards the River Derwent, discharging approximately 1 km south&ndash;east of the investigation site; Nottingham Road therefore forms part of the downstream pathway for concentrated urban runoff during intense rainfall. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Nottingham Road, Spondon",England,"Surface water from Willowcroft Road enters the public surface water sewer network at/near Nottingham Road and is conveyed towards the River Derwent, discharging approximately 1 km south–east of the investigation site; Nottingham Road therefore forms part of the downstream pathway for concentrated urban runoff during intense rainfall. (p6)",,GB-DER_5_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_5_2014-07-19,Spondon flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Willowcroft Road, Spondon, 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Willowcroft-Road-Spondon-S19.pdf
GB-DER,5,2014-07-19,52.9224633,-1.4005373,"<div id=""html_db8788761fd4ebdddef1b5e6d626b3c5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Moor Street, Spondon</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Moor Street is explicitly identified as part of the large urban catchment whose runoff drains into the surface water sewer system feeding Willowcroft Road and downstream receptors, contributing to concentrated surface water flow and flood risk during intense rainfall (e.g. 19 July 2014). (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Moor Street, Spondon",England,"Moor Street is explicitly identified as part of the large urban catchment whose runoff drains into the surface water sewer system feeding Willowcroft Road and downstream receptors, contributing to concentrated surface water flow and flood risk during intense rainfall (e.g. 19 July 2014). (p6)",,GB-DER_5_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_5_2014-07-19,Spondon flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Willowcroft Road, Spondon, 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Willowcroft-Road-Spondon-S19.pdf
GB-DER,5,2014-07-19,52.9233938,-1.3963915,"<div id=""html_d32a7d65cc835a19fa8dcf791a15385c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Dale Road, Spondon</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Dale Road is cited as the far northern extent of the urban catchment that supplies runoff to the surface water sewer network draining toward Willowcroft Road and the investigation site, contributing to surface water flow and flood risk during intense rainfall (e.g. 19 July 2014). (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Dale Road, Spondon",England,"Dale Road is cited as the far northern extent of the urban catchment that supplies runoff to the surface water sewer network draining toward Willowcroft Road and the investigation site, contributing to surface water flow and flood risk during intense rainfall (e.g. 19 July 2014). (p6)",,GB-DER_5_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_5_2014-07-19,Spondon flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Willowcroft Road, Spondon, 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Willowcroft-Road-Spondon-S19.pdf
GB-DER,5,2014-07-19,52.9205217,-1.4057218,"<div id=""html_eb109a81919615fc5c9f25eddaaec9d2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Spondon</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Other areas of Spondon experienced surface water flooding during the same event, including isolated cases of internal property flooding affecting nearby localities. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A significant cluster of internally flooded residential properties occurred within Spondon &mdash; specifically on Willowcroft Road &mdash; triggering the formal investigation. Internal flooding affected nearby homes. [IMG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The urban area of Spondon forms the large upstream catchment whose impermeable surfaces and paved areas generate concentrated surface water runoff that drains by gravity towards the investigation area (Willowcroft Road). This runoff contributed to surface water flow along the public surface water sewer system and the natural flow path during intense rainfall (e.g. 19 July 2014), increasing surface water flood risk in the downstream study area. [IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Around 7 homes along Willowcroft Road (north of the A52) experienced flood water in ground&ndash;floor living areas. An undetermined number of nearby properties suffered severe external property flooding, in some cases close to entering ground&ndash;floor living areas. [IMG,PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 19th July 2014 an extremely isolated, high&ndash;intensity storm produced rapid surface runoff from largely impermeable paved areas. The local highway gullies and the public surface water sewer network were inundated and exceeded capacity, directing rapid downslope flows into lower elevations. This led to internal flooding of properties and significant damage to ground&ndash;floor living areas; flow routes were defined by local topography toward the River Derwent. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Spondon was particularly affected by surface water flooding during the intense storm; the investigation focused on a cluster of properties that were internally flooded as drainage was overwhelmed and runoff followed natural flow paths. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>An intense, isolated thunderstorm on the afternoon of 19th July 2014 caused surface water drainage (highway drains and surface water sewers) to be exceeded, resulting in surface water flooding across many areas of Spondon. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 residential properties [IMG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>around 7 homes along Willowcroft Road [IMG,PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,Spondon,England,"Other areas of Spondon experienced surface water flooding during the same event, including isolated cases of internal property flooding affecting nearby localities. (p3)
A significant cluster of internally flooded residential properties occurred within Spondon — specifically on Willowcroft Road — triggering the formal investigation. Internal flooding affected nearby homes. [IMG] (p5)
The urban area of Spondon forms the large upstream catchment whose impermeable surfaces and paved areas generate concentrated surface water runoff that drains by gravity towards the investigation area (Willowcroft Road). This runoff contributed to surface water flow along the public surface water sewer system and the natural flow path during intense rainfall (e.g. 19 July 2014), increasing surface water flood risk in the downstream study area. [IMG] (p6)
Around 7 homes along Willowcroft Road (north of the A52) experienced flood water in ground–floor living areas. An undetermined number of nearby properties suffered severe external property flooding, in some cases close to entering ground–floor living areas. [IMG,PAG] (p10)
On 19th July 2014 an extremely isolated, high–intensity storm produced rapid surface runoff from largely impermeable paved areas. The local highway gullies and the public surface water sewer network were inundated and exceeded capacity, directing rapid downslope flows into lower elevations. This led to internal flooding of properties and significant damage to ground–floor living areas; flow routes were defined by local topography toward the River Derwent. [PAG] (p11)
Spondon was particularly affected by surface water flooding during the intense storm; the investigation focused on a cluster of properties that were internally flooded as drainage was overwhelmed and runoff followed natural flow paths. (p12)
An intense, isolated thunderstorm on the afternoon of 19th July 2014 caused surface water drainage (highway drains and surface water sewers) to be exceeded, resulting in surface water flooding across many areas of Spondon. (p13)","7 residential properties [IMG] (p5)
around 7 homes along Willowcroft Road [IMG,PAG] (p10)
7 properties [PAG] (p11)
7 properties (p12)",GB-DER_5_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_5_2014-07-19,Spondon flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Willowcroft Road, Spondon, 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Willowcroft-Road-Spondon-S19.pdf
GB-LAN,22,2019-07-27,53.7496026,-3.0178175,"<div id=""html_a2e866fcbe0b18b0d63b1181c34bc330"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Royal Lytham and St Annes Golf Club</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rain on 28 July 2019 led to delays to play at the course (event disruption). (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Royal Lytham and St Annes Golf Club,England,Heavy rain on 28 July 2019 led to delays to play at the course (event disruption). (p17),,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27.html,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27,Lancashire flooding 27 Jul 2019 - 01 Aug 2019,27 July – 1 August 2019 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-july-august-2019-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,22,2019-07-27,53.615364,-2.155756,"<div id=""html_a8a5224e3d876c3e4a26ba4374a3eebc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rochdale Metropolitan District</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple properties across Lancashire were flooded as a result of intense, persistent rainfall; heavy rain affected Rochdale and nearby areas which contributed to flooding in neighbouring towns. [PAG] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>25 properties [PAG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Rochdale Metropolitan District,England,"Multiple properties across Lancashire were flooded as a result of intense, persistent rainfall; heavy rain affected Rochdale and nearby areas which contributed to flooding in neighbouring towns. [PAG] (p13)",25 properties [PAG] (p13),GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27.html,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27,Lancashire flooding 27 Jul 2019 - 01 Aug 2019,27 July – 1 August 2019 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-july-august-2019-flooding.pdf
