GB-LAN,22,2019-07-27,53.6668765,-2.1711264,"<div id=""html_ab5863ccdaec128a606edfb195726e41"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Millfold, Whitworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the Millfold area were reported as affected by flooding during the Whitworth incident associated with the flood warning on 28 July 2019. [MUL] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Millfold, Whitworth",England,Properties in the Millfold area were reported as affected by flooding during the Whitworth incident associated with the flood warning on 28 July 2019. [MUL] (p16),,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27.html,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27,Lancashire flooding 27 Jul 2019 - 01 Aug 2019,27 July – 1 August 2019 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-july-august-2019-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,22,2019-07-27,53.6648413,-2.1737183,"<div id=""html_2ffe749dc51b6c57f407a21de087423a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>John Street, Whitworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>John Street was affected by flooding on 28 July 2019; a flood warning sign was placed and photographs document wet/flooded road conditions and warnings to road users. [IMG,MUL] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"John Street, Whitworth",England,"John Street was affected by flooding on 28 July 2019; a flood warning sign was placed and photographs document wet/flooded road conditions and warnings to road users. [IMG,MUL] (p16)",,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27.html,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27,Lancashire flooding 27 Jul 2019 - 01 Aug 2019,27 July – 1 August 2019 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-july-august-2019-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,22,2019-07-27,53.6634793,-2.1728506,"<div id=""html_69269192023cdc60d9ddc6051a4251ec"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Daniel Street, Whitworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the area around Daniel Street were reported as affected by flooding associated with the Whitworth flood warning on 28 July 2019. [MUL] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Daniel Street, Whitworth",England,Properties in the area around Daniel Street were reported as affected by flooding associated with the Whitworth flood warning on 28 July 2019. [MUL] (p16),,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27.html,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27,Lancashire flooding 27 Jul 2019 - 01 Aug 2019,27 July – 1 August 2019 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-july-august-2019-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,22,2019-07-27,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_9c546a9b1c70bb582ef6872a2a01f87d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Lancashire experienced flooding during the event spanning 27 July to 1 August 2019. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Summer storms (27&ndash;29 July 2019) and further rainfall on 1 August 2019 temporarily overwhelmed local drainage systems across Lancashire, causing extensive flooding of properties and highways. Records show 102 properties flooded (91 homes and 11 commercial/agricultural properties), with 14 homes flooded internally to at least one habitable room; there is a report of one further property potentially flooded (possible total 103 properties). [MUL] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of Lancashire experienced flooding during the event; the area covered by the Earby and Salterforth Internal Drainage Board was affected by floodwater. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding occurred across large areas of the county as a series of intense rainfall events between 27 July 2019 and 1 August 2019, affecting multiple communities and prompting localised site inspections by risk management authorities. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall across the county resulted in property flooding: one property in Fylde flooded on 27 July 2019; on 28 July 2019 a total of 25 properties were reported flooded within Lancashire (4 in western Lancashire across Fylde, Chorley and Preston; 1 in Pendle; 20 in Rossendale &mdash; all 20 in the town of Whitworth). [IMG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread external flooding to residential properties across multiple districts within the county and standing surface water on main and residential roads, causing travel disruptions. [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding affected properties across multiple districts within the county and widespread standing water and travel disruption on the local road network. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Repeated bands of heavy rain across the county between 27 July and 1 August 2019 caused flooding; county council Highway Service inspected affected highway locations, removed silt from gullies and drainage systems, and flood waters subsided the following morning. [PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme rainfall between 27 July and 1 August 2019 overwhelmed many drainage networks in parts of Lancashire, causing flooding that damaged homes and belongings and raised serious concerns for personal safety among affected people. [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme rainfall between 27 July and 1 August 2019 overwhelmed local drainage networks across the county, causing flooding of homes and business premises and damage to people's homes and belongings; significant concern for personal safety was reported. [PAG] (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>102 properties; 91 homes; 11 commercial/agricultural properties; 14 homes flooded internally; possible total of 103 properties [MUL] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (27 Jul 2019); 25 properties (28 Jul 2019); 20 properties (in Whitworth, Rossendale) [IMG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>75 properties across the county (29 Jul 2019: 21 properties; 30&ndash;31 Jul 2019: 34 properties; 1 Aug 2019: 20 properties) [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties (Chorley); 1 property (Hyndburn); 1 property (Preston); 2 properties (Ribble Valley); 1 property (Rossendale); 10 properties (West Lancashire); 8 properties (Whitworth) [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>103 individual homes and business premises [PAG] (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Lancashire experienced flooding during the event spanning 27 July to 1 August 2019. (p1)
Summer storms (27–29 July 2019) and further rainfall on 1 August 2019 temporarily overwhelmed local drainage systems across Lancashire, causing extensive flooding of properties and highways. Records show 102 properties flooded (91 homes and 11 commercial/agricultural properties), with 14 homes flooded internally to at least one habitable room; there is a report of one further property potentially flooded (possible total 103 properties). [MUL] (p3)
Part of Lancashire experienced flooding during the event; the area covered by the Earby and Salterforth Internal Drainage Board was affected by floodwater. (p10)
Widespread flooding occurred across large areas of the county as a series of intense rainfall events between 27 July 2019 and 1 August 2019, affecting multiple communities and prompting localised site inspections by risk management authorities. [PAG] (p12)
Heavy rainfall across the county resulted in property flooding: one property in Fylde flooded on 27 July 2019; on 28 July 2019 a total of 25 properties were reported flooded within Lancashire (4 in western Lancashire across Fylde, Chorley and Preston; 1 in Pendle; 20 in Rossendale — all 20 in the town of Whitworth). [IMG] (p13)
Widespread external flooding to residential properties across multiple districts within the county and standing surface water on main and residential roads, causing travel disruptions. [PAG] (p15)
External flooding affected properties across multiple districts within the county and widespread standing water and travel disruption on the local road network. [PAG] (p16)
Repeated bands of heavy rain across the county between 27 July and 1 August 2019 caused flooding; county council Highway Service inspected affected highway locations, removed silt from gullies and drainage systems, and flood waters subsided the following morning. [PAG] (p17)
Extreme rainfall between 27 July and 1 August 2019 overwhelmed many drainage networks in parts of Lancashire, causing flooding that damaged homes and belongings and raised serious concerns for personal safety among affected people. [PAG] (p19)
Extreme rainfall between 27 July and 1 August 2019 overwhelmed local drainage networks across the county, causing flooding of homes and business premises and damage to people's homes and belongings; significant concern for personal safety was reported. [PAG] (p20)","102 properties; 91 homes; 11 commercial/agricultural properties; 14 homes flooded internally; possible total of 103 properties [MUL] (p3)
1 property (27 Jul 2019); 25 properties (28 Jul 2019); 20 properties (in Whitworth, Rossendale) [IMG] (p13)
75 properties across the county (29 Jul 2019: 21 properties; 30–31 Jul 2019: 34 properties; 1 Aug 2019: 20 properties) [PAG] (p15)
5 properties (Chorley); 1 property (Hyndburn); 1 property (Preston); 2 properties (Ribble Valley); 1 property (Rossendale); 10 properties (West Lancashire); 8 properties (Whitworth) [PAG] (p16)
103 individual homes and business premises [PAG] (p20)",GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27.html,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27,Lancashire flooding 27 Jul 2019 - 01 Aug 2019,27 July – 1 August 2019 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-july-august-2019-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,22,2019-07-27,53.6109397,-2.8565713,"<div id=""html_79467d564fb479eb734dbf469b5a4d26"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy, persistent rainfall caused surface water flooding affecting properties in western Lancashire (including Fylde district). One property in Fylde was reported flooded on 27 July 2019, and on 28 July 2019 four properties across the western Lancashire districts (Fylde, Chorley and Preston) were among those reported flooded. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties flooded following heavy rainfall. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding to properties reported across the event: 3 properties flooded on 29 July 2019; 10 properties flooded on 30&ndash;31 July 2019; and a further 10 properties flooded on 1 August 2019. [PAG] (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (27 Jul 2019); 4 properties (28 Jul 2019 across Fylde, Chorley and Preston) (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties on 29 July 2019 (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (29 Jul 2019); 10 properties (30&ndash;31 Jul 2019); 10 properties (1 Aug 2019) [PAG] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,West Lancashire,England,"Heavy, persistent rainfall caused surface water flooding affecting properties in western Lancashire (including Fylde district). One property in Fylde was reported flooded on 27 July 2019, and on 28 July 2019 four properties across the western Lancashire districts (Fylde, Chorley and Preston) were among those reported flooded. (p13)
Properties flooded following heavy rainfall. (p14)
External flooding to properties reported across the event: 3 properties flooded on 29 July 2019; 10 properties flooded on 30–31 July 2019; and a further 10 properties flooded on 1 August 2019. [PAG] (p15)","1 property (27 Jul 2019); 4 properties (28 Jul 2019 across Fylde, Chorley and Preston) (p13)
