GB-LAN,22,2019-07-27,53.914757,-2.1356368,"<div id=""html_105138ae5429f9e47b2bf1ed5455f2fb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Earby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the area covered by the Earby and Salterforth internal drainage board was affected by flooding during the event. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Earby,England,Part of the area covered by the Earby and Salterforth internal drainage board was affected by flooding during the event. (p10),,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27.html,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27,Lancashire flooding 27 Jul 2019 - 01 Aug 2019,27 July – 1 August 2019 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-july-august-2019-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,22,2019-07-27,53.9053347,-2.1714623,"<div id=""html_5b9d2eaa1c8d10d97d1f6d501038272d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Salterforth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the area covered by the Earby and Salterforth internal drainage board was affected by flooding during the event. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Salterforth,England,Part of the area covered by the Earby and Salterforth internal drainage board was affected by flooding during the event. (p10),,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27.html,GB-LAN_22_2019-07-27,Lancashire flooding 27 Jul 2019 - 01 Aug 2019,27 July – 1 August 2019 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-july-august-2019-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,22,2019-07-27,53.66924745,-2.1852538962618415,"<div id=""html_cd8933fc6272251452ce4ec5c59ffd0e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whitworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Concentrated property flooding in the town of Whitworth (southern/SE Rossendale) caused by the heavy, persistent rainfall on 28 July 2019. [PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties in the town flooded following heavy, localised rainfall. [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding to properties in Whitworth: 7 properties flooded on 29 July 2019 and 3 properties flooded on 30&ndash;31 July 2019 (these counts are reported as Whitworth&ndash;specific within the Rossendale totals). [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At least 8 properties in Whitworth flooded during the event; a rest centre was opened for affected residents (it was later closed unused). Properties around Station Road, Millfold, John Street and Daniel Street and the football ground were affected and a flood warning was issued. [IMG,MUL] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes and gardens in Whitworth were flooded by surface water during the event; affected residents engaged with investigations and local response efforts (including the Whitworth Flood Action Group). (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall on 28 July 2019 produced rapid runoff from open fields and moorland which was funnelled by estate roads and footpaths into a deep flow, causing particularly devastating flood damage in Whitworth. (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>20 properties (28 Jul 2019) [PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>20 properties on 28 July 2019; 7 properties on 29 July 2019; total 27 properties [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (29 Jul 2019); 3 properties (30&ndash;31 Jul 2019) [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties [IMG,MUL] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Whitworth,England,"Concentrated property flooding in the town of Whitworth (southern/SE Rossendale) caused by the heavy, persistent rainfall on 28 July 2019. [PAG] (p13)
