GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.8770582,-1.3062493,"<div id=""html_4bc77f017f332c40035e491537d0f6f5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Trent</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Later, longer river responses to heavy rainfall were recorded downstream on the River Trent (near Shardlow). The Shardlow gauging station on the River Trent produced the 5th highest ranked flow on record in response to Storm Babet. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5th highest ranked flow on record (Shardlow station) (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,River Trent,England,"Later, longer river responses to heavy rainfall were recorded downstream on the River Trent (near Shardlow). The Shardlow gauging station on the River Trent produced the 5th highest ranked flow on record in response to Storm Babet. (p3)",5th highest ranked flow on record (Shardlow station) (p3),GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.020111540117746,-1.327014903846829,"<div id=""html_a49abc33543c15d455f9d127bfee28e4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Derby Road Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Erewash overtopped the Derby Road bridge with water high enough to flow over the bridge deck; wrack marks on the upstream face indicate the peak water level reached the bridge and contributed to flooding on Derby Road. (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Erewash overtopped the upstream face of Derby Road bridge during the event, causing floodwater to flow onto and along Derby Road. Wrack marks on the upstream face record the peak level, and overtopping contributed to flooding of the adjacent highway and damage to pavement and underground services. [PAG,IMG] (p31)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>wrack level 59.9mAOD; floodwater depths of approximately 1m reported in multiple locations [PAG,IMG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Derby Road Bridge,England,"The River Erewash overtopped the Derby Road bridge with water high enough to flow over the bridge deck; wrack marks on the upstream face indicate the peak water level reached the bridge and contributed to flooding on Derby Road. (p30)
The River Erewash overtopped the upstream face of Derby Road bridge during the event, causing floodwater to flow onto and along Derby Road. Wrack marks on the upstream face record the peak level, and overtopping contributed to flooding of the adjacent highway and damage to pavement and underground services. [PAG,IMG] (p31)","wrack level 59.9mAOD; floodwater depths of approximately 1m reported in multiple locations [PAG,IMG] (p31)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.8978745,-1.3306383,"<div id=""html_f4ae2b45faa25ff031438058a680c330"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Gregory Avenue, Breaston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on/adjacent to Gregory Avenue experienced internal flooding caused by overtopping/overflow from nearby Golden Stream and associated drainage ditch during Storm Babet; flooding occurred on the community floodplain and was exacerbated by surface water runoff. [PAG,IMG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties and two non&ndash;residential properties at the eastern end of the street during the Storm Babet event; flooding occurred as river levels rose and surface water/urban flooding affected the community. [PAG,IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from an obstructed/overgrown ditch and the Golden Stream flowed into the street and properties. Photographs show depths up to 0.8 m; residents reported internal flooding. Videos show flow moving from Gregory Avenue into Hind Avenue, Spring Close and Festival Avenue. [IMG,PAG] (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>49 residential properties and 2 non&ndash;residential properties suffered internal flooding in west Breaston (community&ndash;wide total) [PAG,IMG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 residential properties; 2 non&ndash;residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 residential properties; 2 non&ndash;residential properties; 0.8 m flood depth [IMG,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Gregory Avenue, Breaston",England,"Properties on/adjacent to Gregory Avenue experienced internal flooding caused by overtopping/overflow from nearby Golden Stream and associated drainage ditch during Storm Babet; flooding occurred on the community floodplain and was exacerbated by surface water runoff. [PAG,IMG] (p4)
