GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0214771,-1.3284942,"<div id=""html_0ea50b18534d18aba93e784c06c9cdc6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Dean Street, Langley Mill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Dean Street has a recorded history of internal flooding and is identified as having a high risk of surface&ndash;water flooding; properties in the local area flooded internally during the October 2023 event. [IMG,PAG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties on Dean Street caused by overtopping&ndash;related floodwaters from the River Erewash (with canal/brook interactions contributing locally). [TAB] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties on Dean Street caused by floodwater that flowed south along Cromford Road after the River Erewash overtopped its bank. (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drainage issues at Deans Street were identified during the investigation and are under further investigation by Severn Trent in relation to flooding from the event. (p32)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (3 residential, 12 non&ndash;residential) previously flooded across the community; 21 residential and 29 non&ndash;residential properties flooded internally during Storm Babet are shown in Flood Zone 2 (remaining properties in Flood Zone 3). [IMG,PAG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 homes; 4 non&ndash;residential [TAB] (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Dean Street, Langley Mill",England,"Dean Street has a recorded history of internal flooding and is identified as having a high risk of surface–water flooding; properties in the local area flooded internally during the October 2023 event. [IMG,PAG] (p25)
