GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0274573,-1.3437556,"<div id=""html_2779be0e217892c2b3eaf065bc054a50"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cromford Road, Langley Mill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Cromford Road have a recorded history of internal flooding; during the October 2023 event (Storm Babet) properties in the community flooded internally and many properties on Cromford Road are also identified as having a high risk of surface&ndash;water flooding. [PAG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwaters overtopped the River Erewash embankment (first overtopping identified at a 90&deg; bend) and flowed across the Frametrade UK Ltd yard onto Cromford Road, causing internal flooding of properties on the street. [TAB,PAG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater reached Cromford Road and flowed southwards, causing internal flooding of properties on adjacent streets (Queen Street, Dean Street, Derby Road). Floodwater also arrived via overtopping behind the DandD Transport car park which flowed onto Cromford Road. [PAG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed southwards down Cromford Road after River Erewash overtopped (including overtopping behind the DandD Transport car park), causing external flooding on Cromford Road and internal flooding of properties on adjacent streets (including Queen Street, Dean Street and Derby Road). Flood damage included inundation entering properties via doors, drains and through walls, and damage to an underground electrical cable at the roundabout with Derby Road that blew a hole in the pavement. [PAG] (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (3 residential, 12 non&ndash;residential) previously flooded across the community; 21 residential and 29 non&ndash;residential properties flooded internally during Storm Babet are shown in Flood Zone 2 (remaining properties in Flood Zone 3). [PAG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 homes; 21 non&ndash;residential [TAB,PAG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1m floodwater depths reported in multiple locations [PAG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Cromford Road, Langley Mill",England,"Properties on Cromford Road have a recorded history of internal flooding; during the October 2023 event (Storm Babet) properties in the community flooded internally and many properties on Cromford Road are also identified as having a high risk of surface–water flooding. [PAG] (p25)
Floodwaters overtopped the River Erewash embankment (first overtopping identified at a 90° bend) and flowed across the Frametrade UK Ltd yard onto Cromford Road, causing internal flooding of properties on the street. [TAB,PAG] (p28)
