GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0200883,-1.326643,"<div id=""html_470ed793f44781fdf915ff53a5dbc17d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Station Road, Langley Mill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Station Road has recorded previous internal flooding (Historic Flood Map) and is identified on the Long Term Flood Risk Map as having a high risk of surface&ndash;water flooding; properties in the community flooded internally during Storm Babet. (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties on Station Road resulting from overtopping of the River Erewash and transfer of floodwater via the canal/brook system. [TAB] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of homes reached the height of skirting boards. External flooding on Station Road reached ankle depth. Floodwater entered properties via doors, drains backing up, toilets and through brickwork. (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (3 residential, 12 non&ndash;residential) previously flooded across the community; 21 residential and 29 non&ndash;residential properties flooded internally during Storm Babet are shown in Flood Zone 2 (remaining properties in Flood Zone 3). (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 homes; 6 non&ndash;residential [TAB] (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Station Road, Langley Mill",England,"Station Road has recorded previous internal flooding (Historic Flood Map) and is identified on the Long Term Flood Risk Map as having a high risk of surface–water flooding; properties in the community flooded internally during Storm Babet. (p25)
