22 residential properties (across Adelaide Walk, Regent Court and Deepdale) [PAG] (p35)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0645304,-1.3452314,"<div id=""html_8eaf19d3b577540abc4a918d96f2d12f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Nottingham Lane, Ironville</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the River Erewash overflowed the west bank upstream of the Midland Railway Line, travelled over fields onto Nottingham Lane (south of the properties), flowed through the underpass beneath the railway (resident reported water 'higher than a car bonnet') and moved southwards along Nottingham Lane into Ironville. Floodwater then crossed recreational playing fields and contributed to internal flooding of houses at Regent Court and Deepdale and caused flooding along Victoria Street and the B6016 to the south&ndash;east of the community. [PAG,IMG] (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the overflowing Erewash flowed over fields onto Nottingham Lane, then southwards via the railway underpass; a resident reported water at the underpass higher than a car bonnet. Water from Nottingham Lane continued south across recreational fields and into residential streets (Regent Court, Deepdale) and along Victoria Street/B6016. (p35)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Nottingham Lane, Ironville",England,"Floodwater from the River Erewash overflowed the west bank upstream of the Midland Railway Line, travelled over fields onto Nottingham Lane (south of the properties), flowed through the underpass beneath the railway (resident reported water 'higher than a car bonnet') and moved southwards along Nottingham Lane into Ironville. Floodwater then crossed recreational playing fields and contributed to internal flooding of houses at Regent Court and Deepdale and caused flooding along Victoria Street and the B6016 to the south–east of the community. [PAG,IMG] (p34)
Floodwater from the overflowing Erewash flowed over fields onto Nottingham Lane, then southwards via the railway underpass; a resident reported water at the underpass higher than a car bonnet. Water from Nottingham Lane continued south across recreational fields and into residential streets (Regent Court, Deepdale) and along Victoria Street/B6016. (p35)","22 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p34)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0860272,-1.3233893,"<div id=""html_5bc74ef756d467a1c7c7ebd1579860f0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Alexander Terrace, Pinxton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the residential community in the south&ndash;west of Pinxton experienced internal flooding during Storm Babet. Alexander Terrace is mapped within that residential area; while the report confirms 22 properties in the community were internally flooded, it does not give street&ndash;level counts. It is therefore likely (but not explicitly stated) that properties on or adjacent to Alexander Terrace were among those flooded. [IMG] (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Alexander Terrace were flooded during Storm Babet. Properties are within Flood Zone 2 and some are identified as at high risk of surface&ndash;water flooding; flooding is associated with the nearby River Erewash. [IMG] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff pooled at a local low point on Alexandra Terrace (sic), directing water into the community. The sewer network became surcharged and manhole covers were observed lifted when the sewers could not discharge to the River Erewash because river levels were very high. This combination of surface water runoff and sewer surcharge (exacerbated by elevated river levels) contributed to flooding of properties in the locality. (p39)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 properties (total within the flooded Pinxton community) [IMG] (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2.65 metres (peak River Erewash level recorded at Pinxton gauge on 20 Oct 2023); 300 metres (approximate distance of the Pinxton gauge downstream of the community) (p39)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Alexander Terrace, Pinxton",England,"Part of the residential community in the south–west of Pinxton experienced internal flooding during Storm Babet. Alexander Terrace is mapped within that residential area; while the report confirms 22 properties in the community were internally flooded, it does not give street–level counts. It is therefore likely (but not explicitly stated) that properties on or adjacent to Alexander Terrace were among those flooded. [IMG] (p36)
Residential properties on Alexander Terrace were flooded during Storm Babet. Properties are within Flood Zone 2 and some are identified as at high risk of surface–water flooding; flooding is associated with the nearby River Erewash. [IMG] (p37)
Surface water runoff pooled at a local low point on Alexandra Terrace (sic), directing water into the community. The sewer network became surcharged and manhole covers were observed lifted when the sewers could not discharge to the River Erewash because river levels were very high. This combination of surface water runoff and sewer surcharge (exacerbated by elevated river levels) contributed to flooding of properties in the locality. (p39)","22 properties (total within the flooded Pinxton community) [IMG] (p36)
2.65 metres (peak River Erewash level recorded at Pinxton gauge on 20 Oct 2023); 300 metres (approximate distance of the Pinxton gauge downstream of the community) (p39)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0856682,-1.3240228,"<div id=""html_20a5c772e823ff0918c947da7dbb6084"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>York Terrace, Pinxton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>York Terrace is located inside the residential area in the south&ndash;west of Pinxton where a community of 22 properties suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet. The report does not specify exactly which streets were affected, so York Terrace is likely to have been within the impacted area but street&ndash;level details are not provided. [IMG] (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on York Terrace were flooded during Storm Babet. These properties are within Flood Zone 2 and some are identified as at high risk of surface&ndash;water flooding; flooding is associated with the nearby River Erewash. [IMG] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on York Terrace experienced flooding: external flooding began around 06:30&ndash;06:45 and at least one property suffered internal flooding by 11:00 on 20 Oct. Flooding was caused by sewer network surcharge (manhole covers lifted), surface water pooling at a local low point, and likely contribution from high River Erewash levels and overflow of a nearby unnamed watercourse. (p39)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 properties (total within the flooded Pinxton community) [IMG] (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"York Terrace, Pinxton",England,"York Terrace is located inside the residential area in the south–west of Pinxton where a community of 22 properties suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet. The report does not specify exactly which streets were affected, so York Terrace is likely to have been within the impacted area but street–level details are not provided. [IMG] (p36)
Residential properties on York Terrace were flooded during Storm Babet. These properties are within Flood Zone 2 and some are identified as at high risk of surface–water flooding; flooding is associated with the nearby River Erewash. [IMG] (p37)
Properties on York Terrace experienced flooding: external flooding began around 06:30–06:45 and at least one property suffered internal flooding by 11:00 on 20 Oct. Flooding was caused by sewer network surcharge (manhole covers lifted), surface water pooling at a local low point, and likely contribution from high River Erewash levels and overflow of a nearby unnamed watercourse. (p39)",22 properties (total within the flooded Pinxton community) [IMG] (p36),GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0861213,-1.3242758,"<div id=""html_710d187e3e846e5ea5ecae9cb37c22d7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sleights Lane, Pinxton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sleights Lane lies within the residential area north of the River Erewash where a group of 22 properties were internally flooded during Storm Babet. The source text does not state which individual streets were flooded, so Sleights Lane is probably within the affected community but specific impacts on the lane are not recorded. [IMG] (p36)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 properties (total within the flooded Pinxton community) [IMG] (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Sleights Lane, Pinxton",England,"Sleights Lane lies within the residential area north of the River Erewash where a group of 22 properties were internally flooded during Storm Babet. The source text does not state which individual streets were flooded, so Sleights Lane is probably within the affected community but specific impacts on the lane are not recorded. [IMG] (p36)",22 properties (total within the flooded Pinxton community) [IMG] (p36),GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0886279,-1.3240146,"<div id=""html_fd2a953dcd22367f7fb400dd8ca7826a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Park Lane, Pinxton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Park Lane is shown within the residential area north of the River Erewash where a community of 22 properties sustained internal flooding during Storm Babet. The report does not provide street&ndash;by&ndash;street details, so Park Lane is likely within the affected area but specific damage to the street is not documented. [IMG] (p36)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 properties (total within the flooded Pinxton community) [IMG] (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Park Lane, Pinxton",England,"Park Lane is shown within the residential area north of the River Erewash where a community of 22 properties sustained internal flooding during Storm Babet. The report does not provide street–by–street details, so Park Lane is likely within the affected area but specific damage to the street is not documented. [IMG] (p36)",22 properties (total within the flooded Pinxton community) [IMG] (p36),GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0865188,-1.3221219,"<div id=""html_d71edfd8d37afbd39db6d0a457c49aa1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mill Lane, Pinxton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the south&ndash;west Pinxton residential community where properties were internally flooded during Storm Babet. The community of twenty&ndash;two properties suffered internal flooding; emergency services carried out evacuations (boats) during the event. [IMG] (p36)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 properties (community total) [IMG] (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Mill Lane, Pinxton",England,Part of the south–west Pinxton residential community where properties were internally flooded during Storm Babet. The community of twenty–two properties suffered internal flooding; emergency services carried out evacuations (boats) during the event. [IMG] (p36),22 properties (community total) [IMG] (p36),GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0886231,-1.31506,"<div id=""html_b82b8f3ce1c52b1b1d1ee37a03f45298"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brookhill Road, Pinxton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Located within the Pinxton residential area described as being affected by Storm Babet; the community experienced internal flooding (twenty&ndash;two properties) with emergency evacuations carried out by Derbyshire Fire and Rescue. [IMG] (p36)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 properties (community total) [IMG] (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Brookhill Road, Pinxton",England,Located within the Pinxton residential area described as being affected by Storm Babet; the community experienced internal flooding (twenty–two properties) with emergency evacuations carried out by Derbyshire Fire and Rescue. [IMG] (p36),22 properties (community total) [IMG] (p36),GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.8604355,-1.3900205,"<div id=""html_637d74f9a2838dae4c48052b2f053cdc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Weston Road, Aston-On-Trent</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One residential property on Weston Road suffered internal flooding. [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A ditch at the boundary of the field to the west of Weston Road was overwhelmed and spilled onto Weston Road, allowing runoff to flow into the residential area and reach properties. [IMG,PAG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flow routed across the local topography through Aston&ndash;on&ndash;Trent during the event, causing horizontal ploughing/erosion of the farmland immediately west of Weston Road. (p44)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 home [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [IMG,PAG] (p43)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Weston Road, Aston-On-Trent",England,"One residential property on Weston Road suffered internal flooding. [IMG,PAG] (p41)
A ditch at the boundary of the field to the west of Weston Road was overwhelmed and spilled onto Weston Road, allowing runoff to flow into the residential area and reach properties. [IMG,PAG] (p43)
