9 residential properties in Aston–on–Trent; 1 home on Weston Road; 8 homes on Yates Avenue [IMG] (p41)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.9543064,-1.2916163,"<div id=""html_5f2142b82b33139d7a3c7573f38d0b54"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Erewash Canal</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Acted as a conduit for fluvial floodwater from the River Erewash into the urban area (transporting river water through the canal) &mdash; it was not the source of the flooding. [IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding concentrated along the Erewash Canal (and adjacent River Erewash) contributed to the inundation of the local residential community in Sandiacre; Flood Zone 3 is concentrated closest to the canal, placing adjacent streets and properties at highest risk during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas immediately adjacent to the Erewash Canal were shown as having the highest surface&ndash;water flood risk on the map. Properties close to the canal (for example Canal Street) are reported as having experienced internal flooding during the event associated with Storm Babet and the flooding is linked to high water levels in the local watercourses. [PAG,IMG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flood water from the River Erewash entered the canal which acted as a conduit, raising canal water levels and creating a secondary flow path that carried floodwater south across the community and contributed to internal property flooding. [PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Erewash overtopped and flowed into the Erewash Canal north of Gas Street (opposite Brookfield Mews). The canal acted as a conduit for flood water, water levels rose and created a secondary flow path which flowed south across the community, causing rapid onset flooding and significant property damage (several properties had floors lifted). [PAG,IMG] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas adjacent to the Erewash Canal are mapped as Flood Zone 3 (highest fluvial risk) and the map analysis links the highest flood risk to the canal corridor. These Flood Zone 3 areas are associated with properties that flooded internally during Storm Babet (Oct 2023), so the canal corridor was implicated in the fluvial flooding that affected properties in Langley Mill during 18 Oct 2023 &ndash; 21 Oct 2023. Exact numbers of properties adjacent to the canal that flooded are not specified in the text. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Acted as a conduit for transfer of floodwater from the River Erewash and Nether Green Brook; the canal overtopped (entirely due to inflows from the river and brook) and this contributed to property flooding in the community. (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Erewash Canal overtopped because inflows from the River Erewash and Nether Green Brook entered the canal; the canal overtopping was a direct pathway contributing to flooding of adjacent areas in Langley Mill. [IMG,PAG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The canal acted as a conduit for floodwater entering from Nether Green Brook, causing flooding across Langley Mill Boatyard, overtopping lock gates, and transferring floodwater southwards; overflow from the canal's west banks flowed overland towards the River Erewash and contributed to downstream flooding. (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>129 properties flooded (community total linked to canal conveyance) [PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>129 homes and businesses [PAG,IMG] (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Erewash Canal,England,"Acted as a conduit for fluvial floodwater from the River Erewash into the urban area (transporting river water through the canal) — it was not the source of the flooding. [IMG] (p12)
Flooding concentrated along the Erewash Canal (and adjacent River Erewash) contributed to the inundation of the local residential community in Sandiacre; Flood Zone 3 is concentrated closest to the canal, placing adjacent streets and properties at highest risk during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p15)
Areas immediately adjacent to the Erewash Canal were shown as having the highest surface–water flood risk on the map. Properties close to the canal (for example Canal Street) are reported as having experienced internal flooding during the event associated with Storm Babet and the flooding is linked to high water levels in the local watercourses. [PAG,IMG] (p16)
Fluvial flood water from the River Erewash entered the canal which acted as a conduit, raising canal water levels and creating a secondary flow path that carried floodwater south across the community and contributed to internal property flooding. [PAG] (p17)
The River Erewash overtopped and flowed into the Erewash Canal north of Gas Street (opposite Brookfield Mews). The canal acted as a conduit for flood water, water levels rose and created a secondary flow path which flowed south across the community, causing rapid onset flooding and significant property damage (several properties had floors lifted). [PAG,IMG] (p18)
Areas adjacent to the Erewash Canal are mapped as Flood Zone 3 (highest fluvial risk) and the map analysis links the highest flood risk to the canal corridor. These Flood Zone 3 areas are associated with properties that flooded internally during Storm Babet (Oct 2023), so the canal corridor was implicated in the fluvial flooding that affected properties in Langley Mill during 18 Oct 2023 – 21 Oct 2023. Exact numbers of properties adjacent to the canal that flooded are not specified in the text. [PAG,IMG] (p26)
Acted as a conduit for transfer of floodwater from the River Erewash and Nether Green Brook; the canal overtopped (entirely due to inflows from the river and brook) and this contributed to property flooding in the community. (p28)
The Erewash Canal overtopped because inflows from the River Erewash and Nether Green Brook entered the canal; the canal overtopping was a direct pathway contributing to flooding of adjacent areas in Langley Mill. [IMG,PAG] (p29)
The canal acted as a conduit for floodwater entering from Nether Green Brook, causing flooding across Langley Mill Boatyard, overtopping lock gates, and transferring floodwater southwards; overflow from the canal's west banks flowed overland towards the River Erewash and contributed to downstream flooding. (p30)","129 properties flooded (community total linked to canal conveyance) [PAG] (p17)
129 homes and businesses [PAG,IMG] (p18)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.01965327176416,-1.3242217915065189,"<div id=""html_4642a61c84e795ada97ac8d8989b80db"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Langley Mill Boatyard</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Nether Green Brook surcharged; once water entered the Erewash Canal the canal acted as a conduit and transferred floodwater into and across the Langley Mill Boatyard. Lock gates were overtopped and water flowed southwards along the canal, contributing to flooding at the boatyard. (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Langley Mill Boatyard,England,"Nether Green Brook surcharged; once water entered the Erewash Canal the canal acted as a conduit and transferred floodwater into and across the Langley Mill Boatyard. Lock gates were overtopped and water flowed southwards along the canal, contributing to flooding at the boatyard. (p30)",,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0036824,-1.3124773,"<div id=""html_7a561557ddd3ef574367830f83a33e29"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Shipley Lock</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater conveyed along the Erewash Canal overtopped lock gates; the canal acted as a conduit transferring floodwater southwards and contributed to overbank flow toward the River Erewash and local flooding. [PAG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Shipley Lock,England,Floodwater conveyed along the Erewash Canal overtopped lock gates; the canal acted as a conduit transferring floodwater southwards and contributed to overbank flow toward the River Erewash and local flooding. [PAG] (p31),,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.084649,-1.3249441,"<div id=""html_a0046913a24437a4c70be829124ec819"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pinxton Wharf</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties at Pinxton Wharf experienced surface water inundation and sewer network backup that led to internal flooding of residential properties; drainage systems could not discharge because of very high River Erewash levels. [PAG,IMG] (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Survey evidence showed River Erewash floodwater entered Pinxton Wharf, raising pond levels above bank wrack marks. Elevated wharf levels likely prevented an unnamed watercourse from discharging, causing it to back up and overflow toward the rear of York Terrace. (p39)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Pinxton Wharf,England,"Properties at Pinxton Wharf experienced surface water inundation and sewer network backup that led to internal flooding of residential properties; drainage systems could not discharge because of very high River Erewash levels. [PAG,IMG] (p38)
Survey evidence showed River Erewash floodwater entered Pinxton Wharf, raising pond levels above bank wrack marks. Elevated wharf levels likely prevented an unnamed watercourse from discharging, causing it to back up and overflow toward the rear of York Terrace. (p39)",,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.9232778,-1.2892153,"<div id=""html_d5cc9f191dbb3424e105baa2a5d59bec"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sandiacre</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A later, longer river response to heavy rainfall was recorded on the River Erewash near Sandiacre. The Sandiacre station produced one of the highest&ndash;ranked flows or levels on record in response to Storm Babet. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential area between the River Erewash and the Erewash Valley Canal suffered internal flooding &mdash; terraces, flats and several businesses/commercial properties were flooded. Erewash Borough Council provided flood recovery assistance to affected residents. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential community between the River Erewash and Erewash Valley Canal experienced internal flooding during the storm: terraced housing, flats and several businesses/commercial properties were internally flooded. Community sits on the River Erewash floodplain and flooded residential properties have flooded previously from the river. [PAG,MUL] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential community (terraced housing and flats) and several businesses/commercial properties were flooded during the event. Flooding occurred on the River Erewash floodplain; all residential properties that flooded from Storm Babet had previously flooded from the River Erewash. Surface water flooding risk affected many streets (some properties on Bridge Street, Canal Street, Grasmere Street, Regent Street and Cross Street had medium/high surface water risk). [PAG,IMG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding from the River Erewash (including flow conveyed via the Erewash Canal) inundated the community with a rapid onset, causing significant property damage (including floors being lifted by the force of water). (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>129 properties (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>129 properties [PAG,MUL] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>104 homes; 25 businesses; 129 properties flooded (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Sandiacre,England,"A later, longer river response to heavy rainfall was recorded on the River Erewash near Sandiacre. The Sandiacre station produced one of the highest–ranked flows or levels on record in response to Storm Babet. (p3)
Residential area between the River Erewash and the Erewash Valley Canal suffered internal flooding — terraces, flats and several businesses/commercial properties were flooded. Erewash Borough Council provided flood recovery assistance to affected residents. (p13)
Residential community between the River Erewash and Erewash Valley Canal experienced internal flooding during the storm: terraced housing, flats and several businesses/commercial properties were internally flooded. Community sits on the River Erewash floodplain and flooded residential properties have flooded previously from the river. [PAG,MUL] (p14)
Residential community (terraced housing and flats) and several businesses/commercial properties were flooded during the event. Flooding occurred on the River Erewash floodplain; all residential properties that flooded from Storm Babet had previously flooded from the River Erewash. Surface water flooding risk affected many streets (some properties on Bridge Street, Canal Street, Grasmere Street, Regent Street and Cross Street had medium/high surface water risk). [PAG,IMG] (p16)
Fluvial flooding from the River Erewash (including flow conveyed via the Erewash Canal) inundated the community with a rapid onset, causing significant property damage (including floors being lifted by the force of water). (p17)","129 properties (p13)
129 properties [PAG,MUL] (p14)
104 homes; 25 businesses; 129 properties flooded (p17)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.8980803,-1.3189508,"<div id=""html_fd48bb36f3971392ddc2102b62ff2f64"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Breaston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties in the west of Breaston; the flooded area is adjacent to Golden Stream (a main river) and a drainage ditch that flows between the properties and Johnson's Meadow. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding occurred in the west of Breaston during Storm Babet. Forty&ndash;nine residential properties and two non&ndash;residential properties suffered internal flooding. The flooded area is adjacent to Golden Stream and a drainage ditch; floodwaters from these watercourses flow through the community towards Golden Brook. The Midlands Main Line railway running through the area also flooded during the event. [IMG,PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties within the Breaston community were flooded during the Storm Babet event. The community sits on the floodplain of the Golden Stream and Golden Brook; homes within Flood Zone 2 and Flood Zone 3 were affected. Properties that flooded in this event have documented previous flooding in 2000, 2019 and 2020. The railway running through the area also flooded during Storm Babet. [PAG,IMG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential and some non&ndash;residential properties during Storm Babet; properties on multiple streets were internally flooded. [PAG,IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Golden Stream and an overgrown/obstructed drainage ditch and culvert caused flow to back up and overtop banks. Overtopping and blocked channels sent water into back gardens and roads across the community, resulting in internal flooding of homes and some non&ndash;residential properties. [IMG] (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>49 residential properties; 2 non&ndash;residential properties (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>49 residential properties; 2 non&ndash;residential properties [IMG,PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>42 homes; 4 non&ndash;residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>49 homes; 17 residential properties on Gregory Avenue; 4 on Hind Avenue; 13 on Festival Avenue; 2 on Spring Close; 13 on the A6005 (Draycott Road); 2 non&ndash;residential properties at eastern end of Gregory Avenue. [PAG,IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>49 homes flooded internally; 2 non&ndash;residential properties flooded [IMG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Breaston,England,"Internal flooding of properties in the west of Breaston; the flooded area is adjacent to Golden Stream (a main river) and a drainage ditch that flows between the properties and Johnson's Meadow. (p3)
