GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.8985715,-1.270813,"<div id=""html_48755541e280f5d27a45eb3b93895cf8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Long Eaton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Received downstream flows from Golden Brook during Storm Babet as part of the flood pathway connecting the flooded area in Breaston to the River Erewash (conveyance of floodwater through the town). (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties suffered internal flooding adjacent to the River Erewash. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties in the town adjacent to the River Erewash; community comprises mixed housing and some local businesses. Two care homes and a school are present in the area (no reports of those groups suffering internal flooding are recorded). [IMG,PAG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties within the town during Storm Babet. [IMG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Erewash overflowed into the Long Eaton community, sending flow routes into Doncaster Road and other streets and causing internal flooding of homes and gardens. [TAB] (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>102 residential properties (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>102 residential properties [IMG,PAG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>102 residential properties [IMG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>102 properties internally flooded [TAB] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Long Eaton,England,"Received downstream flows from Golden Brook during Storm Babet as part of the flood pathway connecting the flooded area in Breaston to the River Erewash (conveyance of floodwater through the town). (p3)
