GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.97109,-1.307171,"<div id=""html_ee44c03d2ae0869eff0c3adc7b26bac7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ilkeston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential and non&ndash;residential properties adjacent to the River Erewash as a result of Storm Babet. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential and non&ndash;residential properties adjacent to the River Erewash. Flooding affected streets including Wentworth Street, Station Street and Digby Street; community sits on the River Erewash floodplain and many properties lie in Flood Zone 3. [IMG,PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Ilkeston community experienced combined river (fluvial) and surface water flooding during the event. Fifty&ndash;three homes flooded internally across the community and fourteen non&ndash;residential properties reported flooding. Parts of the community are within Flood Zone 3 and were covered by EA flood alerts/warnings (Flood Alert issued 19 Oct; Flood Warning issued 20 Oct). [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Community experienced widespread flooding: internal flooding of homes and businesses, railway station and lines flooded, road network impacted, basement flooding (including reports of water entering through floors and rising via drains), and a nearby sewage treatment works affected and later returned to normal operations. [IMG] (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>53 residential and 14 non&ndash;residential properties [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>53 residential properties; 14 non&ndash;residential properties [IMG,PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>53 homes; 14 non&ndash;residential properties [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>53 homes; 14 non&ndash;residential properties [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Ilkeston,England,"Internal flooding of residential and non–residential properties adjacent to the River Erewash as a result of Storm Babet. [PAG] (p8)
Internal flooding of residential and non–residential properties adjacent to the River Erewash. Flooding affected streets including Wentworth Street, Station Street and Digby Street; community sits on the River Erewash floodplain and many properties lie in Flood Zone 3. [IMG,PAG] (p9)
The Ilkeston community experienced combined river (fluvial) and surface water flooding during the event. Fifty–three homes flooded internally across the community and fourteen non–residential properties reported flooding. Parts of the community are within Flood Zone 3 and were covered by EA flood alerts/warnings (Flood Alert issued 19 Oct; Flood Warning issued 20 Oct). [PAG] (p11)
Community experienced widespread flooding: internal flooding of homes and businesses, railway station and lines flooded, road network impacted, basement flooding (including reports of water entering through floors and rising via drains), and a nearby sewage treatment works affected and later returned to normal operations. [IMG] (p12)","53 residential and 14 non–residential properties [PAG] (p8)
53 residential properties; 14 non–residential properties [IMG,PAG] (p9)
53 homes; 14 non–residential properties [PAG] (p11)
53 homes; 14 non–residential properties [IMG] (p12)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.0206084,-1.3356727,"<div id=""html_b09f20487d41493272c4ccd8f59d7cb4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Langley Mill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>There were river&ndash;canal interactions upstream at Langley Mill during the event that likely elevated canal levels prior to the River Erewash overtopping downstream, contributing to the canal acting as a conduit for flood flows. (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Langley Mill experienced internal property flooding during Storm Babet (properties are mapped within Flood Zones associated with river flooding) and the community has documented historical flooding. The Long Term Flood Risk Map shows all residential properties have at least a low risk of surface water flooding, with many locations (Station Road, Dean Street, Cromford Road, Enterprise Road) at high surface&ndash;water flood risk. Flood mapping and protection assets (embankments, flood walls) are concentrated along the River Erewash and Erewash Canal within the community. [IMG,PAG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of homes and non&ndash;residential properties across the Langley Mill community caused by the River Erewash overtopping; the Erewash Canal acted as a conduit and Nether Green Brook contributed in locations. Overtopping was first identified at a 90&deg; bend south of the Crabapple Drive allotments; floodwaters flowed across the Frametrade UK Ltd yard and onto Cromford Road. Flood defences (west and east embankments and an upstream floodwall) are present but were overtopped. Flood Alert issued 19 Oct 2023 01:13; Flood Warning issued 20 Oct 2023 06:44; internal flooding began ~20 Oct 2023 14:00. [TAB,PAG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area experienced flooding from two interacting mechanisms: overtopping of the River Erewash (west&ndash;side flooding) and overflow of the Erewash Canal influenced by the River Erewash and Nether Green Brook (east&ndash;side). Floodwater routes led to internal flooding of properties on Cromford Road and adjacent streets (Queen Street, Dean Street, Derby Road) and overtopping across yards and car parks. [IMG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater entered the Erewash Canal system and resulted in flooding across Langley Mill Boatyard; canal overtopped lock gates and overflowed west banks, with overland flow encouraged by local topography contributing to flooding towards the River Erewash. (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Local watercourses and the Erewash Canal contributed to flooding in Langley Mill. Restricted culvert capacity on Nether Green Brook caused surcharging and overtopping; once into the canal, floodwater was conveyed across the Langley Mill Boatyard and overtopped lock gates, with overland flow directed toward the River Erewash. Homes and commercial properties on Cromford Road, Station Road and Derby Road experienced internal and external flooding. [PAG] (p31)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of homes on local streets (localized residential flooding). [IMG] (p41)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties previously flooded (3 residential and 12 non&ndash;residential); 21 residential and 29 non&ndash;residential properties that flooded internally during Storm Babet are located within Flood Zone 2 [IMG,PAG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>28 homes; 35 non&ndash;residential properties [TAB,PAG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>five culverts along Nether Green Brook (local to Langley Mill); floodwater depths reported approximately 1m in multiple locations; internal flooding at Frametrade UK Ltd reached approximately 0.9m [PAG] (p31)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 home on Weston Road; 8 homes on Yates Avenue [IMG] (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Langley Mill,England,"There were river–canal interactions upstream at Langley Mill during the event that likely elevated canal levels prior to the River Erewash overtopping downstream, contributing to the canal acting as a conduit for flood flows. (p17)
Langley Mill experienced internal property flooding during Storm Babet (properties are mapped within Flood Zones associated with river flooding) and the community has documented historical flooding. The Long Term Flood Risk Map shows all residential properties have at least a low risk of surface water flooding, with many locations (Station Road, Dean Street, Cromford Road, Enterprise Road) at high surface–water flood risk. Flood mapping and protection assets (embankments, flood walls) are concentrated along the River Erewash and Erewash Canal within the community. [IMG,PAG] (p26)
Internal flooding of homes and non–residential properties across the Langley Mill community caused by the River Erewash overtopping; the Erewash Canal acted as a conduit and Nether Green Brook contributed in locations. Overtopping was first identified at a 90° bend south of the Crabapple Drive allotments; floodwaters flowed across the Frametrade UK Ltd yard and onto Cromford Road. Flood defences (west and east embankments and an upstream floodwall) are present but were overtopped. Flood Alert issued 19 Oct 2023 01:13; Flood Warning issued 20 Oct 2023 06:44; internal flooding began ~20 Oct 2023 14:00. [TAB,PAG] (p28)
Area experienced flooding from two interacting mechanisms: overtopping of the River Erewash (west–side flooding) and overflow of the Erewash Canal influenced by the River Erewash and Nether Green Brook (east–side). Floodwater routes led to internal flooding of properties on Cromford Road and adjacent streets (Queen Street, Dean Street, Derby Road) and overtopping across yards and car parks. [IMG] (p29)
Floodwater entered the Erewash Canal system and resulted in flooding across Langley Mill Boatyard; canal overtopped lock gates and overflowed west banks, with overland flow encouraged by local topography contributing to flooding towards the River Erewash. (p30)
Local watercourses and the Erewash Canal contributed to flooding in Langley Mill. Restricted culvert capacity on Nether Green Brook caused surcharging and overtopping; once into the canal, floodwater was conveyed across the Langley Mill Boatyard and overtopped lock gates, with overland flow directed toward the River Erewash. Homes and commercial properties on Cromford Road, Station Road and Derby Road experienced internal and external flooding. [PAG] (p31)
Internal flooding of homes on local streets (localized residential flooding). [IMG] (p41)","15 properties previously flooded (3 residential and 12 non–residential); 21 residential and 29 non–residential properties that flooded internally during Storm Babet are located within Flood Zone 2 [IMG,PAG] (p26)
28 homes; 35 non–residential properties [TAB,PAG] (p28)
five culverts along Nether Green Brook (local to Langley Mill); floodwater depths reported approximately 1m in multiple locations; internal flooding at Frametrade UK Ltd reached approximately 0.9m [PAG] (p31)
1 home on Weston Road; 8 homes on Yates Avenue [IMG] (p41)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.8816601,-1.2999406,"<div id=""html_f64e34bf78cf2a02049a7be12ecf57cf"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sawley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents and businesses in Sawley (Lower Erewash) were affected by flooding; a drop&ndash;in event for those affected was held post&ndash;event. (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Sawley,England,Residents and businesses in Sawley (Lower Erewash) were affected by flooding; a drop–in event for those affected was held post–event. (p19),,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.061502,-1.3494131,"<div id=""html_e821c8092ff81d3cebc84cbe8830ae37"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ironville</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A large culvert at Ironville on the River Erewash became unblocked and appeared to drain very quickly at around 11:00 on 20 Oct 2023; this rapid release of water is reported as a possible contributor to high downstream flows and flooding. (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Twenty&ndash;two residential properties in the Adelaide Walk area suffered internal flooding during the event; the community sits on the floodplain of the River Erewash. [IMG] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Twenty&ndash;two residential properties in the Adelaide Walk area of Ironville suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet. [PAG,IMG] (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The community experienced river flooding during Storm Babet: floodwaters from the River Erewash overtopped the west bank upstream of the Midland Railway Line, flowed over fields onto Nottingham Lane, through the railway underpass, across recreational playing fields and into residential areas. Flooding affected houses in Regent Court and Deepdale and also caused inundation along Victoria Street (B6016) between Ironville and Jacksdale. [PAG,IMG] (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Community areas were impacted by overland flow from the overflowing River Erewash: internal flooding of residential properties on Adelaide Walk, Regent Court and Deepdale (22 properties in total), local roads (Victoria Street/B6016) were flooded, and recreational playing fields and a nearby business depot experienced floodwater. The Severn Trent pumping station was overwhelmed because it had nowhere to pump to. (p35)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approx. 4 km upstream (location of the culvert); 20 Oct 2023 at ~11:00 (timing of the reported unblocking) (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 residential properties [IMG] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 residential properties flooded internally [PAG,IMG] (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 residential properties; 0.9m internal depth at one property in Regent Court; up to 0.5m depth at properties within the Adelaide Park area (p35)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Ironville,England,"A large culvert at Ironville on the River Erewash became unblocked and appeared to drain very quickly at around 11:00 on 20 Oct 2023; this rapid release of water is reported as a possible contributor to high downstream flows and flooding. (p30)
Twenty–two residential properties in the Adelaide Walk area suffered internal flooding during the event; the community sits on the floodplain of the River Erewash. [IMG] (p32)
Twenty–two residential properties in the Adelaide Walk area of Ironville suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet. [PAG,IMG] (p33)
The community experienced river flooding during Storm Babet: floodwaters from the River Erewash overtopped the west bank upstream of the Midland Railway Line, flowed over fields onto Nottingham Lane, through the railway underpass, across recreational playing fields and into residential areas. Flooding affected houses in Regent Court and Deepdale and also caused inundation along Victoria Street (B6016) between Ironville and Jacksdale. [PAG,IMG] (p34)
Community areas were impacted by overland flow from the overflowing River Erewash: internal flooding of residential properties on Adelaide Walk, Regent Court and Deepdale (22 properties in total), local roads (Victoria Street/B6016) were flooded, and recreational playing fields and a nearby business depot experienced floodwater. The Severn Trent pumping station was overwhelmed because it had nowhere to pump to. (p35)","approx. 4 km upstream (location of the culvert); 20 Oct 2023 at ~11:00 (timing of the reported unblocking) (p30)
22 residential properties [IMG] (p32)
22 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p33)
22 residential properties flooded internally [PAG,IMG] (p34)
22 residential properties; 0.9m internal depth at one property in Regent Court; up to 0.5m depth at properties within the Adelaide Park area (p35)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,53.094869349999996,-1.324225944201034,"<div id=""html_676e74380338b510a9187741132151b0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pinxton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>In the south&ndash;west corner of Pinxton twenty&ndash;two residential properties were internally flooded during Storm Babet. The flooded community lies immediately north of the River Erewash and adjacent to an unnamed ordinary watercourse, both of which contributed to the flooding of the terraced housing. [IMG,PAG] (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential terraced properties in the Pinxton community were flooded by the River Erewash during Storm Babet. The flooded area is residential (terraced housing); no known vulnerable institutions were within the flooded properties, though Longwood Infant Academy is located immediately north of the flooded properties. [IMG,PAG] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties occurred on the morning of 20 Oct 2023. Primary mechanisms were surface water runoff and the sewer network being overwhelmed; the sewer network could not discharge because of high river levels, and Derbyshire County Council observed manhole covers had lifted due to sewer network surcharge. [IMG] (p38)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>22 properties [IMG,PAG] (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Pinxton,England,"In the south–west corner of Pinxton twenty–two residential properties were internally flooded during Storm Babet. The flooded community lies immediately north of the River Erewash and adjacent to an unnamed ordinary watercourse, both of which contributed to the flooding of the terraced housing. [IMG,PAG] (p36)
Residential terraced properties in the Pinxton community were flooded by the River Erewash during Storm Babet. The flooded area is residential (terraced housing); no known vulnerable institutions were within the flooded properties, though Longwood Infant Academy is located immediately north of the flooded properties. [IMG,PAG] (p37)
Internal flooding of residential properties occurred on the morning of 20 Oct 2023. Primary mechanisms were surface water runoff and the sewer network being overwhelmed; the sewer network could not discharge because of high river levels, and Derbyshire County Council observed manhole covers had lifted due to sewer network surcharge. [IMG] (p38)","22 properties [IMG,PAG] (p36)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.8613422,-1.3840477,"<div id=""html_368fa200ddb9e97b59d132b0890d8d12"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Aston-On-Trent</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties resulting in property damage and disruption to households. (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Some properties in the Aston&ndash;on&ndash;Trent community were flooded by surface water during Storm Babet; the Environment Agency Historic Flood Map shows the properties that flooded during this event had not flooded previously. The primary school and a retirement village in the community did not flood. (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Run&ndash;off from ploughed farmland west of Weston Road overwhelmed a field boundary ditch which spilled onto Weston Road and flowed into the residential area, reaching properties on Yates Avenue and causing internal flooding. [IMG] (p43)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 residential properties (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 homes (8 on Yates Avenue; 1 on Weston Road) [IMG] (p43)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Aston-On-Trent,England,"Internal flooding of residential properties resulting in property damage and disruption to households. (p41)
Some properties in the Aston–on–Trent community were flooded by surface water during Storm Babet; the Environment Agency Historic Flood Map shows the properties that flooded during this event had not flooded previously. The primary school and a retirement village in the community did not flood. (p42)
Run–off from ploughed farmland west of Weston Road overwhelmed a field boundary ditch which spilled onto Weston Road and flowed into the residential area, reaching properties on Yates Avenue and causing internal flooding. [IMG] (p43)","9 residential properties (p41)
9 homes (8 on Yates Avenue; 1 on Weston Road) [IMG] (p43)",GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,7,2023-10-18,52.95146665998597,-1.284904542487508,"<div id=""html_6806d6d5b5a174bfb422bc6a2023a1ef"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hallam Fields Sewage Treatment Works</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Impacted when the River Erewash overtopped its banks; the works' operations were disrupted and impacts were resolved a few days later, after which normal operations resumed. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Hallam Fields Sewage Treatment Works,England,"Impacted when the River Erewash overtopped its banks; the works' operations were disrupted and impacts were resolved a few days later, after which normal operations resumed. (p12)",,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_7_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-7-trent-and-lower-erewash-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-LAN,24,2020-08-04,54.0145848,-2.8059849,"<div id=""html_6ade9052dc7a155d333003e67e28e65d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Burrow Beck</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flows in Burrow Beck increased rapidly during heavy overnight rainfall and, aided by a series of channel obstructions, the river overflowed its banks. The overflow carried water onto Lentworth Road and into nearby homes. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overflowed its banks near Lancaster (reported as due to an obstruction), causing a localised flooding incident close to Hala. Multiple properties were flooded and emergency services evacuated residents and undertook pumping to reduce water levels; road closures were put in place. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The main river Burrow Beck was carrying high volumes of storm water and its channel was obstructed by excessive debris downstream of a local pedestrian footbridge. The river flowed out of bank, across open grass and onto Lentworth Drive before entering nearby residential premises. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On the night of 4&ndash;5 August 2020 an extremely heavy deluge overwhelmed the capacity of Burrow Beck. The river's channel capacity had been temporarily reduced by a collection of loose debris and, combined with very high flows, the river overflowed its banks and discharged into Lentworth Drive, causing flooding to nearby residential properties. Obstructions were urgently removed to restore flow. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse at the location of the flooding incident; its conveyance function and maintenance were central to the event. The report highlights the need to respect channel capacity and avoid obstruction by loose debris, and describes Environment Agency maintenance activity on the channel in the reach involved in the incident. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 multi&ndash;storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; around 50 people (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 residential internal properties; 3 residential external properties (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2.6 km maintained section (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Burrow Beck,England,"Flows in Burrow Beck increased rapidly during heavy overnight rainfall and, aided by a series of channel obstructions, the river overflowed its banks. The overflow carried water onto Lentworth Road and into nearby homes. (p3)
Overflowed its banks near Lancaster (reported as due to an obstruction), causing a localised flooding incident close to Hala. Multiple properties were flooded and emergency services evacuated residents and undertook pumping to reduce water levels; road closures were put in place. (p5)
The main river Burrow Beck was carrying high volumes of storm water and its channel was obstructed by excessive debris downstream of a local pedestrian footbridge. The river flowed out of bank, across open grass and onto Lentworth Drive before entering nearby residential premises. (p6)
On the night of 4–5 August 2020 an extremely heavy deluge overwhelmed the capacity of Burrow Beck. The river's channel capacity had been temporarily reduced by a collection of loose debris and, combined with very high flows, the river overflowed its banks and discharged into Lentworth Drive, causing flooding to nearby residential properties. Obstructions were urgently removed to restore flow. (p9)
The watercourse at the location of the flooding incident; its conveyance function and maintenance were central to the event. The report highlights the need to respect channel capacity and avoid obstruction by loose debris, and describes Environment Agency maintenance activity on the channel in the reach involved in the incident. (p10)","2 multi–storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; around 50 people (p5)
10 residential internal properties; 3 residential external properties (p6)
2.6 km maintained section (p10)",GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04.html,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04,Lancaster flooding 04 Aug 2020 - 05 Aug 2020,"4/5 August 2020 Flooding In Lancashire: Lentworth Drive, Lancaster",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-lentworth-drive-lancaster-august-2020.pdf
GB-LAN,24,2020-08-04,54.02993,-2.7929816,"<div id=""html_50b94d978b46ae3c5f8907124cafea89"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lentworth Drive, Bailrigg</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Lentworth Drive in Lancaster was impacted by the flooding of 4/5 August 2020 and is the subject location of the Section 19 investigation. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following the river overflow, a temporary bund was installed along the boundary between the Lentworth Drive carriageway and the adjacent open land to provide a buffer against further river flooding; a permanent bund was later installed by the Environment Agency (2023). (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes on Lentworth Drive were flooded overnight as a result of intense rainfall on 4&ndash;5 August 2020. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Burrow Beck overtopped/overflowed in the area between Newlands Avenue, Lentworth Drive and Whinfell Drive, causing localised inundation of nearby properties. Firefighters assisted moving ground&ndash;floor residents to safety and pumping efforts were undertaken; evacuations included residents from a care home to a temporary rest centre. Road closures were put in place and multi&ndash;agency response worked on reducing water levels; no injuries reported. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from Burrow Beck flowed out of bank and across open ground onto Lentworth Drive and then entered nearby residential premises. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Burrow Beck overtopped its banks after an extreme deluge and, with channel capacity reduced by accumulated debris, flooded into residential properties on Lenthworth Drive; properties showed water marks and some subsidence and a temporary evacuation of residents was required. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwaters from Burrow Beck overflowed into Lentworth Drive on the night of 4&ndash;5 August 2020 and entered local residential properties, resulting in the temporary evacuation of residents. Afterwards, obstructions were removed and a permanent bund was constructed east of Lentworth Drive to provide future protection. [IMG] (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 multi&ndash;storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; 50 people (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>29 residents evacuated [IMG] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Lentworth Drive, Bailrigg",England,"Lentworth Drive in Lancaster was impacted by the flooding of 4/5 August 2020 and is the subject location of the Section 19 investigation. (p1)
Following the river overflow, a temporary bund was installed along the boundary between the Lentworth Drive carriageway and the adjacent open land to provide a buffer against further river flooding; a permanent bund was later installed by the Environment Agency (2023). (p3)
Homes on Lentworth Drive were flooded overnight as a result of intense rainfall on 4–5 August 2020. (p4)
Burrow Beck overtopped/overflowed in the area between Newlands Avenue, Lentworth Drive and Whinfell Drive, causing localised inundation of nearby properties. Firefighters assisted moving ground–floor residents to safety and pumping efforts were undertaken; evacuations included residents from a care home to a temporary rest centre. Road closures were put in place and multi–agency response worked on reducing water levels; no injuries reported. (p5)
Floodwater from Burrow Beck flowed out of bank and across open ground onto Lentworth Drive and then entered nearby residential premises. (p6)
Burrow Beck overtopped its banks after an extreme deluge and, with channel capacity reduced by accumulated debris, flooded into residential properties on Lenthworth Drive; properties showed water marks and some subsidence and a temporary evacuation of residents was required. [IMG] (p8)
Floodwaters from Burrow Beck overflowed into Lentworth Drive on the night of 4–5 August 2020 and entered local residential properties, resulting in the temporary evacuation of residents. Afterwards, obstructions were removed and a permanent bund was constructed east of Lentworth Drive to provide future protection. [IMG] (p9)","2 multi–storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; 50 people (p5)
29 residents evacuated [IMG] (p8)",GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04.html,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04,Lancaster flooding 04 Aug 2020 - 05 Aug 2020,"4/5 August 2020 Flooding In Lancashire: Lentworth Drive, Lancaster",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-lentworth-drive-lancaster-august-2020.pdf
GB-LAN,24,2020-08-04,54.0339192,-2.7842265,"<div id=""html_e0b400ae69665b228d73f64407c2e194"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Newlands Avenue, Bowerham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Burrow Beck overtopped/overflowed in the area between Newlands Avenue, Lentworth Drive and Whinfell Drive, causing localised inundation of nearby properties. Firefighters assisted moving ground&ndash;floor residents to safety and pumping efforts were undertaken; evacuations included residents from a care home to a temporary rest centre. Road closures were put in place and multi&ndash;agency response worked on reducing water levels; no injuries reported. (p5)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 multi&ndash;storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; 50 people (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Newlands Avenue, Bowerham",England,"Burrow Beck overtopped/overflowed in the area between Newlands Avenue, Lentworth Drive and Whinfell Drive, causing localised inundation of nearby properties. Firefighters assisted moving ground–floor residents to safety and pumping efforts were undertaken; evacuations included residents from a care home to a temporary rest centre. Road closures were put in place and multi–agency response worked on reducing water levels; no injuries reported. (p5)",2 multi–storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; 50 people (p5),GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04.html,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04,Lancaster flooding 04 Aug 2020 - 05 Aug 2020,"4/5 August 2020 Flooding In Lancashire: Lentworth Drive, Lancaster",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-lentworth-drive-lancaster-august-2020.pdf
GB-LAN,24,2020-08-04,54.0250037,-2.7931536,"<div id=""html_60892b15e7d00c25d032179ad36c8628"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whinfell Drive, Hala</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Burrow Beck overtopped/overflowed in the area between Newlands Avenue, Lentworth Drive and Whinfell Drive, causing localised inundation of nearby properties. Firefighters assisted moving ground&ndash;floor residents to safety and pumping efforts were undertaken; evacuations included residents from a care home to a temporary rest centre. Road closures were put in place and multi&ndash;agency response worked on reducing water levels; no injuries reported. (p5)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 multi&ndash;storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; 50 people (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Whinfell Drive, Hala",England,"Burrow Beck overtopped/overflowed in the area between Newlands Avenue, Lentworth Drive and Whinfell Drive, causing localised inundation of nearby properties. Firefighters assisted moving ground–floor residents to safety and pumping efforts were undertaken; evacuations included residents from a care home to a temporary rest centre. Road closures were put in place and multi–agency response worked on reducing water levels; no injuries reported. (p5)",2 multi–storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; 50 people (p5),GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04.html,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04,Lancaster flooding 04 Aug 2020 - 05 Aug 2020,"4/5 August 2020 Flooding In Lancashire: Lentworth Drive, Lancaster",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-lentworth-drive-lancaster-august-2020.pdf
