GB-LAN,24,2020-08-04,53.89728410091331,-2.903724352506046,"<div id=""html_77606cf32de781651584d0e55f1c1e31"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wyre</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding affected a residential property in the Wyre district during the storm event. [TAB] (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential external property [TAB] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Wyre,England,External flooding affected a residential property in the Wyre district during the storm event. [TAB] (p6),1 residential external property [TAB] (p6),GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04.html,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04,Lancaster flooding 04 Aug 2020 - 05 Aug 2020,"4/5 August 2020 Flooding In Lancashire: Lentworth Drive, Lancaster",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-lentworth-drive-lancaster-august-2020.pdf
GB-LAN,24,2020-08-04,54.04674035288858,-2.8001777457545383,"<div id=""html_4f008dd66e837b8904861183a7760f0a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancaster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Lancaster experienced flooding during the 4/5 August 2020 event (subject of the Section 19 investigation). (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy overnight rainfall in the Lancaster area caused Burrow Beck to rise and overflow in the south Lancaster area, with floodwater reaching Lentworth Road and entering a number of homes overnight. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes in Lancaster (specifically at Lentworth Drive) were flooded overnight on 4&ndash;5 August 2020. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Serious localised flooding overnight 4&ndash;5 August 2020 at Hala in South Lancaster close to Burrow Beck. Residents (including from a care home) were evacuated to a temporary rest centre; firefighters assisted moving ground&ndash;floor residents to safety; pumping and other measures were used to control water levels; road closures were in place. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overnight from 4&ndash;5 August 2020 properties in Lancaster district were affected by flooding driven by river overflow. Reported impacts include internal flooding of residential properties and flooding of a care home resulting in displaced residents. [TAB] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Within Lancaster, Burrow Beck was overwhelmed by an extremely heavy deluge on 4&ndash;5 August 2020; the ensuing river overflow caused localised flooding into Lentworth Drive and affected nearby residential properties. (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 multi&ndash;storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; around 50 people (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 residential internal properties; 3 residential external properties; 1 care home [TAB] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancaster,England,"Lancaster experienced flooding during the 4/5 August 2020 event (subject of the Section 19 investigation). (p1)
Heavy overnight rainfall in the Lancaster area caused Burrow Beck to rise and overflow in the south Lancaster area, with floodwater reaching Lentworth Road and entering a number of homes overnight. (p3)
Homes in Lancaster (specifically at Lentworth Drive) were flooded overnight on 4–5 August 2020. (p4)
Serious localised flooding overnight 4–5 August 2020 at Hala in South Lancaster close to Burrow Beck. Residents (including from a care home) were evacuated to a temporary rest centre; firefighters assisted moving ground–floor residents to safety; pumping and other measures were used to control water levels; road closures were in place. (p5)
Overnight from 4–5 August 2020 properties in Lancaster district were affected by flooding driven by river overflow. Reported impacts include internal flooding of residential properties and flooding of a care home resulting in displaced residents. [TAB] (p6)
Within Lancaster, Burrow Beck was overwhelmed by an extremely heavy deluge on 4–5 August 2020; the ensuing river overflow caused localised flooding into Lentworth Drive and affected nearby residential properties. (p9)","2 multi–storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; around 50 people (p5)
10 residential internal properties; 3 residential external properties; 1 care home [TAB] (p6)",GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04.html,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04,Lancaster flooding 04 Aug 2020 - 05 Aug 2020,"4/5 August 2020 Flooding In Lancashire: Lentworth Drive, Lancaster",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-lentworth-drive-lancaster-august-2020.pdf
GB-LAN,24,2020-08-04,54.0171572,-2.7876979,"<div id=""html_458421ecbe1c09eddcfafce34b4e2aa6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bailrigg</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Obstructions in the river channel through Bailrigg contributed to raised water levels in Burrow Beck which led to the river overflowing its banks and transporting floodwater towards Lentworth Road and residential areas. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Bailrigg,England,Obstructions in the river channel through Bailrigg contributed to raised water levels in Burrow Beck which led to the river overflowing its banks and transporting floodwater towards Lentworth Road and residential areas. (p3),,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04.html,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04,Lancaster flooding 04 Aug 2020 - 05 Aug 2020,"4/5 August 2020 Flooding In Lancashire: Lentworth Drive, Lancaster",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-lentworth-drive-lancaster-august-2020.pdf
GB-LAN,24,2020-08-04,54.031399,-2.7955641,"<div id=""html_533ff9eb9d69f4a133e0ca3e13b1469f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Scotforth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Channel obstructions in the Scotforth area contributed to elevated levels in Burrow Beck, which overflowed its banks during the heavy rainfall, leading to floodwater moving onto nearby roads and properties. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Scotforth,England,"Channel obstructions in the Scotforth area contributed to elevated levels in Burrow Beck, which overflowed its banks during the heavy rainfall, leading to floodwater moving onto nearby roads and properties. (p3)",,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04.html,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04,Lancaster flooding 04 Aug 2020 - 05 Aug 2020,"4/5 August 2020 Flooding In Lancashire: Lentworth Drive, Lancaster",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-lentworth-drive-lancaster-august-2020.pdf
GB-LAN,24,2020-08-04,54.0263794,-2.7881128,"<div id=""html_6eabe77f9a7516f00fea2e6d40c3ac0b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hala</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Obstructions in the river channel through Hala formed part of the cumulative blockage that raised Burrow Beck's water level and caused it to overflow, sending floodwater towards Lentworth Road and adjacent homes. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Serious flooding near Burrow Beck (overnight 4&ndash;5 Aug 2020) caused evacuation of care home residents to a rest centre; multiple properties flooded; road closures and pumping operations were undertaken; no injuries reported. (p5)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 multi&ndash;storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; around 50 people (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Hala,England,"Obstructions in the river channel through Hala formed part of the cumulative blockage that raised Burrow Beck's water level and caused it to overflow, sending floodwater towards Lentworth Road and adjacent homes. (p3)
Serious flooding near Burrow Beck (overnight 4–5 Aug 2020) caused evacuation of care home residents to a rest centre; multiple properties flooded; road closures and pumping operations were undertaken; no injuries reported. (p5)",2 multi–storey residential properties; 10 domestic properties; around 50 people (p5),GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04.html,GB-LAN_24_2020-08-04,Lancaster flooding 04 Aug 2020 - 05 Aug 2020,"4/5 August 2020 Flooding In Lancashire: Lentworth Drive, Lancaster",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-lentworth-drive-lancaster-august-2020.pdf
GB-HEF,14,2020-02-16,52.2355219,-2.7449348,"<div id=""html_f8a00d5f164bdad8589e550f813e8a80"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Lugg</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Backwater effects from the River Lugg likely increased fluvial flood levels in the vicinity of Moreton on Lugg, contributing to internal flooding of nearby properties; at least one property on the east side experienced internal foul (sewage) flooding when drains backed up. Surface&ndash;water from a small tributary close to the east&ndash;side property also likely contributed and was mapped on the Surface Water Flood Map. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Lugg is identified as the source of fluvial flood risk affecting the area. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Five properties reported internal flooding in Moreton on Lugg during the February 2020 event; the report table records 6 internally flooded properties related to the key flood event. [TAB] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,River Lugg,England,"Backwater effects from the River Lugg likely increased fluvial flood levels in the vicinity of Moreton on Lugg, contributing to internal flooding of nearby properties; at least one property on the east side experienced internal foul (sewage) flooding when drains backed up. Surface–water from a small tributary close to the east–side property also likely contributed and was mapped on the Surface Water Flood Map. [TAB] (p2)
The River Lugg is identified as the source of fluvial flood risk affecting the area. (p3)",Five properties reported internal flooding in Moreton on Lugg during the February 2020 event; the report table records 6 internally flooded properties related to the key flood event. [TAB] (p2),GB-HEF_14_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_14_2020-02-16,Moreton On Lugg flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Moreton On Lugg,055/Herefordshire County/13/Moreton/on/Lugg.pdf
GB-HEF,14,2020-02-16,52.107369,-2.7251963,"<div id=""html_0d2bbf6ff1e37d6eee1f55818f05a56b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Moreton On Lugg</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of domestic properties occurred during the event: internal flood depths recorded between 6 inches and 3 ft. One home on the east side of the village was surrounded by floodwater and experienced internal foul (sewage) flooding when drains backed up into the property and garden. Flood risk from a small local watercourse and surface water may also have contributed. (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Five properties reported internal flooding in Moreton on Lugg during February 2020; report table records 6 internally flooded properties; internal depths recorded between 6 inches and 3 ft; one property had a previous flood in July 2007. (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Moreton On Lugg,England,Internal flooding of domestic properties occurred during the event: internal flood depths recorded between 6 inches and 3 ft. One home on the east side of the village was surrounded by floodwater and experienced internal foul (sewage) flooding when drains backed up into the property and garden. Flood risk from a small local watercourse and surface water may also have contributed. (p2),Five properties reported internal flooding in Moreton on Lugg during February 2020; report table records 6 internally flooded properties; internal depths recorded between 6 inches and 3 ft; one property had a previous flood in July 2007. (p2),GB-HEF_14_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_14_2020-02-16,Moreton On Lugg flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Moreton On Lugg,055/Herefordshire County/13/Moreton/on/Lugg.pdf
GB-BCP,4,2020-08-13,50.7435602,-1.7141291,"<div id=""html_217705a25ae0fa9be58f6e847b97f808"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Highcliffe and Walkford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The intense, localised thunderstorm principally affected Walkford and Highcliffe, producing surface water / flash flooding incidents in the area (part of the wider Christchurch impacts such as business internal flooding, garden flooding and short&ndash;lived road flooding). (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one residential property (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Highcliffe and Walkford,England,"The intense, localised thunderstorm principally affected Walkford and Highcliffe, producing surface water / flash flooding incidents in the area (part of the wider Christchurch impacts such as business internal flooding, garden flooding and short–lived road flooding). (p3)",one residential property (p3),GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13.html,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13,Christchurch flooding 13 Aug 2020,Flooding in the Christchurch Area 13th August 2020: Section 19 Report,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2020/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-13th-August-2020-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,4,2020-08-13,50.72036885518821,-1.7891038858510526,"<div id=""html_19b89db26d6885241abbb24ce44e3990"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>East Southbourne and Tuckton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The storm drifted westwards into Southbourne and Tuckton after peaking over Christchurch, contributing to localised surface water flooding and associated sewer/drain surcharge as the storm moved through these neighbourhoods on 13 August 2020. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",East Southbourne and Tuckton,England,"The storm drifted westwards into Southbourne and Tuckton after peaking over Christchurch, contributing to localised surface water flooding and associated sewer/drain surcharge as the storm moved through these neighbourhoods on 13 August 2020. (p9)",,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13.html,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13,Christchurch flooding 13 Aug 2020,Flooding in the Christchurch Area 13th August 2020: Section 19 Report,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2020/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-13th-August-2020-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,4,2020-08-13,50.7274579,-1.7611768,"<div id=""html_1dd2dc3d1eb8c188812980e35a533b8e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stanpit Marsh</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area affected by the Purewell stream flooding incident. Investigation uncovered a previously unrecorded tidal flap valve at the outfall that was found defective; although the flap valve was not relevant to the 13 Aug event (outfall was not tide&ndash;locked), it was identified as defective and repairs were underway in Dec 2020. (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Stanpit Marsh,England,"Area affected by the Purewell stream flooding incident. Investigation uncovered a previously unrecorded tidal flap valve at the outfall that was found defective; although the flap valve was not relevant to the 13 Aug event (outfall was not tide–locked), it was identified as defective and repairs were underway in Dec 2020. (p21)",,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13.html,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13,Christchurch flooding 13 Aug 2020,Flooding in the Christchurch Area 13th August 2020: Section 19 Report,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2020/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-13th-August-2020-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,4,2020-08-13,50.9025349,-1.404189,"<div id=""html_e629de4e340f79949aa774adca988088"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Southampton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Radar panels for 13 August 2020 show persistent very intense convective rainfall in the area near Southampton (magenta/pink colours indicating &gt;16 mm/hr) between 13:00 and 13:30. Such intense short&ndash;duration rainfall is a known driver of surface&ndash;water and flash flooding and would increase local flood risk during that timeframe (the radar was used as part of the investigation into local flooding). [IMG] (p25)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Southampton,England,Radar panels for 13 August 2020 show persistent very intense convective rainfall in the area near Southampton (magenta/pink colours indicating >16 mm/hr) between 13:00 and 13:30. Such intense short–duration rainfall is a known driver of surface–water and flash flooding and would increase local flood risk during that timeframe (the radar was used as part of the investigation into local flooding). [IMG] (p25),,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13.html,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13,Christchurch flooding 13 Aug 2020,Flooding in the Christchurch Area 13th August 2020: Section 19 Report,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2020/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-13th-August-2020-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,4,2020-08-13,50.800031,-1.0906023,"<div id=""html_5e0f692cdf05ca21a90bedc88ae4a4f4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Portsmouth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Radar images for 13 August 2020 show persistent very intense convective rainfall in the area near Portsmouth (magenta/pink colours) at 13:00&ndash;13:30. This short&ndash;lived intense rainfall is capable of producing surface&ndash;water/flash flooding and is therefore relevant to local flood investigations. [IMG] (p25)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Portsmouth,England,Radar images for 13 August 2020 show persistent very intense convective rainfall in the area near Portsmouth (magenta/pink colours) at 13:00–13:30. This short–lived intense rainfall is capable of producing surface–water/flash flooding and is therefore relevant to local flood investigations. [IMG] (p25),,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13.html,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13,Christchurch flooding 13 Aug 2020,Flooding in the Christchurch Area 13th August 2020: Section 19 Report,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2020/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-13th-August-2020-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,4,2020-08-13,50.743015022883824,-1.7408614159312075,"<div id=""html_f2667de67964abfc2d227c60882a1e66"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Somerford Roundabout</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Wessex Water foul sewage pumping station just south of the Somerford Roundabout was overwhelmed, resulting in sewerage flooding in that area. The sewer flooding was part of the incident on 13 Aug 2020; Wessex Water were notified on 21 Aug and attended the site. (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Somerford Roundabout,England,"The Wessex Water foul sewage pumping station just south of the Somerford Roundabout was overwhelmed, resulting in sewerage flooding in that area. The sewer flooding was part of the incident on 13 Aug 2020; Wessex Water were notified on 21 Aug and attended the site. (p21)",,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13.html,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13,Christchurch flooding 13 Aug 2020,Flooding in the Christchurch Area 13th August 2020: Section 19 Report,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2020/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-13th-August-2020-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,4,2020-08-13,50.7429051,-1.8028742,"<div id=""html_40212eedc1cca9da8d3d7866b54f19e6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Barrack Road, Christchurch</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Barrack Road was inundated with standing water; vehicles drove through the water (causing splashing) and normal traffic flow was impeded; pedestrians observed the flooded street from the sidewalk. [IMG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Standing water covered the full width of the road at the intersection, partially submerging vehicle tyres and causing slowed/congested traffic as vehicles attempted to drive through the inundation. [IMG] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Barrack Road, Christchurch",England,"Barrack Road was inundated with standing water; vehicles drove through the water (causing splashing) and normal traffic flow was impeded; pedestrians observed the flooded street from the sidewalk. [IMG] (p1)
Standing water covered the full width of the road at the intersection, partially submerging vehicle tyres and causing slowed/congested traffic as vehicles attempted to drive through the inundation. [IMG] (p16)",,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13.html,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13,Christchurch flooding 13 Aug 2020,Flooding in the Christchurch Area 13th August 2020: Section 19 Report,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2020/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-13th-August-2020-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,4,2020-08-13,50.7417518,-1.7430889,"<div id=""html_35796af610cf907b3bb96f96e66cdedb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Somerford Road, Christchurch</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Businesses on Somerford Road experienced internal flooding; records show internal inundation of commercial premises. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>four records of internal flooding of businesses (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Somerford Road, Christchurch",England,Businesses on Somerford Road experienced internal flooding; records show internal inundation of commercial premises. (p14),four records of internal flooding of businesses (p14),GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13.html,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13,Christchurch flooding 13 Aug 2020,Flooding in the Christchurch Area 13th August 2020: Section 19 Report,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2020/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-13th-August-2020-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,4,2020-08-13,50.7342188,-1.7735679,"<div id=""html_30e6b53edcda25162fb62f54f5ec378b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bridge Street, Christchurch</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road surface was inundated with standing water, disrupting traffic flow and forcing vehicles to proceed cautiously through flooded conditions. [IMG] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Bridge Street, Christchurch",England,"Road surface was inundated with standing water, disrupting traffic flow and forcing vehicles to proceed cautiously through flooded conditions. [IMG] (p16)",,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13.html,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13,Christchurch flooding 13 Aug 2020,Flooding in the Christchurch Area 13th August 2020: Section 19 Report,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2020/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-13th-August-2020-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,4,2020-08-13,50.73476619269939,-1.7714663074694084,"<div id=""html_d7c9c7789ce641d08a0a7df295669cd4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bridge Street, Christchurch</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Street heavily flooded such that a yellow bus was driving through deep standing water; urban transport was disrupted and the road surface was inundated across the visible carriageway. (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Bridge Street, Christchurch",England,Street heavily flooded such that a yellow bus was driving through deep standing water; urban transport was disrupted and the road surface was inundated across the visible carriageway. (p16),,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13.html,GB-BCP_4_2020-08-13,Christchurch flooding 13 Aug 2020,Flooding in the Christchurch Area 13th August 2020: Section 19 Report,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2020/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-13th-August-2020-Final.pdf"
