GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,50.79511975,-2.5993664646317165,"<div id=""html_895bb7ebd80bfe82ac0dd7bfb8509402"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Dorset</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>West Dorset received the higher rainfall totals during the event causing many watercourses to react quickly and river levels to rise sharply (with two heavier periods late on 6 July and during 7 July). (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood Alert issued for West Dorset Rivers and Streams on 06/07/2012 (19:07) as part of the July 2012 flooding sequence. [TAB,PAG] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,West Dorset,England,"West Dorset received the higher rainfall totals during the event causing many watercourses to react quickly and river levels to rise sharply (with two heavier periods late on 6 July and during 7 July). (p12)
Flood Alert issued for West Dorset Rivers and Streams on 06/07/2012 (19:07) as part of the July 2012 flooding sequence. [TAB,PAG] (p16)",,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06.html,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06,Dorset flooding 06 Jul 2012 - 13 Jul 2012,Dorset County Council July 2012 Flood Investigation Report,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/July 2012 Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,50.62229,-2.4616947,"<div id=""html_b43b80996dbf4478416ebbe467b0236d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Radipole Lake</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding affected properties east of Radipole Lake, with 3 properties flooded in that area (Weymouth). [TAB] (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties [TAB] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,Radipole Lake,England,"Internal flooding affected properties east of Radipole Lake, with 3 properties flooded in that area (Weymouth). [TAB] (p24)",3 properties [TAB] (p24),GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06.html,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06,Dorset flooding 06 Jul 2012 - 13 Jul 2012,Dorset County Council July 2012 Flood Investigation Report,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/July 2012 Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,50.85353494531873,-2.435877886832601,"<div id=""html_9f6e90f9f9f61e793cff22c181e3be45"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Duntish</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties with inundation of internal rooms and flood damage. [TAB] (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [TAB] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,Duntish,England,Internal flooding of properties with inundation of internal rooms and flood damage. [TAB] (p24),1 property [TAB] (p24),GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06.html,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06,Dorset flooding 06 Jul 2012 - 13 Jul 2012,Dorset County Council July 2012 Flood Investigation Report,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/July 2012 Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,50.6991691,-1.9810698,"<div id=""html_4d64a3453f307f6da8fc782c3657f9a4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Poole Harbour</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency Flood Alert issued for Poole Harbour (07/07/2012) and a Flood Warning entry references Poole Harbour at Wareham, indicating flooding risk at Poole Harbour during the period. [TAB] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,Poole Harbour,England,"Environment Agency Flood Alert issued for Poole Harbour (07/07/2012) and a Flood Warning entry references Poole Harbour at Wareham, indicating flooding risk at Poole Harbour during the period. [TAB] (p16)",,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06.html,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06,Dorset flooding 06 Jul 2012 - 13 Jul 2012,Dorset County Council July 2012 Flood Investigation Report,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/July 2012 Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,51.5249085,-2.4867587,"<div id=""html_f36f2686fa2a3596912a5600fb3a2cc6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Frome</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Larger catchments were affected as flood waters passed through the river system on the Rivers Frome (and Stour), contributing to flooding of downstream areas during the days after the initial torrential rain. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High water levels in the River Frome prevented local surface water drainage from discharging to the river, leading to internal flooding in Maiden Newton (Dorchester Road and Whitehall) and contributing to overwhelmed local drainage. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High water levels in the River Frome prevented surface water from discharging into the river, causing river&ndash;related flooding in Maiden Newton and contributing to internal property flooding. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>19 properties (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Contributed to the 19 properties flooded in Maiden Newton; flood depths in Maiden Newton between 70 mm and 700 mm (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,River Frome,England,"Larger catchments were affected as flood waters passed through the river system on the Rivers Frome (and Stour), contributing to flooding of downstream areas during the days after the initial torrential rain. (p2)
High water levels in the River Frome prevented local surface water drainage from discharging to the river, leading to internal flooding in Maiden Newton (Dorchester Road and Whitehall) and contributing to overwhelmed local drainage. (p18)
High water levels in the River Frome prevented surface water from discharging into the river, causing river–related flooding in Maiden Newton and contributing to internal property flooding. (p19)","19 properties (p18)
Contributed to the 19 properties flooded in Maiden Newton; flood depths in Maiden Newton between 70 mm and 700 mm (p19)",GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06.html,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06,Dorset flooding 06 Jul 2012 - 13 Jul 2012,Dorset County Council July 2012 Flood Investigation Report,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/July 2012 Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,50.8686148,-2.1714127,"<div id=""html_8df1975cda59d64789359c4a2e94ec0e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Stour</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Large catchment flows passed through the River Stour during the event; peak flow passed through Bournemouth in the early hours of 10th July which marked the end of the main impact. Rising river levels on the Lower Stour triggered an emergency response and local evacuations. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood Warning remained in force on the River Stour; continuing flood risk from the Stour increased the river flood risk to MEDIUM on 9 July with significant disruption expected that day. River levels began to peak around 10 July, reducing risk thereafter. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,River Stour,England,"Large catchment flows passed through the River Stour during the event; peak flow passed through Bournemouth in the early hours of 10th July which marked the end of the main impact. Rising river levels on the Lower Stour triggered an emergency response and local evacuations. (p2)
Flood Warning remained in force on the River Stour; continuing flood risk from the Stour increased the river flood risk to MEDIUM on 9 July with significant disruption expected that day. River levels began to peak around 10 July, reducing risk thereafter. (p9)",,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06.html,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06,Dorset flooding 06 Jul 2012 - 13 Jul 2012,Dorset County Council July 2012 Flood Investigation Report,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/July 2012 Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,50.6903411,-2.4545215,"<div id=""html_6ee10e74dd3e9116926061926f046f1d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River South Winterbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water and rising groundwater caused flooding along the South Winterbourne, inundating properties and leading to elevated levels that persisted for around two weeks and to road closures. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The South Winterbourne watercourse was unable to cope with the high rate of surface water input, leading to overflow and contributing to flooding of adjacent properties and transport routes. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding along the South Winterbourne affected adjacent communities and drainage mechanisms; a consultant review was recommended to identify flooding mechanisms and measures to reduce flood impacts. [TAB] (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>More than 40 properties (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>42 properties (combined across Winterbourne Abbas, Winterbourne Steepleton and Martinstown) (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,River South Winterbourne,England,"Surface water and rising groundwater caused flooding along the South Winterbourne, inundating properties and leading to elevated levels that persisted for around two weeks and to road closures. (p2)
The South Winterbourne watercourse was unable to cope with the high rate of surface water input, leading to overflow and contributing to flooding of adjacent properties and transport routes. (p19)
Flooding along the South Winterbourne affected adjacent communities and drainage mechanisms; a consultant review was recommended to identify flooding mechanisms and measures to reduce flood impacts. [TAB] (p22)","More than 40 properties (p2)
42 properties (combined across Winterbourne Abbas, Winterbourne Steepleton and Martinstown) (p19)",GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06.html,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06,Dorset flooding 06 Jul 2012 - 13 Jul 2012,Dorset County Council July 2012 Flood Investigation Report,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/July 2012 Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,50.7457796,-2.8755932,"<div id=""html_aac172eb7bcb5c0c56460de81d8d8cc2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Char</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Char rose sharply following the intense rainfall, indicating rapid river level increases and flooding potential. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,River Char,England,"The River Char rose sharply following the intense rainfall, indicating rapid river level increases and flooding potential. (p12)",,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06.html,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06,Dorset flooding 06 Jul 2012 - 13 Jul 2012,Dorset County Council July 2012 Flood Investigation Report,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/July 2012 Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,50.7654174,-2.7442265,"<div id=""html_1696ca51ee5ed2e010737de64dbcc235"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Brit</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Brit rose sharply in response to the heavy rainfall, producing rapid increases in river levels. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,River Brit,England,"The River Brit rose sharply in response to the heavy rainfall, producing rapid increases in river levels. (p12)",,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06.html,GB-DOR_4_2012-07-06,Dorset flooding 06 Jul 2012 - 13 Jul 2012,Dorset County Council July 2012 Flood Investigation Report,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/July 2012 Flood Investigation Report.pdf
