GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,50.70915958098221,-2.533455946001463,"<div id=""html_b9e078aeb656f52cedbb13569a85e4c7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Winterbourne Steepleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties along the South Winterbourne (which flows through Winterbourne Steepleton) were flooded by surface runoff and rising groundwater; high groundwater levels also led to road closures. [MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extensive prolonged flooding (up to two weeks) caused by surface water input overwhelming the local watercourse and by groundwater entering properties directly; internal flood depths up to 150mm and external depths up to 500mm. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced surface water infiltration into the sewer network (contributing to sewer flooding issues); recommended investigations include assessing infiltration and potential manhole raising to reduce future flood/sewer interactions. [TAB,PAG] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water infiltration into the sewerage network was identified at Winterbourne Steepleton during the event; investigation and mitigation (including potential manhole raising in nearby fields) were recommended. (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties with water entering buildings. [TAB] (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than 40 properties (across the South Winterbourne through Winterbourne Abbas, Winterbourne Steepleton and Martinstown) [MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>42 properties (combined across Winterbourne Abbas, Winterbourne Steepleton and Martinstown); internal depths up to 150mm; external depths up to 500mm (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties [TAB] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,Winterbourne Steepleton,England,"Properties along the South Winterbourne (which flows through Winterbourne Steepleton) were flooded by surface runoff and rising groundwater; high groundwater levels also led to road closures. [MUL] (p2)
