GB-DOR,4,2012-07-06,50.6993004,-2.4995713,"<div id=""html_f950392e173c5cb3951fea7552e23da8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Martinstown</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties along the South Winterbourne (which flows through Martinstown) were flooded by surface runoff and rising groundwater; high groundwater levels also led to road closures. [MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties experienced internal flooding from initial high surface water flows overwhelming the local watercourse, with the main impacts from groundwater entering properties and prolonged inundation. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced surface water infiltration to the sewer network contributing to flooding; recommended investigations include assessing infiltration and considering manhole raising to nearby fields to mitigate future impacts. [TAB,PAG] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water infiltration to the sewerage network was identified at Martinstown during the event; investigation and mitigation measures were recommended. (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties; recorded internal flooding incidents affecting the community. [TAB] (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than 40 properties (across the South Winterbourne through Winterbourne Abbas, Winterbourne Steepleton and Martinstown) [MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>42 properties (combined across Winterbourne Abbas, Winterbourne Steepleton and Martinstown); internal depths up to 150mm; external depths up to 500mm (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>20 properties [TAB] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,Martinstown,England,"Properties along the South Winterbourne (which flows through Martinstown) were flooded by surface runoff and rising groundwater; high groundwater levels also led to road closures. [MUL] (p2)
