GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4464556,-1.9200958,"<div id=""html_fd60456a5732f67ecd583ada5b69afab"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oakfield Road, Metchley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One incident of internal property flooding occurred on Oakfield Road during the storm; gardens and the highway on/adjacent to Oakfield Road were also flooded. The flood route started at a breach at Oakfield Road & Garfield Road and flowed east along Oakfield Road before splitting south along Garfield and an adjacent road. [IMG,PAG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from the highway catchment draining these roads followed the highway network to the low spot in Oakfield Road. During the storm water overtopped kerbs and flowed towards properties, causing property flooding where thresholds were not raised. (p31)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [IMG,PAG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Oakfield Road, Metchley",England,"One incident of internal property flooding occurred on Oakfield Road during the storm; gardens and the highway on/adjacent to Oakfield Road were also flooded. The flood route started at a breach at Oakfield Road & Garfield Road and flowed east along Oakfield Road before splitting south along Garfield and an adjacent road. [IMG,PAG] (p30)
Runoff from the highway catchment draining these roads followed the highway network to the low spot in Oakfield Road. During the storm water overtopped kerbs and flowed towards properties, causing property flooding where thresholds were not raised. (p31)","1 property [IMG,PAG] (p30)",GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
