GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4133252,-1.895126,"<div id=""html_bb419e275de862aa2ba0ea7a87802b31"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Jasmin Croft, Druids Heath</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood flow route continued eastward past Jasmin Croft along the street network; map indicates floodwater movement past this location (surface water flow). [IMG] (p100)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Jasmin Croft, Druids Heath",England,Flood flow route continued eastward past Jasmin Croft along the street network; map indicates floodwater movement past this location (surface water flow). [IMG] (p100),,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4117052,-1.888565,"<div id=""html_0f637f5fed0942afeed03952ad3702ad"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Marsham Road, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to residential properties; gardens and garages also flooded. Floodwater was conveyed via the highway to the low spot at Marsham Road, concentrating runoff into the street and properties. [IMG,PAG] (p102)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from the surrounding catchment was conveyed via the highway to the low spot at Marsham Road; water levels built up because drainage could not discharge quickly enough, overtopping kerbs and flooding into properties that lie lower than the road level. Blocked highway gullies were reported to have possibly exacerbated the flooding. (p103)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties [IMG,PAG] (p102)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Marsham Road, Birmingham",England,"Internal flooding to residential properties; gardens and garages also flooded. Floodwater was conveyed via the highway to the low spot at Marsham Road, concentrating runoff into the street and properties. [IMG,PAG] (p102)
Runoff from the surrounding catchment was conveyed via the highway to the low spot at Marsham Road; water levels built up because drainage could not discharge quickly enough, overtopping kerbs and flooding into properties that lie lower than the road level. Blocked highway gullies were reported to have possibly exacerbated the flooding. (p103)","3 properties [IMG,PAG] (p102)",GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.426361,-1.8824193,"<div id=""html_1c2f3782210f27a8faa7c6cba54062a7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ardencote Road, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the storm on 27th May 2018 three incidents of internal property flooding were reported on Ardencote Road; garden flooding was also reported. Floodwaters were from surface water runoff that followed the highway network and local topography; breach points on a nearby ordinary watercourse and the mapped flow route indicate water moving south/southeast along local streets. (p26)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Ardencote Road, Birmingham",England,During the storm on 27th May 2018 three incidents of internal property flooding were reported on Ardencote Road; garden flooding was also reported. Floodwaters were from surface water runoff that followed the highway network and local topography; breach points on a nearby ordinary watercourse and the mapped flow route indicate water moving south/southeast along local streets. (p26),3 properties (p26),GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.444233,-1.9248993,"<div id=""html_22cfbcb15fb911d296b7534e70c946da"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Serpentine Road, Metchley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from the highway catchment draining these roads followed the highway network to the low spot in Oakfield Road. During the storm water overtopped kerbs and flowed towards properties, causing property flooding where thresholds were not raised. (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Serpentine Road, Metchley",England,"Runoff from the highway catchment draining these roads followed the highway network to the low spot in Oakfield Road. During the storm water overtopped kerbs and flowed towards properties, causing property flooding where thresholds were not raised. (p31)",,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4653873,-1.8988344,"<div id=""html_8e3dcb76309acd9d6d97345838878d3f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pershore Road, Digbeth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the storm on 27 May 2018 the Bourn Brook was overwhelmed and breached, sending floodwater across Pershore Road and along road corridors into adjacent residential areas. This caused internal flooding to properties, flooding of gardens and inundation of the highway; flood flows followed mapped routes from the breach into side streets. (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the breached brook flowed across Pershore Road, inundating the carriageway and carrying water into the fronts of properties on Riverside Drive; surface water runoff was also routed along Pershore Road towards St John's Road. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Pershore Road, Digbeth",England,"During the storm on 27 May 2018 the Bourn Brook was overwhelmed and breached, sending floodwater across Pershore Road and along road corridors into adjacent residential areas. This caused internal flooding to properties, flooding of gardens and inundation of the highway; flood flows followed mapped routes from the breach into side streets. (p32)
Floodwater from the breached brook flowed across Pershore Road, inundating the carriageway and carrying water into the fronts of properties on Riverside Drive; surface water runoff was also routed along Pershore Road towards St John's Road. (p33)",,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4486916,-1.9119799,"<div id=""html_44a676ba341d01dccd08de8b7666d5af"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Riverside Drive, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed across Pershore Road into the fronts of properties fronting onto Riverside Drive, causing property flooding. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Riverside Drive, Birmingham",England,"Floodwater flowed across Pershore Road into the fronts of properties fronting onto Riverside Drive, causing property flooding. (p33)",1 property (p33),GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.44767,-1.9118026,"<div id=""html_a54e45a5bf45a0d5ff292de0d1f65066"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fourth Avenue, Kings Heath</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff was routed from St John's Road into Fourth Avenue, causing surface water flooding in the avenue. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Fourth Avenue, Kings Heath",England,"Surface water runoff was routed from St John's Road into Fourth Avenue, causing surface water flooding in the avenue. (p33)",,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.446716,-1.912448,"<div id=""html_a16005e17f918b95b7e7115cad49b1a2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Third Avenue, Kings Heath</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff routed via St John's Road continued into Third Avenue, resulting in surface water flooding there. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Third Avenue, Kings Heath",England,"Surface water runoff routed via St John's Road continued into Third Avenue, resulting in surface water flooding there. (p33)",,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4480236,-1.9113784,"<div id=""html_4b67b92f0836a2655031c1a5bb997416"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sir Johns Road, Selly Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following the flood event the remaining wall at the end of Sir Johns Road was removed and dropped kerbs were installed to allow flood water into the River Rea (alteration made in response to flooding). The location formed part of the local flood flow route. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Sir Johns Road, Selly Park",England,Following the flood event the remaining wall at the end of Sir Johns Road was removed and dropped kerbs were installed to allow flood water into the River Rea (alteration made in response to flooding). The location formed part of the local flood flow route. (p33),,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4441717,-1.9146645,"<div id=""html_7a167b93e2deea2ae0495dde9223b3ee"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pershore Avenue, Selly Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 27th May 2018 four incidents of internal property flooding occurred in Pershore Avenue; gardens were also flooded and floodwater impacted the adjacent public open space/playing field. Flooding resulted from overwhelmed sewers and drainage with water backing up from gullies into properties; river&ndash;related flows are also identified in the report and mapped flow routes show water entering the area. (p36)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Pershore Avenue, Selly Park",England,On 27th May 2018 four incidents of internal property flooding occurred in Pershore Avenue; gardens were also flooded and floodwater impacted the adjacent public open space/playing field. Flooding resulted from overwhelmed sewers and drainage with water backing up from gullies into properties; river–related flows are also identified in the report and mapped flow routes show water entering the area. (p36),4 properties (p36),GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4317803,-1.9310391,"<div id=""html_36448fa17876f1556a930b60c25e9ae1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Laburnum Road, Stirchley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the storm on 27th May 2018 one internal property flood was reported on Laburnum Road; gardens adjacent to the property were also flooded as surface water runoff ponded in the local low spot and was routed along the highway. (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from the surrounding area followed the highway topography and ponded in a low spot on Laburnum Road. Water levels rose because the drainage system could not discharge quickly enough, overtopping kerbs and flooding properties that lie lower than the road level. (p39)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property; 1 incident of internal property flooding (p38)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Laburnum Road, Stirchley",England,"During the storm on 27th May 2018 one internal property flood was reported on Laburnum Road; gardens adjacent to the property were also flooded as surface water runoff ponded in the local low spot and was routed along the highway. (p38)
Runoff from the surrounding area followed the highway topography and ponded in a low spot on Laburnum Road. Water levels rose because the drainage system could not discharge quickly enough, overtopping kerbs and flooding properties that lie lower than the road level. (p39)",1 property; 1 incident of internal property flooding (p38),GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.5199028,-1.8337282,"<div id=""html_8c97d6fdac4cb7c2e5b9b6b9c654d4f1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Spring Lane, Birmingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property experienced internal flooding; gardens and the highway were also flooded as runoff from Spring Lane and Fern Road ponded at a local low point and flowed along the highway network. [PAG] (p60)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff ponded at the low spot in Spring Lane after a large storm; highway gullies were likely at capacity so gullies were unable to discharge. Flood water overtopped dropped kerbs and flooded into lower&ndash;lying property. (p61)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [PAG] (p60)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Spring Lane, Birmingham",England,"One property experienced internal flooding; gardens and the highway were also flooded as runoff from Spring Lane and Fern Road ponded at a local low point and flowed along the highway network. [PAG] (p60)
Runoff ponded at the low spot in Spring Lane after a large storm; highway gullies were likely at capacity so gullies were unable to discharge. Flood water overtopped dropped kerbs and flooded into lower–lying property. (p61)",1 property [PAG] (p60),GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
