GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4032204,-1.8821733,"<div id=""html_65af6239400a255cdcbcf4f14592cac6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Arundel Road, Highters Heath</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal property flooding was reported in Arundel Road (one of three reported internal flooding incidents across Arundel Road and Maypole Lane). Flooding also affected the highway, footpaths and gardens in the area as runoff ponded at low points. (p72)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from the surrounding catchment followed the highway topography and ponded at a low spot in Arundel Road. Highway gullies were unable to disperse the volume of runoff; water overtopped dropped kerbs and flowed into lower&ndash;lying properties, causing internal flooding of those properties. (p73)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (total across Arundel Road and Maypole Lane) (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,"Arundel Road, Highters Heath",England,"Internal property flooding was reported in Arundel Road (one of three reported internal flooding incidents across Arundel Road and Maypole Lane). Flooding also affected the highway, footpaths and gardens in the area as runoff ponded at low points. (p72)
