GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4341996,-1.8915624,"<div id=""html_17974c1980e75dfc7c0fb923327835f4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kings Heath</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The report groups Brandwood Park Road within the Brandwood/Kings Heath area. Floodwaters from an overtopped watercourse (Dawberry Fields), surface water and highway drainage impacted the local streets and properties, with internal flooding reported on Brandwood Park Road and flooding to gardens and the highway. (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water runoff routed via the highway network ponded in a low spot within the Kings Heath/Brandwood locality, causing internal property flooding, garden inundation and highway flooding. (p46)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (combined across Newick Grove and Bryndale Avenue) (p46)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Kings Heath,England,"The report groups Brandwood Park Road within the Brandwood/Kings Heath area. Floodwaters from an overtopped watercourse (Dawberry Fields), surface water and highway drainage impacted the local streets and properties, with internal flooding reported on Brandwood Park Road and flooding to gardens and the highway. (p42)
