2 properties (combined across Newick Grove and Bryndale Avenue) (p46)",GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.52325,-1.8395109,"<div id=""html_bd6826c053f08565068407082ea29dbc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Erdington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water and sewer flooding occurred on Spring Lane within Erdington during the storm, causing one internal property flood and flooding to gardens and the highway. (p60)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p60)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Erdington,England,"Surface water and sewer flooding occurred on Spring Lane within Erdington during the storm, causing one internal property flood and flooding to gardens and the highway. (p60)",1 property (p60),GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.46264,-2.0128138,"<div id=""html_3d4f7113a9a008de826731cec9307620"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Quinton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Within the Quinton area, Amersham Close experienced surface water flooding during the storm: two properties were internally flooded and overland runoff from nearby derelict land and gardens flowed into the rear of properties following the natural topography. (p88)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p88)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Quinton,England,"Within the Quinton area, Amersham Close experienced surface water flooding during the storm: two properties were internally flooded and overland runoff from nearby derelict land and gardens flowed into the rear of properties following the natural topography. (p88)",2 properties (p88),GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-BIR,2,2018-05-27,52.4285007,-1.840403,"<div id=""html_d49d6d15de7238ecfd7c62c38ac47c59"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hall Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Cole exceeded channel capacity and overtopped, flooding surrounding land in the Hall Green area. Floodwaters inundated gardens, public open space and flowed into nearby properties (notably those on Sarehole Road). (p104)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p104)</p></div></div></body></div>",Birmingham,Hall Green,England,"The River Cole exceeded channel capacity and overtopped, flooding surrounding land in the Hall Green area. Floodwaters inundated gardens, public open space and flowed into nearby properties (notably those on Sarehole Road). (p104)",3 properties (p104),GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27.html,GB-BIR_2_2018-05-27,Birmingham flooding 27 May 2018,"May 2018 Flooding: Flood and Water Management Act, Section 19 Investigation",007/Birmingham/007/2018/Birmingham/Flooding/Section/19/Investigation///May/2018//2.0/.pdf
GB-CAM,8,2014-08-01,52.575282,-0.3898341,"<div id=""html_714ebdc6ee422899bfe68cb0a8b1cda9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church Lane, Stibbington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A property on Church Lane flooded internally after heavy rainfall caused the local drainage to surcharge; property being below road level worsened the impact. [IMG] (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [IMG] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Church Lane, Stibbington",England,A property on Church Lane flooded internally after heavy rainfall caused the local drainage to surcharge; property being below road level worsened the impact. [IMG] (p2),1 property [IMG] (p2),GB-CAM_8_2014-08-01.html,GB-CAM_8_2014-08-01,Stibbington flooding August 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Stibbington,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2014/Cambridgeshire County/Flood/Investigation/Report/Stibbington.pdf
GB-CAM,8,2014-08-01,52.5752345,-0.3966915,"<div id=""html_7bbeabc905fd4f0df2210aada5f09b91"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stibbington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property in the village (on Church Lane) experienced internal flooding due to drainage capacity being exceeded during heavy rainfall, with the property's low elevation (below road level) exacerbating flooding. [IMG] (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [IMG] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Stibbington,England,"One property in the village (on Church Lane) experienced internal flooding due to drainage capacity being exceeded during heavy rainfall, with the property's low elevation (below road level) exacerbating flooding. [IMG] (p2)",1 property [IMG] (p2),GB-CAM_8_2014-08-01.html,GB-CAM_8_2014-08-01,Stibbington flooding August 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Stibbington,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2014/Cambridgeshire County/Flood/Investigation/Report/Stibbington.pdf
GB-BPL,1,2017-11-22,53.86826595,-3.030441595597833,"<div id=""html_a77045be935a022c51863297fa2afd67"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Anchorsholme Primary Academy</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The school was subject to flooding during the event. (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Blackpool,Anchorsholme Primary Academy,England,The school was subject to flooding during the event. (p4),,GB-BPL_1_2017-11-22.html,GB-BPL_1_2017-11-22,Blackpool flooding 22 Nov 2017,Section 19 Report: Investigation into flooding on 22nd November 2017,009/Blackpool/009/2017/Blackpool/Blackpool November 2017 FINAL.pdf
GB-BPL,1,2017-11-22,53.8704426569697,-3.046015509677107,"<div id=""html_eff409045428ad28afe9b3e400e8c4b7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Anchorsholme Pumping Station</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The pumping station reached capacity during the extreme rainfall on the night of 22nd November 2017. Pumps were called into duty sequentially as flows arriving from the tunnel rose; the station operated at capacity and could not reduce tunnel levels earlier because pumping only starts once tunnel levels exceed the start height. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High flows arriving at the station triggered sequential automatic activation of pumps; on the evening of 22nd November and during 23rd November the station automatically called the remaining two pumps into service to manage storm&ndash;water. Pump five experienced intermittent tripping during the evening of 22nd November. [PAG,MUL] (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 pumps (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two pumps called into service on the evening of 22nd November; five pumps at the station (total) [PAG,MUL] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Blackpool,Anchorsholme Pumping Station,England,"The pumping station reached capacity during the extreme rainfall on the night of 22nd November 2017. Pumps were called into duty sequentially as flows arriving from the tunnel rose; the station operated at capacity and could not reduce tunnel levels earlier because pumping only starts once tunnel levels exceed the start height. (p5)
High flows arriving at the station triggered sequential automatic activation of pumps; on the evening of 22nd November and during 23rd November the station automatically called the remaining two pumps into service to manage storm–water. Pump five experienced intermittent tripping during the evening of 22nd November. [PAG,MUL] (p6)","5 pumps (p5)
two pumps called into service on the evening of 22nd November; five pumps at the station (total) [PAG,MUL] (p6)",GB-BPL_1_2017-11-22.html,GB-BPL_1_2017-11-22,Blackpool flooding 22 Nov 2017,Section 19 Report: Investigation into flooding on 22nd November 2017,009/Blackpool/009/2017/Blackpool/Blackpool November 2017 FINAL.pdf
GB-BPL,1,2017-11-22,53.8179442,-3.0509812,"<div id=""html_95a47cacef17c2a00850d5acc788835e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Blackpool</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread surface&ndash;water flooding reported across the Blackpool and Lancashire area on 22 November 2017, affecting multiple streets and local communities. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Town&ndash;wide flooding on 22 Nov 2017 affecting multiple streets and infrastructure: specific locations named include Limerick Road and Lockhurst Avenue; major flooding under Devonshire Road Bridge (road closure); Anchorsholme Academy was flooded. The report attributes the flooding to an exceptionally severe storm that overwhelmed highway drainage and sewers. [IMG,PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The sewer/tunnel system serving Blackpool was operating at full storage capacity during prolonged rainfall from 20 November and the sequential operation of pumping stations culminated in extreme conditions on the night of 22 November 2017. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread property&ndash;level flooding across the borough: council data recorded property&ndash;level flooding affecting properties and garages; roads and highways were flooded and in parts impassable. Water entered properties (often under the floor), sandbags were ineffective, some properties experienced electrical disruption. Water was recorded to have receded from affected properties during the morning of 23rd November 2017. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas of Blackpool experienced flooding on 22 November 2017 prompting a Section 19 investigation; specific properties (notably on Valentia Road and Limerick Road) were identified for potential flood resilience measures; actions proposed include watercourse clearance, surface water management measures and partnership works to improve storage and flow in local brooks. (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 300 properties (Blackpool and Lancashire) (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 300 properties [IMG,PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>74 properties; 6 garages; road flooding up to 1 m deep at Valentia Road and Limerick Road; highway depths around 500 mm in East Anchorsholme (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Blackpool,Blackpool,England,"Widespread surface–water flooding reported across the Blackpool and Lancashire area on 22 November 2017, affecting multiple streets and local communities. (p3)
Town–wide flooding on 22 Nov 2017 affecting multiple streets and infrastructure: specific locations named include Limerick Road and Lockhurst Avenue; major flooding under Devonshire Road Bridge (road closure); Anchorsholme Academy was flooded. The report attributes the flooding to an exceptionally severe storm that overwhelmed highway drainage and sewers. [IMG,PAG] (p4)
The sewer/tunnel system serving Blackpool was operating at full storage capacity during prolonged rainfall from 20 November and the sequential operation of pumping stations culminated in extreme conditions on the night of 22 November 2017. (p5)
Widespread property–level flooding across the borough: council data recorded property–level flooding affecting properties and garages; roads and highways were flooded and in parts impassable. Water entered properties (often under the floor), sandbags were ineffective, some properties experienced electrical disruption. Water was recorded to have receded from affected properties during the morning of 23rd November 2017. (p7)
Areas of Blackpool experienced flooding on 22 November 2017 prompting a Section 19 investigation; specific properties (notably on Valentia Road and Limerick Road) were identified for potential flood resilience measures; actions proposed include watercourse clearance, surface water management measures and partnership works to improve storage and flow in local brooks. (p9)","approximately 300 properties (Blackpool and Lancashire) (p3)
approximately 300 properties [IMG,PAG] (p4)
74 properties; 6 garages; road flooding up to 1 m deep at Valentia Road and Limerick Road; highway depths around 500 mm in East Anchorsholme (p7)",GB-BPL_1_2017-11-22.html,GB-BPL_1_2017-11-22,Blackpool flooding 22 Nov 2017,Section 19 Report: Investigation into flooding on 22nd November 2017,009/Blackpool/009/2017/Blackpool/Blackpool November 2017 FINAL.pdf
