GB-BPL,1,2017-11-22,53.8444581,-3.0371143,"<div id=""html_94cde129568415e20afa26090d97684a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Valentia Road, Bispham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed by Blackpool Council as having experienced flooding during the intense rainfall event on 22 November 2017; reported to the council as one of the locations affected. [TAB] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highways teams recorded surcharge into properties, across the carriageway and into gardens on 22nd November 2017; water entered properties largely under the floor and some properties experienced electrical disruption. The road was flooded in parts up to 1m deep. Valentia Road was visited by teams after the event. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in this area were affected by flooding linked to Bispham Dyke being connected into the sewer network and surface water runoff from Network Rail land; the report recommends investigating flood resilience for properties on these roads. (p8)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 1m deep on parts of the road (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Blackpool,"Valentia Road, Bispham",England,"Listed by Blackpool Council as having experienced flooding during the intense rainfall event on 22 November 2017; reported to the council as one of the locations affected. [TAB] (p3)
Highways teams recorded surcharge into properties, across the carriageway and into gardens on 22nd November 2017; water entered properties largely under the floor and some properties experienced electrical disruption. The road was flooded in parts up to 1m deep. Valentia Road was visited by teams after the event. (p7)
Properties in this area were affected by flooding linked to Bispham Dyke being connected into the sewer network and surface water runoff from Network Rail land; the report recommends investigating flood resilience for properties on these roads. (p8)",up to 1m deep on parts of the road (p7),GB-BPL_1_2017-11-22.html,GB-BPL_1_2017-11-22,Blackpool flooding 22 Nov 2017,Section 19 Report: Investigation into flooding on 22nd November 2017,009/Blackpool/009/2017/Blackpool/Blackpool November 2017 FINAL.pdf
GB-BPL,1,2017-11-22,53.8636312,-3.0249084,"<div id=""html_eae8156c9aa87adc54ff0329845f7e2b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Warren Drive, Bispham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported at this location as part of the intense rainfall event; the location is listed by Blackpool Council as having experienced flooding during the event on 22 November 2017. [TAB] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Named as part of the East Anchorsholme area that was impassable due to flooding across the highway; area experienced significant surface water and associated sewer surcharge impacts during the event. (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 500mm deep across the highway (area) (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Blackpool,"Warren Drive, Bispham",England,"Flooding was reported at this location as part of the intense rainfall event; the location is listed by Blackpool Council as having experienced flooding during the event on 22 November 2017. [TAB] (p3)
