GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.6884889,-1.8393557,"<div id=""html_bec2e42a948cbc13fba1869507eec49a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Calder</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Calder overtopped its banks and contributed to the flooding in Billington (combined with overland surface water), leading to internal flooding of properties. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Calder overtopped its banks and was identified as the primary source of flooding that caused internal flooding at the local community referenced by MSFW140 on 26 December 2015. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Calder overtopped its banks on 26/12/2015 and was identified as the primary source of internal flooding in Whalley on that date. (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Calder caused fluvial flooding in Whalley (the Environment Agency's work will look into the 26 December 2015 event and its return period). [TAB] (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>50 properties [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>196 properties (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Calder,England,"The River Calder overtopped its banks and contributed to the flooding in Billington (combined with overland surface water), leading to internal flooding of properties. [TAB] (p14)
The River Calder overtopped its banks and was identified as the primary source of flooding that caused internal flooding at the local community referenced by MSFW140 on 26 December 2015. (p18)
The River Calder overtopped its banks on 26/12/2015 and was identified as the primary source of internal flooding in Whalley on that date. (p20)
Flooding from the River Calder caused fluvial flooding in Whalley (the Environment Agency's work will look into the 26 December 2015 event and its return period). [TAB] (p21)","50 properties [TAB] (p14)
3 properties (p18)
