GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.8674307,-2.4188743,"<div id=""html_47c0777ad7e4bf0078da6d761df1a1e0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Ribble</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopped its banks and was identified as a primary source of fluvial flooding that caused internal flooding to properties in Ribchester. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 properties (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Ribble,England,Overtopped its banks and was identified as a primary source of fluvial flooding that caused internal flooding to properties in Ribchester. (p19),17 properties (p19),GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.8420091,-2.3996691,"<div id=""html_ff43f3b391b6f1d8bd43d5fb710d3c29"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whalley Road, Barrow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Local roads including Whalley Road were submerged causing access problems. Highway gullies on Whalley Road were found in January 2016 to need significant cleaning as a result of the event; the cleaning work has since been completed. [TAB] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Whalley Road, Barrow",England,Local roads including Whalley Road were submerged causing access problems. Highway gullies on Whalley Road were found in January 2016 to need significant cleaning as a result of the event; the cleaning work has since been completed. [TAB] (p12),,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.84148968580084,-2.400246313563117,"<div id=""html_49b504e91ebcd3fa0d544c2513961117"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cockerill Terrace, Barrow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties in the Cockerill Terrace area. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Cockerill Terrace, Barrow",England,Internal flooding of residential properties in the Cockerill Terrace area. (p13),2 properties (p13),GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.822996,-2.4055809,"<div id=""html_9be4929bfa173d9ff54f64e174fb4f80"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brookside Close, Whalley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>An ordinary watercourse adjacent to Brookside Close overtopped its banks and was identified as the primary source of internal flooding on 05/12/2015 affecting local properties. The trash screen at the junction with King Street was inspected and maintained after the event and placed on a weekly inspection list. [TAB] (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 properties [TAB] (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Brookside Close, Whalley",England,An ordinary watercourse adjacent to Brookside Close overtopped its banks and was identified as the primary source of internal flooding on 05/12/2015 affecting local properties. The trash screen at the junction with King Street was inspected and maintained after the event and placed on a weekly inspection list. [TAB] (p20),11 properties [TAB] (p20),GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.8199189,-2.4065541,"<div id=""html_463007e6a9ee96fc11f28ea0377aa2fc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>King Street, Whalley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The trash screen at the junction of King Street and Brookside Close was inspected and maintained by Lancashire Highways following the December 2015 flooding and is now on a weekly inspection schedule (response to flooding impacts). [TAB] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The King Street culvert was identified during post&ndash;December 2015 investigations as a potential failure point contributing to flooding; options considered included replacing large sections of the culvert or repairing it if detailed inspection showed it was required. Related highways/drainage works were programmed to address issues near the junction with Brookside Close. [PAG] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"King Street, Whalley",England,"The trash screen at the junction of King Street and Brookside Close was inspected and maintained by Lancashire Highways following the December 2015 flooding and is now on a weekly inspection schedule (response to flooding impacts). [TAB] (p20)
The King Street culvert was identified during post–December 2015 investigations as a potential failure point contributing to flooding; options considered included replacing large sections of the culvert or repairing it if detailed inspection showed it was required. Related highways/drainage works were programmed to address issues near the junction with Brookside Close. [PAG] (p22)",,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_cb9a061f10ec0a4b43282fcf0987465e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding occurred across Lancashire in December 2015, affecting communities and exposing shortcomings in how flood risk messages were communicated to those communities. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storms and heavy rainfall in November&ndash;December 2015 caused widespread flooding across Lancashire during December 2015, flooding properties and damaging private gardens, garages and outbuildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges, retaining walls, water treatment works, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools, village and town halls. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced widespread flooding during two major storm events in December 2015 affecting multiple communities across the county. Consequences included countywide data collection and timelines, a countywide Section 19 investigation and follow&ndash;up 'stage two' reporting, increased household sign&ndash;up to Environment Agency flood warnings and the formation of new local Flood Action Groups to support communities. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property in the Wiswell (Pendleton Road area) suffered internal flooding. An ordinary watercourse was identified close to the affected property but it is not clear whether this was the primary source of the flooding. [TAB] (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [TAB] (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Significant flooding occurred across Lancashire in December 2015, affecting communities and exposing shortcomings in how flood risk messages were communicated to those communities. (p3)
Storms and heavy rainfall in November–December 2015 caused widespread flooding across Lancashire during December 2015, flooding properties and damaging private gardens, garages and outbuildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges, retaining walls, water treatment works, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools, village and town halls. (p9)
Experienced widespread flooding during two major storm events in December 2015 affecting multiple communities across the county. Consequences included countywide data collection and timelines, a countywide Section 19 investigation and follow–up 'stage two' reporting, increased household sign–up to Environment Agency flood warnings and the formation of new local Flood Action Groups to support communities. [PAG] (p10)
One property in the Wiswell (Pendleton Road area) suffered internal flooding. An ordinary watercourse was identified close to the affected property but it is not clear whether this was the primary source of the flooding. [TAB] (p23)","over 2,500 properties (p9)
1 property [TAB] (p23)",GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.8790402,-2.1717795,"<div id=""html_5d16b423c59e0d4d0f285d4eb0e7fabb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pendle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Affected by the extreme storms and rainfall in November&ndash;December 2015 that caused widespread flooding across Lancashire in December 2015. Local residents and businesses in Pendle were impacted and a multi&ndash;agency drop&ndash;in event was held at New Road Community Centre (21 Jan 2016) to provide advice and support on recovery and flood resilience. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Pendle,England,Affected by the extreme storms and rainfall in November–December 2015 that caused widespread flooding across Lancashire in December 2015. Local residents and businesses in Pendle were impacted and a multi–agency drop–in event was held at New Road Community Centre (21 Jan 2016) to provide advice and support on recovery and flood resilience. (p9),,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.6109397,-2.8565713,"<div id=""html_15cf7e877efdccd7df7210e5c7673436"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced impacts from the extreme November&ndash;December 2015 storms that produced county&ndash;wide flooding in December 2015. Residents and businesses in West Lancashire were affected; multi&ndash;agency support events were held in the district (Parbold Village Hall on 25 Jan 2016 and Fiveways Public House on 01 Feb 2016) to assist recovery, provide advice on warnings and resilience, and gather eyewitness reports. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,West Lancashire,England,"Experienced impacts from the extreme November–December 2015 storms that produced county–wide flooding in December 2015. Residents and businesses in West Lancashire were affected; multi–agency support events were held in the district (Parbold Village Hall on 25 Jan 2016 and Fiveways Public House on 01 Feb 2016) to assist recovery, provide advice on warnings and resilience, and gather eyewitness reports. (p9)",,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.70249,-2.201046,"<div id=""html_6443e874d091d2a5fa9fe8c08ddfffeb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rossendale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Communities in Rossendale were affected by the December 2015 floods; recovery support was provided locally, including a drop&ndash;in event in Irwell Vale (10 Feb 2016) for affected residents. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Rossendale,England,"Communities in Rossendale were affected by the December 2015 floods; recovery support was provided locally, including a drop–in event in Irwell Vale (10 Feb 2016) for affected residents. (p9)",,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.9026441,-2.422856,"<div id=""html_b7f65f14da5faf5b4a9dc57accb4f2a0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ribble Valley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>In the Barrow (Barrow Brook) area on 26 December 2015, internal flooding occurred to 1 property and to the local primary school; a report was also made relating to commercial premises. Overflow from Barrow Lodge contributed to local roads being submerged and caused access problems. Other homes are thought likely to have been flooded but were not reported to Ribble Valley District Council at the time of the report. [TAB,PAG] (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property; 1 primary school [TAB,PAG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Ribble Valley,England,"In the Barrow (Barrow Brook) area on 26 December 2015, internal flooding occurred to 1 property and to the local primary school; a report was also made relating to commercial premises. Overflow from Barrow Lodge contributed to local roads being submerged and caused access problems. Other homes are thought likely to have been flooded but were not reported to Ribble Valley District Council at the time of the report. [TAB,PAG] (p11)","1 property; 1 primary school [TAB,PAG] (p11)",GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,54.04674035288858,-2.8001777457545383,"<div id=""html_6ed0981f38c6a6d018669835cda9904c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancaster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Affected by the extreme November&ndash;December 2015 storms that led to widespread flooding across Lancashire in December 2015. Local residents in Lancaster were among those impacted; a multi&ndash;agency drop&ndash;in event was held at Our Lady's Catholic College on 26 Jan 2016 to support affected households and businesses and provide recovery and resilience advice. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancaster,England,Affected by the extreme November–December 2015 storms that led to widespread flooding across Lancashire in December 2015. Local residents in Lancaster were among those impacted; a multi–agency drop–in event was held at Our Lady's Catholic College on 26 Jan 2016 to support affected households and businesses and provide recovery and resilience advice. (p9),,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.6775859865751,-2.316467158860694,"<div id=""html_1f5a0a8f01d8edc71c9f31db1cae7ae8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Irwell Vale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents affected by the December 2015 floods were offered recovery information and support at a multi&ndash;agency drop&ndash;in event held in Irwell Vale on 10 Feb 2016. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Irwell Vale,England,Residents affected by the December 2015 floods were offered recovery information and support at a multi–agency drop–in event held in Irwell Vale on 10 Feb 2016. (p9),,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.8406524,-2.4025937,"<div id=""html_5cde6004316c093336851d5657263730"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Barrow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding on 26 December 2015 affected properties and community buildings in the village. Specifically, 1 property and the local primary school suffered internal flooding, and there was a reported incident relating to commercial premises. The Cockerill Terrace area was also affected (see separate entry) with properties internally flooded. Local roads were submerged, causing access problems. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties in the Cockerill Terrace area of Barrow experienced internal flooding during the December 2015 event. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property; 1 local primary school; 2 properties (Cockerill Terrace) [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Barrow,England,"Internal flooding on 26 December 2015 affected properties and community buildings in the village. Specifically, 1 property and the local primary school suffered internal flooding, and there was a reported incident relating to commercial premises. The Cockerill Terrace area was also affected (see separate entry) with properties internally flooded. Local roads were submerged, causing access problems. [PAG] (p12)
Residential properties in the Cockerill Terrace area of Barrow experienced internal flooding during the December 2015 event. (p13)","1 property; 1 local primary school; 2 properties (Cockerill Terrace) [PAG] (p12)
2 properties (p13)",GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.8164475,-2.421282,"<div id=""html_2659f92726b70410d4b93fc156819bf5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Billington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties in the village; primary sources were a combination of overland surface water flows and the River Calder overtopping its banks. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Calder affected Billington (notably the 26 December 2015 event is being investigated). The event prompted a Strategic Outline Case to assess properties and infrastructure at risk and the economic damages to inform potential government&ndash;funded defences. [TAB,PAG] (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>50 properties [TAB] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Billington,England,"Internal flooding of properties in the village; primary sources were a combination of overland surface water flows and the River Calder overtopping its banks. [TAB] (p14)
Flooding from the River Calder affected Billington (notably the 26 December 2015 event is being investigated). The event prompted a Strategic Outline Case to assess properties and infrastructure at risk and the economic damages to inform potential government–funded defences. [TAB,PAG] (p15)",50 properties [TAB] (p14),GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.8717465,-2.3926783,"<div id=""html_f2f4b0e508fe29b8e7622f6950c031d7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clitheroe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties due to surface water/drainage network failure following the December 2015 event. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Clitheroe,England,Internal flooding of residential properties due to surface water/drainage network failure following the December 2015 event. (p16),8 properties (p16),GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.81359304893992,-2.5320952047206924,"<div id=""html_a62ec252f2207caae5b55d15c7f18998"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ribchester</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to residential properties after local watercourses and rivers (Boyce's Brook, Duddel Brook and the River Ribble) overtopped their banks. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 properties (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Ribchester,England,"Internal flooding to residential properties after local watercourses and rivers (Boyce's Brook, Duddel Brook and the River Ribble) overtopped their banks. (p19)",17 properties (p19),GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,11,2015-12-01,53.82241346770246,-2.4078975614186295,"<div id=""html_6bf40e630ff74c7a8159510ec587d2db"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whalley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>210 properties experienced internal flooding during December 2015: 11 properties internally flooded on 05/12/2015 (primary source: ordinary watercourse adjacent to Brookside Close overtopping), 3 properties internally flooded on 12/12/2015, and 196 properties internally flooded on 26/12/2015 (primary source: River Calder overtopping). (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Whalley experienced flooding during the December 2015 event (including the 26 December 2015 event). Flooding was caused by fluvial overflow from the River Calder combined with intense rainfall and affected properties and infrastructure; the Lead Local Flood Authority completed an investigation and assessed the surface water drainage network and options for managing flood risk. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred in December 2015; the LLFA investigated the key surface water drainage network in the village, identified opportunities for short&ndash;, medium&ndash; and long&ndash;term flood risk management, and recommended further assessments and appraisal to define mitigation works (including consideration of culvert replacement). [PAG] (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>210 properties; 11 properties; 3 properties; 196 properties (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Whalley,England,"210 properties experienced internal flooding during December 2015: 11 properties internally flooded on 05/12/2015 (primary source: ordinary watercourse adjacent to Brookside Close overtopping), 3 properties internally flooded on 12/12/2015, and 196 properties internally flooded on 26/12/2015 (primary source: River Calder overtopping). (p20)
Whalley experienced flooding during the December 2015 event (including the 26 December 2015 event). Flooding was caused by fluvial overflow from the River Calder combined with intense rainfall and affected properties and infrastructure; the Lead Local Flood Authority completed an investigation and assessed the surface water drainage network and options for managing flood risk. [TAB] (p21)
Surface water flooding occurred in December 2015; the LLFA investigated the key surface water drainage network in the village, identified opportunities for short–, medium– and long–term flood risk management, and recommended further assessments and appraisal to define mitigation works (including consideration of culvert replacement). [PAG] (p22)",210 properties; 11 properties; 3 properties; 196 properties (p20),GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_11_2015-12-01,Ribble Valley flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Ribble Valley District Flood Report,069/Lancashire County/ribble-valley-final-report.pdf
