GB-CAM,17,2020-12-01,52.5579482,0.0906246,"<div id=""html_057c42a5f0ce6428a7ebf377f19d1f89"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fenland Hall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement flooding occurred, prompting investigation and consideration of a sump pump to manage internal flooding. (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Fenland Hall,England,"Basement flooding occurred, prompting investigation and consideration of a sump pump to manage internal flooding. (p11)",,GB-CAM_17_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_17_2020-12-01,March flooding December 2020,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/March-December-2020-Flood-Investigation-Report.pdf
GB-CAM,17,2020-12-01,52.5729817,0.149134,"<div id=""html_43f3dc761c9f71793b05af797481af31"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Old Course River Nene</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River&ndash;related flooding divided affected areas into locations north and south of the Old Course River Nene; associated with the area&ndash;wide flooding that generated 67 flood reports (20 internal property floodings) from 23/24 December 2020 and reports from over 50 streets in March. [TAB,PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred in the area north of the Old Course River Nene. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Outfalls to the Old River (Old River Nene) were identified where high silt levels or high water levels are impacting flood risk management; investigations were planned to identify where these factors contributed to flooding in the area. [TAB] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred south of the Old Course River Nene caused by high groundwater, blocked ordinary watercourses and a culvert, low spots causing ponding, cross&ndash;connections between drainage systems, overwhelmed drainage networks and spring/overland flows; resulted in localised ponding and inability for surface water to drain effectively. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 50 streets; 67 flood reports; 20 internally flooded properties [TAB,PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 internally flooded property [TAB,PAG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Old Course River Nene,England,"River–related flooding divided affected areas into locations north and south of the Old Course River Nene; associated with the area–wide flooding that generated 67 flood reports (20 internal property floodings) from 23/24 December 2020 and reports from over 50 streets in March. [TAB,PAG] (p8)
Surface water flooding occurred in the area north of the Old Course River Nene. (p9)
Outfalls to the Old River (Old River Nene) were identified where high silt levels or high water levels are impacting flood risk management; investigations were planned to identify where these factors contributed to flooding in the area. [TAB] (p10)
Surface water flooding occurred south of the Old Course River Nene caused by high groundwater, blocked ordinary watercourses and a culvert, low spots causing ponding, cross–connections between drainage systems, overwhelmed drainage networks and spring/overland flows; resulted in localised ponding and inability for surface water to drain effectively. (p12)","over 50 streets; 67 flood reports; 20 internally flooded properties [TAB,PAG] (p8)
1 internally flooded property [TAB,PAG] (p10)",GB-CAM_17_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_17_2020-12-01,March flooding December 2020,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/March-December-2020-Flood-Investigation-Report.pdf
