GB-IOW,3,2023-10-25,50.7267224,-1.1691224,"<div id=""html_82dbf11d4e5288f906e0dad993fa2c94"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Argyll Street, Binstead</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced flooding that correlates with the 2021 flood event, which was predominantly surface water flooding with localised drainage issues and some fluvial flooding. [MUL] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Argyll Street, Binstead",England,"Experienced flooding that correlates with the 2021 flood event, which was predominantly surface water flooding with localised drainage issues and some fluvial flooding. [MUL] (p22)",,GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25,Ryde flooding 25 Oct 2023,Monktonmead Section 19 – 2024 Addendum,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation Monktonmead addendum Sept 2024 inc App A.pdf
GB-IOW,3,2023-10-25,50.7214588,-1.1697052,"<div id=""html_b797cb985628912bd80a0a557745922f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Partlands Avenue, Binstead</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed among locations where properties flooded as part of the event. (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Partlands Avenue, Binstead",England,Listed among locations where properties flooded as part of the event. (p22),,GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25,Ryde flooding 25 Oct 2023,Monktonmead Section 19 – 2024 Addendum,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation Monktonmead addendum Sept 2024 inc App A.pdf
GB-IOW,3,2023-10-25,50.7219861,-1.1531732,"<div id=""html_22c10cbc5e2515e97e03327ff94693bc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lower Highland Road, Ryde</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Lower Highland Road were flooded as part of the wider Ryde flood event. This location is listed among areas that flooded in the event and correlates with areas that experienced flooding in 2021. (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>At least 14 properties across Ryde (excluding Binstead) flooded (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Lower Highland Road, Ryde",England,Properties on Lower Highland Road were flooded as part of the wider Ryde flood event. This location is listed among areas that flooded in the event and correlates with areas that experienced flooding in 2021. (p22),At least 14 properties across Ryde (excluding Binstead) flooded (p22),GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25,Ryde flooding 25 Oct 2023,Monktonmead Section 19 – 2024 Addendum,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation Monktonmead addendum Sept 2024 inc App A.pdf
GB-IOW,3,2023-10-25,50.7253778,-1.159,"<div id=""html_19507739f8d31d1bab84aa4d379af83e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>St John's Road, Ryde</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on St John's Road were flooded as part of the wider Ryde flood event. The street is listed among locations that flooded and is noted as correlating with areas affected in the 2021 event, when flooding was predominantly surface&ndash;water&ndash;driven with local drainage issues and some fluvial influence. (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>At least 14 properties across Ryde (excluding Binstead) flooded (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"St John's Road, Ryde",England,"Properties on St John's Road were flooded as part of the wider Ryde flood event. The street is listed among locations that flooded and is noted as correlating with areas affected in the 2021 event, when flooding was predominantly surface–water–driven with local drainage issues and some fluvial influence. (p22)",At least 14 properties across Ryde (excluding Binstead) flooded (p22),GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25,Ryde flooding 25 Oct 2023,Monktonmead Section 19 – 2024 Addendum,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation Monktonmead addendum Sept 2024 inc App A.pdf
GB-IOW,3,2023-10-25,50.67108245,-1.3328042802764226,"<div id=""html_fbb67dcfcf3af45274b85c79af594a71"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Isle of Wight</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced heavy rain and associated flooding during Storm Babet (24&ndash;25 October 2023), causing localised surface water flooding and prompting emergency responses across the island. (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The documented flood event affected locations on the Isle of Wight (notably Ryde's Simeon Street area) where flowpaths, flood zones and internal property flooding were mapped; assets such as demountable and Marymead flood walls were present and provided some protection. [IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of the Isle of Wight (notably Ryde) experienced combined fluvial and surface water flooding during the 25 October 2023 event; Ryde recorded over 1001 flooded properties. (p31)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Much of the Isle of Wight received very high rainfall during the 18&ndash;hour flood event (up to ~91 mm), producing widespread surface&ndash;water runoff and heightened flood risk across the island. [IMG] (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall across Hampshire and the Isle of Wight on 24&ndash;25 Oct 2023 contributed to surface water flooding and overloaded drainage in parts of the island (for example the Simeon Recreation Ground area). [TAB] (p37)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 1001 properties (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,Isle of Wight,England,"Experienced heavy rain and associated flooding during Storm Babet (24–25 October 2023), causing localised surface water flooding and prompting emergency responses across the island. (p17)
The documented flood event affected locations on the Isle of Wight (notably Ryde's Simeon Street area) where flowpaths, flood zones and internal property flooding were mapped; assets such as demountable and Marymead flood walls were present and provided some protection. [IMG] (p20)
Parts of the Isle of Wight (notably Ryde) experienced combined fluvial and surface water flooding during the 25 October 2023 event; Ryde recorded over 1001 flooded properties. (p31)
Much of the Isle of Wight received very high rainfall during the 18–hour flood event (up to ~91 mm), producing widespread surface–water runoff and heightened flood risk across the island. [IMG] (p34)
Heavy rainfall across Hampshire and the Isle of Wight on 24–25 Oct 2023 contributed to surface water flooding and overloaded drainage in parts of the island (for example the Simeon Recreation Ground area). [TAB] (p37)",over 1001 properties (p31),GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25,Ryde flooding 25 Oct 2023,Monktonmead Section 19 – 2024 Addendum,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation Monktonmead addendum Sept 2024 inc App A.pdf
GB-IOW,3,2023-10-25,50.7299865,-1.1603699,"<div id=""html_af26e3babd6479409e2b5ba321136e18"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ryde</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties across the town; resident displacement, loss of possessions, negative mental and physical health impacts, road closures and damage to the railway line. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ryde experienced flooding events referenced in the report: it was affected by flooding in 2021 and by the event of 25 October 2023. Properties in Ryde were affected by the October 2023 flooding and may be eligible for Property Flood Resilience grants; the EA published an initial review (10 Nov 2023) and is undertaking a more detailed review into causes of the 25 Oct 2023 flood. [MUL] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding across the town during Storm Babet; the Simeon Street area was disproportionately impacted during the 25 October 2023 event. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding in the town during Storm Babet (25 October 2023). The Monktonmead study area covers a large proportion of Ryde and Simeon Street within Ryde was disproportionately impacted during the 25 October 2023 event; Monktonmead Brook (a main river running through Ryde) is implicated as a contributing watercourse. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High tide on the event day peaked at approximately 08:45 with a slower drop in tide level compared to other days; the report states this high tide level likely had an impact on flooding in Ryde. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall associated with Storm Babet caused surface&ndash;water/urban flooding in Ryde that affected residents, prompted the Isle of Wight Council to establish an Information Hub (initially at Ryde Castle Hotel, later at Aspire) to provide advice, guidance and support, and triggered recovery activity with Ryde Town Council. The heavy rain/flooding also contributed to emergency service demand (large number of calls to HIWFRS on 25 October). [TAB,MUL] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall and raised river levels impeded surface water drainage in Ryde: flows emerged from manholes and gullies, travel along local roads, storage boxes containing drop boards were completely submerged, and areas/roads (route between Newport and Ryde) became impassable. Flood Alerts and Warnings were issued for St Johns/Ryde. [TAB,MUL] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding during heavy rainfall: transport disruption (the road between Newport and Ryde became impassible due to floodwater) and on&ndash;site equipment was submerged (locked storage boxes containing drop boards were completely submerged, preventing installation of additional flood boards). (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood risk concentrated along Monktonmead Brook and adjacent low&ndash;lying areas within the Simeon Street area of Ryde; flowpaths converge toward the brook and Simeon Recreation Ground, with clusters of internal property flooding shown in central/northern parts of the study area. [IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At least 159 residential and commercial properties in Ryde experienced flooding on 25th October; the majority were internal floodings around Simeon Recreation Ground and neighbouring roads. Local businesses were heavily impacted &mdash; many closed for days, basements were swamped and there were reports of knee&ndash;high water causing significant internal damage and socio&ndash;economic impacts (loss of revenue, concern about damage costs and staff hours). (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At least 14 properties across Ryde were flooded during the event. (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding across the town during Storm Babet (October 2023) caused residents to move out of homes (temporary or permanent), loss of carpets, floorboards, furniture and other belongings from ground floors and basements, financial pressures on households, and loss of business for a number of local businesses. (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred in Ryde on 25 October 2023; properties in the town flooded from different sources and the event prompted the EA to publish an initial review and to undertake further investigation. (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff caused flooding that affected properties in Ryde. (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 25 October 2023 intense rainfall and overtopping of Monktonmead Brook caused combined fluvial and surface water flooding in Ryde; over 1001 properties were flooded. [IMG] (p31)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater had submerged the locked storage boxes containing additional drop boards in Ryde, preventing their installation; access was delayed because the road between Newport and Ryde became impassible and the contractor could not reach Ryde until 08:30. (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Unprecedented heavy rainfall caused rapid river rises and surface water flooding across Ryde; significant disruption to transport links and property flooding risk. EA did not fully install flood boards at 05:45 on 25.10.2023 which was a material decision related to maintaining a flood route through wall access points and influenced local flood response. (p40)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>107 properties (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 159 properties; at least 80 internal; 8 external; 33 unknown (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>14 properties (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Community Recovery Grant £500 (households); Business Recovery Grant up to £2,500 (eligible small&ndash;to&ndash;medium businesses); 100% council tax discount for a minimum of three months (flooded households); 100% Business Rate Relief for a minimum of three months (affected businesses) (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 1001 properties [IMG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,Ryde,England,"Internal flooding of properties across the town; resident displacement, loss of possessions, negative mental and physical health impacts, road closures and damage to the railway line. (p7)
Ryde experienced flooding events referenced in the report: it was affected by flooding in 2021 and by the event of 25 October 2023. Properties in Ryde were affected by the October 2023 flooding and may be eligible for Property Flood Resilience grants; the EA published an initial review (10 Nov 2023) and is undertaking a more detailed review into causes of the 25 Oct 2023 flood. [MUL] (p8)
Widespread flooding across the town during Storm Babet; the Simeon Street area was disproportionately impacted during the 25 October 2023 event. (p9)
Widespread flooding in the town during Storm Babet (25 October 2023). The Monktonmead study area covers a large proportion of Ryde and Simeon Street within Ryde was disproportionately impacted during the 25 October 2023 event; Monktonmead Brook (a main river running through Ryde) is implicated as a contributing watercourse. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
High tide on the event day peaked at approximately 08:45 with a slower drop in tide level compared to other days; the report states this high tide level likely had an impact on flooding in Ryde. (p16)
Intense rainfall associated with Storm Babet caused surface–water/urban flooding in Ryde that affected residents, prompted the Isle of Wight Council to establish an Information Hub (initially at Ryde Castle Hotel, later at Aspire) to provide advice, guidance and support, and triggered recovery activity with Ryde Town Council. The heavy rain/flooding also contributed to emergency service demand (large number of calls to HIWFRS on 25 October). [TAB,MUL] (p17)
Heavy rainfall and raised river levels impeded surface water drainage in Ryde: flows emerged from manholes and gullies, travel along local roads, storage boxes containing drop boards were completely submerged, and areas/roads (route between Newport and Ryde) became impassable. Flood Alerts and Warnings were issued for St Johns/Ryde. [TAB,MUL] (p18)
Surface water flooding during heavy rainfall: transport disruption (the road between Newport and Ryde became impassible due to floodwater) and on–site equipment was submerged (locked storage boxes containing drop boards were completely submerged, preventing installation of additional flood boards). (p19)
Flood risk concentrated along Monktonmead Brook and adjacent low–lying areas within the Simeon Street area of Ryde; flowpaths converge toward the brook and Simeon Recreation Ground, with clusters of internal property flooding shown in central/northern parts of the study area. [IMG] (p20)
At least 159 residential and commercial properties in Ryde experienced flooding on 25th October; the majority were internal floodings around Simeon Recreation Ground and neighbouring roads. Local businesses were heavily impacted — many closed for days, basements were swamped and there were reports of knee–high water causing significant internal damage and socio–economic impacts (loss of revenue, concern about damage costs and staff hours). (p21)
At least 14 properties across Ryde were flooded during the event. (p22)
Widespread flooding across the town during Storm Babet (October 2023) caused residents to move out of homes (temporary or permanent), loss of carpets, floorboards, furniture and other belongings from ground floors and basements, financial pressures on households, and loss of business for a number of local businesses. (p25)
Flooding occurred in Ryde on 25 October 2023; properties in the town flooded from different sources and the event prompted the EA to publish an initial review and to undertake further investigation. (p26)
Surface water runoff caused flooding that affected properties in Ryde. (p27)
On 25 October 2023 intense rainfall and overtopping of Monktonmead Brook caused combined fluvial and surface water flooding in Ryde; over 1001 properties were flooded. [IMG] (p31)
Floodwater had submerged the locked storage boxes containing additional drop boards in Ryde, preventing their installation; access was delayed because the road between Newport and Ryde became impassible and the contractor could not reach Ryde until 08:30. (p38)
Unprecedented heavy rainfall caused rapid river rises and surface water flooding across Ryde; significant disruption to transport links and property flooding risk. EA did not fully install flood boards at 05:45 on 25.10.2023 which was a material decision related to maintaining a flood route through wall access points and influenced local flood response. (p40)","107 properties (p7)
at least 159 properties; at least 80 internal; 8 external; 33 unknown (p21)
14 properties (p22)
Community Recovery Grant £500 (households); Business Recovery Grant up to £2,500 (eligible small–to–medium businesses); 100% council tax discount for a minimum of three months (flooded households); 100% Business Rate Relief for a minimum of three months (affected businesses) (p25)
over 1001 properties [IMG] (p31)",GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_3_2023-10-25,Ryde flooding 25 Oct 2023,Monktonmead Section 19 – 2024 Addendum,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation Monktonmead addendum Sept 2024 inc App A.pdf
