GB-KHL,1,2012-08-25,53.7746157,-0.3396504,"<div id=""html_ab70e5f763ac0a4633c3d5b922b866c9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stockholm Road, Kingston Upon Hull</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected the full length of Stockholm Road on 25th August 2012 (listed in Table 1 of flooded locations). (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,"Stockholm Road, Kingston Upon Hull",England,Flooding affected the full length of Stockholm Road on 25th August 2012 (listed in Table 1 of flooded locations). (p6),,GB-KHL_1_2012-08-25.html,GB-KHL_1_2012-08-25,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 25 Aug 2012,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: City Wide Flash Flooding – August 2012,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/FloodInvestigationReportHeavyRainAugust2012.pdf"
GB-KHL,1,2012-08-25,53.7827746,-0.3397579,"<div id=""html_475d6ef9a5479728e1fff441f607117e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cotterdale, Bransholme</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a location affected by the pluvial (surface water) flooding on 25 August 2012 and targeted for road and public&ndash;realm modifications to manage future surface water issues; subsequent de&ndash;silting, blockage removal and jetting works were identified and undertaken by Yorkshire Water. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Minor silt was removed from the Cotterdale surface water sewer and a soft blockage cleared from the foul sewer as part of post&ndash;event investigations. [TAB,PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cotterdale was identified for flood risk management scheme development by the council in response to surface water flooding experienced during the event, indicating it was impacted by the 25 August surface water/pluvial incident. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water (pluvial) flooding occurred and Cotterdale has been identified for delivery of a surface water flood alleviation scheme as a remediation measure following the 25th August 2012 event. [TAB] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,"Cotterdale, Bransholme",England,"Identified as a location affected by the pluvial (surface water) flooding on 25 August 2012 and targeted for road and public–realm modifications to manage future surface water issues; subsequent de–silting, blockage removal and jetting works were identified and undertaken by Yorkshire Water. [PAG] (p11)
