GB-HEF,3,2019-10-26,52.0210748,-2.7074323,"<div id=""html_e5eb4b01e9c8d90ca5f546c0fb7d2dc4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Red Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Red Brook is identified as a smaller watercourse contributing to local, short&ndash;duration flooding; mitigation proposals include a flood storage area on the Red Brook and a flap valve to prevent River Wye backwater from exacerbating flooding at Holme Lacy Road. [MUL] (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>less than a day [MUL] (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Red Brook,England,"Red Brook is identified as a smaller watercourse contributing to local, short–duration flooding; mitigation proposals include a flood storage area on the Red Brook and a flap valve to prevent River Wye backwater from exacerbating flooding at Holme Lacy Road. [MUL] (p3)",less than a day [MUL] (p3),GB-HEF_3_2019-10-26_etc.html,GB-HEF_3_2019-10-26_etc,Lower Bullingham flooding 26 Oct 2019 and Lower Bullingham flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Lower Bullingham,055/Herefordshire County/02/Hereford/Lower/Bullingham.pdf
