GB-HEF,3,2019-10-26,52.0553813,-2.7151735,"<div id=""html_2c365f992a4b47c46a5e7bb9c17fc773"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hereford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Central Hereford experienced very high river levels: the River Wye reached its highest recorded level at the Old Wye Bridge in February, producing a fluvial flood event affecting central Hereford. [IMG,PAG] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Hereford,England,"Central Hereford experienced very high river levels: the River Wye reached its highest recorded level at the Old Wye Bridge in February, producing a fluvial flood event affecting central Hereford. [IMG,PAG] (p1)",,GB-HEF_3_2019-10-26_etc.html,GB-HEF_3_2019-10-26_etc,Lower Bullingham flooding 26 Oct 2019 and Lower Bullingham flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Lower Bullingham,055/Herefordshire County/02/Hereford/Lower/Bullingham.pdf
GB-HEF,3,2019-10-26,52.0406940647801,-2.706952122405482,"<div id=""html_dc29c3e58ad4b1b7d8cf324ac063c401"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lower Bullingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Lower Bullingham lie within Flood Zone 3 adjacent to the River Wye; the map and event table link key flood events (26 October 2019 and 16 February 2020) to the area, indicating fluvial flooding risk/impact to residential and industrial areas within the investigation oval. [IMG,MUL] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding affected Lower Bullingham: roads (Lower Bullingham Lane / Bullingham Lane) were closed on 15 and 16 February 2020; properties have a history of flooding (including one property flooded in 1998) and some properties experienced flood durations of up to 4 days, indicating inundation influenced by the River Wye and smaller watercourses (Withy Brook, Red Brook). [PAG,MUL] (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property; flood durations up to 4 days [PAG,MUL] (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Lower Bullingham,England,"Parts of Lower Bullingham lie within Flood Zone 3 adjacent to the River Wye; the map and event table link key flood events (26 October 2019 and 16 February 2020) to the area, indicating fluvial flooding risk/impact to residential and industrial areas within the investigation oval. [IMG,MUL] (p1)
Fluvial flooding affected Lower Bullingham: roads (Lower Bullingham Lane / Bullingham Lane) were closed on 15 and 16 February 2020; properties have a history of flooding (including one property flooded in 1998) and some properties experienced flood durations of up to 4 days, indicating inundation influenced by the River Wye and smaller watercourses (Withy Brook, Red Brook). [PAG,MUL] (p3)","one property; flood durations up to 4 days [PAG,MUL] (p3)",GB-HEF_3_2019-10-26_etc.html,GB-HEF_3_2019-10-26_etc,Lower Bullingham flooding 26 Oct 2019 and Lower Bullingham flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Lower Bullingham,055/Herefordshire County/02/Hereford/Lower/Bullingham.pdf
GB-HEF,4,2020-02-16,52.06853440476616,-2.722513757080888,"<div id=""html_eebe076a915569673e150306c69113a5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Holmer Church of England Academy</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Holmer C of E Academy Primary School is listed as critical infrastructure affected in the key flood event; no injuries or loss of life were reported. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The school was recorded as flooded during the February 2020 event; it has flooded on multiple occasions. No injuries or loss of life were reported. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>no injuries or loss of life (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Holmer Church of England Academy,England,"Holmer C of E Academy Primary School is listed as critical infrastructure affected in the key flood event; no injuries or loss of life were reported. [TAB] (p2)
The school was recorded as flooded during the February 2020 event; it has flooded on multiple occasions. No injuries or loss of life were reported. (p3)",no injuries or loss of life (p3),GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16,Hereford flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hereford (Racecourse and Widemarsh Brook),055/Herefordshire County/03/Hereford/Race/City/Led.pdf
GB-HEF,4,2020-02-16,52.0750866,-2.7312133,"<div id=""html_8e5c78a39d72fd43e7ccf0fcfd79d1e1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ayles Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ayles Brook was identified as the source of fluvial flooding that contributed to internal flooding of properties in the 'Racecourse to Ledbury Road' area of Hereford. The brook drains into Widemarsh Brook and is culverted under the Racecourse and the A49; its flooding contributed to internal property flooding at depths reported from 1 ft up to 5 ft, with flood durations of about 1&ndash;2 days. Six respondents recorded outbuildings flooded to depths less than 6 inches. [PAG] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as the source of fluvial flooding for properties in Flood Zones 2 and 3. The Ayles Brook is culverted under Hereford Racecourse; the culvert has limited capacity and could not convey water beneath the A49, causing water to become overland flow and contribute to surface water flooding in the racecourse area and nearby streets. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a location requiring a feasibility study because of existing fluvial flood risk to properties; DEFRA grant funding bids are based on flood risk in this area. (p4)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>34 properties; 6 outbuildings; depths of 1 ft up to 5 ft; duration 1&ndash;2 days [PAG] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Ayles Brook,England,"Ayles Brook was identified as the source of fluvial flooding that contributed to internal flooding of properties in the 'Racecourse to Ledbury Road' area of Hereford. The brook drains into Widemarsh Brook and is culverted under the Racecourse and the A49; its flooding contributed to internal property flooding at depths reported from 1 ft up to 5 ft, with flood durations of about 1–2 days. Six respondents recorded outbuildings flooded to depths less than 6 inches. [PAG] (p2)
Identified as the source of fluvial flooding for properties in Flood Zones 2 and 3. The Ayles Brook is culverted under Hereford Racecourse; the culvert has limited capacity and could not convey water beneath the A49, causing water to become overland flow and contribute to surface water flooding in the racecourse area and nearby streets. [PAG] (p3)
Identified as a location requiring a feasibility study because of existing fluvial flood risk to properties; DEFRA grant funding bids are based on flood risk in this area. (p4)",34 properties; 6 outbuildings; depths of 1 ft up to 5 ft; duration 1–2 days [PAG] (p2),GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16,Hereford flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hereford (Racecourse and Widemarsh Brook),055/Herefordshire County/03/Hereford/Race/City/Led.pdf
