GB-HEF,4,2020-02-16,52.060846,-2.7176732,"<div id=""html_1100d802d6fd2d9cdd172d42b82136ec"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Edgar Street, Hereford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Edgar Street properties experienced internal fluvial flooding during the key event; properties in the Racecourse to Ledbury Road area (including Edgar Street) were flooded to depths of about 1 ft up to 5 ft with durations of 1&ndash;2 days. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widemarsh Brook burst its banks (partly due to backwater from the River Wye), causing fluvial flooding across the Edgar Street grid area; properties in Flood Zones 2 and 3 reported flooding. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,"Edgar Street, Hereford",England,"Edgar Street properties experienced internal fluvial flooding during the key event; properties in the Racecourse to Ledbury Road area (including Edgar Street) were flooded to depths of about 1 ft up to 5 ft with durations of 1–2 days. (p2)
Widemarsh Brook burst its banks (partly due to backwater from the River Wye), causing fluvial flooding across the Edgar Street grid area; properties in Flood Zones 2 and 3 reported flooding. (p3)",7 properties (p2),GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16,Hereford flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hereford (Racecourse and Widemarsh Brook),055/Herefordshire County/03/Hereford/Race/City/Led.pdf
GB-HEF,4,2020-02-16,52.0518165,-2.703826,"<div id=""html_9b9a7a3c5edba050ff9094c35b688ec2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Eign Road, Hereford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Eign Road (grouped with Ledbury Road) was affected by fluvial internal flooding as part of the Racecourse to Ledbury Road area during the key event. (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (Ledbury Road and Eign Road combined) (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,"Eign Road, Hereford",England,Eign Road (grouped with Ledbury Road) was affected by fluvial internal flooding as part of the Racecourse to Ledbury Road area during the key event. (p2),4 properties (Ledbury Road and Eign Road combined) (p2),GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16,Hereford flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hereford (Racecourse and Widemarsh Brook),055/Herefordshire County/03/Hereford/Race/City/Led.pdf
GB-HEF,4,2020-02-16,52.05258292070752,-2.7187509645388275,"<div id=""html_6e1934c99432b07467758fd3a9e40a39"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Old Wye Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Wye reached its highest recorded level at the Old Wye Bridge during the February 2020 event, indicating major fluvial flood conditions at this central Hereford location. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Old Wye Bridge,England,"The River Wye reached its highest recorded level at the Old Wye Bridge during the February 2020 event, indicating major fluvial flood conditions at this central Hereford location. (p3)",,GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16,Hereford flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hereford (Racecourse and Widemarsh Brook),055/Herefordshire County/03/Hereford/Race/City/Led.pdf
GB-HEF,4,2020-02-16,52.0553813,-2.7151735,"<div id=""html_6b1060be935be0d13db03dbdc5f02213"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hereford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas of central Hereford &mdash; specifically the racecourse and the Widmarsh area &mdash; are shown as being within Flood Zone 3 (high probability of fluvial flooding). Proximity to Ayles Brook and low elevation contours (circa 56&ndash;60m) indicate susceptibility to river (fluvial) flooding; parts of the urban area benefit from flood defences but key infrastructure and built&ndash;up areas lie within the high&ndash;risk zone. [IMG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Racecourse to Ledbury Road area of Hereford experienced fluvial and surface water flooding, resulting in internal flooding of residential properties; critical infrastructure impact included Holmer C of E Academy Primary School. [TAB,PAG] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Central Hereford experienced fluvial flooding from the River Wye (backwater causing Widemarsh Brook to burst banks at Edgar Street Grid and Ledbury Road) and surface&ndash;water flooding where the Ayles Brook culvert and local drainage were overwhelmed (notably around Hereford Racecourse and Roman Road). Holmer C of E Academy Primary School is recorded as having flooded during February 2020. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>34 properties; 1 school (Holmer C of E Academy Primary School) identified as affected critical infrastructure [TAB,PAG] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Hereford,England,"Areas of central Hereford — specifically the racecourse and the Widmarsh area — are shown as being within Flood Zone 3 (high probability of fluvial flooding). Proximity to Ayles Brook and low elevation contours (circa 56–60m) indicate susceptibility to river (fluvial) flooding; parts of the urban area benefit from flood defences but key infrastructure and built–up areas lie within the high–risk zone. [IMG] (p1)
The Racecourse to Ledbury Road area of Hereford experienced fluvial and surface water flooding, resulting in internal flooding of residential properties; critical infrastructure impact included Holmer C of E Academy Primary School. [TAB,PAG] (p2)
Central Hereford experienced fluvial flooding from the River Wye (backwater causing Widemarsh Brook to burst banks at Edgar Street Grid and Ledbury Road) and surface–water flooding where the Ayles Brook culvert and local drainage were overwhelmed (notably around Hereford Racecourse and Roman Road). Holmer C of E Academy Primary School is recorded as having flooded during February 2020. [PAG] (p3)","34 properties; 1 school (Holmer C of E Academy Primary School) identified as affected critical infrastructure [TAB,PAG] (p2)",GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_4_2020-02-16,Hereford flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hereford (Racecourse and Widemarsh Brook),055/Herefordshire County/03/Hereford/Race/City/Led.pdf
GB-KEN,12,2021-07-20,51.1653225,0.6190017,"<div id=""html_3bb7f75a130d964525ed0197d4cf5247"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Beult</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties located within the floodplain of the River Beult were affected and pumps from those properties were used to remove floodwater. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding associated with the River Beult inundated nearby central and eastern parts of Yalding, contributing to reported flood incidents at Oast Court, High Street, Mount Avenue, Blunden Lane and Vicarage Road. [IMG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,River Beult,England,"Properties located within the floodplain of the River Beult were affected and pumps from those properties were used to remove floodwater. (p7)
Flooding associated with the River Beult inundated nearby central and eastern parts of Yalding, contributing to reported flood incidents at Oast Court, High Street, Mount Avenue, Blunden Lane and Vicarage Road. [IMG] (p11)",,GB-KEN_12_2021-07-20.html,GB-KEN_12_2021-07-20,Yalding flooding 20 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Yalding,063/Kent/Section-19-Flood-Investigation-Yalding-2021.pdf
GB-KEN,12,2021-07-20,51.226852,0.4353473,"<div id=""html_9c342525f2404806bba142e521c2b84e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mount Avenue, Yalding</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding reported at one property. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culvert under Mount Avenue was surveyed and is reported likely to have been at full capacity during the event; this prevented highway drainage discharging into the watercourse and contributed to localised flooding. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map shows a reported flood incident at Mount Avenue during the 20th July 2021 event; identified as one of the residential streets in the eastern part of Yalding impacted by flooding. [IMG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded as a flood&ndash;affected road in the post&ndash;event survey exercise following the 20 July 2021 flooding; surveys were sent to residents to capture flood impacts. [TAB] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property reported external flooding [TAB] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Mount Avenue, Yalding",England,"External flooding reported at one property. [TAB] (p2)
