GB-KEN,12,2021-07-20,51.2269067,0.4336658,"<div id=""html_c3e76419465d7db1b032fd113221b7f2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Blunden Lane, Yalding</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding to a depth of approximately 10 cm reported at one property. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culvert downstream of Blunden Lane was CCTV&ndash;surveyed (found in very good condition) but is reported likely to have been at full capacity during the intense rainfall, contributing to localised flooding when highway drainage could not discharge. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map shows a reported flood incident at Blunden Lane during the 20th July 2021 event; marked as a flooded location within Yalding's central/eastern area. [IMG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded as a flood&ndash;affected road in the post&ndash;event survey exercise following the 20 July 2021 flooding; a survey engagement was made to capture impacts. [TAB] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property; flood depth approximately 10 cm [TAB] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Blunden Lane, Yalding",England,"External flooding to a depth of approximately 10 cm reported at one property. [TAB] (p2)
The culvert downstream of Blunden Lane was CCTV–surveyed (found in very good condition) but is reported likely to have been at full capacity during the intense rainfall, contributing to localised flooding when highway drainage could not discharge. (p7)
