GB-KEN,12,2021-07-20,51.2219743,0.4407355,"<div id=""html_55e974e3f5e7e417869dc4a8c4e21201"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Vicarage Road, Yalding</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two properties flooded internally (depths estimated up to approximately 15 cm). The road was also reported closed due to carriageway flooding. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Shown on the Environment Agency surface water flood map as high risk for surface water flooding and noted to correspond with the locations of properties affected during the 20 July 2021 flood event. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flow and overwhelmed highway drainage caused flooding on Vicarage Road; the police imposed a road closure. A subsequent CCTV survey found tap roots and silt in the surface water sewer along Vicarage Road, equating to an approximate loss of capacity that would have reduced drainage performance. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map shows a reported flood incident on Vicarage Road during the 20th July 2021 event; listed among the streets in Yalding impacted by flooding, close to the River Beult. [IMG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded as a flood&ndash;affected road in the post&ndash;event survey exercise following the 20 July 2021 flooding; a survey response was received regarding flood impacts. [TAB] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties; flood depths up to approximately 15 cm [TAB] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Vicarage Road, Yalding",England,"Two properties flooded internally (depths estimated up to approximately 15 cm). The road was also reported closed due to carriageway flooding. [TAB] (p2)
Shown on the Environment Agency surface water flood map as high risk for surface water flooding and noted to correspond with the locations of properties affected during the 20 July 2021 flood event. (p4)
