GB-KEN,12,2021-07-20,51.2351352,0.4383708,"<div id=""html_6a20d60beb6affa18f2e62b593b47063"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Yalding Hill, Yalding</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from adjacent fields flowed onto Yalding Hill, causing localised flooding. (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Yalding Hill, Yalding",England,"Surface water runoff from adjacent fields flowed onto Yalding Hill, causing localised flooding. (p7)",,GB-KEN_12_2021-07-20.html,GB-KEN_12_2021-07-20,Yalding flooding 20 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Yalding,063/Kent/Section-19-Flood-Investigation-Yalding-2021.pdf
GB-KEN,12,2021-07-20,51.2077925,0.4306374,"<div id=""html_4fa791e153356767fb942676ffbd0f3f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Emmet Hill Lane, Yalding</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense short&ndash;duration rainfall produced overland surface water that inundated properties on Emmet Hill Lane. (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Emmet Hill Lane, Yalding",England,Intense short–duration rainfall produced overland surface water that inundated properties on Emmet Hill Lane. (p7),2 properties (p7),GB-KEN_12_2021-07-20.html,GB-KEN_12_2021-07-20,Yalding flooding 20 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Yalding,063/Kent/Section-19-Flood-Investigation-Yalding-2021.pdf
GB-KEN,12,2021-07-20,51.2436078,0.4373982,"<div id=""html_0dc30f0d1ffd535562f75abbc7420c84"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hunt Street, West Farleigh</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flow from the intense rainfall inundated at least one property on Hunt Street. (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Hunt Street, West Farleigh",England,Overland flow from the intense rainfall inundated at least one property on Hunt Street. (p7),1 property (p7),GB-KEN_12_2021-07-20.html,GB-KEN_12_2021-07-20,Yalding flooding 20 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Yalding,063/Kent/Section-19-Flood-Investigation-Yalding-2021.pdf
GB-KEN,12,2021-07-20,51.224365,0.4314514,"<div id=""html_c1e0a66084e63e483ac097ebc4cb54f2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Yalding</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall on 20 July 2021 caused surface water runoff from surrounding land that overwhelmed highway surface water and sewerage drainage infrastructure, resulting in property flooding in Yalding. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The village experienced multiple instances of property flooding reported on specific streets (internal and external flooding across the village as summarised in the table). [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall on 20th July 2021 produced rapid overland flow across the southern parts of Yalding (where soils are slowly permeable with high groundwater), causing surface water flooding that inundated properties. The locations of affected properties align with High Street, Kenward Road and Vicarage Road in the southern area of the village. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Yalding experienced the intense rainfall on 20 July 2021 that formed the July flood event. The Event Rarity Calculator assessed the whole event at Yalding as approximately a 1 in 49&ndash;year event, and the intense 15:00&ndash;15:30 burst as approximately a 1 in 108&ndash;year event. The heavy, short&ndash;duration rainfall contributed to flooding in Yalding and its history of surface&ndash;water incidents. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Short, intense rainfall overwhelmed the highway surface water system and caused overland flow from adjacent fields onto the High Street, Vicarage Road and Yalding Hill; gullies and sewers surcharged with foul debris; fire service attended two property flooding incidents on the High Street and police implemented a road closure on Vicarage Road. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A short, very intense period of rainfall overwhelmed local surface&ndash;water drainage, causing flooding of properties and disruption to local roads. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple reported flood incidents across central and eastern residential areas of Yalding, affecting streets labelled on the map: Oast Court, High Street, Mount Avenue, Blunden Lane and Vicarage Road; flooding clustered near main streets and close to the River Beult. [IMG] (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties; 13 properties flooded internally; 2 properties flooded externally (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 properties (High Street internal) ; 2 properties (Vicarage Road internal) ; 1 property (Oast Court internal) ; 2 properties external (Mount Avenue and Blunden Lane) [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two flooding incidents; one road closure (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Yalding,England,"Intense rainfall on 20 July 2021 caused surface water runoff from surrounding land that overwhelmed highway surface water and sewerage drainage infrastructure, resulting in property flooding in Yalding. (p1)
The village experienced multiple instances of property flooding reported on specific streets (internal and external flooding across the village as summarised in the table). [TAB] (p2)
Intense rainfall on 20th July 2021 produced rapid overland flow across the southern parts of Yalding (where soils are slowly permeable with high groundwater), causing surface water flooding that inundated properties. The locations of affected properties align with High Street, Kenward Road and Vicarage Road in the southern area of the village. (p4)
Yalding experienced the intense rainfall on 20 July 2021 that formed the July flood event. The Event Rarity Calculator assessed the whole event at Yalding as approximately a 1 in 49–year event, and the intense 15:00–15:30 burst as approximately a 1 in 108–year event. The heavy, short–duration rainfall contributed to flooding in Yalding and its history of surface–water incidents. (p5)
Short, intense rainfall overwhelmed the highway surface water system and caused overland flow from adjacent fields onto the High Street, Vicarage Road and Yalding Hill; gullies and sewers surcharged with foul debris; fire service attended two property flooding incidents on the High Street and police implemented a road closure on Vicarage Road. (p7)
A short, very intense period of rainfall overwhelmed local surface–water drainage, causing flooding of properties and disruption to local roads. (p8)
Multiple reported flood incidents across central and eastern residential areas of Yalding, affecting streets labelled on the map: Oast Court, High Street, Mount Avenue, Blunden Lane and Vicarage Road; flooding clustered near main streets and close to the River Beult. [IMG] (p11)","15 properties; 13 properties flooded internally; 2 properties flooded externally (p1)
10 properties (High Street internal) ; 2 properties (Vicarage Road internal) ; 1 property (Oast Court internal) ; 2 properties external (Mount Avenue and Blunden Lane) [TAB] (p2)
two flooding incidents; one road closure (p7)
15 properties (p8)",GB-KEN_12_2021-07-20.html,GB-KEN_12_2021-07-20,Yalding flooding 20 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Yalding,063/Kent/Section-19-Flood-Investigation-Yalding-2021.pdf
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7544716,-1.9201772,"<div id=""html_d8d8e2305d3dd2689fae46b71e5d1093"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Turbary Common</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Erosion of footpaths indicates high&ndash;energy runoff from the common; runoff from the common contributed to large flows that poured down Mandale Road and fed the flooding of adjacent streets and properties. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Turbary Common,England,Erosion of footpaths indicates high–energy runoff from the common; runoff from the common contributed to large flows that poured down Mandale Road and fed the flooding of adjacent streets and properties. (p12),,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.76381116115746,-1.8962721840421575,"<div id=""html_9d18ae1d5e7e156084cd0b528fc14d52"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Long Road Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 3 July 2015 considerable flows entered the playground; an upstream fence became blinded with debris and created a dam which reduced the effective capacity of the bunded storage area. The bund stored some water (tide marks indicate storage) but less than expected, allowing overflow through a grassed overflow channel. (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Long Road Park,England,"On 3 July 2015 considerable flows entered the playground; an upstream fence became blinded with debris and created a dam which reduced the effective capacity of the bunded storage area. The bund stored some water (tide marks indicate storage) but less than expected, allowing overflow through a grassed overflow channel. (p13)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.71835,-1.8761166,"<div id=""html_7d2f10c47c04ea02d7f012e2dff41019"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lower Gardens</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Affected by surcharging of foul/combined sewers during the intense storm on 3 July 2015; required a major clean&ndash;up carried out by Wessex Water. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Closed for several days while Wessex Water carried out a major clean&ndash;up after the sewer surcharged during the storm; restricted access to an important local facility and reputational damage despite limited physical damage due to regular flooding and quick recoverability. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Landscaped public areas were inundated; the combined/foul sewer overflowed causing a significant pollution incident and parts of the gardens were closed for cleanup following the flood. (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Lower Gardens,England,"Affected by surcharging of foul/combined sewers during the intense storm on 3 July 2015; required a major clean–up carried out by Wessex Water. (p3)
Closed for several days while Wessex Water carried out a major clean–up after the sewer surcharged during the storm; restricted access to an important local facility and reputational damage despite limited physical damage due to regular flooding and quick recoverability. (p10)
Landscaped public areas were inundated; the combined/foul sewer overflowed causing a significant pollution incident and parts of the gardens were closed for cleanup following the flood. (p16)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7434442,-1.8790087,"<div id=""html_6722a4a994874c9a221c9386043e4d45"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>KFC</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater covered the street and reached storefront entrances, including the KFC shown in the photo; the road was impassable and the shop frontage was inundated by floodwater. [IMG] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",KFC,England,"Floodwater covered the street and reached storefront entrances, including the KFC shown in the photo; the road was impassable and the shop frontage was inundated by floodwater. [IMG] (p14)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.76724526192537,-1.885822907103926,"<div id=""html_15676ba3259a37ff9f3c69986d0a1608"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Redhill and Northbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the Redhill and Northbourne ward where flood incidents were reported on 3rd July 2015; incidents include external and highway flooding across the ward and internal/combined internal&ndash;external incidents concentrated toward the southern area. [IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Redhill and Northbourne show clustering of flooding incidents on 3 July 2015 and overlap with earlier reported incidents, indicating localised and recurring surface&ndash;water flooding in the ward area. (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Redhill / Northbourne ward is shown on the map with actual flood points from 3 July 2015, indicating instances of surface water flooding in the ward during the event and partial overlap with predicted magenta zones. (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Redhill and Northbourne,England,"Part of the Redhill and Northbourne ward where flood incidents were reported on 3rd July 2015; incidents include external and highway flooding across the ward and internal/combined internal–external incidents concentrated toward the southern area. [IMG] (p26)
