GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.74666863306883,-1.9055488226078086,"<div id=""html_afaa2c36a08499b62869075191b35e16"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wallisdown and Winton West</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clusters of flood incidents were noted in the southern part of the Wallisdown and Winton West area on 3rd July 2015; external and highway flooding were present throughout the ward alongside some internal and combined incidents. [IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding incidents occurred in Wallisdown / Winton West on 3 July 2015, with mapped locations showing both July 2015 events and previous incidents overlapping, indicating repeated localised flooding. (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of the Wallisdown / Winton West ward experienced surface water flooding on 3 July 2015 (red points), with some events occurring along linear predicted flood corridors shown on the map. (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Observed surface&ndash;water flooding locations on 3rd July 2015 are shown within the Wallisdown / Winton West ward (red points on the map); some observed points overlap the modelled 1&ndash;in&ndash;100&ndash;year (>150mm) predicted flood areas (magenta). [IMG,PAG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Wallisdown and Winton West,England,"Clusters of flood incidents were noted in the southern part of the Wallisdown and Winton West area on 3rd July 2015; external and highway flooding were present throughout the ward alongside some internal and combined incidents. [IMG] (p26)
