GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.719101024402754,-1.8773163889572546,"<div id=""html_66fb155c81ecba358c6f8cbbe41d39d6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bourne Stream</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Bourne Stream regularly over&ndash;spills onto the Lower Gardens floodplain and contributed to inundation in this incident. (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Bourne Stream,England,The Bourne Stream regularly over–spills onto the Lower Gardens floodplain and contributed to inundation in this incident. (p16),,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.9025349,-1.404189,"<div id=""html_ec043481520a15fe86f449fb22e795f3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Southampton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The precipitation system moved inland over Hampshire during 22:45&ndash;23:15 BST on 03 Jul 2015; heavy rain affected parts of Hampshire, including the area around Southampton, as the system intensified and expanded northeastward. [IMG] (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Southampton,England,"The precipitation system moved inland over Hampshire during 22:45–23:15 BST on 03 Jul 2015; heavy rain affected parts of Hampshire, including the area around Southampton, as the system intensified and expanded northeastward. [IMG] (p21)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7280952,-1.9020605,"<div id=""html_646449acf15e8e50e842807e3e4d6267"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Branksome Wood Road, Bournemouth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water system was overwhelmed in the event, causing internal flooding of properties; Wessex Water installed an interim protection scheme and further upgrades are planned. [MUL] (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>three properties [MUL] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Branksome Wood Road, Bournemouth",England,"Surface water system was overwhelmed in the event, causing internal flooding of properties; Wessex Water installed an interim protection scheme and further upgrades are planned. [MUL] (p15)",three properties [MUL] (p15),GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7595164,-1.9137655,"<div id=""html_82fc88b5fb9196638b786fad33059842"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mandale Road, Bournemouth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road drainage regularly blocked so water ponded in a low spot for many days; during the event flow ran &#8216;kerb to kerb&#8217; down the road driven by runoff from the common/industrial area, gardens and detached garages/outbuildings flooded historically, and in this event two properties flooded internally. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Mandale Road, Bournemouth",England,"Road drainage regularly blocked so water ponded in a low spot for many days; during the event flow ran ‘kerb to kerb’ down the road driven by runoff from the common/industrial area, gardens and detached garages/outbuildings flooded historically, and in this event two properties flooded internally. (p12)",2 properties (p12),GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7595513,-1.9187862,"<div id=""html_7093c5079c109ede9cd6d80aefe7e82f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Nutley Way, Bournemouth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flow routed through rear gardens (natural flow path) from Mandale Road towards Poole Lane; flow was exacerbated by fences and walls which formed mini&ndash;dams, increasing local flooding and flow depths. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Nutley Way, Bournemouth",England,"Overland flow routed through rear gardens (natural flow path) from Mandale Road towards Poole Lane; flow was exacerbated by fences and walls which formed mini–dams, increasing local flooding and flow depths. (p12)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7597193,-1.9177674,"<div id=""html_f5b51690493d139db014c967b66f7747"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Nutley Close, Bournemouth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flow passed through rear gardens on its route to Poole Lane; fences and walls along the flow path aggravated the situation by creating a series of small dams. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Nutley Close, Bournemouth",England,Overland flow passed through rear gardens on its route to Poole Lane; fences and walls along the flow path aggravated the situation by creating a series of small dams. (p12),,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7656407,-1.9072308,"<div id=""html_f371079b97782cbcfe86294679c64d5e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Poole Lane, Kinson</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flow that built up on Mandale Road/Nutley Way/Nutley Close emerged into Poole Lane; highway ponding/standing water has occurred in the vicinity and the reported flow&ndash;path routed runoff and debris through back gardens before emerging into Poole Lane. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Poole Lane, Kinson",England,Flow that built up on Mandale Road/Nutley Way/Nutley Close emerged into Poole Lane; highway ponding/standing water has occurred in the vicinity and the reported flow–path routed runoff and debris through back gardens before emerging into Poole Lane. (p12),,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7634734,-1.9120408,"<div id=""html_432be61ac1a468e8b4fbe26a7a6c9c53"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mayfair Gardens, Kinson</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway flooding in the vicinity; flow overcame a fence and debris built up against it, causing water to build to around 500 mm behind the fence and resulting in internal flooding of properties. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties; 500 mm water build&ndash;up (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Mayfair Gardens, Kinson",England,"Highway flooding in the vicinity; flow overcame a fence and debris built up against it, causing water to build to around 500 mm behind the fence and resulting in internal flooding of properties. (p12)",4 properties; 500 mm water build–up (p12),GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7619445,-1.8895833,"<div id=""html_ad88ed198b13ae5509b55fa1cced0102"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Leybourne Avenue, Kinson</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Leybourne Avenue area flooded on 3 July 2015 when a blockage in the local foul/combined sewer system caused surcharge. A nearby bunded storage area stored less water than expected because an upstream fence became blinded with debris and formed a dam, contributing to the flooding of the area. (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Leybourne Avenue, Kinson",England,"The Leybourne Avenue area flooded on 3 July 2015 when a blockage in the local foul/combined sewer system caused surcharge. A nearby bunded storage area stored less water than expected because an upstream fence became blinded with debris and formed a dam, contributing to the flooding of the area. (p13)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7366928,-1.8802447,"<div id=""html_a1f7911570d3a04a5d69de49da7a9a7a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wimborne Road, Winton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Peters Hill (alias of the Wimborne Road/Winton High Street area) experienced internal flooding of commercial premises during the event; businesses suffered stock damage, required closures and cleaning, and properties were left with silt deposits. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 commercial properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Wimborne Road, Winton",England,"Peters Hill (alias of the Wimborne Road/Winton High Street area) experienced internal flooding of commercial premises during the event; businesses suffered stock damage, required closures and cleaning, and properties were left with silt deposits. (p14)",10 commercial properties (p14),GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7241333,-1.8952598,"<div id=""html_53d9873507423a6225f9bb4d04b69327"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Surrey Road, Bournemouth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 3 July 2015 the event appears to have been the worst recorded at this location, resulting in internal flooding of properties and prompting Wessex Water to install an interim protection scheme; modelling showed the surface&ndash;water system was likely overwhelmed and has limited capacity. [MUL] (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>three properties [MUL] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Surrey Road, Bournemouth",England,"On 3 July 2015 the event appears to have been the worst recorded at this location, resulting in internal flooding of properties and prompting Wessex Water to install an interim protection scheme; modelling showed the surface–water system was likely overwhelmed and has limited capacity. [MUL] (p15)",three properties [MUL] (p15),GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.74737687263831,-2.4192394577688887,"<div id=""html_b09e4f0869f15f12a4f42092f373eb12"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Dorset</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rapid intensification and northeastward movement of a precipitation system produced heavy rainfall that moved onshore and covered much of Dorset during the 22:45&ndash;23:15 BST sequence on 03 Jul 2015, increasing rainfall coverage and intensity over the county. [IMG] (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Dorset,England,"Rapid intensification and northeastward movement of a precipitation system produced heavy rainfall that moved onshore and covered much of Dorset during the 22:45–23:15 BST sequence on 03 Jul 2015, increasing rainfall coverage and intensity over the county. [IMG] (p21)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.67108245,-1.3328042802764226,"<div id=""html_32ca1bba98a00721982b2f91e44d26e3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Isle of Wight</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Moderate to heavy precipitation approached and moved over the Isle of Wight during the 22:45&ndash;23:15 BST radar sequence on 03 Jul 2015, with the system progressing northeastward and increasing in intensity. [IMG] (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Isle of Wight,England,"Moderate to heavy precipitation approached and moved over the Isle of Wight during the 22:45–23:15 BST radar sequence on 03 Jul 2015, with the system progressing northeastward and increasing in intensity. [IMG] (p21)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7201514,-1.8799118,"<div id=""html_5545f365650a09d4176535f99eaac742"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bournemouth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The report investigates flooding that affected Bournemouth on 3rd July 2015; it documents the event for local flood investigation purposes (Section 19). (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread surface water / flash flooding across the conurbation. Sewers and drains surcharged causing damage to the highway; urgent carriageway repairs undertaken by Bournemouth Borough Council and Wessex Water. Foul/combined sewer surcharging required major clean&ndash;up of affected properties and the Lower Gardens. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Many houses and businesses flooded; roads damaged by surcharging sewers; The Lower Gardens closed for several days while a major clean&ndash;up was carried out following a surcharged sewer; numerous properties entered temporary accommodation while properties dried out; businesses lost stock and trading days; reputational damage to a local facility (The Lower Gardens). [TAB,PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme thunderstorm on the night of 3rd July 2015 caused inevitable flash flooding across the town. Limited channel and outfall capacity led to overflows; the main foul/combined sewer also overflowed causing a significant pollution incident. Parts of local gardens were closed for several days for cleanup, and the event attracted local media coverage. [PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported and observed surface&ndash;water/urban flooding across Bournemouth on 3 July 2015; locations of flooding were mapped in the report (Maps 3, 3(a), 3(b), Map 4 and Map 5) and formed the basis for the investigation and response. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rapidly intensifying heavy precipitation moved onshore over Bournemouth during the 22:45&ndash;23:15 BST period on 3 July 2015, producing surface&ndash;water/flash flooding in the urban area associated with the event. [IMG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Very high, localized rainfall rates were observed over central and northern Bournemouth at 23:40 BST on 3 July 2015 (large areas of 16&ndash;32 mm/hour and some &gt;32 mm/hour on radar). This intense, concentrated precipitation produced conditions for rapid surface&ndash;water (pluvial) flooding within and immediately north of the city boundary. [IMG,PAG] (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas near the coastline showed higher densities of reported flooding incidents on 3 July 2015, with multiple external and highway&ndash;type flood reports clustered close to the coast. [IMG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple locations across the urban area experienced flooding incidents on 3rd July 2015 (red dots). Incident clusters overlap with previously reported/observed flooding (light blue), indicating recurring vulnerability in central and southern parts of the town, including areas near the coastline. [IMG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Across Bournemouth wards shown on the map, multiple surface water flood locations on 3 July 2015 are indicated (red points), with predicted 1&ndash;in&ndash;100&ndash;year (>150mm) flood corridors (magenta) overlapping some actual flood sites &mdash; demonstrating urban surface water flooding impacts during the event. [IMG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The map shows scattered observed flooding locations across Bournemouth on 3 July 2015 (red), with clustering in southern and western wards (notably Westbourne/West Cliff). Modelled 1&ndash;in&ndash;100&ndash;year (>150mm) predicted flood zones (magenta) follow watercourses and low&ndash;lying areas and overlap with many observed points, indicating both historical impacts and modelled exposure to high&ndash;return&ndash;period pluvial flooding in parts of the town. [IMG] (p31)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>133 reported or observed incidents of flooding; 56 properties flooded internally (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>133 records; 40 records of internal flooding affecting some 56 properties; 37 records of external flooding; 38 records of highway flooding; 18 records indeterminate. [TAB,PAG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Bournemouth,England,"The report investigates flooding that affected Bournemouth on 3rd July 2015; it documents the event for local flood investigation purposes (Section 19). (p1)
Widespread surface water / flash flooding across the conurbation. Sewers and drains surcharged causing damage to the highway; urgent carriageway repairs undertaken by Bournemouth Borough Council and Wessex Water. Foul/combined sewer surcharging required major clean–up of affected properties and the Lower Gardens. (p3)
Many houses and businesses flooded; roads damaged by surcharging sewers; The Lower Gardens closed for several days while a major clean–up was carried out following a surcharged sewer; numerous properties entered temporary accommodation while properties dried out; businesses lost stock and trading days; reputational damage to a local facility (The Lower Gardens). [TAB,PAG] (p10)
Extreme thunderstorm on the night of 3rd July 2015 caused inevitable flash flooding across the town. Limited channel and outfall capacity led to overflows; the main foul/combined sewer also overflowed causing a significant pollution incident. Parts of local gardens were closed for several days for cleanup, and the event attracted local media coverage. [PAG] (p17)
Reported and observed surface–water/urban flooding across Bournemouth on 3 July 2015; locations of flooding were mapped in the report (Maps 3, 3(a), 3(b), Map 4 and Map 5) and formed the basis for the investigation and response. (p18)
Rapidly intensifying heavy precipitation moved onshore over Bournemouth during the 22:45–23:15 BST period on 3 July 2015, producing surface–water/flash flooding in the urban area associated with the event. [IMG] (p21)
Very high, localized rainfall rates were observed over central and northern Bournemouth at 23:40 BST on 3 July 2015 (large areas of 16–32 mm/hour and some >32 mm/hour on radar). This intense, concentrated precipitation produced conditions for rapid surface–water (pluvial) flooding within and immediately north of the city boundary. [IMG,PAG] (p23)
Areas near the coastline showed higher densities of reported flooding incidents on 3 July 2015, with multiple external and highway–type flood reports clustered close to the coast. [IMG] (p25)
Multiple locations across the urban area experienced flooding incidents on 3rd July 2015 (red dots). Incident clusters overlap with previously reported/observed flooding (light blue), indicating recurring vulnerability in central and southern parts of the town, including areas near the coastline. [IMG] (p29)
Across Bournemouth wards shown on the map, multiple surface water flood locations on 3 July 2015 are indicated (red points), with predicted 1–in–100–year (>150mm) flood corridors (magenta) overlapping some actual flood sites — demonstrating urban surface water flooding impacts during the event. [IMG] (p30)
The map shows scattered observed flooding locations across Bournemouth on 3 July 2015 (red), with clustering in southern and western wards (notably Westbourne/West Cliff). Modelled 1–in–100–year (>150mm) predicted flood zones (magenta) follow watercourses and low–lying areas and overlap with many observed points, indicating both historical impacts and modelled exposure to high–return–period pluvial flooding in parts of the town. [IMG] (p31)","133 reported or observed incidents of flooding; 56 properties flooded internally (p3)
133 records; 40 records of internal flooding affecting some 56 properties; 37 records of external flooding; 38 records of highway flooding; 18 records indeterminate. [TAB,PAG] (p10)",GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.71942676988921,-1.8803193025254896,"<div id=""html_45cc900f6237059e8238f3ee1712bf9b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Town Centre</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Western side of the Town Centre was the focus of the intense thunderstorm and experienced significant surface water / flash flooding. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding of town centre commercial properties; at least one business property confirmed to have flooded internally during the event. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 business property (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Town Centre,England,"Western side of the Town Centre was the focus of the intense thunderstorm and experienced significant surface water / flash flooding. (p3)
Flooding of town centre commercial properties; at least one business property confirmed to have flooded internally during the event. (p16)",1 business property (p16),GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.754408271161196,-1.880625468703562,"<div id=""html_16a954dc8f24cfd686080696ed872f36"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Redhill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clustered flood incidents reported in the Redhill and Northbourne ward on 3rd July 2015; internal flooding and combined internal/external incidents were more concentrated in the southern part of Redhill, with external and highway flooding also present. [IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The map indicates clustering of flooding incidents on 3rd July 2015 in the Redhill area and a dense record of prior flooding, showing repeated localised flood&ndash;prone locations within the ward. [IMG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Redhill area (as part of the Redhill/Northbourne ward) is shown to contain flooding locations from 3 July 2015; some of these lie within or adjacent to predicted 1&ndash;in&ndash;100&ndash;year (>150 mm) zones. [IMG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Redhill,England,"Clustered flood incidents reported in the Redhill and Northbourne ward on 3rd July 2015; internal flooding and combined internal/external incidents were more concentrated in the southern part of Redhill, with external and highway flooding also present. [IMG] (p26)
The map indicates clustering of flooding incidents on 3rd July 2015 in the Redhill area and a dense record of prior flooding, showing repeated localised flood–prone locations within the ward. [IMG] (p28)
The Redhill area (as part of the Redhill/Northbourne ward) is shown to contain flooding locations from 3 July 2015; some of these lie within or adjacent to predicted 1–in–100–year (>150 mm) zones. [IMG] (p30)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7544891,-1.8753728,"<div id=""html_eae0eb668598e081d74337337acddde9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Moordown</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Locations in part of the Moordown ward experienced surface&ndash;water flooding on 3 July 2015; incidents from that date are shown as red dots on the map and overlap with prior reported incidents in some places, indicating repeat flood occurrences. [IMG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded flooding on 3 July 2015 is shown within the ward area (red markers on the map); predicted 1&ndash;in&ndash;100&ndash;year (>150 mm) zones run near some of the observed flood locations. [IMG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Moordown,England,"Locations in part of the Moordown ward experienced surface–water flooding on 3 July 2015; incidents from that date are shown as red dots on the map and overlap with prior reported incidents in some places, indicating repeat flood occurrences. [IMG] (p28)
Recorded flooding on 3 July 2015 is shown within the ward area (red markers on the map); predicted 1–in–100–year (>150 mm) zones run near some of the observed flood locations. [IMG] (p30)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7235524,-1.9041085,"<div id=""html_3ec709677ca7a8b48bc13d86ece2a80b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Westbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas were directly hit by the intense thunderstorm, resulting in significant surface water / flash flooding. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported incidents of internal (building) flooding and highway flooding were plotted in the Westbourne / West Cliff area on 3 July 2015, with notable clusters of internal and highway symbols in the western and central parts of the mapped area; some external and mixed incidents also present. [IMG] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Westbourne / West Cliff area shows flooding incidents on 3rd July 2015 (red) and overlapping previous incidents (light blue), with higher densities near the southern coastal edge indicating repeated local flooding. [IMG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Observed flooding (red dots) clustered in the Westbourne / West Cliff area on 3 July 2015, indicating localised surface&ndash;water flooding impacts from intense rainfall. Modelled 1&ndash;in&ndash;100&ndash;year (>150mm) predicted flood areas (magenta) align with many observed locations, showing the ward is within both historical and modelled flood&ndash;prone zones. [IMG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Westbourne,England,"Areas were directly hit by the intense thunderstorm, resulting in significant surface water / flash flooding. (p3)
Reported incidents of internal (building) flooding and highway flooding were plotted in the Westbourne / West Cliff area on 3 July 2015, with notable clusters of internal and highway symbols in the western and central parts of the mapped area; some external and mixed incidents also present. [IMG] (p27)
Westbourne / West Cliff area shows flooding incidents on 3rd July 2015 (red) and overlapping previous incidents (light blue), with higher densities near the southern coastal edge indicating repeated local flooding. [IMG] (p29)
Observed flooding (red dots) clustered in the Westbourne / West Cliff area on 3 July 2015, indicating localised surface–water flooding impacts from intense rainfall. Modelled 1–in–100–year (>150mm) predicted flood areas (magenta) align with many observed locations, showing the ward is within both historical and modelled flood–prone zones. [IMG] (p31)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7152158,-1.8848209,"<div id=""html_1e6b91a51f0f31307966ff54b46e9429"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Cliff</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported flooding incidents on 3 July 2015 included clusters of internal and highway flooding symbols in the western and central parts of the mapped area, indicating roads and some buildings were affected in Westbourne / West Cliff. [IMG] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clustered locations of flooding incidents on 3rd July 2015 overlapped with previous reported flooding in the Westbourne/West Cliff area, indicating recurring flood occurrences in this ward. [IMG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Observed flooding incidents cluster in the southern/western wards including Westbourne/West Cliff; red dots overlap modelled flood&ndash;prone corridors, indicating localised inundation of low&ndash;lying streets and areas adjacent to watercourses on 3 July 2015. [IMG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",West Cliff,England,"Reported flooding incidents on 3 July 2015 included clusters of internal and highway flooding symbols in the western and central parts of the mapped area, indicating roads and some buildings were affected in Westbourne / West Cliff. [IMG] (p27)
Clustered locations of flooding incidents on 3rd July 2015 overlapped with previous reported flooding in the Westbourne/West Cliff area, indicating recurring flood occurrences in this ward. [IMG] (p29)
Observed flooding incidents cluster in the southern/western wards including Westbourne/West Cliff; red dots overlap modelled flood–prone corridors, indicating localised inundation of low–lying streets and areas adjacent to watercourses on 3 July 2015. [IMG] (p31)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7319361,-1.8509877,"<div id=""html_33495150eb73b1e4ef785169c8205ea8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Springbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>&#8216;East Cliff and Springbourne&#8217; ward label is on the map with observed red flood locations and predicted 1&ndash;in&ndash;100&ndash;year flood areas nearby, indicating localised surface&ndash;water and watercourse flooding impacts on 3 July 2015. [IMG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Springbourne,England,"‘East Cliff and Springbourne’ ward label is on the map with observed red flood locations and predicted 1–in–100–year flood areas nearby, indicating localised surface–water and watercourse flooding impacts on 3 July 2015. [IMG] (p31)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7676415,-1.8842778,"<div id=""html_a3b6caf6c1bef9ca2c04668a7435be5e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Northbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas were directly hit by the intense thunderstorm, resulting in significant surface water / flash flooding. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Northbourne,England,"Areas were directly hit by the intense thunderstorm, resulting in significant surface water / flash flooding. (p3)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.716917044392346,-1.9761308319391357,"<div id=""html_ab21a8b8d134fe4a982d6c6525500d4f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Poole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred in the eastern side of Poole as a result of the same intense thunderstorm. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Poole,England,Flooding occurred in the eastern side of Poole as a result of the same intense thunderstorm. (p3),,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.7428875,-1.8780686,"<div id=""html_8c81315c2f5888c005c211bef4094f90"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Winton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Winton area flooded due to a blockage in the local foul/combined sewer on 3rd July 2015; Wessex Water cleared the blockage. A bunded area stored less water than expected (tide marks), while considerable flows entered a playground upstream where a fence formed a dam, causing that area to store much of the displaced water. (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Winton,England,"The Winton area flooded due to a blockage in the local foul/combined sewer on 3rd July 2015; Wessex Water cleared the blockage. A bunded area stored less water than expected (tide marks), while considerable flows entered a playground upstream where a fence formed a dam, causing that area to store much of the displaced water. (p14)",,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-BCP,1,2015-07-03,50.72902079710117,-1.9228813264732476,"<div id=""html_d88ed7496cbdabfe72c9b08fddace21f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Branksome</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map of 3 July 2015 shows reported internal (property) and highway flooding incidents within the Talbot/Branksome area. Impacts recorded on the map include inundation of highways and internal flooding of buildings in the ward. [IMG] (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Branksome,England,Map of 3 July 2015 shows reported internal (property) and highway flooding incidents within the Talbot/Branksome area. Impacts recorded on the map include inundation of highways and internal flooding of buildings in the ward. [IMG] (p27),,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03.html,GB-BCP_1_2015-07-03,Bournemouth flooding 03 Jul 2015,Flooding In Bournemouth 3rd July 2015 Section 19 Report(Floods And Water Management Act 2010) for Flooding Advisory Group,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2015/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Flood-Report-3rd-July-2015-Final.pdf"
GB-LAN,19,2021-07-01,53.8865272,-2.3617251,"<div id=""html_57f2c03846363c2a6c503041b19b4c2d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clitheroe Road, Chatburn</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clitheroe Road was impacted by the July 2021 flooding and is named in the Section 19 investigation. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected the public highway adjacent to the Garden Centre. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Local drainage on Clitheroe Road was overwhelmed during the event; drainage speed was severely compromised contributing to surface water accumulation that affected the adjacent Garden Centre and the public highway. (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Clitheroe Road, Chatburn",England,"Clitheroe Road was impacted by the July 2021 flooding and is named in the Section 19 investigation. (p1)
Surface water flooding affected the public highway adjacent to the Garden Centre. (p3)
Local drainage on Clitheroe Road was overwhelmed during the event; drainage speed was severely compromised contributing to surface water accumulation that affected the adjacent Garden Centre and the public highway. (p4)",,GB-LAN_19_2021-07-01.html,GB-LAN_19_2021-07-01,Chatburn flooding 01 Jul 2021 - 31 Jul 2021,"July 2021 Flooding In Lancashire: Clitheroe Road, Chatburn, Ribble Valley",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-clitheroe-road-chatburn-july-2021.pdf
GB-LAN,19,2021-07-01,53.8855921,-2.3571849,"<div id=""html_f1b54b842e04245082b7ff0c5c9d3eb8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Worston Road, Chatburn</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected the public highway adjacent to the Garden Centre. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Local drainage capacity and flow from the public highway were severely compromised by constraints in the local watercourse network, causing surface water to accumulate on the highway and contributing to surface water runoff that entered the adjacent Shackleton's Garden Centre car park and business premises. (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Worston Road, Chatburn",England,"Surface water flooding affected the public highway adjacent to the Garden Centre. (p3)
