Flooding of business premises (Shackleton's Garden Centre) occurred when local drainage was overwhelmed during the July 2021 weather, causing surface water to accumulate in the Garden Centre car park and enter the premises through the main doors. (p4)",,GB-LAN_19_2021-07-01.html,GB-LAN_19_2021-07-01,Chatburn flooding 01 Jul 2021 - 31 Jul 2021,"July 2021 Flooding In Lancashire: Clitheroe Road, Chatburn, Ribble Valley",069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-clitheroe-road-chatburn-july-2021.pdf
GB-HEF,5,2020-02-16,52.1769203,-2.7146194,"<div id=""html_7260c22f314524929f548d6221809f7e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>A49 at Hope Under Dinmore</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents reported overland flows from the A49 contributing to property flooding in the area. (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,A49 at Hope Under Dinmore,England,Residents reported overland flows from the A49 contributing to property flooding in the area. (p2),,GB-HEF_5_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_5_2020-02-16,Hope Under Dinmore flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hope Under Dinmore,055/Herefordshire County/04/Hope/under/Dinmore.pdf
GB-HEF,5,2020-02-16,52.1714829,-2.7210031,"<div id=""html_f8c4062a1917dfdca76dc9e19fea655a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cherrybrook Close, Hope Under Dinmore</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway flooded signs were installed at Cherrybrook Close on 16 February 2020; properties in the immediate area reported flooding related to road runoff and the adjacent brook. (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,"Cherrybrook Close, Hope Under Dinmore",England,Highway flooded signs were installed at Cherrybrook Close on 16 February 2020; properties in the immediate area reported flooding related to road runoff and the adjacent brook. (p2),3 properties (p2),GB-HEF_5_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_5_2020-02-16,Hope Under Dinmore flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hope Under Dinmore,055/Herefordshire County/04/Hope/under/Dinmore.pdf
GB-HEF,5,2020-02-16,52.1676535,-2.7220302,"<div id=""html_dd60d7402bf80c1cfb32427869a81d1a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hope Under Dinmore</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cherry Brook broke its banks and caused localised fluvial flooding that flooded the highway (spilling below the railway via a bridge) and contributed to internal flooding of nearby properties. [MUL] (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties; 3 properties at Cherry Brook Close; flooding depths typically 6 inches to 2 ft, with one basement/cellar reported at 2&ndash;3 ft [MUL] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Hope Under Dinmore,England,Cherry Brook broke its banks and caused localised fluvial flooding that flooded the highway (spilling below the railway via a bridge) and contributed to internal flooding of nearby properties. [MUL] (p2),"15 properties; 3 properties at Cherry Brook Close; flooding depths typically 6 inches to 2 ft, with one basement/cellar reported at 2–3 ft [MUL] (p2)",GB-HEF_5_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_5_2020-02-16,Hope Under Dinmore flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Hope Under Dinmore,055/Herefordshire County/04/Hope/under/Dinmore.pdf
GB-CAM,18,2020-12-23,52.28486221017296,-0.2160429033702549,"<div id=""html_b2d697cda377cb3ab63fc665f64fd214"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Millennium Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flows were reported to have come out of bank from the High Street and downstream into the Millennium Green open space, inundating the green during the event; the watercourse then passes through a culvert under the railway where flows were impeded. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse running through Millennium Green was cleared of vegetation and debris by the Parish Council after the flood to improve flow and reduce future blockage. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The ordinary watercourse culvert beneath the railway at Millennium Green was identified for significant maintenance and clearance following the village flooding; the culvert has been inspected/targeted for clearance to reduce future flood risk. (p25)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Millennium Green,England,"Flows were reported to have come out of bank from the High Street and downstream into the Millennium Green open space, inundating the green during the event; the watercourse then passes through a culvert under the railway where flows were impeded. (p14)
The watercourse running through Millennium Green was cleared of vegetation and debris by the Parish Council after the flood to improve flow and reduce future blockage. (p21)
The ordinary watercourse culvert beneath the railway at Millennium Green was identified for significant maintenance and clearance following the village flooding; the culvert has been inspected/targeted for clearance to reduce future flood risk. (p25)",,GB-CAM_18_2020-12-23_etc.html,GB-CAM_18_2020-12-23_etc,Huntingdonshire flooding 23 Dec 2020 and Huntingdonshire flooding 14 Jan 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Offord Cluny & Offord D’arcy,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Offords-Winter-2020-21-Flood-Investigation-inc.-Clarification.pdf
GB-CAM,18,2020-12-23,52.2872136,-0.2139324,"<div id=""html_5db57c6009076c9f2eeebee36877d301"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Offord Cluny</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>North section experienced significant and prolonged highway flooding that resulted in a full road closure. Properties on the High Street (reported as a key risk area) suffered internal flooding with ingress that did not recede for a number of days; some affected properties subsequently experienced loss of access to foul sewerage provision for an extended period. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extensive surface water flooding of the highway (B1043), adjacent gardens and properties. Wetland to the east exceeded capacity and flooded the road, field edges and properties. Flood water reached significant depth and persisted; the Anglian Water sewer system was impacted and some residents were without foul sewerage provision. [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extensive surface water flooding from an overwhelmed wetland and high groundwater flooded the B1043 (High Street) and adjacent field edge, inundating gardens, outbuildings and properties to the east and causing some rear garden flooding. Floodwater reached significant depth and persisted, causing the road to be closed and the Anglian Water sewer system to be impacted, leaving some residents without foul sewerage provision. [TAB] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flows were reported to come out of bank from the High Street and flow downstream into Millennium Green and nearby industrial/business curtilage, contributing to property and open&ndash;space inundation; impeded culvert and vegetation downstream affected flow routes. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reports of flooding at High Street (North) were investigated by RMAs and the LLFA; site visits identified that a substantially blocked small&ndash;diameter Network Rail culvert in the vicinity likely contributed to local flooding at this location, prompting confirmation of maintenance actions. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localised flooding caused by reduced flow in the adjacent watercourse due to vegetation and silt build&ndash;up and an unconsented metal security fence obstructing the channel. Investigation and riparian works were carried out: fence removed (actioned under S23), vegetation and silt clearance advised and undertaken, resulting in improved flow by May 2021. [IMG] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sections of High Street (North and South) were affected during the 23 December 2020 event: surface water flooding occurred (both North and South), and groundwater flooding was recorded in the North. Contributing issues identified for High Street included sewer capacity problems, mis&ndash;connections to foul sewers, RMA operational issues and riparian maintenance shortcomings. [TAB] (p26)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>full road closure lasting approximately 3 weeks [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 45 cm; full road closure lasting approximately 3 weeks; loss of foul sewerage provision to properties for approximately 3 weeks [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 45 cm depth; road closure lasting approximately 3 weeks; approximately 3 weeks without foul sewerage provision [TAB] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flood depths approximately 20&ndash;45cm across the area; residents displaced for 6&ndash;8 months [TAB] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"High Street, Offord Cluny",England,"North section experienced significant and prolonged highway flooding that resulted in a full road closure. Properties on the High Street (reported as a key risk area) suffered internal flooding with ingress that did not recede for a number of days; some affected properties subsequently experienced loss of access to foul sewerage provision for an extended period. [PAG] (p11)
Extensive surface water flooding of the highway (B1043), adjacent gardens and properties. Wetland to the east exceeded capacity and flooded the road, field edges and properties. Flood water reached significant depth and persisted; the Anglian Water sewer system was impacted and some residents were without foul sewerage provision. [PAG,IMG] (p12)
Extensive surface water flooding from an overwhelmed wetland and high groundwater flooded the B1043 (High Street) and adjacent field edge, inundating gardens, outbuildings and properties to the east and causing some rear garden flooding. Floodwater reached significant depth and persisted, causing the road to be closed and the Anglian Water sewer system to be impacted, leaving some residents without foul sewerage provision. [TAB] (p13)
Flows were reported to come out of bank from the High Street and flow downstream into Millennium Green and nearby industrial/business curtilage, contributing to property and open–space inundation; impeded culvert and vegetation downstream affected flow routes. [TAB] (p14)
Reports of flooding at High Street (North) were investigated by RMAs and the LLFA; site visits identified that a substantially blocked small–diameter Network Rail culvert in the vicinity likely contributed to local flooding at this location, prompting confirmation of maintenance actions. [TAB] (p15)
Localised flooding caused by reduced flow in the adjacent watercourse due to vegetation and silt build–up and an unconsented metal security fence obstructing the channel. Investigation and riparian works were carried out: fence removed (actioned under S23), vegetation and silt clearance advised and undertaken, resulting in improved flow by May 2021. [IMG] (p18)
Sections of High Street (North and South) were affected during the 23 December 2020 event: surface water flooding occurred (both North and South), and groundwater flooding was recorded in the North. Contributing issues identified for High Street included sewer capacity problems, mis–connections to foul sewers, RMA operational issues and riparian maintenance shortcomings. [TAB] (p26)","full road closure lasting approximately 3 weeks [PAG] (p11)
approximately 45 cm; full road closure lasting approximately 3 weeks; loss of foul sewerage provision to properties for approximately 3 weeks [PAG,IMG] (p12)
approximately 45 cm depth; road closure lasting approximately 3 weeks; approximately 3 weeks without foul sewerage provision [TAB] (p13)
flood depths approximately 20–45cm across the area; residents displaced for 6–8 months [TAB] (p14)",GB-CAM_18_2020-12-23_etc.html,GB-CAM_18_2020-12-23_etc,Huntingdonshire flooding 23 Dec 2020 and Huntingdonshire flooding 14 Jan 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Offord Cluny & Offord D’arcy,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Offords-Winter-2020-21-Flood-Investigation-inc.-Clarification.pdf
GB-CAM,18,2020-12-23,52.2887905,-0.2155303,"<div id=""html_b93fd91518ab894dd78ccb98f7649586"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Station Lane, Offord Cluny</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported as one of the three key risk areas where internal property flooding occurred; ingress of water into properties did not recede for a number of days. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported as one of three key risk areas where internal property flooding was recorded during the winter 2020/21 event. [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Water levels rose rapidly on 23 December 2020, inundating Station Lane and nearby properties to a significant depth before receding. The banked railway acted as a barrier to runoff; outfalls to the main river were submerged. Overflow from a nearby Anglian Water pumping station was involved in local drainage. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties internally flooded to shallow depths; gardens and outbuildings also inundated. Residents were displaced from their homes. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reports of localised flooding on Station Lane associated with blocked/insufficient culverts, ditches and highway drainage. LLFA attended site to investigate, downstream investigations were initiated and highway gully cleansing frequency was increased as a response. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Station Lane experienced surface water flooding during the 23 December 2020 event. The investigation identified RMA operational issues and riparian maintenance issues as contributing factors to flooding at this location. [TAB] (p26)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 22 cm depth; receded within 5 hours (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>internal flooding up to approximately 22cm; gardens and outbuildings up to approximately 60cm; residents displaced for over 1 month [TAB] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Station Lane, Offord Cluny",England,"Reported as one of the three key risk areas where internal property flooding occurred; ingress of water into properties did not recede for a number of days. [PAG] (p11)
Reported as one of three key risk areas where internal property flooding was recorded during the winter 2020/21 event. [PAG,IMG] (p12)
Water levels rose rapidly on 23 December 2020, inundating Station Lane and nearby properties to a significant depth before receding. The banked railway acted as a barrier to runoff; outfalls to the main river were submerged. Overflow from a nearby Anglian Water pumping station was involved in local drainage. (p13)
Properties internally flooded to shallow depths; gardens and outbuildings also inundated. Residents were displaced from their homes. [TAB] (p14)
Reports of localised flooding on Station Lane associated with blocked/insufficient culverts, ditches and highway drainage. LLFA attended site to investigate, downstream investigations were initiated and highway gully cleansing frequency was increased as a response. [TAB] (p17)
Station Lane experienced surface water flooding during the 23 December 2020 event. The investigation identified RMA operational issues and riparian maintenance issues as contributing factors to flooding at this location. [TAB] (p26)","approximately 22 cm depth; receded within 5 hours (p13)
internal flooding up to approximately 22cm; gardens and outbuildings up to approximately 60cm; residents displaced for over 1 month [TAB] (p14)",GB-CAM_18_2020-12-23_etc.html,GB-CAM_18_2020-12-23_etc,Huntingdonshire flooding 23 Dec 2020 and Huntingdonshire flooding 14 Jan 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Offord Cluny & Offord D’arcy,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Offords-Winter-2020-21-Flood-Investigation-inc.-Clarification.pdf
GB-CAM,18,2020-12-23,52.2863582,-0.2124586,"<div id=""html_d4571b3b8f24e0df9f38dd31f3784022"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Park Way, Offord Cluny</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in the Parkway/Elm Close/Latin Close/New Road/High Street (South) cluster where internal property flooding was reported; affected properties experienced ingress of water that did not recede for several days. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Parkway were flooded internally due to overland surface water flows originating from a blocked section of the ordinary watercourse upstream; flooding affected properties and gardens in the street. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reports of localised flooding associated with an adjacent watercourse: observed silt and vegetation build&ndash;up and an obstructing security fence that impeded flow; site investigations undertaken, fence removed and further vegetation/silt clearance and maintenance planned to restore flow. [IMG] (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 20&ndash;45 cm; residents displaced for 6&ndash;8 months [TAB] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Park Way, Offord Cluny",England,"Included in the Parkway/Elm Close/Latin Close/New Road/High Street (South) cluster where internal property flooding was reported; affected properties experienced ingress of water that did not recede for several days. [PAG] (p11)
Properties on Parkway were flooded internally due to overland surface water flows originating from a blocked section of the ordinary watercourse upstream; flooding affected properties and gardens in the street. [TAB] (p14)
Reports of localised flooding associated with an adjacent watercourse: observed silt and vegetation build–up and an obstructing security fence that impeded flow; site investigations undertaken, fence removed and further vegetation/silt clearance and maintenance planned to restore flow. [IMG] (p18)",approximately 20–45 cm; residents displaced for 6–8 months [TAB] (p14),GB-CAM_18_2020-12-23_etc.html,GB-CAM_18_2020-12-23_etc,Huntingdonshire flooding 23 Dec 2020 and Huntingdonshire flooding 14 Jan 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Offord Cluny & Offord D’arcy,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Offords-Winter-2020-21-Flood-Investigation-inc.-Clarification.pdf
GB-CAM,18,2020-12-23,52.286667,-0.211582,"<div id=""html_4b41088ea491752ba2d0ca15152cb7bf"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Elm Drive, Offord Cluny</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the southern cluster (Parkway/Elm Close (sic)/Latin Close/New Road/High Street (South)) where internal property flooding was reported; properties experienced ingress of water that did not recede for a number of days. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the southern cluster (Parkway/Elm Close (sic)/Latin Close/New Road/High Street South) where internal and external property flooding incidents were reported. [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Elm Drive were flooded by surface water flows originating from blockage&ndash;induced overland flow; internal and external flooding affected properties and gardens. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Subject to investigations for reported flooding caused by obstructed watercourse/culvert and silt/vegetation build&ndash;up; remedial actions included riparian clearance and planned maintenance to reduce future blockages. [IMG] (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flood depths approximately 20&ndash;45cm across the area; residents displaced for 6&ndash;8 months [TAB] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Elm Drive, Offord Cluny",England,"Part of the southern cluster (Parkway/Elm Close (sic)/Latin Close/New Road/High Street (South)) where internal property flooding was reported; properties experienced ingress of water that did not recede for a number of days. [PAG] (p11)
