GB-NNH,24,2020-08-16,52.4175503,-0.6431175,"<div id=""html_ec1d9374e239fee03a3a99090dc9a644"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Northamptonshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in North Northamptonshire were affected by flooding, prompting Section 19 investigations by the Lead Local Flood Authority (NNC) and the need to record assets affecting flood risk on the LLFA register. (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,North Northamptonshire,England,"Properties in North Northamptonshire were affected by flooding, prompting Section 19 investigations by the Lead Local Flood Authority (NNC) and the need to record assets affecting flood risk on the LLFA register. (p26)",,GB-NNH_24_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_24_2020-08-16,Middleton flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Main Street, Middleton, 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Main Street, Middleton.pdf"
GB-NNH,24,2020-08-16,52.50087937173413,-0.7662326210665045,"<div id=""html_813261c9daf14f1b022283cd4a4991f8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Middleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Location of the flood incident in which an internal building flood occurred on Main Street; the incident met the threshold for formal investigation. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The area of Middleton contains unrecorded surface water sewer and a buried culvert; localized surface water ponding on the public highway was observed (westbound carriageway near the Manor House). (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The locality experienced surface water flooding that resulted in at least one internally flooded property (Main Street) and surface water on roads (Main Road) with standing water persisting for several weeks. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense heavy rainfall caused surface water drainage systems across the catchment to be unable to collect and convey rainwater, resulting in excess surface water flowing over ground following localised ground levels to low points around properties; affected areas are shown to be at high risk of surface water flooding. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 building; internal flooding experienced on more than one occasion in the last five years (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 road gullies blocked (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property flooded internally; external flood depth up to 0.5 m; standing water 4&ndash;6 weeks (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Middleton,England,"Location of the flood incident in which an internal building flood occurred on Main Street; the incident met the threshold for formal investigation. (p8)
