1 property flooded internally; external flood depth up to 0.5 m; standing water 4–6 weeks (p16)",GB-NNH_24_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_24_2020-08-16,Middleton flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Main Street, Middleton, 16 August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Main Street, Middleton.pdf"
GB-DER,4,2014-07-19,52.9212617,-1.4761491,"<div id=""html_0f8847d711192adc4b46d74b70b71ed8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Derby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the intense rainfall event on 19 July 2014, large areas of impermeable urban surface drained to adopted highways gullies and to public surface water sewers which outfall to an unnamed tributary of the River Derwent. This contributed to flooding of local roads and drainage infrastructure within the Derby City area. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Large areas experienced surface water flooding as intense rainfall overwhelmed local drainage networks, causing rapid runoff and accumulation in localised low spots; Spondon was particularly affected and a cluster of internally flooded properties occurred within this area. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The storm exceeded local drainage capacity resulting in surface water (highway) flooding and flooding to gardens and external property areas; locally low&ndash;lying areas were worst hit. (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,Derby,England,"During the intense rainfall event on 19 July 2014, large areas of impermeable urban surface drained to adopted highways gullies and to public surface water sewers which outfall to an unnamed tributary of the River Derwent. This contributed to flooding of local roads and drainage infrastructure within the Derby City area. [PAG] (p8)
Large areas experienced surface water flooding as intense rainfall overwhelmed local drainage networks, causing rapid runoff and accumulation in localised low spots; Spondon was particularly affected and a cluster of internally flooded properties occurred within this area. (p14)
The storm exceeded local drainage capacity resulting in surface water (highway) flooding and flooding to gardens and external property areas; locally low–lying areas were worst hit. (p15)",17 properties (p14),GB-DER_4_2014-07-19.html,GB-DER_4_2014-07-19,Spondon flooding 19 Jul 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Sandringham Drive, Spondon 19th July 2014",033/Derby/033/2014/Derby/Sandringham-Drive-Spondon-S19-Report.pdf
GB-DER,4,2014-07-19,52.9204799,-1.3930457,"<div id=""html_9757f8248be2cb44461b4c8a33704133"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sandringham Drive, Derby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe highway and external property flooding and part of the area where a large cluster of properties experienced internal flooding during the intense rainfall event. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Sandringham Drive were internally flooded during the Spondon flood event. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cluster of reported internal and external property flooding and highway flooding incidents (internal properties flooded) associated with the 19 July 2014 flood event. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The northernmost 250 m section of the road was affected by surface water flooding as runoff from higher land drained towards the surface water sewer and its outfall to an unnamed tributary of the River Derwent, leading to inundation of the carriageway. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood water reached ground&ndash;floor living areas of properties; properties in the street were part of a group that experienced severe external property flooding, in some cases close to entering ground&ndash;floor living areas. [MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from paved carriageways, footways and drives during the intense storm caused flooding into ground&ndash;floor living areas of properties. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from paved carriageway, footways and drives caused flooding to ground&ndash;floor living areas. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents reported foul (sewer) water flooding on this street; incidents were reported to Derby City Council and Severn Trent Water were asked to investigate reports on behalf of affected residents. (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 18 properties (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Part of up to 17 residential properties internally flooded (total across Sandringham Drive, Caernarvon Close, Holyrood Close and Harlech Close). (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>around 17 homes in total across Sandringham Drive, Caernarvon Close, Holyrood Close and Harlech Close experienced some depth of flood water in ground&ndash;floor living areas [MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Sandringham Drive, Derby",England,"Severe highway and external property flooding and part of the area where a large cluster of properties experienced internal flooding during the intense rainfall event. (p4)
Residential properties on Sandringham Drive were internally flooded during the Spondon flood event. (p5)
Cluster of reported internal and external property flooding and highway flooding incidents (internal properties flooded) associated with the 19 July 2014 flood event. (p6)
The northernmost 250 m section of the road was affected by surface water flooding as runoff from higher land drained towards the surface water sewer and its outfall to an unnamed tributary of the River Derwent, leading to inundation of the carriageway. (p8)
Flood water reached ground–floor living areas of properties; properties in the street were part of a group that experienced severe external property flooding, in some cases close to entering ground–floor living areas. [MUL] (p11)
Surface water runoff from paved carriageways, footways and drives during the intense storm caused flooding into ground–floor living areas of properties. (p13)
Surface water runoff from paved carriageway, footways and drives caused flooding to ground–floor living areas. (p14)
Residents reported foul (sewer) water flooding on this street; incidents were reported to Derby City Council and Severn Trent Water were asked to investigate reports on behalf of affected residents. (p17)","up to 18 properties (p4)
Part of up to 17 residential properties internally flooded (total across Sandringham Drive, Caernarvon Close, Holyrood Close and Harlech Close). (p5)
around 17 homes in total across Sandringham Drive, Caernarvon Close, Holyrood Close and Harlech Close experienced some depth of flood water in ground–floor living areas [MUL] (p11)
