GB-DER,4,2014-07-19,52.9222738,-1.3940171,"<div id=""html_54e6ce86d108f4ac35c37b3fafce5dc5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Caernarvon Close, Derby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe highway and external property flooding during the intense short&ndash;duration rainfall event. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Caernarvon Close were internally flooded during the Spondon flood event. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cluster of reported internal and external property flooding and highway flooding incidents (internal properties flooded) associated with the 19 July 2014 flood event. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced surface water flooding as part of the same urban drainage system that drains to the surface water sewer and its outfall to an unnamed tributary of the River Derwent, resulting in road inundation during the event. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Some properties experienced flood water in ground&ndash;floor living areas; areas also suffered severe external property flooding which in some cases approached or may have entered ground&ndash;floor living areas. [MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from the overwhelmed urban drainage and from inadequately draining flat roofs led to water entering properties (including via walls and high&ndash;level windows). Garden and highway flooding were widely reported; in one case foul water contributed with water rising into bathrooms. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding entered internal property areas; garden and highway flooding were also widely reported on the street. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Foul (sewer) water entered a property internally; report suggests surface water may have entered the foul system due to misconnections. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents reported foul (sewer) water flooding on this street; incidents were reported to Derby City Council and Severn Trent Water were asked to investigate reports on behalf of affected residents. (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 18 properties (event&ndash;wide) (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Part of up to 17 residential properties internally flooded (total across Sandringham Drive, Caernarvon Close, Holyrood Close and Harlech Close). (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>around 17 homes (total across Sandringham Drive, Caernarvon Close, Holyrood Close and Harlech Close) [MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>nine properties (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derby,"Caernarvon Close, Derby",England,"Severe highway and external property flooding during the intense short–duration rainfall event. (p4)
Residential properties on Caernarvon Close were internally flooded during the Spondon flood event. (p5)
Cluster of reported internal and external property flooding and highway flooding incidents (internal properties flooded) associated with the 19 July 2014 flood event. (p6)
