Highway flooding and flooding of external areas of properties occurred along Westway during the 12th July 2021 event; gullies on Westway had been included in a high–priority cleansing programme and most recently cleaned in Sept 2020. Access for emergency vehicles remained possible. [PAG] (p56)
The main surface–water sewer at Westway exhibited capacity and backflow issues contributing to flooding; proposed actions include increased inspection frequency and enlarging the sewer to limit backflows and increase capacity. [MUL] (p71)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.4040355,-0.2361652,"<div id=""html_90262f232d10dcb0d6b8573102266651"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Barnes Lane, London Borough of Merton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported in the report as a flooded location investigated (non&ndash;Section 19 investigation) under Hotspot 3 (West Barnes) associated with the 12 July rainfall event. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced flooding during the earlier (2016/2017) incidents and was one of the locations that flooded again during the July 2021 events. [MUL] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced flooding when river levels are high due to issues with the culverted Pyl Brook and a lateral connection with the sewer network; a private extension foundation severed and blocked the TWUL surface water line into the Pyl Brook culvert, contributing to flooding. TWUL progressing repair to improve capacity. [TAB] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>West Barnes Lane is recorded as a primary flooded location in the report and experienced surface&ndash;water flooding associated with the July 2021 events. [TAB,MUL] (p31)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway and external areas flooded during the 12th July 2021 rainfall event; runoff conveyed into the culverted section of the Pyl Brook and location is shown as being at medium&ndash;to&ndash;high surface water risk. [PAG] (p56)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>West Barnes Lane experienced flooding; on 25th July 2021 the number of flood reports was few, but the location experienced more substantial flooding during the 12th July 2021 event. [MUL] (p69)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme rainfall and increased surface runoff contributed to flooding risk along West Barnes Lane; recommendations include highway SuDS retrofits (e.g. permeable paving) to improve infiltration and reduce runoff into the local drainage system. [MUL] (p71)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"West Barnes Lane, London Borough of Merton",England,"Reported in the report as a flooded location investigated (non–Section 19 investigation) under Hotspot 3 (West Barnes) associated with the 12 July rainfall event. [PAG] (p8)
Experienced flooding during the earlier (2016/2017) incidents and was one of the locations that flooded again during the July 2021 events. [MUL] (p16)
Experienced flooding when river levels are high due to issues with the culverted Pyl Brook and a lateral connection with the sewer network; a private extension foundation severed and blocked the TWUL surface water line into the Pyl Brook culvert, contributing to flooding. TWUL progressing repair to improve capacity. [TAB] (p20)
West Barnes Lane is recorded as a primary flooded location in the report and experienced surface–water flooding associated with the July 2021 events. [TAB,MUL] (p31)
Highway and external areas flooded during the 12th July 2021 rainfall event; runoff conveyed into the culverted section of the Pyl Brook and location is shown as being at medium–to–high surface water risk. [PAG] (p56)
West Barnes Lane experienced flooding; on 25th July 2021 the number of flood reports was few, but the location experienced more substantial flooding during the 12th July 2021 event. [MUL] (p69)
Extreme rainfall and increased surface runoff contributed to flooding risk along West Barnes Lane; recommendations include highway SuDS retrofits (e.g. permeable paving) to improve infiltration and reduce runoff into the local drainage system. [MUL] (p71)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.3995208,-0.2424677,"<div id=""html_b9fbd0482541ecc54c3e71fd72206f40"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Burlington Road, West Barnes</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported in the report as a flooded location (including Shannon Corner junction) investigated as a non&ndash;Section 19 location under Hotspot 3 following the 12 July rainfall event. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded flooding during the borough's earlier incidents and again in the July 2021 flooding events. [MUL] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Burlington Road (with the Shannon Corner junction) is listed as a primary flooded location and experienced surface&ndash;water flooding during the July 2021 events. [TAB,MUL] (p31)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Junction area (Burlington Road and Shannon Corner) identified as one of the primarily affected locations within the hotspot during the 12th July 2021 rainfall event; highway flooding occurred at the junction. (p56)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding during 12th July 2021 was constrained to the highway at the eastern end of Burlington Road near Shannon Corner roundabout; likely caused by sewer surcharge/backflows due to limited sewer gradient and heavy siltation of local surface water sewers, with surface water flooding a contributory factor. Despite the highway flooding, emergency vehicle access remained possible. The location is known to have flooded during earlier incidents. [PAG] (p57)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>This location is known to flood regularly and flooded during the 12th July 2021 event. Flooding was likely caused by surcharging and backflows from the surface water sewer (limited gradient and heavy siltation), with surface water runoff likely contributory. [PAG] (p58)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Burlington Road and Shannon Corner junction experienced flooding; few reports were recorded on 25th July 2021 but the location experienced more substantial flooding during the 12th July 2021 event. [MUL] (p69)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water and sewer capacity issues affected Burlington Road; recommendations include increasing surface water sewer capacity and increasing gully&ndash;cleaning frequency to reduce street flooding. [MUL] (p72)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>three previous rainfall incidents [PAG] (p57)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>three previous rainfall incidents [PAG] (p58)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Burlington Road, West Barnes",England,"Reported in the report as a flooded location (including Shannon Corner junction) investigated as a non–Section 19 location under Hotspot 3 following the 12 July rainfall event. [PAG] (p8)
