GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.408999,-0.2213303,"<div id=""html_1ee66a9d05f1836673822db4d9809ec3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Dupont Road, London Borough of Merton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the Apostles area affected on 12 July 2021; experienced external flooding as part of hotspot&ndash;wide impacts and contributed to clustered internal/external/highway flooding across the area. [IMG] (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Thames Water visited Dupont Road and cleaned surface water sewer, removing a large quantity of concrete as part of actions to address surface&ndash;water flooding issues in the area. [TAB,MUL] (p45)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Most of Dupont Road was flooded by sewer overflow on 12th July 2021; the local surface water pipe (230&ndash;305mm) contains three 90&deg; turns where it joins the main on Bushey Road, creating blockage issues that contributed to the flooding. (p48)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Dupont Road, London Borough of Merton",England,"Part of the Apostles area affected on 12 July 2021; experienced external flooding as part of hotspot–wide impacts and contributed to clustered internal/external/highway flooding across the area. [IMG] (p33)
