GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.383422,-0.2209217,"<div id=""html_911c4031936e377dbc876bd1de382fae"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lynmouth Avenue, London Borough of Merton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported in the report as a flooded location in the Lower Morden area and investigated as a non&ndash;Section 19 location (grouped with Kingsbridge Road and Garth Road) following the 25 July rainfall event. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred at Lynmouth Avenue during the reported events; modelled maximum Hydromaster return period 1 in 2 to 1 in 5 yr (25 July 2021). [TAB] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooded the highway and external areas of properties; surface water was reported to run between properties from Kingsbridge Road into Lynmouth Avenue. Flooding was limited to external areas (no confirmed internal property flooding reported in Lynmouth Avenue during the event) and access for emergency vehicles remained possible. [PAG] (p67)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area between Garth Road and Lynmouth Avenue (including Lynmouth Gardens) was identified for use as flood storage to limit fluvial flooding from the nearby watercourse and to reduce surface&ndash;water impacts on adjacent properties and highways. [MUL] (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Lynmouth Avenue, London Borough of Merton",England,"Reported in the report as a flooded location in the Lower Morden area and investigated as a non–Section 19 location (grouped with Kingsbridge Road and Garth Road) following the 25 July rainfall event. (p8)
