Area between Garth Road and Lynmouth Avenue (including Lynmouth Gardens) was identified for use as flood storage to limit fluvial flooding from the nearby watercourse and to reduce surface–water impacts on adjacent properties and highways. [MUL] (p72)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.3849717,-0.2210763,"<div id=""html_b8888e111d92f1dd814e6f0e38452828"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kingsbridge Road, Lower Morden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road and surrounding residential area affected by flooding during the 25th July 2021 rainfall event (listed as a non&ndash;Section 19 flooded location under Hotspot 5 &ndash; Lower Morden). (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred at Kingsbridge Road during the reported events; modelled Hydromaster maximum return periods were 1 in 10 to 1 in 20 yr (12 July 2021) and <1 in 1 yr (25 July 2021). [TAB,MUL] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water affected highways and external areas of properties; surface water flow ran between properties from Kingsbridge Road toward Lynmouth Avenue. Flooding reported was largely external and did not meet the threshold for widespread internal property flooding. (p67)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Kingsbridge Road, Lower Morden",England,"Road and surrounding residential area affected by flooding during the 25th July 2021 rainfall event (listed as a non–Section 19 flooded location under Hotspot 5 – Lower Morden). (p8)
