GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.3901736,-0.2263873,"<div id=""html_c45f6bde4e82e7dc8201dbd9600de4d9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lower Morden Lane, Lower Morden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Lower Morden Lane was one of the Hydromaster hotspot gauge locations monitored on 25th July 2021 and experienced short&ndash;duration rainfall within the period of concentrated storm activity; it lay within the area of clustered surface water flood reports during the event. [IMG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A dislodged manhole cover was reported on Lower Morden Lane during the 25th July 2021 storm, associated with sewer surcharge activity as part of the combined sewer/surface&ndash;water flooding at this location. (p69)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Lower Morden Lane, Lower Morden",England,"Lower Morden Lane was one of the Hydromaster hotspot gauge locations monitored on 25th July 2021 and experienced short–duration rainfall within the period of concentrated storm activity; it lay within the area of clustered surface water flood reports during the event. [IMG] (p28)
A dislodged manhole cover was reported on Lower Morden Lane during the 25th July 2021 storm, associated with sewer surcharge activity as part of the combined sewer/surface–water flooding at this location. (p69)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.4212825,-0.1570466,"<div id=""html_875d6b8bb52860dbbfbe42a1593d20dd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Seely Road, London Borough of Merton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded as a Hydromaster hotspot gauge location showing intense, short&ndash;duration rainfall during the 25th July 2021 event; identified as part of an area where flood reports were clustered during the July 2021 rainfall events. [IMG] (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Seely Road, London Borough of Merton",England,"Recorded as a Hydromaster hotspot gauge location showing intense, short–duration rainfall during the 25th July 2021 event; identified as part of an area where flood reports were clustered during the July 2021 rainfall events. [IMG] (p28)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.3893834,-0.2264592,"<div id=""html_94c900e755f615985ab316d0e029e94d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wydell Close, Lower Morden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected Wydell Close during the reported event; Hydromaster analysis indicates a return period of 1 in 2 to 1 in 5 years and the TWUL/FEH13 return period is reported as 1 in 78.03 years for the event. [TAB] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of the road experienced flooding during the 25th July 2021 storm as a combination of surface water and sewer flooding; local sewer capacity was likely reduced by high Pyl Brook levels. Gullies across the location were inspected and cleared after the event. [PAG] (p69)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Wydell Close, Lower Morden",England,"Surface water flooding affected Wydell Close during the reported event; Hydromaster analysis indicates a return period of 1 in 2 to 1 in 5 years and the TWUL/FEH13 return period is reported as 1 in 78.03 years for the event. [TAB] (p32)
Parts of the road experienced flooding during the 25th July 2021 storm as a combination of surface water and sewer flooding; local sewer capacity was likely reduced by high Pyl Brook levels. Gullies across the location were inspected and cleared after the event. [PAG] (p69)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.3888279,-0.2263542,"<div id=""html_90239467b8ca25ce0664819f25bd1a97"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rosebery Close, London Borough of Merton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred at Rosebery Close (part of the Wydell/Rosebery/Essex/Garth Close group) during the reported events; modelled maximum Hydromaster return period 1 in 2 to 1 in 5 yr (25 July 2021). [TAB] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced sewer and surface&ndash;water flooding during the 25th July 2021 storm. Foul water and sewer surcharges (originating from Garth Road and local sewer network) flowed down to Rosebery Close due to topography and reduced sewer capacity associated with high adjacent Pyl Brook levels; properties lie predominantly within Flood Zone 3. (p69)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Rosebery Close, London Borough of Merton",England,"Surface water flooding occurred at Rosebery Close (part of the Wydell/Rosebery/Essex/Garth Close group) during the reported events; modelled maximum Hydromaster return period 1 in 2 to 1 in 5 yr (25 July 2021). [TAB] (p32)
Experienced sewer and surface–water flooding during the 25th July 2021 storm. Foul water and sewer surcharges (originating from Garth Road and local sewer network) flowed down to Rosebery Close due to topography and reduced sewer capacity associated with high adjacent Pyl Brook levels; properties lie predominantly within Flood Zone 3. (p69)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.3871949,-0.2253093,"<div id=""html_f4f372e1f119ea3682cd4f737c72204b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Garth Close, London Borough of Merton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Garth Close experienced surface water flooding on 25th July 2021 (Hydromaster modelling indicates a return period of 1 in 2 to 1 in 5 years for the event). [TAB] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Impacted on 25th July 2021 by sewer surcharges and surface water flooding; foul water surcharges from Garth Road flowed downslope into the local roads, and high Pyl Brook levels likely reduced sewer capacity. Gullies were later inspected and cleared. (p69)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Garth Close, London Borough of Merton",England,"Garth Close experienced surface water flooding on 25th July 2021 (Hydromaster modelling indicates a return period of 1 in 2 to 1 in 5 years for the event). [TAB] (p32)
Impacted on 25th July 2021 by sewer surcharges and surface water flooding; foul water surcharges from Garth Road flowed downslope into the local roads, and high Pyl Brook levels likely reduced sewer capacity. Gullies were later inspected and cleared. (p69)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.4114983,-0.2367156,"<div id=""html_4ed4f3641042da2844fd2f20997feec7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Richmond Road, Cottenham Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to a residential property (reported as part of two residential properties affected in the hotspot) on 12 July 2021; contributed to local highway disruption and access issues within the hotspot. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Richmond Road, Cottenham Park",England,Internal flooding to a residential property (reported as part of two residential properties affected in the hotspot) on 12 July 2021; contributed to local highway disruption and access issues within the hotspot. (p33),,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.4404999,-0.1943572,"<div id=""html_a9a8078e7ebed90d0282f84615e5aeb4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Acuba Road, London Borough of Merton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Council requested funding for SuDS features proposed along Mount Acuba Road (sic) as a response to flooding at the Raynes Park hotspot. [TAB] (p45)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Acuba Road, London Borough of Merton",England,Council requested funding for SuDS features proposed along Mount Acuba Road (sic) as a response to flooding at the Raynes Park hotspot. [TAB] (p45),,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.40821,-0.2280071,"<div id=""html_797608ccf93bb3cc591009b963ec48bf"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clifton Park Avenue, The Apostles</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Clifton Park Avenue were flooded by sewer overflow during the event; flooding was reported as primarily due to surface water sewer flooding. (p48)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Clifton Park Avenue, The Apostles",England,Parts of Clifton Park Avenue were flooded by sewer overflow during the event; flooding was reported as primarily due to surface water sewer flooding. (p48),,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.4048687,-0.2375022,"<div id=""html_54fd54a1dbea14cb52b6ded561312197"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bushey Road, London Borough of Merton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The rectangular trunk surface water sewer on Bushey Road received flows from Apostles area roads; its configuration and connections contributed to flow blockage and sewer overflows that caused flooding to nearby roads (notably Dupont Road and parts of Clifton Park Avenue) during the event. [PAG] (p48)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Bushey Road, London Borough of Merton",England,The rectangular trunk surface water sewer on Bushey Road received flows from Apostles area roads; its configuration and connections contributed to flow blockage and sewer overflows that caused flooding to nearby roads (notably Dupont Road and parts of Clifton Park Avenue) during the event. [PAG] (p48),,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.4263312,-0.2008793,"<div id=""html_3913a541b1f45f90248aaf910a6deeb2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Strathearn Road, Merton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding incidents at the Home Park Road hotspot were concentrated near the junction with Strathearn Road; nearby properties along the eastern section of Home Park Road experienced external and highways flooding. It is therefore likely the immediate junction area was affected by the same surface&ndash;water/sewer&ndash;driven flooding, though the report locates most impacts on Home Park Road itself. [IMG] (p49)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Strathearn Road, Merton",England,"Flooding incidents at the Home Park Road hotspot were concentrated near the junction with Strathearn Road; nearby properties along the eastern section of Home Park Road experienced external and highways flooding. It is therefore likely the immediate junction area was affected by the same surface–water/sewer–driven flooding, though the report locates most impacts on Home Park Road itself. [IMG] (p49)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.4294171,-0.2000866,"<div id=""html_b082642045914617df103646ca70a10d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kenilworth Avenue, London Borough of Merton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The eastern&ndash;most portion of Home Park Road flooded near the junction with Kenilworth Avenue; properties in that stretch experienced external and highways flooding, indicating the immediate junction area was affected by the same surface&ndash;water/sewer&ndash;driven flooding. The report does not explicitly state flooding within Kenilworth Avenue itself. [IMG] (p49)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flows and a 305mm diameter sewer from Kenilworth Avenue converge onto the 380mm pipe at the eastern end of Home Park Road; the high&ndash;risk stretch of Home Park Road extends from its junction with Kenilworth Avenue to its junction with Vineyard Hill Road, and runoff from Kenilworth contributed to surface water accumulation and flooding at the Home Park Road low point and nearby properties during the 12th July 2021 event. [PAG] (p51)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Kenilworth Avenue, London Borough of Merton",England,"The eastern–most portion of Home Park Road flooded near the junction with Kenilworth Avenue; properties in that stretch experienced external and highways flooding, indicating the immediate junction area was affected by the same surface–water/sewer–driven flooding. The report does not explicitly state flooding within Kenilworth Avenue itself. [IMG] (p49)
Surface water flows and a 305mm diameter sewer from Kenilworth Avenue converge onto the 380mm pipe at the eastern end of Home Park Road; the high–risk stretch of Home Park Road extends from its junction with Kenilworth Avenue to its junction with Vineyard Hill Road, and runoff from Kenilworth contributed to surface water accumulation and flooding at the Home Park Road low point and nearby properties during the 12th July 2021 event. [PAG] (p51)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.429871,-0.2009572,"<div id=""html_75f7c4039d584a130e57d3cfd78b7540"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Dora Road, Wimbledon Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A surface water sewer running below Home Park Road near the junction with Dora Road partially collapsed during the event. This sewer failure was associated with local sewer overflow/flooding and contributed to the internal and external flooding experienced by properties in the Home Park Road hotspot. [IMG] (p49)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>305mm diameter surface water pipes from Dora Road flow toward and converge onto the 380mm pipe at the eastern end of Home Park Road, contributing runoff into the Home Park Road low point and increasing surface water flooding risk during the 12th July 2021 rainfall event. [PAG] (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The surface water sewer along Home Park Road at the junction with Dora Road partially collapsed during the 12 July 2021 rainfall event, reducing the sewer system's capacity and thereby exacerbating flood impacts in the immediate area. (p55)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential properties; 4 instances of sewer flooding [IMG] (p49)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Dora Road, Wimbledon Park",England,"A surface water sewer running below Home Park Road near the junction with Dora Road partially collapsed during the event. This sewer failure was associated with local sewer overflow/flooding and contributed to the internal and external flooding experienced by properties in the Home Park Road hotspot. [IMG] (p49)
305mm diameter surface water pipes from Dora Road flow toward and converge onto the 380mm pipe at the eastern end of Home Park Road, contributing runoff into the Home Park Road low point and increasing surface water flooding risk during the 12th July 2021 rainfall event. [PAG] (p51)
The surface water sewer along Home Park Road at the junction with Dora Road partially collapsed during the 12 July 2021 rainfall event, reducing the sewer system's capacity and thereby exacerbating flood impacts in the immediate area. (p55)",2 residential properties; 4 instances of sewer flooding [IMG] (p49),GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.3940315,-0.2354095,"<div id=""html_0f3e2737d528be3019502b8acbd447af"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Arthur Road, West Barnes</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding incidents (a mix of internal, external and highway surface water flooding) were concentrated near the intersection with Arthur Road, indicating the Arthur Road area/adjacent junction experienced flood impacts during the event. [IMG] (p49)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood incident markers are clustered near the intersection of Home Park Road and Arthur Road. This indicates highways flooding on the adjacent section of Home Park Road (road covered by several inches of floodwater) and nearby external flooding of property gardens; the event was associated with sewer failure in the vicinity (partial collapse of a surface water sewer near the Dora Road junction). It is unclear whether properties on Arthur Road itself were internally flooded, but flood markers are concentrated at the intersection. [IMG] (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Steep topography from Arthur Road (approx. 18m fall to its junction with Home Park Road) generated runoff that flowed downslope towards the eastern low point of Home Park Road, contributing to surface water accumulation and flooding at the low point and properties behind it during the 12th July 2021 rainfall event. (p51)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two residential properties [IMG] (p50)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Arthur Road, West Barnes",England,"Flooding incidents (a mix of internal, external and highway surface water flooding) were concentrated near the intersection with Arthur Road, indicating the Arthur Road area/adjacent junction experienced flood impacts during the event. [IMG] (p49)
Flood incident markers are clustered near the intersection of Home Park Road and Arthur Road. This indicates highways flooding on the adjacent section of Home Park Road (road covered by several inches of floodwater) and nearby external flooding of property gardens; the event was associated with sewer failure in the vicinity (partial collapse of a surface water sewer near the Dora Road junction). It is unclear whether properties on Arthur Road itself were internally flooded, but flood markers are concentrated at the intersection. [IMG] (p50)
Steep topography from Arthur Road (approx. 18m fall to its junction with Home Park Road) generated runoff that flowed downslope towards the eastern low point of Home Park Road, contributing to surface water accumulation and flooding at the low point and properties behind it during the 12th July 2021 rainfall event. (p51)",two residential properties [IMG] (p50),GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.4309505,-0.2015354,"<div id=""html_3ae4a8fe5cb4dd7eab6b1dec0925e2b4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Vineyard Hill Road, Wimbledon Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A 305mm diameter surface water sewer flows from Vineyard Hill Road and converges onto the 380mm pipe at the eastern end of Home Park Road, conveying runoff that contributed to surface water accumulation and flooding at Home Park Road and adjacent properties during the 12th July 2021 intense rainfall. [PAG] (p51)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Vineyard Hill Road, Wimbledon Park",England,"A 305mm diameter surface water sewer flows from Vineyard Hill Road and converges onto the 380mm pipe at the eastern end of Home Park Road, conveying runoff that contributed to surface water accumulation and flooding at Home Park Road and adjacent properties during the 12th July 2021 intense rainfall. [PAG] (p51)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.403324,-0.2338602,"<div id=""html_df5e90d68bcee633a7df2eae7995ebb9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Linkway, West Barnes</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One instance of internal flooding to a garage outbuilding within a residential property on Linkway during the 12th July 2021 rainfall event; surrounding highways/external areas in the locality also flooded. [PAG] (p56)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 garage outbuilding [PAG] (p56)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Linkway, West Barnes",England,One instance of internal flooding to a garage outbuilding within a residential property on Linkway during the 12th July 2021 rainfall event; surrounding highways/external areas in the locality also flooded. [PAG] (p56),1 garage outbuilding [PAG] (p56),GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.4053145,-0.2123873,"<div id=""html_2afa4785940d8473de0f5e5d6913a796"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cannon Hill Lane, Merton Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced flooding during the rainfall event on 12th July 2021. Flooding extent was limited and was not sufficiently extensive to trigger a full Section 19 investigation. (p58)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,"Cannon Hill Lane, Merton Park",England,Experienced flooding during the rainfall event on 12th July 2021. Flooding extent was limited and was not sufficiently extensive to trigger a full Section 19 investigation. (p58),,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
