GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.4079938,-0.2019654,"<div id=""html_8b4f9b5faecad0ecdc50cf31f378f167"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Merton Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Merton Park ward (including Leafield Road) experienced flooding during the rainfall event on 12th July 2021; extent was limited. (p58)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Streets within the Merton Park ward (including Crown Lane and Stratton Road) experienced surface water flooding during the 25th July 2021 event. (p69)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,Merton Park,England,"Parts of Merton Park ward (including Leafield Road) experienced flooding during the rainfall event on 12th July 2021; extent was limited. (p58)
Streets within the Merton Park ward (including Crown Lane and Stratton Road) experienced surface water flooding during the 25th July 2021 event. (p69)",,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc.html,GB-MRT_1_2021-07-12_etc,London Borough of Merton flooding 12 Jul 2021 and London Borough of Merton flooding 25 Jul 2021,Merton Section 19 Flood Risk Investigation Report,079/Merton/Merton S19 Report v1.3 (inc DGF Obs).pdf
GB-MRT,1,2021-07-12,51.39625412125298,-0.23998191541154293,"<div id=""html_63b07eaaae220ab49457621ec5d35a18"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Motspur Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding incidents in the Motspur Park area were concentrated along Marina Avenue, causing internal flooding to residential properties, extensive highway and footway flooding on Marina Avenue, and inundation of adjacent playing fields. [IMG] (p59)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding across Sir Joseph Hood Memorial Park and playing fields during the 25 July 2021 event: internal flooding to one residential property within the pavilion on council&ndash;owned land; large areas of the playing fields (particularly those nearer the river line to the west) were inundated; a TWUL record indicates one instance of sewer flooding in postcode KT3 6 within this hotspot. (p60)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding on 25th July 2021 affected the Marina Avenue & Sir Joseph Hood hotspot in Motspur Park. Flood Zone 3 inundation reached properties within the Sir Joseph Hood area and rear external areas of residential properties along the south side of Marina Avenue; Marina Avenue and nearby road/highway areas experienced flood impacts (map also shows internal/external/highways flooding symbols along Marina Avenue and adjacent infrastructure such as the Sports/Leisure Centre). [IMG] (p63)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential properties; 1 residential property (pavilion in Sir Joseph Hood Memorial Park); approximately 30m of road; approximately 65m of footway [IMG] (p59)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential property; one instance of sewer flooding in postcode KT3 6 (p60)</p></div></div></body></div>",Merton,Motspur Park,England,"Flooding incidents in the Motspur Park area were concentrated along Marina Avenue, causing internal flooding to residential properties, extensive highway and footway flooding on Marina Avenue, and inundation of adjacent playing fields. [IMG] (p59)
Flooding across Sir Joseph Hood Memorial Park and playing fields during the 25 July 2021 event: internal flooding to one residential property within the pavilion on council–owned land; large areas of the playing fields (particularly those nearer the river line to the west) were inundated; a TWUL record indicates one instance of sewer flooding in postcode KT3 6 within this hotspot. (p60)
Fluvial flooding on 25th July 2021 affected the Marina Avenue & Sir Joseph Hood hotspot in Motspur Park. Flood Zone 3 inundation reached properties within the Sir Joseph Hood area and rear external areas of residential properties along the south side of Marina Avenue; Marina Avenue and nearby road/highway areas experienced flood impacts (map also shows internal/external/highways flooding symbols along Marina Avenue and adjacent infrastructure such as the Sports/Leisure Centre). [IMG] (p63)","2 residential properties; 1 residential property (pavilion in Sir Joseph Hood Memorial Park); approximately 30m of road; approximately 65m of footway [IMG] (p59)
