GB-CAM,19,2020-12-04,52.3759996,-0.0950096,"<div id=""html_95a60058007beccad8a3e6e843c0e552"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Warboys Road, Old Hurst</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater affected external premises (gardens) along Warboys Road; no internal property flooding recorded for the Warboys Road entry in the table. [TAB] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Warboys Road area was associated with flooding in winter 2020; a nearby ditch (south and east of the flooded area) had poor long&ndash;term maintenance which likely increased local flood risk. At LLFA request the highways authority CCTV&ndash;surveyed surface water and highways drains on Warboys Road; maintenance works were carried out including removal of a blocked piped access crossing and identification of pipe sections requiring repair to improve conveyance. [IMG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Gardens were flooded; floodwater reached up to about 15 cm depth and was recorded approximately 2.5 cm below property thresholds. [TAB,PAG] (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>0 properties with internal property flooding [TAB] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>c.15cm (depth); 2.5cm below threshold [TAB,PAG] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Warboys Road, Old Hurst",England,"Floodwater affected external premises (gardens) along Warboys Road; no internal property flooding recorded for the Warboys Road entry in the table. [TAB] (p10)
