GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.2458716,-1.6173324,"<div id=""html_869c1578f2ff7edd61bce921f97efd29"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cock Hill, Baslow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Cock Hill were internally flooded as floodwaters from Bar Brook reached the street low point in Nether End. [IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cock Hill sits at a local low point in the valley adjacent to Bar Brook. Flood mapping and the report indicate properties and the road at Cock Hill lie within Flood Zone 3 and were affected by flooding during the October 2023 event, causing property inundation and transport/access disruption adjacent to the watercourse. [IMG,PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Bar Brook exceeded its banks and the long&ndash;term surface&ndash;water risk map shows the highest surface&ndash;water flood risk where watercourses cross Cock Hill; properties and the road adjacent to the stream are reported or mapped as being affected by flooding during the incident (inferred from the brook overtopping and the mapped high&ndash;risk area). [PAG,IMG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Large volumes of surface water flowed from north of Cock Hill (from springs related to old mine workings) down the hill toward a low point on Cock Hill (A619). This surface&ndash;water flow, and associated road erosion (and anecdotal reports of a burst water main), contributed to flooding of the Nether End car park, Baslow Village Hall and nearby properties. (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 homes [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Cock Hill, Baslow",England,"Residential properties on Cock Hill were internally flooded as floodwaters from Bar Brook reached the street low point in Nether End. [IMG] (p12)
Cock Hill sits at a local low point in the valley adjacent to Bar Brook. Flood mapping and the report indicate properties and the road at Cock Hill lie within Flood Zone 3 and were affected by flooding during the October 2023 event, causing property inundation and transport/access disruption adjacent to the watercourse. [IMG,PAG] (p13)
Bar Brook exceeded its banks and the long–term surface–water risk map shows the highest surface–water flood risk where watercourses cross Cock Hill; properties and the road adjacent to the stream are reported or mapped as being affected by flooding during the incident (inferred from the brook overtopping and the mapped high–risk area). [PAG,IMG] (p14)
Large volumes of surface water flowed from north of Cock Hill (from springs related to old mine workings) down the hill toward a low point on Cock Hill (A619). This surface–water flow, and associated road erosion (and anecdotal reports of a burst water main), contributed to flooding of the Nether End car park, Baslow Village Hall and nearby properties. (p15)",4 homes [IMG] (p12),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.2461829,-1.6201611,"<div id=""html_802cc20885119e19309f6926762cf332"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church Lane, Baslow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Church Lane were internally flooded due to overtopping/flooding from Bar Brook (properties lie on the brook's floodplain and within Flood Zone 3). [IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Church Lane is identified on the flood&ndash;zone map as falling within the Flood Zone / Flood Alert area along Bar Brook. Properties and sections of Church Lane adjacent to the brook were within Flood Zone 3 and experienced flooding impacts during the October 2023 event, affecting buildings and transport routes. [IMG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The surface&ndash;water risk map highlights high risk where the watercourse crosses Church Lane and, given Bar Brook overtopped its banks during the event, buildings and the road at Church Lane are reported or mapped as being affected by flooding. [PAG,IMG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water runoff flowed through the low point/triangle of grass and trees between Church Lane and Cock Hill, directing water southwards and contributing to flooding of Nether End car park and Baslow Village Hall. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood&ndash;related gravel accumulation occurred downstream of the bridge at Church Lane; the Environment Agency removed the gravel. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 homes flooded [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Church Lane, Baslow",England,"Residential properties on Church Lane were internally flooded due to overtopping/flooding from Bar Brook (properties lie on the brook's floodplain and within Flood Zone 3). [IMG] (p12)
Church Lane is identified on the flood–zone map as falling within the Flood Zone / Flood Alert area along Bar Brook. Properties and sections of Church Lane adjacent to the brook were within Flood Zone 3 and experienced flooding impacts during the October 2023 event, affecting buildings and transport routes. [IMG] (p13)
The surface–water risk map highlights high risk where the watercourse crosses Church Lane and, given Bar Brook overtopped its banks during the event, buildings and the road at Church Lane are reported or mapped as being affected by flooding. [PAG,IMG] (p14)
Surface–water runoff flowed through the low point/triangle of grass and trees between Church Lane and Cock Hill, directing water southwards and contributing to flooding of Nether End car park and Baslow Village Hall. (p15)
Flood–related gravel accumulation occurred downstream of the bridge at Church Lane; the Environment Agency removed the gravel. (p16)",5 homes flooded [IMG] (p12),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
