Soughs (old mine drainage) surcharged and flooded properties and The Nook road; surface water runoff from the steep hillside also contributed to flooding of low–lying properties adjacent to the watercourse. [PAG] (p40)",part of 7 homes flooded internally; part of 3 non–residential properties flooded [PAG] (p39),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.273015030608015,-1.6485779337316915,"<div id=""html_50c8e56f902c62e3a3ae9f82495f709e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Edge View, Stoney Middleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected the highway and existing properties in the Edge View/Meadow Close area; Derbyshire County Council is delivering a small mitigation scheme to reduce flood risk to the highway and properties. (p40)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Edge View, Stoney Middleton",England,Flooding affected the highway and existing properties in the Edge View/Meadow Close area; Derbyshire County Council is delivering a small mitigation scheme to reduce flood risk to the highway and properties. (p40),,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.2730241,-1.648594,"<div id=""html_966ed85dcd741e4e0427faf48b694916"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Meadow Close, Stoney Middleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected properties in the Edge View/Meadow Close area; a small mitigation scheme will be delivered by Derbyshire County Council to reduce flood risk to the highway and existing properties. (p40)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Meadow Close, Stoney Middleton",England,Flooding affected properties in the Edge View/Meadow Close area; a small mitigation scheme will be delivered by Derbyshire County Council to reduce flood risk to the highway and existing properties. (p40),,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9861914,-1.4865131,"<div id=""html_7df52b588bd32b283459a277d9ee27a2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ecclesbourne Avenue, Duffield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes on Ecclesbourne Avenue were flooded during the event; flooding is spatially associated with the nearby River Ecclesbourne and nearby culverted watercourses, and the street is noted as having a medium chance of surface water flooding. [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Some properties on Ecclesbourne Avenue are reported as having flooded and are identified as having a medium chance (1%&ndash;3.3% AEP) of surface water flooding. [PAG] (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Ecclesbourne Avenue were among those that flooded during the event; these properties are shown on the Long Term Flood Risk Map as having a medium chance (1%&ndash;3.3% AEP) of surface water flooding. [IMG,PAG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the tennis courts flowed into rear gardens and onto the road around 14:47 on 20 October 2023, with several properties on the road internally flooding. (p44)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the overtopped tennis courts and overflowing River Ecclesbourne flowed into rear gardens and onto the road, causing several properties on Ecclesbourne Avenue to flood internally. [IMG] (p45)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 homes flooded [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>23 homes (combined on Village Court and Ecclesbourne Avenue) (p44)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>23 homes (across Village Court and Ecclesbourne Avenue) [IMG] (p45)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Ecclesbourne Avenue, Duffield",England,"Homes on Ecclesbourne Avenue were flooded during the event; flooding is spatially associated with the nearby River Ecclesbourne and nearby culverted watercourses, and the street is noted as having a medium chance of surface water flooding. [IMG,PAG] (p41)
