Flood defence walls were overtopped at about 14:04 on 20 Oct 2023, causing floodwater to run across the tennis courts and into properties on Village Court (including the tennis club). [IMG,PAG] (p46)","19 homes [IMG,PAG] (p41)
23 homes (combined on Village Court and Ecclesbourne Avenue) [PAG] (p44)
23 homes (across Village Court and Ecclesbourne Avenue) (p45)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9852889,-1.4910953,"<div id=""html_f62626b4c5f813461700a5a855f3d7f2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wirksworth Road, Duffield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Ecclesbourne led to internal flooding of one property on Wirksworth Road. (p44)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Wirksworth Road, Duffield",England,Flooding from the River Ecclesbourne led to internal flooding of one property on Wirksworth Road. (p44),1 property (p44),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9876338,-1.4873368,"<div id=""html_668ff2248a8f62aafad890322165b556"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chapel Street, Duffield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Ecclesbourne corridor at/adjacent to Chapel Street is mapped as a concentrated high surface&ndash;water&ndash;flood&ndash;risk area. Maintenance works (600 tonnes of silt removed under the bridge at Town Street and Chapel Street) were carried out two months before the 18&ndash;21 Oct 2023 event to improve conveyance, and the area was within the Duffield locations associated with flooded properties and flood warnings during that event. It is therefore identified as being in the area affected by flooding risk during 18&ndash;21 Oct 2023 (some uncertainty remains about whether individual properties on Chapel Street were recorded as flooded). [IMG,PAG] (p43)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>33 flooded properties across Duffield were reported during Storm Babet; 33 flooded properties were within flood alert/warning areas (community&ndash;wide figure). [IMG,PAG] (p43)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Chapel Street, Duffield",England,"The River Ecclesbourne corridor at/adjacent to Chapel Street is mapped as a concentrated high surface–water–flood–risk area. Maintenance works (600 tonnes of silt removed under the bridge at Town Street and Chapel Street) were carried out two months before the 18–21 Oct 2023 event to improve conveyance, and the area was within the Duffield locations associated with flooded properties and flood warnings during that event. It is therefore identified as being in the area affected by flooding risk during 18–21 Oct 2023 (some uncertainty remains about whether individual properties on Chapel Street were recorded as flooded). [IMG,PAG] (p43)","33 flooded properties across Duffield were reported during Storm Babet; 33 flooded properties were within flood alert/warning areas (community–wide figure). [IMG,PAG] (p43)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9846214,-1.4894557,"<div id=""html_686e2a6abacb005571fbb02ed2fb905c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ecclesbourne Close, Duffield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map evidence and Flood Zone extents indicate the street lies within the river floodplain adjacent to the River Ecclesbourne, putting properties on Ecclesbourne Close at risk of river flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p42)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Ecclesbourne Close, Duffield",England,"Map evidence and Flood Zone extents indicate the street lies within the river floodplain adjacent to the River Ecclesbourne, putting properties on Ecclesbourne Close at risk of river flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p42)",,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9836871,-1.492348,"<div id=""html_734e0e64a5eb121528929cfb1601fd21"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Granville Close, Duffield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The map shows Flood Zone extents encroaching into residential streets in this area; Granville Close is labelled within that area and therefore was at risk of, and likely affected by, river flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p42)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Granville Close, Duffield",England,"The map shows Flood Zone extents encroaching into residential streets in this area; Granville Close is labelled within that area and therefore was at risk of, and likely affected by, river flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p42)",,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9848579,-1.4961235,"<div id=""html_5e95f85f2390a245eab9cb85f6d1b54c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hill View, Duffield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hill View appears within the mapped Flood Zone extents that extend from the River Ecclesbourne into nearby residential streets, indicating exposure to river flooding during the event. [IMG] (p42)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Hill View, Duffield",England,"Hill View appears within the mapped Flood Zone extents that extend from the River Ecclesbourne into nearby residential streets, indicating exposure to river flooding during the event. [IMG] (p42)",,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9892811,-1.4940365,"<div id=""html_ab8594085d6220fc3a3139f28b2f38ef"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Holloway Road, Duffield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Holloway Road is shown on the flood map in an area where Flood Zone shading extends into built&ndash;up streets adjacent to the River Ecclesbourne, indicating it was exposed to river flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Ecclesbourne overflowed its left bank and flowed overland via the riverside footpath, leading to flooding on Holloway Road (and Tamworth Street); one property on Holloway Road internally flooded. (p44)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the overflowing watercourse at Duck Island reached Holloway Road, causing flooding of the road surface. [IMG] (p46)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Holloway Road, Duffield",England,"Holloway Road is shown on the flood map in an area where Flood Zone shading extends into built–up streets adjacent to the River Ecclesbourne, indicating it was exposed to river flooding during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p42)
River Ecclesbourne overflowed its left bank and flowed overland via the riverside footpath, leading to flooding on Holloway Road (and Tamworth Street); one property on Holloway Road internally flooded. (p44)
Floodwater from the overflowing watercourse at Duck Island reached Holloway Road, causing flooding of the road surface. [IMG] (p46)",1 property (p44),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9864411,-1.4877732,"<div id=""html_0e3b0e0a56893172d440b7b228e45540"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Town Street, Duffield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Town Street (A6) is mapped with a high chance of surface&ndash;water flooding. Two months before the 18&ndash;21 Oct 2023 event, 600 tonnes of silt were removed from under the bridge at Town Street (and Chapel Street) to improve conveyance. Town Street was therefore within the area of concern and mapped high&ndash;risk corridors associated with the reported flooding and flood warnings during 18&ndash;21 Oct 2023 (uncertain which specific Town Street properties flooded). [IMG,PAG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the River Ecclesbourne and overtopping defences flowed down Town Street (by ~16:00 on 20 Oct), leading to road closure and internal flooding of residential and non&ndash;residential properties. (p44)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Water flowed down Town Street, forcing the road to be closed for safety. [IMG] (p46)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>33 flooded properties across Duffield were reported during Storm Babet; 33 flooded properties were within flood alert/warning areas (community&ndash;wide figure). [IMG,PAG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 homes internally flooded; 2 non&ndash;residential properties internally flooded (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Town Street, Duffield",England,"Town Street (A6) is mapped with a high chance of surface–water flooding. Two months before the 18–21 Oct 2023 event, 600 tonnes of silt were removed from under the bridge at Town Street (and Chapel Street) to improve conveyance. Town Street was therefore within the area of concern and mapped high–risk corridors associated with the reported flooding and flood warnings during 18–21 Oct 2023 (uncertain which specific Town Street properties flooded). [IMG,PAG] (p43)
Floodwater from the River Ecclesbourne and overtopping defences flowed down Town Street (by ~16:00 on 20 Oct), leading to road closure and internal flooding of residential and non–residential properties. (p44)
