GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.1628532,-1.4200396,"<div id=""html_6bf2cecc14c1a527467a84d909252f8f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Windermere Road, Clay Cross</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Windermere Road flooded internally during Storm Babet; the east side of Windermere Road is within Flood Zone 3 and was among the locations where homes were inundated. [IMG,PAG] (p56)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties adjacent to Windermere Road were located within Flood Zones 2 and 3 and experienced flooding risk from Smithy Brook (river flooding). The Long Term Flood Risk Map indicates many properties on the east side have medium&ndash;high surface water flood risk and some properties (including on the west side) experienced internal flooding during the event. [IMG,PAG] (p57)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread internal flooding of residential properties: all properties on the east side of Windemere Road flooded internally and the majority of properties on the west side flooded; floodwater marked about halfway up a door/wall in at least one property. (p58)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>45 residential properties (across the affected Clay Cross area including Rydal Way and Windermere Road) [IMG,PAG] (p56)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>45 properties (homes) internally flooded across the community; this total includes all properties on the east side of Windemere Road and the majority on the west side. (p58)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Windermere Road, Clay Cross",England,"Properties on Windermere Road flooded internally during Storm Babet; the east side of Windermere Road is within Flood Zone 3 and was among the locations where homes were inundated. [IMG,PAG] (p56)
Residential properties adjacent to Windermere Road were located within Flood Zones 2 and 3 and experienced flooding risk from Smithy Brook (river flooding). The Long Term Flood Risk Map indicates many properties on the east side have medium–high surface water flood risk and some properties (including on the west side) experienced internal flooding during the event. [IMG,PAG] (p57)
Widespread internal flooding of residential properties: all properties on the east side of Windemere Road flooded internally and the majority of properties on the west side flooded; floodwater marked about halfway up a door/wall in at least one property. (p58)","45 residential properties (across the affected Clay Cross area including Rydal Way and Windermere Road) [IMG,PAG] (p56)
45 properties (homes) internally flooded across the community; this total includes all properties on the east side of Windemere Road and the majority on the west side. (p58)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.1632548,-1.4212512,"<div id=""html_b962b9b43319ea22dbd7c4eb63f847f3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rydal Way, Clay Cross</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties adjacent to Smithy Brook/Meadow Farm Pond caused by the watercourse overtopping during Storm Babet; the pink&ndash;mapped cluster of 45 homes (concentrated along Rydal Way and Windermere Road) flooded internally. [IMG] (p56)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties and the road adjacent to Rydal Way are mapped within or immediately adjacent to Flood Zones 2 and 3 along Smithy Brook; the Flood Map shows properties that flooded were located in these zones, indicating the Rydal Way area experienced river&ndash;flooding impacts during 18 Oct 2023 &ndash; 21 Oct 2023. [IMG] (p57)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>45 residential properties flooded internally (cluster including Rydal Way and Windermere Road) [IMG] (p56)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Rydal Way, Clay Cross",England,"Internal flooding of residential properties adjacent to Smithy Brook/Meadow Farm Pond caused by the watercourse overtopping during Storm Babet; the pink–mapped cluster of 45 homes (concentrated along Rydal Way and Windermere Road) flooded internally. [IMG] (p56)
Residential properties and the road adjacent to Rydal Way are mapped within or immediately adjacent to Flood Zones 2 and 3 along Smithy Brook; the Flood Map shows properties that flooded were located in these zones, indicating the Rydal Way area experienced river–flooding impacts during 18 Oct 2023 – 21 Oct 2023. [IMG] (p57)",45 residential properties flooded internally (cluster including Rydal Way and Windermere Road) [IMG] (p56),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.1623026,-1.4184956,"<div id=""html_2ef50314aa3aef68aa4205550a9245ed"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clay Lane, Clay Cross</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clay Lane is mapped as falling within Flood Zone 2; the report states that all properties that flooded were located in Flood Zone 2 or 3, so Clay Lane lies within the area exposed to river flooding during 18 Oct 2023 &ndash; 21 Oct 2023. [IMG,PAG] (p57)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Some properties on Clay Lane experienced internal flooding during the event; the highest flood risk areas on the map are concentrated near Clay Lane along the waterway. [IMG] (p58)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Clay Lane, Clay Cross",England,"Clay Lane is mapped as falling within Flood Zone 2; the report states that all properties that flooded were located in Flood Zone 2 or 3, so Clay Lane lies within the area exposed to river flooding during 18 Oct 2023 – 21 Oct 2023. [IMG,PAG] (p57)
Some properties on Clay Lane experienced internal flooding during the event; the highest flood risk areas on the map are concentrated near Clay Lane along the waterway. [IMG] (p58)",,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.1622839,-1.4213501,"<div id=""html_c2ef36385579d028430b42a06880308c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Coniston Drive, Clay Cross</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Some properties on Coniston Drive experienced internal flooding during the event. [IMG] (p58)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Coniston Drive, Clay Cross",England,Some properties on Coniston Drive experienced internal flooding during the event. [IMG] (p58),,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.1632652,-1.4212177,"<div id=""html_e63ee5c9b3f584e18875e18255aa706a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Grasmere Avenue, Clay Cross</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Some properties on Grasmere Avenue experienced internal flooding during the event (reported in the investigation). [IMG] (p58)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,"Grasmere Avenue, Clay Cross",England,Some properties on Grasmere Avenue experienced internal flooding during the event (reported in the investigation). [IMG] (p58),,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.1666927,-1.5833223,"<div id=""html_2e46329e755b3350bffecc28b677fe5f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Derbyshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple communities within the county experienced flooding during the storm: internal flooding of homes in Amber Valley (Ridgeway) and Drover&#8217;s Way, widespread local responses including sandbag requests, pumping of water and silt by Fire and Rescue at Lilac Way, and culvert blockage and siltation that impeded drainage (silt subsequently removed). [PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Communities within Derbyshire (notably Ridgeway along the River Amber) experienced river flooding during Storm Babet, resulting in internal flooding of residential properties. [PAG,IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Communities in Derbyshire adjacent to the River Amber experienced river flooding that resulted in internal and external flooding of residential properties; affected properties fall within EA River Amber flood alert/warning areas. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The county experienced a flood event tied to the River Amber and associated surface&ndash;water and sewer impacts: flood warnings/alerts were issued, local pumping infrastructure was overwhelmed causing sewer backup and foul flooding around properties, and surface water runoff contributed to property inundation with internal depths recorded up to 0.9 m. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The report records internal flooding within Derbyshire at Baslow (Baslow East) during Storm Babet: properties located on the floodplain of Bar Brook were inundated, resulting in internal flooding of homes and non&ndash;residential buildings in the Baslow East community. [IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Baslow East community (within Derbyshire) experienced river flooding when Bar Brook exceeded capacity and flooded residential properties; flood alerts and a flood warning were issued for areas in Derbyshire during the event. [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Upper River Derwent in Derbyshire was issued a flood alert by the Environment Agency on 20 Oct 2023 at 09:26. [IMG,PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High flows in Bottle Brook during Storm Babet caused river overtopping and internal flooding of residential properties in Lower Kilburn. Surface water and foul sewer systems were overwhelmed (manhole surcharging reported); the Little Eaton pumping station pumped throughout but was overwhelmed by flows. Severn Trent identified an ordinary watercourse connected to their surface water network and report the flap valve on the system outfall would have closed when Bottle Brook levels were high, impacting the network's ability to discharge. [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Communities within Derbyshire (for example Breadsall) experienced river flooding when Dam Brook and Boosemoor Brook overflowed during Storm Babet, causing internal flooding of residential properties. (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in the Breadsall area during 18&ndash;21 Oct 2023 included a Flood Alert for the Lower Derwent on 19 Oct and internal flooding of six residential properties on 20 Oct 2023. (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Within Derbyshire, the village of Castleton experienced river flooding from Peakshole Water during Storm Babet, resulting in internal flooding of properties. [IMG,PAG] (p52)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 100 requests for sandbags; 15 requests responded to; 16 residential properties internally flooded in Ridgeway; 3 homes flooded on Drover's Way [PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 homes internally flooded; 4 homes externally flooded; 3 homes flooded on Drovers Way (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>0.9 m internal flooding depth (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 residential properties; 11 non&ndash;residential properties [IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 residential properties; 14 homes on Derby Road [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>six residential properties (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>24 residential properties; 5 non&ndash;residential properties [IMG,PAG] (p52)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Derbyshire,England,"Multiple communities within the county experienced flooding during the storm: internal flooding of homes in Amber Valley (Ridgeway) and Drover’s Way, widespread local responses including sandbag requests, pumping of water and silt by Fire and Rescue at Lilac Way, and culvert blockage and siltation that impeded drainage (silt subsequently removed). [PAG] (p7)
Communities within Derbyshire (notably Ridgeway along the River Amber) experienced river flooding during Storm Babet, resulting in internal flooding of residential properties. [PAG,IMG] (p8)
Communities in Derbyshire adjacent to the River Amber experienced river flooding that resulted in internal and external flooding of residential properties; affected properties fall within EA River Amber flood alert/warning areas. (p10)
The county experienced a flood event tied to the River Amber and associated surface–water and sewer impacts: flood warnings/alerts were issued, local pumping infrastructure was overwhelmed causing sewer backup and foul flooding around properties, and surface water runoff contributed to property inundation with internal depths recorded up to 0.9 m. (p11)
The report records internal flooding within Derbyshire at Baslow (Baslow East) during Storm Babet: properties located on the floodplain of Bar Brook were inundated, resulting in internal flooding of homes and non–residential buildings in the Baslow East community. [IMG] (p12)
The Baslow East community (within Derbyshire) experienced river flooding when Bar Brook exceeded capacity and flooded residential properties; flood alerts and a flood warning were issued for areas in Derbyshire during the event. [PAG] (p14)
The Upper River Derwent in Derbyshire was issued a flood alert by the Environment Agency on 20 Oct 2023 at 09:26. [IMG,PAG] (p16)
High flows in Bottle Brook during Storm Babet caused river overtopping and internal flooding of residential properties in Lower Kilburn. Surface water and foul sewer systems were overwhelmed (manhole surcharging reported); the Little Eaton pumping station pumped throughout but was overwhelmed by flows. Severn Trent identified an ordinary watercourse connected to their surface water network and report the flap valve on the system outfall would have closed when Bottle Brook levels were high, impacting the network's ability to discharge. [PAG,IMG] (p20)
Communities within Derbyshire (for example Breadsall) experienced river flooding when Dam Brook and Boosemoor Brook overflowed during Storm Babet, causing internal flooding of residential properties. (p28)
Flooding in the Breadsall area during 18–21 Oct 2023 included a Flood Alert for the Lower Derwent on 19 Oct and internal flooding of six residential properties on 20 Oct 2023. (p32)
Within Derbyshire, the village of Castleton experienced river flooding from Peakshole Water during Storm Babet, resulting in internal flooding of properties. [IMG,PAG] (p52)","over 100 requests for sandbags; 15 requests responded to; 16 residential properties internally flooded in Ridgeway; 3 homes flooded on Drover's Way [PAG] (p7)
16 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p8)
16 homes internally flooded; 4 homes externally flooded; 3 homes flooded on Drovers Way (p10)
0.9 m internal flooding depth (p11)
9 residential properties; 11 non–residential properties [IMG] (p12)
17 residential properties; 14 homes on Derby Road [PAG,IMG] (p20)
six residential properties (p28)
6 properties (p32)
24 residential properties; 5 non–residential properties [IMG,PAG] (p52)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.2226728,-1.5239286,"<div id=""html_ef0f5cc80e5b7bddd0b23cdad993b267"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North East Derbyshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A surface water drainage pathway in the district (Lilac Way area) was overwhelmed during Storm Babet, causing overflow of a culverted ordinary watercourse and internal flooding to residential properties. [PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Forty&ndash;five homes internally flooded in the community; all properties on the east side of Windemere Road and the majority on the west side flooded. Some properties on Clay Lane, Coniston Drive and Grasmere Avenue also flooded. Flood water reached about halfway up the front door and adjacent wall of at least one property. (p59)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>six properties flooded internally; three properties flooded externally [PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>45 homes (p59)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,North East Derbyshire,England,"A surface water drainage pathway in the district (Lilac Way area) was overwhelmed during Storm Babet, causing overflow of a culverted ordinary watercourse and internal flooding to residential properties. [PAG] (p6)
Forty–five homes internally flooded in the community; all properties on the east side of Windemere Road and the majority on the west side flooded. Some properties on Clay Lane, Coniston Drive and Grasmere Avenue also flooded. Flood water reached about halfway up the front door and adjacent wall of at least one property. (p59)","six properties flooded internally; three properties flooded externally [PAG] (p6)
45 homes (p59)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.029057,-1.4624954,"<div id=""html_68a2581d90925a96c657e24dc24036da"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Amber Valley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sixteen residential properties in the hamlet of Ridgeway (within Amber Valley) suffered internal flooding as a result of Storm Babet; three additional homes on Drover's Way (about 400 m north&ndash;east) were also flooded. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localised flooding affected properties in the borough: internal flooding entered homes via doorways with reported depths reaching 0.9 m; a local pumping station was overwhelmed and had no free outlet so the sewer/network backed up and residents experienced foul flooding overflowing from drains around their properties; surface water flowed downhill from the railway/Bullbridge area to the north of Riversdale contributing to inundation. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties in the Amber Valley (Lower Kilburn) experienced internal flooding during the event; Bottle Brook (which flows through the community) contributed to the flooding of properties east of the brook. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Denby Bottles (within Amber Valley) experienced internal flooding of properties during Storm Babet; low ground adjacent to Bottle Brook was part of the affected area. (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 residential properties; 3 homes (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>0.9 m internal flooding depth (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 residential properties (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>35 properties; 30 homes; 5 non&ndash;residential (including businesses) (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Amber Valley,England,"Sixteen residential properties in the hamlet of Ridgeway (within Amber Valley) suffered internal flooding as a result of Storm Babet; three additional homes on Drover's Way (about 400 m north–east) were also flooded. (p7)
Localised flooding affected properties in the borough: internal flooding entered homes via doorways with reported depths reaching 0.9 m; a local pumping station was overwhelmed and had no free outlet so the sewer/network backed up and residents experienced foul flooding overflowing from drains around their properties; surface water flowed downhill from the railway/Bullbridge area to the north of Riversdale contributing to inundation. (p11)
Residential properties in the Amber Valley (Lower Kilburn) experienced internal flooding during the event; Bottle Brook (which flows through the community) contributed to the flooding of properties east of the brook. (p19)
Denby Bottles (within Amber Valley) experienced internal flooding of properties during Storm Babet; low ground adjacent to Bottle Brook was part of the affected area. (p23)","16 residential properties; 3 homes (p7)
