35 properties; 30 homes; 5 non–residential (including businesses) (p23)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9380048,-1.3513172,"<div id=""html_bc372306e940acfe0cecca9a47c5f461"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Erewash</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The village of Breadsall (within the Borough of Erewash) experienced internal flooding of six residential properties when local brooks overflowed during Storm Babet. (p28)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>six residential properties (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Erewash,England,The village of Breadsall (within the Borough of Erewash) experienced internal flooding of six residential properties when local brooks overflowed during Storm Babet. (p28),six residential properties (p28),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.986103,-1.4888648,"<div id=""html_31a68bf2f5eeff2f4ab6e85edb611911"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Duffield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The gauging station at Duffield on the River Ecclesbourne recorded the shortest lag between peak rainfall and peak flow, indicating a rapid river response during Storm Babet. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties in the village during the event; a mix of terraced, semi&ndash;detached and detached homes and businesses were affected. [PAG] (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of local properties during Storm Babet; flooding concentrated near open and culverted watercourses (notably around Ecclesbourne Avenue and Village Court). Flooded premises include a mix of terraced, semi&ndash;detached and detached homes and businesses; vulnerable community facilities and groups are present in the flooded area. [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding associated with the River Ecclesbourne and surface&ndash;water/urban runoff during 18 Oct 2023&ndash;21 Oct 2023 caused properties in Duffield to flood and affected local transport routes. The event led to multiple property flood incidents in the town; local roads in the vicinity of the watercourses were impacted. [PAG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Ecclesbourne exceeded capacity and overflowed banks and formal defences through Duffield during Storm Babet, causing overtopping of defence walls (e.g. at Village Court and Duffield Tennis Club), flow across Duffield Tennis Club onto rear gardens and roads, flooding down Town Street (road closure) and internal flooding of multiple residential and non&ndash;residential properties. [PAG] (p44)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localized flooding across the village from overland flow routes and overflowing watercourses. Notable impacts include overflow points at Duck Island and Village Court, overtopping of flood defence walls (Village Court and Duffield Tennis Club), road closures (Town Street) and evacuations. [IMG,PAG] (p46)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>34 properties; 31 residential properties; 3 non&ndash;residential properties [PAG] (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>34 properties internally flooded; 31 residential; 3 non&ndash;residential (including Duffield Meadows Primary School); map annotations show 5 homes flooded on Ecclesbourne Avenue and 19 homes flooded on Village Court [IMG,PAG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>33 flooded properties within a flood alert or flood warning area; 1 flooded property not within a Flood Alert Area or Flood Warning Area [PAG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>31 homes internally flooded; 3 non&ndash;residential properties internally flooded [PAG] (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Duffield,England,"The gauging station at Duffield on the River Ecclesbourne recorded the shortest lag between peak rainfall and peak flow, indicating a rapid river response during Storm Babet. (p3)
Internal flooding to properties in the village during the event; a mix of terraced, semi–detached and detached homes and businesses were affected. [PAG] (p40)
Internal flooding of local properties during Storm Babet; flooding concentrated near open and culverted watercourses (notably around Ecclesbourne Avenue and Village Court). Flooded premises include a mix of terraced, semi–detached and detached homes and businesses; vulnerable community facilities and groups are present in the flooded area. [IMG,PAG] (p41)
Flooding associated with the River Ecclesbourne and surface–water/urban runoff during 18 Oct 2023–21 Oct 2023 caused properties in Duffield to flood and affected local transport routes. The event led to multiple property flood incidents in the town; local roads in the vicinity of the watercourses were impacted. [PAG] (p43)
River Ecclesbourne exceeded capacity and overflowed banks and formal defences through Duffield during Storm Babet, causing overtopping of defence walls (e.g. at Village Court and Duffield Tennis Club), flow across Duffield Tennis Club onto rear gardens and roads, flooding down Town Street (road closure) and internal flooding of multiple residential and non–residential properties. [PAG] (p44)
Localized flooding across the village from overland flow routes and overflowing watercourses. Notable impacts include overflow points at Duck Island and Village Court, overtopping of flood defence walls (Village Court and Duffield Tennis Club), road closures (Town Street) and evacuations. [IMG,PAG] (p46)","34 properties; 31 residential properties; 3 non–residential properties [PAG] (p40)
34 properties internally flooded; 31 residential; 3 non–residential (including Duffield Meadows Primary School); map annotations show 5 homes flooded on Ecclesbourne Avenue and 19 homes flooded on Village Court [IMG,PAG] (p41)
