31 homes internally flooded; 3 non–residential properties internally flooded [PAG] (p44)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.0142944,-1.4402785,"<div id=""html_bce605b2bd701c87caf0ff732a3e7318"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rawson Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Gauging stations near Rawson Green (on the River Ecclesbourne and Bottle Brook) produced some of the highest&ndash;ranked flows or levels on record in response to Storm Babet, reflecting an early and short river response to the heavy rainfall. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential areas at Rawson Green are shown on the surface&ndash;water risk map as having properties in high and medium surface&ndash;water flood risk and are within the Bottle Brook flood alert and 'Bottle Brook at Rawson Green' flood warning areas. The surface&ndash;water map includes all properties that suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet, and the flood warning issued on 20 October covered the flooded properties in this area. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Rawson Green,England,"Gauging stations near Rawson Green (on the River Ecclesbourne and Bottle Brook) produced some of the highest–ranked flows or levels on record in response to Storm Babet, reflecting an early and short river response to the heavy rainfall. (p3)
Residential areas at Rawson Green are shown on the surface–water risk map as having properties in high and medium surface–water flood risk and are within the Bottle Brook flood alert and 'Bottle Brook at Rawson Green' flood warning areas. The surface–water map includes all properties that suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet, and the flood warning issued on 20 October covered the flooded properties in this area. [PAG,IMG] (p26)",,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.0592048,-1.4340909,"<div id=""html_1e76a9c9726ae0f9f320de1082501345"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lower Hartshay</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A gauging station in Lower Hartshay (on one of the tributaries cited) produced one of the highest&ndash;ranked flows or levels on record in response to Storm Babet. (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Lower Hartshay,England,A gauging station in Lower Hartshay (on one of the tributaries cited) produced one of the highest–ranked flows or levels on record in response to Storm Babet. (p3),,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.1258526,-1.407305,"<div id=""html_914046239d123b63bccdfb30a48eb35a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Shirland</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the village (Lilac Way) experienced internal flooding of residential properties adjacent to a culverted ordinary watercourse. [IMG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced rapid&ndash;onset flooding during which residents requested sandbags; over 100 sandbag requests were recorded and 15 requests were responded to by Derbyshire County Council. (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 residential properties (on Lilac Way) [IMG] (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Shirland,England,"Part of the village (Lilac Way) experienced internal flooding of residential properties adjacent to a culverted ordinary watercourse. [IMG] (p4)
Experienced rapid–onset flooding during which residents requested sandbags; over 100 sandbag requests were recorded and 15 requests were responded to by Derbyshire County Council. (p7)",6 residential properties (on Lilac Way) [IMG] (p4),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.058172462205334,-1.4650602223168254,"<div id=""html_b652c560daf6c9e80bbd5f2a9f91a48c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ridgeway</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties caused by Storm Babet, concentrated along the A610 (locally Riversdale and Ripley Road); floodwater impacted homes and required response and recovery. [PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties along the A610 (Riversdale / Ripley Road) caused by the River Amber overflowing during Storm Babet; flooding affected low&ndash;lying houses east of the river on the floodplain. [PAG,IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential community experienced river flooding from the River Amber; homes to the east of the River Amber were flooded. The community is low&ndash;lying on the River Amber floodplain and flooded properties are located within Flood Zone 3. [PAG,IMG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Amber overtopping its banks led to internal and external flooding of homes within the Ridgeway community (properties on Riversdale and nearby streets). [PAG] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 residential properties; 3 homes [PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 homes internally flooded; 4 homes externally flooded; 3 homes flooded on Drovers Way [PAG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Ridgeway,England,"Internal flooding of residential properties caused by Storm Babet, concentrated along the A610 (locally Riversdale and Ripley Road); floodwater impacted homes and required response and recovery. [PAG] (p7)
Internal flooding of residential properties along the A610 (Riversdale / Ripley Road) caused by the River Amber overflowing during Storm Babet; flooding affected low–lying houses east of the river on the floodplain. [PAG,IMG] (p8)
Residential community experienced river flooding from the River Amber; homes to the east of the River Amber were flooded. The community is low–lying on the River Amber floodplain and flooded properties are located within Flood Zone 3. [PAG,IMG] (p9)
Flooding from the River Amber overtopping its banks led to internal and external flooding of homes within the Ridgeway community (properties on Riversdale and nearby streets). [PAG] (p10)","16 residential properties; 3 homes [PAG] (p7)
