16 homes internally flooded; 4 homes externally flooded; 3 homes flooded on Drovers Way [PAG] (p10)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.0604187,-1.4808654,"<div id=""html_40e68912dc64f9d1e56256e7f21947b5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ambergate</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal floodwaters reached about 0.9 m and entered homes via doorways. The local pumping station was overwhelmed and had no free outlet, causing the sewer network to back up and residents to experience foul flooding overflowing from drains around properties. Surface water flowing downhill from the railway/Bullbridge area to the north of Riversdale contributed to the flooding. (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>0.9 m internal flooding depth (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Ambergate,England,"Internal floodwaters reached about 0.9 m and entered homes via doorways. The local pumping station was overwhelmed and had no free outlet, causing the sewer network to back up and residents to experience foul flooding overflowing from drains around properties. Surface water flowing downhill from the railway/Bullbridge area to the north of Riversdale contributed to the flooding. (p11)",0.9 m internal flooding depth (p11),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.2469579,-1.6201639,"<div id=""html_27bfb35bbf6b1a9ea62da103d47b65fc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Baslow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Baslow East community (Nether End area) suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet. Properties on the floodplain of Bar Brook were inundated, with flooding concentrated at the low point on Cock Hill and affecting streets adjacent to the brook; vehicle waves prior to a road closure were reported to have increased flood ingress to homes. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties in the Baslow East / Nether End community were flooded during the event. Flooded homes are located within Flood Zone 2 and the majority are within Flood Zone 3 adjacent to Bar Brook. Local roads (including Cock Hill and Church Lane) and several buildings lie within these flood zones and were impacted or at risk during the flooding. [IMG,PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Bar Brook exceeded its capacity and overflowed its banks, causing flooding of residential properties in the Baslow East community. Flooded homes are located within Flood Zone 2 and Flood Zone 3 (the majority in Zone 3). Many properties in the community are also mapped with a high long&ndash;term surface water flood risk. [PAG,IMG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties in the Baslow East community flooded after Bar Brook exceeded its banks and from large volumes of surface water runoff. Nether End car park and Baslow Village Hall were flooded. [IMG,PAG] (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 residential properties; 11 non&ndash;residential properties; 4 homes on Cock Hill; 5 homes on Church Lane; 11 non&ndash;residential properties in Nether End (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Baslow,England,"The Baslow East community (Nether End area) suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet. Properties on the floodplain of Bar Brook were inundated, with flooding concentrated at the low point on Cock Hill and affecting streets adjacent to the brook; vehicle waves prior to a road closure were reported to have increased flood ingress to homes. (p12)
Residential properties in the Baslow East / Nether End community were flooded during the event. Flooded homes are located within Flood Zone 2 and the majority are within Flood Zone 3 adjacent to Bar Brook. Local roads (including Cock Hill and Church Lane) and several buildings lie within these flood zones and were impacted or at risk during the flooding. [IMG,PAG] (p13)
Bar Brook exceeded its capacity and overflowed its banks, causing flooding of residential properties in the Baslow East community. Flooded homes are located within Flood Zone 2 and Flood Zone 3 (the majority in Zone 3). Many properties in the community are also mapped with a high long–term surface water flood risk. [PAG,IMG] (p14)
Residential properties in the Baslow East community flooded after Bar Brook exceeded its banks and from large volumes of surface water runoff. Nether End car park and Baslow Village Hall were flooded. [IMG,PAG] (p15)",9 residential properties; 11 non–residential properties; 4 homes on Cock Hill; 5 homes on Church Lane; 11 non–residential properties in Nether End (p12),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.2458198,-1.6144739,"<div id=""html_bb779876ddb0232622fd99b175820aad"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Baslow Nether End</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Nether End (the eastern part of Baslow) had the highest concentration of internally flooded properties during Storm Babet; non&ndash;residential premises in Nether End were internally flooded and the area is located on the floodplain of Bar Brook. [IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Bar Brook exceeded its capacity and overflowed into the community; surface&ndash;water runoff from Cock Hill (A619), springs related to old mine workings and an erosion&ndash;related burst water main contributed to large volumes of surface water running downhill. These combined mechanisms flooded the Nether End car park, Baslow Village Hall and nearby residential properties. [IMG] (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 non&ndash;residential properties [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Baslow Nether End,England,"Nether End (the eastern part of Baslow) had the highest concentration of internally flooded properties during Storm Babet; non–residential premises in Nether End were internally flooded and the area is located on the floodplain of Bar Brook. [IMG] (p12)
Bar Brook exceeded its capacity and overflowed into the community; surface–water runoff from Cock Hill (A619), springs related to old mine workings and an erosion–related burst water main contributed to large volumes of surface water running downhill. These combined mechanisms flooded the Nether End car park, Baslow Village Hall and nearby residential properties. [IMG] (p15)",11 non–residential properties [IMG] (p12),GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9689324,-1.4614667,"<div id=""html_9f9838c20d7950e1a92eded4e18329fb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Little Eaton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storm Babet caused Bottle Brook to flood, resulting in internal flooding of residential properties clustered around Croft End on the west side of Bottle Brook and one property on the east side off Alfreton Road. Little Eaton Primary School, although near Bottle Brook, did not flood. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding affected residential properties in the village during the event, concentrated around Croft End on the west side of Bottle Brook (with one affected property on the east side off Alfreton Road). Little Eaton Primary School, located near Bottle Brook and the affected properties, did not experience flooding. [PAG,IMG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties occurred in the community (afternoon/evening of 20 October 2023). Seven properties on Croft End (west of Bottle Brook) and one property on Alfreton Road (east of Bottle Brook) flooded internally. Manhole covers in Croft End were observed to surcharge; the cause of flooding at Alfreton Road is unclear but may be linked to a foul pumping&ndash;station failure. [PAG,IMG] (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 residential properties (7 west of Bottle Brook; 1 east of Bottle Brook) (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 residential properties; 1 property (east side of Bottle Brook) [PAG,IMG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 homes; 7 properties on Croft End; 1 property on Alfreton Road [PAG,IMG] (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Little Eaton,England,"Storm Babet caused Bottle Brook to flood, resulting in internal flooding of residential properties clustered around Croft End on the west side of Bottle Brook and one property on the east side off Alfreton Road. Little Eaton Primary School, although near Bottle Brook, did not flood. (p16)
Internal flooding affected residential properties in the village during the event, concentrated around Croft End on the west side of Bottle Brook (with one affected property on the east side off Alfreton Road). Little Eaton Primary School, located near Bottle Brook and the affected properties, did not experience flooding. [PAG,IMG] (p17)
Internal flooding of residential properties occurred in the community (afternoon/evening of 20 October 2023). Seven properties on Croft End (west of Bottle Brook) and one property on Alfreton Road (east of Bottle Brook) flooded internally. Manhole covers in Croft End were observed to surcharge; the cause of flooding at Alfreton Road is unclear but may be linked to a foul pumping–station failure. [PAG,IMG] (p18)","8 residential properties (7 west of Bottle Brook; 1 east of Bottle Brook) (p16)
8 residential properties; 1 property (east side of Bottle Brook) [PAG,IMG] (p17)
8 homes; 7 properties on Croft End; 1 property on Alfreton Road [PAG,IMG] (p18)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.006126241640004,-1.4412032894868765,"<div id=""html_d02e2d08268ae4007d65ca4bfae7711c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lower Kilburn</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Seventeen residential properties suffered internal flooding during the event; all flooded properties were east of Bottle Brook. [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties east of Bottle Brook; properties are on the Bottle Brook floodplain and previously flooded in prior years. [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties in the community have been flooded from both Bottle Brook (river flooding) and surface water. The Environment Agency and local records show previous flooding (1977, 2007, November 2019) and residents reported frequent flooding in the five years preceding the assessment; an Environment Agency assessment was conducted following Storm Babet indicating recent flooding impacts in the area. Flooded homes in the community are mapped in Flood Zone 2. [PAG,IMG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Combination of fluvial and surface water flooding affected the community. Seventeen properties on Derby Road flooded internally. Flooding of Derby Road (the main road through the community) would have caused travel disruption. [PAG] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map and text link Derby Road (the main road through Lower Kilburn) with flooding&ndash;related travel disruption; the area around Bottle Brook is low&ndash;lying and likely contributed to flood impacts during Storm Babet. (There is some uncertainty: the text implies travel disruption but does not explicitly record internal property flooding within Lower Kilburn.) [IMG,PAG] (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 residential properties [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 properties [PAG] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Lower Kilburn,England,"Seventeen residential properties suffered internal flooding during the event; all flooded properties were east of Bottle Brook. [PAG] (p19)
Internal flooding of residential properties east of Bottle Brook; properties are on the Bottle Brook floodplain and previously flooded in prior years. [PAG,IMG] (p20)
Residential properties in the community have been flooded from both Bottle Brook (river flooding) and surface water. The Environment Agency and local records show previous flooding (1977, 2007, November 2019) and residents reported frequent flooding in the five years preceding the assessment; an Environment Agency assessment was conducted following Storm Babet indicating recent flooding impacts in the area. Flooded homes in the community are mapped in Flood Zone 2. [PAG,IMG] (p21)
Combination of fluvial and surface water flooding affected the community. Seventeen properties on Derby Road flooded internally. Flooding of Derby Road (the main road through the community) would have caused travel disruption. [PAG] (p22)
Map and text link Derby Road (the main road through Lower Kilburn) with flooding–related travel disruption; the area around Bottle Brook is low–lying and likely contributed to flood impacts during Storm Babet. (There is some uncertainty: the text implies travel disruption but does not explicitly record internal property flooding within Lower Kilburn.) [IMG,PAG] (p23)","17 residential properties [PAG] (p19)
17 residential properties [PAG,IMG] (p20)
17 properties [PAG] (p22)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.0131438,-1.4299181,"<div id=""html_8301ace9003600bae3ceb296ca3f39b2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Denby Bottles</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential and non&ndash;residential properties during Storm Babet; flooding clustered along Derby Road and Prospect Road and closely associated with the course and culverted sections of Bottle Brook. [IMG,PAG] (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in Denby Bottles experienced internal flooding during Storm Babet. Flooding was associated with Bottle Brook and coincided with high surface&ndash;water risk shown on long&ndash;term maps; most flooded homes were terraced residential properties located within Flood Zone 3. [PAG,IMG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in Denby Bottles suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet (18 Oct 2023 &ndash; 21 Oct 2023). Most of the flooded residential properties were terraced homes. All flooded homes are located in Flood Zone 3 and were within the 'Bottle Brook Derbyshire' Flood Alert Area and the 'Bottle Brook at Rawson Green' Flood Warning Area. The Long Term Flood Risk (surface water) mapping shows the flooded properties lie within a high surface&ndash;water&ndash;risk area. [PAG,IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The community experienced fluvial flooding driven by Bottle Brook overtopping. Thirty&ndash;five properties across three areas in Denby Bottles suffered internal flooding: two non&ndash;residential properties within the Denby Institute and Recreation Ground, twenty&ndash;eight homes and three businesses on Derby Road, and two homes on Prospect Road. Flooding concentrated in lower elevation zones adjacent to the watercourses. [IMG] (p27)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>35 properties internally flooded; 30 homes; 5 non&ndash;residential (including businesses); 28 terraced homes on Derby Road; 2 internally flooded homes on Prospect Road; 2 internally flooded non&ndash;residential properties north of Derby Road. [IMG,PAG] (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>35 properties internally flooded; breakdown: 2 non&ndash;residential properties (Denby Institute and Recreation Ground); 28 homes and 3 non&ndash;residential properties (Derby Road); 2 homes (Prospect Road) [IMG] (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Denby Bottles,England,"Internal flooding of residential and non–residential properties during Storm Babet; flooding clustered along Derby Road and Prospect Road and closely associated with the course and culverted sections of Bottle Brook. [IMG,PAG] (p24)
Properties in Denby Bottles experienced internal flooding during Storm Babet. Flooding was associated with Bottle Brook and coincided with high surface–water risk shown on long–term maps; most flooded homes were terraced residential properties located within Flood Zone 3. [PAG,IMG] (p25)
Properties in Denby Bottles suffered internal flooding during Storm Babet (18 Oct 2023 – 21 Oct 2023). Most of the flooded residential properties were terraced homes. All flooded homes are located in Flood Zone 3 and were within the 'Bottle Brook Derbyshire' Flood Alert Area and the 'Bottle Brook at Rawson Green' Flood Warning Area. The Long Term Flood Risk (surface water) mapping shows the flooded properties lie within a high surface–water–risk area. [PAG,IMG] (p26)
The community experienced fluvial flooding driven by Bottle Brook overtopping. Thirty–five properties across three areas in Denby Bottles suffered internal flooding: two non–residential properties within the Denby Institute and Recreation Ground, twenty–eight homes and three businesses on Derby Road, and two homes on Prospect Road. Flooding concentrated in lower elevation zones adjacent to the watercourses. [IMG] (p27)","35 properties internally flooded; 30 homes; 5 non–residential (including businesses); 28 terraced homes on Derby Road; 2 internally flooded homes on Prospect Road; 2 internally flooded non–residential properties north of Derby Road. [IMG,PAG] (p24)
35 properties internally flooded; breakdown: 2 non–residential properties (Denby Institute and Recreation Ground); 28 homes and 3 non–residential properties (Derby Road); 2 homes (Prospect Road) [IMG] (p27)",GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_3_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-3-derwent-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9537226,-1.4504293,"<div id=""html_c134ba006f32e4c0323402d6308e2c89"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Breadsall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Six residential properties suffered internal flooding when Dam Brook and Boosemoor Brook reached capacity and overflowed their banks during Storm Babet. [PAG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple residential properties internally flooded when Dam Brook and Bostemoor (Boosemoor) Brook reached capacity and overtopped their banks during Storm Babet; flooded properties are within Flood Zone 2 and also at high surface&ndash;water risk where drainage could not discharge to the brooks. [IMG,PAG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties in the village experienced internal flooding. Flooded homes lie within Flood Zone 2 (river flood extent) and all internally flooded properties are in areas mapped at high chance (>3.3% AEP) of surface water flooding, driven by local topography and drainage networks being unable to discharge to nearby brooks. [PAG,IMG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the community suffered internal flooding during the October 2023 event. Flooding is associated with surface water runoff and local drainage networks being unable to discharge to nearby ordinary watercourses (Dam Brook and Boosemoor Brook). A property on Brookside Road is recorded as having experienced internal flooding despite having a demountable driveway flood gate. [PAG] (p31)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The community experienced flooding from Dam Brook and Boosemoor Brook. Internal flooding of six residential properties occurred on the afternoon and evening of 20 October 2023 (two properties on Brookside Road, one on Moor Road and three on Rectory Lane). Dam Brook was reported to have overtopped around 08:30 on 20 October before receding and then rising again; Brookside Road flooded to about 0.5 m in low spots and remained flooded until around 15:00, after which levels began to recede. Sewer network surcharge associated with the road flooding contributed to internal property flooding. (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding affected at least one property (water entering buildings) and floodwater from drainage surcharge impacted property access; a demountable driveway flood barrier prevented flood water reaching another property. [PAG] (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>six residential properties [PAG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 homes flooded internally [IMG,PAG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>six homes; two properties on Brookside Road; one property on Moor Road; three properties on Rectory Lane; 0.5 m depth (road low spots) (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [PAG] (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Breadsall,England,"Six residential properties suffered internal flooding when Dam Brook and Boosemoor Brook reached capacity and overflowed their banks during Storm Babet. [PAG] (p28)
Multiple residential properties internally flooded when Dam Brook and Bostemoor (Boosemoor) Brook reached capacity and overtopped their banks during Storm Babet; flooded properties are within Flood Zone 2 and also at high surface–water risk where drainage could not discharge to the brooks. [IMG,PAG] (p29)
