GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,52.9212078,-1.3720785,"<div id=""html_a7618063eeaaed2c44a32d88edfd466a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ockbrook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties caused by Ock Brook overtopping/river flooding, resulting in homes being inundated and internal water damage. [PAG] (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties during Storm Babet. The affected community is entirely residential; no schools, hospitals or care homes were reported flooded. Properties lie within or close to the floodplain of Ock Brook and the village sits in a local topographic low underlain by alluvium. [PAG] (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to residential properties caused by Ock Brook overtopping after a culvert under Cole Lane was partially blocked; floodwater flowed westwards along Cole Lane and Collier Lane, entering homes. The affected community is entirely residential and contains no known vulnerable institutions. [PAG] (p35)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 residential properties [PAG] (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 residential properties; 4 residential properties on Collier Lane; 4 residential properties on Cole Lane [PAG] (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 homes; 4 properties on Cole Lane; 4 properties on Collier Lane [PAG] (p35)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Ockbrook,England,"Internal flooding of residential properties caused by Ock Brook overtopping/river flooding, resulting in homes being inundated and internal water damage. [PAG] (p33)
Internal flooding of residential properties during Storm Babet. The affected community is entirely residential; no schools, hospitals or care homes were reported flooded. Properties lie within or close to the floodplain of Ock Brook and the village sits in a local topographic low underlain by alluvium. [PAG] (p34)
Internal flooding to residential properties caused by Ock Brook overtopping after a culvert under Cole Lane was partially blocked; floodwater flowed westwards along Cole Lane and Collier Lane, entering homes. The affected community is entirely residential and contains no known vulnerable institutions. [PAG] (p35)","8 residential properties [PAG] (p33)
