GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.2756112,-1.6595362,"<div id=""html_e1af85c7903597a07e1e0ca7a3e01461"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stoney Middleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced internal flooding of properties due to the storm: floodwaters from nearby Dale Brook caused inundation within the village. [PAG] (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties in the village during Storm Babet; flooded properties are located along the valley bottom adjacent to Dale Brook and were within the local river floodplain and at medium&ndash;high surface&ndash;water flood risk. [PAG] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential and non&ndash;residential properties caused by Dale Brook overtopping culverts and local surface water/sough surcharging; flood damage observed around The Nook and along The Dale. (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding to properties surrounding The Nook and damage to The Nook road. Flooding was linked to old mine drainage (soughs) surcharging and surface water runoff from the steep hillside and from the field behind Denman Crescent, which caused internal flooding to at least one home. (p40)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>ten properties; seven residential properties; three non&ndash;residential properties [PAG] (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 properties; 7 residential properties; 3 non&ndash;residential properties [PAG] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 homes; 3 non&ndash;residential properties (p39)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Stoney Middleton,England,"Experienced internal flooding of properties due to the storm: floodwaters from nearby Dale Brook caused inundation within the village. [PAG] (p36)
Internal flooding of properties in the village during Storm Babet; flooded properties are located along the valley bottom adjacent to Dale Brook and were within the local river floodplain and at medium–high surface–water flood risk. [PAG] (p37)
Internal flooding of residential and non–residential properties caused by Dale Brook overtopping culverts and local surface water/sough surcharging; flood damage observed around The Nook and along The Dale. (p39)
Flooding to properties surrounding The Nook and damage to The Nook road. Flooding was linked to old mine drainage (soughs) surcharging and surface water runoff from the steep hillside and from the field behind Denman Crescent, which caused internal flooding to at least one home. (p40)","ten properties; seven residential properties; three non–residential properties [PAG] (p36)
