GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.3273166,-1.7411554,"<div id=""html_6c5abfb3bd4e1b4f51c73a55844a0a1e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bradwell</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential and non&ndash;residential properties concentrated along Bradwell Brook; impacts to homes, holiday lets, commercial properties and public buildings in the village. [IMG] (p47)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding has affected the village on multiple occasions. The community impacted has included residential properties, holiday lets, commercial properties and businesses, public buildings, schools and churches. The majority of flooded homes are shown as being in Flood Zone 3 (greater than 1% AEP from rivers). The village is described as vulnerable to flooding from main river, ordinary watercourse, surface water and old mining drains. [IMG,PAG] (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple sources of flooding (Bradwell Brook, an unnamed watercourse and surface water) caused internal flooding of properties across the village during Storm Babet. Properties on Church Street, Brookside, Soft Water Lane and other streets were affected; flood warnings and alerts covered the village. [IMG,PAG] (p49)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple sources of flooding affected the village: Bradwell Brook, an unnamed watercourse and surface water runoff. Twenty&ndash;nine properties internally flooded across the village (26 residential, 3 non&ndash;residential). Surface water flooded the B6049 along its full width (shallow). One property is built over Bradwell Brook where a culvert with silt/debris may have reduced capacity, contributing to local flooding. [IMG,PAG] (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in the village linked to reduced culvert capacity under a property on Soft Water Lane (Bradwell Brook). Reported road flooding depths: Church Street near the bridge was reported as shin&ndash;deep and depths on Soft Water Lane were reported deeper. The Environment Agency issued a Flood Alert (19 Oct 2023 19:13) and a Flood Warning (20 Oct 2023 13:16) for Bradwell; EA operatives removed large blockages during the event and conducted CCTV surveys prior to Storm Babet. [PAG,MUL] (p51)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>26 residential properties; 3 non&ndash;residential properties [IMG] (p47)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Flooding recorded in 1991, 1997, 1998, 2007, 2010, 2015, 2021 and 2022 [IMG,PAG] (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>29 properties internally flooded; 26 residential houses; 3 non&ndash;residential; 17 houses on Church Street; 2 houses on Brookside; 2 houses on Soft Water Lane; 1 house each on The Hills, Town Gate, Bridge Street, New Church Street [IMG,PAG] (p49)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>29 properties; 26 residential houses; 3 non&ndash;residential; 17 houses on Church Street; 2 houses on Brookside; 2 houses on Soft Water Lane; 1 house on The Hills; 1 house on Town Gate; 1 house on Bridge Street; 1 house on New Church Street; 1 property built over Bradwell Brook [IMG,PAG] (p50)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property built over Bradwell Brook [PAG,MUL] (p51)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Bradwell,England,"Internal flooding of residential and non–residential properties concentrated along Bradwell Brook; impacts to homes, holiday lets, commercial properties and public buildings in the village. [IMG] (p47)
