GB-DBY,3,2023-10-18,53.3431214111066,-1.7757540040039734,"<div id=""html_c3692afeef9eb75594231e975b2200a0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Castleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties in the village during Storm Babet; both residential and non&ndash;residential buildings were flooded, affecting homes, businesses and the local tourist economy. (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of domestic and non&ndash;domestic properties in the village: properties located on the floodplain of Peakshole Water were inundated during the event. [IMG,PAG] (p52)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of homes and businesses in the community during the Storm Babet event; residents used sandbags and makeshift defences were built on the Riverside Path. (p53)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Peakshole Water (the main watercourse through the village) and surface water caused internal flooding of homes and businesses; residents used sandbags and makeshift defences; flood alert issued and local flood wardens responded. [IMG,PAG] (p54)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Peakshole Water reached capacity and overtopped its banks: a large volume of water emerging from the cave system caused flooding of The Stones; overflow from Peakshole Water flooded Eades Fold and Vicarage Lane; water breached drystone walls behind Mill Court gardens, flowed onto Millbridge and then surged down Tricketts Close (first recorded flow on this route); flow was constrained by the low bridge on Millbridge causing upstream backup; floodwater also escaped at the culvert grill at Eyre's Farm and flowed south along Hollowford Road. (p55)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>24 residential properties; 5 non&ndash;residential properties (p51)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>24 residential properties; 5 non&ndash;residential properties [IMG,PAG] (p52)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>29 homes and commercial properties internally flooded; includes 17 homes and 3 commercial holiday lets on Millbridge, Trickett Close and Mill Court; 4 homes and 2 commercial properties on The Island; 1 home on Waterside; 1 on The Stones; 1 on Eades Fold. [IMG,PAG] (p54)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Castleton,England,"Internal flooding of properties in the village during Storm Babet; both residential and non–residential buildings were flooded, affecting homes, businesses and the local tourist economy. (p51)
Internal flooding of domestic and non–domestic properties in the village: properties located on the floodplain of Peakshole Water were inundated during the event. [IMG,PAG] (p52)
Internal flooding of homes and businesses in the community during the Storm Babet event; residents used sandbags and makeshift defences were built on the Riverside Path. (p53)
Peakshole Water (the main watercourse through the village) and surface water caused internal flooding of homes and businesses; residents used sandbags and makeshift defences; flood alert issued and local flood wardens responded. [IMG,PAG] (p54)
Peakshole Water reached capacity and overtopped its banks: a large volume of water emerging from the cave system caused flooding of The Stones; overflow from Peakshole Water flooded Eades Fold and Vicarage Lane; water breached drystone walls behind Mill Court gardens, flowed onto Millbridge and then surged down Tricketts Close (first recorded flow on this route); flow was constrained by the low bridge on Millbridge causing upstream backup; floodwater also escaped at the culvert grill at Eyre's Farm and flowed south along Hollowford Road. (p55)","24 residential properties; 5 non–residential properties (p51)
