GB-DEV,2,2016-09-03,50.3516517,-3.5806611,"<div id=""html_f4139ef1c19ce78b3e926461cc4ae28b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Charles Street, Dartmouth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fire service were called and assisted South West Water to pump away water from affected properties; the Fire Service log records this flooding as external. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Devon,"Charles Street, Dartmouth",England,Fire service were called and assisted South West Water to pump away water from affected properties; the Fire Service log records this flooding as external. (p12),,GB-DEV_2_2016-09-03.html,GB-DEV_2_2016-09-03,Devon flooding 03 Sep 2016 - 05 Sep 2016,Flood Investigation Report: Devon Floods 3rd – 5th September 2016,035/Devon County/035/2016/Devon County/Sept 2016 Investigation Report/Final/.pdf
GB-DEV,2,2016-09-03,50.2313564,-3.7791522,"<div id=""html_598cd83d9430a22ea763a1c23b0b3b36"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sandhills Road, Salcombe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road surface showed water accumulation and pooling consistent with surface&ndash;water/highway flooding, creating a hazard for vehicles and pedestrians and indicating poor drainage during the event. [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Devon,"Sandhills Road, Salcombe",England,"Road surface showed water accumulation and pooling consistent with surface–water/highway flooding, creating a hazard for vehicles and pedestrians and indicating poor drainage during the event. [IMG] (p12)",,GB-DEV_2_2016-09-03.html,GB-DEV_2_2016-09-03,Devon flooding 03 Sep 2016 - 05 Sep 2016,Flood Investigation Report: Devon Floods 3rd – 5th September 2016,035/Devon County/035/2016/Devon County/Sept 2016 Investigation Report/Final/.pdf
GB-DEV,2,2016-09-03,50.724140500000004,-3.6607788161410735,"<div id=""html_b1641b83dfc4ff42ac70c290b525b531"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Devon</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread surface&ndash;water / urban flooding across the county between 3 and 5 September 2016. In North Devon this included streets and properties flooded in Braunton and highways flooding elsewhere in the district. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread surface water flooding across the county during September 2016, with flooding concentrated in Braunton and other locations; caused highways to be impassable and prompted development of a local flood alleviation scheme in Braunton. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple surface water flood incidents occurred across Devon during 03 Sep 2016 &ndash; 05 Sep 2016, causing roads to be impassable in locations and water to pond for over 24 hours. The report recommends county&ndash;wide actions and specific interventions for affected communities (notably Braunton). [TAB] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Devon,Devon,England,"Widespread surface–water / urban flooding across the county between 3 and 5 September 2016. In North Devon this included streets and properties flooded in Braunton and highways flooding elsewhere in the district. [PAG] (p11)
