Multiple surface water flood incidents occurred across Devon during 03 Sep 2016 – 05 Sep 2016, causing roads to be impassable in locations and water to pond for over 24 hours. The report recommends county–wide actions and specific interventions for affected communities (notably Braunton). [TAB] (p14)",,GB-DEV_2_2016-09-03.html,GB-DEV_2_2016-09-03,Devon flooding 03 Sep 2016 - 05 Sep 2016,Flood Investigation Report: Devon Floods 3rd – 5th September 2016,035/Devon County/035/2016/Devon County/Sept 2016 Investigation Report/Final/.pdf
GB-DEV,2,2016-09-03,50.724140500000004,-3.6607788161410735,"<div id=""html_cdfcd1c3d5d23385a3304ab269a75801"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Devon</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Short, intense rainfall between 3&ndash;5 September 2016 caused flooding of numerous roads and properties across the county; highway drainage systems struggled or overflowed, producing highway and external property flooding and prompting investigation and recommended maintenance by Devon County Council Highways. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Across Devon (3&ndash;5 Sept 2016) short&ndash;duration, high&ndash;intensity rainfall caused highway drainage and sewer systems in several areas to struggle and sometimes overflow. Roads were closed in parts of South Hams and surface water was reported on roads in South Hams, West Devon, Torridge and Teignbridge; drains became overwhelmed by mud and silt. [IMG,PAG] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties flooded internally [PAG] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Devon,Devon,England,"Short, intense rainfall between 3–5 September 2016 caused flooding of numerous roads and properties across the county; highway drainage systems struggled or overflowed, producing highway and external property flooding and prompting investigation and recommended maintenance by Devon County Council Highways. [PAG] (p8)
