GB-HEF,9,2020-02-16,52.09565855381086,-2.653575999603835,"<div id=""html_f020beac06c9aac9fb3c755c80dc169c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cross Keys</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The settlement is the primary investigation area and is shown within the red&ndash;circled focus on the Environment Agency Flood Map for Planning and adjacent to water features and flood&ndash;prone land, indicating exposure to river flooding risk. [IMG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties and external flooding of outbuildings and gardens. Properties and gardens were inundated by fluvial flows (from the Lugg/Kymin Brook) and surface water; some respondents reported blocked bridges, overflowing ditches and blocked gullies contributing to flood mechanisms. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cross Keys experienced flooding primarily caused by fluvial flows from the Little Lugg and its tributary. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties; depths ranging between less than 6 inches and 2 ft (internal); outbuildings and gardens up to 3 ft; flood durations up to 3 days; five properties with previous flooding (three of which recorded flooding in 2007) (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Cross Keys,England,"The settlement is the primary investigation area and is shown within the red–circled focus on the Environment Agency Flood Map for Planning and adjacent to water features and flood–prone land, indicating exposure to river flooding risk. [IMG] (p1)
