GB-DOR,2,2016-02-07,50.7407081,-2.2666509,"<div id=""html_c000e7a2cfe288e74dbb6744c93969cb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Piddle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Piddle flooding prompted a change to the EA's flood warning threshold to give communities more time to prepare. [TAB] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,River Piddle,England,River Piddle flooding prompted a change to the EA's flood warning threshold to give communities more time to prepare. [TAB] (p17),,GB-DOR_2_2016-02-07.html,GB-DOR_2_2016-02-07,Piddle Valley flooding 07 Feb 2016 - 08 Feb 2016,Flood Investigation Report Piddle Valley 7th - 8th February 2016,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/Feb 2016 Piddle Valley Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,2,2016-02-07,50.80512261060706,-2.4228466281546055,"<div id=""html_17ec76e4fb7b051b5840ab5d07daa026"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church Lane Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Church Lane bridge was identified as a possible restriction to flow that contributed to upstream overtopping; investigations found bed depth could not be reduced due to shallow foundations and no increase in silt was found. [IMG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as posing an issue during flooding; EA worked with DCC to undertake re&ndash;profiling of the grass area in front of the Vicarage to reduce flood impacts at this location. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Church Lane Bridge was identified as a location affected by flooding prompting a feasibility study into reducing flood impacts and investigation of a possible by&ndash;pass channel in Church Lane to alleviate flooding at the bridge. [TAB] (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>three properties [IMG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,Church Lane Bridge,England,"The Church Lane bridge was identified as a possible restriction to flow that contributed to upstream overtopping; investigations found bed depth could not be reduced due to shallow foundations and no increase in silt was found. [IMG] (p13)
