GB-DOR,2,2016-02-07,50.8050263,-2.4223523,"<div id=""html_877ae1b29eb3d5fe270fceca6f2e95db"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church Lane, Piddletrenthide</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Piddle came out of bank upstream of the Church Lane bridge, causing floodwater to overtop and resulting in three properties on Church Lane being flooded internally. Ground and surface water inundation of sewer pipes also caused sewage flooding on Church Lane. [IMG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sewage flooding occurred when ground and surface water inundated sewer pipes in Church Lane. Surface water was also conveyed from the west via a BOAT (byway), and surfacing/blocked gullies contributed to runoff entering Church Lane. Gullies have since been cleared but investigations into improved surfacing and drainage are recommended. [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding impacted Church Lane and its bridge, leading to feasibility work (including a study of a bypass channel) to reduce flood impacts at Church Lane Bridge. [TAB] (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties [IMG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"Church Lane, Piddletrenthide",England,"The River Piddle came out of bank upstream of the Church Lane bridge, causing floodwater to overtop and resulting in three properties on Church Lane being flooded internally. Ground and surface water inundation of sewer pipes also caused sewage flooding on Church Lane. [IMG] (p13)
