GB-DOR,2,2016-02-07,50.7739245,-2.4048353,"<div id=""html_99a5fa5bc1f7703d453cdf281d617c0d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rectory Road, Piddlehinton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding along Rectory Road (approx. 03:30&ndash;04:30 on 08/02/2016); the existing FAS intercepted runoff but was partly overwhelmed and two properties were internally flooded. [IMG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>WDDC carried out jetting through the Flood Alleviation Scheme in Rectory Road, Piddlehinton as a quick&ndash;win maintenance action to address flood conveyance issues. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected Rectory Road, leading to proposals to improve surface water drainage and to modify the entrance to West Lane to allow more surface water into the drainage system. [TAB] (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties [IMG] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"Rectory Road, Piddlehinton",England,"Flooding along Rectory Road (approx. 03:30–04:30 on 08/02/2016); the existing FAS intercepted runoff but was partly overwhelmed and two properties were internally flooded. [IMG] (p15)
