Highway gullies were reported blocked or overwhelmed during the event, producing surface water flow paths at the road edges; this roadside surface water contributed to internal flooding of a property and caused localised roadside inundation. [TAB] (p60)
The Hatchet Leys Lane bridge area experienced overtopping (from Cowerde Brook), causing road flooding and contributing to roads being unpassable in the village. (p64)","13 vehicles; one person [TAB] (p34)
