GB-KEN,16,2019-06-10,51.3353316,0.3604755,"<div id=""html_b2c2064d21d130ec560d4226c4f50a82"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Southfield Shaw, Culverstone Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Post&ndash;flood inspection identified gully issues at the junction with Harvel Road; further investigation and repairs to gullies/soakaway were scheduled. [TAB,PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The junction with Harvel Road was inspected and gullies cleansed after the storm; cleansing identified non&ndash;flowing and connection issues at multiple gullies and further investigative works (including CCTV) and soakaway checks were scheduled. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 gullies; one gully not flowing; 5 gullies; three gullies (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Southfield Shaw, Culverstone Green",England,"Post–flood inspection identified gully issues at the junction with Harvel Road; further investigation and repairs to gullies/soakaway were scheduled. [TAB,PAG] (p9)
The junction with Harvel Road was inspected and gullies cleansed after the storm; cleansing identified non–flowing and connection issues at multiple gullies and further investigative works (including CCTV) and soakaway checks were scheduled. (p10)",7 gullies; one gully not flowing; 5 gullies; three gullies (p10),GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc.html,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc,Gravesham flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Vigo Village and Culverstone,063/Kent/Section-19-flooding-report-for-Vigo-and-Culverstone.pdf
GB-KEN,16,2019-06-10,51.330946,0.3646925,"<div id=""html_6a59dd1e7a04d4d0468c1e022af6182b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Erskine Road, Vigo Village</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowed from the woodland, crossed Erskine (sic) and then travelled along Admers Wood and Beech Mast as part of the overland flood pathway. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Post&ndash;flood cleansing and inspection found the highway drained by 49 gullies and identified two gullies not flowing between Commonly Road and Waterlow Road; CCTV surveys were scheduled to locate faults and soakaways near Ash Keys were scheduled for cleansing as part of recovery works. [TAB,PAG] (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>49 gullies; two gullies [TAB,PAG] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Erskine Road, Vigo Village",England,"Surface water flowed from the woodland, crossed Erskine (sic) and then travelled along Admers Wood and Beech Mast as part of the overland flood pathway. (p8)
Post–flood cleansing and inspection found the highway drained by 49 gullies and identified two gullies not flowing between Commonly Road and Waterlow Road; CCTV surveys were scheduled to locate faults and soakaways near Ash Keys were scheduled for cleansing as part of recovery works. [TAB,PAG] (p9)","49 gullies; two gullies [TAB,PAG] (p9)",GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc.html,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc,Gravesham flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Vigo Village and Culverstone,063/Kent/Section-19-flooding-report-for-Vigo-and-Culverstone.pdf
GB-KEN,16,2019-06-10,51.3265493,0.3422759,"<div id=""html_cff5bd4dd2dc3d29a4d5849ff85dcbfb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Harvel Road, Vigo Village</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Post&ndash;flood inspection identified issues with gullies at the junction with Southfield Shaw; these gullies and the soakaway at this location require further investigation and scheduled works. [TAB,PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At the junction with Southfield Shaw gullies were cleansed as part of the post&ndash;storm response; inspections found one gully (adjacent to No. 20) not flowing and identified connection issues requiring further investigation; CCTV and further investigative works were scheduled. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 gullies; one gully not flowing; 5 gullies; three gullies (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Harvel Road, Vigo Village",England,"Post–flood inspection identified issues with gullies at the junction with Southfield Shaw; these gullies and the soakaway at this location require further investigation and scheduled works. [TAB,PAG] (p9)
At the junction with Southfield Shaw gullies were cleansed as part of the post–storm response; inspections found one gully (adjacent to No. 20) not flowing and identified connection issues requiring further investigation; CCTV and further investigative works were scheduled. (p10)",7 gullies; one gully not flowing; 5 gullies; three gullies (p10),GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc.html,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc,Gravesham flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Vigo Village and Culverstone,063/Kent/Section-19-flooding-report-for-Vigo-and-Culverstone.pdf
GB-KEN,16,2019-06-10,51.3325557,0.3667306,"<div id=""html_fb672219f68de8071bad5515f5305b61"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Commority Road, Vigo Village</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Post&ndash;event cleansing identified drainage faults: two gullies not flowing between Commority Road and Waterlow Road (drainage defects discovered as part of the response to the heavy rainfall that caused flooding). (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two gullies not flowing (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Commority Road, Vigo Village",England,Post–event cleansing identified drainage faults: two gullies not flowing between Commority Road and Waterlow Road (drainage defects discovered as part of the response to the heavy rainfall that caused flooding). (p10),two gullies not flowing (p10),GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc.html,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc,Gravesham flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Vigo Village and Culverstone,063/Kent/Section-19-flooding-report-for-Vigo-and-Culverstone.pdf
GB-KEN,16,2019-06-10,51.3266164,0.3437821,"<div id=""html_35b819bf68640ded542e9c8417afcf81"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Waterlow Road, Vigo Village</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Post&ndash;event cleansing identified drainage faults: two gullies not flowing between Commority Road and Waterlow Road (defects found during investigations following the heavy rainfall that caused flooding). (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two gullies not flowing (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Waterlow Road, Vigo Village",England,Post–event cleansing identified drainage faults: two gullies not flowing between Commority Road and Waterlow Road (defects found during investigations following the heavy rainfall that caused flooding). (p10),two gullies not flowing (p10),GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc.html,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc,Gravesham flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Vigo Village and Culverstone,063/Kent/Section-19-flooding-report-for-Vigo-and-Culverstone.pdf
GB-KEN,16,2019-06-10,51.3409894,0.3513995,"<div id=""html_542facecd51c31c32dccffbaef74bd22"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Carters Hill Lane, Culverstone Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The soakaway at the junction with White Post Land (within Carters Hill Road, sic, junction) was inspected after the storm and found to be functioning but near the end of its useful life; KCC and Gravesham Borough Council are arranging replacement works and junction resurfacing/kerbing. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one soakaway (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Carters Hill Lane, Culverstone Green",England,"The soakaway at the junction with White Post Land (within Carters Hill Road, sic, junction) was inspected after the storm and found to be functioning but near the end of its useful life; KCC and Gravesham Borough Council are arranging replacement works and junction resurfacing/kerbing. (p10)",one soakaway (p10),GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc.html,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc,Gravesham flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Vigo Village and Culverstone,063/Kent/Section-19-flooding-report-for-Vigo-and-Culverstone.pdf
GB-KEN,16,2019-06-10,51.2070749,0.7210362,"<div id=""html_e7d6cae9eb8cddd13cc3f6f1e29e547e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kent</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Very heavy rainfall across Kent on 10 June 2019 led to surface water flooding; areas including West Kingsdown, Vigo, Snodland and Swanley were particularly badly affected. The Vigo/Culverstone area saw properties flooded internally by surface water. [MUL] (p1)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>around 100 properties [MUL] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Kent,England,"Very heavy rainfall across Kent on 10 June 2019 led to surface water flooding; areas including West Kingsdown, Vigo, Snodland and Swanley were particularly badly affected. The Vigo/Culverstone area saw properties flooded internally by surface water. [MUL] (p1)",around 100 properties [MUL] (p1),GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc.html,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc,Gravesham flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Vigo Village and Culverstone,063/Kent/Section-19-flooding-report-for-Vigo-and-Culverstone.pdf
GB-KEN,16,2019-06-10,51.3303854,0.3590695,"<div id=""html_de82f612d30d1da356bae82fab8e0bf9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Vigo Village</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Vigo was described as particularly badly affected by very heavy rainfall on 10 June 2019; properties in the Vigo area were flooded by surface water and many were affected internally. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple residential properties were affected by flooding with clusters of affected properties in the central and eastern residential zones and some on the western edge of the village. [IMG] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The village experienced both external and internal property flooding during the event (including a report under the heading 'Vigo School' of external and internal flooding). Multiple residential properties on named streets in the village were affected (internal and external), and roads were impacted by surface water. [PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding flowed from the woodland south of Admers Wood, crossed Erskine, travelled along Admers Wood and Beech Mast, then along footpaths into Ferndown Road. Fire Brigade attended and pumped flood water. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Prolonged heavy rainfall and overland flows from surrounding woodland and rural catchment led to significant surface water flooding across the village. Surface water runoff combined with overwhelmed private and highway drainage; foul sewers (foul&ndash;only public sewers) contributed to sewer surcharging and manhole overflows in parts of the village. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A heavy rainstorm (reported as a 1&ndash;in&ndash;217&ndash;year event) overwhelmed highway drainage. Overland flows from developed areas, surrounding woodland and rural catchment travelled along dry valleys and collected at local topographical low points, causing flooding to properties in the village. (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>around 100 properties (Vigo and Culverstone combined) (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties on Rhododendron Avenue; 1 property on White Post Lane; 1 property on Meadow Lane; 1 property on Wrotham Road [PAG] (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Vigo Village,England,"Vigo was described as particularly badly affected by very heavy rainfall on 10 June 2019; properties in the Vigo area were flooded by surface water and many were affected internally. (p1)
Multiple residential properties were affected by flooding with clusters of affected properties in the central and eastern residential zones and some on the western edge of the village. [IMG] (p2)
The village experienced both external and internal property flooding during the event (including a report under the heading 'Vigo School' of external and internal flooding). Multiple residential properties on named streets in the village were affected (internal and external), and roads were impacted by surface water. [PAG] (p4)
Surface water flooding flowed from the woodland south of Admers Wood, crossed Erskine, travelled along Admers Wood and Beech Mast, then along footpaths into Ferndown Road. Fire Brigade attended and pumped flood water. (p7)
Prolonged heavy rainfall and overland flows from surrounding woodland and rural catchment led to significant surface water flooding across the village. Surface water runoff combined with overwhelmed private and highway drainage; foul sewers (foul–only public sewers) contributed to sewer surcharging and manhole overflows in parts of the village. [PAG] (p8)
A heavy rainstorm (reported as a 1–in–217–year event) overwhelmed highway drainage. Overland flows from developed areas, surrounding woodland and rural catchment travelled along dry valleys and collected at local topographical low points, causing flooding to properties in the village. (p11)","around 100 properties (Vigo and Culverstone combined) (p1)
5 properties on Rhododendron Avenue; 1 property on White Post Lane; 1 property on Meadow Lane; 1 property on Wrotham Road [PAG] (p4)",GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc.html,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc,Gravesham flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Vigo Village and Culverstone,063/Kent/Section-19-flooding-report-for-Vigo-and-Culverstone.pdf
GB-KEN,16,2019-06-10,51.3412115,0.3478821,"<div id=""html_716bf5797002ddfee11006bfa7743790"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Culverstone Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in Culverstone were flooded by surface water during the 10 June 2019 event; many properties were affected internally. Additional flooding incidents affecting properties in Culverstone occurred on 20 December 2019 and 9 February 2020 following further heavy rain on saturated ground. [MUL] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in Culverstone were affected by flooding; roads in the area received emergency repairs (locations marked on the map). [IMG] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At least one property in Culverstone (Heron Hill Lane) reported internal flooding to the cellar. [PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected roads (including Rhododendron Avenue) and caused internal flooding to at least one property in the village. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A heavy rainstorm overwhelmed drainage and caused overland flows from developed areas and surrounding catchments to flow along dry valleys and collect in local topographical lows, causing flooding to properties in the village and vicinity. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The same extreme storm overwhelmed drainage causing overland flows to follow dry valleys and collect at local low points, resulting in flooding to properties. Drainage asset issues were identified: the soakaway at the junction of White Post Lane and Carters Hill Road is functioning but nearing end of life; soakaways at Whitepost Lane/Rhododendron Avenue and Meadow Lane were found in good condition; gullies at Harvel Road and Southfield Shaw require further investigation and the soakaway at that location is to be inspected. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>around 100 properties (Vigo and Culverstone combined) [MUL] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Culverstone Green,England,"Properties in Culverstone were flooded by surface water during the 10 June 2019 event; many properties were affected internally. Additional flooding incidents affecting properties in Culverstone occurred on 20 December 2019 and 9 February 2020 following further heavy rain on saturated ground. [MUL] (p1)
Properties in Culverstone were affected by flooding; roads in the area received emergency repairs (locations marked on the map). [IMG] (p2)
At least one property in Culverstone (Heron Hill Lane) reported internal flooding to the cellar. [PAG] (p4)
Surface water flooding affected roads (including Rhododendron Avenue) and caused internal flooding to at least one property in the village. (p8)
A heavy rainstorm overwhelmed drainage and caused overland flows from developed areas and surrounding catchments to flow along dry valleys and collect in local topographical lows, causing flooding to properties in the village and vicinity. [PAG] (p10)
The same extreme storm overwhelmed drainage causing overland flows to follow dry valleys and collect at local low points, resulting in flooding to properties. Drainage asset issues were identified: the soakaway at the junction of White Post Lane and Carters Hill Road is functioning but nearing end of life; soakaways at Whitepost Lane/Rhododendron Avenue and Meadow Lane were found in good condition; gullies at Harvel Road and Southfield Shaw require further investigation and the soakaway at that location is to be inspected. [PAG] (p11)","around 100 properties (Vigo and Culverstone combined) [MUL] (p1)
1 property [PAG] (p4)
one property (p8)",GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc.html,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc,Gravesham flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Vigo Village and Culverstone,063/Kent/Section-19-flooding-report-for-Vigo-and-Culverstone.pdf
GB-KEN,16,2019-06-10,51.342944665244204,0.2627640552737047,"<div id=""html_7761ce00b5c2efb90cb3e6a2d9a44b65"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Kingsdown</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as being particularly badly affected by the very heavy rainfall and associated surface water flooding on 10 June 2019. (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,West Kingsdown,England,Identified as being particularly badly affected by the very heavy rainfall and associated surface water flooding on 10 June 2019. (p1),,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc.html,GB-KEN_16_2019-06-10_etc,Gravesham flooding 10 Jun 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Vigo Village and Culverstone,063/Kent/Section-19-flooding-report-for-Vigo-and-Culverstone.pdf
GB-KEN,9,2021-07-25,51.1340666,0.4443803,"<div id=""html_2b0c3cf763668488ab7b9359e7213aef"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Capel Cross</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map shows reported flood location(s) at or adjacent to Capel Cross. Flooding is concentrated on approach roads and junctions, causing localised inundation of road(s) and potential disruption to vehicular access to Horsmonden. [IMG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Capel Cross,England,"Map shows reported flood location(s) at or adjacent to Capel Cross. Flooding is concentrated on approach roads and junctions, causing localised inundation of road(s) and potential disruption to vehicular access to Horsmonden. [IMG] (p13)",,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25.html,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25,Horsmonden flooding 25 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Horsmonden,063/Kent/Horsmonden-section-19-flood-investigation.pdf
GB-KEN,9,2021-07-25,51.1014817,0.3915671,"<div id=""html_73d361a6de94cbf23e2fe1d8e746484b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Teise</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Unnamed tributaries of the River Teise are associated with high risk of surface&ndash;water flooding. These tributaries act as natural overland flow paths where runoff can accumulate in local depressions during or after heavy rainfall; their locations are relatively consistent with reported properties affected by the flood event. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Teise is cited as being associated with multiple historic flood events affecting Horsmonden and the surrounding area. [IMG] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,River Teise,England,"Unnamed tributaries of the River Teise are associated with high risk of surface–water flooding. These tributaries act as natural overland flow paths where runoff can accumulate in local depressions during or after heavy rainfall; their locations are relatively consistent with reported properties affected by the flood event. (p4)
The River Teise is cited as being associated with multiple historic flood events affecting Horsmonden and the surrounding area. [IMG] (p5)",,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25.html,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25,Horsmonden flooding 25 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Horsmonden,063/Kent/Horsmonden-section-19-flood-investigation.pdf
GB-KEN,9,2021-07-25,51.1502614,0.4236353,"<div id=""html_a363175630edb6ab085b898d40de410e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Furnace Lane, Horsmonden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties experienced internal and external flooding; emergency services pumped water from properties. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water affected the road; blocked gully identified which led to flooding of the carriageway. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from nearby agricultural land (where impermeable plastic sheeting had been used between blackcurrant crops) increased runoff volumes and flow, overwhelming existing drainage and causing flooding to properties on Furnace Lane. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>KFRS attended a flooding incident here during the 25 July 2021 event and undertook actions such as creating channels to aid water flow and distributing sandbags. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Impermeable agricultural coverings (plastic sheeting) on land near Furnace Lane likely increased overland flows and surface runoff during the intense rainfall, increasing volumes entering the highway drainage and contributing to the systems being overwhelmed. The agricultural plastic sheeting between crops near Furnace Lane was removed in February 2022. [MUL] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed in Appendix A as a road to which flood surveys were sent; flood surveys were distributed and responses recorded for this location. [TAB] (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties flooded internally; 2 properties flooded externally; 30 cm &ndash; 100 cm of flood water within properties; KFRS pumped floodwater from 4 properties [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 flooding incident (part of 4 incidents in Horsmonden) (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Furnace Lane, Horsmonden",England,"Properties experienced internal and external flooding; emergency services pumped water from properties. [TAB] (p2)
Surface water affected the road; blocked gully identified which led to flooding of the carriageway. (p6)
Surface water runoff from nearby agricultural land (where impermeable plastic sheeting had been used between blackcurrant crops) increased runoff volumes and flow, overwhelming existing drainage and causing flooding to properties on Furnace Lane. (p10)
KFRS attended a flooding incident here during the 25 July 2021 event and undertook actions such as creating channels to aid water flow and distributing sandbags. (p11)
Impermeable agricultural coverings (plastic sheeting) on land near Furnace Lane likely increased overland flows and surface runoff during the intense rainfall, increasing volumes entering the highway drainage and contributing to the systems being overwhelmed. The agricultural plastic sheeting between crops near Furnace Lane was removed in February 2022. [MUL] (p12)
