GB-KEN,9,2021-07-25,51.1317461,0.4218213,"<div id=""html_42e9ca6167ae600a6755ddd789b9cdaa"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lamberhurst Road, Horsmonden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported property flooding (internal/external not specified) and carriageway flooding affecting the road surface. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road flooded as water from a blocked gully entered the carriageway. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The highway drainage system surcharged when pipe capacity was exceeded, producing road (carriageway) flooding; residents reported the road surface started to break up as a result of floodwater. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>KCC Highways attended Lamberhurst Road during the 25 July 2021 event. A road closure was put in place at the junction with Fromandez Drive, a manhole was damaged due to floodwater surcharging, and a tanker attended the location. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway surface water drainage and culverted watercourses surcharged during the intense rainfall, resulting in carriageway flooding. Culvert beneath Lamberhurst Road is identified for further investigation and some highway drainage pipes were upsized as a remedial action. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map shows flood&ndash;location markers along main approach roads including Lamberhurst Road, indicating surface water flooding that may impede access along this road. [IMG] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 road closure; 1 manhole damaged; 1 tanker attended (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Lamberhurst Road, Horsmonden",England,"Reported property flooding (internal/external not specified) and carriageway flooding affecting the road surface. [TAB] (p2)
