GB-KEN,9,2021-07-25,51.1338318,0.444293,"<div id=""html_96cc2c301a435272b33594f3e38c1187"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Goudhurst Road, Horsmonden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road/carriageway flooded due to a blocked drain/gully. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood&ndash;location markers are distributed along main roads entering Horsmonden, including Goudhurst Road, indicating flooding that could disrupt traffic and access on this route. [IMG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Goudhurst Road, Horsmonden",England,"Road/carriageway flooded due to a blocked drain/gully. (p6)
Flood–location markers are distributed along main roads entering Horsmonden, including Goudhurst Road, indicating flooding that could disrupt traffic and access on this route. [IMG] (p13)",,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25.html,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25,Horsmonden flooding 25 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Horsmonden,063/Kent/Horsmonden-section-19-flood-investigation.pdf
GB-KEN,9,2021-07-25,51.1392191,0.4297665,"<div id=""html_a3bf967eea5b19c6851fe324dbfd947c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Heath, Horsmonden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property was damaged by flooding. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"The Heath, Horsmonden",England,Property was damaged by flooding. (p6),,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25.html,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25,Horsmonden flooding 25 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Horsmonden,063/Kent/Horsmonden-section-19-flood-investigation.pdf
GB-KEN,9,2021-07-25,51.1527257,0.4329868,"<div id=""html_796c2a6ba84175835e03adb0abd65b3f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Yew Tree Green Road, Horsmonden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ponding and surface water flooding along the road causing inundation of the carriageway. (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 inches deep (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Yew Tree Green Road, Horsmonden",England,Ponding and surface water flooding along the road causing inundation of the carriageway. (p6),8 inches deep (p6),GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25.html,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25,Horsmonden flooding 25 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Horsmonden,063/Kent/Horsmonden-section-19-flood-investigation.pdf
GB-KEN,9,2021-07-25,51.1384413,0.4291331,"<div id=""html_b37fa0ae002f1a287fded6632a36a7fa"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Gun Back Lane, Horsmonden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The local highway drainage system in the vicinity (junction with Lamberhurst Road) was overwhelmed during the intense rainfall; a new gully was installed at the junction with Lamberhurst Road as a remedial measure. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Gun Back Lane, Horsmonden",England,The local highway drainage system in the vicinity (junction with Lamberhurst Road) was overwhelmed during the intense rainfall; a new gully was installed at the junction with Lamberhurst Road as a remedial measure. (p12),,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25.html,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25,Horsmonden flooding 25 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Horsmonden,063/Kent/Horsmonden-section-19-flood-investigation.pdf
GB-KEN,9,2021-07-25,51.140942949999996,0.44196746604559434,"<div id=""html_aa3444a77ffc43df4700fe229757ca59"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Horsmonden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple streets within Horsmonden reported internal and external property flooding and carriageway flooding during the event (see listed roads in Table 1). (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the village experienced internal and external flooding and local carriageway flooding; KFRS pumped floodwater from four properties and made one property safe. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas of Horsmonden are indicated to be at high risk of surface&ndash;water flooding, mainly associated with the unnamed tributaries of the River Teise. Local loamy/clayey soils with impeded drainage promote overland runoff, causing accumulation in depressions that is consistent with the locations of reported properties affected during the flood event. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The village and surrounding areas have flooded on a number of historic occasions associated with the River Teise, ordinary watercourses, surface water runoff and blocked drains. [IMG,TAB] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Affected properties in Horsmonden were associated with the flood event on 25 July 2021; rainfall recorded at the nearby Horsmonden gauge and radar across the local catchment were used in the analysis of the event. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A flood event in the village affected properties (recorded flooded properties are referenced). The radar&ndash;derived rainfall distribution and catchment analysis were used specifically because the radar grid squares covered the recorded flooded properties in Horsmonden; the most intense hourly rainfall occurred between 11:00&ndash;12:00 during the event. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents reported flooding between 13:00 and 14:00 when intense rainfall and surface runoff overwhelmed drainage and sewer systems, causing carriageway flooding and flooding of properties within Horsmonden. [IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 25 July 2021 Horsmonden experienced multiple flooding incidents where watercourse blockages and culvert overtopping affected residential streets (Brenchley Road, Furnace Lane, Marle Place Road and Olivers Court). (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The report states it is possible that the Hormonden area was impacted by a more intensive, localised rainfall event (on 25 July 2021) that was not accurately recorded by gauges/radar and which may have contributed to the level of flooding experienced. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred at multiple locations within the village (red&ndash;dotted points), concentrated along main roads and at entry/junction points, creating vulnerability to transport access and local movement. [IMG] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties flooded internally (Furnace Lane); 2 properties flooded externally (Furnace Lane); 2 properties internal (Spout Lane); 1 property internal (Olivers Court); KFRS pumped floodwater from 10 properties (Olivers Court) and from 4 properties (Furnace Lane); 1 property internal (Marle Place Road); carriageway flooding reported at Lamberhurst Road, Lamberts Place and Oast View; depths reported: 30 cm &ndash; 100 cm (Furnace Lane); up to 25 cm (Spout Lane); 8 &ndash; 10 cm (Marle Place Road) (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (Brenchley Road internal); 4 properties (pumped by KFRS); 1 property (Green Road internal); 1 property (Fromandez Drive external); 1 property (Orchard Close internal); 1 property (Kirkins Close flooding, internal unknown); 1 property (Back Lane flooding, internal unknown) (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 flooding incidents (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>20 properties flooded internally; 4 properties flooded externally (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Horsmonden,England,"Multiple streets within Horsmonden reported internal and external property flooding and carriageway flooding during the event (see listed roads in Table 1). (p2)
Properties in the village experienced internal and external flooding and local carriageway flooding; KFRS pumped floodwater from four properties and made one property safe. (p3)
Areas of Horsmonden are indicated to be at high risk of surface–water flooding, mainly associated with the unnamed tributaries of the River Teise. Local loamy/clayey soils with impeded drainage promote overland runoff, causing accumulation in depressions that is consistent with the locations of reported properties affected during the flood event. (p4)
The village and surrounding areas have flooded on a number of historic occasions associated with the River Teise, ordinary watercourses, surface water runoff and blocked drains. [IMG,TAB] (p5)
Affected properties in Horsmonden were associated with the flood event on 25 July 2021; rainfall recorded at the nearby Horsmonden gauge and radar across the local catchment were used in the analysis of the event. (p8)
A flood event in the village affected properties (recorded flooded properties are referenced). The radar–derived rainfall distribution and catchment analysis were used specifically because the radar grid squares covered the recorded flooded properties in Horsmonden; the most intense hourly rainfall occurred between 11:00–12:00 during the event. (p9)
Residents reported flooding between 13:00 and 14:00 when intense rainfall and surface runoff overwhelmed drainage and sewer systems, causing carriageway flooding and flooding of properties within Horsmonden. [IMG] (p10)
On 25 July 2021 Horsmonden experienced multiple flooding incidents where watercourse blockages and culvert overtopping affected residential streets (Brenchley Road, Furnace Lane, Marle Place Road and Olivers Court). (p11)
The report states it is possible that the Hormonden area was impacted by a more intensive, localised rainfall event (on 25 July 2021) that was not accurately recorded by gauges/radar and which may have contributed to the level of flooding experienced. (p12)
Flooding occurred at multiple locations within the village (red–dotted points), concentrated along main roads and at entry/junction points, creating vulnerability to transport access and local movement. [IMG] (p13)","4 properties flooded internally (Furnace Lane); 2 properties flooded externally (Furnace Lane); 2 properties internal (Spout Lane); 1 property internal (Olivers Court); KFRS pumped floodwater from 10 properties (Olivers Court) and from 4 properties (Furnace Lane); 1 property internal (Marle Place Road); carriageway flooding reported at Lamberhurst Road, Lamberts Place and Oast View; depths reported: 30 cm – 100 cm (Furnace Lane); up to 25 cm (Spout Lane); 8 – 10 cm (Marle Place Road) (p2)
1 property (Brenchley Road internal); 4 properties (pumped by KFRS); 1 property (Green Road internal); 1 property (Fromandez Drive external); 1 property (Orchard Close internal); 1 property (Kirkins Close flooding, internal unknown); 1 property (Back Lane flooding, internal unknown) (p3)
4 flooding incidents (p11)
20 properties flooded internally; 4 properties flooded externally (p12)",GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25.html,GB-KEN_9_2021-07-25,Horsmonden flooding 25 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Horsmonden,063/Kent/Horsmonden-section-19-flood-investigation.pdf
GB-NNH,9,2016-06-13,52.4915362,-0.7231198,"<div id=""html_011bbb220ef5dc710a44b1ffc2be0ae2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cottingham Road, Corby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding occurred within the Medical Practice premises (areas of the building were flooded internally). (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The road was flooded during the heavy rainfall event, predominantly to the side of the carriageway nearest the Medical Practice. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cottingham Road was affected by the flooding incident; Main Rivers were not considered to have been a factor in the cause of flooding at this location. (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Cottingham Road, Corby",England,"Internal flooding occurred within the Medical Practice premises (areas of the building were flooded internally). (p11)
The road was flooded during the heavy rainfall event, predominantly to the side of the carriageway nearest the Medical Practice. (p13)
Cottingham Road was affected by the flooding incident; Main Rivers were not considered to have been a factor in the cause of flooding at this location. (p18)",,GB-NNH_9_2016-06-13.html,GB-NNH_9_2016-06-13,Corby flooding 13 Jun 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Medical Practice, Cottingham Road, Corby, 13th June 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/23134/FIR/Cottingham-Road/Corby/Rev-03.pdf
GB-NNH,9,2016-06-13,52.487736,-0.7032713,"<div id=""html_82af960f83da900df88eba234f964a04"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Corby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At least one property in Corby (the Medical Practice on Cottingham Road) experienced internal flooding due to heavy short&ndash;duration rainfall and overwhelmed surface water drainage. [MUL] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense short&ndash;duration rainfall produced surface water run&ndash;off in Corby that caused flooding at a Medical Practice (basement staff room and storage area). [TAB,MUL] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property&ndash;level flooding occurred in Corby; investigations identified that no external sources of surface water were considered a factor and that surveys of privately owned drainage systems on the affected property are required to fully understand the flooding issue and identify possible solutions. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Mapped area around the site in Corby shows convergence of surface water flow and a schematic area of flooding indicating overland/surface water and urban flooding affecting parts of the town during the incident. The inset map highlights a catchment with a history of a flood incident, showing hydrological connectivity relevant to flood impacts in Corby. [IMG] (p29)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [MUL] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Corby,England,"At least one property in Corby (the Medical Practice on Cottingham Road) experienced internal flooding due to heavy short–duration rainfall and overwhelmed surface water drainage. [MUL] (p7)
Intense short–duration rainfall produced surface water run–off in Corby that caused flooding at a Medical Practice (basement staff room and storage area). [TAB,MUL] (p12)
Property–level flooding occurred in Corby; investigations identified that no external sources of surface water were considered a factor and that surveys of privately owned drainage systems on the affected property are required to fully understand the flooding issue and identify possible solutions. (p15)
Mapped area around the site in Corby shows convergence of surface water flow and a schematic area of flooding indicating overland/surface water and urban flooding affecting parts of the town during the incident. The inset map highlights a catchment with a history of a flood incident, showing hydrological connectivity relevant to flood impacts in Corby. [IMG] (p29)",1 property [MUL] (p7),GB-NNH_9_2016-06-13.html,GB-NNH_9_2016-06-13,Corby flooding 13 Jun 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Medical Practice, Cottingham Road, Corby, 13th June 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/23134/FIR/Cottingham-Road/Corby/Rev-03.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.6671337,-2.5690019,"<div id=""html_a61804e4279948cdb7aa73c5f9f55c4c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>B3157 at Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flows from Front Street and surrounding lanes conveyed onto the B3157 Coast Road, causing significant traffic disruption and closure of the road for an extended period; highway inundated by floodwater. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Mud and debris from the event contributed to blocking highway gullies along the B3157, impairing drainage and leading to surface water issues on the road. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwaters flowed onto and across the B3157; vehicles travelling the road produced bow&ndash;waves that exacerbated property flooding. Residents reported delays in road closure during the event. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater reached the bottom of Front Street and flowed onto the B3157 Coast Road, causing carriageway inundation and prompting an emergency response. (p26)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flood depths of up to approximately 400mm on the highway (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,B3157 at Portesham,England,"Flows from Front Street and surrounding lanes conveyed onto the B3157 Coast Road, causing significant traffic disruption and closure of the road for an extended period; highway inundated by floodwater. (p8)
Mud and debris from the event contributed to blocking highway gullies along the B3157, impairing drainage and leading to surface water issues on the road. (p13)
Floodwaters flowed onto and across the B3157; vehicles travelling the road produced bow–waves that exacerbated property flooding. Residents reported delays in road closure during the event. (p15)
Floodwater reached the bottom of Front Street and flowed onto the B3157 Coast Road, causing carriageway inundation and prompting an emergency response. (p26)",flood depths of up to approximately 400mm on the highway (p8),GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.6828918,-2.5657829,"<div id=""html_1ff7569f41bf3eed5d2901fcc72761c8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Portesham Hill, Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Steep ground on Portesham Hill produced rapid surface runoff that conveyed high&ndash;velocity and high&ndash;volume flows toward Portesham village, contributing to inundation of highway drainage. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface runoff and silt deposition from the hillside contributed to local flooding; Natural Flood Management measures (e.g. silt traps, cross drains) were recommended to reduce run&ndash;off and silt deposition. [TAB] (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"Portesham Hill, Portesham",England,"Steep ground on Portesham Hill produced rapid surface runoff that conveyed high–velocity and high–volume flows toward Portesham village, contributing to inundation of highway drainage. (p8)
Surface runoff and silt deposition from the hillside contributed to local flooding; Natural Flood Management measures (e.g. silt traps, cross drains) were recommended to reduce run–off and silt deposition. [TAB] (p18)",,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.6712178,-2.5632486,"<div id=""html_00d58a8cb4f8a423e755812c0ee6f0bb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Front Street, Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Front Street experienced surface water flooding when overland flows and out&ndash;of&ndash;bank flows from Portesham Stream inundated the road; flooding then conveyed onto the B3157 Coast Road causing major traffic disruption and closure. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property experienced internal flooding due to fluvial (river) flooding during the event. [TAB] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water was conveyed downhill towards Front Street, carrying and depositing a large amount of silt and gravel from the surrounding hills, Rocky Lane and the eroding verge beside the C112 road. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High&ndash;velocity surface water and runoff from the surrounding hills and C112 overwhelmed the highway drainage; the highway drain surcharged and flowed along Front Street. A watercourse on the western side overtopped upstream of several culverts and flowed back onto the road. A locked sluice gate prevented additional flows being diverted to the elevated eastern channel. Obstructions within the channel caused one property to flood. [IMG,PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Exceedance flows were conveyed onto Front Street; mud and debris contributed to blocking highway gullies, causing surface water to flow/pond on the carriageway. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Front Street was subject to flooding risk that prompted actions to formalise a management plan and coordinate bodies to manage drainage and reduce future surface water flooding. [TAB] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater overtopped boundaries and ran from raised garden areas onto the pavement and carriageway, inundating the road outside residential properties; muddy runoff and soil washed over the pavement and across the carriageway. [PAG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Footpath and adjacent carriageway were inundated; water flowing over the sidewalk beside a stone wall with emergency vehicles on the road responding to the flooding. [PAG] (p26)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flood depths up to approximately 400 mm on the highway (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [TAB] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property [IMG,PAG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"Front Street, Portesham",England,"Front Street experienced surface water flooding when overland flows and out–of–bank flows from Portesham Stream inundated the road; flooding then conveyed onto the B3157 Coast Road causing major traffic disruption and closure. (p8)
One property experienced internal flooding due to fluvial (river) flooding during the event. [TAB] (p9)
Surface water was conveyed downhill towards Front Street, carrying and depositing a large amount of silt and gravel from the surrounding hills, Rocky Lane and the eroding verge beside the C112 road. (p10)
High–velocity surface water and runoff from the surrounding hills and C112 overwhelmed the highway drainage; the highway drain surcharged and flowed along Front Street. A watercourse on the western side overtopped upstream of several culverts and flowed back onto the road. A locked sluice gate prevented additional flows being diverted to the elevated eastern channel. Obstructions within the channel caused one property to flood. [IMG,PAG] (p11)
Exceedance flows were conveyed onto Front Street; mud and debris contributed to blocking highway gullies, causing surface water to flow/pond on the carriageway. (p13)
Front Street was subject to flooding risk that prompted actions to formalise a management plan and coordinate bodies to manage drainage and reduce future surface water flooding. [TAB] (p18)
Floodwater overtopped boundaries and ran from raised garden areas onto the pavement and carriageway, inundating the road outside residential properties; muddy runoff and soil washed over the pavement and across the carriageway. [PAG] (p25)
Footpath and adjacent carriageway were inundated; water flowing over the sidewalk beside a stone wall with emergency vehicles on the road responding to the flooding. [PAG] (p26)","flood depths up to approximately 400 mm on the highway (p8)
1 property [TAB] (p9)
one property [IMG,PAG] (p11)",GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.672998028614074,-2.56207198441046,"<div id=""html_e1884e7e9189ac73254d33d5288db2c7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rocky Lane, Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced surface water flooding from overland flows originating on higher ground after heavy rainfall; runoff from the tarmacked track on Rocky Lane was reported by residents as contributing to surface water issues that reached the village. [PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding impacted Rocky Lane during the 19 January 2019 event; runoff issues from Rocky Lane were reported and one property experienced internal flooding. [TAB] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Erosion of the verge/hills around Rocky Lane mobilised silt and gravel that were conveyed downhill in the flood flows and deposited on Front Street, contributing debris in the flood. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flows from surrounding hills were conveyed via a farm track and the Right of Way onto Rocky Lane, bringing significant silt and gravel which blocked highway gullies and increased silt load in the watercourse. A soakaway at the entrance to the RoW could not cope with the volume of surface water. A recently tarmacked section increased surface water run&ndash;off velocity and changed the camber, directing flow towards properties on the southern side of the lane; one property experienced internal flooding. [IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water runoff and silt deposition caused overland flow and flooding affecting Rocky Lane; recommended Natural Flood Management interventions to reduce runoff and silt deposition. [TAB] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected the lane; the soakaway was inspected because flows were unable to enter the system and the surface water drainage of the adjacent tarmacked track requires improvements to pass flows. [TAB] (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property internally flooded [TAB] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"Rocky Lane, Portesham",England,"Experienced surface water flooding from overland flows originating on higher ground after heavy rainfall; runoff from the tarmacked track on Rocky Lane was reported by residents as contributing to surface water issues that reached the village. [PAG] (p8)
Surface water flooding impacted Rocky Lane during the 19 January 2019 event; runoff issues from Rocky Lane were reported and one property experienced internal flooding. [TAB] (p9)
Erosion of the verge/hills around Rocky Lane mobilised silt and gravel that were conveyed downhill in the flood flows and deposited on Front Street, contributing debris in the flood. (p11)
Overland flows from surrounding hills were conveyed via a farm track and the Right of Way onto Rocky Lane, bringing significant silt and gravel which blocked highway gullies and increased silt load in the watercourse. A soakaway at the entrance to the RoW could not cope with the volume of surface water. A recently tarmacked section increased surface water run–off velocity and changed the camber, directing flow towards properties on the southern side of the lane; one property experienced internal flooding. [IMG] (p12)
Surface–water runoff and silt deposition caused overland flow and flooding affecting Rocky Lane; recommended Natural Flood Management interventions to reduce runoff and silt deposition. [TAB] (p18)
Surface water flooding affected the lane; the soakaway was inspected because flows were unable to enter the system and the surface water drainage of the adjacent tarmacked track requires improvements to pass flows. [TAB] (p19)","1 property internally flooded [TAB] (p9)
one property [IMG] (p12)",GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.6707982,-2.5424092,"<div id=""html_2fdff82fcad5e800095692b596946d00"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Winters Lane, Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced surface water flooding during the heavy rainfall event; reported as receiving overland flows from the surrounding hills which inundated the highway drainage. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Mud and debris from the slippage of the farm track, mixed with exceedance flows, resulted in flooding of Winters Lane. Local ditches/culverts were overwhelmed or blocked during the event. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Obstructed ditches and culverts caused runoff to flood the carriageway; actions recommended to inspect and clear obstructions and undertake regular maintenance to reduce flooding onto the highway. [TAB] (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"Winters Lane, Portesham",England,"Experienced surface water flooding during the heavy rainfall event; reported as receiving overland flows from the surrounding hills which inundated the highway drainage. (p8)
Mud and debris from the slippage of the farm track, mixed with exceedance flows, resulted in flooding of Winters Lane. Local ditches/culverts were overwhelmed or blocked during the event. (p13)
Obstructed ditches and culverts caused runoff to flood the carriageway; actions recommended to inspect and clear obstructions and undertake regular maintenance to reduce flooding onto the highway. [TAB] (p18)",,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.6682918,-2.5691121,"<div id=""html_395fc7c3f731cc101a8e11aff8157e1b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Malthouse Meadows, Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding caused internal flooding to properties in Malthouse Meadows during the 19 January 2019 event. [TAB] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Silt build&ndash;up and downstream obstructions caused the watercourse to come out of bank, resulting in property flooding. During the 19 January 2019 event the railway culvert was operating at approximately 75% capacity; the upstream weir was lowered to route more flow into the site attenuation pond (which filled more quickly) and this reduced downstream out&ndash;of&ndash;bank flows. The attenuation pond did not overspill onto the highway on this occasion. The downstream watercourse was de&ndash;silted shortly after the event. [IMG,MUL] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The drainage scheme at Malthouse Meadows was identified for maintenance and compliance with an agreed management plan due to flood/drainage performance issues following the event. [TAB] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Culvert under the railway embankment was discharging muddy, fast&ndash;moving water into the channel, indicating surcharged drainage/runoff that contributed to local flooding and stressed the drainage asset. (p26)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property internally flooded [TAB] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"Malthouse Meadows, Portesham",England,"Fluvial flooding caused internal flooding to properties in Malthouse Meadows during the 19 January 2019 event. [TAB] (p9)
Silt build–up and downstream obstructions caused the watercourse to come out of bank, resulting in property flooding. During the 19 January 2019 event the railway culvert was operating at approximately 75% capacity; the upstream weir was lowered to route more flow into the site attenuation pond (which filled more quickly) and this reduced downstream out–of–bank flows. The attenuation pond did not overspill onto the highway on this occasion. The downstream watercourse was de–silted shortly after the event. [IMG,MUL] (p14)
The drainage scheme at Malthouse Meadows was identified for maintenance and compliance with an agreed management plan due to flood/drainage performance issues following the event. [TAB] (p18)
Culvert under the railway embankment was discharging muddy, fast–moving water into the channel, indicating surcharged drainage/runoff that contributed to local flooding and stressed the drainage asset. (p26)",1 property internally flooded [TAB] (p9),GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.6686206,-2.5664725,"<div id=""html_b82efbf6d36511348d80e72a1c61f5ac"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Goose Hill, Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties at Goose Hill caused by a combination of surface water runoff and fluvial (river) flooding; highway flooding is also reported in the event narrative for the afternoon rainfall. [TAB] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwaters from exceedance flows were conveyed towards Goose Hill during the event, indicating overland/surface water impacts in that area. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water and fluvial floodwater flowed through the village and onto the B3157, bypassing the upstream open ditch due to topography and road camber. Floodwater collected against properties and across the road; vehicles travelling on the B3157 generated 'bow&ndash;waves' that pushed water above low external thresholds and into properties. [IMG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flows from Goose Hill contributed to flooding downstream; a flood alleviation scheme was proposed to intercept these flows. [TAB] (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties [TAB] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>six properties [IMG] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"Goose Hill, Portesham",England,"Internal flooding of residential properties at Goose Hill caused by a combination of surface water runoff and fluvial (river) flooding; highway flooding is also reported in the event narrative for the afternoon rainfall. [TAB] (p9)
Floodwaters from exceedance flows were conveyed towards Goose Hill during the event, indicating overland/surface water impacts in that area. (p13)
Surface water and fluvial floodwater flowed through the village and onto the B3157, bypassing the upstream open ditch due to topography and road camber. Floodwater collected against properties and across the road; vehicles travelling on the B3157 generated 'bow–waves' that pushed water above low external thresholds and into properties. [IMG] (p15)
Overland flows from Goose Hill contributed to flooding downstream; a flood alleviation scheme was proposed to intercept these flows. [TAB] (p18)","6 properties [TAB] (p9)
six properties [IMG] (p15)",GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.6705575,-2.5620198,"<div id=""html_05222051b2343953d09780a0057176c9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Winters Close, Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A portion of surface water was discharged into a culvert along the back of properties in Winters Close as part of the exceedance flow path during the event. (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"Winters Close, Portesham",England,A portion of surface water was discharged into a culvert along the back of properties in Winters Close as part of the exceedance flow path during the event. (p13),,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.6708885,-2.566494,"<div id=""html_8aea4a881d226dc76c86aac675d24b78"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cemetery Road, Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water overland flows were conveyed along Cemetery Road and diverted into a highway grip, which led to diversion through a residential garden and external flooding. (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"Cemetery Road, Portesham",England,"Surface water overland flows were conveyed along Cemetery Road and diverted into a highway grip, which led to diversion through a residential garden and external flooding. (p16)",,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.6703176,-2.5651881,"<div id=""html_774a9a45b7aa960263e00ff46252c0c4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>New Road, Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from adjoining areas flowed onto the road surface toward New Road, contributing to inundation of the carriageway and affecting access to nearby residences. (p25)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,"New Road, Portesham",England,"Floodwater from adjoining areas flowed onto the road surface toward New Road, contributing to inundation of the carriageway and affecting access to nearby residences. (p25)",,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
GB-DOR,3,2019-01-19,50.66954807866514,-2.5646342164140012,"<div id=""html_4dd23c5846e65d4c3307f08ec1909b03"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Portesham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Portesham stream flows southwards through the village and splits into raised channels; the village is the subject of the Flood Investigation Report and the catchment&#8217;s flashy response to storm rainfall is identified as causing flood risk to the settlement. [IMG,PAG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flows from higher ground converged on the village leading to surface water inundation of streets and properties; local drainage was overwhelmed. [IMG,PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Village&ndash;wide flooding during the 19 January 2019 event: property and highway flooding occurred during a highly localised afternoon rainfall. Drainage issues were reported (blocked/restricted culverts, blocked highway gullies, and non&ndash;operating flow control sluices) which contributed to flood impacts across the village. [TAB,PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from the saturated catchment (hills to the north and from the C112 road) was conveyed downhill into the village, bringing large amounts of silt and gravel from surrounding hills, Rocky Lane and the eroding verge of the C112 road. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from surrounding hills and C112 and overtopping of the local stream caused flooding on Front Street in Portesham, surcharging highway drains, depositing silt and gravel, and resulting in at least one property being flooded. [IMG,PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood&ndash;response and mitigation works implemented after the event: culvert under the track to the Dairy Farm cleared and the upstream watercourse desilted; Malthouse Meadows side weir set to the agreed level and formed in brick; obstructions cleared from the swale on the inlet to the attenuation pond; attenuation pond base level corrected (soil removed and now operating at design capacity); a rain gauge was installed by the LLFA to record storm events. [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The village experienced surface&ndash;water runoff and overland flow during the event, causing highway flooding, silt deposition and drainage problems (references to Front Street, Malthouse Meadows and sluice gate operation are made in relation to managing flood risk). [TAB,PAG] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Village experienced surface water flooding associated with intense rainfall on 19 January 2019, prompting a Section 19 flood investigation. [IMG,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood extents from a 1:100&ndash;year surface water event encroached on built&ndash;up areas of Portesham, with infrastructure such as roads and parking areas affected. Appendix photos show flooding in the elevated western channel looking north&ndash;east towards Front Street. [IMG,PAG] (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties [IMG,PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties internally flooded (total); includes 6 properties in Goose Hill, 1 in Rocky Lane, 1 in Malthouse Meadows, 1 on Front Street [TAB,PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property [IMG,PAG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Dorset,Portesham,England,"Portesham stream flows southwards through the village and splits into raised channels; the village is the subject of the Flood Investigation Report and the catchment’s flashy response to storm rainfall is identified as causing flood risk to the settlement. [IMG,PAG] (p6)
Overland flows from higher ground converged on the village leading to surface water inundation of streets and properties; local drainage was overwhelmed. [IMG,PAG] (p8)
Village–wide flooding during the 19 January 2019 event: property and highway flooding occurred during a highly localised afternoon rainfall. Drainage issues were reported (blocked/restricted culverts, blocked highway gullies, and non–operating flow control sluices) which contributed to flood impacts across the village. [TAB,PAG] (p9)
Surface water from the saturated catchment (hills to the north and from the C112 road) was conveyed downhill into the village, bringing large amounts of silt and gravel from surrounding hills, Rocky Lane and the eroding verge of the C112 road. [PAG] (p10)
Surface water runoff from surrounding hills and C112 and overtopping of the local stream caused flooding on Front Street in Portesham, surcharging highway drains, depositing silt and gravel, and resulting in at least one property being flooded. [IMG,PAG] (p11)
Flood–response and mitigation works implemented after the event: culvert under the track to the Dairy Farm cleared and the upstream watercourse desilted; Malthouse Meadows side weir set to the agreed level and formed in brick; obstructions cleared from the swale on the inlet to the attenuation pond; attenuation pond base level corrected (soil removed and now operating at design capacity); a rain gauge was installed by the LLFA to record storm events. [TAB,PAG] (p17)
The village experienced surface–water runoff and overland flow during the event, causing highway flooding, silt deposition and drainage problems (references to Front Street, Malthouse Meadows and sluice gate operation are made in relation to managing flood risk). [TAB,PAG] (p18)
Village experienced surface water flooding associated with intense rainfall on 19 January 2019, prompting a Section 19 flood investigation. [IMG,PAG] (p21)
Flood extents from a 1:100–year surface water event encroached on built–up areas of Portesham, with infrastructure such as roads and parking areas affected. Appendix photos show flooding in the elevated western channel looking north–east towards Front Street. [IMG,PAG] (p24)","9 properties [IMG,PAG] (p8)
9 properties internally flooded (total); includes 6 properties in Goose Hill, 1 in Rocky Lane, 1 in Malthouse Meadows, 1 on Front Street [TAB,PAG] (p9)
one property [IMG,PAG] (p11)",GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19.html,GB-DOR_3_2019-01-19,Portesham flooding 19 Jan 2019,Flood Investigation Report: Portesham 19th January 2019 Event,037/Dorset/037/2020/Dorset/January 2019 Portesham Flood Investigation Report.pdf
