approx 750mm deep internal flooding [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p11)
50mm; one property internally flooded; one additional property had drainage unable to discharge [PAG] (p12)",GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09,Raunds flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Brick Kiln Road/North Street, Raunds, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22520/FIR-Raunds/Rev03/190916.pdf
GB-NNH,7,2016-03-09,52.3624324,-0.5173041,"<div id=""html_fdca93fbf10b28bcde8177129e39c5bf"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brooks Road, Raunds</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A watercourse flows into the north of Raunds along Brooks Road and this watercourse is part of the Main River through Raunds. The report attributes the March 2016 event to ordinary watercourse flooding (alongside surface water and agricultural runoff), so the watercourse along Brooks Road was implicated in the ordinary watercourse flooding during the 9 March 2016 event. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Brooks Road, Raunds",England,"A watercourse flows into the north of Raunds along Brooks Road and this watercourse is part of the Main River through Raunds. The report attributes the March 2016 event to ordinary watercourse flooding (alongside surface water and agricultural runoff), so the watercourse along Brooks Road was implicated in the ordinary watercourse flooding during the 9 March 2016 event. (p10)",,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09,Raunds flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Brick Kiln Road/North Street, Raunds, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22520/FIR-Raunds/Rev03/190916.pdf
GB-NNH,7,2016-03-09,52.3425697,-0.5375262,"<div id=""html_e098fe064789efce33c8ef9f6e109a13"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brook Street, Raunds</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Main River through Raunds is joined near Brook Street by a second Main River from Butts Road. The report identifies ordinary watercourse flooding as a cause of the March 2016 event, so the Main River route joining near Brook Street was implicated in ordinary watercourse flooding during that event. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Brook Street, Raunds",England,"The Main River through Raunds is joined near Brook Street by a second Main River from Butts Road. The report identifies ordinary watercourse flooding as a cause of the March 2016 event, so the Main River route joining near Brook Street was implicated in ordinary watercourse flooding during that event. (p10)",,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09,Raunds flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Brick Kiln Road/North Street, Raunds, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22520/FIR-Raunds/Rev03/190916.pdf
GB-NNH,7,2016-03-09,52.3409543,-0.5439991,"<div id=""html_805d0d971d95fea37018a9ffecefbc49"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mackenzie Road, Raunds</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse flows south through the centre of Raunds parallel with High Street, Brook Street and MacKenzie Road and then flows to the River Nene. The report attributes the March 2016 event to ordinary watercourse flooding among other causes, so the watercourse running parallel to MacKenzie Road was implicated in the ordinary watercourse flooding during the 9 March 2016 event. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Mackenzie Road, Raunds",England,"The watercourse flows south through the centre of Raunds parallel with High Street, Brook Street and MacKenzie Road and then flows to the River Nene. The report attributes the March 2016 event to ordinary watercourse flooding among other causes, so the watercourse running parallel to MacKenzie Road was implicated in the ordinary watercourse flooding during the 9 March 2016 event. (p10)",,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09,Raunds flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Brick Kiln Road/North Street, Raunds, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22520/FIR-Raunds/Rev03/190916.pdf
GB-NNH,7,2016-03-09,52.3491556,-0.5341038,"<div id=""html_d2a85a04a9d7d970213710d17736dd3b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Furnells Close, Raunds</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The ditch in the south verge was reported blocked at the point where it enters a pipe immediately north of Furnells Close; the blockage caused the ditch to overtop and made a significant contribution to surface water flowing onto Brick Kiln Road and towards North Street. During the 25 April investigation ditch systems were observed to back up at the same location due to the reported blockage (though rainfall on that date was not enough to overtop). [MUL] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Furnells Close, Raunds",England,The ditch in the south verge was reported blocked at the point where it enters a pipe immediately north of Furnells Close; the blockage caused the ditch to overtop and made a significant contribution to surface water flowing onto Brick Kiln Road and towards North Street. During the 25 April investigation ditch systems were observed to back up at the same location due to the reported blockage (though rainfall on that date was not enough to overtop). [MUL] (p12),,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09,Raunds flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Brick Kiln Road/North Street, Raunds, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22520/FIR-Raunds/Rev03/190916.pdf
GB-NNH,7,2016-03-09,52.3500142,-0.5367678,"<div id=""html_4f1fa254189328ad3c8a0b813d7ee9d9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Enterprise Road, Raunds</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The map marks Q2 showing muddy water flowing from Enterprise Road into the overland flow routes. This indicates Enterprise Road generated or conveyed runoff that contributed to surface&ndash;water overland flooding affecting nearby residential areas during the incident. [IMG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from Enterprise Road flowed onto Brick Kiln Road and was channelled along the road edge into a road gully during heavy rainfall; runoff was muddy indicating sediment transport. [IMG] (p57)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowed from Enterprise Road onto Brick Kiln Road at the intersection, crossing the curb and contributing to pooling and runoff on Brick Kiln Road; this indicates insufficient drainage and a source of roadway flooding and hazard. [IMG,PAG] (p58)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface runoff and muddy surface water originating from Enterprise Road flowed onto Brick Kiln Road, contributing to carriageway contamination and surface water issues. [IMG,PAG] (p68)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Muddy surface water and muddy patches on the pavement originating from Enterprise Road and flowing onto Brick Kiln Road; visible runoff from the adjacent parking/parking area toward the road. [IMG,PAG] (p69)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Enterprise Road, Raunds",England,"The map marks Q2 showing muddy water flowing from Enterprise Road into the overland flow routes. This indicates Enterprise Road generated or conveyed runoff that contributed to surface–water overland flooding affecting nearby residential areas during the incident. [IMG] (p30)
Surface water runoff from Enterprise Road flowed onto Brick Kiln Road and was channelled along the road edge into a road gully during heavy rainfall; runoff was muddy indicating sediment transport. [IMG] (p57)
Surface water flowed from Enterprise Road onto Brick Kiln Road at the intersection, crossing the curb and contributing to pooling and runoff on Brick Kiln Road; this indicates insufficient drainage and a source of roadway flooding and hazard. [IMG,PAG] (p58)
Surface runoff and muddy surface water originating from Enterprise Road flowed onto Brick Kiln Road, contributing to carriageway contamination and surface water issues. [IMG,PAG] (p68)
Muddy surface water and muddy patches on the pavement originating from Enterprise Road and flowing onto Brick Kiln Road; visible runoff from the adjacent parking/parking area toward the road. [IMG,PAG] (p69)",,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09,Raunds flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Brick Kiln Road/North Street, Raunds, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22520/FIR-Raunds/Rev03/190916.pdf
GB-NNH,7,2016-03-09,52.3450436,-0.5360257,"<div id=""html_613525ddec0dba17dd3544ddf92ed9e9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Raunds</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Main River entrance to the culvert under High Street was heavily obstructed by dense vegetation and overgrowth, preventing access and restricting inspection/maintenance. The blockage would have reduced culvert conveyance during the 9th March 2016 flood, increasing local flood risk at the culvert inlet. [IMG,PAG] (p71)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Main River was actively flowing into the culvert entrance beneath High Street; the inlet showed turbid, sediment&ndash;laden water and visible debris at the culvert mouth, indicating elevated river flows affecting the culvert. [IMG,PAG] (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"High Street, Raunds",England,"The Main River entrance to the culvert under High Street was heavily obstructed by dense vegetation and overgrowth, preventing access and restricting inspection/maintenance. The blockage would have reduced culvert conveyance during the 9th March 2016 flood, increasing local flood risk at the culvert inlet. [IMG,PAG] (p71)
The Main River was actively flowing into the culvert entrance beneath High Street; the inlet showed turbid, sediment–laden water and visible debris at the culvert mouth, indicating elevated river flows affecting the culvert. [IMG,PAG] (p72)",,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09,Raunds flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Brick Kiln Road/North Street, Raunds, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22520/FIR-Raunds/Rev03/190916.pdf
GB-NNH,7,2016-03-09,52.3106138,-0.8659129831915817,"<div id=""html_b80a6f6b4576c5624c783774e3ff277b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Northamptonshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Across Northamptonshire the same heavy rainfall event (9 March 2016) caused widespread issues: drainage and watercourses contributed to flooding. Over 70 properties were reported flooded internally across the county and there were over 200 reports of flooding from a combination of agricultural runoff, surface water runoff and ordinary watercourse flooding. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 9 March 2016 approximately 30 mm of rain fell across Northamptonshire; the event produced over 200 reports of flooding across the county including over 70 properties reported internally flooded, from a combination of agricultural runoff, surface water runoff and ordinary watercourse flooding. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Approximately 30 mm of rain fell across the county in the first 12 hours of 9 March 2016. Over 70 properties were reported flooded internally and there were a total of over 200 reports of flooding across Northamptonshire from a combination of agricultural runoff, surface water runoff and ordinary watercourse flooding. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 70 properties (internally flooded); over 200 reports of flooding (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 70 properties; over 200 reports of flooding [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Over 70 properties; over 200 reports of flooding [PAG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Northamptonshire,England,"Across Northamptonshire the same heavy rainfall event (9 March 2016) caused widespread issues: drainage and watercourses contributed to flooding. Over 70 properties were reported flooded internally across the county and there were over 200 reports of flooding from a combination of agricultural runoff, surface water runoff and ordinary watercourse flooding. (p7)
On 9 March 2016 approximately 30 mm of rain fell across Northamptonshire; the event produced over 200 reports of flooding across the county including over 70 properties reported internally flooded, from a combination of agricultural runoff, surface water runoff and ordinary watercourse flooding. [PAG] (p9)
Approximately 30 mm of rain fell across the county in the first 12 hours of 9 March 2016. Over 70 properties were reported flooded internally and there were a total of over 200 reports of flooding across Northamptonshire from a combination of agricultural runoff, surface water runoff and ordinary watercourse flooding. [PAG] (p10)","over 70 properties (internally flooded); over 200 reports of flooding (p7)
over 70 properties; over 200 reports of flooding [PAG] (p9)
Over 70 properties; over 200 reports of flooding [PAG] (p10)",GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09,Raunds flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Brick Kiln Road/North Street, Raunds, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22520/FIR-Raunds/Rev03/190916.pdf
GB-NNH,7,2016-03-09,52.34671,-0.5265435,"<div id=""html_d00d0547e5c999f57d890db6aec5a623"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Raunds</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The flood incident at Brick Kiln Road / North Street in Raunds (9 March 2016) resulted in internal flooding of a property in Raunds; the cause is described as heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment with drainage unable to convey water, producing overland flow to low points near properties. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood incident on 9 March 2016 led to internal flooding in the town: causes reported include agricultural runoff, surface water runoff and ordinary watercourse flooding. The investigation recorded internal flooding and repeated incidents at the Brick Kiln Road/North Street location. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Raunds was affected during the event: the town is crossed by a Main River (the Hog Dyke) and associated watercourses and ditches that connect to drainage in the town. The report records an internally flooded property in Raunds (on North Street). (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment caused drainage systems across Raunds to be unable to collect and convey rainwater to larger watercourses, resulting in excess surface water following natural contours to low points around private properties. Drainage systems (including ditches in the south verge) became backed up or overtopped, main drainage systems were fully surcharged causing carriageway ponding and domestic drainage backups with reported internal flooding of property(ies). A reported blockage where a ditch enters a pipe immediately north of Furnells Close caused local backing up of the verge ditch. [PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Main drainage systems at low points were fully surcharged causing ponding in carriageways; surcharge led to domestic drainage backing up and reported internal flooding of property(ies). (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Site of flood incidents prompting a Section 19 investigation by the LLFA (NCC); the report discusses identifying causes and recording assets and hotspots related to flooding in Raunds. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (internally flooded) (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 70 properties; over 200 reports of flooding [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property internally flooded (on North Street) (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one property (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Raunds,England,"The flood incident at Brick Kiln Road / North Street in Raunds (9 March 2016) resulted in internal flooding of a property in Raunds; the cause is described as heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment with drainage unable to convey water, producing overland flow to low points near properties. (p7)
Flood incident on 9 March 2016 led to internal flooding in the town: causes reported include agricultural runoff, surface water runoff and ordinary watercourse flooding. The investigation recorded internal flooding and repeated incidents at the Brick Kiln Road/North Street location. [PAG] (p9)
Raunds was affected during the event: the town is crossed by a Main River (the Hog Dyke) and associated watercourses and ditches that connect to drainage in the town. The report records an internally flooded property in Raunds (on North Street). (p10)
Heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment caused drainage systems across Raunds to be unable to collect and convey rainwater to larger watercourses, resulting in excess surface water following natural contours to low points around private properties. Drainage systems (including ditches in the south verge) became backed up or overtopped, main drainage systems were fully surcharged causing carriageway ponding and domestic drainage backups with reported internal flooding of property(ies). A reported blockage where a ditch enters a pipe immediately north of Furnells Close caused local backing up of the verge ditch. [PAG] (p13)
Main drainage systems at low points were fully surcharged causing ponding in carriageways; surcharge led to domestic drainage backing up and reported internal flooding of property(ies). (p14)
Site of flood incidents prompting a Section 19 investigation by the LLFA (NCC); the report discusses identifying causes and recording assets and hotspots related to flooding in Raunds. (p16)","one property (internally flooded) (p7)
