1 property internally flooded (on North Street) (p10)
one property (p14)",GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_7_2016-03-09,Raunds flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Brick Kiln Road/North Street, Raunds, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22520/FIR-Raunds/Rev03/190916.pdf
GB-NNH,28,2020-12-23,52.4398752,-0.6905157,"<div id=""html_90e1d539dd745d459a496ec40524f3e8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Newton Road, Geddington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Subject of a North Northamptonshire Council (LLFA) Section 19 flood investigation into flooding at Stamford Road/Newton Road, Geddington. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding occurred at properties on Newton Road; water entered buildings during the event. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding at Newton Road on 23rd December 2020 led to internal flooding of properties in the area and contributed to a formal S19 investigation being undertaken. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland / surface water flooding inundated rear gardens and caused internal flooding in several properties (ground floor and an integral garage). One resident moved out for a period after internal flooding and has since installed their own flood barriers. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland sheet flow and two distinct flow routes ran north&ndash;south through rear gardens leading to internal flooding of properties. Road gullies were reported lacking capacity, and a recently constructed property's bund on the northern boundary likely diverted and concentrated flows toward two other Newton Road properties. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Property 1 (north): external ~460mm; internal ~50&ndash;75mm. Property 2 (north): external ~150&ndash;200mm; internal ~25&ndash;45mm. Property 3 (north): external flooding (no depth given). Property 4 (north): external ~250mm (close to causing internal flooding). Property 5 (north): external ~25mm. Property 1 (south): internal flooding of integral garage ~200mm. Total: 3 properties internally flooded on Newton Road. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (internally flooded) [PAG] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Newton Road, Geddington",England,"Subject of a North Northamptonshire Council (LLFA) Section 19 flood investigation into flooding at Stamford Road/Newton Road, Geddington. (p2)
Internal flooding occurred at properties on Newton Road; water entered buildings during the event. (p6)
Flooding at Newton Road on 23rd December 2020 led to internal flooding of properties in the area and contributed to a formal S19 investigation being undertaken. (p8)
Overland / surface water flooding inundated rear gardens and caused internal flooding in several properties (ground floor and an integral garage). One resident moved out for a period after internal flooding and has since installed their own flood barriers. (p15)
Overland sheet flow and two distinct flow routes ran north–south through rear gardens leading to internal flooding of properties. Road gullies were reported lacking capacity, and a recently constructed property's bund on the northern boundary likely diverted and concentrated flows toward two other Newton Road properties. [PAG] (p16)","Property 1 (north): external ~460mm; internal ~50–75mm. Property 2 (north): external ~150–200mm; internal ~25–45mm. Property 3 (north): external flooding (no depth given). Property 4 (north): external ~250mm (close to causing internal flooding). Property 5 (north): external ~25mm. Property 1 (south): internal flooding of integral garage ~200mm. Total: 3 properties internally flooded on Newton Road. (p15)
3 properties (internally flooded) [PAG] (p16)",GB-NNH_28_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_28_2020-12-23,Geddington flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Geddington, 23 December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Stamford Road and Newton Road, Geddington.pdf"
GB-NNH,28,2020-12-23,52.4290499,-0.6906393,"<div id=""html_1c18d515e30a5f91eaeba237ba24fac5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stamford Road, Geddington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding occurred at properties on Stamford Road; water entered buildings during the event. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding at Stamford Road on 23rd December 2020 led to internal flooding of properties in the area and contributed to a formal S19 investigation being undertaken. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding affected rear gardens and the frontage from the carriageway; no internal flooding reported for the properties listed. Other dwellings on Stamford Road also reported external rear&ndash;garden flooding. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A ditch running parallel to Stamford Road breached at a culvert, causing overland flows that affected footways and front gardens. One property on Stamford Road was reported to have flooded internally. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Property 1: external flooding approx. 75mm (from carriageway); Property 4: external flooding approx. 200mm. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (internally flooded) [PAG] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Stamford Road, Geddington",England,"Internal flooding occurred at properties on Stamford Road; water entered buildings during the event. (p6)
Flooding at Stamford Road on 23rd December 2020 led to internal flooding of properties in the area and contributed to a formal S19 investigation being undertaken. (p8)
External flooding affected rear gardens and the frontage from the carriageway; no internal flooding reported for the properties listed. Other dwellings on Stamford Road also reported external rear–garden flooding. (p15)
A ditch running parallel to Stamford Road breached at a culvert, causing overland flows that affected footways and front gardens. One property on Stamford Road was reported to have flooded internally. [PAG] (p16)","Property 1: external flooding approx. 75mm (from carriageway); Property 4: external flooding approx. 200mm. (p15)
1 property (internally flooded) [PAG] (p16)",GB-NNH_28_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_28_2020-12-23,Geddington flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Geddington, 23 December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Stamford Road and Newton Road, Geddington.pdf"
GB-NNH,28,2020-12-23,52.4344234,-0.6909737,"<div id=""html_f98a03ccc988465252009b45d351d23e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>New Road, Geddington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding caused internal flooding to a conservatory in one property and external flooding to other properties. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Converging overland flow routes crossed Newton Road and affected properties on the southern side of Newton Road and New Road; properties experienced overland/external flooding and there were localised areas of standing water. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Property 1: internal (conservatory) ~200mm and external ~300mm. Property 2: external flooding estimated ~200&ndash;300mm. Total: 1 property internally flooded on New Road. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"New Road, Geddington",England,"Surface water flooding caused internal flooding to a conservatory in one property and external flooding to other properties. (p15)
Converging overland flow routes crossed Newton Road and affected properties on the southern side of Newton Road and New Road; properties experienced overland/external flooding and there were localised areas of standing water. (p16)",Property 1: internal (conservatory) ~200mm and external ~300mm. Property 2: external flooding estimated ~200–300mm. Total: 1 property internally flooded on New Road. (p15),GB-NNH_28_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_28_2020-12-23,Geddington flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Geddington, 23 December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Stamford Road and Newton Road, Geddington.pdf"
GB-NNH,28,2020-12-23,52.43782548021765,-0.6857582948220019,"<div id=""html_6392025f4ccdbc6328df10869fb808e4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Geddington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding at the Stamford Road / Newton Road area of Geddington caused internal flooding of several properties. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding occurred at several properties in Geddington during the event on 23rd December 2020, prompting a formal S19 flood investigation. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense, short&ndash;duration heavy rainfall produced overland flows from agricultural land that converged and caused internal flooding of dwellings. Lack of ditches immediately upstream of the affected homes allowed uncontrolled flows to reach properties; there were no community or property&ndash;level resilience measures in place. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The village was the subject of a Section 19 flood investigation following flooding on 23rd December 2020. (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Geddington,England,"Flooding at the Stamford Road / Newton Road area of Geddington caused internal flooding of several properties. (p6)
Internal flooding occurred at several properties in Geddington during the event on 23rd December 2020, prompting a formal S19 flood investigation. (p8)
Intense, short–duration heavy rainfall produced overland flows from agricultural land that converged and caused internal flooding of dwellings. Lack of ditches immediately upstream of the affected homes allowed uncontrolled flows to reach properties; there were no community or property–level resilience measures in place. (p18)
The village was the subject of a Section 19 flood investigation following flooding on 23rd December 2020. (p21)",4 properties (p18),GB-NNH_28_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_28_2020-12-23,Geddington flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Geddington, 23 December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Stamford Road and Newton Road, Geddington.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.719069,-1.9178217,"<div id=""html_45abc4e5305095204895ade7bd691f35"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Branksome Park Wood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>An open watercourse that receives flow from the Wessex Water surface water sewer runs down Branksome Park Wood; this channel conveyed excess runoff during the event (including 4 June 2022). A debris screen at the culvert leading into this watercourse was cleared at the end of October 2022 to improve drainage after the flooding. [PAG] (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The debris screen at the end of the culvert that leads into the watercourse in Branksome Park Wood was blocking drainage (contributing to reduced drainage capacity) and was cleared at the end of October 2022, which improved the drainage capability. [MUL] (p25)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Branksome Park Wood,England,"An open watercourse that receives flow from the Wessex Water surface water sewer runs down Branksome Park Wood; this channel conveyed excess runoff during the event (including 4 June 2022). A debris screen at the culvert leading into this watercourse was cleared at the end of October 2022 to improve drainage after the flooding. [PAG] (p24)
The debris screen at the end of the culvert that leads into the watercourse in Branksome Park Wood was blocking drainage (contributing to reduced drainage capacity) and was cleared at the end of October 2022, which improved the drainage capability. [MUL] (p25)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.71835,-1.8761166,"<div id=""html_c6c2e082df69589686cb8d35e08e3682"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lower Gardens</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater covered much of the park area, submerging benches and pathways as shown in imagery and described in the report; one kiosk likely flooded. [IMG] (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one kiosk [IMG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Lower Gardens,England,"Floodwater covered much of the park area, submerging benches and pathways as shown in imagery and described in the report; one kiosk likely flooded. [IMG] (p30)",one kiosk [IMG] (p30),GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.73681543722981,-1.9407545054998117,"<div id=""html_22f96e626a0fefca0fdc0ecad3ae95e2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Newtown and Heatherlands</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced internal flooding of residential properties during the event. [TAB] (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential properties [TAB] (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Newtown and Heatherlands,England,Experienced internal flooding of residential properties during the event. [TAB] (p19),2 residential properties [TAB] (p19),GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.741102556132695,-1.9146957283486086,"<div id=""html_e1c76e7e89975e47c299521be9a6814d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Alderney and Bourne Valley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced internal flooding of commercial property during the event. [TAB] (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial property [TAB] (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Alderney and Bourne Valley,England,Experienced internal flooding of commercial property during the event. [TAB] (p19),1 commercial property [TAB] (p19),GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.76724526192537,-1.885822907103926,"<div id=""html_bb195e4cfc135ca1b91b1164515c3262"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Redhill and Northbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a residential property (home flooded internally). [TAB] (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential property [TAB] (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Redhill and Northbourne,England,Internal flooding of a residential property (home flooded internally). [TAB] (p19),1 residential property [TAB] (p19),GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7269859,-1.9987384,"<div id=""html_985105f11fa1188cc6d30a82362b70fc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Holes Bay</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Downstream channel capacity within the SSSI in Holes Bay restricted the outfall&#8217;s ability to discharge surface water after the flood event, contributing to reduced drainage efficiency from upstream (including Blandford Road). [IMG] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Holes Bay,England,"Downstream channel capacity within the SSSI in Holes Bay restricted the outfall’s ability to discharge surface water after the flood event, contributing to reduced drainage efficiency from upstream (including Blandford Road). [IMG] (p22)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7642066,-1.9240679,"<div id=""html_e361521eb106b7afc63329067a3e453c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ringwood Road, Bournemouth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reports on social media described Ringwood Road as flooded during the intense rainfall on the night of 4&ndash;5 June 2022, indicating highway/surface&ndash;water flooding affecting the road. (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Ringwood Road, Bournemouth",England,"Reports on social media described Ringwood Road as flooded during the intense rainfall on the night of 4–5 June 2022, indicating highway/surface–water flooding affecting the road. (p20)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7125533,-1.9981511,"<div id=""html_02de5998909ecbf948fbf2b7a04d0ca7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Blandford Road, Poole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water accumulated at the low point on Blandford Road causing localised flooding of the highway; runoff south of the railway entered highway gullies and drained into a channel near Hewitt Road that discharges to Holes Bay. Following the flooding event, outfall channels were desilted and reprofiled to improve drainage, and highways gully improvements were carried out. [PAG] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Blandford Road is at a low point where surface water accumulates south of the railway, flows into highway gullies and drains into a channel near Hewitt Road toward Holes Bay. The location has experienced flooding (investigated for the 20 July 2021 rainfall event) and is shown to be at risk on local surface water flood maps; this topographic and tidal situation limits the effectiveness of partial works and suggests property&ndash;level resilience measures should be considered. (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Blandford Road, Poole",England,"Surface water accumulated at the low point on Blandford Road causing localised flooding of the highway; runoff south of the railway entered highway gullies and drained into a channel near Hewitt Road that discharges to Holes Bay. Following the flooding event, outfall channels were desilted and reprofiled to improve drainage, and highways gully improvements were carried out. [PAG] (p22)
Blandford Road is at a low point where surface water accumulates south of the railway, flows into highway gullies and drains into a channel near Hewitt Road toward Holes Bay. The location has experienced flooding (investigated for the 20 July 2021 rainfall event) and is shown to be at risk on local surface water flood maps; this topographic and tidal situation limits the effectiveness of partial works and suggests property–level resilience measures should be considered. (p23)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7242302,-1.9250543,"<div id=""html_9bfd889acc78d69d2db3f6f688277379"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Archway Road, Penn Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff was channelled to a low point at the bottom of Archway Road where drainage was overwhelmed beyond design capacity, resulting in flooding during the event on 4 June 2022. Blocked highway gullies (exacerbated by pine needles and debris) and the connection to a Wessex Water surface water sewer contributed to the issue. Post&ndash;event works included an additional gully connection completed in October 2022 and clearance of the downstream culvert debris screen to improve drainage. (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected the area around Archway Road during the rainfall event of 4&ndash;5 June 2022, leading to the area being identified for a Surface Water Management Plan study and consideration of long&ndash;term flood alleviation measures. [TAB] (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Archway Road, Penn Hill",England,"Surface water runoff was channelled to a low point at the bottom of Archway Road where drainage was overwhelmed beyond design capacity, resulting in flooding during the event on 4 June 2022. Blocked highway gullies (exacerbated by pine needles and debris) and the connection to a Wessex Water surface water sewer contributed to the issue. Post–event works included an additional gully connection completed in October 2022 and clearance of the downstream culvert debris screen to improve drainage. (p24)
Surface water flooding affected the area around Archway Road during the rainfall event of 4–5 June 2022, leading to the area being identified for a Surface Water Management Plan study and consideration of long–term flood alleviation measures. [TAB] (p33)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7238809,-1.9259572,"<div id=""html_06ad79e3521a7f19819d7fca3617452d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Lodge Road, Penn Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Described as being on the route of surface water flow paths that channel runoff toward the low point at the bottom of Archway Road; this routing contributed to the drainage being overwhelmed and the subsequent flooding experienced on 4 June 2022. (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","North Lodge Road, Penn Hill",England,Described as being on the route of surface water flow paths that channel runoff toward the low point at the bottom of Archway Road; this routing contributed to the drainage being overwhelmed and the subsequent flooding experienced on 4 June 2022. (p24),,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7225759,-1.9335096,"<div id=""html_1c0e18d5ea116a9e789f294994ece4eb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Penn Hill Avenue, Penn Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Penn Hill Avenue are identified as being on the flow paths directing runoff toward the low point at Archway Road; this contributed to drainage being overwhelmed and flooding during the 4 June 2022 event. (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Penn Hill Avenue, Penn Hill",England,Parts of Penn Hill Avenue are identified as being on the flow paths directing runoff toward the low point at Archway Road; this contributed to drainage being overwhelmed and flooding during the 4 June 2022 event. (p24),,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7102325,-1.9262284,"<div id=""html_e0fa5672c041a560608f072f13e3591a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Canford Cliffs Road, Poole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of these roads are on surface water flow paths that direct runoff toward the low point at the bottom of Archway Road; runoff from these streets contributed to the drainage being overwhelmed and to flooding recorded on 4 June 2022. (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Canford Cliffs Road, Poole",England,Parts of these roads are on surface water flow paths that direct runoff toward the low point at the bottom of Archway Road; runoff from these streets contributed to the drainage being overwhelmed and to flooding recorded on 4 June 2022. (p24),,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7189077,-1.9303618,"<div id=""html_0ccaccbaf493e8f54f40b45168db7f6e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kings Avenue, Penn Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of these roads are on surface water flow paths that direct runoff toward the low point at the bottom of Archway Road; runoff from these streets contributed to the drainage being overwhelmed and to flooding recorded on 4 June 2022. (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Kings Avenue, Penn Hill",England,Parts of these roads are on surface water flow paths that direct runoff toward the low point at the bottom of Archway Road; runoff from these streets contributed to the drainage being overwhelmed and to flooding recorded on 4 June 2022. (p24),,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7176609,-1.9813076,"<div id=""html_f37ac601a4e1403079075c39b4ddd0b5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kingland Crescent, Poole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Kingland Crescent experienced flooding during the event; the Poole Food Bank storage facility located on this street had its ground floor flooded and lost stock. [PAG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ground&ndash;floor flooding at the Poole Food Bank storage facility resulted in stock losses; the store closed for stock assessment and cleanup and later reopened on 14 June 2022. [PAG] (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Kingland Crescent, Poole",England,"Kingland Crescent experienced flooding during the event; the Poole Food Bank storage facility located on this street had its ground floor flooded and lost stock. [PAG] (p26)
Ground–floor flooding at the Poole Food Bank storage facility resulted in stock losses; the store closed for stock assessment and cleanup and later reopened on 14 June 2022. [PAG] (p27)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7116626,-1.9954954,"<div id=""html_f17dc777bc22c92afb64efc7b7b619a6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Blandford Road, Poole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as an area impacted by surface water flooding during the 4&ndash;5 June 2022 rainfall event and nominated as a candidate for a Surface Water Management Plan and potential flood alleviation measures. [TAB] (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole","Blandford Road, Poole",England,Identified as an area impacted by surface water flooding during the 4–5 June 2022 rainfall event and nominated as a candidate for a Surface Water Management Plan and potential flood alleviation measures. [TAB] (p33),,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7201514,-1.8799118,"<div id=""html_d0fc42edb05d4ee73516d17297280be5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense convective rainfall on the night of 4&ndash;5 June 2022 produced extensive surface water / urban flooding across the BCP conurbation, causing internal flooding of residential and commercial properties. Some reports indicated foul sewage was present in floodwater. Six of the previously flooded properties were recorded as flooding internally again during a heavy rainfall event on 5 September 2022. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded cluster of flooding incidents on 4&ndash;5 June 2022 concentrated over Poole, including internal property flooding, internal + sewage incidents, external + sewage incidents and highway (road) flooding; social media and reports captured gardens, highways and roads flooding across the area. (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>21 residential properties; 4 commercial properties; 6 properties (subsequently flooded again on 5 September 2022) (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole,England,"Intense convective rainfall on the night of 4–5 June 2022 produced extensive surface water / urban flooding across the BCP conurbation, causing internal flooding of residential and commercial properties. Some reports indicated foul sewage was present in floodwater. Six of the previously flooded properties were recorded as flooding internally again during a heavy rainfall event on 5 September 2022. (p5)
Recorded cluster of flooding incidents on 4–5 June 2022 concentrated over Poole, including internal property flooding, internal + sewage incidents, external + sewage incidents and highway (road) flooding; social media and reports captured gardens, highways and roads flooding across the area. (p20)",21 residential properties; 4 commercial properties; 6 properties (subsequently flooded again on 5 September 2022) (p5),GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.74737687263831,-2.4192394577688887,"<div id=""html_46049e80e4fa43bedeb0bf76936f8980"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Dorset</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Local and media reports described a thunderstorm on 4&ndash;5 June 2022 that &#8216;brought flash flooding&#8217; across Dorset; specific local reports (e.g. Upton) described torrential rain and flooding impacts associated with the event. (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense thunderstorm on the night of 4&ndash;5 June 2022 produced flash and surface&ndash;water flooding across the county: social media and news reports describe gardens and highways flooding (reports specifically naming Ringwood Road, Whitecliff, Lilliput and Canford Cliffs), flooded roads in Parkstone, and widespread intense rainfall, thunder and lightning. The storm is also associated with severe road&ndash;surface damage reported in Poole. [IMG,PAG] (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Dorset,England,"Local and media reports described a thunderstorm on 4–5 June 2022 that ‘brought flash flooding’ across Dorset; specific local reports (e.g. Upton) described torrential rain and flooding impacts associated with the event. (p20)
Intense thunderstorm on the night of 4–5 June 2022 produced flash and surface–water flooding across the county: social media and news reports describe gardens and highways flooding (reports specifically naming Ringwood Road, Whitecliff, Lilliput and Canford Cliffs), flooded roads in Parkstone, and widespread intense rainfall, thunder and lightning. The storm is also associated with severe road–surface damage reported in Poole. [IMG,PAG] (p21)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.71932710846497,-1.9795429619647233,"<div id=""html_4947fe4199435b74ec91bee2bd34a629"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>George Roundabout</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A subway near The George Roundabout reportedly flooded to a shallow depth during the event, indicating localized surface water inundation affecting pedestrian infrastructure. [PAG] (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",George Roundabout,England,"A subway near The George Roundabout reportedly flooded to a shallow depth during the event, indicating localized surface water inundation affecting pedestrian infrastructure. [PAG] (p27)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7201514,-1.8799118,"<div id=""html_4287b7454b75b82f1e226c8e33c7c4c9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bournemouth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Bournemouth experienced intense, short&ndash;duration rainfall (examples in the text include Southbourne and small numbers of reports in Northbourne), resulting in surface water flooding and internal flooding of residential and commercial properties in parts of the town. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localized, intense rainfall on the evening of 4 June 2022 produced surface&ndash;water/urban flooding in Bournemouth; the event is the subject of this flood investigation and was highlighted by Met Office radar showing the heaviest rainfall concentrated around Bournemouth and adjacent areas. [IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Bournemouth,England,"Parts of Bournemouth experienced intense, short–duration rainfall (examples in the text include Southbourne and small numbers of reports in Northbourne), resulting in surface water flooding and internal flooding of residential and commercial properties in parts of the town. (p5)
Localized, intense rainfall on the evening of 4 June 2022 produced surface–water/urban flooding in Bournemouth; the event is the subject of this flood investigation and was highlighted by Met Office radar showing the heaviest rainfall concentrated around Bournemouth and adjacent areas. [IMG] (p10)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.716917044392346,-1.9761308319391357,"<div id=""html_63ca49635965021d683b3d273272e50a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Poole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas of the conurbation within Poole (examples given include Hamworthy and Upper Parkstone) experienced the intense rainfall event and associated surface water flooding; the Livingstone Road Junior School rain gauge in Upper Parkstone recorded ~31 mm in one hour during the event. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential and commercial properties flooded internally during the event; internal flooding recorded in homes and businesses. [TAB] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Poole Town Centre around Kingland Road/Crescent flooded during the event; two buildings in the area flooded internally and a subway near The George Roundabout flooded to a shallow depth. [PAG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred at Poole Bus Station (photographed) and surrounding low&ndash;lying areas; two buildings in the area flooded internally; a subway near The George Roundabout flooded to a shallow depth. [PAG,IMG] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense, localised rainfall on 04&ndash;05 Jun 2022 caused surface water/urban flooding that mainly affected properties in Poole. Most drainage coped but a few local areas experienced drainage failures and property flooding; investigations and remedial highway drainage and watercourse clearance works have been undertaken. (p31)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential properties; 2 commercial properties [TAB] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 buildings; 1 subway [PAG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 buildings; 1 subway [PAG,IMG] (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Poole,England,"Areas of the conurbation within Poole (examples given include Hamworthy and Upper Parkstone) experienced the intense rainfall event and associated surface water flooding; the Livingstone Road Junior School rain gauge in Upper Parkstone recorded ~31 mm in one hour during the event. (p5)
Residential and commercial properties flooded internally during the event; internal flooding recorded in homes and businesses. [TAB] (p19)
Parts of Poole Town Centre around Kingland Road/Crescent flooded during the event; two buildings in the area flooded internally and a subway near The George Roundabout flooded to a shallow depth. [PAG] (p26)
Flooding occurred at Poole Bus Station (photographed) and surrounding low–lying areas; two buildings in the area flooded internally; a subway near The George Roundabout flooded to a shallow depth. [PAG,IMG] (p27)
Intense, localised rainfall on 04–05 Jun 2022 caused surface water/urban flooding that mainly affected properties in Poole. Most drainage coped but a few local areas experienced drainage failures and property flooding; investigations and remedial highway drainage and watercourse clearance works have been undertaken. (p31)","2 residential properties; 2 commercial properties [TAB] (p19)
2 buildings; 1 subway [PAG] (p26)
2 buildings; 1 subway [PAG,IMG] (p27)",GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7178289,-2.012165,"<div id=""html_996d49438c29b2e5e7ef8f2d883bcb43"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hamworthy</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced intense, short&ndash;duration surface water/urban flooding during the 4&ndash;5 June 2022 heavy rainfall event. The area was within the western sector where the heaviest rainfall and most flood reports were recorded; the event caused localized surface water inundation and contributed to internal flooding incidents in the western conurbation. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hamworthy experienced an intense convective rainfall event on the night of 4 June 2022 (heavy downpour starting around 23:15). Rainfall observations record approximately 22.6 mm between 23:00 and 00:00 on 4 June 2022, producing conditions associated with local surface&ndash;water/flash flooding and significant drainage stress in the Hamworthy area. [IMG] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water accumulated south of the railway and ponded at a low point on Blandford Road causing highway flooding. Water flowed into gullies and a nearby channel that discharges to Holes Bay; restricted channel capacity downstream (within the Holes Bay SSSI) limited discharge. Post&ndash;event works (desilting and reprofiling of outfall channels in late Oct 2022) were carried out to improve channel and outfall capacity. BCP Highways improved the local gully system and plan increased gully inspection frequency; Wessex Water plan to improve a pipe junction in a manhole near the Blandford Road low point to improve drainage. [IMG] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Channels became clogged leading to local surface water flooding; channel clearance works were organised to alleviate drainage blockages. (p31)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the area affected by surface water flooding on 4&ndash;5 June 2022 (including Blandford Road); highlighted for further study and potential mitigation measures (SWMP, flood alleviation options). [TAB] (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Hamworthy,England,"Experienced intense, short–duration surface water/urban flooding during the 4–5 June 2022 heavy rainfall event. The area was within the western sector where the heaviest rainfall and most flood reports were recorded; the event caused localized surface water inundation and contributed to internal flooding incidents in the western conurbation. (p5)
Hamworthy experienced an intense convective rainfall event on the night of 4 June 2022 (heavy downpour starting around 23:15). Rainfall observations record approximately 22.6 mm between 23:00 and 00:00 on 4 June 2022, producing conditions associated with local surface–water/flash flooding and significant drainage stress in the Hamworthy area. [IMG] (p18)
Surface water accumulated south of the railway and ponded at a low point on Blandford Road causing highway flooding. Water flowed into gullies and a nearby channel that discharges to Holes Bay; restricted channel capacity downstream (within the Holes Bay SSSI) limited discharge. Post–event works (desilting and reprofiling of outfall channels in late Oct 2022) were carried out to improve channel and outfall capacity. BCP Highways improved the local gully system and plan increased gully inspection frequency; Wessex Water plan to improve a pipe junction in a manhole near the Blandford Road low point to improve drainage. [IMG] (p22)
Channels became clogged leading to local surface water flooding; channel clearance works were organised to alleviate drainage blockages. (p31)
Part of the area affected by surface water flooding on 4–5 June 2022 (including Blandford Road); highlighted for further study and potential mitigation measures (SWMP, flood alleviation options). [TAB] (p33)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7676415,-1.8842778,"<div id=""html_e97dd1c5c3db80dc468fb28cef36a1f1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Northbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A small number of flood reports were recorded in Northbourne during the 4&ndash;5 June 2022 intense rainfall event, indicating localized surface water flooding impacts in the area. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Northbourne,England,"A small number of flood reports were recorded in Northbourne during the 4–5 June 2022 intense rainfall event, indicating localized surface water flooding impacts in the area. (p5)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7224115,-1.9272815,"<div id=""html_5eff018302596e8eb7c75cb4a2f556d1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Penn Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties flooded internally during the event. [TAB] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Penn Hill area directs surface water runoff down local roads toward a low point (bottom of Archway Road) where drainage was overwhelmed, causing flooding on multiple occasions including 4 June 2022. Accumulation of pine needles in gullies and urban creep increasing impermeable surfaces were identified as contributing factors. (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred in Penn Hill (notably the area around Archway Road) during 4&ndash;5 June 2022 and was identified for further investigation and a potential Surface Water Management Plan and flood alleviation options. [TAB] (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 residential properties [TAB] (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Penn Hill,England,"Residential properties flooded internally during the event. [TAB] (p19)
The Penn Hill area directs surface water runoff down local roads toward a low point (bottom of Archway Road) where drainage was overwhelmed, causing flooding on multiple occasions including 4 June 2022. Accumulation of pine needles in gullies and urban creep increasing impermeable surfaces were identified as contributing factors. (p24)
Surface water flooding occurred in Penn Hill (notably the area around Archway Road) during 4–5 June 2022 and was identified for further investigation and a potential Surface Water Management Plan and flood alleviation options. [TAB] (p33)",5 residential properties [TAB] (p19),GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.72298,-1.9513429,"<div id=""html_95742e83b20a996090029fe83ac28888"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Parkstone</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a commercial property (business premises flooded internally). [TAB] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooded roads reported during the 4&ndash;5 June 2022 storm (social media/comments on local articles noted flooded roads in Parkstone). (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial property [TAB] (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Parkstone,England,"Internal flooding of a commercial property (business premises flooded internally). [TAB] (p19)
Flooded roads reported during the 4–5 June 2022 storm (social media/comments on local articles noted flooded roads in Parkstone). (p20)",1 commercial property [TAB] (p19),GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.731529,-1.975416,"<div id=""html_3b26336ea29df39e51921227eeb78710"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oakdale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties (homes flooded internally). [TAB] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Oakdale was affected by surface water/highway/internal flooding on 4&ndash;5 June 2022; some reports related to the watercourse beside Oakdale Junior School and debris screens were opened, contributing to local drainage issues. (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ten reports of internal, external and highway flooding were recorded in the Oakdale/Sterte area on 04&ndash;05 Jun 2022. Flooding was linked to the watercourse adjacent to Oakdale Junior School and surface water drainage that discharges via the Sterte Surface Water Pumping Station into the Sterte Channel. BCP staff observed a number of debris screens along the watercourse had been opened following the event. Post&ndash;event modelling for a 1 in 30 year 1 hour event showed the highest modeled depths (0.5&ndash;1.545 m) concentrated near watercourses and low&ndash;lying areas adjacent to the school and allotments. [PAG,IMG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Local surface water/urban flooding with blocked channels and debris issues; prompted consideration of debris screens and organisation of channel clearance to restore drainage capacity. (p31)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential properties [TAB] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 reports of flooding (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 reports of flooding [PAG,IMG] (p29)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Oakdale,England,"Internal flooding of residential properties (homes flooded internally). [TAB] (p19)
Oakdale was affected by surface water/highway/internal flooding on 4–5 June 2022; some reports related to the watercourse beside Oakdale Junior School and debris screens were opened, contributing to local drainage issues. (p28)
