GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7071063,-1.9088698,"<div id=""html_b110580eccb08df5a4eabe4c45d19a8e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Branksome Chine</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Branksome Chine is the downstream receiver of the open watercourse that conveyed excess surface water runoff from the Penn Hill/Archway Road area during the event (including 4 June 2022). (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Branksome Chine,England,Branksome Chine is the downstream receiver of the open watercourse that conveyed excess surface water runoff from the Penn Hill/Archway Road area during the event (including 4 June 2022). (p24),,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7230966,-1.987281,"<div id=""html_beaf491ffc7c5a49e6867e8a18278f59"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sterte</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported in the Sterte area as part of the Oakdale/Sterte incidents on 4&ndash;5 June 2022; flows in the low&ndash;lying area required pumping to the Sterte Channel via the Sterte Surface Water Pumping Station and debris screens along the adjacent watercourse had been opened following the event. (p28)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 reports of flooding (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Sterte,England,Flooding was reported in the Sterte area as part of the Oakdale/Sterte incidents on 4–5 June 2022; flows in the low–lying area required pumping to the Sterte Channel via the Sterte Surface Water Pumping Station and debris screens along the adjacent watercourse had been opened following the event. (p28),10 reports of flooding (p28),GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
GB-BCP,2,2022-06-04,50.7179979,-1.9782703020313623,"<div id=""html_99d0e65ee9ba9d5faeb9dad82dd65217"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Poole Bus Station</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater covered the bus station platform and surrounding pavement, with water reflecting station structures; the station appeared non&ndash;operational due to inundation. [IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Poole Food Bank's storage facility on Kingland Crescent had its ground floor substantially flooded, causing stock losses and forcing the store to close while stock was assessed and a clean&ndash;up took place (reopened 14 Jun 2022). Poole Bus Station flooded (photographic evidence). Two nearby buildings flooded internally and a subway near The George Roundabout flooded to a shallow depth. [PAG,IMG] (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>","Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole",Poole Bus Station,England,"Floodwater covered the bus station platform and surrounding pavement, with water reflecting station structures; the station appeared non–operational due to inundation. [IMG] (p26)
Poole Food Bank's storage facility on Kingland Crescent had its ground floor substantially flooded, causing stock losses and forcing the store to close while stock was assessed and a clean–up took place (reopened 14 Jun 2022). Poole Bus Station flooded (photographic evidence). Two nearby buildings flooded internally and a subway near The George Roundabout flooded to a shallow depth. [PAG,IMG] (p27)",,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04.html,GB-BCP_2_2022-06-04,Bournemouth Christchurch and Poole flooding 04 Jun 2022 - 05 Jun 2022,Flood Investigation Report: 4th – 5th June 2022,"011/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/011/2022/Bournemouth, Christchurch and Poole/Section-19-Flood-Report-June-2022.pdf"
