GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.5111383,-0.2169495,"<div id=""html_5d39a29ca7e40c8616e1752ffb6313bc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>St Anns Road, Lancaster West Estate</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Council officers made site visits after flooding on 12 July 2021; residents of St Ann's Road reported being affected by the flood and officers observed continuing impacts on individuals and the community. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Street flooded during the 12 July 2021 event (surface water/urban flooding). Listed in RBKC gully cleaning programme as cleaned twice a year. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 12th July 2021 the street experienced overland flow and surface water flooding as roads acted as channels conveying water. Surcharging sewers in the local network contributed to manhole eruptions and increased flows, synchronising with neighbouring streets and raising water levels. (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater entered properties via property drains (backing up through toilets, sinks and drains) flooding basement/ground&ndash;floor accommodation on St Anns Road. [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater affected the street and adjacent properties; basement properties were inundated by overland flows collecting at basement level and by sewage/sewer water backing up through toilets, sinks and drains into basements. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A large amount of sewer flooding came up through drains and manholes onto the street and then flowed into properties; floodwater also entered from the rear of properties. There were reports of a burst pipe nearby (no record by Thames Water). [TAB] (p85)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties; average internal depth 60 cm; maximum internal depth 100 cm [TAB] (p85)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"St Anns Road, Lancaster West Estate",England,"Council officers made site visits after flooding on 12 July 2021; residents of St Ann's Road reported being affected by the flood and officers observed continuing impacts on individuals and the community. (p19)
Street flooded during the 12 July 2021 event (surface water/urban flooding). Listed in RBKC gully cleaning programme as cleaned twice a year. [TAB] (p37)
On 12th July 2021 the street experienced overland flow and surface water flooding as roads acted as channels conveying water. Surcharging sewers in the local network contributed to manhole eruptions and increased flows, synchronising with neighbouring streets and raising water levels. (p61)
Floodwater entered properties via property drains (backing up through toilets, sinks and drains) flooding basement/ground–floor accommodation on St Anns Road. [TAB] (p64)
Floodwater affected the street and adjacent properties; basement properties were inundated by overland flows collecting at basement level and by sewage/sewer water backing up through toilets, sinks and drains into basements. [TAB] (p65)
