GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.5172639,-0.2111019,"<div id=""html_f8829b8b5b864c2fe8a466fe7265140a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ladbroke Grove, Bayswater</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents and community on the street were affected by flooding; council site visits on 12 July 2021 collected first&ndash;hand accounts and noted ongoing impacts. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ladbroke Grove was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event; surface water inundation affected the street. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sewers became surcharged and intense surface runoff produced overland flow along Ladbroke Grove; the road network conveyed and synchronised flows, raising water levels and causing localized street flooding. (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater entered properties through drains, toilets and sinks, causing internal flooding of properties/basement flats. [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding reported on Ladbroke Grove during the 12th July 2021 event: surface water inundation of the street and sewer backup through property drains, affecting the carriageway and adjacent properties (including potential basement inundation and internal drainage/backflow). [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement properties were flooded by overland flows that collected at basement level and by sewer flooding with sewage backflow from toilets and drains, causing staining and damage to walls and flooring requiring replacement of finishes. [TAB] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overflowing highway drains and surcharged sewers caused water to collect in gardens and enter basement properties; floodwater entered properties along the street and residents reported rooftop/gutter drainage failures. [TAB] (p79)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overflowing highway drains and surcharged sewers caused water to collect in gardens and enter basement properties (inside and outside). Local roof/gutter drainage issues were reported. Kensal House and North Kensington Library at the north end were flooded. (p80)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 properties [TAB] (p79)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Ladbroke Grove, Bayswater",England,"Residents and community on the street were affected by flooding; council site visits on 12 July 2021 collected first–hand accounts and noted ongoing impacts. (p19)
