GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.5069945,-0.2068763,"<div id=""html_302fb4ad24c1ebc41a1ac5367d97d3b7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clarendon Road, Notting Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Council officers included Clarendon Road in site visits after the 12 July 2021 flood; residents reported being affected and continuing impacts on individuals and the community were observed. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clarendon Road was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event; experienced surface water inundation. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooded by overland flows and sewer surcharge resulting from extreme rainfall; the road acted as a conduit conveying water into adjacent streets, contributing to raised water levels locally. (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clarendon Road was reported flooded. Flooding impacted basement properties via overland flows collecting at basement level and via sewer surcharging that entered properties through toilets, sinks and drains. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement properties were flooded by overland flows that collected at basement level and by sewer flooding (sewage/backflow from toilets and drains). Sewage caused staining and damage to walls and flooring requiring replacement. [TAB] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water drainage and combined sewer capacity were exceeded during the storm, causing overflowing drains and overland surface water flow at the Clarendon Road junction. [TAB,PAG] (p75)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall caused surface water drainage / combined sewer capacity to be exceeded. Drains overflowed mainly at the front of properties (with some rear and roof&ndash;drainage&ndash;related flooding), allowing water to enter and flood internal areas; part of the North Kensington Storm Relief sewer runs beneath the street. [TAB] (p76)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 properties flooded internally; average internal depth 10 cm; maximum internal depth 40 cm [TAB] (p76)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Clarendon Road, Notting Hill",England,"Council officers included Clarendon Road in site visits after the 12 July 2021 flood; residents reported being affected and continuing impacts on individuals and the community were observed. (p19)
