GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.5132134,-0.2096211,"<div id=""html_efc3d726c11119523c20fa606c3d3da7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Elgin Crescent, Notting Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in Council site visits to the worst affected areas after flooding on 12 July 2021; residents reported flood impacts and officers observed ongoing effects on the community. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Street was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event; listed in the report as one of the streets affected. Gully cleaning frequency for this street is once a year. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Elgin Crescent experienced sewers surcharging and surface&ndash;water overland flow; the street conveyed floodwater from surrounding areas, contributing to localized urban flooding. (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater entered property drains and basements via toilets, sinks and drains due to sewer capacity being exceeded and backup, causing internal property flooding. [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported on this street during the 12th July 2021 event. Floodwater inundated the street and contributed to basement flooding through overland flows collecting at basement level and sewer backup entering properties via toilets, sinks and drains. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement properties were flooded by overland flows that collected at basement level and by sewer flooding (sewage/backflow from toilets and drains). Sewage caused staining and damage to walls and flooring requiring replacement. [TAB] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drains and sewers overflowed; communal garden and neighbouring road ponding led to garden&ndash;to&ndash;property flows and rapid surface water across roads entering properties; sewage came up from toilets into basement flats; many basements suffered extensive damage to flooring and walls and some households evacuated via basement windows. [TAB] (p77)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater entered Elgin Crescent from Portobello Road/Colville Terrace, inundating businesses at the junction. [TAB] (p81)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater arriving from Colville Terrace across Portobello Road inundated businesses and properties at the junction with Portobello Road. (p83)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One of the worst&ndash;affected streets in the borough during the 12 July 2021 event: multiple properties reported internal flooding and engaged with different organisations and local flood groups. (p96)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one of 76 streets reported flooded [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>21 properties; average internal depth 25 cm; maximum internal depth 90 cm [TAB] (p77)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>21 properties that reported flooding; 19 properties reported to at least Thames Water, their neighbourhood flood group, or the RBKC investigation; 3 properties reported to Thames Water; 1 property reported to both Thames Water and the RBKC questionnaire (p96)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Elgin Crescent, Notting Hill",England,"Included in Council site visits to the worst affected areas after flooding on 12 July 2021; residents reported flood impacts and officers observed ongoing effects on the community. (p19)
