GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.5161314,-0.2062039,"<div id=""html_fb81910dd3071ab2c701d003189466a0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kensington Park Road, Notting Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Affected by flooding on 12 July 2021; council site visits to the area gathered resident accounts and observed continuing impacts to individuals and the community. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed in the report as one of the streets that was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Kensington Park Road were recorded as flooded in the RBKC/Thames Water dataset for the event. [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding reported on the street on 12 July 2021; properties (including basements) were affected by overland flows collecting at basement level and by sewer backup entering through drains, toilets and sinks. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant surface&ndash;water ponding occurred at the junction of Kensington Park Road and Elgin Crescent; surface water flowed rapidly across roads and entered properties. [TAB] (p77)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drains and sewers were overloaded (and in one case inadequate roof drainage contributed), causing flooding into properties on the street. [TAB,PAG] (p79)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sewers surcharged and manholes came up; large volumes of water collected in basements with multiple properties flooded to depths of over 1 m. Addisland Court was particularly badly affected with flood depths reaching up to 3 m, basements entirely flooded, water reaching ground floor, car park (basement level) inundated. Pumps in the building were overwhelmed and caused electrical short&ndash;circuiting; many flats became uninhabitable and residents were displaced into temporary accommodation; temporary boiler and electricity supplied while repairs ongoing. (p80)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; average internal depth 10 cm; maximum internal depth 10 cm [TAB,PAG] (p79)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 FLIPs; flood depths up to 3 m (p80)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Kensington Park Road, Notting Hill",England,"Affected by flooding on 12 July 2021; council site visits to the area gathered resident accounts and observed continuing impacts to individuals and the community. (p19)
