GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.5179184,-0.2066293,"<div id=""html_024ac10853d894f959e041e7f9785043"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Portobello Road, North Kensington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Portobello Road was among the streets affected by the 12 July 2021 flooding; site visits recorded resident reports and ongoing community impacts. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Portobello Road experienced overland flow driven by extreme rainfall and sewer surcharge; the road acted as a channel conveying floodwater, contributing to elevated local flood depths. [PAG] (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Portobello Road was heavily flooded on 12 July 2021 with water covering the entire street surface and reaching up to street furniture and storefronts; flooding was caused by intense rainfall and sewer surcharge leading to overland flow, making the street impassable and impacting local businesses and access. [PAG] (p62)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported on 12th July 2021. Basement properties were affected by overland flows collecting at basement level and by sewer flooding that backed up through toilets, sinks and drains. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement properties were flooded by overland flows that collected at basement level and by sewer flooding with sewage backflow from toilets and drains, causing staining and damage to walls and flooring requiring replacement of finishes. [TAB] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall and surcharged drains caused large volumes of water to flow down the road flooding businesses and properties; basements were badly affected by sewer flooding (sewage coming up through toilets); vehicles created bow waves that inundated properties; floodwater largely drained away after about two hours as sewer levels lowered. [TAB] (p81)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall and surcharged drains produced a large volume of water flowing down the road, flooding several businesses and inundating basements. Sewer flooding occurred with sewage overflowing through manholes in the street and coming up through toilets in properties&#8217; basements. Gullies were blocked and vehicles created bow waves that further inundated properties; the water then drained away suddenly after about two hours. There was considerable variation in impact between properties depending on floor level, and insurance premiums for many properties increased. (p83)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one of 76 streets reported flooded [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties; average internal depth 140 cm; maximum internal depth 150 cm [TAB] (p81)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Portobello Road, North Kensington",England,"Portobello Road was among the streets affected by the 12 July 2021 flooding; site visits recorded resident reports and ongoing community impacts. (p19)
