GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.515638,-0.2014108,"<div id=""html_576aecc95ea48ff0e92431bf07977023"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Colville Terrace, Notting Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents on Colville Terrace were affected by flooding on 12 July 2021; council site visits captured first&ndash;hand accounts and observed continuing impacts. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported on 12 July 2021. Floodwater affected the street and properties on it, including basement flooding from overland flows collecting at basement level and sewer water backing up through toilets, sinks and drains into properties. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Located in an area of high hydraulic connectivity, the street was flooded during intense rainfall; floodwater flowed towards Portobello Road and at least one property experienced internal flooding. [TAB] (p76)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed from Colville Terrace across Portobello Road into Elgin Crescent and contributed to inundation of businesses at the junction. [TAB] (p81)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed from Colville Terrace across Portobello Road into Elgin Crescent, contributing to inundation of businesses at the junction. (p83)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>≥1 property flooded internally [TAB] (p76)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Colville Terrace, Notting Hill",England,"Residents on Colville Terrace were affected by flooding on 12 July 2021; council site visits captured first–hand accounts and observed continuing impacts. (p19)
