GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.4963829,-0.1988716,"<div id=""html_5d22ea23e48a81ab331d1e1e17fb03d4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pembroke Square, Kensington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Named in the report as part of the Kensington site visits where residents reported flooding on 12 July 2021 and ongoing impacts were observed. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Street was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event; listed in the report as one of the streets affected. Gully cleaning frequency for this street is once a year. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties caused by sewer capacity being exceeded and floodwater backing up through property drains, entering via toilets, sinks and drains. [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported on this street during the 12th July 2021 event. Floodwater inundated the street and contributed to basement flooding through overland flows collecting at basement level and sewer backup entering properties via toilets, sinks and drains. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement properties were flooded by both overland flows that collected at basement level and by sewer flooding that came up from toilets and drains into basements at a similar level to the local sewer; sewage caused staining to walls and flooring that required replacement. [TAB] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sewage overflowed in the street and also came up through toilets/manholes into basements; multiple properties experienced internal flooding with variable impacts between properties. [TAB] (p81)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall overwhelmed surface water drainage and combined sewer capacity, causing surface water and sewer flooding on the street. (p82)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one of 76 streets reported flooded [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties; average internal depth 10 cm; maximum internal depth 30 cm [TAB] (p81)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Pembroke Square, Kensington",England,"Named in the report as part of the Kensington site visits where residents reported flooding on 12 July 2021 and ongoing impacts were observed. (p19)
