GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.5066423,-0.2107377,"<div id=""html_b6a0227f45d7a13e3f22730a9f4c4c02"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Norland Square, Notting Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Norland Square was flooded during the 12 July 2021 surface water/urban flooding event; the street is listed among those flooded in the borough. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 12th July 2021 Norland Square experienced overland flow and surface water flooding as part of the contiguous area where roads channelled floodwater and sewers became surcharged, causing manhole discharges and raised water levels from synchronised flows. (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported on 12 July 2021. The square and adjacent properties experienced floodwater, including basement inundation from overland flows and sewer backflow entering properties via drains and toilets. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement properties experienced sewer surcharge and overland/ surface water flows that entered basements; sewage from toilets and drains came up into basements, causing staining to walls and flooring that required replacement. [TAB] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Norland Square experienced flooding damage during the event (photographed in Figure 9&ndash;8), with internal flooding and property damage from sewer/overland flows. [PAG] (p70)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple basement properties experienced sewer flooding (sewage coming up through toilets) and others had overland floodwater enter properties as drains and sewers overflowed. [TAB] (p81)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall caused surface water drainage and combined sewer capacity to be exceeded, producing surface water and sewer flooding on the street. (p82)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties on the street with substantial water depths recorded inside buildings, as reported by residents. [PAG,IMG] (p90)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties; average internal depth 15 cm; maximum internal depth 30 cm [TAB] (p81)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Approx. 104 cm average internal flood depth (reported by residents) [PAG,IMG] (p90)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Norland Square, Notting Hill",England,"Norland Square was flooded during the 12 July 2021 surface water/urban flooding event; the street is listed among those flooded in the borough. [TAB] (p37)
