GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.5042002,-0.2109738,"<div id=""html_8a65d67edfe39c8fab09b9c1b5bdcfc3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Addison Road, Notting Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed in the report as one of the streets that was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced overland flows and surface water flooding when intense rainfall and surcharged sewers caused roads to act as channels, increasing water levels and conveying floodwater through the street. (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Addison Road experienced internal flooding caused by sewer surcharge/backflow into property drains, allowing floodwater to enter dwellings (including basements) via toilets, sinks and drains. [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported flooded on 12 July 2021; floodwater covered the street and was associated with overland flows collecting at basement level and sewer backups that entered properties via toilets, sinks and drains. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sewers and drains surcharged causing sewage&ndash;laden floodwater to flow overland into properties and to come up from toilets in basement properties; extensive internal flooding requiring major repairs to basements and lifts. [TAB] (p74)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The report records a large number of FLIPs (resident flood reports) on Addison Road associated with the event, indicating properties in the road experienced flooding and that these FLIPs could influence local hydraulics. (p88)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties flooded internally; average internal depth 25 cm; maximum internal depth 50 cm [TAB] (p74)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Addison Road, Notting Hill",England,"Listed in the report as one of the streets that was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event. [TAB] (p37)
