GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.4980615,-0.2092639,"<div id=""html_d44760045736b74a881dd9ae823e8e62"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Russell Road, Kensington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Russell Road was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event; surface water inundation affected the street. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding reported on Russell Road during the 12th July 2021 event: surface water inundation of the street and sewer backup through property drains, affecting the carriageway and adjacent properties (including potential basement inundation and internal drainage/backflow). [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement properties were flooded by overland flows and sewer flooding; sewage from toilets and drains entered basements, staining walls and flooring and requiring replacement and major repairs. [TAB] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Several properties were flooded internally by sewage coming up from toilets and shower drains in basements and by floodwater from overflowing drains and manholes that collected in basements. Large amounts of water entered properties, with floodwater collecting in basements. [TAB] (p85)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>12 properties; average internal depth 30 cm; maximum internal depth 60 cm [TAB] (p85)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Russell Road, Kensington",England,"Russell Road was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event; surface water inundation affected the street. [TAB] (p37)
