GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.516304,-0.2174646,"<div id=""html_469b7448d8ed0fea7dd7718ec8589627"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bramley Road, North Kensington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Bramley Road was flooded during the 12th July 2021 event, experiencing surface water inundation on the street. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as the upstream start of a flow&ndash;path that contributed to surface water flooding through the local street network; experienced overland flows and sewer surcharge that fed downstream flooding along St Anns Road and into the Royal Crescent/Holland Villas Road area. (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater affected the street and adjacent properties; basement properties were inundated by overland flows collecting at basement level and by sewage/sewer water backing up through toilets, sinks and drains into basements. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement properties were flooded by overland flows and sewer flooding; sewage from toilets and drains entered basements, staining walls and flooring and requiring replacement and major repairs. [TAB] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Local sewer capacity was exceeded and basement flooding occurred; back&ndash;up pumps for a block of flats reportedly failed, worsening flooding and causing damage to property and possessions. The North Kensington Storm Relief sewer begins at the north end of the street. [TAB] (p75)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe internal flooding of properties on Bramley Road; residents reported deep inundation of internal spaces during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p90)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties; average internal depth 135 cm; maximum internal depth 135 cm [TAB] (p75)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>average internal flood depth 135 cm [PAG,IMG] (p90)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Bramley Road, North Kensington",England,"Bramley Road was flooded during the 12th July 2021 event, experiencing surface water inundation on the street. [TAB] (p37)
