GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.5168988,-0.2136676,"<div id=""html_46cd31123f667e55fa63be5c24a80dda"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>St Mark's Road, Bayswater</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Street was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event. [TAB] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surcharged sewers produced fountains at manholes that ejected stormwater onto the street, causing localized street flooding and contributing to overland flows that were conveyed along road channels. [PAG] (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple properties on St Marks Road were flooded; incidents are recorded in the RBKC/Thames Water dataset for the event. [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>St Marks Road was reported flooded. Basement properties were affected when overland flows collected at basement level and when sewer flooding backed up into basements through toilets, sinks and drains. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement properties experienced sewer surcharge and overland/ surface water flows that entered basements; sewage from toilets and drains came up into basements, causing staining to walls and flooring that required replacement. [TAB] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drains on St Mark's Road overflowed during the storm, generating surface water that flowed downhill and contributed to overland flooding toward lower&ndash;lying streets. [TAB] (p75)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from overflowing drains flowed downhill from St Marks Road (including a drain by Thomas Jones Primary School). Limited highway gullies routed water as overland flow down the hill, collecting at the bottom (Camelford Walk). Drain overflow contributed to substantial overland flow on the street. [TAB] (p76)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The intersection with Lancaster Road produced a ~1 m high fountain that prevented vehicles passing, indicating flooding affected this road and adjacent areas. [TAB] (p79)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surcharged drains and sewers created a 1 m high fountain at the junction with Lancaster Road that prevented vehicles passing; floodwater then entered gardens and properties, causing basement flooding and sewage flows along the street. (p80)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff flowed south down the incline causing flooding near the end of the road; Thomas Jones Primary School and the local Learning Disability Community Team were flooded. [TAB] (p86)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties [TAB] (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties flooded internally [TAB] (p86)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"St Mark's Road, Bayswater",England,"Street was flooded during the 12 July 2021 event. [TAB] (p37)
