GB-KEC,1,2021-07-12,51.4968449,-0.2055197,"<div id=""html_1cef0ce79056b80a6d3081dc5430b57b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Holland Road, Kensington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded as flooded during the intense rainfall event on 12th July 2021; surface water inundation affected the street. [TAB] (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported flooded on 12 July 2021; floodwater affected the street and was associated with overland flows and sewer surcharging that contributed to basement/property flooding. [TAB] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Basement properties were flooded by overland flows collecting at basement level and by sewer flooding that came up from toilets and drains into basements; sewage caused staining and damage to walls and flooring requiring replacement. [TAB] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall caused surface water drainage/combined sewer capacity to be exceeded; sewers surcharged and sewage came up from toilets and flowed into basement properties, flooding them internally. [TAB] (p79)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surcharged sewers caused sewage to flow onto the carriageway; a manhole produced a 1 m high fountain and sewage entered properties from the road. [PAG] (p82)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Holland Road is recorded as having many FLIPs in the area during the event, indicating property flood reports and contribution to local flood hydraulics. (p88)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 properties flooded; average internal depth 50 cm; maximum internal depth 100 cm [TAB] (p79)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kensington and Chelsea,"Holland Road, Kensington",England,"Recorded as flooded during the intense rainfall event on 12th July 2021; surface water inundation affected the street. [TAB] (p38)
