GB-HRT,4,2016-09-16,51.7197427,-0.5374508,"<div id=""html_55bb47c792a69c9ff6c7744d11997542"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Eastnor, Bovingdon</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Eastnor were reported flooded during the surface water flooding incident on 16 September 2016 and the street was included within the Section 19 investigation area following resident questionnaire responses. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water overland flow and surcharging drains affected properties; foul sewage was present within the overland flow. Reported flood depths up to 0.75 m at properties on this road. [TAB] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Eastnor area lies within the defined investigation area; gullies and infiltration devices in the area (including the vicinity of the identified infiltration tank) would have been unable to cope with the short&ndash;duration, high&ndash;volume storm on 16 September 2016, contributing to surface water flooding on roads and affecting adjacent properties. [IMG] (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>More than 5 properties flooded across the investigation area (including streets listed such as Eastnor) (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 responses; 4 properties confirmed flooding; 3 properties internally flooded; flood depths up to 0.75 m [TAB] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Hertfordshire,"Eastnor, Bovingdon",England,"Properties on Eastnor were reported flooded during the surface water flooding incident on 16 September 2016 and the street was included within the Section 19 investigation area following resident questionnaire responses. (p8)
