GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.6643396,-2.6080142,"<div id=""html_5a441ca654626c545522bb1c83dfbb42"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Black Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High discharge in Black Brook caused flooding of a property. [TAB] (p35)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [TAB] (p35)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Black Brook,England,High discharge in Black Brook caused flooding of a property. [TAB] (p35),1 property [TAB] (p35),GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.6062209,-2.9649408,"<div id=""html_7278534c6bae645929e45a09f6dd9c23"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Carr Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Carr Brook overtopped its banks and was identified as the primary source of the flooding that caused internal flooding to nearby properties. [TAB] (p44)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties [TAB] (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Carr Brook,England,Carr Brook overtopped its banks and was identified as the primary source of the flooding that caused internal flooding to nearby properties. [TAB] (p44),6 properties [TAB] (p44),GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.7408403,-2.5677883,"<div id=""html_7cbafc58f967e2fb0fd3b44875aeb313"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Darwen</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Preliminary reports identify the River Darwen as the primary source of flooding that led to internal flooding of nearby properties in Brindle. Specifically, 4 properties in the Brindle (Hoghton Area) suffered internal flooding during the event. [TAB] (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties [TAB] (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Darwen,England,"Preliminary reports identify the River Darwen as the primary source of flooding that led to internal flooding of nearby properties in Brindle. Specifically, 4 properties in the Brindle (Hoghton Area) suffered internal flooding during the event. [TAB] (p18)",4 properties [TAB] (p18),GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.57531,-2.7159472,"<div id=""html_5fa45dc1857d3e39975d9e056c3447f5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Douglas</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A breach occurred to the raised earth embankment on the River Douglas leading to severe flood warnings; actual flooding was ultimately limited to farmland between the breach and the nearby village. (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>638 properties (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Douglas,England,A breach occurred to the raised earth embankment on the River Douglas leading to severe flood warnings; actual flooding was ultimately limited to farmland between the breach and the nearby village. (p30),638 properties (p30),GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.645309,-2.6575423,"<div id=""html_a9ece42888916a686a7a76a1d3343bb0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Yarrow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water drainage could not discharge into the River Yarrow which initiated flooding in the village; as river levels rose upstream the riverbank was overtopped causing more serious flooding in Croston. The Croston Flood Risk Management Scheme (upstream storage basin) was under construction and not available to reduce flood effects. [TAB] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Yarrow overtopped its banks near Towngate; Yarrow River Bridge restriction also contributed to observed flooding at The Mill Race. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>344 properties [TAB] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Yarrow,England,"Surface water drainage could not discharge into the River Yarrow which initiated flooding in the village; as river levels rose upstream the riverbank was overtopped causing more serious flooding in Croston. The Croston Flood Risk Management Scheme (upstream storage basin) was under construction and not available to reduce flood effects. [TAB] (p30)
The River Yarrow overtopped its banks near Towngate; Yarrow River Bridge restriction also contributed to observed flooding at The Mill Race. (p33)",344 properties [TAB] (p30),GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.7048432,-2.6582336,"<div id=""html_e2567938551d167e75c3985caa5dd7b4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Lostock</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High river levels within the River Lostock prevented Holker Brook from discharging, contributing to flooding and internal property flooding in Ulnes Walton. [TAB] (p41)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (Fieldsway); 2 properties (Southport Road) [TAB] (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Lostock,England,"High river levels within the River Lostock prevented Holker Brook from discharging, contributing to flooding and internal property flooding in Ulnes Walton. [TAB] (p41)",1 property (Fieldsway); 2 properties (Southport Road) [TAB] (p41),GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
