GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.6510606,-2.7331084,"<div id=""html_3856d748b549b1feed99925943ee91c0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Towngate, Eccleston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Yarrow overtopped its banks near Towngate (overtopping noted at this location). (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Towngate, Eccleston",England,The River Yarrow overtopped its banks near Towngate (overtopping noted at this location). (p33),,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.6425225,-2.6057121,"<div id=""html_1591b826d99925064f0b34660a301eb8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Long Lane, Limbrick</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road closure occurred during the flood event; bridge on/adjacent to Long Lane was damaged; LCC Highways carried out gully cleaning on Long Lane following the flood. [TAB] (p38)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Long Lane, Limbrick",England,Road closure occurred during the flood event; bridge on/adjacent to Long Lane was damaged; LCC Highways carried out gully cleaning on Long Lane following the flood. [TAB] (p38),,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.6740288,-2.7459275,"<div id=""html_42f57ab115577b3eb5507e247efaa11d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ulnes Walton Lane, Ulnes Walton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A culvert running through Fieldsway (affecting flow to the west side of Ulnes Walton Lane) may have surcharged on Boxing Day causing the reported problems. LCC Highways carried out drainage investigations and installed new manholes, cleaned ditches and culverts to improve flow to the west side of the lane; monitoring will continue to see if issues are resolved. [TAB] (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Ulnes Walton Lane, Ulnes Walton",England,"A culvert running through Fieldsway (affecting flow to the west side of Ulnes Walton Lane) may have surcharged on Boxing Day causing the reported problems. LCC Highways carried out drainage investigations and installed new manholes, cleaned ditches and culverts to improve flow to the west side of the lane; monitoring will continue to see if issues are resolved. [TAB] (p41)",,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.6635878,-2.7501236,"<div id=""html_9615ef3eadc6cb0f08be949010072a5d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Southport Road, Ulnes Walton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred at the valley point of the road; highway drainage was affected leading to repeated gully cleaning and repair of a blockage on the highway drainage system. [TAB] (p42)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Southport Road, Ulnes Walton",England,Flooding occurred at the valley point of the road; highway drainage was affected leading to repeated gully cleaning and repair of a blockage on the highway drainage system. [TAB] (p42),,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.6915831,-2.6385308,"<div id=""html_cf4e15b9f757626e681bad9c544e99ff"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Carrbrook Close, Whittle-Le-Woods</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culvert beneath Carr Brook Close (Sic) was unable to convey the full flow; water built up upstream and the backed&ndash;up water eventually overtopped the right bank, contributing to the flooding of properties. [TAB,MUL] (p44)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties [TAB,MUL] (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Carrbrook Close, Whittle-Le-Woods",England,"The culvert beneath Carr Brook Close (Sic) was unable to convey the full flow; water built up upstream and the backed–up water eventually overtopped the right bank, contributing to the flooding of properties. [TAB,MUL] (p44)","6 properties [TAB,MUL] (p44)",GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.684838,-2.6357171,"<div id=""html_dbcda80a54d7e5446452ad7719722e64"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Town Lane, Whittle-Le-Woods</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Town Lane area impacted by the flood event; associated drainage infrastructure required works (culvert de&ndash;silted, gullies cleaned and larger catchment gullies installed, flap valves fitted on outfalls). [TAB] (p46)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Town Lane, Whittle-Le-Woods",England,"Town Lane area impacted by the flood event; associated drainage infrastructure required works (culvert de–silted, gullies cleaned and larger catchment gullies installed, flap valves fitted on outfalls). [TAB] (p46)",,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_d5bc0e9711b82e0a3326da45784fbbe5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding hit Lancashire in December 2015, affecting local communities and exposing weaknesses in communication and coordination of flood risk management; this led to the development of district&ndash;level reports to inform and support affected homeowners and businesses. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme storms and rainfall in November&ndash;December 2015 caused flooding throughout December 2015 affecting Lancashire: over 2,500 properties were flooded and there was damage to private gardens, garages and out&ndash;buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges, retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools and village/town halls. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple communities across the county experienced flooding as a result of two major storm events in December 2015; the LLFA recorded and verified data, established flood timelines, identified affected communities and initiated a countywide Section 19 investigation and follow&ndash;on (stage two) reporting to track recommended remedial actions. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Significant flooding hit Lancashire in December 2015, affecting local communities and exposing weaknesses in communication and coordination of flood risk management; this led to the development of district–level reports to inform and support affected homeowners and businesses. [PAG] (p3)
Extreme storms and rainfall in November–December 2015 caused flooding throughout December 2015 affecting Lancashire: over 2,500 properties were flooded and there was damage to private gardens, garages and out–buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges, retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools and village/town halls. (p9)
Multiple communities across the county experienced flooding as a result of two major storm events in December 2015; the LLFA recorded and verified data, established flood timelines, identified affected communities and initiated a countywide Section 19 investigation and follow–on (stage two) reporting to track recommended remedial actions. [PAG] (p10)","over 2,500 properties (p9)",GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.70249,-2.201046,"<div id=""html_7a7bfadeb07f9abdc1b3c15f01091c8c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rossendale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas within Rossendale were impacted by the extreme storms and flooding of November&ndash;December 2015; a recovery 'drop&ndash;in' event was held in Irwell Vale (Rossendale) on 10 Feb 2016 to support affected residents and businesses. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Rossendale,England,Areas within Rossendale were impacted by the extreme storms and flooding of November–December 2015; a recovery 'drop–in' event was held in Irwell Vale (Rossendale) on 10 Feb 2016 to support affected residents and businesses. (p9),,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_2_2015-12-01,Chorley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Chorley District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/chorley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.64704799368739,-2.6735276397097056,"<div id=""html_0ce7b1f9c5e919570bfce88991a1cfd6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chorley District</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding affected properties in Adlington (Anderton Area): 3 properties suffered internal flooding. [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Within the borough two separate properties are recorded as having suffered internal flooding during the event (one at Limbrick and one at Lower Copthurst); Chorley BC provided support to an individual householder regarding repairs and property&ndash;level protection. [TAB] (p38)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (Limbrick) on 26 December 2015; 1 property (Lower Copthurst) on 26 December 2015 [TAB] (p38)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Chorley District,England,"Internal flooding affected properties in Adlington (Anderton Area): 3 properties suffered internal flooding. [TAB] (p11)
Within the borough two separate properties are recorded as having suffered internal flooding during the event (one at Limbrick and one at Lower Copthurst); Chorley BC provided support to an individual householder regarding repairs and property–level protection. [TAB] (p38)","3 properties [TAB] (p11)
