GB-LAN,2,2015-12-01,53.6892898,-2.6390093,"<div id=""html_e8b99b989075ab3da10d06efa7f87c2f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whittle-Le-Woods</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties in Whittle&ndash;le&ndash;Woods: 6 properties in the Carr Brook area suffered internal flooding. In the Carr Brook area the culvert under Carr Brook Close was unable to convey full flow during high flow, the water level built up upstream and eventually overtopped the right bank causing flooding. Separately, 1 property in the Johnson's Hillock area suffered internal flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p44)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties in at least two named areas of the village (Johnson's Hillock area and Town Lane area). Following the event, relevant risk management authorities met to discuss primary flood mechanisms and community impacts; the Lead Local Flood Authority encouraged property&ndash;level resilience measures and a detailed drainage study was planned. [TAB] (p45)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties in the Town Lane area. (p46)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties; 1 property [TAB,PAG] (p44)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (Johnson's Hillock area); 10 properties (Town Lane area) [TAB] (p45)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 properties (p46)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Whittle-Le-Woods,England,"Internal flooding of residential properties in Whittle–le–Woods: 6 properties in the Carr Brook area suffered internal flooding. In the Carr Brook area the culvert under Carr Brook Close was unable to convey full flow during high flow, the water level built up upstream and eventually overtopped the right bank causing flooding. Separately, 1 property in the Johnson's Hillock area suffered internal flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p44)
