GB-BDF,3,2020-12-25,52.4617238,0.6975642,"<div id=""html_c15ea050b71468a3cb96af4115a092cc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>East Anglia</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>December 2020 had unusually high rainfall across East Anglia, producing saturated ground that contributed to rivers (including the Great Ouse) overtopping their banks and regional flood impacts; Main River asset inspections across East Anglia were carried out after the event and remedial needs were identified. [TAB] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,East Anglia,England,"December 2020 had unusually high rainfall across East Anglia, producing saturated ground that contributed to rivers (including the Great Ouse) overtopping their banks and regional flood impacts; Main River asset inspections across East Anglia were carried out after the event and remedial needs were identified. [TAB] (p2)",,GB-BDF_3_2020-12-25.html,GB-BDF_3_2020-12-25,Bedford flooding 25 Dec 2020,Section 19 Flood Investigation Report: Bedford Priory Lake Area,005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford-Priory-Lake/July/2021.pdf
GB-WNH,3,2019-10-01,52.0327883,-1.1460385,"<div id=""html_6863d2c7ad47dd9f75ea7a28fe9623bc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Manor Court, Brackley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding occurred within a residential property on Manor Court; flooding was reported on more than one occasion, prompting a Section 19 flood investigation. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a residential property caused by surface water runoff following saturated ground and heavy rainfall; floodwater followed surface water flow paths through the local catchment concentrating on Manor Court. [MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowed east down Manor Court, collecting and puddling in the carriageway; flow was fast and deepened at low points, overtopped the kerb and ran down a private driveway to the garage threshold, overwhelming road gullies and the outfall and causing internal flooding of the property's garage. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred at Manor Court after above&ndash;average antecedent rainfall and heavy rainfall on the day; local drainage systems lacked capacity to collect and dispose of surface water and there is no overland flow route to direct surface water away, resulting in surface water affecting properties and highway infrastructure. (p4)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [MUL] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>200mm (depth of floodwater in the garage) (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",West Northamptonshire,"Manor Court, Brackley",England,"Internal flooding occurred within a residential property on Manor Court; flooding was reported on more than one occasion, prompting a Section 19 flood investigation. (p1)
Internal flooding of a residential property caused by surface water runoff following saturated ground and heavy rainfall; floodwater followed surface water flow paths through the local catchment concentrating on Manor Court. [MUL] (p2)
Surface water flowed east down Manor Court, collecting and puddling in the carriageway; flow was fast and deepened at low points, overtopped the kerb and ran down a private driveway to the garage threshold, overwhelming road gullies and the outfall and causing internal flooding of the property's garage. (p3)
Flooding occurred at Manor Court after above–average antecedent rainfall and heavy rainfall on the day; local drainage systems lacked capacity to collect and dispose of surface water and there is no overland flow route to direct surface water away, resulting in surface water affecting properties and highway infrastructure. (p4)","1 property (p1)
1 property [MUL] (p2)
200mm (depth of floodwater in the garage) (p3)",GB-WNH_3_2019-10-01.html,GB-WNH_3_2019-10-01,West Northamptonshire flooding 01 Oct 2019,2019 Flood Investigations,090/West Northamptonshire/2019/west northamptonshire.pdf
GB-WNH,3,2019-10-01,52.0298672,-1.1489965,"<div id=""html_9aa86ffcc281fa5a9577ef2caec06987"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Manor Road, Brackley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the event surface water runoff from higher ground was intercepted by Manor Road and flowed north; this routing of surface water contributed to runoff reaching Manor Court and the resulting internal flooding at a property. (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",West Northamptonshire,"Manor Road, Brackley",England,During the event surface water runoff from higher ground was intercepted by Manor Road and flowed north; this routing of surface water contributed to runoff reaching Manor Court and the resulting internal flooding at a property. (p2),,GB-WNH_3_2019-10-01.html,GB-WNH_3_2019-10-01,West Northamptonshire flooding 01 Oct 2019,2019 Flood Investigations,090/West Northamptonshire/2019/west northamptonshire.pdf
GB-WNH,3,2019-10-01,52.2040796,-1.0584685,"<div id=""html_d911a07f8f74dfc968033d2515b42a2c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Francis Row, Upper Stowe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowed to the southwest bend of Francis Row from the north, east and west, causing internal flooding at a residential property (converted farm building). [PAG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water from the carriageway, roofs, driveways and nearby agricultural land flowed to the southwest bend, bypassed an offset road gully, ponded at the low point, overtopped the highway and flowed into the driveway of an affected property; drainage at the low point could not cope with the volume and intensity of rain. (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential property [PAG] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",West Northamptonshire,"Francis Row, Upper Stowe",England,"Surface water flowed to the southwest bend of Francis Row from the north, east and west, causing internal flooding at a residential property (converted farm building). [PAG] (p5)
