GB-LAN,15,2016-06-08,53.7898112,-2.2944211,"<div id=""html_3d0c5cb50e7308484e5acb77ee5e362a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Green Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as the outfall for a culvert that became dysfunctional; culvert overflow/discharge routed into Green Brook system and contributed to water running across ground and flooding nearby properties. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Green Brook,England,Identified as the outfall for a culvert that became dysfunctional; culvert overflow/discharge routed into Green Brook system and contributed to water running across ground and flooding nearby properties. (p15),,GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08.html,GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08,Lancashire flooding 08 Jun 2016,8 June 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation – Covering Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-8-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,15,2016-06-08,53.7907123,-2.2917112,"<div id=""html_cb7a0c6383954534ab4355f95b56f4ef"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lowerhouse Lane, Burnley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Officers from Lancashire Fire and Rescue Service and Burnley Borough Council attended in response to calls from residents reporting water 30&ndash;60 mm deep across the ground floor of their homes and standing water in garden areas; roads and footways were inundated in the area. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road/street flooding with internal property flooding on the lane; emergency services attended in response to resident calls. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area experienced flooding during the rainfall event; emergency services (Lancashire Fire and Rescue Service) attended and Burnley Borough Council provided assistance to residents. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Devastating flooding where multiple houses were flooded at the same time; a dysfunctional culvert under/near Lowerhouse Lane caused water to come out of the pipe and run across the ground, inundating properties. Culvert defects were later corrected, restoring capacity and functionality. (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>30&ndash;60 mm deep (water across ground floors) (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties; water 30&ndash;60 mm deep across the ground floor of many homes (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>64 properties; 50 homes internally flooded (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Lowerhouse Lane, Burnley",England,"Officers from Lancashire Fire and Rescue Service and Burnley Borough Council attended in response to calls from residents reporting water 30–60 mm deep across the ground floor of their homes and standing water in garden areas; roads and footways were inundated in the area. (p3)
