GB-LAN,15,2016-06-08,53.791016,-2.289754,"<div id=""html_801a11c729e9e1d2c8cd0fbf3e7f01c6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lowerhouse Fold, Burnley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential garden experienced standing surface water two hours after rainfall, with water pooling across a significant portion of the rear garden and extending toward a gazebo/shed, indicating poor drainage and localized inundation. [IMG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple houses were flooded during the same flooding event affecting the Lowerhouse Lane area; flooding was linked to water emerging from a dysfunctional culvert that ran under/near the locality. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Lowerhouse Fold, Burnley",England,"Residential garden experienced standing surface water two hours after rainfall, with water pooling across a significant portion of the rear garden and extending toward a gazebo/shed, indicating poor drainage and localized inundation. [IMG] (p14)
Multiple houses were flooded during the same flooding event affecting the Lowerhouse Lane area; flooding was linked to water emerging from a dysfunctional culvert that ran under/near the locality. (p15)",,GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08.html,GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08,Lancashire flooding 08 Jun 2016,8 June 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation – Covering Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-8-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,15,2016-06-08,53.79086103049588,-2.2895975663372106,"<div id=""html_511716dfa8debd549f4125c5fbdcd2d6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Thornhill Street, Burnley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple houses were flooded during the same flooding event affecting the Lowerhouse Lane area; flooding was associated with a dysfunctional culvert that caused water to run across the ground and flood properties. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Thornhill Street, Burnley",England,Multiple houses were flooded during the same flooding event affecting the Lowerhouse Lane area; flooding was associated with a dysfunctional culvert that caused water to run across the ground and flood properties. (p15),,GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08.html,GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08,Lancashire flooding 08 Jun 2016,8 June 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation – Covering Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-8-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,15,2016-06-08,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_6690c2b93f91aef7a5ec9d5e597145f0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy rainfall across the county produced surface water flooding: roads and footways were inundated in various locations and properties flooded during the event. Overall 64 properties were reported as flooded in the event, of which 50 were homes that had been internally flooded. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding events occurred on 8 June 2016; reports of those flooding events were made to the Lead Local Flood Authority by individuals, councillors and Food Action Groups, and reports were provided by Risk Management Authorities as part of the investigation. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread surface water flooding across the county during heavy downpours on 8 June 2016; roads and footways inundated in various locations and properties flooded in multiple towns. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Roads and footways were inundated in various locations across the county; Lancashire County Council Highways teams attended affected areas and many locations had begun recovering before 18:00 that evening. [PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The extreme rainfall event of 6 June 2016 (sic) overwhelmed natural and man&ndash;made drainage networks in Lancashire, producing particularly damaging flooding across Burnley and Lancaster districts. A culvert in the county was found dysfunctional in multiple locations, causing water to come out of the pipe and run across the ground and flood properties; correcting those defects restored capacity and functionality to the culvert. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme rainfall on 6 June 2016 (sic) overwhelmed natural and man&ndash;made drainage networks across locations in Lancashire, producing particularly damaging flooding in parts of the county (notably Burnley and Lancaster districts). [PAG] (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>64 properties; 50 homes internally flooded [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>64 properties reported as flooding; 50 homes internally flooded [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>64 properties flooded overall; 50 homes internally flooded [PAG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Heavy rainfall across the county produced surface water flooding: roads and footways were inundated in various locations and properties flooded during the event. Overall 64 properties were reported as flooded in the event, of which 50 were homes that had been internally flooded. [PAG] (p3)
Flooding events occurred on 8 June 2016; reports of those flooding events were made to the Lead Local Flood Authority by individuals, councillors and Food Action Groups, and reports were provided by Risk Management Authorities as part of the investigation. (p10)
Widespread surface water flooding across the county during heavy downpours on 8 June 2016; roads and footways inundated in various locations and properties flooded in multiple towns. [PAG] (p12)
Roads and footways were inundated in various locations across the county; Lancashire County Council Highways teams attended affected areas and many locations had begun recovering before 18:00 that evening. [PAG] (p13)
The extreme rainfall event of 6 June 2016 (sic) overwhelmed natural and man–made drainage networks in Lancashire, producing particularly damaging flooding across Burnley and Lancaster districts. A culvert in the county was found dysfunctional in multiple locations, causing water to come out of the pipe and run across the ground and flood properties; correcting those defects restored capacity and functionality to the culvert. [PAG] (p16)
Extreme rainfall on 6 June 2016 (sic) overwhelmed natural and man–made drainage networks across locations in Lancashire, producing particularly damaging flooding in parts of the county (notably Burnley and Lancaster districts). [PAG] (p17)","64 properties; 50 homes internally flooded [PAG] (p3)
64 properties reported as flooding; 50 homes internally flooded [PAG] (p12)
64 properties flooded overall; 50 homes internally flooded [PAG] (p13)",GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08.html,GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08,Lancashire flooding 08 Jun 2016,8 June 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation – Covering Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-8-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,15,2016-06-08,53.9026441,-2.422856,"<div id=""html_37217e2d54704ff5bd34db9c40f50665"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ribble Valley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Named as the district containing affected places (Chatburn and Rimmington) and listed among other affected places in Lancashire for the flood event. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>64 properties flooded in the event; 50 homes internally flooded (overall across affected locations including this district). (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Ribble Valley,England,Named as the district containing affected places (Chatburn and Rimmington) and listed among other affected places in Lancashire for the flood event. (p13),64 properties flooded in the event; 50 homes internally flooded (overall across affected locations including this district). (p13),GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08.html,GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08,Lancashire flooding 08 Jun 2016,8 June 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation – Covering Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-8-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,15,2016-06-08,53.78981570277851,-2.290457662389783,"<div id=""html_92167c58a00426f76e7e56aac3bdefd7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lowerhouse</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The most intense rainfall was experienced over the Lowerhouse area of Burnley; residents reported water 30&ndash;60 mm deep across ground floors of their homes and/or standing water in garden areas. Roads and footways in the area were inundated and properties were flooded. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Most intense rainfall in the event occurred over the Lowerhouse area of Burnley; residents experienced their first flooding event for 36 years. Substantial but short&ndash;lived impact to local roads and footways; telephone landlines were out of action for a period. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>In the Lowerhouse area of Burnley the adverse effects of the 6 June 2016 (sic) event were exacerbated by defects in a historic culverted watercourse, worsening flooding impacts locally. (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>30&ndash;60 mm deep (water inside/around homes) (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lowerhouse,England,"The most intense rainfall was experienced over the Lowerhouse area of Burnley; residents reported water 30–60 mm deep across ground floors of their homes and/or standing water in garden areas. Roads and footways in the area were inundated and properties were flooded. (p3)
