GB-LAN,15,2016-06-08,53.790726,-2.2439196,"<div id=""html_32a82bd80070fd2cdb478e76ee016851"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Burnley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple locations in Burnley experienced surface water flooding during the intense rainfall; roads and footways were inundated and properties (including homes in Lowerhouse) were flooded. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area of Burnley (Lowerhouse) experienced intense rainfall and inundation of roads and footways; emergency attendees (fire service and borough council) responded to flooding in the Lowerhouse Lane area. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Lancashire Fire and Rescue Service attended the Lowerhouse Lane area and requested assistance from Burnley Borough Council; the council provided prompt assistance during the flooding response. [PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The 6 June 2016 (sic) rainfall caused particularly damaging flooding across Burnley district; adverse effects in the Lowerhouse area were exacerbated by defects in a historic culverted watercourse. (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Burnley,England,"Multiple locations in Burnley experienced surface water flooding during the intense rainfall; roads and footways were inundated and properties (including homes in Lowerhouse) were flooded. (p3)
