GB-LAN,15,2016-06-08,54.04674035288858,-2.8001777457545383,"<div id=""html_3c1fae6e58a3bb665790f50a0cac3de6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancaster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The 6 June 2016 (sic) rainfall produced particularly damaging flooding across Lancaster district. (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancaster,England,The 6 June 2016 (sic) rainfall produced particularly damaging flooding across Lancaster district. (p17),,GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08.html,GB-LAN_15_2016-06-08,Lancashire flooding 08 Jun 2016,8 June 2016 Flood In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation – Covering Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-8-june-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-CAM,16,2020-12-23,52.3156904,-0.1450631,"<div id=""html_45d6524542e28f59f7bf43a407203aaf"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Harcourt Farm</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Riparian landowners/tenants for the Harcourt Farm access road were to be followed up by the LLFA regarding adjacent watercourses after flooding, indicating the access area experienced flood&ndash;related issues requiring riparian maintenance. [TAB] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Harcourt Farm,England,"Riparian landowners/tenants for the Harcourt Farm access road were to be followed up by the LLFA regarding adjacent watercourses after flooding, indicating the access area experienced flood–related issues requiring riparian maintenance. [TAB] (p17)",,GB-CAM_16_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_16_2020-12-23,Godmanchester flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Godmanchester,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Godmanchester-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,16,2020-12-23,52.3120637,-0.1787039,"<div id=""html_8b9f4fa25b8cb86d9be214def411df10"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stoneyhill Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The brook cannot discharge into the River Great Ouse when river levels are high (outfall submerged), causing backwater and increased flood risk to nearby properties; the brook is silted and losing conveyance capacity upstream of its outfall, reducing discharge ability. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Elevated levels and conveyance/restriction issues in Stoneyhill Brook contributed to flooding of adjacent streets (including West Street and Silver Street); culvert removal/opening and other works were undertaken following the flooding to improve flow. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse had flow obstructions and limited conveyance to the River Great Ouse, contributing to flood risk upstream; residents cleared sections of the brook to improve flow and reduce flooding risk, and authorities evaluated the channel and engaged riparian owners to ensure channel capacity and remove obstructions. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Obstructions/culvert in the brook were identified as impairing flow; actions taken include removal of the culvert to open the watercourse, resident clearance of brook sections, and engagement with landowners to ensure riparian maintenance to reduce flood risk. (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Stoneyhill Brook,England,"The brook cannot discharge into the River Great Ouse when river levels are high (outfall submerged), causing backwater and increased flood risk to nearby properties; the brook is silted and losing conveyance capacity upstream of its outfall, reducing discharge ability. (p13)
Elevated levels and conveyance/restriction issues in Stoneyhill Brook contributed to flooding of adjacent streets (including West Street and Silver Street); culvert removal/opening and other works were undertaken following the flooding to improve flow. [TAB] (p17)
The watercourse had flow obstructions and limited conveyance to the River Great Ouse, contributing to flood risk upstream; residents cleared sections of the brook to improve flow and reduce flooding risk, and authorities evaluated the channel and engaged riparian owners to ensure channel capacity and remove obstructions. (p18)
Obstructions/culvert in the brook were identified as impairing flow; actions taken include removal of the culvert to open the watercourse, resident clearance of brook sections, and engagement with landowners to ensure riparian maintenance to reduce flood risk. (p19)",,GB-CAM_16_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_16_2020-12-23,Godmanchester flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Godmanchester,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Godmanchester-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,16,2020-12-23,52.3210521,-0.1672709,"<div id=""html_400250661f99f6e25c648cc0e1177dd5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>A1307 at Godmanchester</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Culvert passing under the roundabout/A1307 overpass and the area immediately north of the A1307 intersection require survey and cleansing following the flood. (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,A1307 at Godmanchester,England,Culvert passing under the roundabout/A1307 overpass and the area immediately north of the A1307 intersection require survey and cleansing following the flood. (p20),,GB-CAM_16_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_16_2020-12-23,Godmanchester flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Godmanchester,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Godmanchester-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,16,2020-12-23,52.1278302,-0.4250206,"<div id=""html_90e235d23d6de89c185d6ca179cc02fc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Great Ouse</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High water volumes and levels in the Great River Ouse contributed to flooding pressure on drainage and surrounding land in Godmanchester, exacerbating surface water flooding of properties and overwhelming surface water drainage systems. (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>river flow upstream of Godmanchester recorded at 47.98 m3/s (204% of long&ndash;term average); river gauge levels exceeded those of 1998 and were the highest on record (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,River Great Ouse,England,"High water volumes and levels in the Great River Ouse contributed to flooding pressure on drainage and surrounding land in Godmanchester, exacerbating surface water flooding of properties and overwhelming surface water drainage systems. (p7)",river flow upstream of Godmanchester recorded at 47.98 m3/s (204% of long–term average); river gauge levels exceeded those of 1998 and were the highest on record (p7),GB-CAM_16_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_16_2020-12-23,Godmanchester flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Godmanchester,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Godmanchester-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,16,2020-12-23,52.3222861,-0.1519477,"<div id=""html_854a2edd52dface5617b9a92c59d3e6b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cow Lane, Godmanchester</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External highway flooding was reported on Cow Lane. [TAB] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding affected the highway on Cow Lane. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas adjacent to Cambridge Road and Cow Lane had flood&ndash;related issues with nearby watercourses; LLFA and District Council to follow up riparian owners and evaluate the condition of the awarded watercourse adjacent to Cow Lane to remove obstructions and reduce flood risk. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Watercourse adjacent to Cow Lane to be evaluated for obstructions; culvert under Cambridge Road (immediately north of the A1307 intersection) identified for cleansing following the flood. (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>At least 1 property (Cambridge Villas, Cambridge Road and Cow Lane) [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>0 properties internal [TAB] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Cow Lane, Godmanchester",England,"External highway flooding was reported on Cow Lane. [TAB] (p10)
