GB-KEN,6,2021-07-20,51.3911133,0.1670936,"<div id=""html_65bf413fcb3a9aaaa44bb9dbf15baccb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Heather End, St Mary's</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>One property experienced external flooding. [TAB] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The carriageway of Heather End was inundated by surface water runoff during the intense rainfall event; floodwater was channelled southward within High Firs Estate and Heather End is shown as an affected flooded road on the map (red dot), indicating localised road flooding and likely disruption to access. [IMG] (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property external flooding [TAB] (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Heather End, St Mary's",England,"One property experienced external flooding. [TAB] (p3)
The carriageway of Heather End was inundated by surface water runoff during the intense rainfall event; floodwater was channelled southward within High Firs Estate and Heather End is shown as an affected flooded road on the map (red dot), indicating localised road flooding and likely disruption to access. [IMG] (p16)",1 property external flooding [TAB] (p3),GB-KEN_6_2021-07-20_etc.html,GB-KEN_6_2021-07-20_etc,Swanley flooding 20 Jul 2021 and Swanley flooding 20 Oct 2021 - 21 Oct 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Swanley,063/Kent/Flooding-report-affecting-Swanley-on-20-July-and-20-to-21-October-2021.pdf
GB-KEN,6,2021-07-20,51.3985896,0.1695457,"<div id=""html_7ed4f864ab963c65ec8097f0916126a3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oliver Road, Swanley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple properties were flooded: on 20th July 2021 the report records three properties with internal flooding and one property also recorded (table text repeats internal flooding) and external flood depths were estimated at knee to waist height; on 20th&ndash;21st October 2021 one property was reported with external flooding. [TAB,MUL] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple properties experienced flooding; external flood depths at properties were estimated at knee&ndash;to&ndash;waist height. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding reported to one property. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from the higher ground around Oliver Road is described as having exacerbated surface water flows along Hart Dyke Road and into lower areas such as Almond Drive and Hibbs Close; an adjacent alleyway between Oliver Road and Almond Drive had estimated flood depths of approximately 75 cm. It is not explicitly stated whether Oliver Road itself was inundated. [IMG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood surveys were sent to addresses on Oliver Road following flooding on 20 July 2021, indicating the street was affected by surface water flooding. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties internal flooding; 1 property internal flooding; external depths described as knee to waist height; 1 property external flooding (20th&ndash;21st Oct 2021) [TAB,MUL] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties; 1 property (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (external) (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>75 cm (estimated flood depth in the alleyway between Oliver Road and Almond Drive) [IMG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 flood surveys sent; 1 flood survey received [TAB] (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Oliver Road, Swanley",England,"Multiple properties were flooded: on 20th July 2021 the report records three properties with internal flooding and one property also recorded (table text repeats internal flooding) and external flood depths were estimated at knee to waist height; on 20th–21st October 2021 one property was reported with external flooding. [TAB,MUL] (p3)
