GB-KEN,6,2021-07-20,51.3900606,0.1722948,"<div id=""html_3a75a790e7c66943d8a2334c5a03508a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Overmead, High Firs</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two properties experienced internal flooding. [TAB] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties experienced internal flooding. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flows from the south of the A20 and from the A20 itself flowed towards Overmead, contributing to the heavy flooding experienced in the area during the intense rainfall on 20th July 2021. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overmead was inundated by surface water runoff during the intense rainfall, with floodwater following the estate flow routes; Overmead is shown as an affected flooded road on the map (red dot), indicating localised road flooding and likely access disruption. [IMG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents returned flood surveys reporting flooding on the street during the 20 July 2021 event. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties internal flooding [TAB] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 flood survey received [TAB] (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Overmead, High Firs",England,"Two properties experienced internal flooding. [TAB] (p3)
