GB-KEN,6,2021-07-20,51.3900643,0.1729661,"<div id=""html_2d6afcc25046297c7575d179554c43cb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pinks Hill, High Firs</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 20th July 2021, 17 properties were reported flooded (10 internal, 4 external, 3 unknown) with external depths reported up to 90 cm and internal depths up to 15 cm. On 20th&ndash;21st October 2021, six properties were reported with internal flooding with depths estimated at about 10 cm. [TAB,MUL] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from Pinks Hill flowed in a south&ndash;westerly to north&ndash;easterly direction toward Waylands. Because Pinks Hill/Waylands is lower topography and highway gullies surcharged during the intense rainfall, there was significant flooding causing flooding to properties on 20th July 2021. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Pinks Hill was affected by surface water flooding driven by the estate's southward flow lines during the intense rainfall; it is marked as an affected flooded road on the map (red dot), indicating road inundation and disruption to movement. [IMG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Pinks Hill experienced flooding and required pumping to remove floodwater; local residents were provided with electric pumps to assist with pump&ndash;out. [MUL] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents returned flood surveys reporting flooding on the street during the 20 July 2021 event. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties (required pumping) and carriageway flooding; blocked drain externally flooded properties. (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties experienced internal flooding (water ingress) to depths reported around 50 cm; properties also externally flooded. Carriageway flooding reported on nearby roads. (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 properties (10 internal, 4 external, 3 unknown); external depths up to 90 cm; internal depths up to 15 cm; 6 properties internal flooding (Oct 2021 at ~10 cm) [TAB,MUL] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 flood surveys received [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties; 50 cm internal depth (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Pinks Hill, High Firs",England,"On 20th July 2021, 17 properties were reported flooded (10 internal, 4 external, 3 unknown) with external depths reported up to 90 cm and internal depths up to 15 cm. On 20th–21st October 2021, six properties were reported with internal flooding with depths estimated at about 10 cm. [TAB,MUL] (p3)
Surface water runoff from Pinks Hill flowed in a south–westerly to north–easterly direction toward Waylands. Because Pinks Hill/Waylands is lower topography and highway gullies surcharged during the intense rainfall, there was significant flooding causing flooding to properties on 20th July 2021. (p15)
Pinks Hill was affected by surface water flooding driven by the estate's southward flow lines during the intense rainfall; it is marked as an affected flooded road on the map (red dot), indicating road inundation and disruption to movement. [IMG] (p16)
