GB-KEN,14,2020-02-09,51.181698495537916,0.34515307020293007,"<div id=""html_b16224d224138e6bff402d067a0b3aea"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Five Oak Green Road, Five Oak Green</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Commercial properties experienced internal flooding. [TAB] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Alder Stream overtopped its banks upstream of the culvert beneath Five Oak Green Road during the 9th February 2020 event; highway drainage and the local sewer network were overwhelmed, causing flooding in the area around the road and affecting nearby properties. The culvert inlet trash screen was reported free of debris and peak flows gradually subsided. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Local surface water drainage was overwhelmed with ponding on roads and internal flooding of nearby properties; emergency services attended and a road closure was put in place in the locality. [IMG,PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High&ndash;intensity rainfall during Storm Ciara overwhelmed highway drains on Five Oak Green Road leading to gully blockages and drainage defects; KCC undertook gully cleansing and remedial work. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 commercial properties flooded internally [TAB] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 30 cm internal flood depth [IMG,PAG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Five Oak Green Road, Five Oak Green",England,"Commercial properties experienced internal flooding. [TAB] (p3)
Alder Stream overtopped its banks upstream of the culvert beneath Five Oak Green Road during the 9th February 2020 event; highway drainage and the local sewer network were overwhelmed, causing flooding in the area around the road and affecting nearby properties. The culvert inlet trash screen was reported free of debris and peak flows gradually subsided. (p12)
Local surface water drainage was overwhelmed with ponding on roads and internal flooding of nearby properties; emergency services attended and a road closure was put in place in the locality. [IMG,PAG] (p13)
High–intensity rainfall during Storm Ciara overwhelmed highway drains on Five Oak Green Road leading to gully blockages and drainage defects; KCC undertook gully cleansing and remedial work. [TAB] (p15)","5 commercial properties flooded internally [TAB] (p3)
