GB-LAN,3,2017-11-22,53.8461465,-2.9904844,"<div id=""html_379bfa24c8b76fb09e562612b908edc0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Poulton-Le-Fylde</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localised flooding linked to the weather event coincided with power outages in the area. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>part of 500 properties (across Blackpool, Thornton&ndash;Cleveleys and Poulton) (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Poulton-Le-Fylde,England,Localised flooding linked to the weather event coincided with power outages in the area. (p12),"part of 500 properties (across Blackpool, Thornton–Cleveleys and Poulton) (p12)",GB-LAN_3_2017-11-22.html,GB-LAN_3_2017-11-22,Lancashire flooding 22 Nov 2017 - 23 Nov 2017,22/23 November 2017 Floods In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation,069/Lancashire County/covering-report-nov-2017-section-19.pdf
GB-LAN,3,2017-11-22,53.75873650867573,-2.7040270676854843,"<div id=""html_8f635bebc17a3fefa6366e887fcad4bb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Preston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intermittent power cuts reported in the Preston area linked to the extreme weather and described as a consequence of localised flooding. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Preston,England,Intermittent power cuts reported in the Preston area linked to the extreme weather and described as a consequence of localised flooding. (p12),,GB-LAN_3_2017-11-22.html,GB-LAN_3_2017-11-22,Lancashire flooding 22 Nov 2017 - 23 Nov 2017,22/23 November 2017 Floods In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation,069/Lancashire County/covering-report-nov-2017-section-19.pdf
GB-LAN,3,2017-11-22,53.952724,-2.8475857,"<div id=""html_96c9a8fdbf749bbdfdeee7fd863aa545"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cockerham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified on the track of the heaviest rainfall and therefore part of the area of most intense flooding during the event on 22/23 November 2017. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Cockerham,England,Identified on the track of the heaviest rainfall and therefore part of the area of most intense flooding during the event on 22/23 November 2017. (p12),,GB-LAN_3_2017-11-22.html,GB-LAN_3_2017-11-22,Lancashire flooding 22 Nov 2017 - 23 Nov 2017,22/23 November 2017 Floods In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation,069/Lancashire County/covering-report-nov-2017-section-19.pdf
GB-LAN,3,2017-11-22,54.04674035288858,-2.8001777457545383,"<div id=""html_11e956b0160ae162924435e2c925e5b5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancaster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The extreme rainfall travelled over Lancaster city to the River Lune; overtopping of watercourses in the Ellel and Galgate area (within the district) and flooding from tributaries caused encroachment into homes and outbuildings and obstructed highways. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme rainfall near Lancaster University caused local watercourses to overtop in the Ellel and Galgate area; combined flooding from the River Conder and Burrow Beck led to high volumes of water encroaching into homes and outbuildings and obstructing highways. Similar surface&ndash;water flows affected Caton and Halton with silt washed off fields. [IMG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancaster,England,"The extreme rainfall travelled over Lancaster city to the River Lune; overtopping of watercourses in the Ellel and Galgate area (within the district) and flooding from tributaries caused encroachment into homes and outbuildings and obstructed highways. (p12)
Extreme rainfall near Lancaster University caused local watercourses to overtop in the Ellel and Galgate area; combined flooding from the River Conder and Burrow Beck led to high volumes of water encroaching into homes and outbuildings and obstructing highways. Similar surface–water flows affected Caton and Halton with silt washed off fields. [IMG] (p13)",,GB-LAN_3_2017-11-22.html,GB-LAN_3_2017-11-22,Lancashire flooding 22 Nov 2017 - 23 Nov 2017,22/23 November 2017 Floods In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation,069/Lancashire County/covering-report-nov-2017-section-19.pdf
GB-LAN,3,2017-11-22,54.0746926,-2.7189779,"<div id=""html_6f0872ea65b1c889020d0726bed32db1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Caton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Caton was affected by river flooding when the heaviest rainfall tracked to the River Lune at Caton, causing the river to contribute to local flooding. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Village was overwhelmed by surface water emerging from local watercourses; floodwaters ran across fields carrying large quantities of silt onto roads and into houses. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Community in Caton experienced flooding during the 22/23 November 2017 rainfall event; local people reported their experiences to RMAs and a recovery/drop&ndash;in meeting was held (at The Victoria Institute) where RMAs collected additional flood reports to inform investigations. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Caton,England,"Caton was affected by river flooding when the heaviest rainfall tracked to the River Lune at Caton, causing the river to contribute to local flooding. (p12)
