Location of the flooded church property; flooding at this address resulted in internal inundation of the building on site. (p8)","one building (p6)
1 building (p8)",GB-NNH_22_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_22_2020-12-23,Corby flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Church Property, Rockingham Road, Corby, 23 December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Church Property, Rockingham Road, Corby.pdf"
GB-NNH,22,2020-12-23,52.3106138,-0.8659129831915817,"<div id=""html_bab0e001eb78f807a48f73f3621026df"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Northamptonshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of one Church building on Rockingham Road, Corby. The building experienced internal flooding on 23rd December 2020 and has been internally flooded on more than one occasion within the last five years, triggering the formal investigation. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 23/12/2020 heavy rainfall caused catchment saturation and high surface&ndash;water runoff across the county, and the Environment Agency issued flood warnings and alerts covering rivers in Northamptonshire. Localised flooding occurred (including reported basement flooding in Corby). (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one building (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 24 Flood Warnings; 24 Flood Alerts; 1 basement flooded (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Northamptonshire,England,"Internal flooding of one Church building on Rockingham Road, Corby. The building experienced internal flooding on 23rd December 2020 and has been internally flooded on more than one occasion within the last five years, triggering the formal investigation. (p8)
On 23/12/2020 heavy rainfall caused catchment saturation and high surface–water runoff across the county, and the Environment Agency issued flood warnings and alerts covering rivers in Northamptonshire. Localised flooding occurred (including reported basement flooding in Corby). (p9)","one building (p8)
at least 24 Flood Warnings; 24 Flood Alerts; 1 basement flooded (p9)",GB-NNH_22_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_22_2020-12-23,Corby flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Church Property, Rockingham Road, Corby, 23 December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Church Property, Rockingham Road, Corby.pdf"
GB-NNH,22,2020-12-23,52.487736,-0.7032713,"<div id=""html_e025ac8833311ec29ea177c51d4c3e2c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Corby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The church property in Corby (on Rockingham Road) was the subject of a Section 19 flood investigation. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense heavy rainfall caused surface water drainage systems in Corby to be unable to convey rainwater effectively, producing excess surface water that flowed to low points and entered properties, including internal flooding of a church building. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Contained a property (church on Rockingham Road) that suffered internal flooding during the incident. (p8)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one building (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 building (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,Corby,England,"The church property in Corby (on Rockingham Road) was the subject of a Section 19 flood investigation. (p2)
Intense heavy rainfall caused surface water drainage systems in Corby to be unable to convey rainwater effectively, producing excess surface water that flowed to low points and entered properties, including internal flooding of a church building. (p6)
Contained a property (church on Rockingham Road) that suffered internal flooding during the incident. (p8)","one building (p6)
1 building (p8)",GB-NNH_22_2020-12-23.html,GB-NNH_22_2020-12-23,Corby flooding 23 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Church Property, Rockingham Road, Corby, 23 December 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood investigation report - Church Property, Rockingham Road, Corby.pdf"
GB-NYK,2,2022-02-01,53.8855754,-1.2582267,"<div id=""html_88a9ca63aa26d9a63b2c194c537868fa"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tadcaster Medical Centre</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe flooding in February 2022 with floodwater reaching the entrance ramp and encroaching on the building; vehicles were partially submerged and access to the facility was impeded, threatening property and likely disrupting services. [IMG] (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Tadcaster Medical Centre,England,"Severe flooding in February 2022 with floodwater reaching the entrance ramp and encroaching on the building; vehicles were partially submerged and access to the facility was impeded, threatening property and likely disrupting services. [IMG] (p5)",,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01.html,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding February 2022,Flood Investigation Report into the flooding in February 2022,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood and Water Management Act 2010 Section 19 Investigation.pdf
GB-NYK,2,2022-02-01,53.88634248415339,-1.2604922306472186,"<div id=""html_d2ccf17d68ab8b514923b00a82a6d73e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sainsbury's</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Wharfe overtopped/breached its banks on the left bank immediately adjacent to the Sainsbury's site, allowing floodwater to escape the channel at that location. [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Sainsbury's,England,"River Wharfe overtopped/breached its banks on the left bank immediately adjacent to the Sainsbury's site, allowing floodwater to escape the channel at that location. [IMG] (p12)",,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01.html,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding February 2022,Flood Investigation Report into the flooding in February 2022,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood and Water Management Act 2010 Section 19 Investigation.pdf
GB-NYK,2,2022-02-01,54.7023545,-3.2765753,"<div id=""html_d0d249c9d3be36df85ba831330389526"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>UK</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A series of storms moved across the UK between 16 and 21 February 2022, including Storm Franklin on 20 February, producing prolonged rainfall that saturated catchments and led to high river levels and flooding in affected parts of the UK (notably North Yorkshire). (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,UK,England,"A series of storms moved across the UK between 16 and 21 February 2022, including Storm Franklin on 20 February, producing prolonged rainfall that saturated catchments and led to high river levels and flooding in affected parts of the UK (notably North Yorkshire). (p8)",,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01.html,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding February 2022,Flood Investigation Report into the flooding in February 2022,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood and Water Management Act 2010 Section 19 Investigation.pdf
GB-NYK,2,2022-02-01,53.7213972,-1.1705201,"<div id=""html_41d40dcee28d596bbebe4cbbe7a82275"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Marsh Drain</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The ordinary watercourse (Marsh Drain) surcharged and backed up into the sewer system, causing the foul sewer to surcharge and resulting in internal flooding of properties and loss of toilet facilities. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties internally flooded; 18 properties left without toilet facilities (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Marsh Drain,England,"The ordinary watercourse (Marsh Drain) surcharged and backed up into the sewer system, causing the foul sewer to surcharge and resulting in internal flooding of properties and loss of toilet facilities. (p13)",3 properties internally flooded; 18 properties left without toilet facilities (p13),GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01.html,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding February 2022,Flood Investigation Report into the flooding in February 2022,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood and Water Management Act 2010 Section 19 Investigation.pdf
GB-NYK,2,2022-02-01,53.910881,-1.6910531,"<div id=""html_e71294d926f4924ecc8d8f1a435506cd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Wharfe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as the most significant mechanism causing flooding within Tadcaster (i.e. river overflow leading to town flooding). (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Very high river levels in the River Wharfe (reported as the second&ndash;highest in 30 years at Tadcaster) contributed to widespread flooding locally &mdash; most notably the major flood impact at Tadcaster &mdash; and to internally flooded properties elsewhere in the catchment. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The lower River Wharfe experienced very high river levels (recorded as the second highest in 30 years at Tadcaster) and was a cause of flooding to communities in the Selby District (notably Tadcaster). (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Wharfe overtopped and/or breached its banks at multiple specific locations through Tadcaster: near the Old Mill property adjacent to the weir (left bank); adjacent to Sainsbury's (left bank); a small site upstream where the defence takes a 90&deg; turn and the footpath crosses (right bank); and downstream of the bridge near the plinth for the temporary footbridge (right bank). [IMG,PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High flows during the February 2022 flood event prompted additional EA surveys and changes to flood warning/alert triggers at Tadcaster; the river's high water levels contributed to the breach/circumvention of the defence embankment at Ulleskelf and to flooding/surcharging of Ulleskelf Ings. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High water levels on the River Wharfe caused the breach/circumvention of the flood defence embankment behind West End properties in Ulleskelf, contributed to surcharging of the Ulleskelf Ings and triggered widespread flood warnings across the catchment. [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties within the Wharfe catchment were internally flooded; at Kirkby Wharfe (on the Wharfe) one property was internally flooded and both approach roads were cut off by flooding. Community HESCO bank initially held floodwater but was overtopped and the Aquadam then came into play; pumps could not match percolation beneath the Aquadam leading to the property flood. [TAB,PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>EA reprofiling of low spots within the River Wharfe to reduce the risk of the river breaching; the river is linked in the report to flooding in Tadcaster (including the 2015 event) and the February 2022 event. [TAB,MUL] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced significant flooding as part of the February 2022 catchment flood events; subject of a formal flood investigation by NYCC. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>63 properties internally flooded in Tadcaster; 6 properties internally flooded in Ulleskelf; an additional 15 internally flooded properties across the Nidd, Wharfe and Aire catchments. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Second highest in 30 years at Tadcaster; linked to 63 internally flooded properties in Tadcaster (flooding from the River Wharfe listed among causes) (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 locations [IMG,PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (Kirkby Wharfe); 15 properties (combined across Nidd and Wharfe catchments) [TAB,PAG] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,River Wharfe,England,"Identified as the most significant mechanism causing flooding within Tadcaster (i.e. river overflow leading to town flooding). (p2)
Very high river levels in the River Wharfe (reported as the second–highest in 30 years at Tadcaster) contributed to widespread flooding locally — most notably the major flood impact at Tadcaster — and to internally flooded properties elsewhere in the catchment. (p8)
The lower River Wharfe experienced very high river levels (recorded as the second highest in 30 years at Tadcaster) and was a cause of flooding to communities in the Selby District (notably Tadcaster). (p10)
River Wharfe overtopped and/or breached its banks at multiple specific locations through Tadcaster: near the Old Mill property adjacent to the weir (left bank); adjacent to Sainsbury's (left bank); a small site upstream where the defence takes a 90° turn and the footpath crosses (right bank); and downstream of the bridge near the plinth for the temporary footbridge (right bank). [IMG,PAG] (p12)
High flows during the February 2022 flood event prompted additional EA surveys and changes to flood warning/alert triggers at Tadcaster; the river's high water levels contributed to the breach/circumvention of the defence embankment at Ulleskelf and to flooding/surcharging of Ulleskelf Ings. (p13)
High water levels on the River Wharfe caused the breach/circumvention of the flood defence embankment behind West End properties in Ulleskelf, contributed to surcharging of the Ulleskelf Ings and triggered widespread flood warnings across the catchment. [PAG] (p14)
Properties within the Wharfe catchment were internally flooded; at Kirkby Wharfe (on the Wharfe) one property was internally flooded and both approach roads were cut off by flooding. Community HESCO bank initially held floodwater but was overtopped and the Aquadam then came into play; pumps could not match percolation beneath the Aquadam leading to the property flood. [TAB,PAG] (p15)
EA reprofiling of low spots within the River Wharfe to reduce the risk of the river breaching; the river is linked in the report to flooding in Tadcaster (including the 2015 event) and the February 2022 event. [TAB,MUL] (p16)
Experienced significant flooding as part of the February 2022 catchment flood events; subject of a formal flood investigation by NYCC. (p18)","63 properties internally flooded in Tadcaster; 6 properties internally flooded in Ulleskelf; an additional 15 internally flooded properties across the Nidd, Wharfe and Aire catchments. (p8)
Second highest in 30 years at Tadcaster; linked to 63 internally flooded properties in Tadcaster (flooding from the River Wharfe listed among causes) (p10)
4 locations [IMG,PAG] (p12)
1 property (Kirkby Wharfe); 15 properties (combined across Nidd and Wharfe catchments) [TAB,PAG] (p15)",GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01.html,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding February 2022,Flood Investigation Report into the flooding in February 2022,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood and Water Management Act 2010 Section 19 Investigation.pdf
GB-NYK,2,2022-02-01,54.0322022,-1.5638727,"<div id=""html_a47c1812a5478f288467e841d08cb47a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Nidd</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties within the Nidd catchment were internally flooded as part of the wider event affecting the Nidd, Wharfe and Aire catchments. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Subject to post&ndash;February 2022 visual inspections by the EA to re&ndash;assess asset condition and identify localised low spots following the flood event; results used to inform the recovery programme. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties within the Nidd catchment were internally flooded as part of the February 2022 event. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced significant flooding as part of the February 2022 catchment flood events; subject of a formal flood investigation by NYCC. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (collectively across the Nidd, Wharfe and Aire catchments) [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (combined across Nidd and Wharfe catchments) [TAB] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,River Nidd,England,"Properties within the Nidd catchment were internally flooded as part of the wider event affecting the Nidd, Wharfe and Aire catchments. [IMG] (p8)
Subject to post–February 2022 visual inspections by the EA to re–assess asset condition and identify localised low spots following the flood event; results used to inform the recovery programme. (p12)
Properties within the Nidd catchment were internally flooded as part of the February 2022 event. [TAB] (p15)
Experienced significant flooding as part of the February 2022 catchment flood events; subject of a formal flood investigation by NYCC. (p18)","15 properties (collectively across the Nidd, Wharfe and Aire catchments) [IMG] (p8)
15 properties (combined across Nidd and Wharfe catchments) [TAB] (p15)",GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01.html,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding February 2022,Flood Investigation Report into the flooding in February 2022,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood and Water Management Act 2010 Section 19 Investigation.pdf
GB-NYK,2,2022-02-01,53.8034294,-1.5829169,"<div id=""html_7824636195de5326484f5500bcb27dcc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Aire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties within the Aire catchment were internally flooded as part of the wider event affecting the Nidd, Wharfe and Aire catchments. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High river levels on the River Aire (recorded as the second highest in 27 years at Castleford near Brotherton) contributed to flooding that affected communities in the area, including Brotherton/Castleford. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced significant flooding as part of the February 2022 catchment flood events; subject of a formal flood investigation by NYCC. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (collectively across the Nidd, Wharfe and Aire catchments) [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Second highest in 27 years at Castleford; associated with flooded properties in nearby communities (report lists Brotherton among locations affected) (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,River Aire,England,"Properties within the Aire catchment were internally flooded as part of the wider event affecting the Nidd, Wharfe and Aire catchments. [IMG] (p8)
High river levels on the River Aire (recorded as the second highest in 27 years at Castleford near Brotherton) contributed to flooding that affected communities in the area, including Brotherton/Castleford. (p10)
Experienced significant flooding as part of the February 2022 catchment flood events; subject of a formal flood investigation by NYCC. (p18)","15 properties (collectively across the Nidd, Wharfe and Aire catchments) [IMG] (p8)
Second highest in 27 years at Castleford; associated with flooded properties in nearby communities (report lists Brotherton among locations affected) (p10)",GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01.html,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding February 2022,Flood Investigation Report into the flooding in February 2022,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood and Water Management Act 2010 Section 19 Investigation.pdf
