GB-NYK,2,2022-02-01,53.88450063328629,-1.2605782988212546,"<div id=""html_bf541324478c9975a03cdd7f40889a38"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bridge Street, Tadcaster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties around Bridge Street were internally flooded as part of the Tadcaster flooding; many flooded premises were businesses and contributed to the overall estimated £400,000 of damages in Tadcaster. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>63 properties internally flooded in Tadcaster (majority located around Bridge Street and Commercial Street) (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Bridge Street, Tadcaster",England,"Properties around Bridge Street were internally flooded as part of the Tadcaster flooding; many flooded premises were businesses and contributed to the overall estimated £400,000 of damages in Tadcaster. (p10)",63 properties internally flooded in Tadcaster (majority located around Bridge Street and Commercial Street) (p10),GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01.html,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding February 2022,Flood Investigation Report into the flooding in February 2022,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood and Water Management Act 2010 Section 19 Investigation.pdf
GB-NYK,2,2022-02-01,53.88584674673925,-1.258822906813994,"<div id=""html_d6727353660560f8a9746d7e2ea72dc0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Commercial Street, Tadcaster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Commercial Street were internally flooded as part of the Tadcaster event; many flooded premises were businesses and contributed to the estimated £400,000 of damages. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>63 properties internally flooded in Tadcaster (majority located around Bridge Street and Commercial Street) (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Commercial Street, Tadcaster",England,"Properties on Commercial Street were internally flooded as part of the Tadcaster event; many flooded premises were businesses and contributed to the estimated £400,000 of damages. (p10)",63 properties internally flooded in Tadcaster (majority located around Bridge Street and Commercial Street) (p10),GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01.html,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding February 2022,Flood Investigation Report into the flooding in February 2022,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood and Water Management Act 2010 Section 19 Investigation.pdf
GB-NYK,2,2022-02-01,53.85526066346393,-1.2149722086632646,"<div id=""html_439dd4cefa96e93b29ff06b4094ff861"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West End, Ulleskelf</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Six properties at West End were internally flooded. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The flood defence embankment to the rear of properties in the West End was breached/circumvented by high River Wharfe levels, allowing floodwater to enter to the rear of properties; flood extents mirrored approximately Flood Zone 2. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The flood defence embankment to the rear of properties in West End was breached/circumvented by high River Wharfe levels; Ulleskelf Ings (EA&ndash;managed water storage area) surcharged and pushed water up through drains onto Main Street (drains surcharged but defences were not breached there). Pumps were deployed to prevent internal property flooding. Residents reported flood warnings with short lead time. [IMG,PAG] (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties internally flooded (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"West End, Ulleskelf",England,"Six properties at West End were internally flooded. (p10)
The flood defence embankment to the rear of properties in the West End was breached/circumvented by high River Wharfe levels, allowing floodwater to enter to the rear of properties; flood extents mirrored approximately Flood Zone 2. (p13)
The flood defence embankment to the rear of properties in West End was breached/circumvented by high River Wharfe levels; Ulleskelf Ings (EA–managed water storage area) surcharged and pushed water up through drains onto Main Street (drains surcharged but defences were not breached there). Pumps were deployed to prevent internal property flooding. Residents reported flood warnings with short lead time. [IMG,PAG] (p14)",6 properties internally flooded (p10),GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01.html,GB-NYK_2_2022-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding February 2022,Flood Investigation Report into the flooding in February 2022,089/North Yorkshire County/Flood and Water Management Act 2010 Section 19 Investigation.pdf
