Internal flooding occurred at properties in Ulleskelf; specifically six properties were internally flooded at the location called West End. (p10)
Flood defence embankment to the rear of West End properties was breached/circumvented by high River Wharfe levels; Ulleskelf Ings (EA–managed water storage area) filled and flood extents mirrored Flood Zone 2; on Main Street water from the Ings surcharged up through drains (did not breach defences) and pumps were deployed to prevent internal property flooding. (p13)
High River Wharfe levels breached/circumvented the flood defence embankment to the rear of properties in West End, leading to property flooding; flood extents matched approximately Flood Zone 2. Water from the Ings surcharged through drains onto Main Street; pumps were deployed to stop internal flooding of properties. [IMG,PAG] (p14)
High river levels breached the river in Ulleskelf causing internal flooding of properties. (p15)
Properties in Ulleskelf are reported to have flooded internally. [TAB,PAG] (p16)
