GB-KEN,17,2019-06-10,51.3185158,0.436801,"<div id=""html_41eca3be3af6e56150e8790bb9682b16"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lakeside, Snodland</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater reached sufficient depth to affect 6 properties and caused damage to vehicles. [TAB] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water collected at the topographical low point, flooding the highway and entering property. Drainage had nowhere to disperse and was overwhelmed. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Tanker attended to clear flood water and all gullies were cleansed. CCTV of soakaways found all were holding water at inspection; groundwater ingress has reduced soakaway capacity and one soakaway had a foul misconnection from a private property, compromising their ability to accept surface water. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties; damage to vehicles (number not specified) [TAB] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Lakeside, Snodland",England,"Floodwater reached sufficient depth to affect 6 properties and caused damage to vehicles. [TAB] (p2)
