13 residential properties; 4 properties (external flooding to gardens/outbuildings); 1 property (residents temporarily moved out) (p60)",GB-BKM_24_2020-12-23.html,GB-BKM_24_2020-12-23,Gawcott flooding 23 Dec 2020,Gawcott Section 19 Flood Investigation: Final Technical Report,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2020/Buckinghamshire County/gawcott-report-dec-2020.pdf
GB-BKM,24,2020-12-23,51.998318,-0.9786725,"<div id=""html_45105d1161e1bcc3b1e518866fab389e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Buckingham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road closures were implemented across Buckingham as part of the wider response and main roads in the area became impassable in places, disrupting transport and access. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Buckingham,England,"Road closures were implemented across Buckingham as part of the wider response and main roads in the area became impassable in places, disrupting transport and access. (p33)",,GB-BKM_24_2020-12-23.html,GB-BKM_24_2020-12-23,Gawcott flooding 23 Dec 2020,Gawcott Section 19 Flood Investigation: Final Technical Report,018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2020/Buckinghamshire County/gawcott-report-dec-2020.pdf
GB-KHL,3,2019-10-27,53.7472446,-0.398271,"<div id=""html_ae0c2625e3813b6c2dbd424f50fba3b3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Anlaby Common</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense upstream rainfall overwhelmed the trunk sewer network draining through Anlaby Common; the local sewer system could not discharge quickly enough into the trunk sewers, and flooding was experienced in the Anlaby Common area. (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,Anlaby Common,England,"Intense upstream rainfall overwhelmed the trunk sewer network draining through Anlaby Common; the local sewer system could not discharge quickly enough into the trunk sewers, and flooding was experienced in the Anlaby Common area. (p13)",,GB-KHL_3_2019-10-27_etc.html,GB-KHL_3_2019-10-27_etc,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 27 Oct 2019 and Kingston Upon Hull flooding 10 Nov 2019,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: Section 19 – Prolonged Rain October/November 2019,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/ProlongedRainOctoberNovember2019.pdf"
GB-KHL,3,2019-10-27,53.806199178478806,-0.3295612815835089,"<div id=""html_3d35049927f666e49284168c21969205"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Carr Ward</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Contained Cumbrian Way, which experienced extensive flooding of roads and gardens and was identified as one of the two most affected areas during the 10 November 2019 event. (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,North Carr Ward,England,"Contained Cumbrian Way, which experienced extensive flooding of roads and gardens and was identified as one of the two most affected areas during the 10 November 2019 event. (p4)",,GB-KHL_3_2019-10-27_etc.html,GB-KHL_3_2019-10-27_etc,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 27 Oct 2019 and Kingston Upon Hull flooding 10 Nov 2019,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: Section 19 – Prolonged Rain October/November 2019,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/ProlongedRainOctoberNovember2019.pdf"
GB-KHL,3,2019-10-27,53.7435722,-0.3394758,"<div id=""html_1e78e333b77ed732cea2f22c1390d5dd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kingston Upon Hull</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The city experienced internal flooding of properties and widespread road/garden flooding during two separate events. On 27 October 2019 overtopping of the Old Fleet Drain led to internal flooding of properties; following heavy rain on 10 November 2019 there was repeat flooding at multiple locations and high levels in Old Fleet Drain persisted for several days. [MUL] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two properties within the city were reported to have experienced minor internal flooding during the event on 10 November 2019. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 10 November 2019 the Old Fleet Drain overtopped causing local flooding in the city. Reports were received of two further properties: one at Victoria Dock (reports of flooding unconfirmed) and one at Sutton Park where water flowed from a higher footpath across an impervious front garden causing slight internal flooding via an air brick. There were also reports of extensive road flooding at Cumbrian Way and North Carr Road and gardens submerged in Norland Avenue. Record high levels on the Holderness Drain caused some flooding to property outside the city boundary. [IMG,PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Catchment saturation from heavy rainfall (September) and increased rainfall in October and November led watercourses in the Hull area to overtop and drainage systems to be overwhelmed. [PAG,MUL] (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>five properties (27 October 2019); two properties (10 November 2019) [MUL] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two properties [IMG,PAG] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,Kingston Upon Hull,England,"The city experienced internal flooding of properties and widespread road/garden flooding during two separate events. On 27 October 2019 overtopping of the Old Fleet Drain led to internal flooding of properties; following heavy rain on 10 November 2019 there was repeat flooding at multiple locations and high levels in Old Fleet Drain persisted for several days. [MUL] (p4)
Two properties within the city were reported to have experienced minor internal flooding during the event on 10 November 2019. (p5)
On 10 November 2019 the Old Fleet Drain overtopped causing local flooding in the city. Reports were received of two further properties: one at Victoria Dock (reports of flooding unconfirmed) and one at Sutton Park where water flowed from a higher footpath across an impervious front garden causing slight internal flooding via an air brick. There were also reports of extensive road flooding at Cumbrian Way and North Carr Road and gardens submerged in Norland Avenue. Record high levels on the Holderness Drain caused some flooding to property outside the city boundary. [IMG,PAG] (p8)
Catchment saturation from heavy rainfall (September) and increased rainfall in October and November led watercourses in the Hull area to overtop and drainage systems to be overwhelmed. [PAG,MUL] (p30)","five properties (27 October 2019); two properties (10 November 2019) [MUL] (p4)
2 properties (p5)
two properties [IMG,PAG] (p8)",GB-KHL_3_2019-10-27_etc.html,GB-KHL_3_2019-10-27_etc,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 27 Oct 2019 and Kingston Upon Hull flooding 10 Nov 2019,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: Section 19 – Prolonged Rain October/November 2019,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/ProlongedRainOctoberNovember2019.pdf"
GB-KHL,3,2019-10-27,53.7124015,-0.3652257,"<div id=""html_708e2f22d56ddc9e0199de95eb23e99a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Humber</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Tidal behaviour in the Humber caused high tidal flows that led the outfall doors at Lord's Clough to close; the higher tide range meant low tides allowed greater outfall but while doors were locked the tidal influence caused fluvial flows to back up into Old Fleet Drain. [MUL] (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,River Humber,England,Tidal behaviour in the Humber caused high tidal flows that led the outfall doors at Lord's Clough to close; the higher tide range meant low tides allowed greater outfall but while doors were locked the tidal influence caused fluvial flows to back up into Old Fleet Drain. [MUL] (p21),,GB-KHL_3_2019-10-27_etc.html,GB-KHL_3_2019-10-27_etc,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 27 Oct 2019 and Kingston Upon Hull flooding 10 Nov 2019,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: Section 19 – Prolonged Rain October/November 2019,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/ProlongedRainOctoberNovember2019.pdf"
GB-KHL,3,2019-10-27,53.7617167,-0.2545376,"<div id=""html_352ea63f7fff214cd5dd9d743f33b783"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bexhill Avenue, Kingston Upon Hull</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a property at 34 Bexhill Avenue was reported on 27 October 2019; emergency services (Humberside Fire and Rescue) and Hull City Council used pumps and gully cleaners to assist. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents noticed rising flood water around their houses on the street; floodwater rose around properties. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping of the nearby Old Fleet Drain caused water to run through a garden, across an area of public open space and into houses on Bexhill Avenue. On 2 April 2018 a single property flooded internally. On 27 October 2019 a larger overtopping event caused internal flooding of five properties. On 10 November 2019 a resident reported flooding again but the subsequent investigation found water contained to the garden with no internal flooding. The fire service and Hull City Council attended the 27 October 2019 incident. [IMG,PAG,MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred at Bexhill (flows backed up due to tide&ndash;locked outfall); HCC and EA deployed pumps and personnel to manage water levels; the bank at Bexhill Avenue was identified as being lower at this location, increasing flood risk; a temporary sandbag wall was constructed (15 Nov) as a defence. [MUL] (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (34 Bexhill Avenue) (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (2 April 2018); 5 properties internally (27 October 2019); 1 property garden&ndash;only (10 November 2019); houses 16, 24 and 34 highlighted on map [IMG,PAG,MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Hull City Council deployed 5 operatives and a pump (shifts reported) at Bexhill Avenue; 2 HCC operatives and a pump attended for a total of 36 hours over 2 days with a manager in attendance for 16 hours over the 2 days. [MUL] (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,"Bexhill Avenue, Kingston Upon Hull",England,"Internal flooding of a property at 34 Bexhill Avenue was reported on 27 October 2019; emergency services (Humberside Fire and Rescue) and Hull City Council used pumps and gully cleaners to assist. (p4)
Residents noticed rising flood water around their houses on the street; floodwater rose around properties. [PAG] (p10)
Overtopping of the nearby Old Fleet Drain caused water to run through a garden, across an area of public open space and into houses on Bexhill Avenue. On 2 April 2018 a single property flooded internally. On 27 October 2019 a larger overtopping event caused internal flooding of five properties. On 10 November 2019 a resident reported flooding again but the subsequent investigation found water contained to the garden with no internal flooding. The fire service and Hull City Council attended the 27 October 2019 incident. [IMG,PAG,MUL] (p11)
Flooding occurred at Bexhill (flows backed up due to tide–locked outfall); HCC and EA deployed pumps and personnel to manage water levels; the bank at Bexhill Avenue was identified as being lower at this location, increasing flood risk; a temporary sandbag wall was constructed (15 Nov) as a defence. [MUL] (p21)","1 property (34 Bexhill Avenue) (p4)
1 property (2 April 2018); 5 properties internally (27 October 2019); 1 property garden–only (10 November 2019); houses 16, 24 and 34 highlighted on map [IMG,PAG,MUL] (p11)
Hull City Council deployed 5 operatives and a pump (shifts reported) at Bexhill Avenue; 2 HCC operatives and a pump attended for a total of 36 hours over 2 days with a manager in attendance for 16 hours over the 2 days. [MUL] (p21)",GB-KHL_3_2019-10-27_etc.html,GB-KHL_3_2019-10-27_etc,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 27 Oct 2019 and Kingston Upon Hull flooding 10 Nov 2019,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: Section 19 – Prolonged Rain October/November 2019,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/ProlongedRainOctoberNovember2019.pdf"
