GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6201344,-1.1176495,"<div id=""html_f51643d4d4b586af7ac7fce380a63c6a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Queens Road, Clarendon Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map shows a Flood Impact Area outlined at or near the intersection of Queens Road and Thurlow Road indicating surface water accumulation on Queens Road and increased flood risk to adjacent properties and streets. [IMG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"Queens Road, Clarendon Park",England,Map shows a Flood Impact Area outlined at or near the intersection of Queens Road and Thurlow Road indicating surface water accumulation on Queens Road and increased flood risk to adjacent properties and streets. [IMG] (p30),,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6466974,-1.0680222,"<div id=""html_67836bd9de7a425f6a50bbdbe6b1a7c8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Arncliffe Road, Leicester Unitary Authority</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Marked on the Abbots Road South map as a key location within the surface&ndash;water flood risk zones adjacent to Scraptoft Brook; medium/low risk zones extend into Arncliffe Road, indicating potential surface water inundation of the street and nearby properties during the event. [IMG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"Arncliffe Road, Leicester Unitary Authority",England,"Marked on the Abbots Road South map as a key location within the surface–water flood risk zones adjacent to Scraptoft Brook; medium/low risk zones extend into Arncliffe Road, indicating potential surface water inundation of the street and nearby properties during the event. [IMG] (p31)",,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6363439,-1.1150616,"<div id=""html_e934dc9c7488e5e365e5136b29f2bf53"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Melbourne Street, Leicester Unitary Authority</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included among streets shown with Flood Impact Areas on the Nedham Street map; within medium/high surface water flood risk and subject to overland flow and inundation during the event. [IMG] (p32)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"Melbourne Street, Leicester Unitary Authority",England,Included among streets shown with Flood Impact Areas on the Nedham Street map; within medium/high surface water flood risk and subject to overland flow and inundation during the event. [IMG] (p32),,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.637638,-1.1147177,"<div id=""html_fe0ee11e80d3328d77507d1ce0941919"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Maynard Road, Spinney Hills</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Marked with Flood Impact Areas on the Nedham Street map. Maynard Road lies in medium/high surface water flood risk zones and was exposed to overland flow and inundation during the event. [IMG] (p32)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"Maynard Road, Spinney Hills",England,Marked with Flood Impact Areas on the Nedham Street map. Maynard Road lies in medium/high surface water flood risk zones and was exposed to overland flow and inundation during the event. [IMG] (p32),,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6439687,-1.1094811,"<div id=""html_fa6eda7f5c442e7c726e0e649ebf0074"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ash Street, Spinney Hills</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Willow Brook experienced a sudden, short&ndash;lived surge in river level on the afternoon of 22/06/2023: a rapid rise to a peak then a gradual fall over the evening, indicating a transient river&ndash;flooding/flash response at Ash Street. [IMG] (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>peak ≈ 1.6 m river level [IMG] (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"Ash Street, Spinney Hills",England,"Willow Brook experienced a sudden, short–lived surge in river level on the afternoon of 22/06/2023: a rapid rise to a peak then a gradual fall over the evening, indicating a transient river–flooding/flash response at Ash Street. [IMG] (p33)",peak ≈ 1.6 m river level [IMG] (p33),GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6555589,-1.0595296,"<div id=""html_5bffcdd5658a3326977a02632d17328e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Burdock Close, Leicester Unitary Authority</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Start of an overland surface water flow route from open land at the rear of properties, causing surface water to affect Burdock Close. [TAB] (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"Burdock Close, Leicester Unitary Authority",England,"Start of an overland surface water flow route from open land at the rear of properties, causing surface water to affect Burdock Close. [TAB] (p34)",,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6447467,-1.087856,"<div id=""html_55b4de3496df51d29cfffa2680565e6a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hallaton Road, Humberstone</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in the Lotus Road/Lily Road/Halation (Hallaton) Road grouping where the west end of the development is a low spot; pluvial/overland flows and a pumping&ndash;station discharge into Portway Brook contribute to localised surface&ndash;water flooding risk. (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"Hallaton Road, Humberstone",England,Included in the Lotus Road/Lily Road/Halation (Hallaton) Road grouping where the west end of the development is a low spot; pluvial/overland flows and a pumping–station discharge into Portway Brook contribute to localised surface–water flooding risk. (p34),,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6383219,-1.105206,"<div id=""html_30c91a19946ab5db98cbc52d6638a6b8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Asfordby Street, Spinney Hills</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water collected in a low spot behind the flats, causing surface water flooding that affected properties on 22nd June 2023. [TAB] (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"Asfordby Street, Spinney Hills",England,"Surface water collected in a low spot behind the flats, causing surface water flooding that affected properties on 22nd June 2023. [TAB] (p34)",,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6439651,-1.0921023,"<div id=""html_34271d206ccb3b30fb0d700a2343a8ec"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Portwey, North Evington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flows from the east (allotments site and Lotus Road development) along The Portway (sic); pumping/storm flows into the Portway Brook and low&ndash;lying sections led to flooding of The Portway and adjoining properties. [TAB] (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"The Portwey, North Evington",England,Surface water flows from the east (allotments site and Lotus Road development) along The Portway (sic); pumping/storm flows into the Portway Brook and low–lying sections led to flooding of The Portway and adjoining properties. [TAB] (p34),,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6035925,-1.1193522,"<div id=""html_e97eee237337e659ad64e3b73257604c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Welford Road, Leicester Unitary Authority</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Pluvial low&ndash;spot above Saffron Brook led to surface&ndash;water flooding that affected properties on Welford Road. [TAB] (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"Welford Road, Leicester Unitary Authority",England,Pluvial low–spot above Saffron Brook led to surface–water flooding that affected properties on Welford Road. [TAB] (p34),,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6242705,-1.0956914,"<div id=""html_979ceec88c07fa744a7ac05ccf7bf1d0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Norwood Road, Leicester Unitary Authority</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a source/flow route for surface water; surface water low spot and flows originating or routing from Norwood Road contributed to flooding along the downstream flow path. (p35)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,"Norwood Road, Leicester Unitary Authority",England,Identified as a source/flow route for surface water; surface water low spot and flows originating or routing from Norwood Road contributed to flooding along the downstream flow path. (p35),,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.587067,-1.0997802,"<div id=""html_085d41f4726256e06a31139473cfb1b6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oadby and Wigston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>An intense thunderstorm on 22 June 2023 produced very high short&ndash;duration rainfall over Oadby and Wigston. The rainfall rates were reported as exceeding the design capacity of conventional drainage systems, so sewers in the area were likely to have surcharged and generated rapid overland flow toward low&ndash;lying areas. (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,Oadby and Wigston,England,"An intense thunderstorm on 22 June 2023 produced very high short–duration rainfall over Oadby and Wigston. The rainfall rates were reported as exceeding the design capacity of conventional drainage systems, so sewers in the area were likely to have surcharged and generated rapid overland flow toward low–lying areas. (p7)",,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.68491375,-1.1847653085946246,"<div id=""html_007145e9694c55ca33e3ef534e134cc0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Leicestershire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The 22 June 2023 storm produced localized very high rainfall totals across parts of Leicestershire (central and southern band shown on the rainfall map). These totals exceeded typical drainage design capacities in affected areas, leading to likely sewer surcharge and rapid overland flows in low&ndash;lying locations outside the city boundary. [IMG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,Leicestershire,England,"The 22 June 2023 storm produced localized very high rainfall totals across parts of Leicestershire (central and southern band shown on the rainfall map). These totals exceeded typical drainage design capacities in affected areas, leading to likely sewer surcharge and rapid overland flows in low–lying locations outside the city boundary. [IMG] (p7)",,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6152364,-1.1172746,"<div id=""html_82c8b640ee0dc7df981a4890dd56d7d4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clarendon Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area was affected by the flooding; parking suspensions were put in place in September and October 2023 to enable highway drainage crews to access and clean gullies and repair drainage infrastructure following the flood. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water flooding affected the northern and western edges of Clarendon Park on the map. Flood Impact Areas are marked on St. Leonards Road, Cradock Road and near the Queens Road / Thurlow Road intersection; high flood risk is shown adjacent to the Education Facility and along Victoria Park Road. Surface water flow is shown moving from the north and west toward the centre/south&ndash;east, causing accumulation in residential streets and flood impact zones. [IMG] (p30)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,Clarendon Park,England,"Area was affected by the flooding; parking suspensions were put in place in September and October 2023 to enable highway drainage crews to access and clean gullies and repair drainage infrastructure following the flood. (p10)
Surface–water flooding affected the northern and western edges of Clarendon Park on the map. Flood Impact Areas are marked on St. Leonards Road, Cradock Road and near the Queens Road / Thurlow Road intersection; high flood risk is shown adjacent to the Education Facility and along Victoria Park Road. Surface water flow is shown moving from the north and west toward the centre/south–east, causing accumulation in residential streets and flood impact zones. [IMG] (p30)",,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
GB-LCE,1,2023-06-22,52.6385926,-1.1087713,"<div id=""html_ab37a9e50b779ee1dc78113314778393"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Spinney Hills</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area was affected by the flooding; parking suspensions were put in place in September and October 2023 to allow highway drainage maintenance crews to clean gullies and repair drainage infrastructure following the flood. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal property flooding reported within the ward (Gwendolen Road, Evington Drive); flow routes cited along Evington Brook and from Norwood Road, with fluvial influence at Gwendolen Road. [TAB] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Evington Brook at Spinney Hills Park recorded a rapid rise in river level on 22/06/2023, peaking at about 1.2 m around 17:15 and then declining through the evening. [IMG] (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Spinney Hills ward experienced surface water flooding on multiple streets (including Gwendolen Road, Evington Drive and Linton Street), with low spots and flow routes producing inundation of streets and properties. [TAB,PAG] (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ward contains streets described as having surface water low spots and being on surface&ndash;water flow routes (e.g. Gwendolen Road). Local topography and blocked flow routes caused surface water ponding and flow into residential areas. (p35)</p></div></div></body></div>",Leicester,Spinney Hills,England,"Area was affected by the flooding; parking suspensions were put in place in September and October 2023 to allow highway drainage maintenance crews to clean gullies and repair drainage infrastructure following the flood. (p10)
Internal property flooding reported within the ward (Gwendolen Road, Evington Drive); flow routes cited along Evington Brook and from Norwood Road, with fluvial influence at Gwendolen Road. [TAB] (p16)
Evington Brook at Spinney Hills Park recorded a rapid rise in river level on 22/06/2023, peaking at about 1.2 m around 17:15 and then declining through the evening. [IMG] (p33)
The Spinney Hills ward experienced surface water flooding on multiple streets (including Gwendolen Road, Evington Drive and Linton Street), with low spots and flow routes producing inundation of streets and properties. [TAB,PAG] (p34)
Ward contains streets described as having surface water low spots and being on surface–water flow routes (e.g. Gwendolen Road). Local topography and blocked flow routes caused surface water ponding and flow into residential areas. (p35)",,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22.html,GB-LCE_1_2023-06-22,Leicester Unitary Authority flooding 22 Jun 2023,Flood Investigation Report of the Flood Event Thursday 22nd June 2023 (South and East Leicester City),071/Leicester/flood-investigation-report-22-06-2023-section-19/v2-0.pdf
