GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.478645,-2.0770211,"<div id=""html_fddbfd6cddd547591da4c9ef70e30adf"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tameside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal (ground&ndash;floor) flooding of properties from surface water. (Tameside borough reported surface water impacts in the dataset.) [TAB] (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property flooded (surface water) [TAB] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Tameside,England,Internal (ground–floor) flooding of properties from surface water. (Tameside borough reported surface water impacts in the dataset.) [TAB] (p17),1 property flooded (surface water) [TAB] (p17),GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.54572,-2.6264625,"<div id=""html_68d4910ce870587ea8e497c6fed2004d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wigan</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding across the borough from multiple sources (main river, ordinary watercourses, sewers and surface water) caused internal flooding to properties. [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Wigan was affected by the Boxing Day flooding; RMAs held a local drop&ndash;in event and conducted visual inspections of flood&ndash;risk assets following the event. (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred around Wigan on 26 December 2015; homes were evacuated by emergency services as part of the response and the local area contributed to the wider travel disruption and infrastructure impacts noted after the event. (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A total of 93 properties in Wigan borough experienced internal flooding from multiple sources. Worst&ndash;affected areas included Platt Bridge (18 properties flooded from Hey Brook), Bickershaw and Abram (15 properties flooded from Hey Brook/main river and ordinary watercourse), Worsley Mesnes (9 properties flooded from sewer), Aspull (4 properties flooded from surface water and/or sewers), Standish (6 properties flooded from River Douglas, Frodshams Brook, surface water and sewer) and Hindley (5 properties flooded from combined sources including surface water, sewers and main river). [IMG,PAG] (p146)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A total of 93 properties in the Wigan borough experienced internal flooding on 26 December 2015. Worst&ndash;affected locations and primary sources recorded were: Platt Bridge (18 properties flooded from Hey Brook), Bickershaw and Abram (15 properties flooded from Hey Brook and an ordinary watercourse), Worsley Mesnes (9 properties flooded from sewers), Aspull (4 properties flooded from surface water and/or sewers), Standish (6 properties flooded from River Douglas, Frodshams Brook, surface water and sewer), and Hindley (5 properties flooded from combined sources including surface water and sewers). [IMG,PAG] (p147)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>In this location a total of 9 properties were flooded &mdash; 8 from surface water (direct standing water or from drains unable to discharge due to high levels in Smithy Brook) and 1 from sewer flooding. (p159)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Five properties were flooded when high river levels caused Borsdane Brook to overtop its left bank and flow along Platt Lane into Prescott Street, through Aughton Street and Meadows Close before returning to the brook; other affected locations included Atherton Road and Lord Street. Two properties were reported flooded from sewers. Silt deposits and watermarks were observed on Lord Street and Aughton Street. Wigan Metropolitan Borough Council sandbagged a large number of properties as an immediate response. [PAG,MUL] (p162)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>93 properties [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Around 2,250 properties flooded internally across Greater Manchester (figure applies to multiple affected areas including Wigan); homes were evacuated in several locations including Wigan. (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>93 properties; 18 properties; 15 properties; 9 properties; 4 properties; 6 properties; 5 properties [IMG,PAG] (p146)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>93 properties; 18 properties; 15 properties; 9 properties; 4 properties; 6 properties; 5 properties [IMG,PAG] (p147)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties; 8 properties; 1 property (p159)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; 2 properties [PAG,MUL] (p162)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Wigan,England,"Flooding across the borough from multiple sources (main river, ordinary watercourses, sewers and surface water) caused internal flooding to properties. [TAB,PAG] (p17)
Wigan was affected by the Boxing Day flooding; RMAs held a local drop–in event and conducted visual inspections of flood–risk assets following the event. (p27)
Flooding occurred around Wigan on 26 December 2015; homes were evacuated by emergency services as part of the response and the local area contributed to the wider travel disruption and infrastructure impacts noted after the event. (p29)
A total of 93 properties in Wigan borough experienced internal flooding from multiple sources. Worst–affected areas included Platt Bridge (18 properties flooded from Hey Brook), Bickershaw and Abram (15 properties flooded from Hey Brook/main river and ordinary watercourse), Worsley Mesnes (9 properties flooded from sewer), Aspull (4 properties flooded from surface water and/or sewers), Standish (6 properties flooded from River Douglas, Frodshams Brook, surface water and sewer) and Hindley (5 properties flooded from combined sources including surface water, sewers and main river). [IMG,PAG] (p146)
A total of 93 properties in the Wigan borough experienced internal flooding on 26 December 2015. Worst–affected locations and primary sources recorded were: Platt Bridge (18 properties flooded from Hey Brook), Bickershaw and Abram (15 properties flooded from Hey Brook and an ordinary watercourse), Worsley Mesnes (9 properties flooded from sewers), Aspull (4 properties flooded from surface water and/or sewers), Standish (6 properties flooded from River Douglas, Frodshams Brook, surface water and sewer), and Hindley (5 properties flooded from combined sources including surface water and sewers). [IMG,PAG] (p147)
In this location a total of 9 properties were flooded — 8 from surface water (direct standing water or from drains unable to discharge due to high levels in Smithy Brook) and 1 from sewer flooding. (p159)
Five properties were flooded when high river levels caused Borsdane Brook to overtop its left bank and flow along Platt Lane into Prescott Street, through Aughton Street and Meadows Close before returning to the brook; other affected locations included Atherton Road and Lord Street. Two properties were reported flooded from sewers. Silt deposits and watermarks were observed on Lord Street and Aughton Street. Wigan Metropolitan Borough Council sandbagged a large number of properties as an immediate response. [PAG,MUL] (p162)","93 properties [TAB,PAG] (p17)
