GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.556371645618974,-2.3274739421712667,"<div id=""html_a9762b99b5d0c7db3467e90d8866dff2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lomax Street, Radcliffe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A small bridge carrying cables at Lomax Street was destroyed by the floods; temporary measures (overhead line and rerouting) were used to restore supply. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A footbridge carrying a sewer and gas main collapsed, rupturing the gas main which caused a fire and explosion and discharging sewage into the river. Temporary measures by the council reopened the bridge to pedestrian traffic. (p58)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood&ndash;related failure led to the collapse of a footbridge carrying a sewer and gas main at Lomax Street; the collapse ruptured the gas main and discharged sewage into the river as part of the flood impacts. [PAG] (p61)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A footbridge carrying a sewer and a gas main collapsed (in the course of the flood event), rupturing the gas main which ignited and caused a fire and explosion; the sewer rupture discharged sewage into the River Irwell. As a result, around 900 domestic properties experienced low gas pressure (without loss of supply). [IMG,PAG] (p62)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 bridge destroyed (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>900 domestic properties affected by low gas pressure [IMG,PAG] (p62)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Lomax Street, Radcliffe",England,"A small bridge carrying cables at Lomax Street was destroyed by the floods; temporary measures (overhead line and rerouting) were used to restore supply. (p21)
