GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5788673,-2.3415022,"<div id=""html_57994e4b3cbc205588198d1aeabc77f4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Higher Ainsworth Road, Bury</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the Higher Ainsworth Road area were flooded due to the combined effects of a culverted ordinary watercourse and surface water run&ndash;off; businesses in the area were affected in the short and longer term, with some relocating outside the Borough. (p61)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Higher Ainsworth Road, Bury",England,"Properties in the Higher Ainsworth Road area were flooded due to the combined effects of a culverted ordinary watercourse and surface water run–off; businesses in the area were affected in the short and longer term, with some relocating outside the Borough. (p61)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5667762,-2.3059816,"<div id=""html_0e36433c313a73be6c59d1a78dddeb7b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Riverside Road, Whitefield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Riverside residential estate was inundated with brown floodwater that submerged the ground floor of homes and gardens, with water reaching up to ground&ndash;floor windows, causing significant disruption and damage to properties and belongings. [IMG] (p61)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Riverside Road, Whitefield",England,"Riverside residential estate was inundated with brown floodwater that submerged the ground floor of homes and gardens, with water reaching up to ground–floor windows, causing significant disruption and damage to properties and belongings. [IMG] (p61)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.56575328792104,-2.3038483120773487,"<div id=""html_54d2cd4f2f96442ef6ea028f1d7b6106"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Parkside Close, Blackford Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Maximum flood depth above ground level reached 1.45 m at Parkside Close; properties at this location were flooded. (p63)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parkside Close is included in the River Irwell (Pioneer Mills and Parkside Close GM100) Flood Warning Area which was reviewed after the flood; threshold levels for warnings were to be altered if necessary and recovery work (gravel removal and repairs to the Pioneer Mills gauging station) was scheduled as part of the response. (p66)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1.45 m maximum flood depth (p63)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Parkside Close, Blackford Bridge",England,"Maximum flood depth above ground level reached 1.45 m at Parkside Close; properties at this location were flooded. (p63)
Parkside Close is included in the River Irwell (Pioneer Mills and Parkside Close GM100) Flood Warning Area which was reviewed after the flood; threshold levels for warnings were to be altered if necessary and recovery work (gravel removal and repairs to the Pioneer Mills gauging station) was scheduled as part of the response. (p66)",1.45 m maximum flood depth (p63),GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5760224,-2.3128677,"<div id=""html_59ba0b5e193842c74ae466960a25f450"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Warth Fold Road, Radcliffe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A culverted watercourse that runs under the Metrolink line and along Warth Fold Road is prone to blockage, causing flooding of the carriageway; floodwater from the carriageway can then flow across Radcliffe Road onto adjacent farmland and has affected a small number of properties served by the culvert. (p69)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Warth Fold Road, Radcliffe",England,"A culverted watercourse that runs under the Metrolink line and along Warth Fold Road is prone to blockage, causing flooding of the carriageway; floodwater from the carriageway can then flow across Radcliffe Road onto adjacent farmland and has affected a small number of properties served by the culvert. (p69)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5764605,-2.2979734,"<div id=""html_5ac187cbf6413e414ba2efafdc8bde9f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lakeland Crescent, Bury</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties in the Lakeland Crescent area were affected by surface water run&ndash;off and issues related to a culverted watercourse; investigations indicate the culverted watercourse to the south likely contributed to the flooding. [PAG] (p69)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 26 December 2015 the Lakeland Crescent area was affected by surface water run&ndash;off and/or culvert&ndash;related flooding; investigations are ongoing to assess the viability of improvement works. (p70)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Lakeland Crescent, Bury",England,"Residential properties in the Lakeland Crescent area were affected by surface water run–off and issues related to a culverted watercourse; investigations indicate the culverted watercourse to the south likely contributed to the flooding. [PAG] (p69)
On 26 December 2015 the Lakeland Crescent area was affected by surface water run–off and/or culvert–related flooding; investigations are ongoing to assess the viability of improvement works. (p70)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.64899724869948,-2.3124653176293193,"<div id=""html_4b9f36dd95e6720c7486c5f9660c9e09"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kenyon Street, Ramsbottom</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Businesses in the Kenyon Street/Bridge Street area were affected by a combination of River Irwell flooding and surface water; water flowed down roads and ponded behind the Kenyon Street flood defence; residential properties further from the river were affected by surface water run&ndash;off and inundated culverts on 26 December 2015. (p72)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River levels exceeded the defence line protecting Kenyon Street during the event; the basement access area was inundated/left muddy and required clean&ndash;up. Raised flood defences at this reach were overtopped or reached crest level. [IMG] (p74)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>26 properties protected (p72)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>26 properties [IMG] (p74)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Kenyon Street, Ramsbottom",England,"Businesses in the Kenyon Street/Bridge Street area were affected by a combination of River Irwell flooding and surface water; water flowed down roads and ponded behind the Kenyon Street flood defence; residential properties further from the river were affected by surface water run–off and inundated culverts on 26 December 2015. (p72)
River levels exceeded the defence line protecting Kenyon Street during the event; the basement access area was inundated/left muddy and required clean–up. Raised flood defences at this reach were overtopped or reached crest level. [IMG] (p74)","26 properties protected (p72)
