GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.6489095,-2.3164103,"<div id=""html_922691472cc1c1108e2a29d8b65c9119"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Crow Lane, Ramsbottom</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A culvert at the junction of Crow Lane and Bridge Street was damaged during the Boxing Day (26 December 2015) event, causing large additional volumes of water to flow down Crow Lane and contributing to local flooding; the culvert damage was repaired in the days immediately following the event. (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Crow Lane, Ramsbottom",England,"A culvert at the junction of Crow Lane and Bridge Street was damaged during the Boxing Day (26 December 2015) event, causing large additional volumes of water to flow down Crow Lane and contributing to local flooding; the culvert damage was repaired in the days immediately following the event. (p72)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.64811634649451,-2.3159094049829454,"<div id=""html_c85a1e82dfddd7f5bebbd7e2a23d5862"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bridge Street, Ramsbottom</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A culvert at the junction of Crow Lane and Bridge Street was damaged, producing large additional volumes of water flowing down Crow Lane; businesses in the Kenyon Street/Bridge Street area were affected by a combination of river and surface&ndash;water flooding. (p72)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 culvert (p72)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Bridge Street, Ramsbottom",England,"A culvert at the junction of Crow Lane and Bridge Street was damaged, producing large additional volumes of water flowing down Crow Lane; businesses in the Kenyon Street/Bridge Street area were affected by a combination of river and surface–water flooding. (p72)",1 culvert (p72),GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.6474977,-2.3101001,"<div id=""html_1b28fcdf6409ec65f5e922ba280e80e6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Peel Brow, Ramsbottom</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The weir just upstream of Peel Brow and the adjacent canoe pass were damaged by the flood; the local gauging station nearby recorded extreme levels prompting inspection and repair works and the Local Authority sought quotes to repair the canoe pass. (p74)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Peel Brow, Ramsbottom",England,The weir just upstream of Peel Brow and the adjacent canoe pass were damaged by the flood; the local gauging station nearby recorded extreme levels prompting inspection and repair works and the Local Authority sought quotes to repair the canoe pass. (p74),,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.61424895534916,-2.3466502958778506,"<div id=""html_bd0e3f70f7f5317a3692a0a825e358d3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Harwood Road, Tottington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A riparian culvert at Harwood Road flooded on 26th December 2015, producing substantial flows down Harwood Road. Overland flows along the carriageway flooded a number of downstream properties; the culvert outfalls to recreational land near Turton Road. Investigations into the culvert and a possible branch from Cann Street are ongoing. [IMG,PAG] (p77)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A riparian culvert at Harwood Road flooded on Boxing Day, producing substantial flows down Harwood Road and causing overland flows along the carriageway that flooded a number of downstream properties. The culvert outfalls to recreational land near Turton Road. [PAG] (p78)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Harwood Road, Tottington",England,"A riparian culvert at Harwood Road flooded on 26th December 2015, producing substantial flows down Harwood Road. Overland flows along the carriageway flooded a number of downstream properties; the culvert outfalls to recreational land near Turton Road. Investigations into the culvert and a possible branch from Cann Street are ongoing. [IMG,PAG] (p77)
A riparian culvert at Harwood Road flooded on Boxing Day, producing substantial flows down Harwood Road and causing overland flows along the carriageway that flooded a number of downstream properties. The culvert outfalls to recreational land near Turton Road. [PAG] (p78)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.56851027230534,-2.023844559961621,"<div id=""html_85bee94a23fc724b8aff8f4886800f47"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Delph</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was exacerbated at the bridge on High Street where bridge&ndash;related flow restriction caused river levels to rise and water to come out of bank, increasing local flooding. (p92)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwaters overtopped the channel at the bridge on High Street; debris on the grass marks the maximum reach of the overflow. Water inundated the area adjacent to the bridge and threatened nearby buildings (lower windows/doors at risk). [IMG,PAG] (p94)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The street was inundated with floodwater reaching up to building fronts; the channel at the bridge had discharged over its banks (debris marks the extent), and a stone wall and nearby footbridge were partially submerged. [IMG,PAG] (p95)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"High Street, Delph",England,"Flooding was exacerbated at the bridge on High Street where bridge–related flow restriction caused river levels to rise and water to come out of bank, increasing local flooding. (p92)
Floodwaters overtopped the channel at the bridge on High Street; debris on the grass marks the maximum reach of the overflow. Water inundated the area adjacent to the bridge and threatened nearby buildings (lower windows/doors at risk). [IMG,PAG] (p94)
The street was inundated with floodwater reaching up to building fronts; the channel at the bridge had discharged over its banks (debris marks the extent), and a stone wall and nearby footbridge were partially submerged. [IMG,PAG] (p95)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.567601400272586,-2.0236034801995535,"<div id=""html_5bc2ca03172fbf99cb4233984e3340ee"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>King Street, Delph</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater covered King Street in the vicinity of the bridge, inundating the roadway and threatening adjacent buildings as seen looking from the bridge toward Brookside Terrace. [IMG] (p95)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"King Street, Delph",England,"Floodwater covered King Street in the vicinity of the bridge, inundating the roadway and threatening adjacent buildings as seen looking from the bridge toward Brookside Terrace. [IMG] (p95)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5825964,-1.9973496,"<div id=""html_d03e96f892f795eed2bfdb87e067533b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bleak Hey Nook Lane, Diggle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Bleak Hey Nook Lane experienced flooding caused by a blocked culvert; the culvert was cleared by the council to address the flooding during the event. (p96)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Bleak Hey Nook Lane, Diggle",England,Properties on Bleak Hey Nook Lane experienced flooding caused by a blocked culvert; the culvert was cleared by the council to address the flooding during the event. (p96),,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.54991535269183,-2.0051970734545432,"<div id=""html_0d8b893fb043c1277ce5decd3a12174d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Uppermill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Water seepage occurred through the channel wall at the site of the café on the bridge at High Street during the flood; the bridge and channel conditions were identified as part of the post&ndash;event investigation. [PAG] (p98)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Water seepage through the channel wall at the site of the cafe on the bridge, leading to internal flooding of premises (water inside up to window sills). [IMG,PAG] (p99)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected High Street at ground&ndash;floor level (including the church), with floodwater covering the street surface and access restrictions in place. [IMG,PAG] (p101)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The road and adjacent pavements on High Street were inundated with floodwater, impeding access and prompting community response efforts on the street. [IMG,PAG] (p102)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"High Street, Uppermill",England,"Water seepage occurred through the channel wall at the site of the café on the bridge at High Street during the flood; the bridge and channel conditions were identified as part of the post–event investigation. [PAG] (p98)
Water seepage through the channel wall at the site of the cafe on the bridge, leading to internal flooding of premises (water inside up to window sills). [IMG,PAG] (p99)
Flooding affected High Street at ground–floor level (including the church), with floodwater covering the street surface and access restrictions in place. [IMG,PAG] (p101)
The road and adjacent pavements on High Street were inundated with floodwater, impeding access and prompting community response efforts on the street. [IMG,PAG] (p102)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5472593,-2.0070593,"<div id=""html_b07a325f3cae1d523315625c2c4c64d3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Moorgate Street, Uppermill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Moorgate Street were flooded during the event but the mechanism causing that flooding was unclear; Risk Management Authorities continued investigations to determine how flooding occurred at this location. (p98)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Moorgate Street, Uppermill",England,Properties on Moorgate Street were flooded during the event but the mechanism causing that flooding was unclear; Risk Management Authorities continued investigations to determine how flooding occurred at this location. (p98),,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5361939,-2.0487335,"<div id=""html_076d44a6cd9dfbca71a741bf8792f767"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Coverhill Road, Saddleworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road and adjacent footway inundated; standing water covered the full width of the carriageway and extended onto the pavement, restricting vehicular and pedestrian access and partially surrounding parked vehicles. [IMG] (p109)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Coverhill Road, Saddleworth",England,"Road and adjacent footway inundated; standing water covered the full width of the carriageway and extended onto the pavement, restricting vehicular and pedestrian access and partially surrounding parked vehicles. [IMG] (p109)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5379908,-2.0115648,"<div id=""html_92c6f414365376c80460bde311cce79f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chew Valley Road, Greenfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road shown and reported as flooded (photo credited to Saddleworth/Newsham Chronicle), indicating surface water inundation affecting the carriageway and likely access. (p109)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Chew Valley Road, Greenfield",England,"Road shown and reported as flooded (photo credited to Saddleworth/Newsham Chronicle), indicating surface water inundation affecting the carriageway and likely access. (p109)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5298499,-2.0300141,"<div id=""html_7f53466ba6a71134aa6ce25eac91d977"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Calf Lane, Micklehurst</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A nearby house 'just off Calf Lane' flooded from surface water; flooding affected properties adjacent to this street. [IMG] (p112)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Calf Lane, Micklehurst",England,A nearby house 'just off Calf Lane' flooded from surface water; flooding affected properties adjacent to this street. [IMG] (p112),,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.6151364,-2.161137,"<div id=""html_4ac120e5b77d1e2c3eac8506be999088"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Esplanade, Rochdale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Opening up the Esplanade culvert as part of prior works allowed floodwater to re&ndash;enter the river near the town centre during the Boxing Day event, which is reported to have reduced the flood extent and limited flood depths in the town centre. (p114)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Esplanade, Rochdale",England,"Opening up the Esplanade culvert as part of prior works allowed floodwater to re–enter the river near the town centre during the Boxing Day event, which is reported to have reduced the flood extent and limited flood depths in the town centre. (p114)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.64369377237706,-2.094790173449477,"<div id=""html_e026dd5cfca66d2714e611d7759b4ce2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Garden Mews, Littleborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwaters overtopped defences and natural bank levels, reaching depths that inundated properties at the location. (p117)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flood depths up to 1.2 m (p117)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Garden Mews, Littleborough",England,"Floodwaters overtopped defences and natural bank levels, reaching depths that inundated properties at the location. (p117)",flood depths up to 1.2 m (p117),GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.6543621,-2.0865711,"<div id=""html_34eefbf5618774135888311babb0c35a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Todmorden Road, Rochdale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Most of the property flooding occurred on or near Todmorden Road; some properties on the road have flooded on multiple occasions. Flood&ndash;related infrastructure damage (culvert damage) was reported on Todmorden Road. (p117)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Todmorden Road, Rochdale",England,Most of the property flooding occurred on or near Todmorden Road; some properties on the road have flooded on multiple occasions. Flood–related infrastructure damage (culvert damage) was reported on Todmorden Road. (p117),,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.6567063,-2.0954081,"<div id=""html_ab5ccd881c0d17cc930826403b54c468"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Calderbrook Road, Rochdale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding caused damage to a culvert on Calderbrook Road; overland flows were reported in nearby areas associated with the event. (p117)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Infrastructure damage in the area included culvert damage at Calderbrook Rd, Todmorden Road and Halifax Road; gully blockage and damage occurred throughout the area including to rural paths. A landslip at Whitfield Brow led to evacuation of properties and is subject to further investigation regarding attribution to Storm Eva. (p118)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>culvert damage at 3 locations (p118)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Calderbrook Road, Rochdale",England,"Flooding caused damage to a culvert on Calderbrook Road; overland flows were reported in nearby areas associated with the event. (p117)
Infrastructure damage in the area included culvert damage at Calderbrook Rd, Todmorden Road and Halifax Road; gully blockage and damage occurred throughout the area including to rural paths. A landslip at Whitfield Brow led to evacuation of properties and is subject to further investigation regarding attribution to Storm Eva. (p118)",culvert damage at 3 locations (p118),GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.6477896,-2.0593487,"<div id=""html_f77dbe34d40b714cc26c1805c730aa69"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Halifax Road, Rochdale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood&ndash;related culvert damage occurred at Halifax Road as part of the event's infrastructure impacts. (p117)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Halifax Road, Rochdale",England,Flood–related culvert damage occurred at Halifax Road as part of the event's infrastructure impacts. (p117),,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.65286633037888,-2.0879240065840725,"<div id=""html_e3e5a3a4b78f5a2dc79fd3d09d925719"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whitfield Brow, Littleborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A landslip occurred at Whitfield Brow, which led to the evacuation of properties; the landslip is linked to saturated ground and heavy rainfall associated with the flooding and is subject to further investigation regarding attribution to Storm Eva. (p117)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"Whitfield Brow, Littleborough",England,"A landslip occurred at Whitfield Brow, which led to the evacuation of properties; the landslip is linked to saturated ground and heavy rainfall associated with the flooding and is subject to further investigation regarding attribution to Storm Eva. (p117)",,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.6171307,-2.1568165,"<div id=""html_cc1e27fd89b1f58930d1b2cf5d09d1b5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Butts, Rochdale</h1><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>properties flooded up to 1.5 metres deep at The Butts (p121)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,"The Butts, Rochdale",England,,properties flooded up to 1.5 metres deep at The Butts (p121),GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
