GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.648384,-2.315696,"<div id=""html_5b7b021dc946e616718aa14e104d68e8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ramsbottom</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties in Ramsbottom caused by main river and surface water; properties experienced internal (ground&ndash;floor) flooding. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ramsbottom and Breightmet are listed as affected by the 26 December 2015 floods; a River Irwell gauge at Ramsbottom reached 3.39m, a 10&ndash;year record high. (p56)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Irwell reached a record high level at Ramsbottom, producing flooding in the town during the event. The extreme river level was associated with residential and commercial flooding in affected areas listed in the report. [PAG] (p57)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties were flooded by main river (river corridor) and by surface water; flooding concentrated in central and southern Ramsbottom within mapped Flood Zone 3, with clusters of flooded properties shown along the main river and near watercourses. [IMG] (p71)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Town centre and riverside areas experienced significant river flooding: cricket and football grounds flooded from the main river; river channel walls at Nuttall Park were damaged and required repair; bridges were closed temporarily and inspected; emergency sandbags were distributed and a multi&ndash;day clean&ndash;up (including free skips) took place. Recovery actions and reviews of flood warnings for the Ramsbottom area were initiated. [PAG] (p74)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>47 properties (main river); 12 properties (surface water); 59 properties (total) [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3.39m (127.42m AOD)