These places are listed under locations affected by the 26 December 2015 flooding; multiple locations across the borough experienced flooding and required local authority response. (p18)","2 properties [TAB,PAG] (p17)",GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5249679,-2.4905799,"<div id=""html_8d4cc24068e0c567c8225cd844cc3bfc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Atherton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to property caused by sewer flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>These places are listed under locations affected by the 26 December 2015 flooding; multiple locations across the borough experienced flooding and required local authority response. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property flooded [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Atherton,England,"Internal flooding to property caused by sewer flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p17)
These places are listed under locations affected by the 26 December 2015 flooding; multiple locations across the borough experienced flooding and required local authority response. (p18)","1 property flooded [TAB,PAG] (p17)",GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5335298,-2.5778214,"<div id=""html_0f09e64f373c52d9f689d274ea4b08e4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hindley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties due to main river (river) flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in the list of places affected during the 26 December 2015 floods; experienced flooding that formed part of the multiple local incidents requiring response. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties occurred due to combined sources (main river, surface water and sewers). [IMG,PAG] (p146)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties from combined sources (surface water, sewers and main river influence). [PAG] (p147)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hey Brook came out of its channel downstream of Hindley, causing out&ndash;of&ndash;channel flow and localised river flooding in the area adjacent to the town. (p150)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from Borsdane Brook caused high river levels to spill over the left bank and flow along Platt Lane into Prescott Street, through Aughton Street and Meadows Close before returning to the brook; other affected streets included Atherton Road and Lord Street. Surface&ndash;water flooding (standing water and blocked drains due to high levels in Smithy Brook) flooded properties. Sewer flooding affected one property. [IMG] (p160)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood warning issued for the area; overflow from local watercourses (notably Borsdane Brook) led to street and property flooding in Hindley. Local response included widespread sandbagging and investigation of improvements to flood protection following extreme river levels. (p162)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties flooded [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties [IMG,PAG] (p146)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties [PAG] (p147)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; 8 properties; 1 property [IMG] (p160)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties flooded; 2 properties reported as flooded from sewers (p162)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Hindley,England,"Internal flooding to properties due to main river (river) flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p17)
Included in the list of places affected during the 26 December 2015 floods; experienced flooding that formed part of the multiple local incidents requiring response. (p18)
Internal flooding of properties occurred due to combined sources (main river, surface water and sewers). [IMG,PAG] (p146)
Internal flooding of properties from combined sources (surface water, sewers and main river influence). [PAG] (p147)
Hey Brook came out of its channel downstream of Hindley, causing out–of–channel flow and localised river flooding in the area adjacent to the town. (p150)
Flooding from Borsdane Brook caused high river levels to spill over the left bank and flow along Platt Lane into Prescott Street, through Aughton Street and Meadows Close before returning to the brook; other affected streets included Atherton Road and Lord Street. Surface–water flooding (standing water and blocked drains due to high levels in Smithy Brook) flooded properties. Sewer flooding affected one property. [IMG] (p160)
Flood warning issued for the area; overflow from local watercourses (notably Borsdane Brook) led to street and property flooding in Hindley. Local response included widespread sandbagging and investigation of improvements to flood protection following extreme river levels. (p162)","5 properties flooded [TAB,PAG] (p17)
