GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.54552,-2.3678584,"<div id=""html_a2be32687ea31bb9bf1d4d693cd425e2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stoneclough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe internal flooding to homes from the main river; flooding inside homes reached up to head height. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>57 properties (Prestolee and Stoneclough) [TAB] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Stoneclough,England,Severe internal flooding to homes from the main river; flooding inside homes reached up to head height. [TAB] (p17),57 properties (Prestolee and Stoneclough) [TAB] (p17),GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5757428,-2.2978435,"<div id=""html_f9f49eeb3e1c6f60188ce95c87b1bc7d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Redvales</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe internal flooding to properties, predominantly caused by main river flooding; appraisals were noted to reduce future risk in this area. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected Redvales, with residential properties inundated; a scheme has been proposed to assess options for reducing flood risk in the area. [IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in Radcliffe/Redvales affected properties in the area. (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Irwell inundated residential and commercial areas in Radcliffe and Redvales; communities and businesses were the most severely affected locally. (p56)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Redvales experienced overbank flooding with general flood depths around 0.6 to 0.8m; the River Irwell at Redvales flood warning area (GM41/GM42) coverage and threshold levels were reviewed for improvement following the event. (p63)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Irwell affected the Redvales area, leading the Environment Agency and Bury Council to consider proposing flood defence measures for the Redvales and Radcliffe area and to review local flood warning thresholds. (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties were flooded on 26 December 2015; flooding is described as surface water / culvert&ndash;related affecting homes in the Redvales area. (p69)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>671 properties (in Radcliffe and Redvales combined); 644 properties flooded by main river; 7 by ordinary watercourse; 1 by sewer; 19 by surface water [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Over 670 properties flooded [IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>670 properties (Radcliffe/Redvales combined) (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>671 properties; maximum flood depth above ground level 1.4 m; typical flood depth 0.6&ndash;0.8 m (p56)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>0.6 to 0.8m flood depth (p63)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Redvales,England,"Severe internal flooding to properties, predominantly caused by main river flooding; appraisals were noted to reduce future risk in this area. [TAB] (p17)
