Flooding from Bessy Brook occurred when the long culvert beneath Sudbury Drive / Ashridge Close gardens, Regent Road and the railway embankment was overwhelmed. Debris at the culvert inlet exacerbated the flooding; properties were inundated above ground level (within Flood Zone 3). [MUL] (p47)","7 properties [TAB] (p17)
