GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.6201588,-2.1289111,"<div id=""html_d17739fadd85669cb25d8478dbb9049f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Belfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties in Belfield caused by main river flooding. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported clusters of property flooding concentrated along the main river and Flood Zone 3. River Beal flows overtopped banks and culvert capacity was exceeded at the culvert inlet, causing flooding of adjoining units and yard areas. Ten industrial storage units at Firgrove Business Park were flooded. [IMG] (p135)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 properties [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>10 industrial storage units; up to 60 properties [IMG] (p135)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Belfield,England,"Internal flooding to properties in Belfield caused by main river flooding. [TAB] (p17)
Reported clusters of property flooding concentrated along the main river and Flood Zone 3. River Beal flows overtopped banks and culvert capacity was exceeded at the culvert inlet, causing flooding of adjoining units and yard areas. Ten industrial storage units at Firgrove Business Park were flooded. [IMG] (p135)","10 properties [TAB] (p17)
10 industrial storage units; up to 60 properties [IMG] (p135)",GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.60825,-2.1099477,"<div id=""html_122e9c562b11cc7bd30d40a3f6111bdb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Milnrow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Milnrow (Station Road / River Beal) experienced high river levels on 26 December 2015 that resulted in river flooding in the locality. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties in Milnrow from multiple sources including main river, sewer and surface water. [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Raised River Beal levels and local drainage/retaining wall configuration allowed flood water to spill into cottage grounds and pool in a natural land dip; floodwater entered a commercial building through the rear wall alongside the river. Overall surface&ndash;water/river flooding affected properties in the Milnrow area. [IMG,PAG] (p131)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area experienced flooding driven by high River Beal levels and associated surface water: floodwater flowed down Lily Street onto Bridge Street, pooled in natural low spots and entered residential and commercial properties (including cottages and a commercial unit where water entered via the back wall). (p132)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 properties (1 main river; 1 sewer; 9 surface water) [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties [IMG,PAG] (p131)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties; external flood depths 200&ndash;900mm (p132)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Milnrow,England,"Milnrow (Station Road / River Beal) experienced high river levels on 26 December 2015 that resulted in river flooding in the locality. (p16)
Internal flooding to properties in Milnrow from multiple sources including main river, sewer and surface water. [TAB,PAG] (p17)
Raised River Beal levels and local drainage/retaining wall configuration allowed flood water to spill into cottage grounds and pool in a natural land dip; floodwater entered a commercial building through the rear wall alongside the river. Overall surface–water/river flooding affected properties in the Milnrow area. [IMG,PAG] (p131)
Area experienced flooding driven by high River Beal levels and associated surface water: floodwater flowed down Lily Street onto Bridge Street, pooled in natural low spots and entered residential and commercial properties (including cottages and a commercial unit where water entered via the back wall). (p132)","11 properties (1 main river; 1 sewer; 9 surface water) [TAB,PAG] (p17)
