GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5086727,-2.5952405,"<div id=""html_d3c9d6a3fa07c8e64f04383d7768f7b8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Abram</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties caused by main river and ordinary watercourse flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>These places are listed under locations affected by the 26 December 2015 flooding; multiple locations across the borough experienced flooding and required local authority response. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hey Brook (main river and ordinary watercourse) caused flooding that resulted in 15 properties being internally flooded in the Bickershaw and Abram area. (p146)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Abram/Bickershaw area was affected by flooding associated with main rivers (Brookside Brook and Hey Brook); post&ndash;event actions included investigating improvements to the standard of flood protection for Abram/Bickershaw. (p150)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (p146)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Abram,England,"Internal flooding to properties caused by main river and ordinary watercourse flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p17)
