GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5690061,-2.4010571,"<div id=""html_0d0d1f4e2e6525678f10520794ad05d8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Darcy Lever</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties caused by main&ndash;river flooding. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Darcy Lever experienced flooding driven by the River Croal, forming a local flood cluster and causing internal property flooding. (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Croal inundated properties at Darcy Lever; event led to properties being flooded and is the subject of an Environment Agency investigation. (p55)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 flooded properties: 2 residential and 6 businesses (p55)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Darcy Lever,England,"Internal flooding to properties caused by main–river flooding. [TAB] (p17)
