GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5144859,-2.4661714,"<div id=""html_5c2f42c6038254618768b5e7796508c4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tyldesley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties resulting from main river flooding and sewer&ndash;related flooding. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (2 by main river; 2 by sewer) [TAB] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Tyldesley,England,Internal flooding to properties resulting from main river flooding and sewer–related flooding. [TAB] (p17),4 properties (2 by main river; 2 by sewer) [TAB] (p17),GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.5032866,-2.2344764,"<div id=""html_95843efb3fba7086afbf22722958bb1f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cheetham Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties in Cheetham Hill caused by main river flooding. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties flooded internally as part of the December 2015 flooding; area included in the ~750 properties flooded across Lower Kersal, Lower Broughton and Cheetham Hill. Flood storage works were under construction to reduce future risk (protecting up to 1,900 homes/businesses). [IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clusters of properties in the Cheetham Hill area were flooded; Environment Agency led investigations indicating flooding originated from nearby watercourses/main river. Flooded properties occurred on both sides of the district boundary within the Cheetham Hill area. [IMG] (p82)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Irwell overtopped raised defences and natural banks and the surface water network exceeded capacity, causing flooding in the Cheetham Hill area. Non&ndash;residential properties in the area were affected and internal flooding occurred in properties. [IMG] (p83)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Record high River Irwell levels at Salford (5.67m) generated a Flood Warning for the River Irwell (Salford Area B) and placed properties at Cheetham Hill at risk of river flooding; flood storage basins (Castle Irwell and Lower Kersal) are cited as measures to reduce flood risk to these properties. [PAG] (p84)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>27 properties [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Approximately 750 properties (across Lower Kersal, Lower Broughton and Cheetham Hill) [IMG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 47 non&ndash;residential properties; 27 properties flooded internally [IMG] (p83)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Cheetham Hill,England,"Internal flooding to properties in Cheetham Hill caused by main river flooding. [TAB] (p17)
Properties flooded internally as part of the December 2015 flooding; area included in the ~750 properties flooded across Lower Kersal, Lower Broughton and Cheetham Hill. Flood storage works were under construction to reduce future risk (protecting up to 1,900 homes/businesses). [IMG] (p20)
Clusters of properties in the Cheetham Hill area were flooded; Environment Agency led investigations indicating flooding originated from nearby watercourses/main river. Flooded properties occurred on both sides of the district boundary within the Cheetham Hill area. [IMG] (p82)
The River Irwell overtopped raised defences and natural banks and the surface water network exceeded capacity, causing flooding in the Cheetham Hill area. Non–residential properties in the area were affected and internal flooding occurred in properties. [IMG] (p83)
