GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.54799,-2.3722131,"<div id=""html_5294c2615313d89ff284d4e7611c5889"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Prestolee</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe internal flooding to homes from the main river; flooding inside homes reached up to head height. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency river flow/level gauging station at Prestolee on the River Irwell was completely destroyed by the flooding; pumping stations at Prestolee were also affected, degrading local monitoring and flood&ndash;response infrastructure. (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Homes were evacuated by emergency services because of the flooding. (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Irwell inundated homes in Prestolee; properties experienced internal flooding, with water depths recorded up to 1.5 metres. (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Prestolee pumping station sustained damage during the flood event. (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties at Prestolee were flooded by the River Irwell: Riverside Drive (a cul&ndash;de&ndash;sac) was flooded to depths up to 1.5 m, and apartments on Stoneclough Rise (including Langcliffe Place) sustained internal flooding up to about 200 mm. A localised river&ndash;bank slip occurred west of Prestolee New Bridge. Community recovery and local Flood Action Group activity followed the event. [PAG] (p44)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Prestolee was affected by very high river levels at the River Irwell (included in the same flood&ndash;warning area as Ringley Bridges) and localised bank failure nearby; future defensive options (a raised left&ndash;bank wall) were proposed to protect Prestolee following the event. (p45)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>57 properties (Prestolee and Stoneclough) [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>57 homes; flood depths up to 1.5 metres (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 pumping station damaged (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Riverside Drive flooded to depths up to 1.5m; apartments on Stoneclough Rise flooded up to 200mm [PAG] (p44)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1.6m higher (p45)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Prestolee,England,"Severe internal flooding to homes from the main river; flooding inside homes reached up to head height. [TAB] (p17)
