158 properties flooded above ground floor level; 17 properties flooded from surface water; flood depths up to 1.2m at Garden Mews; flood warning issued to over 690 properties [PAG] (p117)
over 690 properties [IMG,PAG] (p118)",GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
GB-BOL,2,2015-12-26,53.6211615,-2.1446492,"<div id=""html_207279267e41fcdab304ce30700d9d61"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wardleworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties due to main river flooding (Wardleworth / Hey Brook area). [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding (from Hey Brook and associated watercourses) caused internal flooding of properties in the Wardleworth area. [PAG] (p113)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Wardleworth (including Hey Brook area) experienced internal property flooding associated with river flooding on 26 December 2015. (p114)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Communities in Wardleworth and Littleborough were affected by the Boxing Day flooding and received ongoing support through a pre&ndash;existing community resilience programme; the National Flood Forum continued to provide support post&ndash;event, and Risk Management Authorities and the Council held community drop&ndash;in sessions and promoted resilience and recovery grant schemes. (p115)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Map and appendix show clusters of reported property flooding in the Wardleworth and Hey Brook area associated with the main river, ordinary watercourses and surface water. Flood extents broadly matched, or slightly exceeded, Flood Zone 3 in places; largest clusters were concentrated in the western section of the mapped area. [IMG] (p124)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Wardleworth experienced flooding on 26 December 2015: properties close to the River Roch flooded internally (reported depths up to 400mm), cellars flooded from surface water/groundwater, a flood warning was issued, local rest centre set up and sandbags distributed, nearby electrical substations were flooded causing loss of power to properties; allotments on Kellet Street also flooded (they had flooded previously in 2012). [PAG,MUL] (p126)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>36 properties (Wardleworth / Hey Brook area) [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>36 properties (Wardleworth and Hey Brook) (p113)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>36 properties flooded (Wardleworth and Hey Brook) (p114)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 houses (cellars flooded in 2012) [PAG,MUL] (p126)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bolton,Wardleworth,England,"Internal flooding to properties due to main river flooding (Wardleworth / Hey Brook area). [TAB] (p17)
Flooding (from Hey Brook and associated watercourses) caused internal flooding of properties in the Wardleworth area. [PAG] (p113)
Wardleworth (including Hey Brook area) experienced internal property flooding associated with river flooding on 26 December 2015. (p114)
Communities in Wardleworth and Littleborough were affected by the Boxing Day flooding and received ongoing support through a pre–existing community resilience programme; the National Flood Forum continued to provide support post–event, and Risk Management Authorities and the Council held community drop–in sessions and promoted resilience and recovery grant schemes. (p115)
Map and appendix show clusters of reported property flooding in the Wardleworth and Hey Brook area associated with the main river, ordinary watercourses and surface water. Flood extents broadly matched, or slightly exceeded, Flood Zone 3 in places; largest clusters were concentrated in the western section of the mapped area. [IMG] (p124)
Wardleworth experienced flooding on 26 December 2015: properties close to the River Roch flooded internally (reported depths up to 400mm), cellars flooded from surface water/groundwater, a flood warning was issued, local rest centre set up and sandbags distributed, nearby electrical substations were flooded causing loss of power to properties; allotments on Kellet Street also flooded (they had flooded previously in 2012). [PAG,MUL] (p126)","36 properties (Wardleworth / Hey Brook area) [TAB] (p17)
36 properties (Wardleworth and Hey Brook) (p113)
36 properties flooded (Wardleworth and Hey Brook) (p114)
4 houses (cellars flooded in 2012) [PAG,MUL] (p126)",GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26.html,GB-BOL_2_2015-12-26,Greater Manchester flooding 26 Dec 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Greater Manchester 26 December 2015,010/Bolton/010/2015/Bolton/Boxing/Day/2015///Flood/report.pdf
