GB-LAN,16,2016-08-21,53.873855500000005,-2.950319910579624,"<div id=""html_cb06e01fa7058b43ba1232622893fb80"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hambleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water sewers in the Hambleton/Stalmine area failed to operate as normal because of excessive water levels linked to high river and watercourse levels, leading to local drainage/sewering impacts. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Hambleton,England,"Surface water sewers in the Hambleton/Stalmine area failed to operate as normal because of excessive water levels linked to high river and watercourse levels, leading to local drainage/sewering impacts. (p15)",,GB-LAN_16_2016-08-21.html,GB-LAN_16_2016-08-21,Lancashire flooding 21 Aug 2016 - 23 Aug 2016,21-23 August 2016 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-august-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,16,2016-08-21,53.901688,-2.9536934,"<div id=""html_7df964a277e01a0d676b327f9721f2a5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stalmine</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water sewers failed to operate normally in the Hambleton/Stalmine area due to excessive water levels associated with high river and watercourse levels. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Stalmine,England,Surface water sewers failed to operate normally in the Hambleton/Stalmine area due to excessive water levels associated with high river and watercourse levels. (p15),,GB-LAN_16_2016-08-21.html,GB-LAN_16_2016-08-21,Lancashire flooding 21 Aug 2016 - 23 Aug 2016,21-23 August 2016 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-august-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-LAN,16,2016-08-21,53.877117,-2.7638138,"<div id=""html_d136e4cc502e20c5c3f767f52c7d5f1f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Catterall Basin</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Activated by the Environment Agency at 09:45 on 22 Aug 2016 in response to heavy downpours; reached full capacity at 22:00 on 22 Aug 2016. (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Catterall Basin,England,Activated by the Environment Agency at 09:45 on 22 Aug 2016 in response to heavy downpours; reached full capacity at 22:00 on 22 Aug 2016. (p14),,GB-LAN_16_2016-08-21.html,GB-LAN_16_2016-08-21,Lancashire flooding 21 Aug 2016 - 23 Aug 2016,21-23 August 2016 Flooding In Lancashire: Section 19 Investigation Report,069/Lancashire County/section-19-flood-investigation-report-august-2016-flooding.pdf
GB-IOW,2,2023-10-25,50.7568167,-1.2917692,"<div id=""html_4d33d8295aed7a5dbb45ddc35dea355f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Medina</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Medina flooded during the event on 25 October 2023 and is implicated in the fluvial flooding affecting the area; river level data was requested to understand the magnitude of the fluvial flooding. (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,River Medina,England,The River Medina flooded during the event on 25 October 2023 and is implicated in the fluvial flooding affecting the area; river level data was requested to understand the magnitude of the fluvial flooding. (p27),,GB-IOW_2_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_2_2023-10-25,East Cowes flooding 25 Oct 2023,East Cowes - Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation East Cowes Sept 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,2,2023-10-25,50.75864190606896,-1.288928254963918,"<div id=""html_f4945bf203e8011b51def90c2a9e0438"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Well Road Roundabout</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a high RoFSW (surface water) risk location; the roundabout and immediate carriageways were within the area impacted by the October 2023 surface water flooding event. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storm pumps were operated at the roundabout to extract flood water. [TAB] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Roundabout and adjacent pedestrian island submerged by floodwater; traffic bollard and street signs nearly surrounded by water, indicating inundation of the junction and impaired access. (p36)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,Well Road Roundabout,England,"Identified as a high RoFSW (surface water) risk location; the roundabout and immediate carriageways were within the area impacted by the October 2023 surface water flooding event. (p18)
Storm pumps were operated at the roundabout to extract flood water. [TAB] (p30)
Roundabout and adjacent pedestrian island submerged by floodwater; traffic bollard and street signs nearly surrounded by water, indicating inundation of the junction and impaired access. (p36)",,GB-IOW_2_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_2_2023-10-25,East Cowes flooding 25 Oct 2023,East Cowes - Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation East Cowes Sept 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,2,2023-10-25,50.7580656,-1.2866913,"<div id=""html_be6fa8a32281b7f3d64dfea11736efa9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church Path, East Cowes</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hydraulic overloading of the Church Path watercourse during the event, contributing to overload of local drainage systems that discharge to the channel and increasing flood risk in the immediate drainage network. [TAB] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Church Path watercourse (an Environment Agency main river) discharged into the Medina Estuary and is identified as a key pathway in the October 2023 event. Flooding occurred when tide levels were rising; tide locking likely blocked discharge from the watercourse and local drainage, causing backing up of water, overtopping and exceedance of drainage channels and contributing to flooding in adjacent areas. (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Pedestrian path was submerged under several inches of floodwater and rendered impassable; floodwater covered the pavement and extended up to nearby building entrances and the bases of street furniture. [IMG] (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse at Church Path was identified as a location where capacity is insufficient and contributed to flooding; a feasibility study into increasing the watercourse capacity was recommended. (p58)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse at Church Path is identified as having capacity concerns contributing to local flooding; a feasibility study to increase its capacity was proposed to reduce flood risk. (p59)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Church Path, East Cowes",England,"Hydraulic overloading of the Church Path watercourse during the event, contributing to overload of local drainage systems that discharge to the channel and increasing flood risk in the immediate drainage network. [TAB] (p10)
The Church Path watercourse (an Environment Agency main river) discharged into the Medina Estuary and is identified as a key pathway in the October 2023 event. Flooding occurred when tide levels were rising; tide locking likely blocked discharge from the watercourse and local drainage, causing backing up of water, overtopping and exceedance of drainage channels and contributing to flooding in adjacent areas. (p33)
Pedestrian path was submerged under several inches of floodwater and rendered impassable; floodwater covered the pavement and extended up to nearby building entrances and the bases of street furniture. [IMG] (p37)
The watercourse at Church Path was identified as a location where capacity is insufficient and contributed to flooding; a feasibility study into increasing the watercourse capacity was recommended. (p58)
The watercourse at Church Path is identified as having capacity concerns contributing to local flooding; a feasibility study to increase its capacity was proposed to reduce flood risk. (p59)",,GB-IOW_2_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_2_2023-10-25,East Cowes flooding 25 Oct 2023,East Cowes - Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation East Cowes Sept 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,2,2023-10-25,50.7580145,-1.2874871,"<div id=""html_b7b6115ca92172c0ff5ce04217fc4304"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Well Road, East Cowes</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Well Road experienced flooding on 25 October 2023 and is located within the tidal extent of Flood Zones 2 and 3, indicating the flood was associated with tidal inundation. (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included among the most affected areas in East Cowes during the October 2023 flood. Flooding was driven by extreme rainfall, tide locking of outfalls to the Medina Estuary and hydraulic overloading of watercourses and local drainage; clogged road drains and overloaded combined sewers (with overspill and burst manholes) contributed to flooding of the road and nearby properties. (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Street level flooding with water covering the road surface as viewed looking towards the ferry terminal; built environment and access along Well Road affected by standing floodwater. (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The majority of the flooding impacted the area in the vicinity of Well Road; roads and nearby properties experienced flooding, with some properties reporting internal flooding. [MUL] (p38)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Well Road, East Cowes",England,"Well Road experienced flooding on 25 October 2023 and is located within the tidal extent of Flood Zones 2 and 3, indicating the flood was associated with tidal inundation. (p17)
Included among the most affected areas in East Cowes during the October 2023 flood. Flooding was driven by extreme rainfall, tide locking of outfalls to the Medina Estuary and hydraulic overloading of watercourses and local drainage; clogged road drains and overloaded combined sewers (with overspill and burst manholes) contributed to flooding of the road and nearby properties. (p33)
Street level flooding with water covering the road surface as viewed looking towards the ferry terminal; built environment and access along Well Road affected by standing floodwater. (p36)
The majority of the flooding impacted the area in the vicinity of Well Road; roads and nearby properties experienced flooding, with some properties reporting internal flooding. [MUL] (p38)",,GB-IOW_2_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_2_2023-10-25,East Cowes flooding 25 Oct 2023,East Cowes - Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation East Cowes Sept 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,2,2023-10-25,50.7582131,-1.2895673,"<div id=""html_f43e093577d6aa42bc69dd8aefecf798"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Castle Street, East Cowes</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced flooding during the event on 25 October 2023; the street lies within the tidal extent of Flood Zones 2 and 3 (subject to tidal flooding from the Medina Estuary/The Solent). (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a low&ndash;lying area that received a large amount of rainwater/runoff from Spring Hill during the event, leading to surface water flooding of the area on the main event date. (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported flooding in the vicinity of Castle Street as part of the town&ndash;centre flood incidents. [PAG] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified among areas with significant flood impacts in East Cowes during the October 2023 event. Flooding was driven by extreme rainfall with tide locking and hydraulic overloading of drainage and the Church Path watercourse, causing blocked drains, sewer overload with overspill and burst manhole covers and resulting in flooding of roads and surrounding properties. (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Manholes in Castle Street surcharged and flooded the road; floodwater followed local topography causing internal flooding of commercial buildings and residential dwellings on Castle Street. Residential properties were heavily affected, with residents displaced to alternative accommodation and loss of carpets, floorboards, furniture and other ground&ndash;floor belongings. Local businesses on Castle Street closed and suffered loss of income; residents experienced stress and anxiety. (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Manholes in Castle Street surcharged, causing road flooding and internal flooding of commercial buildings and residential dwellings. Residents were displaced (temporary or permanent moves), lost ground&ndash;floor carpets, floorboards, furniture and other belongings; local businesses closed, lost income and made insurance claims. [IMG] (p35)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater covers the full width of the street, reaching up to shopfronts and building entrances; sandbags placed at some doorways indicating attempts to prevent water ingress and disruption to businesses and pedestrian access. (p36)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Low kerb levels were noted on Castle Street and during the event flood water encroached onto properties causing internal flooding. (p51)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Castle Street, East Cowes",England,"Experienced flooding during the event on 25 October 2023; the street lies within the tidal extent of Flood Zones 2 and 3 (subject to tidal flooding from the Medina Estuary/The Solent). (p17)
