GB-IOW,2,2023-10-25,50.7564545,-1.2856281,"<div id=""html_f3b743fb920e5ec393c3469c73094732"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>York Avenue, East Cowes</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced flooding during the event on 25 October 2023; the avenue lies within the tidal extent of Flood Zones 2 and 3 (subject to tidal flooding from the Medina Estuary/The Solent). (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rainwater originating on Spring Hill flowed into this low&ndash;lying street during the event, causing surface water flooding and internal flooding of properties. (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported flooding in the vicinity of York Avenue as part of the town&ndash;centre flood incidents. [PAG] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed among areas with the most significant flood impacts in East Cowes during the October 2023 event. Flooding was caused by extreme rainfall combined with tide locking and hydraulic overloading of the local watercourse and drainage, leading to blocked drains and backup of water. The East Cowes combined sewer catchment was overloaded, with reports of sewage overspill and burst manhole covers contributing to road and property flooding. (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on York Avenue were heavily internally flooded on the morning of 25 October 2023. Residents were forced to move into alternative accommodation (temporary or permanent), lost carpets, floorboards, furniture and other ground&ndash;floor belongings, and experienced stress and anxiety. There were wider economic impacts from business disruption reported in the affected area. (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties; residents were heavily affected on the morning of 25 October 2023, with displacement in