two stone courses above the blue band of bricks [IMG] (p41)",GB-NNH_2_2016-03-09.html,GB-NNH_2_2016-03-09,Brigstock flooding 09 Mar 2016,"Flood Investigation Report: Grafton Road, Brigstock, 9th March 2016",090/North Northamptonshire/22327/FIR-Brigstock/Rev03/151216.pdf
GB-NNH,2,2016-03-09,52.4449422,-0.6166142,"<div id=""html_733d9b483b600c0c4be09d3476a20b19"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Grafton Road, Brigstock</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a private property: surface water entered the building as a result of heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment and overwhelmed local drainage, with excess water flowing over ground to low points around the property. [MUL] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a property on Grafton Road; the same property has experienced internal flooding on more than one occasion within the preceding five years. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Repeated highway flooding around property on Grafton Road caused by high water levels in Harpers Brook overtopping onto the road; one property on Grafton Road was internally flooded and bow waves from vehicles exacerbated flooding of properties. [TAB,MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area adjacent to the Grafton Road bridge over Harpers Brook sits low; water leaving the brook flowed onto the road and surrounding area and rose until it entered residential properties. One property on Grafton Road was internally flooded. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The road junction at the intersection (Grafton Road/Sudborough Road) showed ponding/standing water during the event, affecting the immediate carriageway and verge areas. [IMG] (p42)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [MUL] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property internally flooded [TAB,MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [PAG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Grafton Road, Brigstock",England,"Internal flooding of a private property: surface water entered the building as a result of heavy rainfall on a saturated catchment and overwhelmed local drainage, with excess water flowing over ground to low points around the property. [MUL] (p7)
