GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.0848946,-5.5391423,"<div id=""html_8fdc7329409190cf836a6ae582cc50ac"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Foxes Lane, Mousehole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from the Paul Stream breakout and surface water flowed down Foxes Lane. (p35)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,"Foxes Lane, Mousehole",England,Runoff from the Paul Stream breakout and surface water flowed down Foxes Lane. (p35),,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.084502245874184,-5.5398946547334535,"<div id=""html_fa4eee66a3b3ddfdae3347ff83bc4c7e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chapel Place, Mousehole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overflow of the Paul Stream at 'The Dam' caused flows down Chapel Place (reported as Chapel Place/Duck Street). (p35)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,"Chapel Place, Mousehole",England,Overflow of the Paul Stream at 'The Dam' caused flows down Chapel Place (reported as Chapel Place/Duck Street). (p35),,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.0843192,-5.5395881,"<div id=""html_c11f9d3777122073c6dee8c385480cd1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Duck Street, Mousehole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overflow of the Paul Stream at 'The Dam' caused flows down Duck Street (reported as Chapel Place/Duck Street). (p35)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,"Duck Street, Mousehole",England,Overflow of the Paul Stream at 'The Dam' caused flows down Duck Street (reported as Chapel Place/Duck Street). (p35),,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.0819657,-5.5390384,"<div id=""html_aca1b6befd72518a1108e72d4671d5d2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Portland Place, Mousehole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy surface water flows ran onto Portland Place; many manhole covers lifted on both the culverted stream and the combined sewer system. (p35)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,"Portland Place, Mousehole",England,Heavy surface water flows ran onto Portland Place; many manhole covers lifted on both the culverted stream and the combined sewer system. (p35),,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.416667,-4.75,"<div id=""html_7e995b03e586f2f88b74c5f4e4a6a8eb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cornwall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Heavy and prolonged rainfall, together with storm surge and large swell at times, caused surface water, fluvial and coastal/tidal flooding across the county. Roads and properties were flooded (properties specifically reported in Bugle, St Austell, Penzance, Camborne and Redruth); sea defences were badly damaged at Long Rock; coastal flooding affected Looe, Mevagissey, Fowey and other settlements; tidal flood gates were shut in places (e.g. Truro, Polperro). [MUL] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding across the county: coastal overtopping and wave&ndash;driven flooding of properties on the south coast when spring tides coincided with low pressure and strong south&ndash;easterly winds; widespread river, surface water and groundwater&ndash;related flooding during the late&ndash;December rainfall event (starting 18 Dec and lasting ~2 weeks) affecting many of the same properties flooded in November. [PAG] (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred across Cornwall during the late&ndash;November 2012 event. [TAB,PAG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding occurred across Cornwall during the event; the report records internal flooding of properties in Hessenford as part of this event. [PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding occurred across Cornwall during the late&ndash;November 2012 event; the report states flooding occurred across Cornwall. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding occurred across Cornwall during the event; surface water runoff from hillsides and elevated river levels contributed to flooding in the county. [TAB,PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred across Cornwall during the November 2012 event; the incident in Newlyn formed part of this wider flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred across Cornwall during the late&ndash;November 2012 event; widespread elevated river levels and saturated ground contributed to flooding in the area. [TAB,PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred across Cornwall during the event; at least six properties flooded internally. High groundwater, saturated soils and elevated river levels contributed to widespread flooding. [PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River water discharged from a culvert onto the road and then into rear gardens of a terrace of houses in Trenear, causing internal flooding of properties. [TAB,PAG] (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>260 properties [MUL] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties (1 commercial, 4 residential) [PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>five or more properties flooded internally (in Millbrook) [TAB,PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>five or more properties flooded internally (in Newlyn) [TAB,PAG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Cornwall,England,"Heavy and prolonged rainfall, together with storm surge and large swell at times, caused surface water, fluvial and coastal/tidal flooding across the county. Roads and properties were flooded (properties specifically reported in Bugle, St Austell, Penzance, Camborne and Redruth); sea defences were badly damaged at Long Rock; coastal flooding affected Looe, Mevagissey, Fowey and other settlements; tidal flood gates were shut in places (e.g. Truro, Polperro). [MUL] (p1)
Widespread flooding across the county: coastal overtopping and wave–driven flooding of properties on the south coast when spring tides coincided with low pressure and strong south–easterly winds; widespread river, surface water and groundwater–related flooding during the late–December rainfall event (starting 18 Dec and lasting ~2 weeks) affecting many of the same properties flooded in November. [PAG] (p2)
Flooding occurred across Cornwall during the late–November 2012 event. [TAB,PAG] (p5)
Widespread flooding occurred across Cornwall during the event; the report records internal flooding of properties in Hessenford as part of this event. [PAG] (p7)
Widespread flooding occurred across Cornwall during the late–November 2012 event; the report states flooding occurred across Cornwall. [PAG] (p9)
Widespread flooding occurred across Cornwall during the event; surface water runoff from hillsides and elevated river levels contributed to flooding in the county. [TAB,PAG] (p11)
Flooding occurred across Cornwall during the November 2012 event; the incident in Newlyn formed part of this wider flooding. [TAB,PAG] (p13)
Flooding occurred across Cornwall during the late–November 2012 event; widespread elevated river levels and saturated ground contributed to flooding in the area. [TAB,PAG] (p15)
Flooding occurred across Cornwall during the event; at least six properties flooded internally. High groundwater, saturated soils and elevated river levels contributed to widespread flooding. [PAG] (p17)
River water discharged from a culvert onto the road and then into rear gardens of a terrace of houses in Trenear, causing internal flooding of properties. [TAB,PAG] (p19)","260 properties [MUL] (p1)
5 properties (1 commercial, 4 residential) [PAG] (p7)
five or more properties flooded internally (in Millbrook) [TAB,PAG] (p11)
five or more properties flooded internally (in Newlyn) [TAB,PAG] (p13)",GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.1213173,-5.5329266,"<div id=""html_51da9e9858192d43ad1de7ae72909fff"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Penzance</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding inundated properties during heavy rainfall; coastal flooding and large waves (storm surge / spring tides) caused overtopping/impact on the foreshore and resulted in the promenade being closed. [PAG,MUL] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Large waves associated with the coastal event resulted in the closing of the promenade. (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Penzance,England,"Surface water flooding inundated properties during heavy rainfall; coastal flooding and large waves (storm surge / spring tides) caused overtopping/impact on the foreshore and resulted in the promenade being closed. [PAG,MUL] (p1)
Large waves associated with the coastal event resulted in the closing of the promenade. (p2)",,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.26526,-5.05436,"<div id=""html_366b2be8db7303d8a209cfdfd5eb860a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Truro</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Businesses in Bridge Street were inundated by surface water running off the highway. During the December coastal event tidal flood gates were shut at Truro. [PAG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Tidal flood gates were shut to manage the threat from tidal/coastal flooding during the event. (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Truro,England,"Businesses in Bridge Street were inundated by surface water running off the highway. During the December coastal event tidal flood gates were shut at Truro. [PAG] (p1)
Tidal flood gates were shut to manage the threat from tidal/coastal flooding during the event. (p2)",,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.3916159,-4.3802821,"<div id=""html_4089aa5265160b6bc4a27e37916392bb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hessenford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hessenford was the subject of a Flood Investigation Report following flooding associated with the prolonged rainfall event (22&ndash;27 November 2012), indicating local flooding impacts during that event. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Seaton (Main River) resulted in internal flooding of properties in Ladock. [TAB] (p8)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties (1 commercial, 4 residential) [TAB] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Hessenford,England,"Hessenford was the subject of a Flood Investigation Report following flooding associated with the prolonged rainfall event (22–27 November 2012), indicating local flooding impacts during that event. (p1)
Flooding from the River Seaton (Main River) resulted in internal flooding of properties in Ladock. [TAB] (p8)","5 properties (1 commercial, 4 residential) [TAB] (p8)",GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.3342449,-4.2006531,"<div id=""html_8a13af33e0621467ec6c7211709f8fcb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kingsand</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Kingsand was included in the list of locations with Flood Investigation Reports after the November 2012 prolonged rainfall event, indicating the village experienced flooding during that event. (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Kingsand,England,"Kingsand was included in the list of locations with Flood Investigation Reports after the November 2012 prolonged rainfall event, indicating the village experienced flooding during that event. (p1)",,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.31996756947228,-4.960511311655367,"<div id=""html_044e7140b941a55bf179868682a6539d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ladock</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ladock was identified as a location with a Flood Investigation Report following the November 2012 prolonged rainfall event, indicating local flooding impacts during that period. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Subject of a Flood Investigation Report and included in the December rainfall analysis &mdash; affected by flooding during the late&ndash;December event with elevated river levels and surface water runoff impacting properties. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High river levels caused the Tresillian River to overtop its channel banks (notably in the village hall car park) and the river came out of bank further downstream, causing flooding of a section of the road; river flows combined with surface&ndash;water flows on the main road when the river overtopped. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The river broke out (overtopped) around the road bridge and flowed down the B3275, causing internal flooding to properties on the opposite side of the road to the river. (p29)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>five or more properties flooded internally; at least one property had flooded internally within the previous five years (p29)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Ladock,England,"Ladock was identified as a location with a Flood Investigation Report following the November 2012 prolonged rainfall event, indicating local flooding impacts during that period. (p1)
Subject of a Flood Investigation Report and included in the December rainfall analysis — affected by flooding during the late–December event with elevated river levels and surface water runoff impacting properties. (p2)
High river levels caused the Tresillian River to overtop its channel banks (notably in the village hall car park) and the river came out of bank further downstream, causing flooding of a section of the road; river flows combined with surface–water flows on the main road when the river overtopped. (p9)
The river broke out (overtopped) around the road bridge and flowed down the B3275, causing internal flooding to properties on the opposite side of the road to the river. (p29)",five or more properties flooded internally; at least one property had flooded internally within the previous five years (p29),GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
