GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.10319,-5.27045,"<div id=""html_21c4f2bdbd0f77631a049ec26270a63a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Helston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in the December rainfall/flood investigation analysis &mdash; experienced flooding associated with the late&ndash;December heavy/rainfall event when soils and groundwater were already saturated and river levels elevated, resulting in flooding of properties. (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Helston,England,"Included in the December rainfall/flood investigation analysis — experienced flooding associated with the late–December heavy/rainfall event when soils and groundwater were already saturated and river levels elevated, resulting in flooding of properties. (p2)",,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.40748,-4.6678176,"<div id=""html_2bf1b52ceb7b4c6609f8a4d244cb3be9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lostwithiel</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed in the Flood Investigation Reports and rainfall analysis for the December event &mdash; experienced flooding associated with elevated river levels and heavy rainfall, affecting properties (including ones also flooded in November). (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Lostwithiel,England,"Listed in the Flood Investigation Reports and rainfall analysis for the December event — experienced flooding associated with elevated river levels and heavy rainfall, affecting properties (including ones also flooded in November). (p2)",,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.0839943,-5.5389614,"<div id=""html_469a3264b7a590110aa55a6f2b7b1de3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mousehole</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified in Flood Investigation Reports; as a south&ndash;coast location it was affected by coastal overtopping and large waves (sea&ndash;defence overtopping and flooding of properties) when spring tides coincided with strong winds, and was also included in the December rainfall event impacts. [MUL] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Mousehole,England,"Identified in Flood Investigation Reports; as a south–coast location it was affected by coastal overtopping and large waves (sea–defence overtopping and flooding of properties) when spring tides coincided with strong winds, and was also included in the December rainfall event impacts. [MUL] (p2)",,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.0678647,-5.0796265,"<div id=""html_049ac0dc07e438d652223bec5dc34d11"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Porthallow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Named in the Flood Investigation Reports; as a south&ndash;coast community it was affected by wave and tide&ndash;driven overtopping of sea defences leading to flooding of properties and was included in the December rainfall/flooding impacts. [MUL] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Porthallow,England,Named in the Flood Investigation Reports; as a south–coast community it was affected by wave and tide–driven overtopping of sea defences leading to flooding of properties and was included in the December rainfall/flooding impacts. [MUL] (p2),,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-CON,1,2012-10-17,50.331493,-4.201951,"<div id=""html_53acc991f85bb458b386c9652696f6c6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cawsand</h1><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; 1 shop; 1 pub; 2 residential properties; 1 gig clubhouse (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cornwall,Cawsand,England,,5 properties; 1 shop; 1 pub; 2 residential properties; 1 gig clubhouse (p6),GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc.html,GB-CON_1_2012-10-17_etc,Cornwall flooding 17 Oct 2012 - 22 Dec 2012,Flood Investigation Reports 2012,027/Cornwall/027/2012/Cornwall/flood-investigation-report-2012.pdf
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.734379,-0.34887420081953086,"<div id=""html_5a415c11ca390dc41f5eced0026ffa1c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Albert Dock</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At the height of the tidal surge (peak ~5.8mAOD) sea water entered into Albert Dock over defences and through the lock gates; once the dock rapidly filled this water flowed onwards into the city and contributed to flooding of the city centre. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as the origin/source area for tidal ingress during the event; low defences allowed tidal water to enter the dock area and into local sewer/drainage, contributing to sewer surcharging and downstream flooding impacts. [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Defence levels at Albert Dock are known to be lower than other parts of the city and were a focus during the flood event; temporary and long&ndash;term raising of defences was being considered following the event. The dock was the subject of defence operations during the 5th December tidal/extreme levels. [IMG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Riverside areas of Albert Dock were overwashed by tidal waters; the volume of water grossly exceeded the dock basin's storage capacity and so could not prevent flood flows entering the city. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Tidal surge caused overtopping into the dock, raising dock levels; once the dock filled, flood waters passed from the dock into the city. Investigation found that water entering the dock over low points in the riverside defences far exceeded the amount entering through the lock. The dock provided some informal storage which limited impacts elsewhere but did not prevent significant flooding on the date of the event. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Operational procedures for the lock gates were not fully finalised during the tidal surge; recommendations call for full and final implementation of procedures and consideration of optimising agreements so the dock can provide an informal flood storage role. Defence improvements in the Albert Dock area were identified as a highest priority following the event. [TAB] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The riverside quay at Albert Dock had the lowest defence levels in the city; significant tidal flood waters overwhelmed the dock and flowed through it into adjacent areas (notably English Street). [PAG] (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>43 properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,Albert Dock,England,"At the height of the tidal surge (peak ~5.8mAOD) sea water entered into Albert Dock over defences and through the lock gates; once the dock rapidly filled this water flowed onwards into the city and contributed to flooding of the city centre. (p5)
Identified as the origin/source area for tidal ingress during the event; low defences allowed tidal water to enter the dock area and into local sewer/drainage, contributing to sewer surcharging and downstream flooding impacts. [PAG] (p14)
Defence levels at Albert Dock are known to be lower than other parts of the city and were a focus during the flood event; temporary and long–term raising of defences was being considered following the event. The dock was the subject of defence operations during the 5th December tidal/extreme levels. [IMG] (p17)
Riverside areas of Albert Dock were overwashed by tidal waters; the volume of water grossly exceeded the dock basin's storage capacity and so could not prevent flood flows entering the city. (p19)
Tidal surge caused overtopping into the dock, raising dock levels; once the dock filled, flood waters passed from the dock into the city. Investigation found that water entering the dock over low points in the riverside defences far exceeded the amount entering through the lock. The dock provided some informal storage which limited impacts elsewhere but did not prevent significant flooding on the date of the event. (p21)
Operational procedures for the lock gates were not fully finalised during the tidal surge; recommendations call for full and final implementation of procedures and consideration of optimising agreements so the dock can provide an informal flood storage role. Defence improvements in the Albert Dock area were identified as a highest priority following the event. [TAB] (p22)
The riverside quay at Albert Dock had the lowest defence levels in the city; significant tidal flood waters overwhelmed the dock and flowed through it into adjacent areas (notably English Street). [PAG] (p23)",43 properties (p14),GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.72795300476825,-0.37202713380475244,"<div id=""html_54f3f81b4915a6beaf77f283852e6a5f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>St Andrews Quay Retail Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping and road flooding occurred at the St Andrews Quay retail park during the tidal surge. (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,St Andrews Quay Retail Park,England,Overtopping and road flooding occurred at the St Andrews Quay retail park during the tidal surge. (p6),,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.739037,-0.34491345,"<div id=""html_74c21edb79230143c0945ed4300e26ec"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kingston Retail Park</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater inundated retail properties/commercial premises within the retail park. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood waters flowed through the retail park causing inundation of the retail park car park and surrounding areas; significant cleanup and recovery ongoing. [IMG] (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>13 properties [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,Kingston Retail Park,England,"Floodwater inundated retail properties/commercial premises within the retail park. [TAB] (p7)
Flood waters flowed through the retail park causing inundation of the retail park car park and surrounding areas; significant cleanup and recovery ongoing. [IMG] (p16)",13 properties [TAB] (p7),GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.7377479,-0.3338444,"<div id=""html_7f006d2e9a91afb159a408a8b3b962b5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Victoria Pier</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Victoria Pier sustained significant damage as a result of the tidal/coastal flooding during the event. (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,Victoria Pier,England,Victoria Pier sustained significant damage as a result of the tidal/coastal flooding during the event. (p14),,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.73756525,-0.33768542840347754,"<div id=""html_302a43c44fdbc3e25b3a2cb672387fa3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Humber Quays</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surcharging gullies and evidence of sewer surcharging with accumulated silt and debris; no properties reported threatened but local sewer systems were overwhelmed due to tidal ingress. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,Humber Quays,England,Surcharging gullies and evidence of sewer surcharging with accumulated silt and debris; no properties reported threatened but local sewer systems were overwhelmed due to tidal ingress. (p15),,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.7423739,-0.343203,"<div id=""html_5f3f3322a2651edce2833850667f60b2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Osborne Street Police Station</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Building inundated by floodwater as flood flows reached Osborne Street in the city centre. (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,Osborne Street Police Station,England,Building inundated by floodwater as flood flows reached Osborne Street in the city centre. (p16),,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.7422151,-0.3439202,"<div id=""html_60ca74fd24f0d27842a562f4340e91e9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ibis Hotel</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hotel inundated by floodwater when flood flows reached Osborne Street in the city centre. (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,Ibis Hotel,England,Hotel inundated by floodwater when flood flows reached Osborne Street in the city centre. (p16),,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.7435722,-0.3394758,"<div id=""html_284e4f890a3c39227f8589c8e0aa01ac"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kingston Upon Hull</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Record tidal levels and a positive surge caused seawater ingress into parts of the city (notably English Street), flows spread into the city centre and as far west as Hessle Road; defences limited overtopping but low points (Riverside Quay/Albert Dock) allowed seawater into the dock which then flowed into the city; overall large&ndash;scale tidal flooding impacts across the city. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Tidal inundation (from the Humber tidal source) caused flooding of properties and roads across central and southern parts of Kingston upon Hull including the city centre and docklands; flood flow routes are indicated across the urban area on the map. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding entered the city around the time severe flood warnings were issued (18:56 on 5th December); CCTV recorded deep, fast&ndash;flowing flood waters in the English Street area; riverside defences (e.g. Victoria Dock) showed evidence of overtopping as surge and wind/wave direction changed and forecasts increased. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood flows moved through the city centre, causing severe traffic disruption, inundation of buildings and vehicles, and closure of the A63. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>City defences generally withstood the tidal level; the council opened the Civic control room, set up rest centres and evacuated residents from care homes on Victoria Dock Village and Ferensway. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The city experienced tidal flood threat and impacts on 5 December; defences prevented inundation across vast parts of the city but flood flows did pass into the city where defences were overtopped (including sewer and riverside inundation in parts of the urban area). [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced a tidal surge that produced record tide levels in the city; existing flood defences protected properties but warnings were issued close to the onset of flooding limiting time for emergency deployment. Recommendations include full topographic surveys of all flooded locations, review of incident room activities, and incorporation of model findings into planning and policy. [TAB] (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>115 businesses; 149 residential properties; 19,000 properties protected (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>114 businesses and 149 residential properties (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than 50 residents (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than 19,000 properties [TAB] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,Kingston Upon Hull,England,"Record tidal levels and a positive surge caused seawater ingress into parts of the city (notably English Street), flows spread into the city centre and as far west as Hessle Road; defences limited overtopping but low points (Riverside Quay/Albert Dock) allowed seawater into the dock which then flowed into the city; overall large–scale tidal flooding impacts across the city. (p4)
Tidal inundation (from the Humber tidal source) caused flooding of properties and roads across central and southern parts of Kingston upon Hull including the city centre and docklands; flood flow routes are indicated across the urban area on the map. [IMG] (p8)
Flooding entered the city around the time severe flood warnings were issued (18:56 on 5th December); CCTV recorded deep, fast–flowing flood waters in the English Street area; riverside defences (e.g. Victoria Dock) showed evidence of overtopping as surge and wind/wave direction changed and forecasts increased. (p12)
Flood flows moved through the city centre, causing severe traffic disruption, inundation of buildings and vehicles, and closure of the A63. (p16)
City defences generally withstood the tidal level; the council opened the Civic control room, set up rest centres and evacuated residents from care homes on Victoria Dock Village and Ferensway. (p18)
The city experienced tidal flood threat and impacts on 5 December; defences prevented inundation across vast parts of the city but flood flows did pass into the city where defences were overtopped (including sewer and riverside inundation in parts of the urban area). [PAG] (p19)
Experienced a tidal surge that produced record tide levels in the city; existing flood defences protected properties but warnings were issued close to the onset of flooding limiting time for emergency deployment. Recommendations include full topographic surveys of all flooded locations, review of incident room activities, and incorporation of model findings into planning and policy. [TAB] (p22)","115 businesses; 149 residential properties; 19,000 properties protected (p4)
114 businesses and 149 residential properties (p12)
more than 50 residents (p18)
more than 19,000 properties [TAB] (p22)",GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.74416152052869,-0.3464565014408229,"<div id=""html_74633a68799421032ccbf2bd9629c32f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hull Station</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Located in the city centre within the mapped extent, Hull Paragon Interchange lies within the area where Figure 1 shows concentration of flooded locations and flow routes; the map indicates transport infrastructure in the city centre was within the inundation footprint on 5 December 2013 (interchange may have been affected by flooded roads/flows). [IMG] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,Hull Station,England,"Located in the city centre within the mapped extent, Hull Paragon Interchange lies within the area where Figure 1 shows concentration of flooded locations and flow routes; the map indicates transport infrastructure in the city centre was within the inundation footprint on 5 December 2013 (interchange may have been affected by flooded roads/flows). [IMG] (p8)",,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.7124015,-0.3652257,"<div id=""html_c56bc2472862020130d7f9861bdefcb2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Humber</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The storm surge moved down the East coast into the Humber Estuary and caused tidal flooding in East Yorkshire; resulted in flooding on the north bank (East Riding) and significant flooding on the south bank of the Humber. [PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A tidal surge in the Humber arrived about 30 minutes before the astronomical tide, producing a peak tidal level recorded at 5.8mAOD at Hull which caused significant ingress of seawater into the city (English Street area and city centre) and contributed to widespread flooding. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A tidal surge increased levels in the River Humber, causing overtopping and contributing to flooding across the city's southern boundary; this surge led to overtopping and road flooding at locations including St Andrews Quay retail park and Victoria Dock Village residential area. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Tidal surge from the River Humber was the sole flood source for the event on 5 December 2013, driving tidal inundation into Kingston upon Hull that produced the mapped flooded properties, flooded roads and flood flow routes shown in Figure 1. [IMG,PAG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A tidal surge on 5 December 2026 (initial forecasts 5.5m AOD, later increased by about 400mm) combined with changing wind/wave direction increased surge levels and the risk of overtopping defences, prompted severe flood warnings and consideration of evacuations and led to flooding into Hull. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High sea levels and surge tides on the Humber contributed to overtopping of riverside defences and consequent flooding across the city, leading to inundation of properties and businesses. [PAG] (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Tidal surge/flows in the Humber caused overtopping of defences and contributed to tidal inundation and overwash of riverside areas affecting the city and port facilities. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than 400 properties [PAG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>115 businesses; 149 residential properties (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than 250 properties (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>114 businesses; 149 residential properties (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>114 businesses; 149 residential properties [PAG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,River Humber,England,"The storm surge moved down the East coast into the Humber Estuary and caused tidal flooding in East Yorkshire; resulted in flooding on the north bank (East Riding) and significant flooding on the south bank of the Humber. [PAG] (p4)
A tidal surge in the Humber arrived about 30 minutes before the astronomical tide, producing a peak tidal level recorded at 5.8mAOD at Hull which caused significant ingress of seawater into the city (English Street area and city centre) and contributed to widespread flooding. (p5)
A tidal surge increased levels in the River Humber, causing overtopping and contributing to flooding across the city's southern boundary; this surge led to overtopping and road flooding at locations including St Andrews Quay retail park and Victoria Dock Village residential area. (p6)
Tidal surge from the River Humber was the sole flood source for the event on 5 December 2013, driving tidal inundation into Kingston upon Hull that produced the mapped flooded properties, flooded roads and flood flow routes shown in Figure 1. [IMG,PAG] (p8)
A tidal surge on 5 December 2026 (initial forecasts 5.5m AOD, later increased by about 400mm) combined with changing wind/wave direction increased surge levels and the risk of overtopping defences, prompted severe flood warnings and consideration of evacuations and led to flooding into Hull. (p12)
High sea levels and surge tides on the Humber contributed to overtopping of riverside defences and consequent flooding across the city, leading to inundation of properties and businesses. [PAG] (p13)
Tidal surge/flows in the Humber caused overtopping of defences and contributed to tidal inundation and overwash of riverside areas affecting the city and port facilities. (p19)","more than 400 properties [PAG] (p4)
115 businesses; 149 residential properties (p5)
more than 250 properties (p6)
114 businesses; 149 residential properties (p12)
114 businesses; 149 residential properties [PAG] (p13)",GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.7276262,-0.3706045,"<div id=""html_07f3f338361ce31e05bab67ce96f7bed"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>St Andrews Quay, Kingston Upon Hull</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Defences at St Andrews Quay were at their design limits during the tidal surge and only narrowly avoided overtopping. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater affected the St Andrews Quay area, inundating premises. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced marginal overtopping and spray during the event; waves broke over the defences producing dramatic inundation of the foreshore and contributing to visible inundation in the adjacent Victoria Dock Village (flooded roads, water in gardens). [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping of defences observed along the St Andrews Quay frontage; volumes were minimal and businesses reported no issues. Road gullies in the area took the flows. (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>St Andrews Quay experienced limited tidal flood impacts during the tidal surge; local defences were close to being overwhelmed. (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,"St Andrews Quay, Kingston Upon Hull",England,"Defences at St Andrews Quay were at their design limits during the tidal surge and only narrowly avoided overtopping. (p4)
Floodwater affected the St Andrews Quay area, inundating premises. [TAB] (p7)
Experienced marginal overtopping and spray during the event; waves broke over the defences producing dramatic inundation of the foreshore and contributing to visible inundation in the adjacent Victoria Dock Village (flooded roads, water in gardens). [PAG] (p14)
Overtopping of defences observed along the St Andrews Quay frontage; volumes were minimal and businesses reported no issues. Road gullies in the area took the flows. (p17)
St Andrews Quay experienced limited tidal flood impacts during the tidal surge; local defences were close to being overwhelmed. (p23)",2 properties [TAB] (p7),GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.7367763,-0.3488198,"<div id=""html_6183b41ce8745d7f04fd474208e5bddf"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>English Street, Kingston Upon Hull</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant ingress of flood waters occurred into the English Street area; flows spread into the city centre and reached as far as Hessle Road, causing recorded flood damage associated with the event. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property flooding affecting premises on English Street. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>CCTV records show deep, fast&ndash;flowing flood waters in the English Street area at the time severe flood warnings were issued, indicating flooding entered the street during the surge event. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood flows entered the full extent of the English Street area (including Jackson Street and Lister Street). Flows arrived quickly, reaching depths up to 1.5m in places, causing floating cars, floating heavy debris, pedestrians taking refuge, destruction of a wall, and widespread damage requiring significant clean&ndash;up and recovery. [IMG,PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood flows passed into the central English Street area (water marks were observed), indicating inundation of the street area from flows routed via Porter Street. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The sewerage system in the English Street area was inundated by tidal waters during the event. (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Tidal flood waters passed through the overwhelmed Albert Dock and inundated the English Street area. (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>115 businesses; 149 residential properties (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>24 properties [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>flood levels up to 1.5m [IMG,PAG] (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,"English Street, Kingston Upon Hull",England,"Significant ingress of flood waters occurred into the English Street area; flows spread into the city centre and reached as far as Hessle Road, causing recorded flood damage associated with the event. (p4)
Property flooding affecting premises on English Street. [TAB] (p7)
CCTV records show deep, fast–flowing flood waters in the English Street area at the time severe flood warnings were issued, indicating flooding entered the street during the surge event. (p12)
Flood flows entered the full extent of the English Street area (including Jackson Street and Lister Street). Flows arrived quickly, reaching depths up to 1.5m in places, causing floating cars, floating heavy debris, pedestrians taking refuge, destruction of a wall, and widespread damage requiring significant clean–up and recovery. [IMG,PAG] (p15)
Flood flows passed into the central English Street area (water marks were observed), indicating inundation of the street area from flows routed via Porter Street. [PAG] (p16)
The sewerage system in the English Street area was inundated by tidal waters during the event. (p19)
Tidal flood waters passed through the overwhelmed Albert Dock and inundated the English Street area. (p23)","115 businesses; 149 residential properties (p4)
24 properties [TAB] (p7)
flood levels up to 1.5m [IMG,PAG] (p15)",GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.7365775,-0.3579566,"<div id=""html_fc924cf9dbeae5147e79619f1e4250d9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hessle Road, Kingston Upon Hull</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flows from the tidal surge spread west into the city centre and reached as far as Hessle Road. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected Hessle Road with properties/areas impacted. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood flows spread to Hessle Road and its side streets; this was recorded as the northern extent of the flooding with minimal depths but heavy spray and extensive standing water observed. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood waters passed through to the city centre and Hessle Road (to the west), causing inundation that damaged properties and businesses and caused major travel disruption with large sections of the A63 under tidal flood water. (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than 260 properties and businesses (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,"Hessle Road, Kingston Upon Hull",England,"Flows from the tidal surge spread west into the city centre and reached as far as Hessle Road. (p4)
Flooding affected Hessle Road with properties/areas impacted. [TAB] (p7)
Flood flows spread to Hessle Road and its side streets; this was recorded as the northern extent of the flooding with minimal depths but heavy spray and extensive standing water observed. (p16)
Flood waters passed through to the city centre and Hessle Road (to the west), causing inundation that damaged properties and businesses and caused major travel disruption with large sections of the A63 under tidal flood water. (p23)","5 properties [TAB] (p7)
more than 260 properties and businesses (p23)",GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05.html,GB-KHL_4_2013-12-05,Kingston Upon Hull flooding 05 Dec 2013,Hull City Council Flood Investigation Report: December 2013 City Centre Tidal Surge Flood Event,"064/Kingston upon Hull, City of/TidalSurgeDecember2013.pdf"
GB-KHL,4,2013-12-05,53.7431356,-0.3464102,"<div id=""html_42ea82fb5806f4753ff41194328993be"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Anlaby Road, Kingston Upon Hull</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road flooding from the tidal surge / increased River Humber levels extended to the northerly extreme at Anlaby Road; the road was inundated as part of the wider flood extent moving from the west bank through to the city centre. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Anlaby Road were flooded; Anlaby Road was also part of the area bounded by Walker Street, A63 and Ferensway that experienced widespread flooding. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood flows reached almost to the Anlaby Road / Anne Street / Carr Lane junction, indicating the easterly extent of inundation in the city centre reached close to Anlaby Road. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>more than 250 properties flooded (area&ndash;wide) (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property; also part of an area including Walker Street, A63 and Ferensway that had 50 properties flooded [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kingston upon Hull,"Anlaby Road, Kingston Upon Hull",England,"Road flooding from the tidal surge / increased River Humber levels extended to the northerly extreme at Anlaby Road; the road was inundated as part of the wider flood extent moving from the west bank through to the city centre. (p6)
