Highway flooded with water collecting at the lowest point, reaching depths of up to 0.3m; water flowed through doorways into a nearby commercial property causing flooding to the ground floor and basement. [IMG,PAG] (p26)","1 commercial property [TAB,PAG] (p7)
one commercial property; 0.3m depth [IMG,PAG] (p26)",GB-KEN_4_2015-08-24.html,GB-KEN_4_2015-08-24,Tunbridge Wells flooding 24 Aug 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area On 24th August 2015,063/Kent/Flooding-affecting-Tunbridge-Wells-investigation-24-August-2015.pdf
GB-KEN,4,2015-08-24,51.1249414,0.2618936,"<div id=""html_d4320c6029afeb3f58346389402f7cd3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cumberland Walk, Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Central shopping and pedestrian areas (Nevill Street, The Pantiles, Cumberland Walk, Warwick Park, Market Street) experienced localised flooding and inundation during the event, affecting public spaces and streets. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the Pantiles area affected by surface water ponding during the event; flooding was reported in the wider Pantiles/Nevill Street area. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A piece of concrete was found blocking the public combined sewer lateral leading from Cumberland Walk to a submersible pump at Warwick Park. This blockage reduced sewer capacity for the block of properties between Cumberland Walk, Nevill Park and Warwick Park and contributed to hydraulic overload and surface water / sewer surcharging during the intense rainfall, which led to flooding of properties in the block. (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sewer&ndash;related flooding issues noted at Cumberland Walk: Southern Water to assess the capacity of the submersible pump serving the sewer on Cumberland Walk and to survey the sewer beneath Tunbridge Wells railway station, indicating flooding/surcharging impacts in this location during the event. (p29)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Cumberland Walk, Tunbridge Wells",England,"Central shopping and pedestrian areas (Nevill Street, The Pantiles, Cumberland Walk, Warwick Park, Market Street) experienced localised flooding and inundation during the event, affecting public spaces and streets. (p8)
Part of the Pantiles area affected by surface water ponding during the event; flooding was reported in the wider Pantiles/Nevill Street area. (p15)
A piece of concrete was found blocking the public combined sewer lateral leading from Cumberland Walk to a submersible pump at Warwick Park. This blockage reduced sewer capacity for the block of properties between Cumberland Walk, Nevill Park and Warwick Park and contributed to hydraulic overload and surface water / sewer surcharging during the intense rainfall, which led to flooding of properties in the block. (p17)
Sewer–related flooding issues noted at Cumberland Walk: Southern Water to assess the capacity of the submersible pump serving the sewer on Cumberland Walk and to survey the sewer beneath Tunbridge Wells railway station, indicating flooding/surcharging impacts in this location during the event. (p29)",,GB-KEN_4_2015-08-24.html,GB-KEN_4_2015-08-24,Tunbridge Wells flooding 24 Aug 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area On 24th August 2015,063/Kent/Flooding-affecting-Tunbridge-Wells-investigation-24-August-2015.pdf
GB-KEN,4,2015-08-24,51.1254528,0.2567758,"<div id=""html_68515020478e0553d89d3cc4d17f07e6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Linden Park Road, Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Linden Park Road (at its junction with Sussex Mews) is within the affected low&ndash;lying area identified as high risk of surface water flooding; nearby properties and basements were impacted by floodwater during the event. (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Linden Park Road, Tunbridge Wells",England,Linden Park Road (at its junction with Sussex Mews) is within the affected low–lying area identified as high risk of surface water flooding; nearby properties and basements were impacted by floodwater during the event. (p16),,GB-KEN_4_2015-08-24.html,GB-KEN_4_2015-08-24,Tunbridge Wells flooding 24 Aug 2015,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Tunbridge Wells Area On 24th August 2015,063/Kent/Flooding-affecting-Tunbridge-Wells-investigation-24-August-2015.pdf
GB-KEN,4,2015-08-24,51.1371483,0.2673446,"<div id=""html_07b2e509212bc5acc1eefcf83aca5016"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tunbridge Wells</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Tunbridge Wells area was affected by flooding (report heading states a flood event impacted the area). [PAG] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding on 24 August 2015 that inundated properties and caused disruption to traffic and transportation. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding reported across the Tunbridge Wells area on 24 August 2015: highways and pedestrian areas flooded and impassable; multiple residential and commercial properties internally flooded; railway track flooded and closed until flooding subsided. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple localised incidents of flooding occurred across central Tunbridge Wells on the date of the event, affecting streets, public spaces and transport access in the town centre. [IMG] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localised, intense summer storm produced heavy rainfall over Tunbridge Wells, coinciding with the first reports of flooding received at 17:34 on the day; this caused surface water / flash flooding in the Tunbridge Wells area. [IMG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Central Royal Tunbridge Wells (notably the Pantiles/Nevill Street/Warwick Park area) experienced surface&ndash;water flooding on 24 August 2015, reported in local media with photographs. The area includes low points (e.g. Nevill Street, The Pantiles, Warwick Park, Market Street, Sussex Mews) where floodwater accumulated, and many buildings affected have basements below street level. The uFMfSW map shows these locations as high risk for surface&ndash;water flooding. Existing drainage discharges to the public combined sewer and the area has a history of sewer hydraulic overload (reported at Warwick Park in 2009 and 2012), contributing to flood impacts. [IMG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Public combined sewer capacity was exceeded during the 24 August 2015 event, causing flooding across the town; a concrete blockage in a combined sewer lateral (recovered from the pipe) likely increased the extent of flooding. Internal flooding of properties in the area between Cumberland Walk, Nevill Park and Warwick Park was reported on 13 Aug, 16 Sep and 21 Sep (subsequent events). [MUL] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The central area of Royal Tunbridge Wells (area of interest) experienced surface water flooding risk and localized surface water flooding during the event, with impacts concentrated around London Road and Castle Street. [IMG] (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding of the railway track bed caused by an overflowing manhole; required temporary closure of the Tonbridge to Hastings rail line. [IMG] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 24/08/2015 intense rainfall exceeded drainage capacity across Tunbridge Wells, causing surface water to collect in topographical low points and reach depths sufficient to enter property; combined sewer surcharging occurred at the railway station causing flooding to the track bed and disruption to train services. [PAG] (p28)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (Nevill Street); 2 properties (Market Street); 1 property (Warwick Park); 1 property (Sussex Mews); at least 2 properties (London Road); 1 commercial property (Castle Street); 1 commercial property (Mount Pleasant Road) [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one residential property; two commercial properties [MUL] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>0.15 m (depth of floodwater on the station track bed) [IMG] (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Tunbridge Wells,England,"The Tunbridge Wells area was affected by flooding (report heading states a flood event impacted the area). [PAG] (p1)
Significant flooding on 24 August 2015 that inundated properties and caused disruption to traffic and transportation. (p5)
