On and after 17 January 2014 the High Street was flooded (road and above kerb line) when a flap valve was blocked, causing river water to back up through a nearby gully and flow eastward along the street; water entered basements (notably the Elephant and Castle pub). Parking and movement of temporary defences affected flow paths. The most severe event overnight 06–07 February 2014 caused internal flooding of properties along the High Street for several days. The primary cause included a partial culvert restriction under The Maltings; EA bypass pumping and culvert jetting (from 12 Feb 2014) removed the restriction and halted further flooding. [PAG,MUL] (p21)
