Storm Babet (18–21 Oct 2023) produced heavy rainfall and high river flows in the Dove catchment; part of Derbyshire (Ashbourne) experienced property flooding — 16 properties in west Ashbourne suffered internal flooding. [PAG,IMG] (p4)","16 properties (p3)
16 properties (13 residential, 3 non–residential) [PAG,IMG] (p4)",GB-DBY_5_2023-10-18.html,GB-DBY_5_2023-10-18,Derbyshire flooding 18 Oct 2023 - 21 Oct 2023,Derbyshire County Council Section 19 Investigation Report – Storm Babet 18/10/23 – 21/10/23,034/Derbyshire County/034/2023/Derbyshire County/section-5-dove-catchment-final-storm-babet-dcc-section-19-report.pdf
GB-DBY,5,2023-10-18,53.016778,-1.732231,"<div id=""html_6efa19800113dd20af9d164e4ba0c769"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ashbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties to the west of Ashbourne as a result of Storm Babet / rapid response of Henmore Brook; affected primarily the Almshouses complex on School Lane, properties on Coachmans Close (north of Henmore Brook), and three non&ndash;residential buildings (Oswald's Church Centre hall, Kingdom Hall, and the Bridge Public House on Dig Street). [MUL] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties to the west of Ashbourne due to flooding on Henmore Brook and local surface water; affected buildings include the Almshouses complex (School Lane), residential properties on Coachmans Close, and non&ndash;residential properties including Oswald's Church Centre, Kingdom Hall and the Bridge Public House on Dig Street. [PAG,IMG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in Ashbourne (central area adjacent to Henmore Brook) experienced internal flooding during the event; historic records indicate similar flood extents in 1960 and September 2008. [PAG,IMG] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in Ashbourne were internally flooded during Storm Babet. Flood defences in the locality were overtopped when their design level was exceeded. Non&ndash;residential properties reported flooded included St Oswald's Church Centre (hall), Kingdom Hall and the Bridge Public House on Dig Street. [PAG] (p6)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 properties internally flooded (13 residential, 3 non&ndash;residential). [MUL] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 properties (13 residential, 3 non&ndash;residential) [PAG,IMG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 flood defences overtopped [PAG] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Ashbourne,England,"Internal flooding of properties to the west of Ashbourne as a result of Storm Babet / rapid response of Henmore Brook; affected primarily the Almshouses complex on School Lane, properties on Coachmans Close (north of Henmore Brook), and three non–residential buildings (Oswald's Church Centre hall, Kingdom Hall, and the Bridge Public House on Dig Street). [MUL] (p3)
