GB-DBY,5,2023-10-18,52.869667394936194,-1.6281444382899535,"<div id=""html_8352db6452003b57f3608e608267ea4e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hilton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties in the community during Storm Babet (October 2023). The report text states residential and commercial properties suffered internal flooding; map annotations show flooding concentrated on Uttoxeter Road and Mill Lane. [IMG,PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties in the village during Storm Babet; most flooded homes were west of Hilton Brook on the brook's floodplain. Flood risk maps show affected properties lie in Flood Zone 2 and Flood Zone 3 and have at least low long&ndash;term surface water risk; areas off Main Street have high surface water risk. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties within the Hilton community experienced internal flooding when Hilton Brook overflowed upstream of the village and water flowed onto Uttoxeter Road before reaching the relief channel. Some properties experienced internal depths of almost 1 m; semi&ndash;detached properties in the area are known to flood frequently. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overflow from Hilton Brook (about 600 m upstream of the Uttoxeter Road culvert) caused floodwater to escape the channel, flow into the village along Uttoxeter Road and Mill Lane, and internally flood residential and commercial properties; internal flood depths reached almost 1 m at some properties. Culvert blockage and a weir/sharp bend upstream were reported as contributing factors. [PAG,IMG] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 residential properties; 2 commercial properties (report text); map annotations: 7 homes and 1 business internally flooded on Uttoxeter Road; 1 home internally flooded on Mill Lane (map) [IMG,PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 residential properties and 2 commercial properties [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Five homes and three commercial properties flooded internally; internal flood depth almost 1 m at some properties [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 homes; 3 commercial properties; 7 properties on Uttoxeter Road; 1 home on Mill Lane [PAG,IMG] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Derbyshire,Hilton,England,"Internal flooding of properties in the community during Storm Babet (October 2023). The report text states residential and commercial properties suffered internal flooding; map annotations show flooding concentrated on Uttoxeter Road and Mill Lane. [IMG,PAG] (p9)
Internal flooding of properties in the village during Storm Babet; most flooded homes were west of Hilton Brook on the brook's floodplain. Flood risk maps show affected properties lie in Flood Zone 2 and Flood Zone 3 and have at least low long–term surface water risk; areas off Main Street have high surface water risk. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Properties within the Hilton community experienced internal flooding when Hilton Brook overflowed upstream of the village and water flowed onto Uttoxeter Road before reaching the relief channel. Some properties experienced internal depths of almost 1 m; semi–detached properties in the area are known to flood frequently. [PAG] (p12)
Overflow from Hilton Brook (about 600 m upstream of the Uttoxeter Road culvert) caused floodwater to escape the channel, flow into the village along Uttoxeter Road and Mill Lane, and internally flood residential and commercial properties; internal flood depths reached almost 1 m at some properties. Culvert blockage and a weir/sharp bend upstream were reported as contributing factors. [PAG,IMG] (p13)","4 residential properties; 2 commercial properties (report text); map annotations: 7 homes and 1 business internally flooded on Uttoxeter Road; 1 home internally flooded on Mill Lane (map) [IMG,PAG] (p9)
4 residential properties and 2 commercial properties [PAG,IMG] (p10)
