GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.31713528250995,0.6603129625305648,"<div id=""html_652e5397f37dfda91404def006b03adc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pett Road, Stockbury</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway flooding on Pett Road/Stockbury Valley resulted in stranded vehicles. [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Pett Road, Stockbury",England,Highway flooding on Pett Road/Stockbury Valley resulted in stranded vehicles. [TAB] (p7),,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29.html,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29,Swale flooding 29 May 2018,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Swale Area On 29 May 2018,063/Kent/Flooding-report-affecting-the-Swale-area-of-Kent-on-29-May-2018.pdf
GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.337602,0.7501921,"<div id=""html_8317ec93aad6daa346d191fd9c1fd30c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Canterbury Road, Sittingbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to residential properties. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Kent Police closed Canterbury Road to prevent vehicles from exacerbating flooding by creating bow waves, indicating the road was affected by surface water flooding. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Roadway and adjacent green space at Canterbury Road were inundated by standing surface water that encroached toward nearby properties, impeding vehicle and pedestrian movement. (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Soakaways beneath the green adjacent to the Greenways had reached the end of their design life and did not operate effectively; during the intense rainfall the system overflowed and the public sewer reached capacity, producing above&ndash;ground flooding across the green. (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drainage system was inspected and cleansed after flooding; soakaways serving the system were found to be no longer fully operational and require refurbishment. (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water drainage around Canterbury Road and the Greenways was overwhelmed by the intense rainfall, causing flooding issues on the highway; KCC will explore options to improve drainage there. (p40)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Canterbury Road, Sittingbourne",England,"Internal flooding to residential properties. [TAB] (p7)
Kent Police closed Canterbury Road to prevent vehicles from exacerbating flooding by creating bow waves, indicating the road was affected by surface water flooding. (p21)
Roadway and adjacent green space at Canterbury Road were inundated by standing surface water that encroached toward nearby properties, impeding vehicle and pedestrian movement. (p22)
Soakaways beneath the green adjacent to the Greenways had reached the end of their design life and did not operate effectively; during the intense rainfall the system overflowed and the public sewer reached capacity, producing above–ground flooding across the green. (p24)
Drainage system was inspected and cleansed after flooding; soakaways serving the system were found to be no longer fully operational and require refurbishment. (p38)
Surface water drainage around Canterbury Road and the Greenways was overwhelmed by the intense rainfall, causing flooding issues on the highway; KCC will explore options to improve drainage there. (p40)",6 properties [TAB] (p7),GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29.html,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29,Swale flooding 29 May 2018,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Swale Area On 29 May 2018,063/Kent/Flooding-report-affecting-the-Swale-area-of-Kent-on-29-May-2018.pdf
GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.3393206,0.7566343,"<div id=""html_2235261d2f7a658689f9a0e67f8e1b00"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Coombe Drive, Sittingbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affecting residential properties. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Blocked/compromised road drainage gullies on Coombe Drive, Elm Grove, Farm Crescent and Galena Close were cleaned to restore flow; specific works include gullies cleansed from Lansdown Road, gully outside 58/60 cleansed, and gullies outside No.3 and other local gullies cleared and returned to free flow. (p35)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,"Coombe Drive, Sittingbourne",England,"Flooding affecting residential properties. [TAB] (p7)
