GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.3144088,0.8911894,"<div id=""html_07051559a0518e1258008738cd2704e6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Faversham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected commercial and residential properties on named streets (East Street, Ospringe Street, Preston Avenue, Priory Road). (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood event locations are shown along the corridor toward Faversham and in surrounding areas, indicating localised flooding affecting the town and nearby rural/transport areas. [IMG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced individual or small&ndash;scale surface water flooding during the intense rainfall; highways and topographical lows caused water to collect where drainage was overwhelmed. (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple domestic and commercial properties across the town were flooded due to overwhelmed local drainage and overloaded surface water sewers (locations include Preston Avenue, Priory Road, Ospringe Street and East Street). (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial property; 1 commercial property; 1 property; 1 property (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Faversham,England,"Flooding affected commercial and residential properties on named streets (East Street, Ospringe Street, Preston Avenue, Priory Road). (p8)
