GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.33315720501293,0.7046624909521414,"<div id=""html_efdc162eaf9628202731bf720393299e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Borden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to a residential property on Munsgore Lane. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced localised surface water flooding during the intense rainfall event; runoff and overwhelmed drainage caused small&ndash;scale incidents of flooding in the area. (p32)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Borden,England,"Internal flooding to a residential property on Munsgore Lane. (p8)
Experienced localised surface water flooding during the intense rainfall event; runoff and overwhelmed drainage caused small–scale incidents of flooding in the area. (p32)",1 property (p8),GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29.html,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29,Swale flooding 29 May 2018,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Swale Area On 29 May 2018,063/Kent/Flooding-report-affecting-the-Swale-area-of-Kent-on-29-May-2018.pdf
GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.339737,0.7342319,"<div id=""html_36ea9a68722f5adbb171bce2c8422832"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sittingbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Recorded flood events occurred within and around Sittingbourne, with clustering of events in the urban area and along transport corridors, indicating localised inundation of urban streets and nearby land. [IMG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sittingbourne rain gauge measurements were used to represent rainfall over the nearby Iwade Stream catchment for the 29 May 2018 event; the measured storm intensity was used to estimate the rarity of rainfall that contributed to flooding in the catchment. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Eighteen properties reported flooding during and after the event; flooding reports came from three areas of Sittingbourne. Emergency measures were taken locally (see Canterbury Road closure and assistance to residents). (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Canterbury Road at Snipeshill was inundated with standing water that covered the roadway and extended onto adjacent green spaces and up to the front of residential properties, impeding vehicle and pedestrian movement and posing risk to property. (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intensive rainfall exceeded the capacity of local drainage (soakaways) causing runoff to collect in low points, resulting in road flooding and water entering properties situated lower than the road. [MUL] (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple gullies across Sittingbourne (including Anatase Close, Avenue of Remembrance, Bell Road, Burnup Bank, Brier Road, Canterbury Road, Charlotte Street, Chegworth Gardens, Lansdown Road, London Road and many others) were cleansed and found to be free&ndash;flowing; soakaways were cleaned in some locations. These works were performed as part of the response and recovery after the May 2018 flooding. [TAB] (p35)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall and rapid runoff overwhelmed local drainage and watercourses causing flooding of properties and highways in Sittingbourne; the storm extremity at Sittingbourne was around a 1 in 55 year event. (p40)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 reported occasions (see KCC records) [MUL] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Sittingbourne,England,"Recorded flood events occurred within and around Sittingbourne, with clustering of events in the urban area and along transport corridors, indicating localised inundation of urban streets and nearby land. [IMG] (p9)
Sittingbourne rain gauge measurements were used to represent rainfall over the nearby Iwade Stream catchment for the 29 May 2018 event; the measured storm intensity was used to estimate the rarity of rainfall that contributed to flooding in the catchment. (p11)
Eighteen properties reported flooding during and after the event; flooding reports came from three areas of Sittingbourne. Emergency measures were taken locally (see Canterbury Road closure and assistance to residents). (p21)
Canterbury Road at Snipeshill was inundated with standing water that covered the roadway and extended onto adjacent green spaces and up to the front of residential properties, impeding vehicle and pedestrian movement and posing risk to property. (p22)
Intensive rainfall exceeded the capacity of local drainage (soakaways) causing runoff to collect in low points, resulting in road flooding and water entering properties situated lower than the road. [MUL] (p24)
Multiple gullies across Sittingbourne (including Anatase Close, Avenue of Remembrance, Bell Road, Burnup Bank, Brier Road, Canterbury Road, Charlotte Street, Chegworth Gardens, Lansdown Road, London Road and many others) were cleansed and found to be free–flowing; soakaways were cleaned in some locations. These works were performed as part of the response and recovery after the May 2018 flooding. [TAB] (p35)
Intense rainfall and rapid runoff overwhelmed local drainage and watercourses causing flooding of properties and highways in Sittingbourne; the storm extremity at Sittingbourne was around a 1 in 55 year event. (p40)","18 properties (p21)
6 reported occasions (see KCC records) [MUL] (p24)",GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29.html,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29,Swale flooding 29 May 2018,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Swale Area On 29 May 2018,063/Kent/Flooding-report-affecting-the-Swale-area-of-Kent-on-29-May-2018.pdf
GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.37633317182615,0.7296742913864316,"<div id=""html_54e9c281872ea0cee022a4f04fdb6742"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Iwade</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial (river) flooding from the Iwade Stream caused internal flooding of properties in the village. High river levels rose rapidly during the storm, contributing to out&ndash;of&ndash;bank flow through gardens and onto roads and resulting in internal flooding of properties on Sheerstone Road, Springvale and The Waterway. [IMG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road travel was made difficult by flooding (notably on the A2) with the public diverted onto country lanes; local culverts began to be overwhelmed requiring operational intervention (pumping and screen checks). (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of the village lie within Flood Zone 3 adjacent to the main river and were exposed to flooding when very heavy rainfall in the Iwade catchment on 29 May 2018 generated high flows in the stream that exceeded capacity, causing inundation risk to residential and farmland areas along the watercourse. [IMG] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Village inundated when the Iwade Stream flooded on 29 May 2018; local channel and culvert capacity within the village was exceeded and residents were affected, triggering local reporting and concern. [IMG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Iwade experienced surface water flooding linked to heavy rainfall and high flows in the Iwade Stream; Meadow Brown View and Purple Emperor Grove are given as affected locations within Iwade. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland surface water flow from adjacent fields affected Meadow Brown View and breached a drainage planning condition; the outfall from the Wienerberger site lacked a required flow gauge (later installed in October 2018). (p38)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Iwade experienced flooding from the intense storm runoff that overwhelmed drainage; the Environment Agency and KCC will explore flood risk management opportunities for Iwade. (p40)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 properties; river level rose by approximately 2.0 m; peak 2.18 m [IMG] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Iwade,England,"Fluvial (river) flooding from the Iwade Stream caused internal flooding of properties in the village. High river levels rose rapidly during the storm, contributing to out–of–bank flow through gardens and onto roads and resulting in internal flooding of properties on Sheerstone Road, Springvale and The Waterway. [IMG] (p14)
Road travel was made difficult by flooding (notably on the A2) with the public diverted onto country lanes; local culverts began to be overwhelmed requiring operational intervention (pumping and screen checks). (p15)
Parts of the village lie within Flood Zone 3 adjacent to the main river and were exposed to flooding when very heavy rainfall in the Iwade catchment on 29 May 2018 generated high flows in the stream that exceeded capacity, causing inundation risk to residential and farmland areas along the watercourse. [IMG] (p18)
Village inundated when the Iwade Stream flooded on 29 May 2018; local channel and culvert capacity within the village was exceeded and residents were affected, triggering local reporting and concern. [IMG] (p19)
Parts of Iwade experienced surface water flooding linked to heavy rainfall and high flows in the Iwade Stream; Meadow Brown View and Purple Emperor Grove are given as affected locations within Iwade. (p21)
Overland surface water flow from adjacent fields affected Meadow Brown View and breached a drainage planning condition; the outfall from the Wienerberger site lacked a required flow gauge (later installed in October 2018). (p38)
Iwade experienced flooding from the intense storm runoff that overwhelmed drainage; the Environment Agency and KCC will explore flood risk management opportunities for Iwade. (p40)",11 properties; river level rose by approximately 2.0 m; peak 2.18 m [IMG] (p14),GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29.html,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29,Swale flooding 29 May 2018,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Swale Area On 29 May 2018,063/Kent/Flooding-report-affecting-the-Swale-area-of-Kent-on-29-May-2018.pdf
GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.3378408,0.7582946,"<div id=""html_e9ad9863671ab1db4ed24609943d53b8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Snipeshill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding covered the roadway in Snipeshill with standing water extending onto grassy areas and up to the front of residential properties, visually blocking vehicle and pedestrian passage. [IMG] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected the greenspace; KCC will investigate options to better manage surface water within the greenspace to reduce future flood risk. (p38)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Snipeshill,England,"Flooding covered the roadway in Snipeshill with standing water extending onto grassy areas and up to the front of residential properties, visually blocking vehicle and pedestrian passage. [IMG] (p22)
Surface water flooding affected the greenspace; KCC will investigate options to better manage surface water within the greenspace to reduce future flood risk. (p38)",,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29.html,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29,Swale flooding 29 May 2018,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Swale Area On 29 May 2018,063/Kent/Flooding-report-affecting-the-Swale-area-of-Kent-on-29-May-2018.pdf
GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.3489261,0.6701158,"<div id=""html_064066c5f69df27174a19039401aebf8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Newington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water run&ndash;off and highway flooding caused flooding within the village, inundating properties and local roads; accumulation of surface water in topographical low points on the highway contributed to impacts. [IMG] (p28)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>13 properties [IMG] (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Newington,England,"Surface water run–off and highway flooding caused flooding within the village, inundating properties and local roads; accumulation of surface water in topographical low points on the highway contributed to impacts. [IMG] (p28)",13 properties [IMG] (p28),GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29.html,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29,Swale flooding 29 May 2018,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Swale Area On 29 May 2018,063/Kent/Flooding-report-affecting-the-Swale-area-of-Kent-on-29-May-2018.pdf
GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.32946492650212,0.8037503997873088,"<div id=""html_c967bad8944769b13f9fdbd4d1aefeae"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Teynham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water accumulated in low&ndash;lying parts of the village and surrounding roads, leading to properties being affected; low points cited include the A2 by Frognal Lane, Lower Road near Harry's Road and Honeyball Walk. [IMG] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred on the Lower Road within Teynham where highway drains and a culvert (under the railway) were partially blocked, reducing drainage capacity and contributing to flooding that entered property and stranded a vehicle. (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culvert under the railway line near Lower Road was identified as needing repair after the flooding, indicating the rail infrastructure was affected by the event. (p38)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties [IMG] (p29)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Teynham,England,"Surface water accumulated in low–lying parts of the village and surrounding roads, leading to properties being affected; low points cited include the A2 by Frognal Lane, Lower Road near Harry's Road and Honeyball Walk. [IMG] (p29)
Surface water flooding occurred on the Lower Road within Teynham where highway drains and a culvert (under the railway) were partially blocked, reducing drainage capacity and contributing to flooding that entered property and stranded a vehicle. (p30)
The culvert under the railway line near Lower Road was identified as needing repair after the flooding, indicating the rail infrastructure was affected by the event. (p38)",9 properties [IMG] (p29),GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29.html,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29,Swale flooding 29 May 2018,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Swale Area On 29 May 2018,063/Kent/Flooding-report-affecting-the-Swale-area-of-Kent-on-29-May-2018.pdf
GB-KEN,8,2018-05-29,51.3269895,0.6828742,"<div id=""html_e24fead43034a568d835fdc3bb862db3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oad Street</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Deep ponding occurred at the junction with the A249 when drainage was overwhelmed by rapid runoff from intense rainfall on 29 May 2018, leading to localized inundation at this location. (p32)</p></div></div></body></div>",Kent,Oad Street,England,"Deep ponding occurred at the junction with the A249 when drainage was overwhelmed by rapid runoff from intense rainfall on 29 May 2018, leading to localized inundation at this location. (p32)",,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29.html,GB-KEN_8_2018-05-29,Swale flooding 29 May 2018,Flood Investigation Report: Flooding Affecting the Swale Area On 29 May 2018,063/Kent/Flooding-report-affecting-the-Swale-area-of-Kent-on-29-May-2018.pdf
