GB-CAM,4,2014-08-08,52.2503527,0.0231618,"<div id=""html_5dd2d7c43e1131941f87c5f2b43303a2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oakington Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported as one of the multiple sources that contributed to the August 2014 flooding in Oakington by overwhelming the receiving watercourse and preventing highway drains and local ditches from discharging, contributing to internal and external property flooding. [TAB] (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 to 60 cm (depths reported inside properties); 57 properties flooded internally; approximately 60 additional properties externally flooded [TAB] (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Oakington Brook,England,"Reported as one of the multiple sources that contributed to the August 2014 flooding in Oakington by overwhelming the receiving watercourse and preventing highway drains and local ditches from discharging, contributing to internal and external property flooding. [TAB] (p3)",5 to 60 cm (depths reported inside properties); 57 properties flooded internally; approximately 60 additional properties externally flooded [TAB] (p3),GB-CAM_4_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_4_2014-08-08,Oakington flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: Oakington,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2014/Cambridgeshire County/Flood/Investigation/Oakington/2014.pdf
