The north side of Newcomen Road was flooded by surface water flowing south from Gordon Road, across a public open space and through rear garden gates/fences into rear of dwellings. Water entered properties via rear doors, air bricks and other voids, causing internal flooding and prompting some residents to board up back gates to try to prevent recurrence. (p18)
Surface water flowed south beneath gates and fencing of rear gardens on the north side of Newcomen Road towards the rear of dwellings. Water entered dwellings via rear doors, air bricks and other voids/weaknesses. Standing water increased in the natural valley so lower properties experienced deeper internal flooding. The foul public sewer at the rear of properties on the south side (also accepting roof water) was exceeded; manhole covers were forcibly lifted and strong flows discharged from open manholes, producing overland flow that contributed to water in the back alley. Roof gutters were also reported overtopping, adding to surface runoff. [PAG] (p19)
Overland/surface water flow from the north entering rear gardens; residents have installed improvised barriers (plastic sheeting, wooden planks, bricks) at the base of walls/gates to block or divert water from entering rear gardens. There is also a significant build–up of fallen leaves that could affect drainage at the carriageway channel, increasing risk of surface water run–off into properties. [IMG,PAG] (p38)
Overland water flow from the north entering rear gardens; residents made attempts to prevent water entering rear gardens. Significant build–up of fallen leaves along the carriageway channel noted, which could impair gully/road drainage and exacerbate surface water runoff into properties' rear gardens. [PAG] (p39)","more than five buildings (p6)
more than five buildings (p8)
250mm (assumed to reach electrical sockets); 15mm depth in one property [TAB] (p17)
8 properties (on Newcomen Road) reported internal flooding; area total 11 properties flooded internally in Wellingborough (p18)",GB-NNH_19_2020-08-16.html,GB-NNH_19_2020-08-16,Wellingborough flooding 16 Aug 2020,"Flood Investigation Report: Newcomen Road, Wellingborough, 16th August 2020","090/North Northamptonshire/Flood Investigation Report - Newcomen Road, Wellingborough.pdf"
GB-NNH,19,2020-08-16,52.3032295,-0.6840371,"<div id=""html_0ad9aa5c4e0597e1156591795e0b9370"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Winstanley Road, Wellingborough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sewer flooding to external areas of a property on Winstanley Road. [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowed from higher rear gardens and the back alley under the rear gate and into the rear of the property causing water entry via a rear air brick and French windows; external water level reached above the French doors and caused internal seepage onto carpet. [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At the rear of Winstanley Road, surface water flowing off rear gardens and roofs of Newcomen Road into the back alley exceeded gullies; water flowed under the gate and into the rear garden of an affected property on Winstanley Road. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>375mm above French doors [TAB] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Winstanley Road, Wellingborough",England,"Sewer flooding to external areas of a property on Winstanley Road. [TAB] (p11)
