GB-CAM,15,2020-12-23,52.2898575,-0.2508088,"<div id=""html_9e108bacc88c6efc254b58f7d9c01370"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lucks Lane, Buckden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Attenuation pond at Lucks Lane Estate recorded a high water level. [TAB] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Lucks Lane, Buckden",England,Attenuation pond at Lucks Lane Estate recorded a high water level. [TAB] (p9),,GB-CAM_15_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_15_2020-12-23,Buckden flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Buckden,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Buckden-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,15,2020-12-23,52.2916248,-0.2513343,"<div id=""html_32b73700bc3313c255ee3de2a482ba51"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Glebe Lane, Buckden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding with significant flow to these roads/areas. (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Glebe Lane, Buckden",England,Surface water flooding with significant flow to these roads/areas. (p11),,GB-CAM_15_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_15_2020-12-23,Buckden flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Buckden,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Buckden-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,15,2020-12-23,52.2965726,-0.2517051618876153,"<div id=""html_73f24b7772f7d4cbd17c81c34d778b91"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Buckden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>LLFA received 15 flood reports for Buckden; community reported eight properties flooded internally and additional external flooding to gardens/garages/outbuildings; Parish and District Council communications indicate more widespread flooding across the parish. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Town&ndash;wide impacts from surface water when watercourses exceeded capacity and from overwhelmed sewer infrastructure (foul water backup); road and transport disruption including a flooded northern underpass beneath the A1 and the A1 being impassable for several hours; loss of access/egress for some flood&ndash;resilient properties (e.g., near Buckden Marina); flooding of amenity land and high water at an attenuation pond. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred when watercourses exceeded channel capacity; Anglian Water assets were overwhelmed with floodwater entering sewers causing foul backups; the northern underpass beneath the A1 was flooded and the road between Buckden Marina and the level crossing was flooded, cutting off an exit from the village; the A1 flooded and was impassable for some hours. [TAB,PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Buckden experienced flooding driven by surface&ndash;water runoff, including from an underpass and contributions from the A1 carriageway. This prompted community engagement and interventions (gully cleansing, highway drainage improvements at High Street, riparian and watercourse maintenance) aimed at alleviation. The report notes no reports of residents needing to leave their properties. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 23 December 2020 a prolonged period of higher&ndash;than&ndash;average rainfall across Autumn 2020 followed by intense rainfall produced rapid runoff that caused significant overland surface water flooding and flooding from drainage systems which exceeded capacity. Flooding overwhelmed highway drainage and prompted actions including highway surface water drainage improvements (installation commenced February 2022) and measures to uphold riparian maintenance; further upstream flood&ndash;alleviation options near Taylor's Lane are being considered. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 flood reports; 8 properties (internal) (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>c.23 properties (total reported in parish table) [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Properties internally up to a depth of 60cm (Taylors Lane and High Street); Gardens up to a depth of 91cm (Taylors Lane); 1 northern underpass flooded [TAB,PAG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Buckden,England,"LLFA received 15 flood reports for Buckden; community reported eight properties flooded internally and additional external flooding to gardens/garages/outbuildings; Parish and District Council communications indicate more widespread flooding across the parish. (p8)
Town–wide impacts from surface water when watercourses exceeded capacity and from overwhelmed sewer infrastructure (foul water backup); road and transport disruption including a flooded northern underpass beneath the A1 and the A1 being impassable for several hours; loss of access/egress for some flood–resilient properties (e.g., near Buckden Marina); flooding of amenity land and high water at an attenuation pond. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Surface water flooding occurred when watercourses exceeded channel capacity; Anglian Water assets were overwhelmed with floodwater entering sewers causing foul backups; the northern underpass beneath the A1 was flooded and the road between Buckden Marina and the level crossing was flooded, cutting off an exit from the village; the A1 flooded and was impassable for some hours. [TAB,PAG] (p11)
Buckden experienced flooding driven by surface–water runoff, including from an underpass and contributions from the A1 carriageway. This prompted community engagement and interventions (gully cleansing, highway drainage improvements at High Street, riparian and watercourse maintenance) aimed at alleviation. The report notes no reports of residents needing to leave their properties. (p12)
On 23 December 2020 a prolonged period of higher–than–average rainfall across Autumn 2020 followed by intense rainfall produced rapid runoff that caused significant overland surface water flooding and flooding from drainage systems which exceeded capacity. Flooding overwhelmed highway drainage and prompted actions including highway surface water drainage improvements (installation commenced February 2022) and measures to uphold riparian maintenance; further upstream flood–alleviation options near Taylor's Lane are being considered. (p16)","15 flood reports; 8 properties (internal) (p8)
c.23 properties (total reported in parish table) [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Properties internally up to a depth of 60cm (Taylors Lane and High Street); Gardens up to a depth of 91cm (Taylors Lane); 1 northern underpass flooded [TAB,PAG] (p11)",GB-CAM_15_2020-12-23.html,GB-CAM_15_2020-12-23,Buckden flooding 23 Dec 2020,Flood Investigation Report: Buckden,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Buckden-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-HRT,2,2016-06-23,51.7507439,-0.2230785,"<div id=""html_5416cb55a71275f3e54857c1013e9116"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oxleys Wood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The ordinary watercourse emerging from Oxleys Wood was identified as playing an important role in the localized flooding on 23rd June 2016, contributing runoff that flowed down the highway and towards downstream properties; culverted sections of this watercourse were noted as relevant to flow paths. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Hertfordshire,Oxleys Wood,England,"The ordinary watercourse emerging from Oxleys Wood was identified as playing an important role in the localized flooding on 23rd June 2016, contributing runoff that flowed down the highway and towards downstream properties; culverted sections of this watercourse were noted as relevant to flow paths. (p12)",,GB-HRT_2_2016-06-23.html,GB-HRT_2_2016-06-23,Hatfield flooding 23 Jun 2016,"Section 19 Flood Investigation: Deerswood Avenue, Hatfield",056/Hertfordshire/deerswood-avenue-hatfield-flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-HRT,2,2016-06-23,51.7517962,-0.2239504,"<div id=""html_8be1af4365be3e8acf0880c1ccc4f4a7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Deerswood Avenue, Hatfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from intense rainfall pooled on the road around residences and entered living areas; internal flooding of property occurred. Highway drainage could not cope with the scale of the rainfall; no evidence ordinary watercourse or surface water sewers were surcharged. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from the road entered property on Deerswood Avenue, causing dampened carpets in the living area and water to enter the garden. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties experienced flooding during the event when water came onto the road and entered from the road/front of properties rather than from the rear; Environment Agency hazard rating for properties on Deerswood Avenue is reported as between 1.25 and 2.00 ('Significant'). [IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A localized, intense thunderstorm passed directly over Deerswood Avenue at about 18:15 on 23 June 2016, producing very high short&ndash;duration rainfall that caused rapid surface&ndash;water/flash flooding on the street associated with the incident. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water (overland) flow from the road ran downhill into the lower&ndash;lying properties, causing those properties to flood; the road acted as the source of the floodwater. (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property reported dampened carpets; garden flooded to 6 inches (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Hertfordshire,"Deerswood Avenue, Hatfield",England,"Surface water runoff from intense rainfall pooled on the road around residences and entered living areas; internal flooding of property occurred. Highway drainage could not cope with the scale of the rainfall; no evidence ordinary watercourse or surface water sewers were surcharged. (p1)
Floodwater from the road entered property on Deerswood Avenue, causing dampened carpets in the living area and water to enter the garden. (p4)
Properties experienced flooding during the event when water came onto the road and entered from the road/front of properties rather than from the rear; Environment Agency hazard rating for properties on Deerswood Avenue is reported as between 1.25 and 2.00 ('Significant'). [IMG] (p6)
A localized, intense thunderstorm passed directly over Deerswood Avenue at about 18:15 on 23 June 2016, producing very high short–duration rainfall that caused rapid surface–water/flash flooding on the street associated with the incident. (p7)
Surface water (overland) flow from the road ran downhill into the lower–lying properties, causing those properties to flood; the road acted as the source of the floodwater. (p9)","1 property (p1)
1 property reported dampened carpets; garden flooded to 6 inches (p4)",GB-HRT_2_2016-06-23.html,GB-HRT_2_2016-06-23,Hatfield flooding 23 Jun 2016,"Section 19 Flood Investigation: Deerswood Avenue, Hatfield",056/Hertfordshire/deerswood-avenue-hatfield-flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-HRT,2,2016-06-23,51.7541867,-0.2245415,"<div id=""html_7bdec61e0daecefc3477712c61e5db33"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Primrose Close, Hatfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A resident letter describes the stream running in culvert between Foxglove Close and Primrose Close; the culverted stream was implicated in the localised flooding that affected properties in the Primrose Close area on 23rd June 2016. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Hertfordshire,"Primrose Close, Hatfield",England,A resident letter describes the stream running in culvert between Foxglove Close and Primrose Close; the culverted stream was implicated in the localised flooding that affected properties in the Primrose Close area on 23rd June 2016. (p12),,GB-HRT_2_2016-06-23.html,GB-HRT_2_2016-06-23,Hatfield flooding 23 Jun 2016,"Section 19 Flood Investigation: Deerswood Avenue, Hatfield",056/Hertfordshire/deerswood-avenue-hatfield-flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-HRT,2,2016-06-23,51.7542607,-0.2227449,"<div id=""html_f7749670cfcdb62dd8ed4a6ada4024a3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Foxglove Close, Hatfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culverted section of the stream located between Foxglove Close and Primrose Close was cited by a resident and is implicated in the localised flooding that occurred on 23rd June 2016; uncertainty over the culvert route was noted as relevant to flood flow. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Hertfordshire,"Foxglove Close, Hatfield",England,The culverted section of the stream located between Foxglove Close and Primrose Close was cited by a resident and is implicated in the localised flooding that occurred on 23rd June 2016; uncertainty over the culvert route was noted as relevant to flood flow. (p12),,GB-HRT_2_2016-06-23.html,GB-HRT_2_2016-06-23,Hatfield flooding 23 Jun 2016,"Section 19 Flood Investigation: Deerswood Avenue, Hatfield",056/Hertfordshire/deerswood-avenue-hatfield-flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-HRT,2,2016-06-23,51.840052299999996,-0.09785519224523963,"<div id=""html_cb8902ff82d0e49b1c45856b6fdbab24"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hertfordshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At least one residential property reported internal flooding (dampened living room carpets) and garden inundation to a depth of about 6 inches; flooding was reported as originating from the road. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 questionnaire return reporting internal dampened carpets; 6 inches of water in the garden (p3)</p></div></div></body></div>",Hertfordshire,Hertfordshire,England,At least one residential property reported internal flooding (dampened living room carpets) and garden inundation to a depth of about 6 inches; flooding was reported as originating from the road. (p3),1 questionnaire return reporting internal dampened carpets; 6 inches of water in the garden (p3),GB-HRT_2_2016-06-23.html,GB-HRT_2_2016-06-23,Hatfield flooding 23 Jun 2016,"Section 19 Flood Investigation: Deerswood Avenue, Hatfield",056/Hertfordshire/deerswood-avenue-hatfield-flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-HRT,2,2016-06-23,51.7634675,-0.2258741,"<div id=""html_915e42c9e5a17e5cd71bd3cdbb0598e9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hatfield</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road&ndash;surface water runoff pooled around residences and caused ingress into living areas; at least one property flooded internally. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At least one property on Deerswood Avenue (in Hatfield) experienced surface water flooding on 23 June 2016 &mdash; dampened carpets and gardens flooded to 6 inches; flooding was reported to have come from the road. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localised surface water / flash flooding occurred during the intense thunderstorm on 23 June 2016, producing rapid runoff and reports of floodwater entering streets and properties (for example in Deerswood Avenue). [IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hatfield experienced very intense, localised rainfall at about 18:15 on 23 June 2016 (estimated on the radar map to be within the high&ndash;intensity band). This extreme short&ndash;duration rainfall coincided with the incident and is associated with localised surface&ndash;water/flash flooding in parts of Hatfield. [IMG] (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p4)</p></div></div></body></div>",Hertfordshire,Hatfield,England,"Road–surface water runoff pooled around residences and caused ingress into living areas; at least one property flooded internally. (p1)
At least one property on Deerswood Avenue (in Hatfield) experienced surface water flooding on 23 June 2016 — dampened carpets and gardens flooded to 6 inches; flooding was reported to have come from the road. (p4)
