GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,53.8662412,-1.1938294,"<div id=""html_bcbcea00dbed95df9bea4f3cb71908f4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oxton Lane, Bolton Percy</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Oxton Lane (Oxton) was recorded among roads affected by flooding and subject to disruption/closures during the February storms in Selby District. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Oxton Lane, Bolton Percy",England,Oxton Lane (Oxton) was recorded among roads affected by flooding and subject to disruption/closures during the February storms in Selby District. (p33),,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,53.854089,-1.2153869,"<div id=""html_11ef358f803ba43b412340675950454e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>New Road, Ulleskelf</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>New Road (reported with Raw Lane) was affected by flooding and suffered closures/disruption as part of the Selby District impacts from the February storms. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"New Road, Ulleskelf",England,New Road (reported with Raw Lane) was affected by flooding and suffered closures/disruption as part of the Selby District impacts from the February storms. (p33),,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,53.8624757,-1.1297603,"<div id=""html_a09236dcd8be4bb942e09d8cd49f1c8a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Back Lane, Acaster Selby</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Back Lane in Acaster Selby was reported as being affected by floodwater and included in the list of roads disrupted by the February storms. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Back Lane, Acaster Selby",England,Back Lane in Acaster Selby was reported as being affected by floodwater and included in the list of roads disrupted by the February storms. (p33),,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,53.8339595,-1.1205035,"<div id=""html_87338e8d959b8f7519297d90c23fea9c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church End, Cawood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road closures due to flooding as part of the Cawood to Marsh Lane / Wistow affected stretch. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Church End, Cawood",England,Road closures due to flooding as part of the Cawood to Marsh Lane / Wistow affected stretch. (p33),,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,53.8055412,-1.0786805,"<div id=""html_49f8babb1283ea21d404d83ab928c055"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wistow, North Yorkshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road closures due to flooding (included in the Cawood to Marsh Lane / Wistow stretch affected by the storms). (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Wistow, North Yorkshire",England,Road closures due to flooding (included in the Cawood to Marsh Lane / Wistow stretch affected by the storms). (p33),,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,54.2213665,-1.6595285,"<div id=""html_777fe3f05e4d55e009e5f9d3f6e6f085"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Red Lane, Masham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Swinney Beck breached through the residents' garden at 27 Red Lane and floodwater flowed down Red Lane, inundating the roadway and affecting adjacent properties; NYCC highways committed to clearing the highway drains along Red Lane. (p40)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Red Lane, Masham",England,"Swinney Beck breached through the residents' garden at 27 Red Lane and floodwater flowed down Red Lane, inundating the roadway and affecting adjacent properties; NYCC highways committed to clearing the highway drains along Red Lane. (p40)",,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,54.2218927,-1.6581368,"<div id=""html_03efb6d9b7f3b7718b84c40e162dafd7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Park Square, Masham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from Swinney Beck flowed down Park Square as part of the route through the town. (p40)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Park Square, Masham",England,Floodwater from Swinney Beck flowed down Park Square as part of the route through the town. (p40),,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,54.2219789008833,-1.6575086110947266,"<div id=""html_dfa322fbfeef2dca943d040fdf973190"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church Street, Masham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood flow tracked down Church Street as the exceedance from Swinney Beck moved through the town, overwhelming road drainage. (p40)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Church Street, Masham",England,"Flood flow tracked down Church Street as the exceedance from Swinney Beck moved through the town, overwhelming road drainage. (p40)",,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,54.2235342,-1.6574448,"<div id=""html_013dcd0d142f1c9f4a616d19acd66d6a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Silver Street, Masham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed into Silver Street, reaching a low point near Beavers' butchers; NYCC highways undertook drain clearing in the town including Silver Street. (p40)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Silver Street, Masham",England,"Floodwater flowed into Silver Street, reaching a low point near Beavers' butchers; NYCC highways undertook drain clearing in the town including Silver Street. (p40)",,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,54.2261031,-1.6901798,"<div id=""html_a241c31fdf8eabaec7525083087d0056"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fearby Road, Masham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road gullies and drains at the Fearby Road end were affected during the February rainfall event; NYCC committed to cleansing the drains there as part of reactive highway maintenance to restore drainage after Swinney Beck overtopped and flow exceedance tracked down roads. (p40)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Fearby Road, Masham",England,Road gullies and drains at the Fearby Road end were affected during the February rainfall event; NYCC committed to cleansing the drains there as part of reactive highway maintenance to restore drainage after Swinney Beck overtopped and flow exceedance tracked down roads. (p40),,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,53.70731499378462,-1.0495469979329788,"<div id=""html_d79101e5bf795c0820eb3cad03af9b49"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hirst Road, West Bank</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>An unauthorised impermeable membrane&ndash;and&ndash;rubble bund (makeshift defence) was constructed along Hurst Road at West Bank and held back river floodwater. Once holding water it introduced a residual risk of breach and posed significant risk to life and property; the defence was retained and reinforced where practicable to minimise that risk. Local tensions arose with claims the bund may have exacerbated flooding to properties on the opposite side of the river. (p45)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,"Hirst Road, West Bank",England,An unauthorised impermeable membrane–and–rubble bund (makeshift defence) was constructed along Hurst Road at West Bank and held back river floodwater. Once holding water it introduced a residual risk of breach and posed significant risk to life and property; the defence was retained and reinforced where practicable to minimise that risk. Local tensions arose with claims the bund may have exacerbated flooding to properties on the opposite side of the river. (p45),,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,53.785097,-1.0990407,"<div id=""html_810d17a6b331ad86af71cf99f12fcb35"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Selby District</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Selby district was affected by the February 2020 flooding events described in the report. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Lower Aire area within Selby District experienced river flooding during February 2020; flooding affected the Hirst Road corridor between the A19 at Chapel Haddlesey and Carlton Bridge, impacting the local transport corridor and communities. [IMG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Aire running through Selby district showed significant peaks during February 2020; monitoring sites within the district recorded monthly or record highs (examples: Chapel Haddesely 3.43 m, Beal Weir 4.1 m, Birkin Westholme Washlands 5.4 m on 25 Feb), contributing to elevated flood conditions across the district. (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to residential properties (18 properties recorded) concentrated around Hirst Courtney, Carlton and Acaster; widespread flooding affected farming assets, roads and bridges; collapse/damage to a flood bank at Temple Hirst requiring immediate EA emergency repairs on 20 Feb; railway embankment damage at Hirst Courtney/West Banks caused single&ndash;track operations and risk to fuel deliveries to Drax Power Station; emergency services responded to vehicle rescues and pumping operations. (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the Selby district were flooded during February 2020. (p49)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>27 properties (p49)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Selby District,England,"Selby district was affected by the February 2020 flooding events described in the report. (p1)
The Lower Aire area within Selby District experienced river flooding during February 2020; flooding affected the Hirst Road corridor between the A19 at Chapel Haddlesey and Carlton Bridge, impacting the local transport corridor and communities. [IMG] (p11)
The River Aire running through Selby district showed significant peaks during February 2020; monitoring sites within the district recorded monthly or record highs (examples: Chapel Haddesely 3.43 m, Beal Weir 4.1 m, Birkin Westholme Washlands 5.4 m on 25 Feb), contributing to elevated flood conditions across the district. (p28)
Internal flooding to residential properties (18 properties recorded) concentrated around Hirst Courtney, Carlton and Acaster; widespread flooding affected farming assets, roads and bridges; collapse/damage to a flood bank at Temple Hirst requiring immediate EA emergency repairs on 20 Feb; railway embankment damage at Hirst Courtney/West Banks caused single–track operations and risk to fuel deliveries to Drax Power Station; emergency services responded to vehicle rescues and pumping operations. (p33)
Properties in the Selby district were flooded during February 2020. (p49)","18 properties (p33)
27 properties (p49)",GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,54.2504584,-1.4368783,"<div id=""html_3bd95e8d5f57d06e9cf06569e425f385"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hambleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hambleton district was affected by the February 2020 flooding events described in the report. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Incidents in Hambleton mainly related to individual properties and to significant infrastructure: the A684 at Morton Flats and Dalton Bridge near the Dalton industrial estate were affected; NYCC undertook further work on two infrastructure projects following the flooding. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Storm&ndash;related rainfall and River Swale overtopping caused repeated road and bridge closures across the district (A684 at Morton and Swale closed including the bridge over the River Swale); road closures at Scruton (13 Feb) and York Bridge at Tollerton; further carriageway flooding and closures on 23 Feb and wide&ndash;spread road closures on 26 Feb (Bedale Road, Hunton, Eldmire Lane, Dalton, Kirby Wiske, Helperby to Myton on Swale, Crakehill, Swainby to Osmotherley, Sandy Field Lane Holme on Swale). Reports of property flooding in Great Langton and severe disruption to the industrial estate at Dalton due to closure of Dalton bridge. [MUL] (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 infrastructure locations (A684 at Morton Flats; Dalton Bridge) (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Hambleton,England,"Hambleton district was affected by the February 2020 flooding events described in the report. (p1)
Incidents in Hambleton mainly related to individual properties and to significant infrastructure: the A684 at Morton Flats and Dalton Bridge near the Dalton industrial estate were affected; NYCC undertook further work on two infrastructure projects following the flooding. (p11)
Storm–related rainfall and River Swale overtopping caused repeated road and bridge closures across the district (A684 at Morton and Swale closed including the bridge over the River Swale); road closures at Scruton (13 Feb) and York Bridge at Tollerton; further carriageway flooding and closures on 23 Feb and wide–spread road closures on 26 Feb (Bedale Road, Hunton, Eldmire Lane, Dalton, Kirby Wiske, Helperby to Myton on Swale, Crakehill, Swainby to Osmotherley, Sandy Field Lane Holme on Swale). Reports of property flooding in Great Langton and severe disruption to the industrial estate at Dalton due to closure of Dalton bridge. [MUL] (p33)",2 infrastructure locations (A684 at Morton Flats; Dalton Bridge) (p11),GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,54.05375295,-2.1615123808472636,"<div id=""html_c2072da60c7a7bb01befb76e7cce8c32"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Craven</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Craven district was affected by the February 2020 flooding events described in the report. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Gildersleets (in Craven) is recorded as one of the worst&ndash;affected settlements in the district during February 2020 and was the focus of the Section 19 investigation for that area. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Monitoring sites within Craven District on the Ribble and Wharfe showed four significant flow peaks through February linked to Storms Ciara, Dennis and Jorge and the 21 Feb rainfall. Highest&ndash;ever levels were recorded in the district (Ribble at Pennybridge 2.87 m; Wharfe at Netherside Hall 3.91 m) and other monthly peaks occurred. [IMG] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Anecdotal reports and linked media indicate flooding occurred in the Craven area during the February storm period. (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in the Craven district were flooded during February 2020. (p49)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>25 properties (p49)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Craven,England,"Craven district was affected by the February 2020 flooding events described in the report. (p1)
Gildersleets (in Craven) is recorded as one of the worst–affected settlements in the district during February 2020 and was the focus of the Section 19 investigation for that area. (p11)
Monitoring sites within Craven District on the Ribble and Wharfe showed four significant flow peaks through February linked to Storms Ciara, Dennis and Jorge and the 21 Feb rainfall. Highest–ever levels were recorded in the district (Ribble at Pennybridge 2.87 m; Wharfe at Netherside Hall 3.91 m) and other monthly peaks occurred. [IMG] (p27)
Anecdotal reports and linked media indicate flooding occurred in the Craven area during the February storm period. (p32)
Properties in the Craven district were flooded during February 2020. (p49)",25 properties (p49),GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,54.1345328,-1.4986285,"<div id=""html_183d27c51891d3c1a0cd760e2d4d1327"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Yorkshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple river flooding impacts across the county including: properties flooded in Settle, Gargrave, Skipton, Pateley Bridge, Masham and Boroughbridge; washlands around Hirst Courtney reached capacity and overtopped causing flooding to West Bank and Hirst Courtney; Black Drain could not discharge to the River Aire because of high river levels, contributing to flooding; properties flooded mostly along the Hirst Road corridor between the A19 and Carlton. [MUL] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding incidents were recorded across the county during February 2020, affecting communities in the western and southern parts of North Yorkshire. Incidents ranged from isolated property flooding to larger corridor flooding (notably the Lower Aire area). (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Prolonged and repeated rainfall throughout February led to many catchments across the county receiving well above the February long&ndash;term average, producing multiple high&ndash;flow peaks on most rivers and raising flood risk countywide. [IMG] (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Across North Yorkshire multiple rivers recorded significant storm&ndash;driven peaks during February 2020: River Nidd at Pateley Bridge reached a highest&ndash;ever 3.93 m (9 Feb), Bedale Beck at Leeming peaked 4.63 m (9 Feb), River Wiske at Romanby 1.99 m (16 Feb), River Aire sites recorded record or monthly peaks (Roall Dyke 5.95 m; Birkin Westholme 5.4 m; West Bank pond 3.38 m highest on record; Wheelan Dyke 4.59 m highest on record), and Ure and Nidd sites showed pronounced peaks&mdash;these measurements reflect widespread river&ndash;flood impacts across the county during the storm sequence. (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>County&ndash;wide flooding during February 2020: nearly every district reported flooding at some level; repeated and prolonged road closures across the month. [PAG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding incidents were recorded across the western and southern parts of the county in February 2020, with isolated incidents linked to Storms Ciara and Denis and to intense rainfall later in the month; localised flood impacts included overwhelmed ordinary watercourses, exceeded beck capacity and overtopping of the River Aire washlands. (p49)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The report refers to February 2020 flooding across the area (including recommendations to monitor Swinney Beck in Masham and for the Environment Agency to review River Aire flows and washlands), indicating the county experienced river flooding during the February 2020 events and that follow&ndash;up assessments and resilience works were required. (p51)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 25 properties internally flooded (Craven District Council reported); 44 properties internally flooded (Harrogate Borough Council reported); 27 properties internally flooded (Selby District Council reported, mostly along the Hirst Road corridor) [MUL] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 26 separate communities (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3.93 m (River Nidd, Pateley Bridge, 9 Feb); 4.63 m (Bedale Beck Leeming, 9 Feb); 1.99 m (River Wiske Romanby, 16 Feb); 5.95 m (Roall/Roal Dyke); 5.4 m (Birkin Westholme); 3.38 m (West Bank pond, highest on record); 4.59 m (Wheelan Dyke, highest on record) (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>52 roads [PAG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 26 communities (p49)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,North Yorkshire,England,"Multiple river flooding impacts across the county including: properties flooded in Settle, Gargrave, Skipton, Pateley Bridge, Masham and Boroughbridge; washlands around Hirst Courtney reached capacity and overtopped causing flooding to West Bank and Hirst Courtney; Black Drain could not discharge to the River Aire because of high river levels, contributing to flooding; properties flooded mostly along the Hirst Road corridor between the A19 and Carlton. [MUL] (p8)
Flooding incidents were recorded across the county during February 2020, affecting communities in the western and southern parts of North Yorkshire. Incidents ranged from isolated property flooding to larger corridor flooding (notably the Lower Aire area). (p11)
Prolonged and repeated rainfall throughout February led to many catchments across the county receiving well above the February long–term average, producing multiple high–flow peaks on most rivers and raising flood risk countywide. [IMG] (p26)
Across North Yorkshire multiple rivers recorded significant storm–driven peaks during February 2020: River Nidd at Pateley Bridge reached a highest–ever 3.93 m (9 Feb), Bedale Beck at Leeming peaked 4.63 m (9 Feb), River Wiske at Romanby 1.99 m (16 Feb), River Aire sites recorded record or monthly peaks (Roall Dyke 5.95 m; Birkin Westholme 5.4 m; West Bank pond 3.38 m highest on record; Wheelan Dyke 4.59 m highest on record), and Ure and Nidd sites showed pronounced peaks—these measurements reflect widespread river–flood impacts across the county during the storm sequence. (p28)
County–wide flooding during February 2020: nearly every district reported flooding at some level; repeated and prolonged road closures across the month. [PAG] (p30)
Flooding incidents were recorded across the western and southern parts of the county in February 2020, with isolated incidents linked to Storms Ciara and Denis and to intense rainfall later in the month; localised flood impacts included overwhelmed ordinary watercourses, exceeded beck capacity and overtopping of the River Aire washlands. (p49)
The report refers to February 2020 flooding across the area (including recommendations to monitor Swinney Beck in Masham and for the Environment Agency to review River Aire flows and washlands), indicating the county experienced river flooding during the February 2020 events and that follow–up assessments and resilience works were required. (p51)","up to 25 properties internally flooded (Craven District Council reported); 44 properties internally flooded (Harrogate Borough Council reported); 27 properties internally flooded (Selby District Council reported, mostly along the Hirst Road corridor) [MUL] (p8)
over 26 separate communities (p11)
