GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,53.75629964225097,-1.4503907004593726,"<div id=""html_0ec76ebe7d66e2a83c6ee07124fce425"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Woodlesford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced elevated river levels during the February 2020 flood period; modelling in the report indicated that changes in river levels from Leeds extended downstream as far as Woodlesford (approx. 6 km downstream). (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Raised river levels from Leeds extended downstream as far as Woodlesford during the February 2020 flood peaks; Woodlesford marked the downstream limit of the Leeds river&ndash;level influence described in the report. [IMG,PAG] (p54)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Woodlesford,England,"Experienced elevated river levels during the February 2020 flood period; modelling in the report indicated that changes in river levels from Leeds extended downstream as far as Woodlesford (approx. 6 km downstream). (p42)
Raised river levels from Leeds extended downstream as far as Woodlesford during the February 2020 flood peaks; Woodlesford marked the downstream limit of the Leeds river–level influence described in the report. [IMG,PAG] (p54)",,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,53.6922269,-1.0297093,"<div id=""html_e4bb03fca06b8b6afe6c89d11b2ee748"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Snaith</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Snaith experienced flooding on 22, 23 and 24 February 2020 and very high river levels on 25 February 2020 caused by filling of the River Aire floodplains over several days, high tidal levels and significant contributing flows from the River Calder. The appended Leeds FAS briefing concluded there was no indication the Leeds FAS made this flooding worse. [PAG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Snaith experienced flooding with high levels on 25 February 2020 caused by filling of the River Aire floodplains over several days, high tidal levels and significant contributing flows from the River Calder. [IMG,PAG] (p54)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Snaith recorded the main flood peak downstream of Leeds (peak water level around 5.1 m) and then showed tidal fluctuations; the peak was delayed relative to Leeds and Castleford, indicating downstream and tidal influence on flooding. [IMG,PAG] (p55)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Snaith,England,"Snaith experienced flooding on 22, 23 and 24 February 2020 and very high river levels on 25 February 2020 caused by filling of the River Aire floodplains over several days, high tidal levels and significant contributing flows from the River Calder. The appended Leeds FAS briefing concluded there was no indication the Leeds FAS made this flooding worse. [PAG] (p43)
Snaith experienced flooding with high levels on 25 February 2020 caused by filling of the River Aire floodplains over several days, high tidal levels and significant contributing flows from the River Calder. [IMG,PAG] (p54)
Snaith recorded the main flood peak downstream of Leeds (peak water level around 5.1 m) and then showed tidal fluctuations; the peak was delayed relative to Leeds and Castleford, indicating downstream and tidal influence on flooding. [IMG,PAG] (p55)",,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-NYK,3,2020-02-01,53.722353,-1.3512543,"<div id=""html_2787dc79e5185b21bed1b01dd04a4c4d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Castleford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Gauge at Castleford recorded a smooth rise and fall in River Aire levels during 24&ndash;27 Feb (peaking just above 3.2 m). The Castleford record shows no abrupt change corresponding to the Leeds weir operations, indicating the weirs did not noticeably influence downstream flows at Castleford. [IMG,PAG] (p55)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Yorkshire,Castleford,England,"Gauge at Castleford recorded a smooth rise and fall in River Aire levels during 24–27 Feb (peaking just above 3.2 m). The Castleford record shows no abrupt change corresponding to the Leeds weir operations, indicating the weirs did not noticeably influence downstream flows at Castleford. [IMG,PAG] (p55)",,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01.html,GB-NYK_3_2020-02-01,North Yorkshire flooding 01 Feb 2020 - 29 Feb 2020,Flood Investigation Report: February 2020,089/North Yorkshire County/Section 19 Report on the February Flooding Events in the Aire Catch.pdf
GB-LAN,5,2015-12-01,53.7651011,-2.8599762,"<div id=""html_646ac6b7f1d085c63946d79fe93b6a88"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lower Lane, Freckleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a commercial property; external flooding occurred at the location on multiple occasions. EA mapping indicates several surface water flow paths converge at this location. [MUL] (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial property; 6 external flooding incidents [MUL] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Lower Lane, Freckleton",England,Internal flooding of a commercial property; external flooding occurred at the location on multiple occasions. EA mapping indicates several surface water flow paths converge at this location. [MUL] (p13),1 commercial property; 6 external flooding incidents [MUL] (p13),GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01,Fylde flooding December 2015,Fylde District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/fylde-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,5,2015-12-01,53.780561,-2.8893851,"<div id=""html_7158975b52f91968170b9b872d7f81b6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ribby Road, Kirkham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Ribby Road were flooded; residents reported blocked land drains as the main source of the flooding, possibly related to nearby new development. EA mapping identifies a high risk of surface water flooding along Ribby Road. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>6 properties [TAB] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Ribby Road, Kirkham",England,"Properties on Ribby Road were flooded; residents reported blocked land drains as the main source of the flooding, possibly related to nearby new development. EA mapping identifies a high risk of surface water flooding along Ribby Road. [TAB] (p14)",6 properties [TAB] (p14),GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01,Fylde flooding December 2015,Fylde District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/fylde-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,5,2015-12-01,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_d142a5b0bf93364c6bb3d921ee6a749c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding in December 2015 affected communities across Lancashire, exposing deficiencies in communication and coordination and prompting the Lead Local Flood Authority to develop district&ndash;level reports and improve RMA communication. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The December 2015 flood event produced the highest river flows on record and caused widespread impacts across the county &mdash; people, homes and businesses were heavily affected and recovery actions were required. [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme storms and rainfall in November&ndash;December 2015 caused flooding throughout December across Lancashire, damaging private gardens, garages and out&ndash;buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges and retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools and village/town halls. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple communities across the county experienced flooding as a result of two major storm events in December 2015; these communities were identified and included within the countywide investigation. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties flooded in Lancashire [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Significant flooding in December 2015 affected communities across Lancashire, exposing deficiencies in communication and coordination and prompting the Lead Local Flood Authority to develop district–level reports and improve RMA communication. [PAG] (p3)
The December 2015 flood event produced the highest river flows on record and caused widespread impacts across the county — people, homes and businesses were heavily affected and recovery actions were required. [TAB] (p8)
Extreme storms and rainfall in November–December 2015 caused flooding throughout December across Lancashire, damaging private gardens, garages and out–buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges and retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools and village/town halls. (p9)
Multiple communities across the county experienced flooding as a result of two major storm events in December 2015; these communities were identified and included within the countywide investigation. [PAG] (p10)","over 2,500 properties flooded in Lancashire [TAB] (p8)
over 2,500 properties (p9)",GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01,Fylde flooding December 2015,Fylde District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/fylde-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,5,2015-12-01,53.70249,-2.201046,"<div id=""html_52b26f6338ec6d959a4b268382295b35"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rossendale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of Lancashire affected by the December 2015 floods; residents and businesses in the district required recovery support and a multi&ndash;agency drop&ndash;in event was held (Irwell Vale, 10 Feb 2016) to provide information and assistance following the floods. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Rossendale,England,"Part of Lancashire affected by the December 2015 floods; residents and businesses in the district required recovery support and a multi–agency drop–in event was held (Irwell Vale, 10 Feb 2016) to provide information and assistance following the floods. (p9)",,GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01,Fylde flooding December 2015,Fylde District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/fylde-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,5,2015-12-01,53.793356,-2.894251,"<div id=""html_6069d5fc4839c012313485b1e3bfb431"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fylde</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At least one residential property within the district (MSFW332, Kirkham) suffered internal flooding during the December 2015 event. [TAB] (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential property [TAB] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Fylde,England,"At least one residential property within the district (MSFW332, Kirkham) suffered internal flooding during the December 2015 event. [TAB] (p11)",1 residential property [TAB] (p11),GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01,Fylde flooding December 2015,Fylde District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/fylde-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,5,2015-12-01,53.9031969,-2.7762038183560396,"<div id=""html_610205271a91937a215b3b01131dc34b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Garstang</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood basins in Garstang were activated as a preparatory/response action to minimise flood damage during the December 2015 flood event. [TAB] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Garstang,England,Flood basins in Garstang were activated as a preparatory/response action to minimise flood damage during the December 2015 flood event. [TAB] (p8),,GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_5_2015-12-01,Fylde flooding December 2015,Fylde District Flood Report Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/fylde-final-report.pdf
