Linked to flood incident reports FI/14/006 (2014) and referenced in the report as part of the 2014 flooding investigations; actions by LLFA/Highways were taken in response to these incidents. (p8)","depths reported by residents vary from 2 inches internally to 12 inches externally (p5)
2“ internally; 12” externally [TAB] (p6)",GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5627252,0.0845293,"<div id=""html_afe220db8c1bf971831e27b6327f2713"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Gold Street, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal and external flooding with foul (sewer) flooding issues. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Lack of highway gullies and surface water sewer contributed to runoff and local flooding; privately owned dyke behind Gold Street was silted/blocked and was cleared by the LLFA following the flood. [TAB] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Absence of highway gullies and a surface water sewer caused runoff issues and contributed to local flooding during the 2014 event. The privately owned dyke behind Gold Street was silted/blocked and was cleared by CCC as a one&ndash;off following investigation. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Linked to flood incident reports FI/14/074 (2014) and referenced in the report as part of the 2014 flooding investigations; subject to LLFA/Highways follow&ndash;up actions. (p8)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depths reported by residents vary from 2 inches internally to 12 inches externally (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2&#8220; internally; 12&#8221; externally [TAB] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Gold Street, March",England,"Internal and external flooding with foul (sewer) flooding issues. (p5)
