GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5467394,0.0791323,"<div id=""html_20302666652e25bd12795df64d38e301"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ellingham Avenue, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant road flooding; road closed by Police. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Anglian Water investigated and jetted their part of the drainage system through to the recreation ground so it is now working; County Council Highways checked the drainage network (found clear) and confirmed the surface water pumping station is working. [TAB] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drainage system investigations and maintenance carried out after flooding: Anglian Water jetted the system through to the recreation ground; Highways checked the drainage network (clear) and confirmed the surface water pumping station was working. (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depths reported by residents vary from 2 inches internally to 12 inches externally (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Ellingham Avenue, March",England,"Significant road flooding; road closed by Police. (p5)
