GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5625732,0.0686529,"<div id=""html_f13569bf17daba221d54635df3b23ae4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hostmoor Avenue, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal and external flooding of properties. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The drainage ditch near the Beetroot Factory in Hostmoor Avenue was silted and full of rubbish after the flood; Cambridgeshire County Council cleared the ditch as a one&ndash;off after the flooding and enforcement action against the riparian owner is ongoing. [TAB] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drainage features in Hostmoor Avenue (including a lagoon and the drainage ditch next to the beetroot factory) were silted and full of rubbish, contributing to local flooding during the 2014 event. Anglian Water cleared silt from their lagoon and CCC cleared the nearby ditch as a one&ndash;off following the flood. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The drainage ditch near the Beetroot Factory in Hostmoor Avenue was found silted and full of rubbish; Anglian Water cleared the connected system that outfalls into this ditch and Cambridgeshire County Council cleared the ditch as a one&ndash;off to improve the situation. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Anglian Water cleared potential additional silt from their lagoon as part of ongoing maintenance following the flooding incident (FI/14/078). (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depths reported by residents vary from 2&#8220; internally to 12&#8221; externally (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Hostmoor Avenue, March",England,"Internal and external flooding of properties. (p5)
