Drainage features in Hostmoor Avenue (including a lagoon and the drainage ditch next to the beetroot factory) were silted and full of rubbish, contributing to local flooding during the 2014 event. Anglian Water cleared silt from their lagoon and CCC cleared the nearby ditch as a one–off following the flood. [TAB,PAG] (p7)
The drainage ditch near the Beetroot Factory in Hostmoor Avenue was found silted and full of rubbish; Anglian Water cleared the connected system that outfalls into this ditch and Cambridgeshire County Council cleared the ditch as a one–off to improve the situation. (p8)
