GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.546715,0.0985852,"<div id=""html_e2d71dfc4d875bb32619aa1de164a51a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Morton Avenue, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal and external flooding of properties. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water pump in Morton Avenue stopped working as a result of a power cut during the floods; Clarion Housing Group assessed and restored emergency operation and completely replaced the pump (Sept 2015). Subsequent works include a SuDS retrofit and Property Level Resilience (PLR) project scoped for the area with funding submissions made to support long&ndash;term reduction of surface water flooding. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A surface water pump in Morton Avenue stopped working due to a power cut during the August 2014 floods; electrics and emergency operation were restored and the pump was completely replaced (Sept 2015). A SuDS retrofit and Property Level Resilience (PLR) alleviation project was developed and funding bids submitted; Anglian Water later adopted the pump and agreed to maintain SuDS features (Oct 2016). [MUL] (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depths reported by residents vary from 2&#8220; internally to 12&#8221; externally (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Morton Avenue, March",England,"Internal and external flooding of properties. (p5)
Surface water pump in Morton Avenue stopped working as a result of a power cut during the floods; Clarion Housing Group assessed and restored emergency operation and completely replaced the pump (Sept 2015). Subsequent works include a SuDS retrofit and Property Level Resilience (PLR) project scoped for the area with funding submissions made to support long–term reduction of surface water flooding. [TAB] (p7)
A surface water pump in Morton Avenue stopped working due to a power cut during the August 2014 floods; electrics and emergency operation were restored and the pump was completely replaced (Sept 2015). A SuDS retrofit and Property Level Resilience (PLR) alleviation project was developed and funding bids submitted; Anglian Water later adopted the pump and agreed to maintain SuDS features (Oct 2016). [MUL] (p9)",depths reported by residents vary from 2“ internally to 12” externally (p5),GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5440874,0.1127124,"<div id=""html_8ded3d843e13cb50a393f960901c97e1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Upwell Road, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding of the road and adjacent properties. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drainage network was investigated and cleared after blockage that caused local surface&ndash;water flooding issues on the road. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water flooding led to investigation and clearance of the road's drainage system to remove blockages and restore drainage function. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depths reported by residents vary from 2&#8220; internally to 12&#8221; externally. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Upwell Road, March",England,"External flooding of the road and adjacent properties. (p5)
