GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5540986,0.0958363,"<div id=""html_b008c7d242089a0ad21af16f4667cda0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Creek Road, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal and external flooding of properties and the street. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Blocked gullies and lateral drains were cleansed and jetted; a new gully was installed at Belmont Road to restore drainage and reduce future surface&ndash;water flooding. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood&ndash;related blocked gullies and lateral drains were cleansed and jetted and left working; further investigation led to installation of a new gully at nearby Belmont Road to address drainage failures after the August 2014 event. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depths reported by residents vary from 2&#8220; internally to 12&#8221; externally. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Creek Road, March",England,"Internal and external flooding of properties and the street. (p5)
Blocked gullies and lateral drains were cleansed and jetted; a new gully was installed at Belmont Road to restore drainage and reduce future surface–water flooding. [TAB] (p7)
