GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5603002,0.0845957,"<div id=""html_6ec7b580576cff49e2e80abf265c01b7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lime Grove, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal and external flooding of properties and the street. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Anglian Water CCTV&ndash;surveyed the drainage pipes and fitted a non&ndash;return valve to an affected property to prevent sewer/backflow impacts to the property. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>After the August 2014 floods a CCTV survey of drainage pipes was undertaken and a non&ndash;return valve was fitted to an affected property to reduce repeat internal/external flooding. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depths reported by residents vary from 2&#8220; internally to 12&#8221; externally. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Lime Grove, March",England,"Internal and external flooding of properties and the street. (p5)
