GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5495824,0.0671793,"<div id=""html_fda4e7116de577ada1afe71d0c07e2a2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Gaul Road, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal and external flooding of properties and the street; foul (sewer) flooding issues reported. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Gaul Road drainage was affected by silt and blockages during the 2014 event; Anglian Water jetted systems and removed silt and carried out CCTV surveys showing the system running freely; non&ndash;return valves were fitted on some properties; Highways jetted outfalls, carried out patching, raised kerbs and installed two new gullies to improve highway drainage; Fenland District Council cleared the Chase drainage up to Gaul Road. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following flooding in August 2014 drainage systems were jetted and silt removed; CCTV showed the system running freely after works. Non&ndash;return valves were fitted to some properties. After further issues Highways jetted offlets, carried out patching, raised curbs and installed additional gullies to reduce surface water flooding. (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>depths reported by residents vary from 2&#8220; internally to 12&#8221; externally. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Gaul Road, March",England,"Internal and external flooding of properties and the street; foul (sewer) flooding issues reported. (p5)
Gaul Road drainage was affected by silt and blockages during the 2014 event; Anglian Water jetted systems and removed silt and carried out CCTV surveys showing the system running freely; non–return valves were fitted on some properties; Highways jetted outfalls, carried out patching, raised kerbs and installed two new gullies to improve highway drainage; Fenland District Council cleared the Chase drainage up to Gaul Road. [TAB] (p7)
Following flooding in August 2014 drainage systems were jetted and silt removed; CCTV showed the system running freely after works. Non–return valves were fitted to some properties. After further issues Highways jetted offlets, carried out patching, raised curbs and installed additional gullies to reduce surface water flooding. (p10)",depths reported by residents vary from 2“ internally to 12” externally. (p5),GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.551744,0.0946699,"<div id=""html_82b261329da54ffd3b4400e0c1fa09d1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Nene Parade, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Road flooding affecting the street (road flooding reported). (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Short section of erosion/subsidence damage to the bank of the River Nene caused by water pouring off the Nene Parade carriageway; repaired jointly by the County Council and the Middle Level Commissioners. Highways installed extra gullies in low spots to reduce future surface water flowing over the banks into the river. (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Nene Parade, March",England,"Road flooding affecting the street (road flooding reported). (p5)
Short section of erosion/subsidence damage to the bank of the River Nene caused by water pouring off the Nene Parade carriageway; repaired jointly by the County Council and the Middle Level Commissioners. Highways installed extra gullies in low spots to reduce future surface water flowing over the banks into the river. (p7)",,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5438342,0.0751492,"<div id=""html_b185c583703b44780e4f86232c9132e7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brewin Avenue, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding reported (listed among streets affected in the summary). (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drainage investigation found the piped system from Brewin Avenue to Butt Avenue terminates at a filled&ndash;in ditch, limiting outfall capacity and contributing to local drainage/flooding problems. Potential remedial options were identified (divert to existing sewer or pipe across to an A141 ditch via third&ndash;party land) and multi&ndash;agency work was proposed to develop a deliverable scheme. [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Brewin Avenue, March",England,"Flooding reported (listed among streets affected in the summary). (p5)
Drainage investigation found the piped system from Brewin Avenue to Butt Avenue terminates at a filled–in ditch, limiting outfall capacity and contributing to local drainage/flooding problems. Potential remedial options were identified (divert to existing sewer or pipe across to an A141 ditch via third–party land) and multi–agency work was proposed to develop a deliverable scheme. [TAB] (p7)",,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5448896,0.0805534,"<div id=""html_70843389dab03352c25a2ec345c0f1ff"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Burrowmoor Road, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding reported (listed among streets affected in the summary). (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in FI/14/054 flood response: the drainage system on Burrowmoor Road was surveyed and cleaned as part of the response to the 2014 flooding; no faults were found. [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Burrowmoor Road, March",England,"Flooding reported (listed among streets affected in the summary). (p5)
Included in FI/14/054 flood response: the drainage system on Burrowmoor Road was surveyed and cleaned as part of the response to the 2014 flooding; no faults were found. [TAB] (p7)",,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5546207,0.069349,"<div id=""html_0484615dfcf94a7e392d200d37e8296c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fishermans Drive, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding of the street/properties (external flooding reported). (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>In 2014 highway drainage works found a collapsed pipe and a pipe blocked by root infestation; both were cleared and repaired to restore the drainage system. Ongoing root regrowth has led to recurrent blockages requiring repeated clearance and jetting, and further works (e.g. pipe lining) were considered to reduce future flooding risk. (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Fishermans Drive, March",England,"External flooding of the street/properties (external flooding reported). (p5)
In 2014 highway drainage works found a collapsed pipe and a pipe blocked by root infestation; both were cleared and repaired to restore the drainage system. Ongoing root regrowth has led to recurrent blockages requiring repeated clearance and jetting, and further works (e.g. pipe lining) were considered to reduce future flooding risk. (p7)",,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5508146,0.0842738,"<div id=""html_7d65e6fa870a1132fcc233a11df1c794"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West End, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding of the street/properties (external flooding reported). (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"West End, March",England,External flooding of the street/properties (external flooding reported). (p5),,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5581951,0.0911112,"<div id=""html_f3223f51cc173608f8b45d9c1f3fc633"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Queens Street, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding of the street/properties (external flooding reported). (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highways inspected and cleared gullies along Queen Street following the flooding incident; one gully was cleared and flushed to restore drainage. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localised highway drainage flooding issues addressed by Highways Authority: gullies along the road were checked and one gully was cleared and flushed. (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Queens Street, March",England,"External flooding of the street/properties (external flooding reported). (p5)
Highways inspected and cleared gullies along Queen Street following the flooding incident; one gully was cleared and flushed to restore drainage. [TAB] (p7)
Localised highway drainage flooding issues addressed by Highways Authority: gullies along the road were checked and one gully was cleared and flushed. (p8)",,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5434061,0.0786333,"<div id=""html_8790fbf19ec4a00d303d87ab65fbefe4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kingswood Road, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas around Kingswood Road, Birchwood Avenue, Brewin Avenue, Burrowmoor Road and Cherrywood/Cherryholt experienced drainage blockages and failures linked to the 2014 incidents. Blockages near Cherrywood Green were cleared; sections of drainage were found to end at a filled&ndash;in ditch, contributing to local highway and potential property flooding. Partnership options were developed to divert or pipe drainage to alleviate future flood risk. [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Kingswood Road, March",England,"Areas around Kingswood Road, Birchwood Avenue, Brewin Avenue, Burrowmoor Road and Cherrywood/Cherryholt experienced drainage blockages and failures linked to the 2014 incidents. Blockages near Cherrywood Green were cleared; sections of drainage were found to end at a filled–in ditch, contributing to local highway and potential property flooding. Partnership options were developed to divert or pipe drainage to alleviate future flood risk. [TAB] (p7)",,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.55266,0.0927121,"<div id=""html_3c431755bbe6d6bae8ed02690ece6c29"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Belmont Road, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A new highway gully was installed at Belmont Road following investigations into blocked gullies to improve drainage and address surface&ndash;water flooding. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following the August 2014 floods, a new gully was installed at Belmont Road to address blocked drainage contributing to surface water flooding. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Belmont Road, March",England,"A new highway gully was installed at Belmont Road following investigations into blocked gullies to improve drainage and address surface–water flooding. [TAB] (p7)
Following the August 2014 floods, a new gully was installed at Belmont Road to address blocked drainage contributing to surface water flooding. (p10)",,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5475168,0.0828013,"<div id=""html_a757bcc36fde5c53922e92bf0a33c5ec"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>The Chase, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drainage system in the Chase was impacted by blockages related to the August 2014 event; Fenland District Council cleared the drainage they are responsible for (from the access point for the bungalow up to Gaul Road) to restore flow. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Chase area had its drainage system cleared by FDC (from the access point for the bungalow up to Gaul Road) after the 2014 floods; piped systems were cleansed and dye&ndash;traced to their outfall into a riparian ditch, and the riparian&ndash;owned ditch at the outfall was cleared to improve flow. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"The Chase, March",England,"Drainage system in the Chase was impacted by blockages related to the August 2014 event; Fenland District Council cleared the drainage they are responsible for (from the access point for the bungalow up to Gaul Road) to restore flow. [TAB] (p7)
The Chase area had its drainage system cleared by FDC (from the access point for the bungalow up to Gaul Road) after the 2014 floods; piped systems were cleansed and dye–traced to their outfall into a riparian ditch, and the riparian–owned ditch at the outfall was cleared to improve flow. (p10)",,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5363056,0.0883124,"<div id=""html_373d5a4996a8100a71dbb5fcc082d270"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Barker's Lane, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Outfall from the Cavalry Drive drainage system discharges into a riparian ditch/attenuation pond adjacent to Barker's Lane that was in need of maintenance. The riparian ditch was cleared to provide extra capacity in heavy rainfall and project proposals were developed to reduce local flood risk. [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Barker's Lane, March",England,Outfall from the Cavalry Drive drainage system discharges into a riparian ditch/attenuation pond adjacent to Barker's Lane that was in need of maintenance. The riparian ditch was cleared to provide extra capacity in heavy rainfall and project proposals were developed to reduce local flood risk. [TAB] (p7),,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5449191,0.077321,"<div id=""html_fc61fb54c46cf015698ab572d6e0d0d4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cherrywood Green, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A blockage located near Cherrywood Green was cleared and flushed as part of the investigations following the August 2014 flooding; dye testing was used to trace flow to the outfall. [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Cherrywood Green, March",England,A blockage located near Cherrywood Green was cleared and flushed as part of the investigations following the August 2014 flooding; dye testing was used to trace flow to the outfall. [TAB] (p7),,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5286516,0.0368764,"<div id=""html_72fe4998e7a64afd1634324162fec732"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Knight's End Road, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Investigative works commissioned following flood reports; investigation identified a possible break in a pipe potentially contributing to local flooding. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Investigative works were commissioned following flooding&ndash;related reports; a possible break in a drainage pipe was identified. (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Knight's End Road, March",England,"Investigative works commissioned following flood reports; investigation identified a possible break in a pipe potentially contributing to local flooding. [TAB] (p7)
Investigative works were commissioned following flooding–related reports; a possible break in a drainage pipe was identified. (p11)",,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5555285,0.0915605,"<div id=""html_c0176261aba4ea59001273f830d05c1e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Station Road, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water drainage blockages were associated with the August 2014 flood (FI/14/097). Gullies and lateral systems were jet&ndash;cleaned; minor blockages were cleared and repaired ahead of resurfacing works. A blockage due to fat deposits was found and cleared. (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Station Road, March",England,Surface water drainage blockages were associated with the August 2014 flood (FI/14/097). Gullies and lateral systems were jet–cleaned; minor blockages were cleared and repaired ahead of resurfacing works. A blockage due to fat deposits was found and cleared. (p10),,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.5561073,0.0964032,"<div id=""html_e954290575c34adbea5820a1990fd7e2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>New Park, March</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Gullies were cleansed (noted in June 2014) and gullies and lateral systems were jetted; most gullies outfall into the Boards drain. The March 5th Board drain is maintained regularly by March Fifth District Drainage Commissioners. Anglian Water checked the AW system and confirmed it was clear to the outfall. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"New Park, March",England,Gullies were cleansed (noted in June 2014) and gullies and lateral systems were jetted; most gullies outfall into the Boards drain. The March 5th Board drain is maintained regularly by March Fifth District Drainage Commissioners. Anglian Water checked the AW system and confirmed it was clear to the outfall. (p12),,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,11,2014-08-08,52.3729017,-0.04493599422000649,"<div id=""html_cc63b80e7db5acbf074feefb0009b0c8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cambridgeshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple locations in the town of March experienced flooding caused by a short, very heavy rainfall event; incidents were concentrated in built&ndash;up areas (clusters in central and northern March) and resulted from surface water runoff, ordinary watercourse (overflow/backing) and foul/sewer flooding. Reports were made by residents and councillors and incidents were reported to local RMAs. [IMG,TAB,PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The town of March in Cambridgeshire experienced surface water flooding during the short, very heavy rainfall on 8/9 August 2014. Flooding was linked to blocked/defective surface water sewers and inadequate or filled&ndash;in ditches to which many sewers outfall; the event affected various locations across March as shown on the incident map and the surface water risk map. [PAG,IMG] (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced intense rainfall events that exceeded drainage design capacity, resulting in surface&ndash;water collecting on roads and flooding of properties in the March area; residents were advised and urged to report prolonged surface water on roads. [MUL] (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Cambridgeshire,England,"Multiple locations in the town of March experienced flooding caused by a short, very heavy rainfall event; incidents were concentrated in built–up areas (clusters in central and northern March) and resulted from surface water runoff, ordinary watercourse (overflow/backing) and foul/sewer flooding. Reports were made by residents and councillors and incidents were reported to local RMAs. [IMG,TAB,PAG] (p3)
The town of March in Cambridgeshire experienced surface water flooding during the short, very heavy rainfall on 8/9 August 2014. Flooding was linked to blocked/defective surface water sewers and inadequate or filled–in ditches to which many sewers outfall; the event affected various locations across March as shown on the incident map and the surface water risk map. [PAG,IMG] (p4)
Experienced intense rainfall events that exceeded drainage design capacity, resulting in surface–water collecting on roads and flooding of properties in the March area; residents were advised and urged to report prolonged surface water on roads. [MUL] (p13)",,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08.html,GB-CAM_11_2014-08-08,March flooding 08 Aug 2014 - 09 Aug 2014,Flood Investigation Report: March,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2019/Cambridgeshire County/March-flood-investigation-2019-v2.pdf
GB-CAM,27,2020-12-01,52.26791964380612,0.18029057747740113,"<div id=""html_55e0ebd0324827e29773ec1922f36671"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ely Road, Waterbeach</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External land of a property adjacent to the A10 was flooded (gardens/outbuildings/roads). [TAB] (p1)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 reported external flooding of gardens/outbuildings/roads; 1 property affected [TAB] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Ely Road, Waterbeach",England,External land of a property adjacent to the A10 was flooded (gardens/outbuildings/roads). [TAB] (p1),1 reported external flooding of gardens/outbuildings/roads; 1 property affected [TAB] (p1),GB-CAM_27_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_27_2020-12-01,Waterbeach flooding December 2020/January 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Waterbeach,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Waterbeach-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,27,2020-12-01,52.3729017,-0.04493599422000649,"<div id=""html_4991185e7d81ba226c11ea128963dc36"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cambridgeshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>County experienced flooding incidents during Dec 2020/Jan 2021. The LLFA received one report for Waterbeach describing external flooding to the external land of a property adjacent to the A10 (gardens, outbuildings and/or roads). [IMG,TAB] (p1)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 flood report in Waterbeach; 0 reported internal flooding at that Waterbeach location; 1 reported external flooding of gardens/outbuildings/roads; 788 reports across the county; approximately 280 involved internal property flooding [IMG,TAB] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Cambridgeshire,England,"County experienced flooding incidents during Dec 2020/Jan 2021. The LLFA received one report for Waterbeach describing external flooding to the external land of a property adjacent to the A10 (gardens, outbuildings and/or roads). [IMG,TAB] (p1)","1 flood report in Waterbeach; 0 reported internal flooding at that Waterbeach location; 1 reported external flooding of gardens/outbuildings/roads; 788 reports across the county; approximately 280 involved internal property flooding [IMG,TAB] (p1)",GB-CAM_27_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_27_2020-12-01,Waterbeach flooding December 2020/January 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Waterbeach,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Waterbeach-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-CAM,27,2020-12-01,52.265766,0.1909734,"<div id=""html_02ce3c774a44cc4028f4ee68f53aa07a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Waterbeach</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>External flooding reported at a property on Ely Road within Waterbeach (gardens/outbuildings/roads affected). [IMG,TAB] (p1)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 reported external flooding; 1 property affected [IMG,TAB] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Waterbeach,England,"External flooding reported at a property on Ely Road within Waterbeach (gardens/outbuildings/roads affected). [IMG,TAB] (p1)","1 reported external flooding; 1 property affected [IMG,TAB] (p1)",GB-CAM_27_2020-12-01.html,GB-CAM_27_2020-12-01,Waterbeach flooding December 2020/January 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Waterbeach,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2020/Cambridgeshire County/Waterbeach-December-2020-Flood-Investigation.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.7025328,-1.2989858,"<div id=""html_29b88a4516d3f7d0dd375e38959afa0c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hunnyhill Aquatics</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in the report as part of an area of interest (with Vicarage Road and Towngate Pond) following the 25 October 2023 floods, indicating localised flooding affected the vicinity. The report notes Source&ndash;Pathway&ndash;Receptor mapping was not produced for many of these localised incidents due to limited internal flooding reports. (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Shop interior was inundated by floodwater; flooding was associated with river/tidal influences and upstream stream backup. [PAG] (p55)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding on 25 October with recorded flood depth of approximately 1200mm inside the shop; shop lost around 99% of its stock and suffered loss of revenue. The site is in Flood Zone 3, located ~100m west of the Gunville Stream/Lukely Brook confluence, and likely experienced tidal locking that increased upstream river levels and caused water to exceed channel capacity. [IMG] (p56)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Debris screens near Hunnyhill Aquatics became blocked during the 25 October 2023 flood; the screens were consequently removed and the blockages impeded river flow, increasing local flood risk. (p83)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>approximately 1200 mm flood depth inside the shop; 99% of stock lost [PAG] (p55)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1200mm internal flood depth; 99% of stock lost [IMG] (p56)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,Hunnyhill Aquatics,England,"Included in the report as part of an area of interest (with Vicarage Road and Towngate Pond) following the 25 October 2023 floods, indicating localised flooding affected the vicinity. The report notes Source–Pathway–Receptor mapping was not produced for many of these localised incidents due to limited internal flooding reports. (p37)
Shop interior was inundated by floodwater; flooding was associated with river/tidal influences and upstream stream backup. [PAG] (p55)
Internal flooding on 25 October with recorded flood depth of approximately 1200mm inside the shop; shop lost around 99% of its stock and suffered loss of revenue. The site is in Flood Zone 3, located ~100m west of the Gunville Stream/Lukely Brook confluence, and likely experienced tidal locking that increased upstream river levels and caused water to exceed channel capacity. [IMG] (p56)
Debris screens near Hunnyhill Aquatics became blocked during the 25 October 2023 flood; the screens were consequently removed and the blockages impeded river flow, increasing local flood risk. (p83)","approximately 1200 mm flood depth inside the shop; 99% of stock lost [PAG] (p55)
1200mm internal flood depth; 99% of stock lost [IMG] (p56)",GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.6978418,-1.2892224,"<div id=""html_fadbcf220821ad4b14195d4319e1a552"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Mill Court</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as an additional area of interest (paired with Furlongs) after the 25 October 2023 floods; experienced localised flooding, but the report states there were fewer reports of internal flooding and no detailed Source&ndash;Pathway&ndash;Receptor model was produced for this location. (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the 25 October 2023 event, intense rainfall combined with a high tide produced elevated river levels and likely tidal locking near the estuary; impeded river drainage and increased channel pressure are stated to have significantly influenced flooding impacts at the Mill Court building. (p53)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Elevated river levels together with a high tide produced tidal locking and impeded river drainage near the site, placing additional pressure on the channel capacity close to the Mill Court building and significantly influencing the impacts of flooding at the building. [IMG,PAG] (p54)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,Mill Court,England,"Identified as an additional area of interest (paired with Furlongs) after the 25 October 2023 floods; experienced localised flooding, but the report states there were fewer reports of internal flooding and no detailed Source–Pathway–Receptor model was produced for this location. (p37)
During the 25 October 2023 event, intense rainfall combined with a high tide produced elevated river levels and likely tidal locking near the estuary; impeded river drainage and increased channel pressure are stated to have significantly influenced flooding impacts at the Mill Court building. (p53)
Elevated river levels together with a high tide produced tidal locking and impeded river drainage near the site, placing additional pressure on the channel capacity close to the Mill Court building and significantly influencing the impacts of flooding at the building. [IMG,PAG] (p54)",,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.7022191,-1.2959856,"<div id=""html_f9a952f265bacb6b11a04e9230a0ad1d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Towngate Pond</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Location of the twin culvert on Gunville Stream (photographed) and therefore recorded as part of the flood pathway during the investigation. (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reeds surrounding Towngate Pond were removed as part of the flood response to reduce flood risk. [TAB] (p35)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified in the report as an area of interest requiring further Source&ndash;Pathway&ndash;Receptor analysis following the Newport flooding on 25 October 2023; included among locations associated with localised flood incidents during that event. (p37)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,Towngate Pond,England,"Location of the twin culvert on Gunville Stream (photographed) and therefore recorded as part of the flood pathway during the investigation. (p8)
Reeds surrounding Towngate Pond were removed as part of the flood response to reduce flood risk. [TAB] (p35)
Identified in the report as an area of interest requiring further Source–Pathway–Receptor analysis following the Newport flooding on 25 October 2023; included among locations associated with localised flood incidents during that event. (p37)",,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.6963179,-1.3038714,"<div id=""html_1dc5c65375019a18a33d97878bacf6f6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lukely Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Triggered flood warnings (Lukely Brook at 04:43 on 25 October 2023) and contributed to flooding in the area due to rapid catchment response; fluvial flow estimated between a 1 in 20 and 1 in 50 year event on 25 October 2023. (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A Flood Warning was issued for Lukely Brook (and River Medina) during the event to warn of flooding risk. [TAB] (p35)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall caused increased volume and velocity in the Lukely Brook leading to channel exceedance; the brook flowed over fords, out of bank into rear gardens backing onto the brook and contributed to internal flooding of nearby properties. (p48)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Debris at the confluence (defined by two arch culverts) is understood to have possibly caused a blockage during the storm, contributing to elevated water levels and flooding at the confluence area. (p55)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Lukely Brook overtopped/flooded into the rear gardens of properties on Caesar's Road, delivering up to 400 mm of water into gardens; levels then subsided as the tide receded into the Medina River. (p58)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High water in the brook overtopped/encroached into adjoining rear gardens; visual evidence of swollen, turbid water close to bank. [IMG] (p59)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The brook is associated with fluvial flood risk; current SFRA flood zone mapping is misaligned with the river course which can lead to areas being omitted from flood alerts and warnings and reduced awareness of flood risk. Recommendation to investigate and update mapping and correctly map ordinary watercourses to clarify riparian ownership and help prevent channel blockages. (p79)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flows in Lukely Brook contributed to downstream flooding that affected the urban extent of Newport and nearby properties; downstream culvert condition and capacity were identified as factors influencing drainage and flood impacts. (p82)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Breach of the river channel during the 25 October 2023 storm, contributing to fluvial flooding and localised property inundation in Newport. (p86)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Out&ndash;of&ndash;bank flows / capacity issues on Lukely Brook contributed to flooding in Newport during the 25 October 2023 event; a feasibility study to increase channel/catchment capacity was recommended in response. [TAB] (p88)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Channel capacity of Lukely Brook was identified as insufficient in the context of the flood investigation following the 25 October 2023 event; a recommendation was made to study increasing its capacity (alongside Gunville Stream) to reduce future flooding. (p90)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,Lukely Brook,England,"Triggered flood warnings (Lukely Brook at 04:43 on 25 October 2023) and contributed to flooding in the area due to rapid catchment response; fluvial flow estimated between a 1 in 20 and 1 in 50 year event on 25 October 2023. (p34)
A Flood Warning was issued for Lukely Brook (and River Medina) during the event to warn of flooding risk. [TAB] (p35)
Intense rainfall caused increased volume and velocity in the Lukely Brook leading to channel exceedance; the brook flowed over fords, out of bank into rear gardens backing onto the brook and contributed to internal flooding of nearby properties. (p48)
Debris at the confluence (defined by two arch culverts) is understood to have possibly caused a blockage during the storm, contributing to elevated water levels and flooding at the confluence area. (p55)
The Lukely Brook overtopped/flooded into the rear gardens of properties on Caesar's Road, delivering up to 400 mm of water into gardens; levels then subsided as the tide receded into the Medina River. (p58)
High water in the brook overtopped/encroached into adjoining rear gardens; visual evidence of swollen, turbid water close to bank. [IMG] (p59)
The brook is associated with fluvial flood risk; current SFRA flood zone mapping is misaligned with the river course which can lead to areas being omitted from flood alerts and warnings and reduced awareness of flood risk. Recommendation to investigate and update mapping and correctly map ordinary watercourses to clarify riparian ownership and help prevent channel blockages. (p79)
Flows in Lukely Brook contributed to downstream flooding that affected the urban extent of Newport and nearby properties; downstream culvert condition and capacity were identified as factors influencing drainage and flood impacts. (p82)
Breach of the river channel during the 25 October 2023 storm, contributing to fluvial flooding and localised property inundation in Newport. (p86)
Out–of–bank flows / capacity issues on Lukely Brook contributed to flooding in Newport during the 25 October 2023 event; a feasibility study to increase channel/catchment capacity was recommended in response. [TAB] (p88)
Channel capacity of Lukely Brook was identified as insufficient in the context of the flood investigation following the 25 October 2023 event; a recommendation was made to study increasing its capacity (alongside Gunville Stream) to reduce future flooding. (p90)",,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.713064,-1.3222218,"<div id=""html_6a31f71b7a605e34a70270d59c593509"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Camp Hill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Listed as an additional area of interest for further Source&ndash;Pathway&ndash;Receptor analysis after widespread flooding in Newport on 25 October 2023; associated with more localised flood incidents during that event. (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flood damage to properties in the Camp Hill area caused by the 25 October event; intense rainfall produced surface water runoff downslope contributing to local inundation. (p58)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,Camp Hill,England,"Listed as an additional area of interest for further Source–Pathway–Receptor analysis after widespread flooding in Newport on 25 October 2023; associated with more localised flood incidents during that event. (p37)
Internal flood damage to properties in the Camp Hill area caused by the 25 October event; intense rainfall produced surface water runoff downslope contributing to local inundation. (p58)",,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.7568167,-1.2917692,"<div id=""html_a31646f662f498cd076948aeb1a16a1c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Medina</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as a main river within the Newport study area and lies inside Environment Agency flood warning areas that cover Newport. Associated with monitoring/forecasting for river flooding and therefore part of the river network contributing to local flood risk (linked spatially to the October 2023 community flood response in Newport; causal link to that event is plausible but not explicitly stated). [PAG,IMG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood warning issued for River Medina on 25 October 2023 (07:28), indicating it was affected by the fluvial response to the storm; fluvial flows on 25 October were estimated between a 1 in 20 and 1 in 50 year event. (p34)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued a flood warning for the River Medina as part of the Lukely Brook / River Medina flood warning on 25 October 2023. [TAB] (p35)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Elevated river levels on 25 October 2023, driven by intense rainfall coupled with a high tide, contributed to impeded drainage and likely tidal locking near the estuary head, which influenced flood impacts at nearby sites such as Mill Court. (p53)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,River Medina,England,"Identified as a main river within the Newport study area and lies inside Environment Agency flood warning areas that cover Newport. Associated with monitoring/forecasting for river flooding and therefore part of the river network contributing to local flood risk (linked spatially to the October 2023 community flood response in Newport; causal link to that event is plausible but not explicitly stated). [PAG,IMG] (p28)
Flood warning issued for River Medina on 25 October 2023 (07:28), indicating it was affected by the fluvial response to the storm; fluvial flows on 25 October were estimated between a 1 in 20 and 1 in 50 year event. (p34)
Environment Agency issued a flood warning for the River Medina as part of the Lukely Brook / River Medina flood warning on 25 October 2023. [TAB] (p35)
Elevated river levels on 25 October 2023, driven by intense rainfall coupled with a high tide, contributed to impeded drainage and likely tidal locking near the estuary head, which influenced flood impacts at nearby sites such as Mill Court. (p53)",,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.6975424,-1.3242904,"<div id=""html_e4d00a403c6c78b4d4ab3ce6e0e5aff2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Arthur Moody Drive, Gunville</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culvert under Arthur Moody Close (sic) was identified for investigation of condition and capacity as part of the analysis of the 25 October 2023 event, implicating it as a potential contributor to the flooding across Newport (combined fluvial, surface water and sewer sources). [TAB] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Water pooled between Arthur Moody Drive and Park Close during the event, indicating localised surface water inundation at this location. (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from the western fields flowed along primary pathways originating near Arthur Moody Drive (numbered source points on mapping). Water pooled between Arthur Moody Drive and Park Close and contributed to inundation of Broadwood Lane. A culvert (300mm) passing under Arthur Moody Drive was noted as conveying flow from neighbouring fields. [PAG,IMG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culvert under Arthur Moody Close (sic) was identified for condition and capacity investigation because it likely restricted flow during the 25th October 2023 event and contributed to local flooding; remediation/upgrade is recommended. [TAB] (p87)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culvert under Arthur Moody Close (sic) was identified for investigation for condition and capacity following the Newport Section 19 flood investigation, indicating the culvert was implicated in flooding and may have contributed to local surface water/urban flooding. [TAB] (p88)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Arthur Moody Drive, Gunville",England,"The culvert under Arthur Moody Close (sic) was identified for investigation of condition and capacity as part of the analysis of the 25 October 2023 event, implicating it as a potential contributor to the flooding across Newport (combined fluvial, surface water and sewer sources). [TAB] (p5)
Water pooled between Arthur Moody Drive and Park Close during the event, indicating localised surface water inundation at this location. (p39)
Surface water runoff from the western fields flowed along primary pathways originating near Arthur Moody Drive (numbered source points on mapping). Water pooled between Arthur Moody Drive and Park Close and contributed to inundation of Broadwood Lane. A culvert (300mm) passing under Arthur Moody Drive was noted as conveying flow from neighbouring fields. [PAG,IMG] (p41)
The culvert under Arthur Moody Close (sic) was identified for condition and capacity investigation because it likely restricted flow during the 25th October 2023 event and contributed to local flooding; remediation/upgrade is recommended. [TAB] (p87)
The culvert under Arthur Moody Close (sic) was identified for investigation for condition and capacity following the Newport Section 19 flood investigation, indicating the culvert was implicated in flooding and may have contributed to local surface water/urban flooding. [TAB] (p88)",,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.6999541,-1.3260252,"<div id=""html_f71d81ac2140b80f101f50013a5eb34c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ash Lane, Gunville</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse at Ash Lane was identified for investigation of condition and capacity as part of the analysis of the 25 October 2023 event, implicating it as a potential contributor to the flooding across Newport (combined fluvial, surface water and sewer sources). [TAB] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At least five properties on Ash Lane experienced internal flooding during the 25 October event. (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties backing onto the Gunville Stream flooded from the stream (river flood) and were left uninhabitable due to flood water damage; site investigation found large electrical appliances with clear flood damage remaining in the properties. (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>At least five properties on Ash Lane experienced internal flooding during the 25 October event attributed to the Gunville Stream and surface water runoff. Properties backing onto the Gunville Stream were later found (site visit 27 February 2024) to remain uninhabited due to flood water damage; large electrical appliances remained in&ndash;situ with clear flood damage. [PAG,IMG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Masonry arch culvert adjacent to Ash Lane shows structural deterioration consistent with flood&ndash;related damage: concrete spalling and local erosion on both headwalls, loss of mortar and a missing stone unit in the arch, mineral seepage and a drainage pipe on the downstream left side continuously discharging into the watercourse during the survey. Daylight was visible through the culvert barrel and the barrel could not be fully inspected from the surface, indicating possible internal voids or damage and potential debris build&ndash;up. A full CCTV inspection was recommended to assess structural damage and blockages. (p62)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Unmapped watercourse and adjacent channel behind Ash Lane properties were photographed and recorded as obstructed, silted and carrying debris; these conveyance problems are shown in images taken at the time of the incident and are implicated in localised flooding of back gardens and adjacent land. [IMG] (p65)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Ash Lane are identified as being at risk from fluvial flooding; a photograph in the report shows an unmapped watercourse on Ash Lane that may contribute to flooding and evacuation risk. [PAG] (p83)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>An unmapped watercourse runs through residential gardens on Ash Lane; properties on the street were identified as needing early warning and potential evacuation, indicating they were affected by fluvial flooding during the event. [IMG,PAG] (p84)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse at Ash Lane was identified for condition and capacity investigation following the 25th October 2023 event as it may have contributed to local flooding; investigation and any necessary works are recommended. [TAB] (p87)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse at Ash Lane was identified for investigation of condition and capacity in the Section 19 investigation, indicating the watercourse was implicated in flooding affecting the locality. [TAB] (p88)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least five properties (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>internal flood depths of up to 450mm (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least five properties [PAG,IMG] (p41)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Ash Lane, Gunville",England,"The watercourse at Ash Lane was identified for investigation of condition and capacity as part of the analysis of the 25 October 2023 event, implicating it as a potential contributor to the flooding across Newport (combined fluvial, surface water and sewer sources). [TAB] (p5)
At least five properties on Ash Lane experienced internal flooding during the 25 October event. (p39)
Properties backing onto the Gunville Stream flooded from the stream (river flood) and were left uninhabitable due to flood water damage; site investigation found large electrical appliances with clear flood damage remaining in the properties. (p40)
At least five properties on Ash Lane experienced internal flooding during the 25 October event attributed to the Gunville Stream and surface water runoff. Properties backing onto the Gunville Stream were later found (site visit 27 February 2024) to remain uninhabited due to flood water damage; large electrical appliances remained in–situ with clear flood damage. [PAG,IMG] (p41)
Masonry arch culvert adjacent to Ash Lane shows structural deterioration consistent with flood–related damage: concrete spalling and local erosion on both headwalls, loss of mortar and a missing stone unit in the arch, mineral seepage and a drainage pipe on the downstream left side continuously discharging into the watercourse during the survey. Daylight was visible through the culvert barrel and the barrel could not be fully inspected from the surface, indicating possible internal voids or damage and potential debris build–up. A full CCTV inspection was recommended to assess structural damage and blockages. (p62)
Unmapped watercourse and adjacent channel behind Ash Lane properties were photographed and recorded as obstructed, silted and carrying debris; these conveyance problems are shown in images taken at the time of the incident and are implicated in localised flooding of back gardens and adjacent land. [IMG] (p65)
Properties on Ash Lane are identified as being at risk from fluvial flooding; a photograph in the report shows an unmapped watercourse on Ash Lane that may contribute to flooding and evacuation risk. [PAG] (p83)
An unmapped watercourse runs through residential gardens on Ash Lane; properties on the street were identified as needing early warning and potential evacuation, indicating they were affected by fluvial flooding during the event. [IMG,PAG] (p84)
The watercourse at Ash Lane was identified for condition and capacity investigation following the 25th October 2023 event as it may have contributed to local flooding; investigation and any necessary works are recommended. [TAB] (p87)
The watercourse at Ash Lane was identified for investigation of condition and capacity in the Section 19 investigation, indicating the watercourse was implicated in flooding affecting the locality. [TAB] (p88)","at least five properties (p39)
internal flood depths of up to 450mm (p40)
at least five properties [PAG,IMG] (p41)",GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.6989968,-1.3226787,"<div id=""html_155429414aa47e66366d382242ce07cf"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Broadwood Lane, Gunville</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rear garden flooding observed (photograph caption explicitly states 'rear garden flooding on Broadwood Lane'). (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties experienced internal flooding from surface water flow paths (flows travelled from Forest Hills down Broadwood Lane to Park Close), causing property and belongings damage and disruption to residents (e.g. inability to reach work). (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff and insufficient drainage caused water to pool and inundate large parts of Broadwood Lane (including junctions with Forest Hills and between Arthur Moody Drive and Park Close). Rear gardens/properties on Broadwood Lane were flooded (photographic evidence). Blocked highway drains exacerbated flooding; levels reportedly dropped within 30 minutes after drains were cleared. [PAG,IMG] (p42)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater was observed pouring through low&ndash;level airbricks into a property, demonstrating direct internal ingress of floodwater through ventilation openings. (p85)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>internal flood depths of up to 450mm (p40)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Broadwood Lane, Gunville",England,"Rear garden flooding observed (photograph caption explicitly states 'rear garden flooding on Broadwood Lane'). (p8)
Residential properties experienced internal flooding from surface water flow paths (flows travelled from Forest Hills down Broadwood Lane to Park Close), causing property and belongings damage and disruption to residents (e.g. inability to reach work). (p40)
Surface water runoff and insufficient drainage caused water to pool and inundate large parts of Broadwood Lane (including junctions with Forest Hills and between Arthur Moody Drive and Park Close). Rear gardens/properties on Broadwood Lane were flooded (photographic evidence). Blocked highway drains exacerbated flooding; levels reportedly dropped within 30 minutes after drains were cleared. [PAG,IMG] (p42)
Floodwater was observed pouring through low–level airbricks into a property, demonstrating direct internal ingress of floodwater through ventilation openings. (p85)",internal flood depths of up to 450mm (p40),GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.6984119,-1.3241182,"<div id=""html_a6a263298faa0e0fb16ef6791cac99cc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Forest Hills, Gunville</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding on Forest Hills (photograph caption) and sandbags placed on Forest Hills to protect properties (photograph caption). (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from fields above flowed at high velocity down Forest Hills (an opening was formed at the top of Forest Hills), directing flows eastwards towards Broadwood Lane and Park Close. [PAG] (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties experienced internal flooding routed by high&ndash;velocity surface water flows diverted onto Forest Hills; resulted in property damage, loss of belongings and contamination of gardens with sewage/faecal matter following blocked drains. (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Street&ndash;level flooding with standing and fast&ndash;flowing surface water down the road; surface water was reported to flow at high velocity eastwards down Forest Hills towards Broadwood Lane and Park Close. Residential properties on Forest Hills experienced internal flooding, causing property damage, mental health impacts and contamination in gardens (faecal matter and toilet paper reported). Sandbags were deployed along the street as a mitigation response. [IMG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water was diverted at the top of Forest Hills (an opening was formed) causing high&ndash;velocity flows eastwards down Forest Hills into Broadwood Lane and Park Close. Residential properties on Forest Hills experienced internal flooding; sandbags were deployed. Flooding contributed to property damage, loss of belongings, and negative impacts on residents' wellbeing (fear, anxiety). Blocked drains were reported with sewage&ndash;related material (faecal matter and toilet paper) present in gardens following drain blockages. [IMG,PAG] (p44)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced intense surface water flooding on 25 October 2023 caused by heavy runoff from fields to the west; limited capacity in sewer networks and drainage from the fields led to overland flow down Forest Hills. Recommendations include drainage improvements and construction of rain gardens to capture excess stormwater and reduce overland flows. (p81)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Forest Hills was identified in the report as an area where surface water flood risk needs addressing (recommendations include Nature Based Solutions/SuDS retrofit and designing surface water drainage to manage off&ndash;site risk), indicating it was affected by surface water flooding during the 25 October 2023 event. (p90)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>internal flood depths of up to 450mm (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>internal flood depths up to 450mm [IMG] (p43)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>internal flood depths of up to 450mm [IMG,PAG] (p44)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Forest Hills, Gunville",England,"Flooding on Forest Hills (photograph caption) and sandbags placed on Forest Hills to protect properties (photograph caption). (p8)
Surface water runoff from fields above flowed at high velocity down Forest Hills (an opening was formed at the top of Forest Hills), directing flows eastwards towards Broadwood Lane and Park Close. [PAG] (p39)
Residential properties experienced internal flooding routed by high–velocity surface water flows diverted onto Forest Hills; resulted in property damage, loss of belongings and contamination of gardens with sewage/faecal matter following blocked drains. (p40)
Street–level flooding with standing and fast–flowing surface water down the road; surface water was reported to flow at high velocity eastwards down Forest Hills towards Broadwood Lane and Park Close. Residential properties on Forest Hills experienced internal flooding, causing property damage, mental health impacts and contamination in gardens (faecal matter and toilet paper reported). Sandbags were deployed along the street as a mitigation response. [IMG] (p43)
Surface water was diverted at the top of Forest Hills (an opening was formed) causing high–velocity flows eastwards down Forest Hills into Broadwood Lane and Park Close. Residential properties on Forest Hills experienced internal flooding; sandbags were deployed. Flooding contributed to property damage, loss of belongings, and negative impacts on residents' wellbeing (fear, anxiety). Blocked drains were reported with sewage–related material (faecal matter and toilet paper) present in gardens following drain blockages. [IMG,PAG] (p44)
Experienced intense surface water flooding on 25 October 2023 caused by heavy runoff from fields to the west; limited capacity in sewer networks and drainage from the fields led to overland flow down Forest Hills. Recommendations include drainage improvements and construction of rain gardens to capture excess stormwater and reduce overland flows. (p81)
Forest Hills was identified in the report as an area where surface water flood risk needs addressing (recommendations include Nature Based Solutions/SuDS retrofit and designing surface water drainage to manage off–site risk), indicating it was affected by surface water flooding during the 25 October 2023 event. (p90)","internal flood depths of up to 450mm (p40)
internal flood depths up to 450mm [IMG] (p43)
internal flood depths of up to 450mm [IMG,PAG] (p44)",GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.6956941,-1.3215676,"<div id=""html_8790233c2846cac06248c486e3ca8607"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Alvington Manor View, Gunville</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rear garden flooding of property (photograph shows rear garden flooding). (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A flood&ndash;related call was received from Alvington Manor View at 05:12 on 25 October 2023; flood rescue activity began and was prioritised on a risk basis. [TAB] (p35)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties experienced internal flooding. (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Five properties experienced internal flooding (reported up to 5 cm internally). Damage included subfloor, insulation, skirting board, floor coverings and low wall damage requiring replacement. Flooding originated from surface water runoff from the fields immediately to the rear/south of the properties. (p45)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water pooled in this low spot during the 25 October 2023 storm, causing localised flooding; community reports linked pooling here with property impacts (including reports of foul sewage entering gardens). (p86)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one call [TAB] (p35)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 reported internal incidents (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; up to 5 cm internal flooding (p45)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Alvington Manor View, Gunville",England,"Rear garden flooding of property (photograph shows rear garden flooding). (p8)
