GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.6916006,-1.3167071,"<div id=""html_c2a3ca9840d2185829e13d87c7ec1b82"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Carisbrooke High Street, Gunville</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced flood&ndash;related incidents (multiple emergency calls) and was a location where sandbags were made available (Carisbrooke High Street car park) as part of the flood response. [TAB] (p35)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on/around the High Street experienced internal flooding. (p37)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The area surrounding Carisbrooke High Street recorded a high number of localised property flooding incidents, with properties suffering internal flooding as drainage capacity was exceeded. (p86)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 calls [TAB] (p35)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 reported internal incidents (p37)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Carisbrooke High Street, Gunville",England,"Experienced flood–related incidents (multiple emergency calls) and was a location where sandbags were made available (Carisbrooke High Street car park) as part of the flood response. [TAB] (p35)
