GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.6999277,-1.3218039,"<div id=""html_552eacf43e2bb435d80fae1ec89ce36c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Gunville Road, Gunville</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water and an unmarked ordinary watercourse flowed beneath and alongside Gunville Road; water flowed downslope towards Gunville Road and the culverted watercourse passed below the road before discharging to the Gunville Stream, contributing to localised flooding risk at the low&ndash;lying Gunville Road bridge area. (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowpaths followed the slope toward lower elevations near the Gunville Road bridge; an unmarked ordinary watercourse was observed to become culverted and pass below Gunville Road before discharging to the Gunville Stream, contributing to local surface water flows during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p41)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Conveyance upstream of the bridge is obstructed by a mature tree, with silt and debris present in the channel&mdash;reducing flow capacity and potentially affecting bridge conveyance during high flows. (p64)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The watercourse adjacent to Gunville Road had conveyance obstructions (silt, debris, mature tree) and erosion/undercutting to channel banks that contributed to localised flooding risk in the Gunville area during the main event. [IMG] (p66)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The area to the west of Gunville Road recorded a high number of localised property flood incidents due to overwhelmed drainage and surface runoff, contributing to internal property flooding. (p86)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Gunville Road, Gunville",England,"Surface water and an unmarked ordinary watercourse flowed beneath and alongside Gunville Road; water flowed downslope towards Gunville Road and the culverted watercourse passed below the road before discharging to the Gunville Stream, contributing to localised flooding risk at the low–lying Gunville Road bridge area. (p39)
Surface water flowpaths followed the slope toward lower elevations near the Gunville Road bridge; an unmarked ordinary watercourse was observed to become culverted and pass below Gunville Road before discharging to the Gunville Stream, contributing to local surface water flows during the event. [PAG,IMG] (p41)
Conveyance upstream of the bridge is obstructed by a mature tree, with silt and debris present in the channel—reducing flow capacity and potentially affecting bridge conveyance during high flows. (p64)
The watercourse adjacent to Gunville Road had conveyance obstructions (silt, debris, mature tree) and erosion/undercutting to channel banks that contributed to localised flooding risk in the Gunville area during the main event. [IMG] (p66)
The area to the west of Gunville Road recorded a high number of localised property flood incidents due to overwhelmed drainage and surface runoff, contributing to internal property flooding. (p86)",,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25.html,GB-IOW_4_2023-10-25,Newport flooding 25 Oct 2023,Newport Section 19 Flood Investigation,059/Isle of Wight/Section 19 flood investigation report Newport September 2024.pdf
GB-IOW,4,2023-10-25,50.6993101,-1.322898,"<div id=""html_c6c6a9b08eac175b79cf731d4994e1ca"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Park Close, Gunville</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water pooled between Arthur Moody Drive and Park Close and the mapped flow pathway ran via Broadwood Lane to Park Close; water travelled via gardens through Park Close, producing localised inundation and flow through the area. [PAG] (p39)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties experienced internal flooding as surface water flowed eastwards down Forest Hills and Broadwood Lane into Park Close, causing property damage and mental&ndash;health impacts for residents. (p40)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water pooled in this low spot during the 25 October 2023 storm, causing localised flooding and contributing to property impacts reported by the community. (p86)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>internal flood depths of up to 450mm (p40)</p></div></div></body></div>",Isle of Wight,"Park Close, Gunville",England,"Surface water pooled between Arthur Moody Drive and Park Close and the mapped flow pathway ran via Broadwood Lane to Park Close; water travelled via gardens through Park Close, producing localised inundation and flow through the area. [PAG] (p39)
