Footpath access to Oasis Pool was reported impassable due to floodwater. Floodwater receding left debris and siltation in affected areas requiring subsequent cleansing and additional maintenance works to local drainage and access routes. (p9)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1323589,-0.469886,"<div id=""html_b901588cafc127ff288f89bf71d690d3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Borough Hall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater surrounded Borough Hall, reaching up to the base of the building and inundating the adjacent grounds and access routes, as shown in nighttime photographs. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Borough Hall,England,"Floodwater surrounded Borough Hall, reaching up to the base of the building and inundating the adjacent grounds and access routes, as shown in nighttime photographs. [PAG,IMG] (p10)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.12718274378504,-0.44401479432699553,"<div id=""html_6d78c5edcce9443390a0197b726999d0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kingsbrook Ward</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Footpath access in the vicinity of Oasis Pool, Cardington Road and Goodmayes Close was impacted by flood waters and/or discharge to local drainage systems/highway culverts and gullies. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Kingsbrook Ward,England,"Footpath access in the vicinity of Oasis Pool, Cardington Road and Goodmayes Close was impacted by flood waters and/or discharge to local drainage systems/highway culverts and gullies. (p5)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.134956367099335,-0.4627879605650807,"<div id=""html_cba047f583057823d8a2cbac461be16d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Castle Ward</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas of Castle Ward experienced flooding that impacted roads, pathways, gardens and open spaces. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Castle Ward,England,"Areas of Castle Ward experienced flooding that impacted roads, pathways, gardens and open spaces. (p5)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.139771172701295,-0.43103478000905615,"<div id=""html_e09c566d2da141e1fb4b73a8f77b492e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Newnham Ward</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas of Newnham Ward experienced flooding that impacted roads, pathways, gardens and open spaces. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Newnham Ward,England,"Areas of Newnham Ward experienced flooding that impacted roads, pathways, gardens and open spaces. (p5)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2501568,-0.4951266,"<div id=""html_2d8b501c5957439d1a240ebc328f2159"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Riseley Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water (Riseley Brook&ndash;related) caused internal flooding of a commercial property in Riseley and made the High Street impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Riseley Brook caused river flooding that affected Riseley and Pertenhall; Environment Agency issued a Flood Alert (23/12/2020 14:48) and a Flood Warning for Riseley Brook (23/12/2020 19:04). [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The community undertook a flooding debrief and ongoing community flood group activity after properties were affected; actions include investigation of non&ndash;return valves where ditches discharge into Riseley Brook and examining a potentially disconnected drainage ditch that feeds the brook. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial property [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Riseley Brook,England,"Surface water (Riseley Brook–related) caused internal flooding of a commercial property in Riseley and made the High Street impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)
Riseley Brook caused river flooding that affected Riseley and Pertenhall; Environment Agency issued a Flood Alert (23/12/2020 14:48) and a Flood Warning for Riseley Brook (23/12/2020 19:04). [TAB] (p14)
The community undertook a flooding debrief and ongoing community flood group activity after properties were affected; actions include investigation of non–return valves where ditches discharge into Riseley Brook and examining a potentially disconnected drainage ditch that feeds the brook. [TAB] (p21)","1 commercial property [TAB,PAG] (p7)",GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1292451,-0.4326079,"<div id=""html_8fa8da500d7fe1e7725bba2330fe6b7b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Priory Lake</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Bedford &ndash; Priory Lake is listed with a flood date of 25/12/2020 and was included in the Flood Alert for the Middle River Great Ouse (22/12/2020), indicating it was among locations affected by river flooding during the event. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Main River assets at Bedford Priory Lake were inspected after the flood; remedial works were identified and a medium&ndash;term action was raised to investigate suitability of property flood protection measures and develop a flood action plan for the affected business/property. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following the flood event the lake and associated assets were scheduled for inspections and remedial works where required as part of the recovery actions. (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Priory Lake,England,"Bedford – Priory Lake is listed with a flood date of 25/12/2020 and was included in the Flood Alert for the Middle River Great Ouse (22/12/2020), indicating it was among locations affected by river flooding during the event. (p14)
Main River assets at Bedford Priory Lake were inspected after the flood; remedial works were identified and a medium–term action was raised to investigate suitability of property flood protection measures and develop a flood action plan for the affected business/property. [TAB,PAG] (p21)
Following the flood event the lake and associated assets were scheduled for inspections and remedial works where required as part of the recovery actions. (p31)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2290464,-0.5538592,"<div id=""html_cc893eca0f6c1a7aaa9ca0568faeb4cc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sharn Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Sharn Brook ordinary watercourse caused internal flooding of two residential properties in Sharnbrook. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sharn Brook caused flooding affecting adjacent Flood Zone 3 areas during December 2020, prompting liaison with riparian owners to set inspection/maintenance regimes and investigations into extending the Flood Warning area. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential properties [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Sharn Brook,England,"The Sharn Brook ordinary watercourse caused internal flooding of two residential properties in Sharnbrook. [TAB,PAG] (p7)
Sharn Brook caused flooding affecting adjacent Flood Zone 3 areas during December 2020, prompting liaison with riparian owners to set inspection/maintenance regimes and investigations into extending the Flood Warning area. [TAB] (p21)","2 residential properties [TAB,PAG] (p7)",GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1326145,-0.4507871,"<div id=""html_b840c29297697b31d1d563091eb36a22"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Boating Lake</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding from the River Great Ouse caused internal flooding of properties at Bedford &ndash; Boating Lake. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial, 1 educational [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Boating Lake,England,Fluvial flooding from the River Great Ouse caused internal flooding of properties at Bedford – Boating Lake. [TAB] (p7),"1 commercial, 1 educational [TAB] (p7)",GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2734465,-0.4049232,"<div id=""html_b5185e3b1302eac3222eac59441c6b65"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pertenhall Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Post&ndash;flood actions include investigating improvements to the Flood Warning for Pertenhall Brook, examining potential land&ndash;level changes between the brook and a residential property to reduce flood risk, and clearing the culvert beneath Wood End Lane/Swineshead Road where debris was removed. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from Pertenhall Brook affected adjacent residential property, prompting investigation of a scheme to alter land levels between the brook and the property to reduce future flood risk. (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Pertenhall Brook,England,"Post–flood actions include investigating improvements to the Flood Warning for Pertenhall Brook, examining potential land–level changes between the brook and a residential property to reduce flood risk, and clearing the culvert beneath Wood End Lane/Swineshead Road where debris was removed. [TAB,PAG] (p21)
Flooding from Pertenhall Brook affected adjacent residential property, prompting investigation of a scheme to alter land levels between the brook and the property to reduce future flood risk. (p33)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1363806,-0.4675041,"<div id=""html_7a6af35f0286021fd2bb0ee7b5b08228"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bedford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Various locations across the borough experienced flooding during the December 2020 flood event. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of the borough experienced widespread and exceptional flooding from both surface water runoff and the River Great Ouse between 23&ndash;26 Dec 2020; rapid overland flows caused villages north of Bedford to flood within several hours; communities required rescue and local assistance. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding affected residential, commercial, community and educational properties across the borough, including internal property flooding reported at multiple locations and resulting in 27 formal investigations of internal flooding. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding across the Borough between 23rd and 26th December 2020 affected multiple wards. Internal property flooding occurred at 27 locations and 27 formal flood investigations were carried out across 20 villages/towns. Roads, footpaths, gardens and open spaces were also inundated, causing access impacts in areas including Kingsbrook Ward (footpath access in the vicinity of Oasis Pool, Cardington Road and Goodmayes Close), Castle Ward, Newnham Ward, Great Barford and Bletsoe. Flood waters and/or discharge to local drainage systems, highway culverts and gullies produced localised access and surface flooding impacts. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clusters of flooding incidents occurred in and around the town, producing access impacts to roads, footpaths and open spaces. Specific local impacts cited include footpath access issues in Kingsbrook Ward (vicinity of Oasis Pool, Cardington Road, Goodmayes Close) and impacts in Castle Ward and Newnham Ward due to flood waters and drainage/culvert discharge. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding caused by River Great Ouse: Bedford &ndash; Boating Lake: 1 commercial and 1 educational property flooded; Bedford &ndash; Priory Lake: 1 commercial property flooded. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Across the borough, surface water and fluvial flooding left debris and siltation in properties, roads, footways, local drainage systems and watercourses; several roads and bridges were reported impassable, hindering access for highways and emergency teams. Rest centres were used by affected residents and evacuations occurred. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple locations within the borough adjacent to the River Great Ouse experienced river (fluvial) flooding during the 23&ndash;26 December 2020 event; Flood Warnings were issued for low&ndash;lying areas in the borough (including Boating Lake and Priory Lake in Bedford on 25/12/2020). [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Above&ndash;average rainfall in the week before 23 December 2020 caused main river and ordinary watercourse levels to rise. Flood Warnings were issued across the Borough shortly before or after flooding in several locations, giving insufficient time for residents to prepare or evacuate; Harrold and Wyboston did not receive a Flood Warning. Inconsistent and changing timing information from the Environment Agency about surges/peaks on the Great River Ouse increased community anxiety and hindered the Council's response. In the absence of timely warnings, Police volunteers and the Resilience Team undertook a mass leaflet drop (24 December) to warn residents of imminent flooding. Surface water flooding affected areas that are generally not covered by flood warnings. [MUL] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The 23 December 2020 flood involved ditch/river capacity issues (Kings Ditch mentioned) and surface water/overland flows affecting properties and highways across the borough, prompting investigations and remedial works by agencies. [TAB] (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High Street highway drainage was investigated due to blockages related to the flood response; blockages were cleared in March 2021 to restore drainage and reduce highway surface water flooding. [PAG,MUL] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Kempston High Street experienced flooding during the event. Culverts on High Street became blocked and required clearance (two culverts were cleared in March 2021). Temporary drainage works were carried out after the flood: grips were dug either side of High Street to divert water into adjacent ditches, and a resident cleared/maintained the ditches following the flood. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in December 2020 affected highways and properties: highway drainage and grips along High Street required inspection and maintenance, a blocked gully on Kennel Hill was cleared (March 2021) as part of post&ndash;flood recovery, and Main River assets were inspected with remedial works identified for some assets. [PAG] (p28)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of the area experienced surface water/urban flooding during the December 2020 event, prompting investigations into highway drainage, culvert condition and property&ndash;level flood protection measures; remedial gullies clearance was carried out in March 2021 and highway drainage works (clearance of blockages) were completed in May 2021. [PAG] (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The December 2020 flood event in Bedford prompted investigations, inspections of river/main&ndash;river assets and highway drainage, remedial works, community flood&ndash;group engagement, and property&ndash;level flood protection investigations across the area. [PAG] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water/urban flooding affected the length of High Street and Green Lane, leading to investigations of highway drainage and culverts and clearance works; the drainage clearing for this length was completed in May 2021 as a response to the flood impacts. [PAG] (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water/urban flooding occurred in Bedford on 23rd December 2020, prompting investigation of culverts and maintenance of ditches and consideration of property&ndash;level flood resilience measures (including for a flooded utility room). [TAB] (p34)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>65 properties; 27 different locations [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>27 locations; 27 investigations; 20 villages/towns (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>27 locations; 27 investigations; 20 villages/towns (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial; 1 educational; 1 commercial [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>five properties; one property; two bridges [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Bedford,England,"Various locations across the borough experienced flooding during the December 2020 flood event. (p1)
Parts of the borough experienced widespread and exceptional flooding from both surface water runoff and the River Great Ouse between 23–26 Dec 2020; rapid overland flows caused villages north of Bedford to flood within several hours; communities required rescue and local assistance. [PAG] (p3)
Widespread flooding affected residential, commercial, community and educational properties across the borough, including internal property flooding reported at multiple locations and resulting in 27 formal investigations of internal flooding. (p4)
Widespread flooding across the Borough between 23rd and 26th December 2020 affected multiple wards. Internal property flooding occurred at 27 locations and 27 formal flood investigations were carried out across 20 villages/towns. Roads, footpaths, gardens and open spaces were also inundated, causing access impacts in areas including Kingsbrook Ward (footpath access in the vicinity of Oasis Pool, Cardington Road and Goodmayes Close), Castle Ward, Newnham Ward, Great Barford and Bletsoe. Flood waters and/or discharge to local drainage systems, highway culverts and gullies produced localised access and surface flooding impacts. (p5)
Clusters of flooding incidents occurred in and around the town, producing access impacts to roads, footpaths and open spaces. Specific local impacts cited include footpath access issues in Kingsbrook Ward (vicinity of Oasis Pool, Cardington Road, Goodmayes Close) and impacts in Castle Ward and Newnham Ward due to flood waters and drainage/culvert discharge. (p6)
Internal flooding caused by River Great Ouse: Bedford – Boating Lake: 1 commercial and 1 educational property flooded; Bedford – Priory Lake: 1 commercial property flooded. [TAB] (p7)
Across the borough, surface water and fluvial flooding left debris and siltation in properties, roads, footways, local drainage systems and watercourses; several roads and bridges were reported impassable, hindering access for highways and emergency teams. Rest centres were used by affected residents and evacuations occurred. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Multiple locations within the borough adjacent to the River Great Ouse experienced river (fluvial) flooding during the 23–26 December 2020 event; Flood Warnings were issued for low–lying areas in the borough (including Boating Lake and Priory Lake in Bedford on 25/12/2020). [TAB] (p14)
Above–average rainfall in the week before 23 December 2020 caused main river and ordinary watercourse levels to rise. Flood Warnings were issued across the Borough shortly before or after flooding in several locations, giving insufficient time for residents to prepare or evacuate; Harrold and Wyboston did not receive a Flood Warning. Inconsistent and changing timing information from the Environment Agency about surges/peaks on the Great River Ouse increased community anxiety and hindered the Council's response. In the absence of timely warnings, Police volunteers and the Resilience Team undertook a mass leaflet drop (24 December) to warn residents of imminent flooding. Surface water flooding affected areas that are generally not covered by flood warnings. [MUL] (p15)
The 23 December 2020 flood involved ditch/river capacity issues (Kings Ditch mentioned) and surface water/overland flows affecting properties and highways across the borough, prompting investigations and remedial works by agencies. [TAB] (p24)
High Street highway drainage was investigated due to blockages related to the flood response; blockages were cleared in March 2021 to restore drainage and reduce highway surface water flooding. [PAG,MUL] (p25)
Kempston High Street experienced flooding during the event. Culverts on High Street became blocked and required clearance (two culverts were cleared in March 2021). Temporary drainage works were carried out after the flood: grips were dug either side of High Street to divert water into adjacent ditches, and a resident cleared/maintained the ditches following the flood. [TAB] (p27)
Flooding in December 2020 affected highways and properties: highway drainage and grips along High Street required inspection and maintenance, a blocked gully on Kennel Hill was cleared (March 2021) as part of post–flood recovery, and Main River assets were inspected with remedial works identified for some assets. [PAG] (p28)
Parts of the area experienced surface water/urban flooding during the December 2020 event, prompting investigations into highway drainage, culvert condition and property–level flood protection measures; remedial gullies clearance was carried out in March 2021 and highway drainage works (clearance of blockages) were completed in May 2021. [PAG] (p30)
The December 2020 flood event in Bedford prompted investigations, inspections of river/main–river assets and highway drainage, remedial works, community flood–group engagement, and property–level flood protection investigations across the area. [PAG] (p32)
Surface water/urban flooding affected the length of High Street and Green Lane, leading to investigations of highway drainage and culverts and clearance works; the drainage clearing for this length was completed in May 2021 as a response to the flood impacts. [PAG] (p33)
Surface water/urban flooding occurred in Bedford on 23rd December 2020, prompting investigation of culverts and maintenance of ditches and consideration of property–level flood resilience measures (including for a flooded utility room). [TAB] (p34)","65 properties; 27 different locations [PAG] (p3)
27 locations; 27 investigations; 20 villages/towns (p4)
27 locations; 27 investigations; 20 villages/towns (p6)
1 commercial; 1 educational; 1 commercial [TAB] (p7)
five properties; one property; two bridges [PAG,IMG] (p10)",GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1278302,-0.4250206,"<div id=""html_15fe9305fc663431519265af967efe15"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Great Ouse</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Main river levels increased and contributed to fluvial flooding across the catchment between 23 and 26 December 2020; the river was named as a source of flooding in multiple locations within the borough. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall across the catchment on 23&ndash;24 December 2020 increased runoff into drainage systems and watercourses, causing river levels to rise and overtop banks and contributing to surface water and fluvial flooding in and around Bedford (including reported basement ingress at some properties). (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Great Ouse generated multiple Flood Alerts and Flood Warnings across the borough (alerts issued 22/12/2020 and warnings 24&ndash;25/12/2020), and is named as the source of fluvial flooding affecting towns such as Turvey, Odell, Clapham, Kempston and Bedford. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surges and peak timings on the Great River Ouse changed considerably during the December 2020 event, driving flooding behaviour and causing forecasts/warnings to change during the event, which contributed to inaccurate information reaching the public and responders. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River flooding in December 2020 affected properties along the River Great Ouse and prompted investigations into flood alleviation schemes and defence measures to increase property resilience. (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,River Great Ouse,England,"Main river levels increased and contributed to fluvial flooding across the catchment between 23 and 26 December 2020; the river was named as a source of flooding in multiple locations within the borough. (p7)
Intense rainfall across the catchment on 23–24 December 2020 increased runoff into drainage systems and watercourses, causing river levels to rise and overtop banks and contributing to surface water and fluvial flooding in and around Bedford (including reported basement ingress at some properties). (p11)
The River Great Ouse generated multiple Flood Alerts and Flood Warnings across the borough (alerts issued 22/12/2020 and warnings 24–25/12/2020), and is named as the source of fluvial flooding affecting towns such as Turvey, Odell, Clapham, Kempston and Bedford. [TAB] (p14)
Surges and peak timings on the Great River Ouse changed considerably during the December 2020 event, driving flooding behaviour and causing forecasts/warnings to change during the event, which contributed to inaccurate information reaching the public and responders. (p15)
River flooding in December 2020 affected properties along the River Great Ouse and prompted investigations into flood alleviation schemes and defence measures to increase property resilience. (p18)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2537681,-0.6199511,"<div id=""html_4cf9a55c51b331c3dccec076790b62d8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Vicarage Lane, Podington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood levels in the vicinity of Vicarage Lane were affected by downstream river levels and the condition/capacity of a culvert beneath High Street, prompting investigation of culvert capacity and downstream influences. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood levels in the vicinity of Vicarage Lane were affected by downstream river levels and a culvert; an investigation was recommended to determine whether localised works or a capital scheme were required to manage flood risk. [TAB] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"Vicarage Lane, Podington",England,"Flood levels in the vicinity of Vicarage Lane were affected by downstream river levels and the condition/capacity of a culvert beneath High Street, prompting investigation of culvert capacity and downstream influences. [TAB] (p21)
Flood levels in the vicinity of Vicarage Lane were affected by downstream river levels and a culvert; an investigation was recommended to determine whether localised works or a capital scheme were required to manage flood risk. [TAB] (p22)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2063431,-0.6141821,"<div id=""html_6222e398d1b21fef9e2dc9fc546d78a9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wood Road, Harrold</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding and capacity issues on the watercourse north of Wood Road were identified; actions include investigating responsibility and maintenance to maximise capacity, and longer&ndash;term proposals (adding a second pipe beneath the road, modifying the diverter to direct flows into the flood channel, and creating an outflow from the flood channel to Tustings Lake) to reduce overtopping onto Wood Road. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood flows overtopped onto Wood Road and the report recommends increasing the capacity of the watercourse crossing (second pipe beneath the road), works to the diverter to encourage flows into the flood channel, and potential outflow works into Tustings Lake to reduce overtopping. [TAB] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"Wood Road, Harrold",England,"Flooding and capacity issues on the watercourse north of Wood Road were identified; actions include investigating responsibility and maintenance to maximise capacity, and longer–term proposals (adding a second pipe beneath the road, modifying the diverter to direct flows into the flood channel, and creating an outflow from the flood channel to Tustings Lake) to reduce overtopping onto Wood Road. [TAB] (p21)
Flood flows overtopped onto Wood Road and the report recommends increasing the capacity of the watercourse crossing (second pipe beneath the road), works to the diverter to encourage flows into the flood channel, and potential outflow works into Tustings Lake to reduce overtopping. [TAB] (p22)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
