GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1894467,-0.5850905,"<div id=""html_276b4fc37317e2ed2d781b4857e14cfd"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pavenham Road, Chellington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from an unnamed ordinary watercourse (tributary to the River Great Ouse) caused internal flooding of dwellings and made the adjacent Pavenham Road impassable. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway drainage and the culvert beneath Pavenham Road were investigated and cleared of debris after the flood to restore conveyance and reduce road and adjacent property flooding risk. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding involved the culvert beneath Pavenham Road and the culvert conveying the watercourse beneath Carlton; investigations and clearing of highway drainage/culvert works were carried out (culvert/clearing completed March 2021) to address road and adjacent property flooding risk. [TAB] (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway drainage and a piped watercourse crossing were blocked following the flood; inspections and clearance works were carried out and the blockages were cleared. [MUL] (p25)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"Pavenham Road, Chellington",England,"Flooding from an unnamed ordinary watercourse (tributary to the River Great Ouse) caused internal flooding of dwellings and made the adjacent Pavenham Road impassable. [TAB] (p7)
