Highway drainage and a piped watercourse crossing were blocked following the flood; inspections and clearance works were carried out and the blockages were cleared. [MUL] (p25)",2 residential [TAB] (p7),GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2060238,-0.4489927,"<div id=""html_f9783692d1e733d3c6297e99cc515bd4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Robins Folly, Bedford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Robins Folly Road was affected by flooding in December 2020; ditches either side of the road were maintained (one by a resident), culvert capacity was investigated and a capital scheme was progressed to add pipe capacity beneath/along the road to reduce future flooding. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ditches either side of the road and culvert beneath the road were found to have limited capacity, leading to road drainage flooding risk/occurrence; a resident has already cleared ditches and a capital scheme is proposed to add an additional pipe (or upsized pipe) beneath the road to provide extra capacity. [TAB] (p29)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"Robins Folly, Bedford",England,"Robins Folly Road was affected by flooding in December 2020; ditches either side of the road were maintained (one by a resident), culvert capacity was investigated and a capital scheme was progressed to add pipe capacity beneath/along the road to reduce future flooding. [TAB] (p21)
