GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.28086874955567,-0.40787381082074275,"<div id=""html_502f7b111b9bfc084bfb41b7e79b007e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wood End Lane, Pertenhall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Wood End Lane and adjacent fields/ditches were affected by flooding during the December 2020 event. Actions taken included liaison with landowners to maintain ditches to maximise capacity, inspection and clearing of culverts beneath the road, and assessment of Property Flood Resilience for an affected utility room. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affecting the highway and surrounding drainage was linked to a culvert beneath Wood End Lane; investigations and clearing of debris, plus liaison with landowners to maintain ditches, were recommended to reduce future flood risk. (p33)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Debris&ndash;blocked culvert beneath Wood End Lane reduced drainage conveyance and required investigation and clearing; identified as a contributor to local surface water flooding during the 23rd December 2020 event. [TAB] (p34)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"Wood End Lane, Pertenhall",England,"Wood End Lane and adjacent fields/ditches were affected by flooding during the December 2020 event. Actions taken included liaison with landowners to maintain ditches to maximise capacity, inspection and clearing of culverts beneath the road, and assessment of Property Flood Resilience for an affected utility room. [TAB,PAG] (p21)
