GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2068055,-0.550438,"<div id=""html_50168b99f69bfc44de0c6af07ccf7d0b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pavenham Road, Felmersham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Pavenham Road experienced muddy floodwater flowing over the carriageway with rapid flow at an overflow point, causing roadway inundation and contributing to debris and siltation on the highway and nearby properties; required subsequent cleansing and maintenance. [IMG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Highway drainage and culvert issues were identified following the December 2020 flood; investigations were carried out into the drainage and culvert beneath Pavenham Road and works to clear blockages were completed in March 2021. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Watercourse crossings beneath the roads were identified as requiring a capacity assessment to find opportunities for improvement after flooding, indicating capacity/flow issues contributed to impacts on the highway. (p25)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"Pavenham Road, Felmersham",England,"Pavenham Road experienced muddy floodwater flowing over the carriageway with rapid flow at an overflow point, causing roadway inundation and contributing to debris and siltation on the highway and nearby properties; required subsequent cleansing and maintenance. [IMG] (p9)
