GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1153008,-0.5036916,"<div id=""html_8b5ad0f9973a2490a4eaf51fd5615758"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Kempston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Kempston High Street suffered surface&ndash;water/urban flooding that blocked highway drainage and culverts. Bedford Highways carried out investigations and cleared blockages (completed January 2021); grips were dug either side of High Street after the flood to help drain water to adjacent ditches. Further investigation into drainage improvements and upstream Natural Flood Management is ongoing. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Kempston High Street is under investigation for drainage and flood&ndash;risk improvements following flooding; work scope is being defined with a consultant team to address flood risk identified after the December 2020 event. (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"High Street, Kempston",England,"Kempston High Street suffered surface–water/urban flooding that blocked highway drainage and culverts. Bedford Highways carried out investigations and cleared blockages (completed January 2021); grips were dug either side of High Street after the flood to help drain water to adjacent ditches. Further investigation into drainage improvements and upstream Natural Flood Management is ongoing. [TAB] (p21)
Kempston High Street is under investigation for drainage and flood–risk improvements following flooding; work scope is being defined with a consultant team to address flood risk identified after the December 2020 event. (p26)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.211094,-0.5877858,"<div id=""html_2fca19a5fa7dd095cf8c4a389b95a730"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Odell</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High Street drainage/ditches were overwhelmed during the December 2020 flood; a resident increased the capacity/maintained the ditches after the event to reduce future flooding. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High Street experienced blocked/blocked culverts and surface water runoff after the flood event; grips were dug either side of the road to divert water into adjacent ditches and culverts were cleared as a remedial measure. [TAB] (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Runoff from fields to the north entered drainage ditches and highway grips adjacent to High Street, prompting a recommendation to set an inspection and maintenance regime for the highway grips to reduce flood risk and support community preparedness. (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"High Street, Odell",England,"High Street drainage/ditches were overwhelmed during the December 2020 flood; a resident increased the capacity/maintained the ditches after the event to reduce future flooding. [TAB] (p21)
High Street experienced blocked/blocked culverts and surface water runoff after the flood event; grips were dug either side of the road to divert water into adjacent ditches and culverts were cleared as a remedial measure. [TAB] (p27)
Runoff from fields to the north entered drainage ditches and highway grips adjacent to High Street, prompting a recommendation to set an inspection and maintenance regime for the highway grips to reduce flood risk and support community preparedness. (p28)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2891964,-0.5179477,"<div id=""html_6791c42f004a4c01bf3df4b59a456f31"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Yelden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water/road flooding and blocked highway drainage occurred along High Street in multiple villages. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Gullies along High Street (and adjacent Church Lane and Spring Lane) were silted/blocked in association with the flood event; gullies were cleared in March 2021 as remedial works and a community debrief/visit was recommended to identify further measures. (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Gullies on High Street were silted/blocked following the December 2020 flood and were cleared in March 2021. The River Till at the western bank by High Street was identified as overtopping to the south, and a potential flood storage area west of High Street was proposed as an NFM measure to reduce overtopping. [PAG,MUL] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"High Street, Yelden",England,"Surface water/road flooding and blocked highway drainage occurred along High Street in multiple villages. [TAB,PAG] (p21)
