GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1451088,-0.5339894,"<div id=""html_c3875bc7783d780041deb8a34b61b656"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bromham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A flooding incident is marked for Bromham on the Borough map and is therefore considered part of the widespread floods that affected the Borough on 23 December 2020; the flooding caused localised inundation consistent with access impacts (streets/low&ndash;lying areas) shown across the Borough. [IMG] (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Bromham,England,A flooding incident is marked for Bromham on the Borough map and is therefore considered part of the widespread floods that affected the Borough on 23 December 2020; the flooding caused localised inundation consistent with access impacts (streets/low–lying areas) shown across the Borough. [IMG] (p6),,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.202622570683715,-0.6097162346363184,"<div id=""html_9782978a771dd456e7b84bf5197cb382"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Harrold</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Harrold is shown as having a flooding location on the Borough map and is therefore part of the widespread flooding event on 23 December 2020, with localised inundation and associated access impacts consistent with the Borough&ndash;wide pattern. [IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties from both an unnamed ordinary watercourse (Harrold North) and the River Great Ouse/tributaries (Harrold South); roads (Carlton Road) and bridges reported impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The settlement experienced inundation of streets (including Carlton Road) with floodwater blocking local access and requiring follow&ndash;up cleansing and maintenance once waters receded. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced fluvial (river) flooding between 23/12/2020 and 25/12/2020. Environment Agency issued a Flood Alert for the Middle River Great Ouse on 22/12/2020; no Flood Warning was issued specifically for Harrold. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A flood warning was not issued for Harrold during the December 2020 event; residents were affected by flooding with insufficient warning, causing concern and anxiety and limiting time to prepare or evacuate. [MUL] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A nearby watercourse overtopped and caused flooding in Harrold (North and South), leading to highway drainage clearance, issuance of flood kits and a community flood plan, and investigations into increasing channel capacity (including adding a second pipe beneath the road), diverting flows into a flood channel and potential outflow to Tustings Lake. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Local flooding from watercourses and constrained culverts affected the village (including Vicarage Lane area); actions recorded include culvert condition investigation, assessment of downstream river influence, maintenance of watercourses, consideration of a flood warning system, and community resilience measures (flood kits, flood plans, PFR information). [TAB] (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential; 4 residential [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Harrold,England,"Harrold is shown as having a flooding location on the Borough map and is therefore part of the widespread flooding event on 23 December 2020, with localised inundation and associated access impacts consistent with the Borough–wide pattern. [IMG] (p6)
Internal flooding of properties from both an unnamed ordinary watercourse (Harrold North) and the River Great Ouse/tributaries (Harrold South); roads (Carlton Road) and bridges reported impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)
The settlement experienced inundation of streets (including Carlton Road) with floodwater blocking local access and requiring follow–up cleansing and maintenance once waters receded. [PAG] (p10)
Experienced fluvial (river) flooding between 23/12/2020 and 25/12/2020. Environment Agency issued a Flood Alert for the Middle River Great Ouse on 22/12/2020; no Flood Warning was issued specifically for Harrold. [TAB] (p14)
A flood warning was not issued for Harrold during the December 2020 event; residents were affected by flooding with insufficient warning, causing concern and anxiety and limiting time to prepare or evacuate. [MUL] (p15)
A nearby watercourse overtopped and caused flooding in Harrold (North and South), leading to highway drainage clearance, issuance of flood kits and a community flood plan, and investigations into increasing channel capacity (including adding a second pipe beneath the road), diverting flows into a flood channel and potential outflow to Tustings Lake. [TAB,PAG] (p21)
Local flooding from watercourses and constrained culverts affected the village (including Vicarage Lane area); actions recorded include culvert condition investigation, assessment of downstream river influence, maintenance of watercourses, consideration of a flood warning system, and community resilience measures (flood kits, flood plans, PFR information). [TAB] (p22)","1 residential; 4 residential [TAB,PAG] (p7)",GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.225548,-0.5508851,"<div id=""html_769fd28cc2c6c56ab29aa0e862554784"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sharnbrook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Sharnbrook is marked on the Borough flooding map as having a flood location and is therefore considered to have experienced localised flooding on 23 December 2020, producing inundation and access disruption in low&ndash;lying areas adjacent to watercourses. [IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported flood date 23/12/2020 and included in an Environment Agency Flood Warning for the River Great Ouse (24/12/2020 21:11). The village was affected by river flooding during the 23&ndash;26 December 2020 event. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential properties [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Sharnbrook,England,"Sharnbrook is marked on the Borough flooding map as having a flood location and is therefore considered to have experienced localised flooding on 23 December 2020, producing inundation and access disruption in low–lying areas adjacent to watercourses. [IMG] (p6)
