GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.16444183376767,-0.500957305703679,"<div id=""html_b7bda3dfa1beabcd1503a0241abb4256"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clapham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clapham is indicated on the Borough map as a flooding location and is therefore considered impacted by the widespread flooding on 23 December 2020, causing localised inundation and likely access impacts consistent with other marked sites. [IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Fluvial flooding from the River Great Ouse caused internal flooding of properties in Clapham and made the High Street impassable. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Clapham was included in a Flood Warning for the River Great Ouse (issued 25/12/2020 05:46 for Oakley and Clapham), indicating it was affected by river flooding risk during the event period. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>LLFA officers communicated with the existing Community Flood Group as part of the flood response and monitoring activities. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High Street highway drainage experienced blockages associated with the flood; blockages were cleared in March 2021 to restore drainage and reduce risk to the road and nearby properties. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 residential, 1 commercial [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Clapham,England,"Clapham is indicated on the Borough map as a flooding location and is therefore considered impacted by the widespread flooding on 23 December 2020, causing localised inundation and likely access impacts consistent with other marked sites. [IMG] (p6)
Fluvial flooding from the River Great Ouse caused internal flooding of properties in Clapham and made the High Street impassable. [TAB] (p7)
Clapham was included in a Flood Warning for the River Great Ouse (issued 25/12/2020 05:46 for Oakley and Clapham), indicating it was affected by river flooding risk during the event period. [TAB] (p14)
LLFA officers communicated with the existing Community Flood Group as part of the flood response and monitoring activities. (p16)
High Street highway drainage experienced blockages associated with the flood; blockages were cleared in March 2021 to restore drainage and reduce risk to the road and nearby properties. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p21)","4 residential, 1 commercial [TAB] (p7)",GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1192011,-0.4930154,"<div id=""html_e52ce92b9af3a64f429e7aa68c2b7401"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Kempston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Kempston is shown with a flooding marker on the Borough map and is therefore treated as having experienced flooding during the 23 December 2020 event, with localised inundation and associated access impacts. [IMG] (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of 5 residential properties; roads impassable (Water Lane and Church Walk). [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas of the town (including Water Lane) experienced significant road flooding with water reaching building frontages, impeding access and necessitating cleansing and maintenance after the event. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A Flood Warning was issued for low&ndash;lying areas close to the River Great Ouse at Kempston (25/12/2020 05:46); Kempston is recorded as having flooding on 25/12/2020 afternoon during the event. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 residential [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Kempston,England,"Kempston is shown with a flooding marker on the Borough map and is therefore treated as having experienced flooding during the 23 December 2020 event, with localised inundation and associated access impacts. [IMG] (p6)
Internal flooding of 5 residential properties; roads impassable (Water Lane and Church Walk). [TAB,PAG] (p7)
Areas of the town (including Water Lane) experienced significant road flooding with water reaching building frontages, impeding access and necessitating cleansing and maintenance after the event. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
