GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.208927,-0.5487778,"<div id=""html_b12702905d15498061c89abccb990307"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Felmersham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties from an unnamed ordinary watercourse (tributary to the River Great Ouse); bridges became impassable. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Pavenham Road in Felmersham experienced significant street flooding with muddy floodwater flowing over the road, visible rapid flow and turbulence; contributed to debris and siltation on the road and adjacent areas requiring cleansing and maintenance after waters receded. [IMG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in an Environment Agency Flood Warning for the River Great Ouse (warning issued 24/12/2020 21:11). The area was affected by river flooding associated with the River Great Ouse during the 23&ndash;26 December 2020 event. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following the December 2020 flood event Felmersham was affected by high flows in local watercourses/ditches. This prompted investigations into the capacity of watercourse crossings beneath Pavenham Road and Grange Road and actions to secure ongoing maintenance of the watercourse through Felmersham. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding prompted inspection of main river assets (sluices, weirs, gates, locks and river banks) and identification of remedial works; investigation of flood protection measures and property flood resilience for affected properties; investigation of highway drainage and a piped watercourse crossing on Pavenham Road with blockages cleared in March 2021; consideration of flood warning improvements and potential community flood group set&ndash;up to improve preparedness. [MUL] (p25)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 residential [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Felmersham,England,"Internal flooding of residential properties from an unnamed ordinary watercourse (tributary to the River Great Ouse); bridges became impassable. [TAB] (p7)
Pavenham Road in Felmersham experienced significant street flooding with muddy floodwater flowing over the road, visible rapid flow and turbulence; contributed to debris and siltation on the road and adjacent areas requiring cleansing and maintenance after waters receded. [IMG] (p9)
Included in an Environment Agency Flood Warning for the River Great Ouse (warning issued 24/12/2020 21:11). The area was affected by river flooding associated with the River Great Ouse during the 23–26 December 2020 event. [TAB] (p14)
