GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1710689,-0.524367,"<div id=""html_20c3860e423ad6b9a9303963622b39d6"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oakley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Low&ndash;lying roads between Harrold and Oakley were the subject of flood alerts and Harrold reported internal flooding: Harrold North (1 residential) and Harrold South (4 residential). Roads and bridges were reported impassable (Carlton Road; bridges). (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Bridges were reported impassable due to floodwater, restricting access and hindering emergency and council response. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Oakley was named in a Flood Warning for the River Great Ouse (issued 25/12/2020 05:46 for Oakley and Clapham); low&ndash;lying areas close to the river were threatened/affected on or around 25/12/2020. [TAB] (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Oakley,England,"Low–lying roads between Harrold and Oakley were the subject of flood alerts and Harrold reported internal flooding: Harrold North (1 residential) and Harrold South (4 residential). Roads and bridges were reported impassable (Carlton Road; bridges). (p7)
