GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.1971276,-0.2987135,"<div id=""html_f0c09653ca98ea3f3dbaa5c367e4a433"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wyboston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Great Ouse caused internal flooding to a commercial property. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Areas adjacent to the River Great Ouse were subject to river flooding; a Flood Alert was issued 24/12/2020 and flooding was recorded on 25/12/2020. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A flood warning was not issued for Wyboston during the December 2020 event; residents were affected and experienced concern and anxiety due to lack of timely warning and limited time to prepare. [MUL] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Blocked gullies and local highway drainage issues contributed to flooding during the December 2020 event. Gullies on High Street, Church Lane and Spring Lane were cleared of siltation and blockages in March 2021. Highway drainage in the vicinity of an affected property was cleared in May 2021 and inspections/remedial works were carried out; a community flood debrief/visit was also undertaken to identify follow&ndash;up measures. [MUL] (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 commercial [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Wyboston,England,"Flooding from the River Great Ouse caused internal flooding to a commercial property. [TAB,PAG] (p7)
