GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2897904,-0.5165551,"<div id=""html_93a85026ad6027bd56aeb6e9f01779d0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Yelden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High Street impassable due to flooding associated with River Till. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood alerts and warnings were issued for rivers affecting Yelden (River Kym / River Till / Riseley Brook) and flooding occurred around 23/12/2020; Flood Alert issued 23/12/2020 and Flood Warning 23/12/2020 16:57. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>LLFA officers communicated with the existing Community Flood Group as part of the response to flooding risk and reports. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River overtopping in the December 2020 event caused flooding affecting High Street and adjacent areas; drainage gullies became silted/blocked as a consequence and community flood debrief actions were recorded afterwards. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood&ndash;related actions for the location are recorded as complete following the December 2020 event; investigations and measures (community group potential, flood action planning and property protection suitability) were considered as part of the response. (p30)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Riverbank at the northern end overtopped toward the south during the flood event, contributing to flooding of areas immediately south of the bank. This prompted investigations into lowering or reinstating riverbank levels, consideration of Natural Flood Management storage areas upstream, and a capacity assessment of watercourse crossings to identify potential improvements. (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Yelden,England,"High Street impassable due to flooding associated with River Till. [TAB,PAG] (p7)
