GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2977267,-0.4672104,"<div id=""html_aaabbbd01a8f40888041b3364ff26c24"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Upper Dean</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overflow from an unnamed ordinary watercourse (tributary to the River Till) caused internal flooding of homes and made Brook Lane and Shay Lane impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Till&ndash;related flooding prompted a Flood Warning for Upper Dean on 23/12/2020 (Flood Warning issued 23/12/2020 16:57), indicating river flooding affected Upper Dean. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Upper Dean experienced flooding during December 2020 leading to actions including capacity checks at watercourse crossings, liaison with landowners to set maintenance regimes, and investigations into Natural Flood Management and potential upsizing to reduce future flood risk. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Upper Dean watercourse required liaison with landowners for inspection/maintenance and capacity checks at watercourse crossings to identify improvements, indicating the watercourse caused flooding impacts to the locality and infrastructure. [TAB] (p29)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The village was affected by flooding that prompted investigations and remedial planning: proposals to create a flood storage area upstream to hold back floodwater (catchment&ndash;wide approach), assessment of a culvert just upstream of an affected property (inspection, maintenance regime and capacity assessment), and investigation of suitability of property&ndash;level flood protection and flood action planning. (p30)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Upper Dean,England,"Overflow from an unnamed ordinary watercourse (tributary to the River Till) caused internal flooding of homes and made Brook Lane and Shay Lane impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)
River Till–related flooding prompted a Flood Warning for Upper Dean on 23/12/2020 (Flood Warning issued 23/12/2020 16:57), indicating river flooding affected Upper Dean. [TAB] (p14)
Upper Dean experienced flooding during December 2020 leading to actions including capacity checks at watercourse crossings, liaison with landowners to set maintenance regimes, and investigations into Natural Flood Management and potential upsizing to reduce future flood risk. [TAB,PAG] (p21)
