GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.25335991646264,-0.6230555173546211,"<div id=""html_0ff5f91c8a1428a05ab9dea0145f0d63"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Podington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a residential property caused by an unnamed ordinary watercourse (tributary to the River Nene); Vicarage Lane reported impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected highway drainage and raised local flood levels in Poddington; highway drainage blockages were cleared (around Orchard Lane in January 2021), the culvert beneath High Street was investigated for condition and capacity, and the influence of downstream river levels on local flood levels was assessed. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple investigations were proposed to reduce water entering the village: investigate a flood warning system on watercourse 2 upstream, investigate a flood storage area (Natural Flood Management) to reduce flows into the village, inspect Main River assets and river crossings (including beneath Mill Lane) for constrictions, and assess suitability of property flood resilience measures for affected properties. [TAB] (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential property [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Podington,England,"Internal flooding of a residential property caused by an unnamed ordinary watercourse (tributary to the River Nene); Vicarage Lane reported impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)
Flooding affected highway drainage and raised local flood levels in Poddington; highway drainage blockages were cleared (around Orchard Lane in January 2021), the culvert beneath High Street was investigated for condition and capacity, and the influence of downstream river levels on local flood levels was assessed. [TAB,PAG] (p21)
Multiple investigations were proposed to reduce water entering the village: investigate a flood warning system on watercourse 2 upstream, investigate a flood storage area (Natural Flood Management) to reduce flows into the village, inspect Main River assets and river crossings (including beneath Mill Lane) for constrictions, and assess suitability of property flood resilience measures for affected properties. [TAB] (p23)","1 residential property [TAB,PAG] (p7)",GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.19037,-0.6049492,"<div id=""html_716eda3990ce79661570163506b8e0ba"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Carlton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple locations in Carlton were affected by flood flows and drainage failures (The Marsh, The Causeway, Pavenham Road). Actions include clearing gullies/drains, community flood group setup, investigation of culverts/ditches, and liaison to construct a bund to divert water away from properties facing The Marsh. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water and overland flow routes directed water onto The Causeway and roads in Carlton, affecting properties; recommendations include ditch maintenance, community flood group set&ndash;up and investigation of local flood protection measures. [TAB] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Carlton,England,"Multiple locations in Carlton were affected by flood flows and drainage failures (The Marsh, The Causeway, Pavenham Road). Actions include clearing gullies/drains, community flood group setup, investigation of culverts/ditches, and liaison to construct a bund to divert water away from properties facing The Marsh. [TAB,PAG,MUL] (p21)
Surface water and overland flow routes directed water onto The Causeway and roads in Carlton, affecting properties; recommendations include ditch maintenance, community flood group set–up and investigation of local flood protection measures. [TAB] (p24)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2152272,-0.4596295,"<div id=""html_6eac9e67cdd85b68bf8176ff805aef32"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Thurleigh</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding caused internal flooding of a residential property. (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following the 23 December 2020 flooding, investigations and actions were required in Thurleigh and Upper Dean including setting up a community flood group, liaison with landowners to establish inspection and maintenance regimes for local watercourses (Upper Dean and Sharn Brook), capacity checks at watercourse crossings, and investigation of ditches/culverts on Robins Folly road with potential capital works to increase local drainage capacity. [TAB] (p29)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Thurleigh,England,"Surface water flooding caused internal flooding of a residential property. (p7)
Following the 23 December 2020 flooding, investigations and actions were required in Thurleigh and Upper Dean including setting up a community flood group, liaison with landowners to establish inspection and maintenance regimes for local watercourses (Upper Dean and Sharn Brook), capacity checks at watercourse crossings, and investigation of ditches/culverts on Robins Folly road with potential capital works to increase local drainage capacity. [TAB] (p29)",1 residential (p7),GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.156906,-0.3484621,"<div id=""html_db9ba314c3a2b68131bedec56ac3b7d4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Great Barford</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Roads, pathways, gardens and open spaces were inundated by flood waters and/or discharge to local drainage systems/highway culverts and gullies, causing access impacts. (p5)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Great Barford,England,"Roads, pathways, gardens and open spaces were inundated by flood waters and/or discharge to local drainage systems/highway culverts and gullies, causing access impacts. (p5)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
