GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.276253916090305,-0.41362359637705176,"<div id=""html_2b28e396c6d0cd4a46f1f95e31f898ef"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pertenhall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding reported: one residential property flooded due to Pertenhall Brook and one residential property flooded on Wood End Lane due to surface water; local road (Wood End) reported impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding associated with Pertenhall Brook affected properties adjacent to the watercourse; investigation recommended altering land levels between the brook and a residential property and carrying out inspections and remedial works to reduce future risk. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 residential property; 1 residential property [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Pertenhall,England,"Internal flooding reported: one residential property flooded due to Pertenhall Brook and one residential property flooded on Wood End Lane due to surface water; local road (Wood End) reported impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)
Flooding associated with Pertenhall Brook affected properties adjacent to the watercourse; investigation recommended altering land levels between the brook and a residential property and carrying out inspections and remedial works to reduce future risk. (p33)","1 residential property; 1 residential property [TAB,PAG] (p7)",GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2790839,-0.4505649,"<div id=""html_4008e1703075b7ad6463e32206e5b2dc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Swineshead</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from an unnamed ordinary watercourse (tributary to Pertenhall Brook) caused internal flooding to two residential properties; local road (High Street) reported impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The village experienced flooding that prompted clearing of highway drainage on High Street and Green Lane (completed May 2021); actions include investigating ditches, balancing pond, culverts, drainage capacity and potential upstream Natural Flood Management to reduce runoff into the village. [TAB,PAG] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Water from the Swineshead watercourse, balancing pond and culverts entered the village during the event; investigations were recommended (including a potential upstream Natural Flood Management scheme) to reduce the amount of water entering the village in future floods. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential properties [TAB,PAG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Swineshead,England,"Flooding from an unnamed ordinary watercourse (tributary to Pertenhall Brook) caused internal flooding to two residential properties; local road (High Street) reported impassable. [TAB,PAG] (p7)
