GB-BDF,2,2020-12-01,52.2057873,-0.5314322,"<div id=""html_16bcebbd2baf4431f3a1b773902cad1a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Radwell</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Bridges were reported impassable due to floodwater, restricting access and hindering emergency and council response. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Radwell,England,"Bridges were reported impassable due to floodwater, restricting access and hindering emergency and council response. (p9)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-01,Bedford flooding December 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-HEF,24,2020-02-16,52.1317117,-3.0632095,"<div id=""html_6516c2a5582674d9fe4df3d1c5b96729"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Millhalf Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The diversion channel was built as an overflow to the Millhalf Stream because of fluvial flood risk. The Millhalf Stream is implicated in the fluvial flooding that affected Whitney on Wye during February 2020; properties in the village experienced internal flooding (see Key Flood Event). (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; 1 outbuilding; internal depths up to 1 ft; outbuilding flooded to 3 ft (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Millhalf Brook,England,The diversion channel was built as an overflow to the Millhalf Stream because of fluvial flood risk. The Millhalf Stream is implicated in the fluvial flooding that affected Whitney on Wye during February 2020; properties in the village experienced internal flooding (see Key Flood Event). (p2),5 properties; 1 outbuilding; internal depths up to 1 ft; outbuilding flooded to 3 ft (p2),GB-HEF_24_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_24_2020-02-16,Whitney-On-Wye flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Whitney On Wye,055/Herefordshire County/23/Whitney/on/Wye.pdf
GB-HEF,24,2020-02-16,52.1186744,-3.0678995,"<div id=""html_644f4d092550a33e1e00d639ae0da77b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whitney Village Road, Whitney-On-Wye</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Whitney Village Road is labelled on the EA flood map and lies close to the river where Flood Zone 3 covers the southern part of the village. The road is therefore exposed to river flooding and likely to have been within the high&ndash;risk flood area during the key event on 16 February 2020; this would make it liable to inundation or floodwater over the carriageway (specific reports of closure or damage are not provided). [IMG] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,"Whitney Village Road, Whitney-On-Wye",England,Whitney Village Road is labelled on the EA flood map and lies close to the river where Flood Zone 3 covers the southern part of the village. The road is therefore exposed to river flooding and likely to have been within the high–risk flood area during the key event on 16 February 2020; this would make it liable to inundation or floodwater over the carriageway (specific reports of closure or damage are not provided). [IMG] (p1),,GB-HEF_24_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_24_2020-02-16,Whitney-On-Wye flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Whitney On Wye,055/Herefordshire County/23/Whitney/on/Wye.pdf
GB-HEF,24,2020-02-16,52.121684,-3.0704285,"<div id=""html_5b8293e170c3cb26b73bfd9a0b7f8e32"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Church Lane, Whitney-On-Wye</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Church Lane is shown on the Environment Agency flood map within the settlement area where Flood Zone 3 is concentrated near the River Wye. It is therefore exposed to river flooding and likely to have been within the high&ndash;risk mapped area during the 16 February 2020 event, making it susceptible to inundation or floodwater on the lane (no specific flood depths or property impacts are stated). [IMG] (p1)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,"Church Lane, Whitney-On-Wye",England,"Church Lane is shown on the Environment Agency flood map within the settlement area where Flood Zone 3 is concentrated near the River Wye. It is therefore exposed to river flooding and likely to have been within the high–risk mapped area during the 16 February 2020 event, making it susceptible to inundation or floodwater on the lane (no specific flood depths or property impacts are stated). [IMG] (p1)",,GB-HEF_24_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_24_2020-02-16,Whitney-On-Wye flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Whitney On Wye,055/Herefordshire County/23/Whitney/on/Wye.pdf
GB-HEF,24,2020-02-16,52.1200196,-3.0682535,"<div id=""html_e12e4a4e1cd526cb96312e284bd75016"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whitney-On-Wye</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Five properties in Whitney on Wye flooded internally in February 2020 with internal depths up to 1 ft lasting 1&ndash;2 days; one outbuilding flooded to a depth of 3 ft. Properties that reported flooding are located in Flood Zone 3. Two listed (cultural heritage) properties are located within the Flood Zone. [PAG] (p2)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; 1 outbuilding; 2 listed properties [PAG] (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Whitney-On-Wye,England,Five properties in Whitney on Wye flooded internally in February 2020 with internal depths up to 1 ft lasting 1–2 days; one outbuilding flooded to a depth of 3 ft. Properties that reported flooding are located in Flood Zone 3. Two listed (cultural heritage) properties are located within the Flood Zone. [PAG] (p2),5 properties; 1 outbuilding; 2 listed properties [PAG] (p2),GB-HEF_24_2020-02-16.html,GB-HEF_24_2020-02-16,Whitney-On-Wye flooding 16 Feb 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report: Whitney On Wye,055/Herefordshire County/23/Whitney/on/Wye.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-23,52.1303703,-0.4481412,"<div id=""html_17e20121212cc261756c31932ba640f3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oasis Beach Pool</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Footpath access in the vicinity of Oasis Pool was impacted by flooding, presenting access issues due to flood waters and/or discharge to local drainage/highway culverts and gullies. (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Access to Oasis Pool via the footpath from Cardington Road was cut off by floodwater; nearby inundation left debris and siltation requiring subsequent cleansing and maintenance. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Oasis Beach Pool,England,"Footpath access in the vicinity of Oasis Pool was impacted by flooding, presenting access issues due to flood waters and/or discharge to local drainage/highway culverts and gullies. (p5)
Access to Oasis Pool via the footpath from Cardington Road was cut off by floodwater; nearby inundation left debris and siltation requiring subsequent cleansing and maintenance. (p9)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-23.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-23,Bedford flooding 23 Dec 2020 - 26 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BDF,2,2020-12-23,52.1323589,-0.469886,"<div id=""html_2e9895082925755275b3248a917ded3f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Borough Hall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Large area of floodwater surrounded Borough Hall, with water extending up to the base of the building and nearby tree, demonstrating inundation of the site and restricting access. [IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,Borough Hall,England,"Large area of floodwater surrounded Borough Hall, with water extending up to the base of the building and nearby tree, demonstrating inundation of the site and restricting access. [IMG] (p10)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-23.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-23,Bedford flooding 23 Dec 2020 - 26 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
