GB-BDF,2,2020-12-23,52.2442973,-0.4035977,"<div id=""html_752505f9ac1ac8b77d9124267e4ac613"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Keysoe Row East, Keysoe Row</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of 2 residential properties caused by surface water. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Pond and culvert blockage/overflow led to surface water flooding affecting the locality and properties; culverts were cleared (Feb&ndash;Mar 2021) and further maintenance/structural works (headwall, pond formalisation) were proposed to improve drainage. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties at Keysoe Row East were affected by flooding caused by overwhelmed ditches/ponds and restricted culvert discharge. Investigations and remedial actions were identified and undertaken (including clearing the culvert connecting the pond to the ditch in Feb&ndash;Mar 2021), and measures such as flood barriers, non&ndash;return valves and a possible new headwall were proposed. Work was also proposed to liaise with landowners to maintain ditches and ponds and to develop a community flood group and property&ndash;level resilience plans for the affected properties. [TAB] (p32)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from surrounding fields contributed to flooding risk; the report recommends formalising the pond north of Keysoe Row East to hold more runoff and clearing/maintaining ditches and culverts to increase capacity. [TAB] (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 residential [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"Keysoe Row East, Keysoe Row",England,"Internal flooding of 2 residential properties caused by surface water. [TAB] (p7)
