GB-BDF,2,2020-12-23,52.2063431,-0.6141821,"<div id=""html_c7eee460cd141e23c69f085aa2778c26"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wood Road, Harrold</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood flows overtopped toward/onto Wood Road; investigations and proposed works were identified (investigate responsibility for the watercourse north of Wood Road, maintenance to maximise capacity, potential addition of a second pipe beneath the road, works to the diverter to direct flows into the flood channel, and an outflow from the flood channel into Tustings Lake) to reduce future overtopping. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood flows overtopped onto Wood Road and the report recommends increasing the capacity of the watercourse crossing (second pipe beneath the road), works to the diverter to encourage flows into the flood channel, and potential outflow works into Tustings Lake to reduce overtopping. [TAB] (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Bedford,"Wood Road, Harrold",England,"Flood flows overtopped toward/onto Wood Road; investigations and proposed works were identified (investigate responsibility for the watercourse north of Wood Road, maintenance to maximise capacity, potential addition of a second pipe beneath the road, works to the diverter to direct flows into the flood channel, and an outflow from the flood channel into Tustings Lake) to reduce future overtopping. [TAB] (p21)
Flood flows overtopped onto Wood Road and the report recommends increasing the capacity of the watercourse crossing (second pipe beneath the road), works to the diverter to encourage flows into the flood channel, and potential outflow works into Tustings Lake to reduce overtopping. [TAB] (p22)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-23.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-23,Bedford flooding 23 Dec 2020 - 26 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
