Surface water and overland flow routes directed water onto The Causeway and roads in Carlton, affecting properties; recommendations include ditch maintenance, community flood group set–up and investigation of local flood protection measures. [TAB] (p24)",,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-23.html,GB-BDF_2_2020-12-23,Bedford flooding 23 Dec 2020 - 26 Dec 2020,"Flood Investigation Report, Locations: Various across Bedford Borough, Flood Event: December 2020",005/Bedford/005/2021/Bedford/Bedford/Oct/2021.pdf
GB-BKM,5,2014-03-01,51.633296692438385,-0.5702658135162323,"<div id=""html_bb82d62debfc07953fd68ce63f96cc07"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Telephone Exchange</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The British Telecom telephone exchange in Chalfont St Giles was impacted by groundwater flooding. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High groundwater levels flooded the BT telephone exchange; BT pumped excess groundwater out of the basement. The over&ndash;pumping contributed to flooding of the village high street and led to closure of the carpark and traffic restrictions. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The BT telephone exchange in Chalfont St Giles was impacted by groundwater flooding. (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The BT telephone exchange was impacted by groundwater flooding during the event; recommendations identify improving its resilience against groundwater flooding and procedures for pumping excess groundwater. [TAB] (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 telephone exchange (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Telephone Exchange,England,"The British Telecom telephone exchange in Chalfont St Giles was impacted by groundwater flooding. (p4)
High groundwater levels flooded the BT telephone exchange; BT pumped excess groundwater out of the basement. The over–pumping contributed to flooding of the village high street and led to closure of the carpark and traffic restrictions. (p18)
The BT telephone exchange in Chalfont St Giles was impacted by groundwater flooding. (p23)
The BT telephone exchange was impacted by groundwater flooding during the event; recommendations identify improving its resilience against groundwater flooding and procedures for pumping excess groundwater. [TAB] (p24)",1 telephone exchange (p23),GB-BKM_5_2014-03-01.html,GB-BKM_5_2014-03-01,Chalfont St Giles flooding March–April 2014,"Chalfont St Giles, March to April 2014",018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2014/Buckinghamshire County/chalfont-st-giles/March/2014.pdf
GB-BKM,5,2014-03-01,51.6480032,-0.5800363,"<div id=""html_b66b633032a58f9507c583ca5bf47527"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Misbourne</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Misbourne valley funnels groundwater, surface water and fluvial flow into the valley bottom, concentrating floodwater into the centre of the village and increasing inundation risk to properties and infrastructure shown on the flood maps. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The chalk stream (River Misbourne) experienced elevated baseflows driven by groundwater recharge; this resulted in fluvial flooding of the Misbourne and groundwater flooding affecting the river corridor during the winter&ndash;spring 2013/14 event. [MUL] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Misbourne was at bank full and in spate, causing minor flooding of bankside gardens and farmland adjacent to the watercourse. (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,River Misbourne,England,"The Misbourne valley funnels groundwater, surface water and fluvial flow into the valley bottom, concentrating floodwater into the centre of the village and increasing inundation risk to properties and infrastructure shown on the flood maps. [PAG] (p12)
The chalk stream (River Misbourne) experienced elevated baseflows driven by groundwater recharge; this resulted in fluvial flooding of the Misbourne and groundwater flooding affecting the river corridor during the winter–spring 2013/14 event. [MUL] (p15)
The River Misbourne was at bank full and in spate, causing minor flooding of bankside gardens and farmland adjacent to the watercourse. (p18)",,GB-BKM_5_2014-03-01.html,GB-BKM_5_2014-03-01,Chalfont St Giles flooding March–April 2014,"Chalfont St Giles, March to April 2014",018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2014/Buckinghamshire County/chalfont-st-giles/March/2014.pdf
GB-BKM,5,2014-03-01,51.6313294,-0.5706319,"<div id=""html_225364bcf0a241ff2a92ab8229517606"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Chalfont St Giles</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Locality affected by the incident; internal flooding of commercial premises and flooding of the BT telephone exchange occurred on the High Street. (p6)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Shown within the mapped flood extents (surface water and fluvial); High Street was identified as being at risk with nearby commercial and residential properties exposed to inundation. [PAG] (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 commercial premises; 1 BT telephone exchange (p6)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,"High Street, Chalfont St Giles",England,"Locality affected by the incident; internal flooding of commercial premises and flooding of the BT telephone exchange occurred on the High Street. (p6)
Shown within the mapped flood extents (surface water and fluvial); High Street was identified as being at risk with nearby commercial and residential properties exposed to inundation. [PAG] (p12)",4 commercial premises; 1 BT telephone exchange (p6),GB-BKM_5_2014-03-01.html,GB-BKM_5_2014-03-01,Chalfont St Giles flooding March–April 2014,"Chalfont St Giles, March to April 2014",018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2014/Buckinghamshire County/chalfont-st-giles/March/2014.pdf
GB-BKM,5,2014-03-01,51.6336986,-0.5677634,"<div id=""html_2c80455fb2d057eb8c949417073fa4a0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pheasant Hill, Chalfont St Giles</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Shown within the mapped flood extents (surface water and fluvial); the road corridor at Pheasant Hill was identified at risk and adjacent commercial and residential properties were exposed to inundation. [PAG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,"Pheasant Hill, Chalfont St Giles",England,Shown within the mapped flood extents (surface water and fluvial); the road corridor at Pheasant Hill was identified at risk and adjacent commercial and residential properties were exposed to inundation. [PAG] (p12),,GB-BKM_5_2014-03-01.html,GB-BKM_5_2014-03-01,Chalfont St Giles flooding March–April 2014,"Chalfont St Giles, March to April 2014",018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2014/Buckinghamshire County/chalfont-st-giles/March/2014.pdf
GB-BKM,5,2014-03-01,51.6321046,-0.5697912,"<div id=""html_1aae8667156bda9549055ed2b102e564"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chalfont St Giles</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Exceptionally high groundwater levels in the chalk aquifer caused groundwater flooding in the village, which affected local critical infrastructure including the Affinity Water pumping station, the British Telecom telephone exchange, and the main access road to the village shops. (p4)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The locality affected by the flood incident was the High Street &mdash; the village centre experienced flooding during the event. [PAG] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water and fluvial flooding affected the valley bottom and centre of the village. Flood extents from the central watercourse overlap residential and commercial property footprints and threaten the main road through the village (Pheasant Hill / High Street); the valley topography funnels groundwater, surface water and fluvial flow into the village centre increasing flood depths and extent. [PAG,IMG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The local river (Misbourne) was at bank full and in spate during the event, causing minor flooding of bankside gardens and farmland in the Chalfont St Giles locality. No reports indicated failings or blockages in highway or surface water drainage that would have worsened the flooding. [PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Exceptionally high groundwater levels in the chalk aquifer flooded parts of the village: a public water supply pumping station and the BT telephone exchange were flooded; over&ndash;pumping from the BT exchange caused flooding of the high street and a carpark, the main street was reduced to one direction of traffic, and there was an economic impact on small businesses. [PAG] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Exceptionally high groundwater levels in the chalk aquifer caused groundwater flooding across the village that affected local critical infrastructure: the Affinity Water pumping station and the BT telephone exchange were impacted, and the main access road to the shops in the village centre was flooded, restricting access. (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Groundwater flooding in spring 2014 impacted the village: local critical infrastructure was affected (Affinity Water pumping station and the BT telephone exchange) and the main access road to the village shops was flooded. [TAB,PAG] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Buckinghamshire,Chalfont St Giles,England,"Exceptionally high groundwater levels in the chalk aquifer caused groundwater flooding in the village, which affected local critical infrastructure including the Affinity Water pumping station, the British Telecom telephone exchange, and the main access road to the village shops. (p4)
The locality affected by the flood incident was the High Street — the village centre experienced flooding during the event. [PAG] (p7)
Surface–water and fluvial flooding affected the valley bottom and centre of the village. Flood extents from the central watercourse overlap residential and commercial property footprints and threaten the main road through the village (Pheasant Hill / High Street); the valley topography funnels groundwater, surface water and fluvial flow into the village centre increasing flood depths and extent. [PAG,IMG] (p12)
The local river (Misbourne) was at bank full and in spate during the event, causing minor flooding of bankside gardens and farmland in the Chalfont St Giles locality. No reports indicated failings or blockages in highway or surface water drainage that would have worsened the flooding. [PAG] (p17)
Exceptionally high groundwater levels in the chalk aquifer flooded parts of the village: a public water supply pumping station and the BT telephone exchange were flooded; over–pumping from the BT exchange caused flooding of the high street and a carpark, the main street was reduced to one direction of traffic, and there was an economic impact on small businesses. [PAG] (p18)
Exceptionally high groundwater levels in the chalk aquifer caused groundwater flooding across the village that affected local critical infrastructure: the Affinity Water pumping station and the BT telephone exchange were impacted, and the main access road to the shops in the village centre was flooded, restricting access. (p23)
Groundwater flooding in spring 2014 impacted the village: local critical infrastructure was affected (Affinity Water pumping station and the BT telephone exchange) and the main access road to the village shops was flooded. [TAB,PAG] (p24)",,GB-BKM_5_2014-03-01.html,GB-BKM_5_2014-03-01,Chalfont St Giles flooding March–April 2014,"Chalfont St Giles, March to April 2014",018/Buckinghamshire County/018/2014/Buckinghamshire County/chalfont-st-giles/March/2014.pdf
GB-CAM,31,2023-05-09,52.675721,0.157651,"<div id=""html_f06412f68426b9eacf76d85440a8de19"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Osborne Road, Wisbech</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Approximate location of reported flooding indicated on the map; flooding led to internal property flooding reported to the LLFA. (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 9 May 2023 a high&ndash;intensity storm rapidly filled the local surface water drainage to capacity; excess surface water flowed down Osborne Road to the low point where it accumulated to about 300 mm above the drain cover. Only one road gully served the collection point, so water levels rose quickly and five properties were flooded. The sewer system was reported to be overwhelmed. The fire service pumped water away and levels had subsided by 20:00. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water collected at a low spot where the drainage was overwhelmed/restricted; gullies required cleaning and further inspection of the surface water system to its outfall was recommended. [TAB] (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; approximately 300 mm accumulation above drain cover; one road gully (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Osborne Road, Wisbech",England,"Approximate location of reported flooding indicated on the map; flooding led to internal property flooding reported to the LLFA. (p1)
