GB-CAM,31,2023-05-09,52.665173,0.1606824,"<div id=""html_d7603467abc754f3fc0230be41c17eaa"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wisbech</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal property flooding reported across the town; LLFA received five flood reports describing internal property flooding. [TAB] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A high&ndash;intensity storm on 9 May 2023 caused surface water flooding in Wisbech (notably Osborne Road). The local surface water drainage and sewer system were overwhelmed; excess water flowed to the lowest point in the road and accumulated to roughly 300 mm above the drain cover. Five properties were flooded. The fire service attended and pumped water away and levels had subsided by 20:00 the same day. (p2)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Intense rainfall on 9th May 2023 overwhelmed the capacity of the surface water drainage network, causing flooding in Wisbech. (p3)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 flood reports [TAB] (p1)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; approximately 300 mm accumulation above drain cover; one road gully at collection point (p2)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Wisbech,England,"Internal property flooding reported across the town; LLFA received five flood reports describing internal property flooding. [TAB] (p1)
