GB-NNH,35,2014-08-10,52.5641762,-0.5180115,"<div id=""html_35adb5b0a4913199a6ea3500fe5b0708"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wood Road, King's Cliffe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Water and soil flowed out of the drainage system from the Sovereign Grange estate onto Wood Road; the flow was mixed with soil (light brown) and passed southeast across Wood Road into rear gardens of properties on West Street, leaving deposits of fine silt. [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residual risk of surface water flooding from the Sovereign Grange development can flow along Wood Road to other properties; the report recommends carrying out works on Wood Road to contain this surface water risk without causing flooding elsewhere or compromising drainage. (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water pooled at the Oak Lane / Wood Road junction during heavy rain on 10th August 2014, resulting in visible road flooding at the junction and indications of drainage overflow or blockage. [IMG,PAG] (p63)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water inundated the carriageway at the Oak Lane / Wood Road junction on Wood Road, with water pooling across most of the road surface and extending toward the junction and adjacent properties/parked vehicles (photographed). [IMG,PAG] (p64)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"Wood Road, King's Cliffe",England,"Water and soil flowed out of the drainage system from the Sovereign Grange estate onto Wood Road; the flow was mixed with soil (light brown) and passed southeast across Wood Road into rear gardens of properties on West Street, leaving deposits of fine silt. [PAG] (p14)
Residual risk of surface water flooding from the Sovereign Grange development can flow along Wood Road to other properties; the report recommends carrying out works on Wood Road to contain this surface water risk without causing flooding elsewhere or compromising drainage. (p23)
Surface water pooled at the Oak Lane / Wood Road junction during heavy rain on 10th August 2014, resulting in visible road flooding at the junction and indications of drainage overflow or blockage. [IMG,PAG] (p63)
Surface water inundated the carriageway at the Oak Lane / Wood Road junction on Wood Road, with water pooling across most of the road surface and extending toward the junction and adjacent properties/parked vehicles (photographed). [IMG,PAG] (p64)",,GB-NNH_35_2014-08-10.html,GB-NNH_35_2014-08-10,King's Cliffe flooding 10 Aug 2014,"Flood Investigation Report: Sovereign Grange, Wood Road, Kings Cliffe, 10th August 2014",090/North Northamptonshire/Kings-Cliffe/021015-2.pdf
GB-NNH,35,2014-08-10,52.5635316,-0.5197143,"<div id=""html_a753d3eb42c84839354e371bba32d55c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Street, King's Cliffe</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from Wood Road flowed through private property to areas around two properties on West Street; internal flooding occurred in one property on West Street (reported incidents). [TAB,MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater from Sovereign Grange, travelling across Wood Road, entered rear gardens of two properties on West Street. At one property water built up against the building walls, infiltrated through the walls and entered internal areas (internal flooding). At a second property areas of the rear garden were submerged. Fine silt deposits were left by the flow; water later flowed around the internally flooded property into the carriageway of West Street and into highway drainage. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two properties; one property [TAB,MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (1 internally flooded; 1 with rear garden submerged) (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",North Northamptonshire,"West Street, King's Cliffe",England,"Floodwater from Wood Road flowed through private property to areas around two properties on West Street; internal flooding occurred in one property on West Street (reported incidents). [TAB,MUL] (p11)
Floodwater from Sovereign Grange, travelling across Wood Road, entered rear gardens of two properties on West Street. At one property water built up against the building walls, infiltrated through the walls and entered internal areas (internal flooding). At a second property areas of the rear garden were submerged. Fine silt deposits were left by the flow; water later flowed around the internally flooded property into the carriageway of West Street and into highway drainage. (p14)","two properties; one property [TAB,MUL] (p11)
