GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.6884889,-1.8393557,"<div id=""html_cdf461583e7b2d068b8126b58eeceed1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Calder</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping of the River Calder banks that was the primary source of the December 2015 flooding in Padiham; contributed to internal flooding of properties. Silt and gravel built up under Padiham Bridge requiring removal works programmed into EA maintenance. [TAB] (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>147 properties [TAB] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Calder,England,Overtopping of the River Calder banks that was the primary source of the December 2015 flooding in Padiham; contributed to internal flooding of properties. Silt and gravel built up under Padiham Bridge requiring removal works programmed into EA maintenance. [TAB] (p24),147 properties [TAB] (p24),GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.7995311,-2.3117253,"<div id=""html_924ff8cd56ba4151e942012308b5c7ec"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Padiham Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Silt and gravel deposition under Padiham Bridge as a result of the River Calder flooding; EA has bid for funds to remove the silt/gravel and this work is scheduled in the EA maintenance programme (planned 2018/19). [TAB] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Padiham Bridge,England,Silt and gravel deposition under Padiham Bridge as a result of the River Calder flooding; EA has bid for funds to remove the silt/gravel and this work is scheduled in the EA maintenance programme (planned 2018/19). [TAB] (p24),,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.7877265,-2.3135429,"<div id=""html_f6a02ae0b949881f3db9a89ff3e2e588"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Manchester Road, Burnley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overland flow from the blocked culverted watercourse reached Manchester Road and likely overwhelmed the existing highway drainage system, causing water to accumulate at the fronts of nearby properties until it drained away. Lancashire Highways carried out a CCTV survey of the highway drainage outside affected properties, identified two drainage faults which have been repaired. An appraisal of the highway drainage on Manchester Road has been recommended. [TAB,PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Volume of water from a blocked culverted watercourse was routed overland and reached Manchester Road, overwhelming the highway drainage and causing water to accumulate at the front of nearby properties until it drained away. Highway drainage faults on Manchester Road were subsequently repaired. [PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A blockage was identified within a culverted watercourse located approximately 6 m north east of Manchester Road; the blockage prevented the Lead Local Flood Authority from completing its investigation at that point so any impact of the blockage during the flood event is unknown. Local residents confirmed no further flooding has occurred at this point since the December 2015 flood event. Lancashire Highways have appraised the highway drainage on Manchester Road and programmed major drainage improvement works. [TAB] (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two drainage faults [TAB,PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two drainage faults [PAG] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Manchester Road, Burnley",England,"Overland flow from the blocked culverted watercourse reached Manchester Road and likely overwhelmed the existing highway drainage system, causing water to accumulate at the fronts of nearby properties until it drained away. Lancashire Highways carried out a CCTV survey of the highway drainage outside affected properties, identified two drainage faults which have been repaired. An appraisal of the highway drainage on Manchester Road has been recommended. [TAB,PAG] (p16)
Volume of water from a blocked culverted watercourse was routed overland and reached Manchester Road, overwhelming the highway drainage and causing water to accumulate at the front of nearby properties until it drained away. Highway drainage faults on Manchester Road were subsequently repaired. [PAG] (p17)
A blockage was identified within a culverted watercourse located approximately 6 m north east of Manchester Road; the blockage prevented the Lead Local Flood Authority from completing its investigation at that point so any impact of the blockage during the flood event is unknown. Local residents confirmed no further flooding has occurred at this point since the December 2015 flood event. Lancashire Highways have appraised the highway drainage on Manchester Road and programmed major drainage improvement works. [TAB] (p18)","two drainage faults [TAB,PAG] (p16)
two drainage faults [PAG] (p17)",GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.7965803,-2.3100642,"<div id=""html_44d35c5e477c4ec4b1616b73961a643b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Melbourne Street, Padiham</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Green Brook at Back Melbourne Street contained debris that required removal; retaining walls adjacent to the street were collapsing and access was being arranged for debris removal and repair (LCC Highways to repair their section in 2017; discussions with other riparian owners ongoing). [TAB] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Melbourne Street, Padiham",England,Green Brook at Back Melbourne Street contained debris that required removal; retaining walls adjacent to the street were collapsing and access was being arranged for debris removal and repair (LCC Highways to repair their section in 2017; discussions with other riparian owners ongoing). [TAB] (p24),,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.7917374,-2.2986353,"<div id=""html_9335a6af2a347bddec6cb278f8cfb6ea"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Printers Fold, Burnley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Retaining wall collapse at the Green Brook channel at Printer Fold with debris in the channel; EA removed debris (difficult access) and riparian private owners are undertaking repairs to the retaining walls. [TAB] (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 retaining wall collapse [TAB] (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Printers Fold, Burnley",England,Retaining wall collapse at the Green Brook channel at Printer Fold with debris in the channel; EA removed debris (difficult access) and riparian private owners are undertaking repairs to the retaining walls. [TAB] (p24),1 retaining wall collapse [TAB] (p24),GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_c6bb0f9984bda79b2cb2e3da03da08b5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding occurred across Lancashire in December 2015, affecting communities and prompting review of communication and coordinated actions by risk management authorities. (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The December 2015 floods caused widespread flooding across the county, affecting homes and businesses; the event resulted in major impacts on people, homes and businesses and led to recommendations for property&ndash;level flood resilience and preparatory/response actions by risk management authorities. [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding during the extreme storms and rainfall of November&ndash;December 2015 that caused damage across the county, including damage to private gardens, garages and out&ndash;buildings, business premises, agricultural property, roads, bridges, retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools, village and town halls. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two major storm events in December 2015 caused flooding across Lancashire, affecting multiple communities; a countywide Section 19&ndash;style investigation was initiated to identify affected communities and priorities. [TAB,PAG] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Significant flooding occurred across Lancashire in December 2015, affecting communities and prompting review of communication and coordinated actions by risk management authorities. (p3)
The December 2015 floods caused widespread flooding across the county, affecting homes and businesses; the event resulted in major impacts on people, homes and businesses and led to recommendations for property–level flood resilience and preparatory/response actions by risk management authorities. [TAB] (p8)
Widespread flooding during the extreme storms and rainfall of November–December 2015 that caused damage across the county, including damage to private gardens, garages and out–buildings, business premises, agricultural property, roads, bridges, retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools, village and town halls. (p9)
Two major storm events in December 2015 caused flooding across Lancashire, affecting multiple communities; a countywide Section 19–style investigation was initiated to identify affected communities and priorities. [TAB,PAG] (p10)","over 2,500 properties [TAB] (p8)
over 2,500 properties (p9)",GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.8790402,-2.1717795,"<div id=""html_1d0526dbad52b6ddfdf126312b90eb1e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Pendle</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents and businesses in Pendle were affected by the December 2015 floods; a local recovery 'drop&ndash;in' event was held on 21 Jan 2016 to provide information, support, gather eyewitness reports and offer advice on recovery, flood warnings and property resilience. (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Pendle,England,"Residents and businesses in Pendle were affected by the December 2015 floods; a local recovery 'drop–in' event was held on 21 Jan 2016 to provide information, support, gather eyewitness reports and offer advice on recovery, flood warnings and property resilience. (p9)","over 2,500 properties (p9)",GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.6109397,-2.8565713,"<div id=""html_94aa4e07c8a93b963cacc57a5a786a52"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents and businesses in West Lancashire were affected by the December 2015 floods; recovery 'drop&ndash;in' events were held in the district (Parbold Village Hall on 25 Jan 2016 and Fiveways Public House on 01 Feb 2016) to support affected people and gather local reports. (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,West Lancashire,England,Residents and businesses in West Lancashire were affected by the December 2015 floods; recovery 'drop–in' events were held in the district (Parbold Village Hall on 25 Jan 2016 and Fiveways Public House on 01 Feb 2016) to support affected people and gather local reports. (p9),"over 2,500 properties (p9)",GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.7764241058126,-2.2199993399289806,"<div id=""html_39441daf9bc9466e96f3ff5237fbfa73"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Burnley District</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of Lancashire which experienced the extreme November&ndash;December 2015 storms and flooding; community infrastructure (including schools) in the county were damaged during the December 2015 flood event. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to residential properties: Briercliffe (Lane Bottom Area) &mdash; 4 properties suffered internal flooding; Brunshaw Area &mdash; 3 properties suffered internal flooding. The LLFA concluded the magnitude and intensity of the rainfall event was likely the primary cause for the Briercliffe flooding. [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Burnley experienced internal property flooding due to heavy rainfall / surface water: the Clow Bridge area had properties internally flooded. [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties from surface water. A blockage in a culverted watercourse on land to the rear of affected properties caused flow to rise to the surface and travel overland towards Manchester Road, overwhelming the highway drainage and allowing water to accumulate at the fronts of properties until it drained away. The culvert blockage was removed and normal flow was restored; no repeated flooding reported since. (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of a residential property in the Ightenhill area. [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>In the Rose Hill area one property suffered internal flooding. [PAG] (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties; 3 properties [PAG] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties (Clow Bridge area); 3 properties (Brunshaw area) [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [PAG] (p19)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property [PAG] (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Burnley District,England,"Part of Lancashire which experienced the extreme November–December 2015 storms and flooding; community infrastructure (including schools) in the county were damaged during the December 2015 flood event. (p9)
Internal flooding to residential properties: Briercliffe (Lane Bottom Area) — 4 properties suffered internal flooding; Brunshaw Area — 3 properties suffered internal flooding. The LLFA concluded the magnitude and intensity of the rainfall event was likely the primary cause for the Briercliffe flooding. [PAG] (p14)
Parts of Burnley experienced internal property flooding due to heavy rainfall / surface water: the Clow Bridge area had properties internally flooded. [PAG] (p15)
Internal flooding of residential properties from surface water. A blockage in a culverted watercourse on land to the rear of affected properties caused flow to rise to the surface and travel overland towards Manchester Road, overwhelming the highway drainage and allowing water to accumulate at the fronts of properties until it drained away. The culvert blockage was removed and normal flow was restored; no repeated flooding reported since. (p16)
Internal flooding of a residential property in the Ightenhill area. [PAG] (p19)
In the Rose Hill area one property suffered internal flooding. [PAG] (p20)","4 properties; 3 properties [PAG] (p14)
5 properties (Clow Bridge area); 3 properties (Brunshaw area) [PAG] (p15)
5 properties (p16)
1 property [PAG] (p19)
1 property [PAG] (p20)",GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.70249,-2.201046,"<div id=""html_ff3ee6a8088baa74c53282c89a3e7658"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rossendale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rossendale had residents affected by the extreme storms and rainfall of Nov&ndash;Dec 2015; the drop&ndash;in event in Irwell Vale (within Rossendale) on 10 Feb 2016 formed part of the recovery/support response for those affected. [MUL] (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (across Lancashire) were flooded in December 2015 [MUL] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Rossendale,England,Rossendale had residents affected by the extreme storms and rainfall of Nov–Dec 2015; the drop–in event in Irwell Vale (within Rossendale) on 10 Feb 2016 formed part of the recovery/support response for those affected. [MUL] (p9),"over 2,500 properties (across Lancashire) were flooded in December 2015 [MUL] (p9)",GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,54.04674035288858,-2.8001777457545383,"<div id=""html_a4be7c29addac5d46cbb0e9bb4b2eff2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancaster</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Lancaster was affected by the December 2015 floods; a recovery 'drop&ndash;in' event was held at Our Lady's Catholic College on 26 Jan 2016 to provide advice and support to residents and businesses and to collect eyewitness accounts. (p9)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancaster,England,Lancaster was affected by the December 2015 floods; a recovery 'drop–in' event was held at Our Lady's Catholic College on 26 Jan 2016 to provide advice and support to residents and businesses and to collect eyewitness accounts. (p9),"over 2,500 properties (p9)",GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.6775859865751,-2.316467158860694,"<div id=""html_4bbe0abd1c47886eb35aa694df60c995"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Irwell Vale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residents in Irwell Vale were affected by the December 2015 floods; a multi&ndash;agency drop&ndash;in event to provide information, support and gather eyewitness reports was held there on 10 Feb 2016. [MUL] (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Irwell Vale,England,"Residents in Irwell Vale were affected by the December 2015 floods; a multi–agency drop–in event to provide information, support and gather eyewitness reports was held there on 10 Feb 2016. [MUL] (p9)",,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.8116715,-2.2039784,"<div id=""html_76d3758de70b1e138fb3ea7f94d1ab32"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Harle Syke</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties in the Harle Syke area of the community. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Harle Syke,England,Internal flooding of residential properties in the Harle Syke area of the community. (p12),4 properties (p12),GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.7871605,-2.2183178,"<div id=""html_2e483684746ccfb560826af03e5b2353"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Brunshaw</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to properties caused by heavy rainfall; three properties suffered internal flooding. (p15)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Brunshaw,England,Internal flooding to properties caused by heavy rainfall; three properties suffered internal flooding. (p15),3 properties (p15),GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,1,2015-12-01,53.7501358,-2.2684401,"<div id=""html_f0073b05c94caa4addc6114de867b8cc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Clow Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Five properties suffered internal flooding from surface water. A culverted watercourse blockage on land to the rear of the properties restricted flow, caused water to rise to the surface and flow overland to Manchester Road, overwhelming highway drainage. The blockage was removed and flow restored; no repeated flooding reported. (p16)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Clow Bridge,England,"Five properties suffered internal flooding from surface water. A culverted watercourse blockage on land to the rear of the properties restricted flow, caused water to rise to the surface and flow overland to Manchester Road, overwhelming highway drainage. The blockage was removed and flow restored; no repeated flooding reported. (p16)",5 properties (p16),GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_1_2015-12-01,Burnley District flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Burnley District Flood Report: Recommended Action,069/Lancashire County/burnley-final-report.pdf
