GB-LAN,27,2015-12-01,53.6899922,-2.6751999,"<div id=""html_efede3be86fd13ac1d8cae36b4bec9a7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Wigan Road, Buckshaw Village</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding occurred at a property on Wigan Road; the property suffered internal inundation during the December 2015 flood event. (p37)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p37)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Wigan Road, Buckshaw Village",England,Internal flooding occurred at a property on Wigan Road; the property suffered internal inundation during the December 2015 flood event. (p37),1 property (p37),GB-LAN_27_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_27_2015-12-01,South Ribble flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,South Ribble District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/south-ribble-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,27,2015-12-01,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_49a981c050af0cf243783ac93a57bd50"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding hit Lancashire in December 2015, affecting local communities and exposing shortcomings in communication and coordination; this prompted the development of district&ndash;level reports to inform affected communities and identify opportunities for future flood risk management. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme storms and rainfall in November/December 2015 caused flooding throughout December 2015 affecting the county: over 2,500 properties flooded and damage to private gardens, garages and out&ndash;buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges and retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools, village and town halls. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two major storm events in December 2015 caused flooding across Lancashire. The countywide event affected numerous communities; the Lead Local Flood Authority recorded and verified data about the December 2015 floods and used that to establish flood timelines and identify affected communities for a countywide Section 19 investigation. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Relevant risk management authorities met to discuss primary flood mechanisms and community impacts. The Lead Local Flood Authority promoted property&ndash;level flood resilience; an affected resident used available grants to install property&ndash;level flood protection measures. (p38)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Significant flooding hit Lancashire in December 2015, affecting local communities and exposing shortcomings in communication and coordination; this prompted the development of district–level reports to inform affected communities and identify opportunities for future flood risk management. [PAG] (p3)
Extreme storms and rainfall in November/December 2015 caused flooding throughout December 2015 affecting the county: over 2,500 properties flooded and damage to private gardens, garages and out–buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges and retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools, village and town halls. (p9)
Two major storm events in December 2015 caused flooding across Lancashire. The countywide event affected numerous communities; the Lead Local Flood Authority recorded and verified data about the December 2015 floods and used that to establish flood timelines and identify affected communities for a countywide Section 19 investigation. [PAG] (p10)
Relevant risk management authorities met to discuss primary flood mechanisms and community impacts. The Lead Local Flood Authority promoted property–level flood resilience; an affected resident used available grants to install property–level flood protection measures. (p38)","over 2,500 properties (p9)",GB-LAN_27_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_27_2015-12-01,South Ribble flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,South Ribble District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/south-ribble-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,27,2015-12-01,53.7271527,-2.7330066,"<div id=""html_719c8752059b7281c50e7451edb0a119"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Ribble</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Area experienced impacts from the December 2015 floods; a recovery drop&ndash;in event was held at The Civic Centre (02 Feb 2016) to support affected residents and businesses. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Two properties in Farington (Bannister Lane area) suffered internal flooding on 26 December 2015. [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties in Higher Walton: 14 properties in the Bannister Hall Lane area and 12 properties in the Cann Bridge area; River Darwen overtopped its banks at Cann Bridge. [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Higher Walton (Cann Bridge area and Higher Walton Road area) experienced internal property flooding when the River Darwen overtopped its banks. The overtopping caused internal flooding to multiple residential properties and prompted inspection and recovery actions by risk management authorities. [TAB] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of residential properties: 4 properties suffered internal flooding in the Higher Walton (Higher Walton Road) area on 26 December 2015 (linked to the River Darwen). 11 properties suffered internal flooding in Leyland (Curlew Close area) on 26 December 2015. [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>South Ribble BC is working with LCC to identify the owner of an ordinary watercourse so necessary maintenance can increase capacity and help alleviate flood risk following the December 2015 flooding. [TAB] (p35)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>26 properties [TAB] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>12 properties; 4 properties [TAB] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties; 11 properties [TAB,PAG] (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,South Ribble,England,"Area experienced impacts from the December 2015 floods; a recovery drop–in event was held at The Civic Centre (02 Feb 2016) to support affected residents and businesses. (p9)
Two properties in Farington (Bannister Lane area) suffered internal flooding on 26 December 2015. [TAB] (p11)
Internal flooding of properties in Higher Walton: 14 properties in the Bannister Hall Lane area and 12 properties in the Cann Bridge area; River Darwen overtopped its banks at Cann Bridge. [TAB] (p15)
Higher Walton (Cann Bridge area and Higher Walton Road area) experienced internal property flooding when the River Darwen overtopped its banks. The overtopping caused internal flooding to multiple residential properties and prompted inspection and recovery actions by risk management authorities. [TAB] (p16)
Internal flooding of residential properties: 4 properties suffered internal flooding in the Higher Walton (Higher Walton Road) area on 26 December 2015 (linked to the River Darwen). 11 properties suffered internal flooding in Leyland (Curlew Close area) on 26 December 2015. [TAB,PAG] (p17)
South Ribble BC is working with LCC to identify the owner of an ordinary watercourse so necessary maintenance can increase capacity and help alleviate flood risk following the December 2015 flooding. [TAB] (p35)","2 properties [TAB] (p11)
26 properties [TAB] (p15)
12 properties; 4 properties [TAB] (p16)
4 properties; 11 properties [TAB,PAG] (p17)",GB-LAN_27_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_27_2015-12-01,South Ribble flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,South Ribble District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/south-ribble-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,27,2015-12-01,53.9026441,-2.422856,"<div id=""html_cdadaf23a337f3a49ee622a55a8e37f5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ribble Valley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Ribble Valley area (including Whalley) experienced impacts from the December 2015 floods; a drop&ndash;in event in Whalley (10 Feb 2016) was provided to support affected residents and businesses. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Ribble Valley,England,The Ribble Valley area (including Whalley) experienced impacts from the December 2015 floods; a drop–in event in Whalley (10 Feb 2016) was provided to support affected residents and businesses. (p9),,GB-LAN_27_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_27_2015-12-01,South Ribble flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,South Ribble District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/south-ribble-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,27,2015-12-01,53.70249,-2.201046,"<div id=""html_1f7565e60a63c633b7f7128455c6f01f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rossendale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Rossendale was part of the countywide flooding during December 2015 that affected Lancashire communities; local residents and businesses were impacted and multi&ndash;agency recovery/support activity (including a drop&ndash;in in Irwell Vale on 10 Feb 2016) was provided to affected people. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Rossendale,England,Rossendale was part of the countywide flooding during December 2015 that affected Lancashire communities; local residents and businesses were impacted and multi–agency recovery/support activity (including a drop–in in Irwell Vale on 10 Feb 2016) was provided to affected people. (p9),,GB-LAN_27_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_27_2015-12-01,South Ribble flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,South Ribble District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/south-ribble-final-report.pdf
