GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.686507,-2.2482811,"<div id=""html_45078c3d89e2c5d09c807abecceeea84"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cowpe Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A minor breach of Cowpe Brook, combined with surface water, caused floodwater to flow from the brook onto Cowpe Road and contributed to internal flooding of properties in Waterfoot. (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>21 properties (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Cowpe Brook,England,"A minor breach of Cowpe Brook, combined with surface water, caused floodwater to flow from the brook onto Cowpe Road and contributed to internal flooding of properties in Waterfoot. (p23)",21 properties (p23),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.7134625,-2.2521213,"<div id=""html_8a094c4cae94785abaa2917362b4af73"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whitewell Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Believed to have caused a groundwater&ndash;related inundation that led to cellar flooding of nearby properties (for example along Bacup Road East and Holt Street) during the December 2015 event. (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Whitewell Brook,England,Believed to have caused a groundwater–related inundation that led to cellar flooding of nearby properties (for example along Bacup Road East and Holt Street) during the December 2015 event. (p23),,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6989204,-2.2789593,"<div id=""html_96969203becf0f8150582fd735bcec13"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lambert's Mill</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Lambert's Mill, situated in a low spot, flooded when a surface water drain backed up as a result of high flows in the River Irwell, resulting in internal flooding at the mill location. (p18)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lambert's Mill,England,"Lambert's Mill, situated in a low spot, flooded when a surface water drain backed up as a result of high flows in the River Irwell, resulting in internal flooding at the mill location. (p18)",,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6023223,-2.2999892,"<div id=""html_58bea30e3e4d6b7c22a7943c109ee0e8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Irwell</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Although the River Irwell did not breach its banks at this location on 26 December 2015, the culvert at Rockliffe Road restricted river flow and put pressure on the drainage network, contributing to a manhole being lifted and subsequent property flooding. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Irwell overtopped its banks and was identified as the primary source of flooding at Hareholme (MSFW131), causing internal flooding to residential properties. (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Backed up at Lumb Bridge, came out of channel and flooded the main village and Meadow Park; contributed to pump inundation and property flooding. [PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High flows in the River Irwell on 26 December 2015 contributed to multiple flooding mechanisms: backing up a surface water drain that caused Lambert's Mill to flood; undermining the foundations of New Hall Hey Business Park which contributed to a channel and culvert blockage and a subsequent river breach; floodwaters then inundated the adjacent cricket pitch and flowed east and west, causing properties to flood at cellar and ground levels. (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Became blocked by unconsented gabion defences that collapsed into the channel and breached through a scoured wall at a cricket pitch, causing inundation and overland flow into nearby streets and parkland. High levels and overtopping also caused inundation of Recreation Gardens, exceeded bunds and led to overtopping near North Street in Strongstry and Chatterton. The river undermined the central pier of Bridgeway Bridge, causing its collapse. [PAG] (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High river levels overtopped banks (left bank into Recreation Gardens and later the right bank), and undermined the central pier of Bridgeway Bridge leading to its collapse. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cellar flooding along Bacup Road (over footbridges of the River Irwell) was believed to be caused by a groundwater issue associated with proximity to the River Irwell. (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>4 properties (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>50 properties; 3 inches of water in cellars (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 properties; 24 properties [PAG] (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Irwell,England,"Although the River Irwell did not breach its banks at this location on 26 December 2015, the culvert at Rockliffe Road restricted river flow and put pressure on the drainage network, contributing to a manhole being lifted and subsequent property flooding. (p12)
The River Irwell overtopped its banks and was identified as the primary source of flooding at Hareholme (MSFW131), causing internal flooding to residential properties. (p15)
Backed up at Lumb Bridge, came out of channel and flooded the main village and Meadow Park; contributed to pump inundation and property flooding. [PAG] (p17)
High flows in the River Irwell on 26 December 2015 contributed to multiple flooding mechanisms: backing up a surface water drain that caused Lambert's Mill to flood; undermining the foundations of New Hall Hey Business Park which contributed to a channel and culvert blockage and a subsequent river breach; floodwaters then inundated the adjacent cricket pitch and flowed east and west, causing properties to flood at cellar and ground levels. (p18)
Became blocked by unconsented gabion defences that collapsed into the channel and breached through a scoured wall at a cricket pitch, causing inundation and overland flow into nearby streets and parkland. High levels and overtopping also caused inundation of Recreation Gardens, exceeded bunds and led to overtopping near North Street in Strongstry and Chatterton. The river undermined the central pier of Bridgeway Bridge, causing its collapse. [PAG] (p20)
High river levels overtopped banks (left bank into Recreation Gardens and later the right bank), and undermined the central pier of Bridgeway Bridge leading to its collapse. (p21)
Cellar flooding along Bacup Road (over footbridges of the River Irwell) was believed to be caused by a groundwater issue associated with proximity to the River Irwell. (p23)","4 properties (p15)
50 properties; 3 inches of water in cellars (p18)
16 properties; 24 properties [PAG] (p20)",GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6813361,-2.3245258,"<div id=""html_5e081ffe204ab0c3fd1c4873c4f61cb8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Ogden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Backed up at Ogden Bridge and overtopped its banks, flowing south east into the main village at Irwell Vale; identified as the primary source of flooding at Helmshore and contributed to fluvial flooding in Irwell Vale. Caused internal flooding of properties in the affected communities. [PAG] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Backed up at Ogden Bridge, overtopped its banks and flowed southeast into the main village, contributing to flooding of properties and the village. (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>3 properties; 62 properties [PAG] (p16)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Ogden,England,"Backed up at Ogden Bridge and overtopped its banks, flowing south east into the main village at Irwell Vale; identified as the primary source of flooding at Helmshore and contributed to fluvial flooding in Irwell Vale. Caused internal flooding of properties in the affected communities. [PAG] (p16)
Backed up at Ogden Bridge, overtopped its banks and flowed southeast into the main village, contributing to flooding of properties and the village. (p17)",3 properties; 62 properties [PAG] (p16),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6457771,-2.1810651,"<div id=""html_29b4cea56f05475fc3471ccecc1fa545"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Spodden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Spodden overtopped its banks and was identified as the primary source of the flooding that led to internal flooding of properties in Shawforth on 26 December 2015. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Spodden,England,The River Spodden overtopped its banks and was identified as the primary source of the flooding that led to internal flooding of properties in Shawforth on 26 December 2015. (p19),9 properties (p19),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.7050911,-2.2025402,"<div id=""html_cf8d574288bca9fbd2caf207ecf52bf7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Burnley Road, Bacup</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Drains along Burnley Road became overwhelmed and blocked on 26 December 2015, causing surface water to enter properties and flow down the road. Vehicle bow waves on the flooded highway also forced water into houses. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 properties (internal flooding at this Bacup location on 26 December 2015) (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Burnley Road, Bacup",England,"Drains along Burnley Road became overwhelmed and blocked on 26 December 2015, causing surface water to enter properties and flow down the road. Vehicle bow waves on the flooded highway also forced water into houses. (p12)",17 properties (internal flooding at this Bacup location on 26 December 2015) (p12),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.7037808,-2.1999156,"<div id=""html_2800e3002d7eb4402a1598ee3bec9053"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Yorkshire Street, Bacup</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ponding occurred in the low spot on Yorkshire Street as surface water flowed down from Burnley Road during the 26 December 2015 event, contributing to local flooding. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Yorkshire Street, Bacup",England,"Ponding occurred in the low spot on Yorkshire Street as surface water flowed down from Burnley Road during the 26 December 2015 event, contributing to local flooding. (p12)",,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.698145,-2.2004574,"<div id=""html_1ddc8f77f46058ef94e90c127b783474"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rockliffe Road, Bacup</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The culvert at Rockliffe Road restricted river flow and put pressure on the drainage network; a manhole cover was lifted under that pressure, causing residential and commercial properties to flood along Rockliffe Road on 26 December 2015. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 properties (internal flooding at this Bacup location on 26 December 2015) (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Rockliffe Road, Bacup",England,"The culvert at Rockliffe Road restricted river flow and put pressure on the drainage network; a manhole cover was lifted under that pressure, causing residential and commercial properties to flood along Rockliffe Road on 26 December 2015. (p12)",17 properties (internal flooding at this Bacup location on 26 December 2015) (p12),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
