GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6653128,-2.3167856,"<div id=""html_9896ecedc73a6a2bf316059d9c60d67e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Street, Strongstry</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Right bank of the River Irwell was overtopped close to residential properties along North Street, contributing to internal flooding at the location. (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>24 properties (combined Strongstry and Chatterton) (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"North Street, Strongstry",England,"Right bank of the River Irwell was overtopped close to residential properties along North Street, contributing to internal flooding at the location. (p21)",24 properties (combined Strongstry and Chatterton) (p21),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6918521,-2.251977,"<div id=""html_b44fd13034e4bd45ab07720dc5f39b4f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Cowpe Road, Edgeside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Floodwater flowed down Cowpe Road (driven by surface water and a minor breach of Cowpe Brook), passing through the locality and re&ndash;entering the brook downstream; this event contributed to internal flooding of properties in the area. (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>21 properties (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Cowpe Road, Edgeside",England,"Floodwater flowed down Cowpe Road (driven by surface water and a minor breach of Cowpe Brook), passing through the locality and re–entering the brook downstream; this event contributed to internal flooding of properties in the area. (p23)",21 properties (p23),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6926872,-2.2556237,"<div id=""html_73e41b39172c3bf6da806d8b501d3570"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bacup Road, Waterfoot</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties along Bacup Road (located over footbridges of the River Irwell) suffered cellar flooding attributed to a groundwater issue. (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Bacup Road, Waterfoot",England,Properties along Bacup Road (located over footbridges of the River Irwell) suffered cellar flooding attributed to a groundwater issue. (p23),,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6941273,-2.2518901,"<div id=""html_cc66f93334352eb65153a9b8737265ab"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Holt Street, Edgeside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Cellar/internal flooding of properties along Holt Street, attributed to a groundwater issue related to the nearby Whitewell Brook during the December 2015 event. (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Holt Street, Edgeside",England,"Cellar/internal flooding of properties along Holt Street, attributed to a groundwater issue related to the nearby Whitewell Brook during the December 2015 event. (p23)",,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.86117,-2.5650887,"<div id=""html_c9cf9839e4ce3f54d03b35b27793bc89"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant flooding occurred across Lancashire in December 2015; the event exposed shortcomings in communication to affected communities and led to the development of district&ndash;level reports and follow&ndash;up actions by risk management authorities. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Lancashire experienced major flooding during December 2015 (the highest recorded river flows and the wettest December), resulting in widespread impacts on people, homes and businesses across the county. [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Extreme storms and rainfall in November and December 2015 caused widespread flooding across Lancashire during December 2015, damaging private gardens, garages and out&ndash;buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges and retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools, village and town halls. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Communities across the county experienced flooding as a result of two major storm events in December 2015. The extent and geographic distribution of flooding led to a countywide investigation to identify affected communities and to track and prioritise remedial actions via stage two reports. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties flooded [TAB] (p8)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>over 2,500 properties (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Significant flooding occurred across Lancashire in December 2015; the event exposed shortcomings in communication to affected communities and led to the development of district–level reports and follow–up actions by risk management authorities. [PAG] (p3)
Lancashire experienced major flooding during December 2015 (the highest recorded river flows and the wettest December), resulting in widespread impacts on people, homes and businesses across the county. [TAB] (p8)
Extreme storms and rainfall in November and December 2015 caused widespread flooding across Lancashire during December 2015, damaging private gardens, garages and out–buildings, business premises, agricultural property and critical public infrastructure including roads, bridges and retaining walls, water treatment plants, power and communications installations, and community buildings such as schools, village and town halls. (p9)
Communities across the county experienced flooding as a result of two major storm events in December 2015. The extent and geographic distribution of flooding led to a countywide investigation to identify affected communities and to track and prioritise remedial actions via stage two reports. [PAG] (p10)","over 2,500 properties flooded [TAB] (p8)
over 2,500 properties (p9)",GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.70249,-2.201046,"<div id=""html_17224566377f9b33162b5a5293d95c74"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rossendale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The borough was affected as part of the county&ndash;wide December 2015 floods; recovery support activities were held in Rossendale (Irwell Vale drop&ndash;in on 10 Feb 2016) for residents impacted by the floods. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>In the Bacup area (within Rossendale) on 26 December 2015, drains along Burnley Road became overwhelmed and blocked, causing surface water to enter properties. Surface water flowed down Burnley Road and ponded at a low spot on Yorkshire Street. A culvert at Rockliffe Road restricted river flow and put pressure on the drainage network; a manhole cover was lifted under the pressure, leading to internal flooding of residential and commercial properties along Rockliffe Road, Market Street and River Street. Vehicle bow waves on the highway also forced water into houses. [TAB] (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 properties [TAB] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Rossendale,England,"The borough was affected as part of the county–wide December 2015 floods; recovery support activities were held in Rossendale (Irwell Vale drop–in on 10 Feb 2016) for residents impacted by the floods. (p9)
In the Bacup area (within Rossendale) on 26 December 2015, drains along Burnley Road became overwhelmed and blocked, causing surface water to enter properties. Surface water flowed down Burnley Road and ponded at a low spot on Yorkshire Street. A culvert at Rockliffe Road restricted river flow and put pressure on the drainage network; a manhole cover was lifted under the pressure, leading to internal flooding of residential and commercial properties along Rockliffe Road, Market Street and River Street. Vehicle bow waves on the highway also forced water into houses. [TAB] (p11)",17 properties [TAB] (p11),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6739986,-2.3198638,"<div id=""html_452455f34dceadc677f004f7e75353eb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lumb Viaduct</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Irwell backed up at Lumb Bridge and came out of channel, contributing to flooding of the main village. (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lumb Viaduct,England,"The River Irwell backed up at Lumb Bridge and came out of channel, contributing to flooding of the main village. (p17)",,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.9031969,-2.7762038183560396,"<div id=""html_582a031945f2a1e5ffeb3b9df32ad1db"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Garstang</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood basins were activated in Garstang as part of preparatory and response actions during the December 2015 floods to reduce risk of damage to properties and infrastructure. [TAB] (p8)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Garstang,England,Flood basins were activated in Garstang as part of preparatory and response actions during the December 2015 floods to reduce risk of damage to properties and infrastructure. [TAB] (p8),,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
