GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.66187410234079,-2.7761246324411504,"<div id=""html_01578e215264ba75f0e4a85497b64e34"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Croston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Environment Agency carried out pumping activities in Croston to remove floodwater during the December 2015 floods. (p9)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Croston,England,The Environment Agency carried out pumping activities in Croston to remove floodwater during the December 2015 floods. (p9),,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6775859865751,-2.316467158860694,"<div id=""html_308b6f657807415d14d05f0bea87368a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Irwell Vale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Community experienced flooding during December 2015; a multi&ndash;agency drop&ndash;in event was held in Irwell Vale on 10 Feb 2016 to provide flood recovery support, gather eyewitness reports and advise affected residents. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Village flooded when both the River Ogden and the River Irwell came out of channel; floodwater flowed into the main village and Meadow Park causing internal flooding to properties. Over&ndash;pumping was used to remove surface water but pumps were later inundated by river peak flows. (p17)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>62 properties (internal flooding) (p17)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Irwell Vale,England,"Community experienced flooding during December 2015; a multi–agency drop–in event was held in Irwell Vale on 10 Feb 2016 to provide flood recovery support, gather eyewitness reports and advise affected residents. (p9)
Village flooded when both the River Ogden and the River Irwell came out of channel; floodwater flowed into the main village and Meadow Park causing internal flooding to properties. Over–pumping was used to remove surface water but pumps were later inundated by river peak flows. (p17)",62 properties (internal flooding) (p17),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6803936,-2.1674433,"<div id=""html_520866b70542fc8bf54190002f42b07e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Shawforth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Spodden overtopped its banks and caused internal flooding to properties in Shawforth. Nine properties are recorded as having suffered internal flooding on 26 December 2015; at least one property on Market Street experienced ground&ndash;floor flooding due to a bow wave from vehicles driving through deep water in the highway. (p19)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>9 properties; 1 property on Market Street (p19)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Shawforth,England,River Spodden overtopped its banks and caused internal flooding to properties in Shawforth. Nine properties are recorded as having suffered internal flooding on 26 December 2015; at least one property on Market Street experienced ground–floor flooding due to a bow wave from vehicles driving through deep water in the highway. (p19),9 properties; 1 property on Market Street (p19),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6927052,-2.2258838,"<div id=""html_4beeecefc1727b150448075e4cc98a90"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stacksteads</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding to residential and commercial properties across the community. 16 properties suffered internal flooding on 26 December 2015. Floodwaters from a River Irwell blockage and breach inundated a cricket pitch, flowed across Brandwood Road and Waterbarn Lane and onto Brandwood Park. Several properties experienced cellar flooding. Groundwater and surface water flooded businesses in a mill on Blackwood Road and entered cellars of properties around Railway Street, flooding the ground floor of a commercial property. (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>16 properties (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Stacksteads,England,"Internal flooding to residential and commercial properties across the community. 16 properties suffered internal flooding on 26 December 2015. Floodwaters from a River Irwell blockage and breach inundated a cricket pitch, flowed across Brandwood Road and Waterbarn Lane and onto Brandwood Park. Several properties experienced cellar flooding. Groundwater and surface water flooded businesses in a mill on Blackwood Road and entered cellars of properties around Railway Street, flooding the ground floor of a commercial property. (p20)",16 properties (p20),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
GB-LAN,12,2015-12-01,53.6648613,-2.317359,"<div id=""html_990703d7dfc0f2bd2daba64784099561"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Strongstry</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal flooding of properties caused by high River Irwell levels overtopping banks combined with surface water run&ndash;off from a disused railway embankment and a local ordinary watercourse. Culvert damage and blockages under the highway and under private property were identified and are being investigated and repaired. [TAB] (p21)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>24 properties (combined Strongstry and Chatterton) [TAB] (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Strongstry,England,Internal flooding of properties caused by high River Irwell levels overtopping banks combined with surface water run–off from a disused railway embankment and a local ordinary watercourse. Culvert damage and blockages under the highway and under private property were identified and are being investigated and repaired. [TAB] (p21),24 properties (combined Strongstry and Chatterton) [TAB] (p21),GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01.html,GB-LAN_12_2015-12-01,Rossendale flooding 01 Dec 2015 - 31 Dec 2015,Rossendale District Flood Report: Recommended Actions,069/Lancashire County/rossendale-final-report.pdf
