GB-HEF,1,2019-10-25,52.083333,-2.75,"<div id=""html_1eda961dc02140824c5ee138a87881ec"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Herefordshire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding across the county during the October 2019 and February 2020 events resulted in properties being flooded internally above ground&ndash;floor level, critical installations being flooded causing loss or potential loss of service, and some facilities rendered inoperable due to impassable access. [MUL] (p5)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple locations within Herefordshire experienced river flooding in February 2020, producing internal property flooding and transport disruption: Cusop (internal property flooding), Letton and surrounding area via Dulas Brook (internal property flooding), highways closed (A438 north and south of Letton), and bridges closed (Bredwardine bridge and Bridge Sollars bridge). Hereford experienced internal property flooding including impact to Hereford Leisure Centre plant room and Manor House Care Home. [TAB] (p7)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property flooding occurred across Herefordshire during the October 2019 event (intense rainfall on 25&ndash;26 October 2019) leading to fluvial flooding; February 2020 produced record&ndash;breaking flows and significant flooding across Herefordshire following successive storms (Ciara, Dennis, Jorge) and saturated antecedent conditions. [MUL] (p16)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced very wet antecedent conditions and high river flows in February 2020 that produced serious fluvial flooding across the county, with a large number of properties flooded and the highest ever recorded peak flows on the River Wye. (p18)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15 properties (Cusop); 22 properties (Letton and surrounding area); 94 properties (Hereford); 2 bridges [TAB] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Herefordshire,Herefordshire,England,"Flooding across the county during the October 2019 and February 2020 events resulted in properties being flooded internally above ground–floor level, critical installations being flooded causing loss or potential loss of service, and some facilities rendered inoperable due to impassable access. [MUL] (p5)
Multiple locations within Herefordshire experienced river flooding in February 2020, producing internal property flooding and transport disruption: Cusop (internal property flooding), Letton and surrounding area via Dulas Brook (internal property flooding), highways closed (A438 north and south of Letton), and bridges closed (Bredwardine bridge and Bridge Sollars bridge). Hereford experienced internal property flooding including impact to Hereford Leisure Centre plant room and Manor House Care Home. [TAB] (p7)
Property flooding occurred across Herefordshire during the October 2019 event (intense rainfall on 25–26 October 2019) leading to fluvial flooding; February 2020 produced record–breaking flows and significant flooding across Herefordshire following successive storms (Ciara, Dennis, Jorge) and saturated antecedent conditions. [MUL] (p16)
Experienced very wet antecedent conditions and high river flows in February 2020 that produced serious fluvial flooding across the county, with a large number of properties flooded and the highest ever recorded peak flows on the River Wye. (p18)",15 properties (Cusop); 22 properties (Letton and surrounding area); 94 properties (Hereford); 2 bridges [TAB] (p7),GB-HEF_1_2019-10-25_etc.html,GB-HEF_1_2019-10-25_etc,Herefordshire flooding 25 Oct 2019 - 26 Oct 2019 and Herefordshire flooding February 2020,Herefordshire 2019/20 Section 19 Report,055/Herefordshire County/Herefordshire/Section/19/Report/2019/20.pdf
