GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7435557,-2.2141832,"<div id=""html_7fa8525896490fc38be7fe327b50a9f4"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whitewell Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Hillside surface water runoff carried gravel, boulders and debris into the Brook and its tributaries, causing blockages that impeded water dispersal; EA removed excess gravel and is assisting with works on tributaries; EA/UU/LCC are investigating culvert and combined sewer capacity and options to route excess surface water into these systems; EA assessing scope for lowering the Brook. (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Whitewell Brook,England,"Hillside surface water runoff carried gravel, boulders and debris into the Brook and its tributaries, causing blockages that impeded water dispersal; EA removed excess gravel and is assisting with works on tributaries; EA/UU/LCC are investigating culvert and combined sewer capacity and options to route excess surface water into these systems; EA assessing scope for lowering the Brook. (p22)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.705124,-2.278509,"<div id=""html_8032303f392ef50b38fbb1ec5a25ea0f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Balladen Clough</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from Balladen Clough led to EA repairs to maintain access to debris screens; the debris screen adjacent to Market Street was replaced and additional screens are being procured. (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Balladen Clough,England,Flooding from Balladen Clough led to EA repairs to maintain access to debris screens; the debris screen adjacent to Market Street was replaced and additional screens are being procured. (p23),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.5894939,-3.0327968,"<div id=""html_f21f21db2e325bda6124fbe56a396ef8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sandy Brook</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred at the culvert inlet of Sandy Brook; this, alongside surface water runoff, contributed to surface water flooding that affected property at the northern end of Altys Lane. (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Sandy Brook,England,"Flooding occurred at the culvert inlet of Sandy Brook; this, alongside surface water runoff, contributed to surface water flooding that affected property at the northern end of Altys Lane. (p27)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,54.009267,-2.771252,"<div id=""html_5e422335150d0b5c401953b9d4f95823"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Conder</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued a Flood Warning for the River Conder at Galgate (timestamped in the timeline), indicating rising river levels and a threat of river flooding to Galgate and immediate vicinity. [IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Conder,England,"Environment Agency issued a Flood Warning for the River Conder at Galgate (timestamped in the timeline), indicating rising river levels and a threat of river flooding to Galgate and immediate vicinity. [IMG] (p10)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6884889,-1.8393557,"<div id=""html_f5bca35efd5a1a1a9609586edc260270"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Calder</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple Flood Warnings and Alerts were issued for locations on the River Calder (including Whalley, Burnley Town Centre and Fulledge) during the event timeline on 22 June 2012, indicating river flooding and significant threat to communities and the town centre along the Calder catchment. [IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Calder came out of bank and caused flooding to properties (Cross House and Abbey Croft). Flood alerts/warnings were issued for the River Calder area in advance of thresholds being reached. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 properties (Cross House, Abbey Croft) (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Calder,England,"Multiple Flood Warnings and Alerts were issued for locations on the River Calder (including Whalley, Burnley Town Centre and Fulledge) during the event timeline on 22 June 2012, indicating river flooding and significant threat to communities and the town centre along the Calder catchment. [IMG] (p10)
The River Calder came out of bank and caused flooding to properties (Cross House and Abbey Croft). Flood alerts/warnings were issued for the River Calder area in advance of thresholds being reached. (p12)","2 properties (Cross House, Abbey Croft) (p12)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6023223,-2.2999892,"<div id=""html_e0144dc7733e77ffb421c5beb67aabb2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Irwell</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple Flood Warnings were issued on the River Irwell during the event for different reaches and communities (e.g. Irwell @ Strongstry/Chatterton 19:07, Irwell Vale 19:08, Irwell @ Waterfoot 19:22, Irwell @ Rawtenstall 19:25, Stubbylee 19:25/19:27, Bacup 19:27 on 22 June 2012), indicating widespread river flooding or imminent flooding across the Irwell catchment. [IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High levels in the River Irwell contributed to flooding at Strongstry and Chatterton, exacerbating property flooding when combined with surface&ndash;water runoff. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping/flow from the River Irwell caused flooding to at least one property at Ewood Bridge; silt accumulation required clearance and a neighbouring property owner raised a wall adjacent to the river. (p24)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Irwell,England,"Multiple Flood Warnings were issued on the River Irwell during the event for different reaches and communities (e.g. Irwell @ Strongstry/Chatterton 19:07, Irwell Vale 19:08, Irwell @ Waterfoot 19:22, Irwell @ Rawtenstall 19:25, Stubbylee 19:25/19:27, Bacup 19:27 on 22 June 2012), indicating widespread river flooding or imminent flooding across the Irwell catchment. [IMG] (p10)
High levels in the River Irwell contributed to flooding at Strongstry and Chatterton, exacerbating property flooding when combined with surface–water runoff. (p21)
Overtopping/flow from the River Irwell caused flooding to at least one property at Ewood Bridge; silt accumulation required clearance and a neighbouring property owner raised a wall adjacent to the river. (p24)",1 property (p24),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.8674307,-2.4188743,"<div id=""html_3b72afff084176f555e3cf5f2b0e0a89"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Ribble</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple flood alerts and formal flood warnings were issued for the River Ribble during the event (Flood Alert &ndash; Upper River Ribble; Flood Alert &ndash; Lower Ribble and Darwen). Specific flood warnings were issued for Ribble locations including Ribchester, Walton&ndash;le&ndash;Dale and Samlesbury on 22 June, indicating significant river flooding risk across the Ribble corridor. [IMG,PAG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Ribble,England,"Multiple flood alerts and formal flood warnings were issued for the River Ribble during the event (Flood Alert – Upper River Ribble; Flood Alert – Lower Ribble and Darwen). Specific flood warnings were issued for Ribble locations including Ribchester, Walton–le–Dale and Samlesbury on 22 June, indicating significant river flooding risk across the Ribble corridor. [IMG,PAG] (p10)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,54.2230168,-2.6021945,"<div id=""html_597f92f42b029c133b418d0371cd35fc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Lune</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A Flood Alert was issued for the Lower River Lune and Conder (14:56) and a Flood Warning was issued for Conder @ Galgate ('A' 17:38) during the June 2012 events, indicating elevated river levels and flood risk to the Conder/Lune corridor. [IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Lune,England,"A Flood Alert was issued for the Lower River Lune and Conder (14:56) and a Flood Warning was issued for Conder @ Galgate ('A' 17:38) during the June 2012 events, indicating elevated river levels and flood risk to the Conder/Lune corridor. [IMG] (p10)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7408403,-2.5677883,"<div id=""html_5f021c97748e120d6f8c994306152430"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Darwen</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood alerts and flood warnings were issued for the Darwen (Flood Alert &ndash; Lower Ribble and Darwen). Formal flood warnings were issued for Darwen locations including Higher Walton and Waterfall on 22 June, indicating river flooding impacts and risk to the Darwen corridor. [IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Darwen caused inundation to properties downstream of Cann Bridge. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Darwen,England,"Flood alerts and flood warnings were issued for the Darwen (Flood Alert – Lower Ribble and Darwen). Formal flood warnings were issued for Darwen locations including Higher Walton and Waterfall on 22 June, indicating river flooding impacts and risk to the Darwen corridor. [IMG] (p10)
Flooding from the River Darwen caused inundation to properties downstream of Cann Bridge. (p13)",5 properties (p13),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7048432,-2.6582336,"<div id=""html_d792e50b2c23cffb375e68a65a687c87"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Lostock</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A Flood Alert was issued for Lostock (paired with Yarrow) during the June 2012 event, indicating an elevated risk of river flooding in the Lostock/Yarrow catchment. [IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Lostock,England,"A Flood Alert was issued for Lostock (paired with Yarrow) during the June 2012 event, indicating an elevated risk of river flooding in the Lostock/Yarrow catchment. [IMG] (p10)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.645309,-2.6575423,"<div id=""html_b2ce2cdc86934e352eb0f7fcec60e037"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Yarrow</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood alerts and subsequent flood warnings were issued for the Yarrow catchment; specific flood warnings were issued for Yarrow at Croston (two warnings) on 22 June, indicating river flooding impacts in the Yarrow area. [IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High river levels in the Yarrow prevented surface water draining from Croston; the river overtopped its channel and surface water built up and flooded properties. A small tributary also exceeded capacity and flooded through a garden and down a road into properties. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High river levels in the River Yarrow prevented surface water draining from the village and the river overtopped its channel, causing surface water to build up and flood properties. A small tributary also exceeded capacity and flooded through a garden and down a road into properties. [IMG,PAG] (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>72 properties (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>72 properties [IMG,PAG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Yarrow,England,"Flood alerts and subsequent flood warnings were issued for the Yarrow catchment; specific flood warnings were issued for Yarrow at Croston (two warnings) on 22 June, indicating river flooding impacts in the Yarrow area. [IMG] (p10)
High river levels in the Yarrow prevented surface water draining from Croston; the river overtopped its channel and surface water built up and flooded properties. A small tributary also exceeded capacity and flooded through a garden and down a road into properties. (p11)
High river levels in the River Yarrow prevented surface water draining from the village and the river overtopped its channel, causing surface water to build up and flood properties. A small tributary also exceeded capacity and flooded through a garden and down a road into properties. [IMG,PAG] (p12)","72 properties (p11)
72 properties [IMG,PAG] (p12)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6457771,-2.1810651,"<div id=""html_3505cc1b8b527b681778a90d678b0be2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>River Spodden</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The River Spodden overtopped in two locations in Whitworth, flooding a leisure centre, industrial units and shop cellars in June; where it is constricted by a resident&ndash;installed culvert at Shawforth it caused flooding of Market Street and eight nearby properties. The EA cleared the channel in response. [PAG,MUL] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopped in two locations in Whitworth, causing flooding of nearby properties (leisure centre, industrial units, shop cellars). (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>2 locations; 8 properties [PAG,MUL] (p22)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two locations (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,River Spodden,England,"The River Spodden overtopped in two locations in Whitworth, flooding a leisure centre, industrial units and shop cellars in June; where it is constricted by a resident–installed culvert at Shawforth it caused flooding of Market Street and eight nearby properties. The EA cleared the channel in response. [PAG,MUL] (p22)
Overtopped in two locations in Whitworth, causing flooding of nearby properties (leisure centre, industrial units, shop cellars). (p23)","2 locations; 8 properties [PAG,MUL] (p22)
two locations (p23)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6602378,-2.773721,"<div id=""html_df403d66bd343405096ebd349022f4d1"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Town Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified for riverbank/wall works and flood gate replacement: right/left bank walls, vegetation clearance, pointing and expansion joint repairs and replacement/repair of flap valves/flood gate as part of River Yarrow interventions at/around Town Bridge. [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Town Bridge,England,"Identified for riverbank/wall works and flood gate replacement: right/left bank walls, vegetation clearance, pointing and expansion joint repairs and replacement/repair of flap valves/flood gate as part of River Yarrow interventions at/around Town Bridge. [IMG] (p12)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6608147,-2.781531,"<div id=""html_f65b4d5e42df47bbf748d1b7e3582c66"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fishery Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Both banks at the Fishery Bridge on the River Yarrow were identified with wall and vegetation issues (and required pointing/expansion joint works) linked to flood risk affecting Croston. [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Fishery Bridge,England,Both banks at the Fishery Bridge on the River Yarrow were identified with wall and vegetation issues (and required pointing/expansion joint works) linked to flood risk affecting Croston. [IMG] (p12),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.8199189,-2.4065541,"<div id=""html_d8bae1250e76cb8ca46e329e43243c06"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>King Street, Whalley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>King Street is named as part of the area where flooding occurred on 22&ndash;23 June, linked to the Mill Race and Calder Brook; properties in this area were affected and some used flood boards. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties (area) (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"King Street, Whalley",England,"King Street is named as part of the area where flooding occurred on 22–23 June, linked to the Mill Race and Calder Brook; properties in this area were affected and some used flood boards. (p12)",18 properties (area) (p12),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.8244822,-2.4078403,"<div id=""html_459cada5cf697856e4a188ca2469bfb3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Riddings Lane, Whalley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Site of Cross House, which flooded when the River Calder came out of bank. (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Riddings Lane, Whalley",England,"Site of Cross House, which flooded when the River Calder came out of bank. (p12)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6607402,-2.7804286,"<div id=""html_4ebe286e18ad5e1667d29d5a08711003"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Shevington Causeway, Croston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified issues on the River Yarrow left bank at Shevington Causeway (bank wall and flap valve problems, vegetation requiring clearance) that were associated with the river flooding risk to Croston and targeted for repair. [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Shevington Causeway, Croston",England,"Identified issues on the River Yarrow left bank at Shevington Causeway (bank wall and flap valve problems, vegetation requiring clearance) that were associated with the river flooding risk to Croston and targeted for repair. [IMG] (p12)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6550019,-2.8111981,"<div id=""html_86830d9a5aad50c0912959c90b7c38fb"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Meadow Lane, Croston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>An embankment at Meadow Lane on the River Yarrow was identified for reconstruction as a result of river flood&ndash;related issues affecting Croston. [IMG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Meadow Lane, Croston",England,An embankment at Meadow Lane on the River Yarrow was identified for reconstruction as a result of river flood–related issues affecting Croston. [IMG] (p12),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6870509,-2.7219996,"<div id=""html_128bbdaa1ebebe793d3d9ca87289bd83"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Curlew Close, Leyland</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on Curlew Close were flooded by surface water with some surcharge of dilute sewage from the combined sewer system; flooding was exacerbated by high water levels in nearby watercourses preventing surface water drainage. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 15 properties (across the listed Leyland roads) (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Curlew Close, Leyland",England,Properties on Curlew Close were flooded by surface water with some surcharge of dilute sewage from the combined sewer system; flooding was exacerbated by high water levels in nearby watercourses preventing surface water drainage. (p13),at least 15 properties (across the listed Leyland roads) (p13),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
