GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7164571,-2.6901438,"<div id=""html_263cc3d7ff9a60fc3a34110af54d1b29"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fowler Avenue, Farington</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on the street were flooded by surface water; flooding included surcharge of dilute sewage from the combined sewerage system which contributed to impacts and prevented drainage in some locations. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 15 properties (total across the Leyland area including Curlew Close, Western Drive, Longmeanygate, Midge Hall, Bannister Drive, Fowler Lane and Fowler Avenue) (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Fowler Avenue, Farington",England,Properties on the street were flooded by surface water; flooding included surcharge of dilute sewage from the combined sewerage system which contributed to impacts and prevented drainage in some locations. (p13),"at least 15 properties (total across the Leyland area including Curlew Close, Western Drive, Longmeanygate, Midge Hall, Bannister Drive, Fowler Lane and Fowler Avenue) (p13)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.8750244,-2.9582055,"<div id=""html_5ee6ee96236eca335367abfa26c2312f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sherbourne Road, Hambleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected properties on Sherbourne Road on 24 September 2012 due to flows from highway drainage and sewer networks. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>12 properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Sherbourne Road, Hambleton",England,Flooding affected properties on Sherbourne Road on 24 September 2012 due to flows from highway drainage and sewer networks. (p14),12 properties (p14),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.9174092,-2.9584545,"<div id=""html_1d63b5e25bdf8e7fe36dbd85e230cd35"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Sunnyside Terrace, Preesall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding was reported to residential properties on Sunnyside Terrace during the September 2012 event. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Sunnyside Terrace, Preesall",England,Flooding was reported to residential properties on Sunnyside Terrace during the September 2012 event. (p14),7 properties (p14),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6653128,-2.3167856,"<div id=""html_3d903ca01d9a24ebf5f5023919986ce9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>North Street, Strongstry</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on North Street were flooded as a result of high River Irwell levels and surface&ndash;water runoff from the railway embankment and a local ordinary watercourse. (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"North Street, Strongstry",England,Properties on North Street were flooded as a result of high River Irwell levels and surface–water runoff from the railway embankment and a local ordinary watercourse. (p21),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7254292,-2.285633,"<div id=""html_cb560ccb1e75abf20074e4e1015f11e7"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Water Street, Crawshawbooth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Folly Clough Brook overtopped due to debris&ndash;screen obstruction, causing flooding that affected Water Street; the EA cleared gravel, installed redesigned debris screens and raised walls at Water Street to increase capacity. (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Water Street, Crawshawbooth",England,"Folly Clough Brook overtopped due to debris–screen obstruction, causing flooding that affected Water Street; the EA cleared gravel, installed redesigned debris screens and raised walls at Water Street to increase capacity. (p21)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.681113,-2.1648798,"<div id=""html_b938edccfb75b0cefbb599f28cf600e3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Market Street, Whitworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Market Street and eight nearby properties suffered flooding where the River Spodden flows through a restricted culvert; surface water from the highway aggravated the flooding. Risk management authorities cleared the channel, increased highway gulley emptying frequency and are investigating changes to overland flow paths. (p22)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties (p22)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Market Street, Whitworth",England,"Market Street and eight nearby properties suffered flooding where the River Spodden flows through a restricted culvert; surface water from the highway aggravated the flooding. Risk management authorities cleared the channel, increased highway gulley emptying frequency and are investigating changes to overland flow paths. (p22)",8 properties (p22),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6962447,-2.2855938,"<div id=""html_341f9da8a070ac19a4e635311d4594ed"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hardman Avenue, Rawtenstall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Following flooding concerns, RBC investigated drainage issues close to Hardman Avenue and the EA checked abstraction arrangements for the upstream reservoir; LCC to liaise with the reservoir owner about outlet arrangements and RBC led on community information for Hardman Avenue. (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Hardman Avenue, Rawtenstall",England,"Following flooding concerns, RBC investigated drainage issues close to Hardman Avenue and the EA checked abstraction arrangements for the upstream reservoir; LCC to liaise with the reservoir owner about outlet arrangements and RBC led on community information for Hardman Avenue. (p23)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.5639768,-2.8893159,"<div id=""html_4a113d59725b7f1c284942450915ce98"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Dyers Lane, Ormskirk</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flows from Railway Path, due to a collapsed culvert, overshot the brook and flooded the north side of Dyers Lane; initial LCC Highways works have mitigated the risk and further surveys/investigations by LCC, UU and Network Rail are underway. (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Dyers Lane, Ormskirk",England,"Surface water flows from Railway Path, due to a collapsed culvert, overshot the brook and flooded the north side of Dyers Lane; initial LCC Highways works have mitigated the risk and further surveys/investigations by LCC, UU and Network Rail are underway. (p26)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6075294,-2.9408421,"<div id=""html_50614584cba1b0e16281d07dfadcba38"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Black Moss Lane, Scarlsbrick</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected the Railway Path residential area including Black Moss Lane (surface water issues were identified and LCC was to investigate). (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Black Moss Lane, Scarlsbrick",England,Surface water flooding affected the Railway Path residential area including Black Moss Lane (surface water issues were identified and LCC was to investigate). (p27),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.5621975,-2.8908275,"<div id=""html_e1277a271657098749e1e1a615f77914"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ryburn Road, Ormskirk</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected the Railway Path residential area including Ryburn Road (surface water issues were identified and LCC was to investigate). (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Ryburn Road, Ormskirk",England,Surface water flooding affected the Railway Path residential area including Ryburn Road (surface water issues were identified and LCC was to investigate). (p27),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.5552474,-2.8816771,"<div id=""html_2b14a78a8b88d2f1ae3e9e8337d6e306"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Altys Lane, Ormskirk</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding at the culvert inlet of Sandy Brook and surface&ndash;water flooding affected property at the northern end of Altys Lane. A temporary bund was installed by LCC Property Group to mitigate overland flow; culvert inspections and drainage checks were undertaken by authorities. (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Altys Lane, Ormskirk",England,Flooding at the culvert inlet of Sandy Brook and surface–water flooding affected property at the northern end of Altys Lane. A temporary bund was installed by LCC Property Group to mitigate overland flow; culvert inspections and drainage checks were undertaken by authorities. (p27),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.5784986,-2.9142494,"<div id=""html_9a12ded0c2e241c77dbadddbdf5dd384"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Asmall Lane, Ormskirk</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water run&ndash;off west of Asmall Lane was identified as the likely main source of flooding that affected nearby properties (notably Altys Lane). (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Asmall Lane, Ormskirk",England,Surface–water run–off west of Asmall Lane was identified as the likely main source of flooding that affected nearby properties (notably Altys Lane). (p27),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.5712671,-2.9395962,"<div id=""html_d0f1d882a0d32ab35c1d2f0367c739ab"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Halsall Lane, Halsall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding and concerns over performance of ordinary watercourse culverts in the vicinity; investigations by LCC/WLBC into culvert blockages, capacity and ability to outfall (which may have caused or exacerbated flooding). Agencies held a community drop&ndash;in and are assessing property protection measures. (p27)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Halsall Lane, Halsall",England,"Surface water flooding and concerns over performance of ordinary watercourse culverts in the vicinity; investigations by LCC/WLBC into culvert blockages, capacity and ability to outfall (which may have caused or exacerbated flooding). Agencies held a community drop–in and are assessing property protection measures. (p27)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.5674018,-2.9489638,"<div id=""html_5aec9d6397f56cdb06285cc54b9927f8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Plex Lane, Halsall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding driven by greenfield runoff and poor performance of ordinary watercourse culverts caused surface water to enter the highway and adjacent land; prompted community drop&ndash;in and response actions including LCC site meetings, highway gulley clearance and jetting, EA ditch clearance and a review of the wider drainage network and responsibilities. (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Plex Lane, Halsall",England,"Flooding driven by greenfield runoff and poor performance of ordinary watercourse culverts caused surface water to enter the highway and adjacent land; prompted community drop–in and response actions including LCC site meetings, highway gulley clearance and jetting, EA ditch clearance and a review of the wider drainage network and responsibilities. (p28)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.5851833,-2.9096548,"<div id=""html_0a8c124651050b1c75ee6a59363556b3"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Southport Road, Ormskirk</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding occurred from a combination of surface water, overtopping of the main river (Hurlston Brook) and ordinary watercourse overtopping, affecting Southport Road; LCC investigated highway drainage functionality and LCC/WLBC/EA arranged culvert investigations while EA modelled Hurlston Brook capacity and inputs. (p28)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Southport Road, Ormskirk",England,"Flooding occurred from a combination of surface water, overtopping of the main river (Hurlston Brook) and ordinary watercourse overtopping, affecting Southport Road; LCC investigated highway drainage functionality and LCC/WLBC/EA arranged culvert investigations while EA modelled Hurlston Brook capacity and inputs. (p28)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7002719,-2.2001618,"<div id=""html_0f490f333d3d85ef8bf6af350052a874"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Henrietta Street, Bacup</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the Bacup town&ndash;centre grouping affected by the summer 2012 floods; properties/garages in this area were flooded. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property and 10 garages (total for Bacup grouping; affects Henrietta St, Oakenclough Rd and Greave Clough) (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Henrietta Street, Bacup",England,Part of the Bacup town–centre grouping affected by the summer 2012 floods; properties/garages in this area were flooded. (p33),"1 property and 10 garages (total for Bacup grouping; affects Henrietta St, Oakenclough Rd and Greave Clough) (p33)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7062077,-2.187627,"<div id=""html_0b314e66a9ea5e7e9e3dd5ec713dbf65"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Oakenclough Road, Bacup</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the Bacup town&ndash;centre grouping affected by the summer 2012 floods; properties/garages in this area were flooded. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property and 10 garages (total for Bacup grouping; affects Henrietta St, Oakenclough Rd and Greave Clough) (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Oakenclough Road, Bacup",England,Part of the Bacup town–centre grouping affected by the summer 2012 floods; properties/garages in this area were flooded. (p33),"1 property and 10 garages (total for Bacup grouping; affects Henrietta St, Oakenclough Rd and Greave Clough) (p33)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7056723,-2.1907226,"<div id=""html_dd5431a4e9f087db3bc259f9a9255d77"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Greave Clough Drive, Bacup</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the Bacup town&ndash;centre grouping affected by the summer 2012 floods; properties/garages in this area were flooded. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property and 10 garages (total for Bacup grouping; affects Henrietta St, Oakenclough Rd and Greave Clough) (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Greave Clough Drive, Bacup",England,Part of the Bacup town–centre grouping affected by the summer 2012 floods; properties/garages in this area were flooded. (p33),"1 property and 10 garages (total for Bacup grouping; affects Henrietta St, Oakenclough Rd and Greave Clough) (p33)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6717743,-2.3055311,"<div id=""html_a689cfc11b356c6000bcf096e72d17cc"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Market Street, Chatterton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Market Street (Edenfield) experienced flooding during the summer 2012 event; cellars/properties were affected by surface water. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 cellar (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Market Street, Chatterton",England,Market Street (Edenfield) experienced flooding during the summer 2012 event; cellars/properties were affected by surface water. (p33),1 cellar (p33),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6797464,-2.3028075,"<div id=""html_3834ed734a5949f46b0c056472a9710a"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fish Rake Lane, Ewood Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Market Street, Fish Rake Lane and Gin Croft Lane were flooded; one cellar in Edenfield also reported flooded. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (Market St, Fish Rake Lane and Gin Croft Lane combined); 1 cellar (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Fish Rake Lane, Ewood Bridge",England,"Residential properties on Market Street, Fish Rake Lane and Gin Croft Lane were flooded; one cellar in Edenfield also reported flooded. (p33)","7 properties (Market St, Fish Rake Lane and Gin Croft Lane combined); 1 cellar (p33)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6703389,-2.3013174,"<div id=""html_3c18bd6404a7eb40704def9bf0852850"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Gincroft Lane, Chatterton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential properties on Market Street, Fish Rake Lane and Gin Croft Lane were flooded; one cellar in Edenfield also reported flooded. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties (Market St, Fish Rake Lane and Gin Croft Lane combined); 1 cellar (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Gincroft Lane, Chatterton",England,"Residential properties on Market Street, Fish Rake Lane and Gin Croft Lane were flooded; one cellar in Edenfield also reported flooded. (p33)","7 properties (Market St, Fish Rake Lane and Gin Croft Lane combined); 1 cellar (p33)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6833453,-2.3350122,"<div id=""html_3c395e6706163291c7a09897b9b4fe83"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Tor End Road, Helmshore</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Tor End Road at Helmshore experienced flooding affecting properties on the road. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>168 properties (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,"Tor End Road, Helmshore",England,Tor End Road at Helmshore experienced flooding affecting properties on the road. (p33),168 properties (p33),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.8611712,-2.5650945,"<div id=""html_7ec947b807ca8398cc2765a76d6c1ee2"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Between June and September 2012 Lancashire experienced a number of significant flooding events: several river levels and rainfall gauging stations hit record highs, monthly&ndash;average September rainfall fell in 2 days in parts of the region, and there was extensive localised and internal property flooding across the county. [PAG] (p3)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Internal property flooding occurred in various places across the county during the summer 2012 flood events; heavy rainfall on 22/23 June 2012 led to rapid river level rises across Lancashire. (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Severe flooding in June affected multiple communities (Croston, Whalley, Leyland, parts of Rossendale and Darwen). Causes recorded included river (Yarrow) overtopping, tributary exceedance and surface water blocking drainage; sewer overloads also caused property flooding. Post&ndash;event repair and flood&ndash;alleviation works were initiated. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Widespread flooding across the county and multiple district areas prompted multi&ndash;agency emergency response and strategic debriefing. The report records property flooding including 7 properties flooded in Sunnyside Terrace. [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>County&ndash;wide response to the June 2012 floods: proactive use of pumping stations to increase watercourse storage capacity in advance of the event; organisation and promotion of community drop&ndash;in facilities to inform and support residents; convening multi&ndash;agency coordination through the Lancashire Resilience Forum debrief (25 July) and Lancashire County Council internal debrief (16 July); actions to improve notification and coordination of rest centres and evacuations; review and follow&ndash;up of flood warning/signup, contact information, trigger levels in LRF plans, teleconferencing and community messaging (including sandbag provision). [PAG] (p17)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding in June 2012 across the county prompted county and multi&ndash;agency response, an LCC internal debrief on 16 July 2012 and additional Making Space for Water meetings; actions were allocated to agencies to improve warnings, communications and operational response. [PAG] (p18)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties within the county were flooded: West Lancashire experienced properties flooded by both river and surface water flooding in September 2012; areas of Rossendale had properties flooded (70 properties in Rossendale were identified as flooded). [PAG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Lancashire was affected by the September 2012 event, with the primary property&ndash;flooding impact occurring in West Lancashire (within the county). (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>County&ndash;wide impact from the 2012 floods that tested flood response and risk&ndash;management arrangements; triggered strategic&ndash;level investigations and operational responses in various districts (including investigations into highway drainage performance and rectification responsibilities for field flooding in West Lancashire); use of district 'Making Space for Water' partnership meetings to agree responsibilities, share investigation findings and identify actions; learning and changes to practice by risk management authorities and emergency services. [PAG] (p29)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Up to 72 properties in Croston identified as having suffered some degree of flooding; UU sample contacts in Lancashire districts include 86 (South Ribble), 58 (Chorley) and 21 (Rossendale). (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>7 properties [PAG] (p15)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>70 properties [PAG] (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>19 properties flooded (in and around Ormskirk, West Lancashire) (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Lancashire,England,"Between June and September 2012 Lancashire experienced a number of significant flooding events: several river levels and rainfall gauging stations hit record highs, monthly–average September rainfall fell in 2 days in parts of the region, and there was extensive localised and internal property flooding across the county. [PAG] (p3)
Internal property flooding occurred in various places across the county during the summer 2012 flood events; heavy rainfall on 22/23 June 2012 led to rapid river level rises across Lancashire. (p9)
Severe flooding in June affected multiple communities (Croston, Whalley, Leyland, parts of Rossendale and Darwen). Causes recorded included river (Yarrow) overtopping, tributary exceedance and surface water blocking drainage; sewer overloads also caused property flooding. Post–event repair and flood–alleviation works were initiated. (p11)
Widespread flooding across the county and multiple district areas prompted multi–agency emergency response and strategic debriefing. The report records property flooding including 7 properties flooded in Sunnyside Terrace. [PAG] (p15)
County–wide response to the June 2012 floods: proactive use of pumping stations to increase watercourse storage capacity in advance of the event; organisation and promotion of community drop–in facilities to inform and support residents; convening multi–agency coordination through the Lancashire Resilience Forum debrief (25 July) and Lancashire County Council internal debrief (16 July); actions to improve notification and coordination of rest centres and evacuations; review and follow–up of flood warning/signup, contact information, trigger levels in LRF plans, teleconferencing and community messaging (including sandbag provision). [PAG] (p17)
Flooding in June 2012 across the county prompted county and multi–agency response, an LCC internal debrief on 16 July 2012 and additional Making Space for Water meetings; actions were allocated to agencies to improve warnings, communications and operational response. [PAG] (p18)
Properties within the county were flooded: West Lancashire experienced properties flooded by both river and surface water flooding in September 2012; areas of Rossendale had properties flooded (70 properties in Rossendale were identified as flooded). [PAG] (p25)
Lancashire was affected by the September 2012 event, with the primary property–flooding impact occurring in West Lancashire (within the county). (p26)
County–wide impact from the 2012 floods that tested flood response and risk–management arrangements; triggered strategic–level investigations and operational responses in various districts (including investigations into highway drainage performance and rectification responsibilities for field flooding in West Lancashire); use of district 'Making Space for Water' partnership meetings to agree responsibilities, share investigation findings and identify actions; learning and changes to practice by risk management authorities and emergency services. [PAG] (p29)","Up to 72 properties in Croston identified as having suffered some degree of flooding; UU sample contacts in Lancashire districts include 86 (South Ribble), 58 (Chorley) and 21 (Rossendale). (p11)
7 properties [PAG] (p15)
70 properties [PAG] (p25)
19 properties flooded (in and around Ormskirk, West Lancashire) (p26)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7271527,-2.7330066,"<div id=""html_569aad54e61bbe003ee9fb0682d1487b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Ribble</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>United Utilities responded to customer reports of wastewater issues (sewer&ndash;related flooding/overloads) during the June incident. [MUL] (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>86 customer contacts reporting wastewater issues between 22 Jun 2012 and 25 Jun 2012. [MUL] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,South Ribble,England,United Utilities responded to customer reports of wastewater issues (sewer–related flooding/overloads) during the June incident. [MUL] (p11),86 customer contacts reporting wastewater issues between 22 Jun 2012 and 25 Jun 2012. [MUL] (p11),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.64704799368739,-2.6735276397097056,"<div id=""html_fbe3f6071af7310d904a9e744d821104"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chorley District</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>United Utilities responded to customer reports of wastewater issues (sewer&ndash;related flooding/overloads) during the June incident. [MUL] (p11)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>58 customer contacts reporting wastewater issues between 22 Jun 2012 and 25 Jun 2012. [MUL] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Chorley District,England,United Utilities responded to customer reports of wastewater issues (sewer–related flooding/overloads) during the June incident. [MUL] (p11),58 customer contacts reporting wastewater issues between 22 Jun 2012 and 25 Jun 2012. [MUL] (p11),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.70249,-2.201046,"<div id=""html_4c7be0043eff679542cbacd06ec8c91e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rossendale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Various parts of Rossendale experienced severe flooding in June; United Utilities also responded to wastewater/sewer&ndash;related customer contacts from the June incident. [MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Localised flooding on 22 June affected multiple settlements across the district, causing property flooding from surface water and from watercourse (brook) flooding. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Approximately 174 properties suffered internal property flooding across Rossendale; multi&ndash;agency flood plan enacted and risk management authorities were mobilised to respond. (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple locations across the Rossendale district experienced flooding. At Ewood Bridge one property was flooded by the River Irwell and six properties flooded due to run&ndash;off from a golf course. Numerous other isolated properties suffered internal property flooding in June where infrastructure deficiencies existed. Local risk management authorities have undertaken remedial actions (wall raised adjacent to the River Irwell, silt clearance by the EA, investigations of culvert and surface water flows) and these activities are being coordinated. (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Communities in Rossendale were affected by flooding during the summer; the EA identified some 70 properties from flooded areas in Rossendale as likely beneficiaries of property flood protection measures. [PAG] (p25)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>21 customer contacts reporting wastewater issues between 22 Jun 2012 and 25 Jun 2012. [MUL] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 24 properties in Bacup; up to 69 properties from Folly Clough Brook; up to 8 properties at Irwell Vale; 17 properties at Strongstry; up to 26 properties at Whitewell Bottoms, Piercy and Edgeside (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>174 properties (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property; 6 properties (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>70 properties [PAG] (p25)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Rossendale,England,"Various parts of Rossendale experienced severe flooding in June; United Utilities also responded to wastewater/sewer–related customer contacts from the June incident. [MUL] (p11)
Localised flooding on 22 June affected multiple settlements across the district, causing property flooding from surface water and from watercourse (brook) flooding. (p13)
Approximately 174 properties suffered internal property flooding across Rossendale; multi–agency flood plan enacted and risk management authorities were mobilised to respond. (p20)
Multiple locations across the Rossendale district experienced flooding. At Ewood Bridge one property was flooded by the River Irwell and six properties flooded due to run–off from a golf course. Numerous other isolated properties suffered internal property flooding in June where infrastructure deficiencies existed. Local risk management authorities have undertaken remedial actions (wall raised adjacent to the River Irwell, silt clearance by the EA, investigations of culvert and surface water flows) and these activities are being coordinated. (p24)
Communities in Rossendale were affected by flooding during the summer; the EA identified some 70 properties from flooded areas in Rossendale as likely beneficiaries of property flood protection measures. [PAG] (p25)","21 customer contacts reporting wastewater issues between 22 Jun 2012 and 25 Jun 2012. [MUL] (p11)
up to 24 properties in Bacup; up to 69 properties from Folly Clough Brook; up to 8 properties at Irwell Vale; 17 properties at Strongstry; up to 26 properties at Whitewell Bottoms, Piercy and Edgeside (p13)
174 properties (p20)
1 property; 6 properties (p24)
70 properties [PAG] (p25)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6109397,-2.8565713,"<div id=""html_2075985ff7b9e80879da1dbfae439bea"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>West Lancashire</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Most severe property flooding in the September event occurred in the borough. Internal flooding of properties resulted from exceptionally intense/localised rainfall, surface water and greenfield runoff, and ordinary watercourse culvert surcharges; extensive field flooding was also reported. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>West Lancashire suffered property flooding during the September 2012 event caused by a combination of surface water, ordinary watercourse and main river issues; community meetings and partner agency meetings were held to develop mitigation proposals and the EA led interest in community flood action groups. (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface&ndash;water / culvert&ndash;related flooding affected communities and properties within the district (locations described include Ormskirk/Altys Lane and Halsall/Plex Lane). (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Multiple locations in West Lancashire were flooded during 2012: Plex Lane (Halsall) experienced flooding driven by greenfield runoff, highway surface water and ordinary watercourse/culvert performance problems; Westhead village flooded from surface water and ordinary watercourse overtopping; Southport Road, Ormskirk flooded from a combination of surface water and overtopping of Hurlston Brook (main river) and ordinary watercourses. Authorities carried out gully/ditch clearance and investigated culvert and drainage capacity. (p28)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Up to 18 residential properties; 2 commercial properties (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>19 properties flooded in and around Ormskirk (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,West Lancashire,England,"Most severe property flooding in the September event occurred in the borough. Internal flooding of properties resulted from exceptionally intense/localised rainfall, surface water and greenfield runoff, and ordinary watercourse culvert surcharges; extensive field flooding was also reported. (p14)
West Lancashire suffered property flooding during the September 2012 event caused by a combination of surface water, ordinary watercourse and main river issues; community meetings and partner agency meetings were held to develop mitigation proposals and the EA led interest in community flood action groups. (p26)
Surface–water / culvert–related flooding affected communities and properties within the district (locations described include Ormskirk/Altys Lane and Halsall/Plex Lane). (p27)
Multiple locations in West Lancashire were flooded during 2012: Plex Lane (Halsall) experienced flooding driven by greenfield runoff, highway surface water and ordinary watercourse/culvert performance problems; Westhead village flooded from surface water and ordinary watercourse overtopping; Southport Road, Ormskirk flooded from a combination of surface water and overtopping of Hurlston Brook (main river) and ordinary watercourses. Authorities carried out gully/ditch clearance and investigated culvert and drainage capacity. (p28)","Up to 18 residential properties; 2 commercial properties (p14)
19 properties flooded in and around Ormskirk (p26)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.9026441,-2.422856,"<div id=""html_ae20c58da7460a0dd1a098a38c35b650"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ribble Valley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>District experienced clustered property flooding during the summer 2012 events reported in the regional analysis. [IMG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Ribble Valley,England,District experienced clustered property flooding during the summer 2012 events reported in the regional analysis. [IMG] (p31),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,54.2720691,-2.7713617,"<div id=""html_2e7673bfa3909f0963dfbb1ac5bd6c5d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>South Lakeland</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Main&ndash;river flooding affected the district during summer 2012, with properties flooded as recorded in the regional summary. [IMG] (p31)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>30 properties [IMG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,South Lakeland,England,"Main–river flooding affected the district during summer 2012, with properties flooded as recorded in the regional summary. [IMG] (p31)",30 properties [IMG] (p31),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7024932,-2.201046,"<div id=""html_ac4d0aa431d37ef104b09aa79d71d726"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bacup</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Record river levels were reached on the upper River Irwell in the Bacup area during the 22/23 June 2012 event. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A flood warning was issued for the River Irwell at Bacup (warning recorded at 19:27 on 22 June 2012), indicating local river flooding risk affecting Bacup. [IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected residential properties in Bacup. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A number of streets in Bacup suffered flooding from surface water, blocked drains and overtopping ordinary watercourses; investigations and drainage repairs (including replacement of a damaged highway drain and clearing an obstructed drainage outlet) were carried out by local authorities. (p23)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 24 properties (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Bacup,England,"Record river levels were reached on the upper River Irwell in the Bacup area during the 22/23 June 2012 event. [PAG] (p9)
A flood warning was issued for the River Irwell at Bacup (warning recorded at 19:27 on 22 June 2012), indicating local river flooding risk affecting Bacup. [IMG] (p10)
Surface water flooding affected residential properties in Bacup. (p13)
A number of streets in Bacup suffered flooding from surface water, blocked drains and overtopping ordinary watercourses; investigations and drainage repairs (including replacement of a damaged highway drain and clearing an obstructed drainage outlet) were carried out by local authorities. (p23)",up to 24 properties (p13),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.701283,-2.2862723,"<div id=""html_17d794d101f9af95612a18152f26034d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Rawtenstall</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Record river levels were reached on the upper River Irwell in the Rawtenstall area during the 22/23 June 2012 event. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from Ballenden Clough and Ballenden Brook affected locations in Rawtenstall; EA repaired and ensured access to debris screens, replaced the screen adjacent to Market Street, and risk management authorities visited units and investigated drainage issues and reservoir/outlet arrangements near Hardman Avenue. (p23)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Rawtenstall,England,"Record river levels were reached on the upper River Irwell in the Rawtenstall area during the 22/23 June 2012 event. [PAG] (p9)
Flooding from Ballenden Clough and Ballenden Brook affected locations in Rawtenstall; EA repaired and ensured access to debris screens, replaced the screen adjacent to Market Street, and risk management authorities visited units and investigated drainage issues and reservoir/outlet arrangements near Hardman Avenue. (p23)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.66187410234079,-2.7761246324411504,"<div id=""html_1a0a504d577ec357b79063a05b2fae1e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Croston</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood Warnings were issued for the River Yarrow at Croston (multiple warnings in the timeline), indicating a river flooding threat to Croston. [IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High River Yarrow levels prevented surface water draining; the river overtopped its channel and surface water built up and flooded properties. A small tributary also exceeded capacity and flowed through a garden and down a road into properties. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>High River Yarrow levels caused the river to overtop its banks and prevented surface water draining from the village. Surface water built up and flooded properties; a small tributary also exceeded capacity and flooded through a garden and down a road into properties. Risk&ndash;management responses include repairs to the River Yarrow floodwall, surface water outfall improvements, Environment Agency working with the local flood action group to develop an improved flood alleviation scheme and a business case; the village&#8217;s proposed accelerated flood defence scheme has attracted indicative national funding. [IMG,PAG] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property flooding occurred in Croston during the 24 September 2012 event (reported as a lesser&ndash;scale location of property flooding). (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 72 properties [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>72 properties [IMG,PAG] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Croston,England,"Flood Warnings were issued for the River Yarrow at Croston (multiple warnings in the timeline), indicating a river flooding threat to Croston. [IMG] (p10)
High River Yarrow levels prevented surface water draining; the river overtopped its channel and surface water built up and flooded properties. A small tributary also exceeded capacity and flowed through a garden and down a road into properties. [PAG] (p11)
High River Yarrow levels caused the river to overtop its banks and prevented surface water draining from the village. Surface water built up and flooded properties; a small tributary also exceeded capacity and flooded through a garden and down a road into properties. Risk–management responses include repairs to the River Yarrow floodwall, surface water outfall improvements, Environment Agency working with the local flood action group to develop an improved flood alleviation scheme and a business case; the village’s proposed accelerated flood defence scheme has attracted indicative national funding. [IMG,PAG] (p12)
Property flooding occurred in Croston during the 24 September 2012 event (reported as a lesser–scale location of property flooding). (p14)","up to 72 properties [PAG] (p11)
