GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.9945538,-2.7872057,"<div id=""html_afa4d680427b7a961cd1983ea33e68a8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Galgate</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A Flood Warning was issued for the River Conder at Galgate (timeline entry), indicating river flooding threat to the village. [IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Galgate,England,"A Flood Warning was issued for the River Conder at Galgate (timeline entry), indicating river flooding threat to the village. [IMG] (p10)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6648613,-2.317359,"<div id=""html_a45bdeb06162fde7eeb9f5b458c326ff"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Strongstry</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A Flood Warning was issued for the River Irwell at Strongstry (timeline entry listing Irwell @ Strongstry/Chatterton), indicating river flooding threat to Strongstry. (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties at Strongstry were flooded from a combination of ordinary watercourse/high river levels, surface water and sewer surcharge. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties on North Street in Strongstry were flooded due to high River Irwell levels, worsened by surface water runoff from the railway embankment and a local ordinary watercourse. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Strongstry was identified as a community affected by flooding during summer 2012; local volunteers were recruited to represent community action and to identify vulnerable residents for prioritised EA support. (p25)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>17 properties (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Strongstry,England,"A Flood Warning was issued for the River Irwell at Strongstry (timeline entry listing Irwell @ Strongstry/Chatterton), indicating river flooding threat to Strongstry. (p10)
Properties at Strongstry were flooded from a combination of ordinary watercourse/high river levels, surface water and sewer surcharge. (p13)
Properties on North Street in Strongstry were flooded due to high River Irwell levels, worsened by surface water runoff from the railway embankment and a local ordinary watercourse. (p21)
Strongstry was identified as a community affected by flooding during summer 2012; local volunteers were recruited to represent community action and to identify vulnerable residents for prioritised EA support. (p25)",17 properties (p13),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6628336,-2.3149128,"<div id=""html_d4e83bd517752e45d12ac28bdf3e0957"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Chatterton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A Flood Warning was issued for the River Irwell at Chatterton (timeline entry listing Irwell @ Strongstry/Chatterton), indicating river flooding threat to Chatterton. [IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding at Chatterton was contributed to by high River Irwell levels, with additional surface&ndash;water runoff from a car park adding to property flooding. (p21)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Chatterton,England,"A Flood Warning was issued for the River Irwell at Chatterton (timeline entry listing Irwell @ Strongstry/Chatterton), indicating river flooding threat to Chatterton. [IMG] (p10)
Flooding at Chatterton was contributed to by high River Irwell levels, with additional surface–water runoff from a car park adding to property flooding. (p21)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.82241346770246,-2.4078975614186295,"<div id=""html_763d59566d103314fb2d2da720bbd862"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whalley</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>The Environment Agency issued multiple flood warnings for the River Calder at Whalley (warnings issued at 19:19, 20:32 and 21:04 on 22 June 2012), indicating imminent/occurring river flooding risk to the Whalley area and riverside assets. [IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Whalley was identified as one of the locations that experienced severe flooding in June 2012; flood alerts and multiple staged flood warnings for the River Calder were issued on 22 June 2012. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flood warnings were issued on 22 June. Flooding occurred around 22&ndash;23 June to properties in the area (Calder Vale/King Street) primarily from the Mill Race leading to Calder Brook. A garden wall collapsed adjacent to Whalley Weir. Cross House (Riddings Lane) and Abbey Croft (The Sands) flooded when the River Calder came out of bank. Some properties used flood boards which were effective at the front of houses. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties; 2 properties (Cross House, Abbey Croft) (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Whalley,England,"The Environment Agency issued multiple flood warnings for the River Calder at Whalley (warnings issued at 19:19, 20:32 and 21:04 on 22 June 2012), indicating imminent/occurring river flooding risk to the Whalley area and riverside assets. [IMG] (p10)
Whalley was identified as one of the locations that experienced severe flooding in June 2012; flood alerts and multiple staged flood warnings for the River Calder were issued on 22 June 2012. [PAG] (p11)
Flood warnings were issued on 22 June. Flooding occurred around 22–23 June to properties in the area (Calder Vale/King Street) primarily from the Mill Race leading to Calder Brook. A garden wall collapsed adjacent to Whalley Weir. Cross House (Riddings Lane) and Abbey Croft (The Sands) flooded when the River Calder came out of bank. Some properties used flood boards which were effective at the front of houses. (p12)","18 properties; 2 properties (Cross House, Abbey Croft) (p12)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.81359304893992,-2.5320952047206924,"<div id=""html_8c94ebce27ce8bdb7b5afc60a1d35497"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ribchester</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ribchester was the subject of a Flood Warning on the River Ribble (Ribble @ Ribchester 'A' at 18:36 on 22 June 2012), indicating river flooding or imminent flooding impacting the settlement area. [IMG] (p10)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Ribchester,England,"Ribchester was the subject of a Flood Warning on the River Ribble (Ribble @ Ribchester 'A' at 18:36 on 22 June 2012), indicating river flooding or imminent flooding impacting the settlement area. [IMG] (p10)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6775859865751,-2.316467158860694,"<div id=""html_2a22738c1fb5d34b24877f7ceba8899f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Irwell Vale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Environment Agency issued a Flood Warning for Irwell Vale (19:08 on 22 June 2012), indicating elevated river levels on the River Irwell and a risk of river flooding to properties and infrastructure in Irwell Vale during the event. [IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in Irwell Vale were flooded from a combination of ordinary watercourse/high river levels, surface water and sewer surcharge. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding resulted from surface water from the hillside and groundwater emergence, with high River Irwell levels hindering drainage; some property&ndash;level resistance measures failed. Actions included EA commissioning an independent appraisal, loaning a pump, providing a site controller and training, and UU identifying a leaking sewer via CCTV. (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Irwell Vale was named as a community affected by flooding in summer 2012; community volunteers were appointed to act as liaison and to identify vulnerable people for prioritised support by the EA. (p25)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 8 properties (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Irwell Vale,England,"Environment Agency issued a Flood Warning for Irwell Vale (19:08 on 22 June 2012), indicating elevated river levels on the River Irwell and a risk of river flooding to properties and infrastructure in Irwell Vale during the event. [IMG] (p10)
Properties in Irwell Vale were flooded from a combination of ordinary watercourse/high river levels, surface water and sewer surcharge. (p13)
Flooding resulted from surface water from the hillside and groundwater emergence, with high River Irwell levels hindering drainage; some property–level resistance measures failed. Actions included EA commissioning an independent appraisal, loaning a pump, providing a site controller and training, and UU identifying a leaking sewer via CCTV. (p20)
Irwell Vale was named as a community affected by flooding in summer 2012; community volunteers were appointed to act as liaison and to identify vulnerable people for prioritised support by the EA. (p25)",up to 8 properties (p13),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.690483,-2.6991336,"<div id=""html_27ea40cd7eaed827522d3cd03e8bed7d"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Leyland</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Leyland was cited as one of the most severely affected Lancashire locations in June 2012; the wider South Ribble area (which includes Leyland) recorded a notable rise in United Utilities customer contacts regarding wastewater issues between 22 and 25 June 2012. (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property flooding on Curlew Close, Western Drive, Longmeanygate, Midge Hall, Bannister Drive, Fowler Lane and Fowler Avenue due to surface water with some surcharge of dilute sewage from the combined sewer system; high water levels in nearby watercourses exacerbated drainage issues. A community drop&ndash;in session was arranged for affected residents. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>at least 15 properties (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Leyland,England,"Leyland was cited as one of the most severely affected Lancashire locations in June 2012; the wider South Ribble area (which includes Leyland) recorded a notable rise in United Utilities customer contacts regarding wastewater issues between 22 and 25 June 2012. (p11)
Property flooding on Curlew Close, Western Drive, Longmeanygate, Midge Hall, Bannister Drive, Fowler Lane and Fowler Avenue due to surface water with some surcharge of dilute sewage from the combined sewer system; high water levels in nearby watercourses exacerbated drainage issues. A community drop–in session was arranged for affected residents. (p13)",at least 15 properties (p13),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.696095,-2.4665093,"<div id=""html_6800bcffb36862477823042b8785cae8"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Darwen</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Darwen is listed among the locations that experienced severe flooding in June 2012 (within the Blackburn with Darwen LLFA area). [PAG] (p11)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Darwen,England,Darwen is listed among the locations that experienced severe flooding in June 2012 (within the Blackburn with Darwen LLFA area). [PAG] (p11),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.9059476,-2.7136994,"<div id=""html_390d77cf04557f3535fb6768f30d8e52"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Calder Vale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding on 22&ndash;23 June affected the Calder Vale area, primarily from the Mill Race leading to Calder Brook; some properties used flood boards which were effective at the front of houses. (p12)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>18 properties (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Calder Vale,England,"Flooding on 22–23 June affected the Calder Vale area, primarily from the Mill Race leading to Calder Brook; some properties used flood boards which were effective at the front of houses. (p12)",18 properties (p12),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.74784,-2.6720357,"<div id=""html_ed923c4008aa85d82d2623011ba41452"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Walton-Le-Dale</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding from the River Darwen affected properties downstream of Cann Bridge; surface water flooding also affected the highway. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>5 properties; 6 businesses (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Walton-Le-Dale,England,Flooding from the River Darwen affected properties downstream of Cann Bridge; surface water flooding also affected the highway. (p13),5 properties; 6 businesses (p13),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7079574,-2.2494907,"<div id=""html_1083fdc80cf99597b06d439d7b124f8f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whitewell Bottoms</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected properties in Whitewell Bottoms (reported together with Piercy and Edgeside). (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>up to 26 properties (combined across Whitewell Bottoms, Piercy and Edgeside) (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Whitewell Bottoms,England,Surface water flooding affected properties in Whitewell Bottoms (reported together with Piercy and Edgeside). (p13),"up to 26 properties (combined across Whitewell Bottoms, Piercy and Edgeside) (p13)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6996999,-2.2453133,"<div id=""html_22dc2860ccd02d3b34693870f5f7d00f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Edgeside</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding affected properties in Edgeside as part of a localised event in Rossendale. (p13)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>Up to 26 properties affected across Whitewell Bottoms, Piercy and Edgeside (collective total) (p13)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Edgeside,England,Surface water flooding affected properties in Edgeside as part of a localised event in Rossendale. (p13),"Up to 26 properties affected across Whitewell Bottoms, Piercy and Edgeside (collective total) (p13)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.56736,-2.8859603,"<div id=""html_e842c612d6d51e9f6730e6be69740498"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ormskirk</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Residential internal property flooding particularly affected Ormskirk and surrounding rural areas; causes cited for the borough included surface water, greenfield runoff and ordinary watercourse culvert surcharges. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Ormskirk experienced property flooding in the September 2012 event (19 properties flooded); community drop&ndash;in and follow&ndash;up meetings were held and there was interest in forming community flood action groups led by the EA. (p26)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in Ormskirk (notably at the northern end of Altys Lane) were affected by surface&ndash;water flooding at a culvert inlet; temporary mitigation (bund) was installed. (p27)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Parts of Ormskirk (notably Southport Road) experienced flooding from surface water and overtopping of Hurlston Brook; local highway drainage and culvert performance were investigated by LCC with multi&ndash;agency culvert investigations and modelling by the EA. (p28)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>19 properties flooded (p26)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Ormskirk,England,"Residential internal property flooding particularly affected Ormskirk and surrounding rural areas; causes cited for the borough included surface water, greenfield runoff and ordinary watercourse culvert surcharges. (p14)
Ormskirk experienced property flooding in the September 2012 event (19 properties flooded); community drop–in and follow–up meetings were held and there was interest in forming community flood action groups led by the EA. (p26)
Properties in Ormskirk (notably at the northern end of Altys Lane) were affected by surface–water flooding at a culvert inlet; temporary mitigation (bund) was installed. (p27)
Parts of Ormskirk (notably Southport Road) experienced flooding from surface water and overtopping of Hurlston Brook; local highway drainage and culvert performance were investigated by LCC with multi–agency culvert investigations and modelling by the EA. (p28)",19 properties flooded (p26),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.873855500000005,-2.950319910579624,"<div id=""html_f618a96c22606f8680d5d6299d6ee73b"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Hambleton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding on 24 September 2012 affected properties on Sherbourne Road due to flows from highway drainage and the sewer network. (p14)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>12 properties (p14)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Hambleton,England,Flooding on 24 September 2012 affected properties on Sherbourne Road due to flows from highway drainage and the sewer network. (p14),12 properties (p14),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.749325,-2.4840567,"<div id=""html_a69d9baa9b24698c0adecff6b5d61f10"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Blackburn</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Significant and/or property flooding occurred in the district; the district council was one of the authorities where property flooding took place and whose representatives attended the LLFA&ndash;led debrief. (p15)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Blackburn,England,Significant and/or property flooding occurred in the district; the district council was one of the authorities where property flooding took place and whose representatives attended the LLFA–led debrief. (p15),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.7239847,-2.2860309,"<div id=""html_f491c1f694c4317f4bf82f6458cd8016"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Crawshawbooth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Community drop&ndash;in sessions were organised in Crawshawbooth for affected property owners to discuss resilience, property protection and insurance following the June 2012 flooding in Rossendale. (p20)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping of Folly Clough Brook (due to obstruction of a debris screen) caused the culvert to overtop and resulted in flooding that affected adjacent properties and Water Street, threatening property and highway assets. (p21)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Crawshawbooth was identified as a community affected by flooding in summer 2012; community volunteers were appointed to represent local action and to identify vulnerable residents for prioritised EA support. (p25)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Crawshawbooth,England,"Community drop–in sessions were organised in Crawshawbooth for affected property owners to discuss resilience, property protection and insurance following the June 2012 flooding in Rossendale. (p20)
Overtopping of Folly Clough Brook (due to obstruction of a debris screen) caused the culvert to overtop and resulted in flooding that affected adjacent properties and Water Street, threatening property and highway assets. (p21)
Crawshawbooth was identified as a community affected by flooding in summer 2012; community volunteers were appointed to represent local action and to identify vulnerable residents for prioritised EA support. (p25)",,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.66924745,-2.1852538962618415,"<div id=""html_a22315d9f0d39eaf83bed6acdd12f55c"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Whitworth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>River Spodden overtopped at two locations in Whitworth causing flooding to the local leisure centre, nearby industrial units and shop cellars in June. Risk management works were carried out including raising a river bank wall near the leisure centre and riparian repairs adjacent to Bridge End industrial units. (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Community of Whitworth was affected by flooding during summer 2012. Local volunteers were identified to represent community action and to help agencies identify vulnerable people so the EA could prioritise support; Whitworth is included in partner plans for property&ndash;level protection for recently flooded communities in Rossendale. (p25)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in Whitworth were flooded during the summer 2012 event, causing property flooding impacts to residential premises. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>two locations (p23)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Whitworth,England,"River Spodden overtopped at two locations in Whitworth causing flooding to the local leisure centre, nearby industrial units and shop cellars in June. Risk management works were carried out including raising a river bank wall near the leisure centre and riparian repairs adjacent to Bridge End industrial units. (p23)
Community of Whitworth was affected by flooding during summer 2012. Local volunteers were identified to represent community action and to help agencies identify vulnerable people so the EA could prioritise support; Whitworth is included in partner plans for property–level protection for recently flooded communities in Rossendale. (p25)
Properties in Whitworth were flooded during the summer 2012 event, causing property flooding impacts to residential premises. (p33)","two locations (p23)
8 properties (p33)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.686832,-2.3119442,"<div id=""html_a6ca987c142e86496401bd78ee5d8165"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Ewood Bridge</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Flooding affected properties at Ewood Bridge: one property flooded by overtopping/flow from the River Irwell; six properties flooded by run&ndash;off from a golf course. Response and investigations (wall raised, silt clearance, culvert feasibility, surface water flow investigations) were undertaken. (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties at Ewood Bridge were flooded; flooding included at least one property flooded by the main river with other properties affected by surface water. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>1 property; 6 properties (p24)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>11 properties (including 1 from main river) (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Ewood Bridge,England,"Flooding affected properties at Ewood Bridge: one property flooded by overtopping/flow from the River Irwell; six properties flooded by run–off from a golf course. Response and investigations (wall raised, silt clearance, culvert feasibility, surface water flow investigations) were undertaken. (p24)
Properties at Ewood Bridge were flooded; flooding included at least one property flooded by the main river with other properties affected by surface water. (p33)","1 property; 6 properties (p24)
11 properties (including 1 from main river) (p33)",GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6445374,-2.8610341,"<div id=""html_d9091c0acf2c1fd09ab78f678e623a67"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Holmeswood</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Experienced flows from a severed culvert and sewer capacity concerns leading to UU modelling and LCC provision of community information to address flood risk. (p24)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Holmeswood,England,Experienced flows from a severed culvert and sewer capacity concerns leading to UU modelling and LCC provision of community information to address flood risk. (p24),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6594147,-2.3207965,"<div id=""html_8010e84965aa89db4f9dae5773a7bbc0"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Stubbins</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Stubbins was named as a community affected by flooding in summer 2012; volunteers were identified to represent the community and to help locate vulnerable people for EA support. (p25)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Stubbins,England,Stubbins was named as a community affected by flooding in summer 2012; volunteers were identified to represent the community and to help locate vulnerable people for EA support. (p25),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,54.1288796,-3.2269008,"<div id=""html_ab8891e495d7691008f112cf0454897f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Barrow-In-Furness</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Property flooding reported as part of a cluster of summer 2012 flood events affecting Barrow&ndash;in&ndash;Furness. [IMG] (p31)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Barrow-In-Furness,England,Property flooding reported as part of a cluster of summer 2012 flood events affecting Barrow–in–Furness. [IMG] (p31),,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-LAN,4,2026-06-01,53.6803936,-2.1674433,"<div id=""html_615df38fc62089d4f78c6f29ed85d7df"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Shawforth</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Properties in Shawforth were flooded during the summer 2012 event, causing property flooding impacts to residential premises. (p33)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>8 properties (p33)</p></div></div></body></div>",Lancashire,Shawforth,England,"Properties in Shawforth were flooded during the summer 2012 event, causing property flooding impacts to residential premises. (p33)",8 properties (p33),GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01.html,GB-LAN_4_2026-06-01,Lancashire flooding June - September 2012,Lancashire County Council Flood Investigation Report: Lancashire Summer 2012,069/Lancashire County/flood-investigation-report.pdf
GB-CAM,29,2021-07-20,52.102427,0.2710864,"<div id=""html_a38bd32d256978384d9fa3ec21fe442e"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Granta</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A floodplain associated with the River Granta runs through Linton and high surface&ndash;water flood risk zones are concentrated along the river. During the intense rainfall on 20 July 2021 significant flooding occurred in Linton; flood extent and surface&ndash;water flooding were closely associated with the River Granta corridor and extended into nearby low&ndash;lying built&ndash;up areas. [PAG,IMG] (p7)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,Granta,England,"A floodplain associated with the River Granta runs through Linton and high surface–water flood risk zones are concentrated along the river. During the intense rainfall on 20 July 2021 significant flooding occurred in Linton; flood extent and surface–water flooding were closely associated with the River Granta corridor and extended into nearby low–lying built–up areas. [PAG,IMG] (p7)",,GB-CAM_29_2021-07-20.html,GB-CAM_29_2021-07-20,Linton flooding 20 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Linton,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2021/Cambridgeshire County/Linton-July-2021-Flood-Investigation-v1.2.pdf
GB-CAM,29,2021-07-20,52.0976156,0.2825711,"<div id=""html_98a6e0ac59d94a2874118e09a5efcf14"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>High Street, Linton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Identified as one of three key risk areas where internal property flooding was reported on 20 July 2021; properties experienced rapid ingress of water with levels receding relatively quickly. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flooding occurred at a topographic low where high surface water flows were directed toward properties; limited highway drainage and low kerbs contributed to inundation. Internal property flooding was reported in this area and water entered properties rapidly before receding. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water pooled in a topographic low and was directed toward properties. Properties were flooded internally and gardens and outbuildings were affected. The area has low kerbs and limited highway drainage which contributed to the flooding. No reports of residents leaving their premises. [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reports of flooding prompted on&ndash;site attendance and investigations by the LLFA and Highway Authority; highway drainage investigations were funded/confirmed and gully maintenance frequency was increased. South Cambridgeshire District Council provided sandbags to properties in the area. [TAB] (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the intense convective storm on 20 July 2021 surface water followed local topography and flowed along High Street. Rainfall rates exceeded drainage capacity, causing surface water flooding of the road and low&ndash;lying points. [TAB] (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"High Street, Linton",England,"Identified as one of three key risk areas where internal property flooding was reported on 20 July 2021; properties experienced rapid ingress of water with levels receding relatively quickly. [PAG] (p9)
Surface water flooding occurred at a topographic low where high surface water flows were directed toward properties; limited highway drainage and low kerbs contributed to inundation. Internal property flooding was reported in this area and water entered properties rapidly before receding. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Surface water pooled in a topographic low and was directed toward properties. Properties were flooded internally and gardens and outbuildings were affected. The area has low kerbs and limited highway drainage which contributed to the flooding. No reports of residents leaving their premises. [TAB] (p11)
Reports of flooding prompted on–site attendance and investigations by the LLFA and Highway Authority; highway drainage investigations were funded/confirmed and gully maintenance frequency was increased. South Cambridgeshire District Council provided sandbags to properties in the area. [TAB] (p14)
During the intense convective storm on 20 July 2021 surface water followed local topography and flowed along High Street. Rainfall rates exceeded drainage capacity, causing surface water flooding of the road and low–lying points. [TAB] (p20)",,GB-CAM_29_2021-07-20.html,GB-CAM_29_2021-07-20,Linton flooding 20 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Linton,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2021/Cambridgeshire County/Linton-July-2021-Flood-Investigation-v1.2.pdf
GB-CAM,29,2021-07-20,52.0978627,0.2841835,"<div id=""html_ad4e399de2ac072ac870c557e48bb455"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Balsham Road, Linton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the Balsham Road/Lamb Fair Court risk area where internal property flooding was reported on 20 July 2021; flooding involved rapid entry of water into properties. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported location of internal property flooding as one of three key risk areas in the village; properties experienced rapid&ndash;onset flooding with water ingress to buildings. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowed down Balsham Road from the highway and surrounding fields; the highways drainage system was inundated. Water flowed over dropped kerbs towards properties on the south side of the road, flooding properties internally and gardens/outbuildings to an approximate depth of 15 cm. Water receded within about 12 hours. Some highway drains were found partially or fully blocked. There are reports of residents having to leave their property for over one month. [TAB] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water runoff from the fields and highway above these roads contributed to flooding; the LLFA is working with Highways and landowners to investigate measures to reduce runoff and whether additional attenuation capacity can be introduced. Highway drainage (gullies) were inspected and works orders raised for cleaning. (p13)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the 20 July 2021 storm surface water flowed along Balsham Road; the drainage network capacity was exceeded. Riparian maintenance issues were also identified as a contributing factor to flooding on this road. [TAB] (p20)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Balsham Road, Linton",England,"Part of the Balsham Road/Lamb Fair Court risk area where internal property flooding was reported on 20 July 2021; flooding involved rapid entry of water into properties. [PAG] (p9)
Reported location of internal property flooding as one of three key risk areas in the village; properties experienced rapid–onset flooding with water ingress to buildings. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Surface water flowed down Balsham Road from the highway and surrounding fields; the highways drainage system was inundated. Water flowed over dropped kerbs towards properties on the south side of the road, flooding properties internally and gardens/outbuildings to an approximate depth of 15 cm. Water receded within about 12 hours. Some highway drains were found partially or fully blocked. There are reports of residents having to leave their property for over one month. [TAB] (p11)
Surface water runoff from the fields and highway above these roads contributed to flooding; the LLFA is working with Highways and landowners to investigate measures to reduce runoff and whether additional attenuation capacity can be introduced. Highway drainage (gullies) were inspected and works orders raised for cleaning. (p13)
During the 20 July 2021 storm surface water flowed along Balsham Road; the drainage network capacity was exceeded. Riparian maintenance issues were also identified as a contributing factor to flooding on this road. [TAB] (p20)",,GB-CAM_29_2021-07-20.html,GB-CAM_29_2021-07-20,Linton flooding 20 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Linton,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2021/Cambridgeshire County/Linton-July-2021-Flood-Investigation-v1.2.pdf
GB-CAM,29,2021-07-20,52.0976516,0.2921274,"<div id=""html_357f21aa4b22927bf696cd30b3cbfbd9"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Lonsdale, Linton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Reported internal property flooding as part of the south&ndash;east residential cluster (grouped with Bakers Lane, Bartlow Road and Finchams Close); flooding was rapid ('flash') with properties affected internally. [PAG,IMG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowing west along Horseheath Road entered Lonsdale; most was captured by the highway drainage system, but there was an initial report of minor flooding at the bottom of Lonsdale where water entered a garage. [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>A retaining wall situated between Lonsdale and Bakers Lane initially held back an inrush of water but then overtopped/failed, releasing a large volume of surface water that flowed towards and into properties in the adjoining streets and exacerbated flooding. (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water flowing across a construction site at Lonsdale prompted meetings and immediate mitigation by the developer (tankers on standby to reduce water in a partly constructed basin, rearranging stored materials to avoid mobilising debris into the basin) to reduce the risk of further flooding. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 20 July 2021 surface water ran along Lonsdale into low points causing surface water flooding. The report also records misconnections/ingress of rainwater into the foul network or sewer at this location, exacerbating sewer&ndash;related flooding risks; riparian maintenance issues were noted as a contributing factor. [TAB] (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>one garage [PAG] (p11)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15&ndash;45cm; 15&ndash;20cm (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Lonsdale, Linton",England,"Reported internal property flooding as part of the south–east residential cluster (grouped with Bakers Lane, Bartlow Road and Finchams Close); flooding was rapid ('flash') with properties affected internally. [PAG,IMG] (p10)
Surface water flowing west along Horseheath Road entered Lonsdale; most was captured by the highway drainage system, but there was an initial report of minor flooding at the bottom of Lonsdale where water entered a garage. [PAG] (p11)
A retaining wall situated between Lonsdale and Bakers Lane initially held back an inrush of water but then overtopped/failed, releasing a large volume of surface water that flowed towards and into properties in the adjoining streets and exacerbated flooding. (p12)
Surface water flowing across a construction site at Lonsdale prompted meetings and immediate mitigation by the developer (tankers on standby to reduce water in a partly constructed basin, rearranging stored materials to avoid mobilising debris into the basin) to reduce the risk of further flooding. (p14)
On 20 July 2021 surface water ran along Lonsdale into low points causing surface water flooding. The report also records misconnections/ingress of rainwater into the foul network or sewer at this location, exacerbating sewer–related flooding risks; riparian maintenance issues were noted as a contributing factor. [TAB] (p20)","one garage [PAG] (p11)
15–45cm; 15–20cm (p12)",GB-CAM_29_2021-07-20.html,GB-CAM_29_2021-07-20,Linton flooding 20 Jul 2021,Flood Investigation Report: Linton,021/Cambridgeshire County/021/2021/Cambridgeshire County/Linton-July-2021-Flood-Investigation-v1.2.pdf
GB-CAM,29,2021-07-20,52.0832298,0.3102951,"<div id=""html_f6ec5051411c2be3bc71d3d5d8e8913f"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Bartlow Road, Linton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in the Lonsdale/Bakers Lane/Bartlow Road/Finchams Close group identified as a key risk area where internal property flooding was reported on 20 July 2021; properties experienced rapid ingress of water. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Group of streets identified as a key risk area where internal property flooding was reported; properties experienced rapid ingress of water consistent with flash flooding. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Overtopping flows from the retaining wall and surface water moving down Lonsdale reached properties on Bartlow Road, causing internal and external flooding to properties and gardens. [TAB] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Part of the Lonsdale/Bakers Lane/Bartlow Road area affected by surface water flowing across a construction site; developer actions taken (tankers, rearranging materials) to reduce risk of further flooding. (p14)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>On 20 July 2021 surface water flowed along Bartlow Road causing surface water flooding. The report identifies misconnections/ingress into the foul/sewer network and riparian maintenance shortcomings as contributing factors. [TAB] (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15&ndash;20cm (reported depth in Bartlow Road) [TAB] (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Bartlow Road, Linton",England,"Included in the Lonsdale/Bakers Lane/Bartlow Road/Finchams Close group identified as a key risk area where internal property flooding was reported on 20 July 2021; properties experienced rapid ingress of water. [PAG] (p9)
