GB-CAM,29,2021-07-20,52.0951631,0.2888571,"<div id=""html_08e6e250b0318619cfe1485dbddd51f5"" style=""width: 100.0%; height: 100.0%;""><head><meta charset=""utf-8""><link href=""../../../../output/html/style.css"" rel=""stylesheet""/></head><body class=""readout""><div><h1 class='h-popup'>Fincham's Close, Linton</h1><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Included in the Lonsdale/Bakers Lane/Bartlow Road/Finchams Close group identified as a key risk area where internal property flooding was reported on 20 July 2021; flooding involved rapid entry into properties with water levels receding relatively quickly. [PAG] (p9)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Group of streets identified as a key risk area where internal property flooding was reported; properties experienced rapid ingress of water consistent with flash flooding. [PAG] (p10)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>Surface water continued towards Finchams Close causing external flooding around properties. Surface water also entered the foul drainage system, causing flooding of the foul (sewer) network. [TAB] (p12)</p></div><div class=""nugget-popup""><p>During the intense storm on 20 July 2021 surface water flowed into Finchams Close producing surface water flooding. Misconnections or ingress to the foul/sewer network and riparian maintenance issues were noted as contributing factors to the flooding here. [TAB] (p20)</p></div><i>Quantified impacts</i><div class=""nugget-popup quant""><p>15&ndash;45cm (depth in Lonsdale); 15&ndash;20cm (depth in Bakers Lane and Bartlow Road); residents displaced for 1&ndash;8 months (p12)</p></div></div></body></div>",Cambridgeshire,"Fincham's Close, Linton",England,"Included in the Lonsdale/Bakers Lane/Bartlow Road/Finchams Close group identified as a key risk area where internal property flooding was reported on 20 July 2021; flooding involved rapid entry into properties with water levels receding relatively quickly. [PAG] (p9)
Group of streets identified as a key risk area where internal property flooding was reported; properties experienced rapid ingress of water consistent with flash flooding. [PAG] (p10)
